window.AKK_MATRIARCH_MANUAL_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_MATRIARCH_MANUAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: Newlywed","paragraphs":["\"I know you feel wronged.\"","This was the first sentence Cheng Zhao's newlywed husband, Zhou Yuanshen, said to her.","When he said this, he had not yet lifted her bridal veil, so Cheng Zhao did not see him.","The young male voice was formal and proper, yet carried a hint of coldness.","\"The situation is a chaotic mess, and we are both but pawns. When the future becomes clear and things are set right, I will help you get a divorce so you can remarry. For now, live here in peace. I will explain things to Chancellor Cheng myself.\"","Hearing this, Cheng Zhao's heart skipped a beat.","After he finished speaking, footsteps echoed in the room. The sound, neither heavy nor light, gradually faded away before Cheng Zhao realized what had happened.","She forcefully pulled off her veil, only to see a tall, straight back disappearing from her line of sight.","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","The room full of dowry maids and older women servants looked at each other in dismay.","\"What is the meaning of this?\" Her head dowry maid, Suyue, had eyes filled with shock and confusion.","Cheng Zhao remained silent.","The room was so quiet you could hear a pin drop.","\"...Fifth Miss?\"","Cheng Zhao had been silent for too long, prompting Suyue to call out to her in a low voice.","\"Help me change my clothes and remove my makeup,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Suyue was appalled. \"Are we not waiting for the groom?\"","\"He won't come. Not only will he not come tonight, but he won't come in the future either,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Suyue's face turned extremely ugly. \"This is too much! Your marriage was bestowed by Her Majesty the Empress. The Ministry of Rites prepared the wedding, and you married into the Duke's estate legitimately and honorably. How dare they?\"","The last few words practically dripped with hostility.","The Cheng family was no poor, lowly household to be bullied by the Zhou family at will.","Cheng Zhao said, \"Change my clothes first. I need to rest.\"","Suyue was still unwilling to let it go.","Then she heard Cheng Zhao say, \"Do you think tomorrow morning will be peaceful? Conserve your energy first.\"","Tomorrow morning?","For the traditional tea-serving ceremony on the second day of the wedding, would the Duke's estate really dare to cause trouble?","The bridal chamber was quiet. The bed curtains were extremely thick, almost completely blocking the glow of the red candles in the room. Cheng Zhao had been tired all day; no matter how heavy her thoughts were, she couldn't fight off her drowsiness, and she fell asleep.","The maid Suyue kept the night watch, resting on the footstool nearby. Hearing her master's even breathing, she felt both sad and amused, and eventually drifted into a deep sleep as well.","At the hour of Yin the next day, Cheng Zhao's dowry nanny came in to wake her up.","The new bride had to perform the tea-serving ceremony, so she needed to dress up grandly once more.","Just as she finished washing up and put on her clothes, but before her hair was combed, Nanny Fan, a manager who served Cheng Zhao's mother-in-law, arrived.","Nanny Fan smiled brightly and said to Cheng Zhao, \"Third Young Madam, our Madam says she is not feeling well today, and the Old Madam also caught a chill last night. You may stay in your own courtyard today; there is no need to go out.\"","She added, \"Rest assured, the gifts for your return visit to your maiden home on the third day have already been prepared for you.\"","The face of Cheng Zhao's head maid, Suyue, darkened like the bottom of a pot. \"Insolent!\"","Nanny Fan glanced at the maid in surprise.","Suyue held her slender neck high and angrily rebuked Nanny Fan, \"Our Madam's marriage was bestowed by Her Majesty the Empress. How dare you treat her so harshly?\"","After a moment of stun, Nanny Fan smiled and said, \"It is not harsh treatment; this is out of consideration for the Third Young Madam. She was tired all day yesterday, wasn't she?\"","\"No matter how tired she is, how can the tea-serving ceremony be delayed?\" Suyue glared at her.","Not consummating the marriage and not performing the tea-serving ceremony meant they simply did not acknowledge this marriage.","From now on, Cheng Zhao living in this estate would be nothing but a joke.","And the return visit on the third day was just a show for the Empress and the Cheng family.","They wanted to put Cheng Zhao under house arrest.","Cheng Zhao came here to be the Duchess.","Suyue trembled with anger.","The Fifth Miss was suddenly granted this marriage, leaving the Ministry of Rites only four months to prepare for the wedding. Because it was an imperial bestowal, all the betrothal gifts and dowry were provided by the Imperial Household Department.","During those four months, the Zhou family of the Duke Chen's estate did not send a single person to the Cheng family to formally acknowledge the ties.","There was absolutely no contact.","The Cheng family all knew this was inappropriate, and that Cheng Zhao's marriage would be fraught with difficulties.","But while the hereditary Duke's estate dared to disregard the Empress's decree, the Cheng family did not dare, so Cheng Zhao had to bite the bullet and marry into the family.","She never expected that this Duke's estate wouldn't even do the bare minimum to keep up appearances.","It wasn't as if the Cheng family was marrying above their station.","The Cheng clan hailed from a prominent aristocratic family in Wu Commandery, highly respected and regarded as a noble and pure lineage since the previous dynasty; furthermore, Cheng Zhao's grandfather was the current Chancellor, with countless disciples.","It wasn't as if Cheng Zhao had to marry into the Zhou family.","Suyue was about to make a move, but Cheng Zhao held her back.","\"Qiubai, escort Nanny Fan back,\" Cheng Zhao called to another dowry maid.","The dowry maid named Qiubai was thin and frail. Like Nanny Fan, she wore a natural smile and appeared extremely gentle and demure.","\"Yes,\" she replied softly, her voice delicate and sweet.","As soon as Nanny Fan went out, Cheng Zhao said, \"Continue, my hair hasn't been combed yet.\"","\"Fifth Miss...\"","Cheng Zhao took Suyue's hand and told her, \"Open that trunk with the gold-plated corners and distribute the items inside.\"","Suyue was startled. \"Truly?\"","\"Naturally.\"","Cheng Zhao's tone was extremely slow.","The dejection on Suyue's face was completely swept away. She opened the trunk with the gold-plated corners, took out six small crossbows, and distributed them to Cheng Zhao's dowry maids.","She wore one herself and saved the remaining one for Qiubai.","Soon, Qiubai returned.","Nanny Li, the manager, had finished combing Cheng Zhao's hair and was inserting a gold hairpin inlaid with rubies.","Qiubai stood behind her.","Cheng Zhao looked at her in the mirror. \"How was it?\"","\"I memorized the route, Fifth Miss,\" Qiubai said. \"The Second Madam's courtyard is called Jiangyun Courtyard; it is not far from your courtyard.\"","Suyue finally realized, \"The Fifth Miss asked you to escort her back just so you could scout the way.\"","Qiubai smiled slightly and silently strapped the small crossbow onto her wrist.","The managing nanny helped Cheng Zhao put on her earrings.","Looking at her, the managing nanny smiled and said, \"This is what a young lady from a noble and distinguished family should look like: well-educated, reasonable, gentle, and amiable.\"","Cheng Zhao smiled and stood up.","\"Let's go. We are going to pay our respects to my parents-in-law,\" she said.","The six maids followed her with quiet steps, heading toward Jiangyun Courtyard where her parents-in-law lived.","When they reached the entrance, Cheng Zhao heard a scolding voice.","\"Marrying such a daughter-in-law, she is inferior to the eldest branch's daughter-in-law in every way! I will never be able to turn my life around; I will be suppressed by the eldest branch for the rest of my life!\"","\"I disagreed with this marriage from the start. But all of you were so cowardly and timid, not daring to decline it for fear of offending Her Majesty the Empress.\"","The frail and slender Qiubai kicked the courtyard door open.","The door latch cracked in response. As it broke and fell, all the voices inside the courtyard instantly vanished, leaving an absolute silence.","Cheng Zhao, walking with the most elegant lotus steps typical of noble ladies of the time, headed toward the main hall of Jiangyun Courtyard.","Her parents-in-law, sitting in the main hall drinking tea, were neatly dressed and waiting for breakfast. It looked like they had been up for a long time.","Seeing the intrusion, they stood up and looked at Cheng Zhao in astonishment.","Someone stepped forward to block her, only to see the maids behind Cheng Zhao each raising a short crossbow.","The small arrows gleamed with a cold light.","The maids and older servants were terribly frightened, also intimidated by the aggressive aura of the door being kicked open just moments ago. Some screamed, some dodged, but absolutely no one dared to approach.","Cheng Zhao's father-in-law, after recovering from his shock, stood up and blocked her mother-in-law behind him.","\"Cheng Shi, if you have something to say, say it properly.\" He pulled a long face. \"Causing such a massive scene, you cannot bear the crime of disrespecting your parents-in-law.\"","\"What Father-in-law says is absolutely right. Your daughter-in-law would not dare to be disrespectful.\" Cheng Zhao smiled and bent her knees in a curtsy. \"Your daughter-in-law, Cheng Shi, pays her respects to Father-in-law and Mother-in-law.\"","The Second Madam: \"...\""]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: The In-Laws' Game","paragraphs":["Armed and holding the line, Cheng Zhao took control of the situation.","Her mother-in-law, the Second Madam of the Zhou family, looked extremely displeased and immediately ordered her maid to bring out her spear.","However, she was stopped by Cheng Zhao's father-in-law, the Second Master Zhou.","\"A mother-in-law and daughter-in-law fighting in the courtyard—if word of this gets out, or even reaches the imperial court, everyone will laugh at us, and others will get exactly what they want,\" the Second Master said.","The Second Madam snapped, \"I don't care!\"","\"The First Branch will laugh.\"","The Second Madam immediately dropped her aggressive stance.","The couple did not tell the kneeling Cheng Zhao to rise, so Cheng Zhao stood up on her own.","She took a few steps closer, pressing toward the Second Madam. \"Mother-in-law, could you bestow the jadeite bracelet on your wrist to your daughter-in-law?\"","The Second Madam flew into a rage. \"You...\"","Without waiting for her to finish, Cheng Zhao slightly raised her voice, cutting her off. \"Mother-in-law, why do you live in the Jiangyun Courtyard instead of Chengming Hall, the main courtyard of the Duke's estate?\"","The Second Master gasped.","This daughter-in-law was truly fierce.","These words hit the Second Madam right where it hurt, and her face turned ashen.","Just as the Second Madam prepared to strike, Cheng Zhao did not retreat an inch. She stared directly into her eyes. \"The Zhou family's noble title is hereditary and passes down without being downgraded.","It was only because the First Master and the two young masters of the First Branch passed away that the title fell to the Second Branch. Yet, even though your son has inherited the title, the honor seems to have nothing to do with the Second Branch.","The massive estate properties of the Duke's mansion, which bring in hundreds of thousands of taels of silver a year, are controlled by the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the First Branch. The most prestigious main courtyard, Chengming Hall, is occupied by them as well.","As the Second Madam, you used to have to listen to the First Branch and were suppressed at every turn. Now, you still cannot turn things around. How could you not be resentful?\"","The Second Madam froze.","She had not expected Cheng Zhao to have found out everything about the Zhou family.","Was it already widely known outside?","Then why wasn't anyone speaking up for her injustice?","\"Mother-in-law, why is this?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","The Second Master thought to himself: Why else? The Old Madam favors the First Branch, of course.","The Second Madam thought the same.","But Cheng Zhao said, \"Because the Old Madam never intended for the Second Branch to inherit the family estate. If the eldest legitimate son of the First Branch hadn't suddenly died of illness, it wouldn't have been the Third Young Master of the Second Branch's turn. Moreover, with my father-in-law, a legitimate son, still alive, she let a legitimate grandson inherit the title. Why does she look down on the Second Branch so much?\"","\"Because she is biased!\" the Second Madam said through gritted teeth.","Cheng Zhao smiled faintly. \"Mother-in-law, this is not bias. You come from the estate of the Pillar of State General, and my father-in-law serves as a military official. The Third Young Master grew up at the border and served in the capital garrison after establishing military merits. The Second Branch carries the spirit of warriors in its blood.\"","\"What's wrong with warriors?\" The Second Madam grew angrier. \"The Old Duke earned his title through military service, helping the late emperor conquer the realm.\"","She added, \"The Old Madam comes from a scholarly family herself, so she looks down on military officials!\"","The Second Master coughed lightly. \"Do not speak ill of Mother.\"","The Second Madam retorted, \"She's biased, and I'm not even allowed to complain?\"","The Second Master was momentarily at a loss for words.","Cheng Zhao looked at her parents-in-law with a serene expression. \"Father-in-law, Mother-in-law, it is not that the Old Madam is biased. Since ancient times, families have been sustained by poetry and literature, not swords and spears.","For a family to endure for a century, the descendants must study to accumulate prestige and earn the respect of others.","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the First Branch both come from scholarly families. The Old Madam values them because she is entrusting the family's century-long legacy to them.","Mother-in-law, given your background, as long as the Old Madam is alive, you will always be suppressed by your eldest sister-in-law.\"","The Second Madam also gasped.","It seemed to be the first time she had heard someone analyze it like this for her, and she looked at Cheng Zhao seriously.","\"Mother-in-law, the Old Madam is very healthy. You will be suppressed for decades to come,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam: \"...\"","It was simply despairing.","She had never gotten along with her eldest sister-in-law, and they constantly competed with each other.","Losing at every turn was infuriating.","\"...Then what should I do?\" She asked Cheng Zhao, treating a dead horse as a living one in a desperate attempt.","Seeing that the conversation had reached this point, Cheng Zhao took a slight half-step back, her attitude becoming much more respectful. \"Mother-in-law, haven't I married into the family?","You can count how many poets, famous scholars, and prime ministers the Cheng clan, a prominent family of Wu Commandery, has produced throughout the dynasties.","When it comes to nobility and a scholarly heritage, which of the maternal families of the First Branch's mother-in-law and daughter-in-law has the right to be arrogant in front of the Cheng clan?\"","The Second Madam: \"...\"","This was exactly what she hated about the Cheng clan.","Every single one of the noble young ladies from these cultured families was annoying.","\"You need to know where the battlefield is,\" Cheng Zhao continued. \"Only by knowing who the enemy is can you win.","What the Old Madam values is not the cleverness or household management skills of the First Branch's mother-in-law and daughter-in-law, but the 'heritage' behind them. From now on, what they have, we have too.","Mother-in-law, as long as we are of one mind, we can move into Chengming Hall within two years. That is the main courtyard of the Duke's mansion, and it should belong to us.\"","The Second Master gave his daughter-in-law a surprised look, then quickly averted his gaze. A father-in-law and daughter-in-law rarely crossed paths under normal circumstances, let alone stared at each other.","The Second Madam's eyes, however, lit up slightly.","Cheng Zhao looked at her. \"Mother-in-law, can you give your daughter-in-law the jadeite bracelet on your wrist now? For today's traditional greeting ceremony, your daughter-in-law needs a 'talisman' to hold down the fort. Only with the precious bracelet you bestow upon me can I establish my footing.\"","The Second Madam hesitated for only a few breaths before taking off the bracelet.","She pulled Cheng Zhao's hand forcefully and slipped the bracelet onto her wrist.","\"Don't be like those scholars, only having a sharp tongue. I want to see your real skills!\" the Second Madam warned fiercely.","Cheng Zhao complied.","She withdrew her hand and smiled radiantly. \"How shall the greeting ceremony begin, Mother?\"","Changing 'Mother-in-law' to 'Mother'—she really knew how to push her luck.","But the Second Madam did not stay angry. Simply because Cheng Zhao's smile was like the first bloom of the morning glow, dazzlingly beautiful.","This daughter-in-law truly had a beautiful face.","The eldest daughter-in-law of the First Branch was pretty, but the Second Madam's daughter-in-law was not bad either.","Very well. Perhaps they really could win and vent this deep-seated frustration!","\"Someone, prepare the firecrackers. Go and announce that the Duchess is about to perform the greeting ceremony,\" the Second Madam said.","Nanny Fan complied.","The Second Madam looked at Cheng Zhao again. \"Tell your people to put away their small crossbows.\"","As if to save face, she added, \"These flashy moves of your maids are nothing to look at. I come from the estate of the Pillar of State General.\"","Cheng Zhao gave Suyue a look.","The maids put away their small crossbows. One by one, they held their breath, lowered their eyes, and slightly hunched their shoulders, looking delicate and fragile.","The Second Madam was dumbfounded.","They could actually do that?","It was as if they hadn't been acting like fierce demons just a moment ago.","\"Yes, my maids cannot compare to even a single hair of Mother's maids,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam snorted, as if to say, It is good that you know.","She walked outward, suddenly catching sight of the broken door latch at the courtyard gate. She turned back and asked, \"Who kicked the door just now?\"","She hadn't seen clearly at the time.","She had only seen Lady Cheng walking in with her people, unhurriedly and gently revealing their weapons.","It was simply shocking.","Cheng Zhao's tone was very light. \"This door latch must have broken on its own due to years of disrepair.\"","She sighed, \"Mother, your daughter-in-law truly feels wronged for you. This Jiangyun Courtyard is so dilapidated; how is it worthy of your status? You are the mother of the Duke.\"","The Second Madam: \"...\""]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: Acknowledgment","paragraphs":["At the entrance of the Duke of Chen's mansion, firecrackers blared in unison.","The servants were shocked and hurried to report the news to their respective masters.","\"Didn't they say the Guankui ceremony wouldn't be held?\" Nanny Sun, who served by the Dowager Madame's side, was truly surprised.","She went inside to inform the Dowager Madame.","The Dowager Madame had risen early to pray to Buddha. She had just stepped out of the small Buddhist hall, preparing to have some breakfast.","Hearing this, the Dowager Madame frowned.","\"What is going on with the second master and his wife? They were the ones making a fuss about not holding the Guankui ceremony, and now they are the ones going back on their word,\" the Dowager Madame said.","Nanny Sun said, \"The Second Madame is truly unreasonable. You shouldn't indulge her.\"","\"The family will have to divide eventually. Their own affairs should be decided by themselves,\" the Dowager Madame said slowly.","As soon as she finished speaking, the Second Madame and the Second Master arrived at the Dowager Madame's Shou'an Courtyard, inviting her to the main hall in the front yard to hold the Guankui ceremony for Cheng Zhao.","The Dowager Madame's gaze was serene. \"Did they consummate the marriage yesterday? I heard that Yuan Shen went to the Capital Garrison in the middle of the night, and a special decree opened the city gates to let him out.\"","\"They did not consummate,\" the Second Madame said in a relaxed tone. \"We have the final say in this matter; how would outsiders know? The Guankui ceremony must be held. After all, the marriage was decreed by Her Majesty the Empress.\"","Seeing her speak so lightly, the Dowager Madame gently closed her eyes.","\"Then let us hold it,\" the Dowager Madame said. \"Second daughter-in-law, do not say I am biased in the future. For your daughter-in-law, I have done everything according to your preferences. You are the one who wants it this way, and you are the one who wants it that way.\"","Second Madame: \"...\"","But you are biased, and I am not allowed to say it?","Everyone in the Duke's mansion was invited to the main hall in the front yard.","The Dowager Madame sat facing south; the Second Madame and the Second Master sat beside her, second only to her.","The Second Madame's manager, Nanny Fan, guided the ceremony. Cheng Zhao paid her respects to the Dowager Madame and her parents-in-law, offering them greeting gifts, which were all shoes and socks.","When Cheng Zhao raised her hands, a precious emerald jade bracelet was revealed from her sleeves. Many people saw it, including the Dowager Madame.","The Dowager Madame glanced at her daughter-in-law, then at Cheng Zhao.","She didn't say anything.","Nanny Fan then led Cheng Zhao to meet the others.","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the eldest branch were the most important.","Cheng Zhao exchanged greetings with them, offering embroidered pouches and handkerchiefs she had made herself. She also met the others, including Miss Mu, who was rumored to become the Secondary Wife to the Duke in the future.","Miss Mu's name was Mu Jiang. She was picked up by the Emperor and raised by the Dowager Madame. She was seventeen years old this year.","She was bright, beautiful, and valiant, dressed in luxurious clothes. Her scarlet dress was even more magnificent than that of Cheng Zhao, the bride.","A pair of almond eyes fell steadily on Cheng Zhao, her gaze sharp.","As an orphaned girl without a formal status, she could not marry the Duke as his primary wife. She could only wait until the primary wife entered the household before being elevated to a concubine.","Because her backers were the Dowager Madame and the Emperor, no one dared to call her a concubine. Even when rumors spread outside, people would say the Emperor would bestow her upon the Duke as a Secondary Wife.","Mu Jiang was not yet a concubine. She mingled among the female relatives of the Duke's mansion, even taking a prominent position near the front.","Cheng Zhao offered a handkerchief.","Mu Jiang accepted it and returned a pouch.","They looked away from each other, not making eye contact again.","When the two of them interacted, everyone's eyes were fixed on them, wishing they could spot something amiss.","As a new bride, Cheng Zhao naturally wouldn't dare to do anything, but Mu Jiang was famously fierce and competitive. They thought she would make a sarcastic remark, but unexpectedly, she was so well-behaved.","On second thought, the Duke went out on his wedding night, and the Guankui ceremony was almost canceled. Neither the Duke nor the Zhou family treated the Cheng woman as one of their own. Mu Jiang was probably too busy gloating; why would she need to provoke her?","The Dowager Madame's attitude remained lukewarm throughout.","Even though Cheng Zhao wore the bracelet gifted by the Second Madame on her wrist.","The others, however, thought more highly of Cheng Zhao because of this bracelet. After all, the Second Madame had accepted her, which was surprising.","\"Since the marriage was decreed, the Second Madame was the one cursing the loudest. How is she the first to play the good guy now?\" Everyone secretly criticized.","After the greeting gifts, came the most important part of the Guankui ceremony: the bride had to show off her culinary skills and offer food to her parents-in-law.","Normally, the kitchen would have already prepared everything. The bride would merely take a stroll to the kitchen for show, and then bring the food over to present to her parents-in-law.","Cheng Zhao also went to the main kitchen.","As soon as she left, the main hall became lively.","\"Second Aunt, I thought there wouldn't be a Guankui ceremony today. Didn't they say the bride was feeling unwell?\" The Zhou family's Eldest Young Madame, the eldest daughter-in-law of the first branch, Huan Qingtang, said this.","The Second Madame was annoyed just looking at her.","Of course, she didn't just hate the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the eldest branch for controlling the noble estate's assets, but also because this Eldest Young Madame had some ambiguous and unclear history with her son.","Originally, Huan Qingtang was supposed to be her daughter-in-law.","It was an old matter, better left unmentioned. The Second Madame had suffered defeat in front of the eldest branch's mother-in-law and daughter-in-law more than once or twice.","\"The marriage was decreed by Her Majesty the Empress; she is the Duchess. How could we not hold the Guankui ceremony?\" the Second Madame said coldly.","Cheng Zhao went to the kitchen but made everyone wait for an hour before returning.","During this time, there was inevitably a lot of whispering.","An hour later, Cheng Zhao returned with the servant women. The servant women carried a few breakfast dishes, and Cheng Zhao took them over.","She first handed a type of pastry to the Dowager Madame.","The Dowager Madame's attitude had remained very cold. She took a symbolic bite, but suddenly froze; then, she took a deep look at Cheng Zhao.","This glance even carried a hint of ruthlessness.","She looked again.","Cheng Zhao did not step back, standing respectfully in front of her.","The Dowager Madame's sharp look flashed by and was quickly concealed. To the onlookers, it seemed she merely paused, took a couple of extra glances at Cheng Zhao, and then a smile surfaced on her face.","\"This jade dumpling cake tastes quite good. The bride is indeed from a prominent family in Wu Commandery; her upbringing is so good, and her culinary skills are outstanding. Having you as the Principal Daughter-in-law is a blessing for the Zhou family,\" the Dowager Madame said with a smile.","As soon as these words came out, the main hall suddenly fell silent.","The two sons of the eldest branch had both passed away. Zhou Yuanshen's ranking had risen from the third son of the Zhou family to the eldest son, and he had also inherited the noble title.","Although it was somewhat inappropriate for the old madame to call Cheng Zhao the Principal Daughter-in-law, it wasn't exactly wrong if it was solely meant to elevate her status.","The faces of the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the eldest branch suddenly looked unnatural.","What did this mean? Was the Dowager Madame really going to hand over the noble estate's assets to this Duchess? But they hadn't petitioned the emperor to grant her an official title yet. Would they petition for her in the future?","The Second Madame was even more shocked.","She had no idea what kind of madness had taken over the Dowager Madame to suddenly favor the second branch, personally acknowledging Cheng Zhao and calling her the Principal Daughter-in-law.","Among those whose interests were tied to this, only the young Mu Jiang instantly changed her expression, looking at the Dowager Madame in astonishment.","The Dowager Madame finished eating the jade dumpling cake and repeatedly praised Cheng Zhao's culinary skills.","Cheng Zhao then offered food to her parents-in-law.","This time, her father-in-law, disregarding whether it was appropriate, took several looks at her face.","It seemed the new bride's capabilities were truly not small.","How strange.","\"She is not among the noble ladies with resounding reputations throughout the capital. The Cheng family also has a few girls with excellent reputations, but this Fifth Miss is not one of them,\" the Second Master Zhou thought.","What was going on?","After the Guankui ceremony, the entire mansion was boiling with excitement, and everyone was discussing it.","Cheng Zhao walked back with her parents-in-law.","The Jiangyun Courtyard and Nonghua Courtyard where they lived were quite far from the main hall, belonging to the secluded courtyards within the Duke's mansion.","The Second Madame's heart was full of questions she wanted to ask, but she didn't know where to begin.","As they neared the entrance of the Jiangyun Courtyard, the Second Madam turned to Cheng Zhao and said, \"You can return the emerald jade bracelet to me now, right?\"","Fearing that Cheng Zhao might think her stingy, she quickly added, \"This is a family heirloom passed down from my mother. If I lose it, the old lady will skin me alive. She is still hale and hearty, you know, strong enough to wield a long spear.\"","Cheng Zhao let out a meaningful \"Oh.\" \"Mother, so there is actually someone you are afraid of? I must pay a visit to Grandmother someday.\"","She then added, \"Grandmother should like me, shouldn't she?\"","The Second Madam thought to herself, more than just like! What she has always wanted most is a daughter just like Cheng Zhao, quiet, gentle, and beautiful.","But wait, something was wrong!","Cheng Zhao gracefully curtsied. \"Father, Mother, your daughter-in-law will take her leave now.\"","She turned and walked away, completely failing to return the emerald jade bracelet to the Second Madam.","Staring at her retreating figure, the Second Madam suddenly snapped to her senses. \"Did I just expose my own weakness? Did I just hand her leverage against me?\"","The Second Master replied, \"Yes. From now on, if you try to bully her, she knows exactly who to complain to. And she even has a token to prove her case, that emerald jade bracelet.\"","The Second Madam was speechless. \"...\""]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: The Snipe and the Clam Grapple","paragraphs":["The Guan Kui ceremony at the Duke's estate was even more bustling than the grand wedding yesterday.","Inside Dowager Madame's Shou'an Courtyard, she sat alone, lost in thought. Nanny Sun offered her some tea, which she took in her hand, remaining silent for a long time.","\"You do not look too well,\" Nanny Sun said with some concern. \"Was there something wrong with that jade rice cake?\"","Dowager Madame pondered.","She suddenly said, \"Nuanyu, in what year did Commandery Princess Zhaoyang die?\"","Nanny Sun's heart skipped a beat.","She was not very willing to bring up this matter, and knowing that Dowager Madame was also afraid to mention it, she equivocated, \"It must have been twenty years ago.\"","\"Eighteen years,\" Dowager Madame corrected her.","Nanny Sun looked at her nervously. \"What is the matter with you?\"","\"What if she didn't die? Could the Cheng family have secretly hidden her?\" Dowager Madame said. \"Was she pregnant with a child back then?\"","Nanny Sun's face turned pale. \"You are overthinking it. She is dead through and through.\"","\"The new bride's given name has the character 'Zhao', and she is seventeen years old this year,\" Dowager Madame said.","Nanny Sun was stunned and almost knocked over the teacup in Dowager Madame's hand.","\"A given name is truly too far-fetched of a connection,\" Nanny Sun said. \"Please do not overthink it. Why would you suddenly recall such unlucky events of the past?\"","Dowager Madame breathed a soft sigh of relief. \"Forget it.\"","She set down the teacup, told Nanny Sun she was tired and wanted to rest, and dismissed her.","Voices could be heard from outside.","Nanny Sun listened closely and said to Dowager Madame, \"Miss Mu is here.\"","Dowager Madame felt somewhat fatigued. \"Tell her to go back.\"","Nanny Sun complied.","After placing a cushion behind Dowager Madame and serving her as she half-reclined, Nanny Sun walked out of the inner bedchamber.","\"Nanny Sun, I need to see Grandmother,\" Mu Jiang said urgently.","\"Dowager Madame is a bit tired and has already rested. Miss Mu, please lower your voice,\" Nanny Sun said.","\"But...\"","Nanny Sun waved her hand.","Mu Jiang did not dare to act out of line and had no choice but to leave Shou'an Courtyard.","She was still in disbelief, shocked by Dowager Madame's use of the term \"principal wife\".","Cheng Shi was nothing but a mere decoration.","It was the Empress who was trying to curry favor with the Chen Duke's estate, not the Zhou family trying to please her. There was absolutely no need to take Cheng Shi, whose marriage was bestowed by the Empress, seriously at all.","Mu Jiang had barely slept last night. She had only felt a bit happier upon hearing that Zhou Yuanshen had gone out; this morning, when she heard there would be no Guan Kui ceremony, she was in an excellent mood.","To go from a clear blue sky to being covered in dark clouds took only a short two hours.","Cheng Shi possessed an exceptionally extraordinary beauty, and for some inexplicable reason, she had managed to win over the Second Madame. Actually, it was understandable. The Second Madame was brainless, stupid, and naive, making her very easy to rope in.","But why would Dowager Madame also elevate Cheng Shi?","Was she setting her up for a fall?","Regardless, the tone of the servants had changed, and Mu Jiang was extremely unwilling to accept this.","She was going to take over the Duke's estate in the future. The ones she relied on behind her were the Emperor and Dowager Madame; no one had the right to step over her.","The Duchess was only one in name. The real power would be held in her hands as the secondary wife, which was also what Dowager Madame had hinted to her.","\"Miss, should we return to our room?\" her personal maid asked.","\"I am going to the capital military camp to find Third Brother,\" Mu Jiang said. \"Things in the estate are getting a bit out of control, and Third Brother does not know yet.\"","She turned to go to the carriage house to select a horse, and the maid could not stop her at all.","She lived more freely than most of the masters in this estate, and none of the servants dared to disrespect her.","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the First Branch remained perfectly quiet.","However, the managing nannies and first-rank senior maids around them were somewhat uneasy.","\"Chengming Hall is the main courtyard of the Duke's estate. As long as Dowager Madame does not tell me to move out for a single day, we will remain the true female masters of the Duke's estate,\" the First Madame said to her trusted confidantes.","She comforted them and told them not to panic.","The Second Madame had absolutely no right to live in Chengming Hall, and she completely lacked the ability to manage the household affairs; the newly married young Madame was even more incapable of doing so.","The transition of power would require bloodshed and death. Dowager Madame would never tolerate the Second Branch snatching it away.","As long as Dowager Madame did not die, the First Branch would always be the masters of the Duke's estate.","The confidantes retreated, and the First Madame fell into deep thought.","\"Mother, please do not worry either,\" the First Young Madame, Huan Qingtang, keenly sensed her mother-in-law's emotions and comforted her softly.","\"No, I am just wondering what Dowager Madame meant by 'principal wife'. You and I are the true principal wives of the Duke's estate.\"","Huan Qingtang smiled. \"It was just a polite remark for the occasion.\"","\"What if Cheng Shi has an heir...\"","\"She won't. Dowager Madame is even more afraid of Cheng Shi having an heir than we are. If she has her own child, where would that leave Mu Jiang? Dowager Madame wants to support Mu Jiang,\" Huan Qingtang said.","\"We must think of a way to ensure Cheng Shi never has an heir. As long as this 'Duchess' does not die and never has a legitimate son, Chengming Hall will forever be ours,\" the First Madame said.","Chengming Hall, of course, did not just refer to this courtyard, but to the status, position, and noble properties attached to it.","The noble properties of the Chen Duke's estate included over two hundred thousand mu of farmland alone, ranking first among the high-ranking noble families in the capital. No one was as wealthy and prominent as the Zhou family.","Although the First Madame was a widow, because she managed the household, she could still go out to socialize as usual, and wherever she went, others would flatter and curry favor with her.","All of these things were given to her by \"Chengming Hall\".","\"Mother, isn't this simple? There are many ways to make a woman unable to bear children,\" Huan Qingtang said.","She added, \"However, there is no need to act rashly for now. The Duke and Mu Jiang are deeply in love. He will naturally let Mu Jiang give birth to the eldest son first before he consummates the marriage with Cheng Shi. We just need to wait for now.\"","She also said, \"Someone else is more anxious than we are.\"","The First Madame nodded slightly.","She looked at Huan Qingtang and said, \"Back then...\"","\"I have absolutely no relationship with Third Brother. He has no affection for me, and I am not familiar with him either. It is all a misunderstanding by outsiders,\" Huan Qingtang said.","The First Madame replied, \"That is not what I meant. You have to adopt a son eventually. Rather than adopting, it would be better to give birth to one yourself.\"","Huan Qingtang's expression remained unchanged. She locked eyes with the First Madame for a few moments, restrained her smile, and sighed. \"Mother, you are making things difficult for your daughter-in-law.\"","\"In the face of survival, forget about a pure reputation,\" the First Madame said. \"How can an adopted son be as close to your heart as one born from your own belly? As long as 'Chengming Hall' is in our hands, we do not need to worry about any rumors or gossip.\"","Huan Qingtang lowered her eyelashes.","\"Mother, this is the second time you have said this,\" she said in a low voice.","The First Madame said, \"I am planning for your future.\"","\"Are you afraid I cannot outscheme Mu Jiang?\" Huan Qingtang asked.","Dowager Madame's heart leaned toward the First Branch; the Second Madame was a hothead who was easy to manipulate; the Duchess, Cheng Shi, was merely a decoration who would never gain status and power in the Zhou family.","The only one who could compete with the First Branch was Mu Jiang.","And Mu Jiang was cheerful, lively, and intelligent. She also shared a deep, illicit affection with Zhou Yuanshen and had the backing of two great mountains. She was very troublesome.","\"We cannot underestimate the enemy,\" the First Madame said.","Huan Qingtang said, \"Let us first have Cheng Shi clash with Mu Jiang to test Cheng Shi's depth.\"","\"Her?\"","\"Mother, do not look down on her,\" Huan Qingtang said.","\"It is not that I look down on her. She was just 'born at the wrong time'. Marrying into the Duke's estate at a time like this, where is there any place for her to gain a foothold?\" the First Madame said.","Huan Qingtang pondered.","She actually wanted to see for herself.","For no other reason than the fact that the Cheng family, an aristocratic family of Wu Commandery, had a resounding reputation, even more prestigious than her own maiden family, the Huan clan. She was somewhat curious about the daughter of the Cheng family.","Perhaps Cheng Zhao would bring her a surprise?"]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: Childhood Sweethearts","paragraphs":["The days passed quickly.","The Zhou family prepared gifts for the bride's visit to her maiden home and arranged for Cheng Zhao's brother-in-law to accompany her.","Early in the morning, Cheng Zhao sent her maid Suyue back first, telling her to inform the Cheng family that the groom had a \"secret mission\" and could not accompany the bride back home today.","This important errand could be a highly confidential mission that couldn't be inquired about.","Given Zhou Yuanshen's status and official position, it was perfectly normal for him to suddenly be entrusted with a secret mission.","First, she blocked the relatives from mocking her to her face.","As for what they discussed behind her back, Cheng Zhao couldn't control it.","For the bride's visit on the third day after the wedding, the newlyweds were the most important. The groom had to meet his parents-in-law and kowtow to the bride's ancestors.","If he couldn't go, doubling the return gifts was also acceptable.","To outdo the eldest branch, Cheng Zhao's mother-in-law deliberately elevated Cheng Zhao's status, preparing triple the return gifts, making it a grand affair.","She also sent Cheng Zhao's brother-in-law to accompany her—since the groom had a secret mission and couldn't go, his brother or another male elder could take his place.","Cheng Zhao had two brothers-in-law.","One was fourteen this year, staying with his uncle at the border; the other was eight, already beginning his studies, looking as exquisite as a carved jade statue, very adorable.","The one accompanying Cheng Zhao back home today was this eight-year-old brother-in-law.","His name was Zhou Yuanqi. He wore a sapphire blue robe with beautiful embroidery on the sleeves, his hair tied in twin knots, with red lips and white teeth, looking very handsome.","\"...You're also the fifth child? I'm the fifth too.\" Cheng Zhao chatted with him.","Zhou Yuanqi put on a serious expression like an old scholar, unsmiling: \"Yes, Third Sister-in-law.\"","\"Have you started your studies?\" Cheng Zhao asked again.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"Those who know do not speak, those who speak do not know.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...Are you telling me to shut up?\"","\"Third Sister-in-law is indeed a scholar,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao couldn't help but be amused by him.","Upon returning to the Cheng family, she heard some news: the day before yesterday, Princess Jiahe's only son was killed. The fight happened in a teahouse, and blood flowed into the street, a very terrifying scene.","The murderer was a relative of a side consort from Prince Rong's mansion.","This involved some romantic affairs and old grudges.","Cheng Zhao's marriage, in comparison, held no weight at this time.","\"My luck is quite good,\" Cheng Zhao told her mother.","With the murder case at Princess Jiahe's mansion, probably no one would gossip about Cheng Zhao's marriage, allowing her to escape the idle talk.","Her mother held her hand.","She asked about her situation over the past few days, and then asked about her husband, Zhou Yuanshen.","Cheng Zhao explained in detail to her mother.","Her mother said: \"The daughters of the Cheng family are meant to be titled ladies; there is no need to bicker over these trivial matters. You did very well.\"","She added, \"'Duchess' is a super-rank title, representing true wealth and honor in the future. The Zhou family's estate is the richest besides the princes. A'Zhao, you've secured half of a good life.\"","\"I will remember,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"You don't necessarily need to bear children yourself. As long as your husband has children, you have heirs. You must not fight with concubines out of jealousy. A 'secondary wife' is just for show; she is still a concubine,\" her mother added.","Cheng Zhao nodded again in agreement: \"I can tolerate her, don't worry.\"","\"...Your grandfather said he will urge the Zhou family to request your title as soon as possible,\" her mother added.","\"With grandfather and the Cheng family backing me, I'm not worried about the title,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"If you have the Old Madam's trust, your parents-in-law's high regard, and your husband's support, you will be able to establish a firm foothold,\" her mother added. \"Spend more effort on the Old Madam; as for your husband, cater to his preferences.\"","Cheng Zhao took her words as golden rules, remembering them all.","She would be an outstanding matriarch of the clan.","The return banquet was very lively. The Cheng family was powerful, and Cheng Zhao had married into a prominent family, so everyone at the banquet made excuses for Zhou Yuanshen.","In the mid-afternoon, Cheng Zhao returned to the Duke of Chen's mansion; the bridal chamber could not be empty within the first month.","At the entrance, she saw warhorses and lieutenants.","Before Cheng Zhao could say anything, her eight-year-old brother-in-law, Zhou Yuanqi, sneered like an old pedant: \"The barbaric brute has returned to the mansion.\"","\"Are you talking about the Duke?\" Cheng Zhao asked with a smile.","\"That's him,\" Zhou Yuanqi said dismissively.","He had not yet shed his childishness, but spoke in a very mature manner. Cheng Zhao found him very amusing.","\"We all have to depend on this brute for a living,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"Are you afraid?\" Zhou Yuanqi sneered.","Cheng Zhao: \"No, I mean don't scold him to his face. Talk about him behind his back.\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\"","All day, he finally looked Cheng Zhao in the eye once.","After looking, he turned his face away, continuing his aloofness.","Cheng Zhao couldn't help but laugh.","Upon returning to the mansion, she first went to Jiangyun Courtyard to pay respects to her parents-in-law.","The Second Madam had some expectations of this new daughter-in-law, but not too high. She also felt that Cheng Zhao didn't have much capability, only a few tricks up her sleeve, and she had just been bluffed by her.","\"The Old Madam sent word: in a month, there will be a concubine-taking ceremony. Miss Mu will be the Duke's secondary wife. You need to be prepared; she will live in the Lijing Courtyard to the east,\" the Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao's expression remained unchanged, and she said gently: \"The location of Lijing Courtyard is better than both of our courtyards.\"","The Second Madam: \"...\"","Her heart was stung again.","The location of the second branch's residence was very far from the main courtyard.","It was like the location of mansions and the imperial city: the closer you were, the more prominent your status; the further away, the less face you had.","Jiangyun Courtyard was quite far from Chengming Hall. When it was cold or hot, one even had to take a small oil carriage to get there, otherwise, they would be covered in frost or sweat, looking extremely pathetic.","And the Lijing Courtyard, which was about to be given to Mu Jiang, was closer to the main courtyard than the second branch.","\"The Old Madam ordered it, what can I do?\" The Second Madam was displeased. \"Stop making sarcastic remarks.\"","\"Yes,\" Cheng Zhao lowered her eyes.","The Second Madam added: \"Yuanshen has returned to the mansion; call him over tonight.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed again, thinking he definitely wouldn't come.","Sure enough, Zhou Yuanshen didn't come to the bridal chamber that night.","Not only that night, but he didn't come for the next half month either.","But from the servants' gossip, Cheng Zhao knew he was in the mansion. The Jingji Camp only required occasional roll calls; he didn't have to go every day.","For the past half month, Cheng Zhao was unhurried, going to pay respects to the Old Madam and her mother-in-law every day, never paying attention to any rumors.","She also didn't ask for \"requesting a title\" or \"managing household affairs,\" things the Zhou family clearly didn't want to give her.","She just waited.","Closing the courtyard door, she practiced swordplay and calligraphy every day.","It wasn't until mid-September, twenty days after Cheng Zhao married into the Duke of Chen's mansion, that she returned from Jiangyun Courtyard in the mid-afternoon and saw someone flying a kite.","\"Flying a kite in this weather?\" she was still muttering to herself.","Then she saw Mu Jiang.","She threw herself into the arms of a tall man, and he caught her.","Cheng Zhao heard a silvery laugh.","She turned into the bamboo grove nearby, avoiding them.","\"Is that the Duke?\" maid Qiubai whispered to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao nodded: \"It's him.\"","When she was granted the marriage, Cheng Zhao was taken by her second brother to a teahouse to look at Zhou Yuanshen from the window.","Her second brother said Zhou Yuanshen was handsome, outstanding in appearance, and skilled in both pen and sword, which was no exaggeration.","Cheng Zhao thought at the time: he didn't have the roughness of a military man she had imagined, and didn't look annoying.","\"...It seems this 'secondary wife' and the Duke are very affectionate,\" maid Qiubai added.","Cheng Zhao nodded: \"They must have grown up together as childhood sweethearts; the bond between them is something we outsiders cannot compare to.\""]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: Taking a Concubine","paragraphs":["A month after Cheng Zhao's wedding, Zhou Yuanshen took a concubine.","Mu Jiang moved into Lijing Courtyard.","However, the concubine-taking ceremony was not as lively as Cheng Zhao had imagined—no banquet was held.","When an ordinary family took a respectable concubine, she would be carried in through the side gate, and two tables of food and wine would be set up for relatives and friends to celebrate; for higher-status families, it just meant a few more tables.","When Zhou Yuanshen took Mu Jiang, there was no banquet. Only a firecracker was set off at the side gate when the small soft sedan chair entered.","\"The new concubine entered the manor tonight,\" said Suyue, one of Cheng Zhao's senior maids, with great disdain.","Her tone carried anger and contempt.","The managing matron, Nanny Li, reminded her, \"You should call her 'Secondary Wife'. Our lady has just arrived; do not stir up trouble over such trivial matters.\"","This was, of course, not for Mu Jiang's sake, but out of respect for the Old Madam.","The Old Madam's status was extraordinary.","Over thirty years ago, when the Emperor was still just the Tenth Prince, he married the eldest daughter of the Zhou family. As a young couple, they were deeply in love.","In his later years, the late Emperor grew senile and paranoid, ruthlessly killing his wives and children. With the imperial court shrouded in treacherous political storms, the Tenth Prince and his wife lived in constant fear.","Later, the Tenth Prince feigned illness, and the Old Madam of the Zhou family used the excuse of visiting relatives to take her entire family, along with her daughter and son-in-law, to the borderlands, thus escaping the power struggle.","When they returned eight years later, the Tenth Prince, who had wisely retreated from the fray, was the only surviving legitimate son of the late Emperor's first wife. The late Emperor no longer had the energy to cause further turmoil.","For those eight years, the Tenth Prince had only studied and completely avoided contact with the border army, behaving with the utmost propriety. He finally won his father's trust. Coupled with the strong backing of the Duke of Chen, he was installed in the Eastern Palace as the Crown Prince.","The following year, the late Emperor passed away, and the Tenth Prince ascended the throne.","It was just a pity for the eldest daughter of the Zhou family; her fragile health could not withstand the bitter cold of the northern frontiers, and she passed away from illness not long after returning to the capital.","During those most dangerous eight years, the Emperor had lived by the side of the Old Madam of the Zhou family. With his first wife dying young, he harbored a deep sense of gratitude and affection, leading him to frequently bestow rewards upon the Zhou family over the past decades.","In the Emperor's heart, the Old Madam was practically half an Empress Dowager.","Now, the Emperor had walked down the same path as the late Emperor, becoming paranoid and murderous.","The Old Madam had stepped forward several times, bringing him pastries made in the Zhou family's kitchen, which would somewhat soothe the Emperor's temper.","Let alone Cheng Zhao, even her grandfather, Chancellor Cheng, had to be mindful of the Old Madam's moods.","Mu Jiang was an orphan raised by the Old Madam, and rumor had it that the Emperor himself had picked her up back then. Regardless of the truth, the Old Madam favored her, and Cheng Zhao could not afford to touch this reverse scale.","At the very least, she could not call Mu Jiang \"Concubine Mu.\"","\"Suyue, do not feel wronged on my behalf,\" Cheng Zhao said to her senior maid. \"We need to establish a firm foothold first. The Zhou family did not ask for this marriage themselves, so it is understandable however they treat me. It will be much harder for me to establish myself than it is for an ordinary daughter-in-law.\"","She added, \"If the Old Madam suddenly assigned a maid to me and inserted her among you, would you be able to tolerate her?\"","Suyue respectfully lowered her head. \"I was wrong, Young Madam.\"","It had been a month since the wedding, and everyone around Cheng Zhao had changed how they addressed her, no longer calling her Fifth Miss.","Cheng Zhao's husband was a Duke, and she should rightfully be called \"Madam,\" but the Old Madam was still alive, and there were two generations of elders above them. Since the eldest young master's wife was called \"Young Madam\" by the servants, Cheng Zhao could only share the same generational title.","Seeing that Suyue had taken the lesson to heart, Cheng Zhao gave a slight nod. \"Let us go. It is time to pay our respects to Madam.\"","The September wind was a bit chilly, so a maid fetched a cloak for Cheng Zhao.","Zhou Yuanshen stood at the entrance of Jiangyun Courtyard, pondering as he looked at the gate, without raising his hand to knock.","There were footsteps behind him—not heavy, with small strides, suggesting the newcomer was short in stature, a child.","He did not move.","The person behind him spoke in a feigned mature voice, \"You are blocking my way.\"","Zhou Yuanshen was speechless.","He turned around and saw a child wearing a powder-blue robe. He looked like a doll carved from jade, with pinkish-white cheeks and pitch-black eyes, as pretty as a little girl.","His expression was serious.","He glanced at his younger brother; his brother tilted his head up, glaring at him with an unfriendly gaze.","Zhou Yuanqi's path had been blocked by his older brother. His little brain originally had several phrases to tell him to \"step aside,\" but then he felt they were too complicated and overly literary. A brute would not understand them, so he had to pick plain words.","\"After you,\" Zhou Yuanshen said, stepping to the side.","Zhou Yuanqi felt he was being teased.","But his brother was so tall, and talking to him was always a strain on Zhou Yuanqi's neck, so he could not be bothered to scold him and just stepped inside.","Zhou Yuanshen remained standing at the door. A moment later, the Second Madam came out.","\"Why don't you come in?\" the Second Madam asked him. \"Are we mother and son still holding grudges?\"","\"Mother ordered me never to step foot into Jiangyun Courtyard again. This son dares not be unfilial.\"","\"...And contradicting me is filial?\" the Second Madam flared up. \"Get in here right now.\"","The last time mother and son argued, the Second Madam had been so furious she wanted to whip him with a soft whip. It was over the matter of Chengming Hall in the Duke of Chen's manor.","The Second Madam wanted to live in Chengming Hall and obtain the honor and wealth that came with the title, but Zhou Yuanshen said that all of it belonged to his grandmother, and she could give it to whomever she pleased.","The mother and son could not see eye to eye, and the Second Madam angrily told him to get lost and forbade him from ever taking half a step inside again.","That was why he had stood at the door for so long.","\"Where is that secondary wife of yours? Why didn't you bring her over?\"","The Second Madam asked after they both sat down.","This was not meant to be nitpicking.","Since Mu Jiang was now with Zhou Yuanshen, she should frequently come to pay her respects to her mother-in-law from now on.","Zhou Yuanshen, however, replied, \"She is but a concubine; Mother need not elevate her status.\"","A concubine had no right to perform the daily morning and evening greetings to a mother-in-law; that was the duty of a daughter-in-law. Concubines in ordinary households were merely confined to their small courtyards, isolated from the world thereafter.","A concubine only needed to pay respects to the primary wife, which was Cheng Zhao.","The Second Madam was surprised. \"Everyone says she is a secondary wife...\"","\"Is a 'secondary wife' not still a concubine?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked in return.","The Second Madam was rendered speechless.","She did not say anything, and the Second Master did not speak up either. To the side, eight-year-old Zhou Yuanqi nodded. \"Those words are correct and very much in line with worldly etiquette. A wife is a wife, and a concubine is a concubine; the moral order cannot be disrupted. You have made progress.\"","Everyone fell silent.","The Second Madam thought to herself, what exactly had she raised?","Three sons, and not a single one acted like a normal son; they either acted like their father or like their ancestors.","After a few more words, Zhou Yuanshen stood up. \"Grandmother has something to discuss with me; I will have dinner over there.\"","The Second Madam asked, \"What is it this time?\"","The Second Master smiled and said, \"Let him go. With all the family affairs and his duties at the imperial court, he is busy enough.\"","The Second Madam said no more.","Zhou Yuanshen walked out the door and remembered there was something he had forgotten to mention to his parents, which he ought to tell them. He turned around and saw a group of people walking over from the eastern path.","The woman leading the group was tall and slender, followed by several maids.","Zhou Yuanshen did not look closely. There were not many masters in the Zhou family, and he remembered what everyone looked like, but this one was a stranger.","Without a doubt, it was the wife the Empress had arranged for him.","He had heard Mu Jiang mention a few things.","She had also said that his mother had already been won over by the new Madam and had even given her the family heirloom, an emerald jade bracelet. It had also been publicly acknowledged by the Old Madam.","These trivial matters held no meaning.","Having no interest in them, Zhou Yuanshen turned and walked away.","Cheng Zhao also caught sight of his back. Sweeping a glance from the corner of her eye, she casually withdrew her gaze and entered Jiangyun Courtyard."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: Blade in Hand","paragraphs":["Second Madam was straightforward and outspoken.","Seeing Cheng Zhao, she said, \"He just left, and you just arrived. Did you run into him?\"","\"I saw someone walking away in the distance, heading towards the main courtyard. I figured it was the Duke,\" Cheng Zhao replied.","Second Madam regretted her words as soon as she said them.","She was afraid Cheng Zhao would complain to her about being neglected by her husband and bring up the Empress's bestowed marriage.","However, after saying that, Cheng Zhao naturally added, \"My small kitchen made some sour radish duck soup. I brought some for Father and Mother to taste.\"","She then teased the child, \"Fifth Brother is in for a treat today. Have an extra bowl.\"","Zhou Yuanqi lifted his head aloofly, ignoring her; Second Madam breathed a sigh of relief.","Second Master had always remembered others saying that a daughter-in-law and father-in-law should never cross paths. But this was his first time being a father-in-law, and his daughter-in-law was so neat and generous that they naturally became acquainted without any awkwardness, so he didn't bother avoiding her.","\"What kind of duck soup is this?\" he asked curiously. \"We've never had it.\"","\"It's a Wu Commandery recipe. My maiden family always cooks it in autumn and winter. It relieves dryness and is very nourishing,\" Cheng Zhao said.","A maid brought forward a large food box containing a covered jar.","Cheng Zhao served the food for her parents-in-law and brother-in-law.","Second Madam was not yet used to putting on the airs of a mother-in-law. Coming from a military family, she was used to freedom and despised the affectations of gentlewomen. She didn't impose many rules on Cheng Zhao either.","\"Sit down and eat with us,\" Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao complied.","The sour radish duck soup was delicious, much more savory than Second Madam had imagined, and the sourness was not too overpowering.","The picky Zhou Yuanqi quickly drank half a bowl and even picked out the duck meat to eat. One must know, he was always finicky and never ate the meat from a soup.","Following the rule of silence during sleep and meals, they finished their dinner quietly.","After dinner, Cheng Zhao served Second Madam to wash her hands and rinse her mouth, then stood up to take her leave.","She didn't mention a single word about Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanqi also returned to his courtyard to review his studies.","As they rested for the evening, Second Madam said to her husband, \"I must say, these well-bred ladies from scholarly families do have their merits.\"","Second Master replied, \"If you want to praise our daughter-in-law, just say so. Did one bowl of soup buy you over?\"","\"Don't interrupt,\" Second Madam said in dissatisfaction.","\"Alright, alright, go on.\"","\"She can keep her composure. It's been a month since she married in, and Mu Jiang has openly become a presence, yet she hasn't cried or made a fuss. I haven't even seen a hint of panic in her. I truly admire this kind of temperament,\" Second Madam said.","Second Master remarked, \"Women in the inner chambers are very good at enduring.\"","\"It's the girls from these scholarly families who can endure. If she were my daughter, I wouldn't bear to let her suffer such grievances,\" Second Madam said.","Second Master sighed.","Second Madam continued, \"You should talk to Yuanshen. You father and son can speak easily; tell him not to neglect his legal wife too much.\"","Second Master replied, \"Yuanshen mentioned it last time: this matter concerns the political situation. It was the Empress's idea, and the underlying intentions are unclear. The Emperor has had a bad temper these past few years, and with no crown prince established, the court is extremely chaotic.","Yuanshen is a close minister to the Emperor; he is better at guessing the imperial will than we are. Since he neglects the person the Empress arranged for him to marry, he naturally has his reasons. Don't interfere.\"","\"Aren't I just pitying Cheng Shi? With such beauty, she's left guarding an empty room.\"","\"I don't think Cheng Shi is making herself miserable; she seems in good spirits,\" Second Master said.","How could someone wallowing in misery have the mind to order the small kitchen to stew such delicious duck soup?","Second Madam worried for Cheng Shi, but Cheng Shi seemed to have a clear head, neither fighting nor snatching, very well-behaved and suited for living a steady life.","If they had a daughter like Cheng Shi, it would seem quite nice.","Second Madam told him he didn't understand and urged him to help persuade Zhou Yuanshen.","Even if they couldn't be affectionate or mutually respectful, if he just made a token appearance at Nonghua Courtyard every month, the servants wouldn't dare bully her.","\"...Alright, I'll talk to Yuanshen next time. But don't make a big fuss about it. Mother wants to support Miss Mu,\" Second Master said.","Uplifting Cheng Shi at this time would be going against Dowager Madame.","\"Mother even calls Cheng Shi the eldest daughter-in-law. I don't believe she would reprimand me,\" Second Madam said.","Second Master: \"She won't do it to your face, but she will drop hints with hidden meanings to point it out to you.\"","Second Madam turned over to sleep, saying lazily, \"I won't understand.\"","If it wasn't a direct scolding to her face, she didn't have the patience to listen.","Anyway, Dowager Madame didn't like her, and she had lived through it for over twenty years.","Second Master: \"...\"","Later, Second Master found an opportunity and said a few words to his son.","Just as Second Master expected, Zhou Yuanshen indeed replied, \"I know what I'm doing; Father doesn't need to worry.\"","He added, \"I have made things clear between Cheng Shi and me. If she doesn't understand, I will tell her again next time.\"","\"Don't be angry with her,\" Second Master said. \"She has a good temper. It wasn't her complaining; it's your mother who is worried.\"","Zhou Yuanshen remained expressionless, and it was unknown whether he took the words to heart.","Returning to the estate that day, Zhou Yuanshen went straight to Nonghua Courtyard.","Nonghua Courtyard had a few servants from the Zhou family, but they only did rough work like sweeping and washing. Those who served in the main room were all Cheng Zhao's dowry servants.","Among the dowry maids was a thin and frail one who looked very inconspicuous. She answered in a low voice, \"The Young Madam went to the Fifth Young Master's courtyard to deliver soup to him.\"","Zhou Yuanshen didn't say a word and turned to leave.","When Cheng Zhao returned and heard that Zhou Yuanshen had visited, she felt slightly surprised.","\"...He didn't look too pleased,\" Qiubai said.","Cheng Zhao recalled her actions over the past few days. She paid her respects to her parents-in-law as usual, never neglecting them; she hadn't run into anyone else from the Zhou family; and the only other thing was delivering soup to Zhou Yuanqi.","She hadn't violated any taboos.","\"Did he say what it was about?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Qiubai shook her head.","Cheng Zhao: \"It shouldn't be anything important. If it were urgent, he would come back.\"","However, Zhou Yuanshen did not come again.","Several incidents had recently occurred in the capital, and Zhou Yuanshen's shadow could be seen in them: two marquis estates were raided and confiscated, both having meddled in the matter of establishing a crown prince and angering the Emperor.","In the imperial court, most officials pleaded for mercy, but only Zhou Yuanshen stood on the Emperor's side and even listed the crimes of these two families.","Cheng Zhao went to Second Madam: \"I would like to make a trip back to my maiden home to see my mother.\"","Second Madam was free-spirited and undisciplined. She couldn't do anything harsh to others, so she merely asked, \"Is my in-law alright?\"","\"I just dreamt of her last night,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam: \"Then go ahead.\"","Cheng Zhao returned home. After seeing her parents, she went to her grandfather's courtyard.","Her grandmother had passed away over a decade ago, and the one serving her grandfather was an elderly concubine. She was gentle and kind, and had taken good care of Cheng Zhao.","\"...Zhou Yuanshen, is he preparing to become the Emperor's blade?\" Cheng Zhao asked straight to the point.","When the Emperor killed his officials, he feared leaving a bad reputation, so at such times, he needed a treacherous official to charge at the forefront.","The downfall of the two marquis estates was because the Emperor wanted to kill them, but many people in the streets were gossiping about Zhou Yuanshen.","\"He has always had the Emperor's favor and is the Emperor's most trusted official,\" her grandfather said.","\"The Zhou family doesn't need to seek wealth and honor through danger. What is he after?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","\"On the path of wealth and status, if you do not advance, you retreat. The Zhou family's heirs are sparse, lacking successors,\" her grandfather replied. \"Every family has its own predicament. Zhou Yuanshen might not want to inherit the ancestral estate.\"","Cheng Zhao understood now."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: Mandarin Wife of Honor","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao returned to the Chen Duke's Estate in the mid-afternoon.","After visiting the Second Madam, she returned to the Nonghua Courtyard.","After dinner, the sky grew dark, and lamps were lit indoors.","Her managing matron, Nanny Li, asked her, \"What did the Prime Minister say?\"","\"Grandfather told me to stay here with peace of mind,\" Cheng Zhao replied. \"He also told me some inside information about the Zhou clan.\"","She added, \"The Duke might take on the lineage of both branches. The Old Madam mentioned this to the Emperor. The Emperor had a headache at the time and didn't hear it clearly, but the head eunuch reminded him later. Grandfather was right there.\"","Nanny Li pondered, \"That makes sense. The Old Madam doesn't want to adopt a child from a collateral branch.\"","Once an adoption occurs, the Old Madam would have to make a decision about which branch gets the noble title and estate. If they don't adopt, the eldest son and eldest grandson would have no one to offer incense to them, leaving them as nameless ghosts, and the maternal families of the First Madam and the Eldest Young Madam would never agree to that.","The only solution was for Zhou Yuanshen to inherit both branches.","This way, his eldest sister-in-law would also become his wife, and the title and estate would smoothly remain with the first branch.","Both the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the first branch were excellent women carefully selected by the Old Madam. Their maternal families had good reputations and could cultivate the noble and pure prestige of the Zhou clan.","The words \"noble and pure\" were envied by everyone; all high-ranking aristocratic families desired such a reputation.","\"...But if that happens, your situation will become even more difficult,\" the managing matron added.","\"I need to find a way to improve my reputation. The time is too short, so many of my methods cannot be put into practice, and they won't show immediate results anyway,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"How about I try paying respects to the Old Madam more often?\"","The managing matron ordered the senior maids to withdraw.","She whispered to Cheng Zhao, \"If the Duke doesn't come to you, you won't be able to board the ship of the Zhou clan.\"","If she didn't board the ship, all the glory and struggles on it would actually have nothing to do with Cheng Zhao.","The best and fastest method was to quickly become a true husband and wife with the Duke and have a child.","Pausing for a moment, the managing matron continued, \"The Old Madam won't change her opinion of you just because you are diligent. Last time, when you used the jade dumpling incident to threaten her, she only grew to resent you more.\"","\"I understand,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"It's just that the Duke has recently taken in Concubine Ru, and the two are deeply in love. Making a move on him now would be rash. We can only wait until Concubine Ru gets pregnant first.\"","The managing matron called Cheng Zhao naive.","\"The Old Madam has already rewarded Concubine Ru with two beautiful maids. Once she is pregnant, these two maids will be elevated to bedchamber maids. The Duke won't possibly be able to leave the Lijing Courtyard,\" the managing matron said.","Cheng Zhao asked, \"You even managed to find that out?\"","\"I asked the older female servants from the Jiangyun Courtyard. The Second Madam is quite well-disposed toward you and is willing to guide us.\"","Cheng Zhao gave a slight nod. \"My mother-in-law has a pure and kind heart and is unguarded against others.\"","She added, \"The Old Madam is just taking advantage of my mother-in-law's good temper. Since the Duke has inherited the title, there must be an explanation regarding the estate. Leaving my mother-in-law suspended like this, neither up nor down, is extremely awkward. Anyone else wouldn't be able to stand it.\"","It was a tremendous slap in the face.","It wasn't just about the title and estate, but also personal dignity. Anyone put in the Second Madam's position would feel a lingering sense of injustice.","The two were chatting idly when they suddenly heard a sharp cry of alarm from outside.","Cheng Zhao immediately stood up.","Night had just fallen. The courtyard still held half a ray of golden sunset light, but the base of the walls was pitch black.","Cheng Zhao's maid, Qiubai, was curled up into a ball. The cry of pain had come from her.","\"Qiubai!\" Cheng Zhao hurried over.","The others quickly gathered around.","Nanny Li brought over a palace lantern. Shining it on Qiubai, she first saw her head covered in cold sweat; then, looking at the hand she was clutching, they saw her thumb starting to turn black.","\"...Something moved, and I thought someone was peeping. As soon as I reached out, it bit me. It's a 'Slow Wind Snake',\" Qiubai said.","She added, \"Quick, bring a knife. This hand must be chopped off to save my life.\"","Suyue immediately ran back to the room to get a knife.","Cheng Zhao's heart ached fiercely.","She knew about the Slow Wind Snake; it was a type of black snake used to transmit messages. It was as thin and long as a rope, but its mouthparts were extremely long. Secret reports could be stuffed into its mouth, and it moved as fast as the wind.","Being so swift, it was deliberately given the lowly name \"Slow Wind.\"","Most Slow Wind Snakes used for messaging had their fangs removed.","Cheng Zhao said to another maid, \"Use a rope to tie Qiubai's wrist tightly, pierce her finger to let out the poisoned blood, I need to go out for a moment!\"","Slow Wind Snakes were very difficult to breed, and military spies used them to pass messages. For it to appear in the Duke's Estate, there was only one possibility: it was raised by Zhou Yuanshen.","Since he raised this snake, he definitely had the antidote.","Cheng Zhao strictly instructed, \"Do not chop off her hand, wait for me to return!\"","She strode out.","As Cheng Zhao walked out of the Nonghua Courtyard, she suddenly realized that she had no idea where Zhou Yuanshen lived.","Marrying into the Duke's Estate, to establish a firm foothold, the Duke himself was not important in the initial stages. She needed to smooth out her path first before she could take a step further: getting household management power and having a child. Only then would she need to use Zhou Yuanshen.","Furthermore, Zhou Yuanshen was avoiding Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao had not planned to accomplish everything at once. She held many of the Zhou family's secrets, but the one thing she didn't know was where Zhou Yuanshen usually rested.","Although her mind buzzed for a second, Cheng Zhao did not stop her steps and ran directly toward the Lijing Courtyard, where Concubine Ru, Mu Jiang, lived.","There was a high probability that Zhou Yuanshen was staying at the Lijing Courtyard.","Cheng Zhao walked extremely fast, with a maid following behind her. The master and servant dashed madly in the direction of the Lijing Courtyard. Her shoes did not fall off, but a hairpin dropped from Cheng Zhao's head, and half of her hair bun came loose.","She knew the location of the Lijing Courtyard.","She knocked forcefully on the door.","A maid opened the door, saw her, didn't recognize her, and frowned: \"Who are you?\"","\"I am the Duke's wife. I need to see the Duke,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The maid immediately tried to close the door: \"The Duke is not here!\"","Cheng Zhao raised her voice, \"My Lord Duke! My Lord Duke, my maid was bitten by a Slow Wind Snake, I need the medicine!\"","Her voice was loud enough to carry into the courtyard.","There was movement inside.","Cheng Zhao saw Concubine Ru, Mu Jiang. She seemed to have already gone to bed, wearing only her inner garments. Her black hair cascaded over her shoulders like a waterfall, looking charming and naive.","Upon seeing Cheng Zhao, she shut the courtyard door without a word.","The courtyard door almost hit Cheng Zhao's nose.","\"The Duke is not a doctor. If your person is injured, go fetch a doctor yourself,\" Mu Jiang replied coldly from behind the door, her voice haughty.","She added, \"Coming to knock on doors in the dead of night shows a lack of upbringing. Even the courtesans in the brothels wouldn't stoop to your methods. You are utterly shameless.\"","Just as Cheng Zhao was about to kick the door, someone suddenly spoke from behind her.","\"Looking for me?\"","It was a young man's voice, cold and clear. She had heard it before, on their first wedding night.","Cheng Zhao turned around.","Her hair was messy, and her face was covered in sweat—whether from the heat of running or a cold sweat—with strands of hair sticking to it. She looked utterly disheveled.","The man was not in the Lijing Courtyard but had come from elsewhere. He stood in the shadows of the courtyard wall, dressed in black robes. His face could not be seen clearly; only his tall, slender silhouette was visible.","\"My Lord Duke, my maid...\"","Before she could finish her sentence, Zhou Yuanshen raised his hand. \"Here is the medicine.\"","He tossed over a medicine bottle.","Cheng Zhao reached out and caught it.","\"She won't die within half an hour. The venom of the Slow Wind Snake is not that terrifying,\" he said.","Cheng Zhao merely said her thanks and hurriedly went back.","She couldn't care about anything else.","However, the incident of her barging into the Lijing Courtyard at night and attempting to steal the man still spread throughout the Chen Duke's Estate.","The servants inevitably gossiped.","They said that Madam Cheng, having been given the cold shoulder for so long, had finally gone mad.","Cheng Zhao barely slept that night; she and her trusted aides stayed gathered around Qiubai.","After being bitten by the snake, Qiubai panicked at first, but a moment later she grew completely calm, even prepared to chop off her own hand to save her life. The others carefully carried her back to the room and bled her fingertips. She then adjusted her internal energy, slowing her breathing to a crawl.","She knew some internal martial arts and could hold her breath underwater for the time it takes a stick of incense to burn. It was exactly this \"turtle breath\" technique that delayed the spread of the snake venom.","Cheng Zhao had also brought back the antidote.","After taking the medicine, Qiubai gradually fell asleep.","Though she slept soundly, Cheng Zhao and the others felt no drowsiness at all.","\"I will stay and watch over her. Young Madam, go take a nap and come back to see her when you wake up,\" Suyue said.","Cheng Zhao agreed.","She went into the inner bedroom and sat on the heated brick bed by the window, completely devoid of sleepiness.","Among her personal maids, Qiubai was the only one with true martial arts skills; Suyue only knew some basic fist and footwork, merely amateur tricks. The other maids had learned to use short crossbows.","On the second day of her marriage, Cheng Zhao had indeed frightened the Second Madam.","When Cheng Zhao's father was in office, he had saved an armed escort's family during a lawsuit. Having no other way to repay the debt, the escort sent his daughter, who had practiced martial arts since childhood, to serve as Cheng Zhao's maid.","Cheng Zhao was seven years old that year. Suyue was also sold into the manor to be a maid that same year. She had spent ten years together with Qiubai and Suyue.","She taught them how to read and do needlework, while Qiubai taught Cheng Zhao and Suyue martial arts.","When they grew a bit older, her mother taught her two older sisters how to manage a household, and Cheng Zhao learned alongside them. She, in turn, taught Qiubai and Suyue how to read account books and cook.","At the rooster's crow, Nanny Li came in and whispered to her, \"Qiubai is awake. She says she is very hungry.\"","She added, \"If she knows she's hungry, it means she should be fine. You should go inform the Second Madam and have the steward take the estate tally to invite a doctor to take a look at Qiubai. That way, you can be completely at ease.\"","\"I will go see her.\"","Qiubai's face was pale. She sat up and said her entire body felt weak.","\"It must be the lingering poison. You need to rest for a few days,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"I will go find Mother and ask her for help in calling a doctor.\"","She turned and left.","Cheng Zhao told the Second Madam the whole story from beginning to end, also mentioning the Slow Wind Snake.","The Second Madam clicked her tongue. \"His uncle gave that to him. It's meant for delivering messages in the military. Who would have thought he wouldn't remove its fangs?\"","She offered a few words of pity for Qiubai, then immediately dispatched an older servant woman with her tally to have the steward invite a doctor skilled in treating snake venom.","Cheng Zhao thanked her repeatedly.","After she left, the Second Madam said to her trusted maid, \"She looks like she hasn't slept all night. A person who knows how to protect her own people has good character.\"","Before the doctor even arrived, the rumors beat him to it.","The estate's tea water room was the liveliest place in the morning, as the masters of every branch required hot water for washing. With so many people bustling about, news spread the fastest there.","The Second Madam's maid returned and told her that Madam Cheng had gone to the Lijing Courtyard the previous night to snatch a person away, only to be harshly scolded by the concubine.","\"...The concubine's insults were incredibly harsh, and those gossiping old women are repeating them everywhere,\" the maid said.","The Second Madam knew exactly what had happened and was so furious she almost suffered a heart attack. \"How dare she spread such slanderous rumors! Tell them all to shut up!\"","But how could they be stopped?","The Second Branch lacked prestige, and the servants had been acting like snobs who served dishes based on the guest's status for far longer than just a day or two.","Everyone was waiting to watch the new madam make a fool of herself. Coupled with their desire to curry favor with Mu Jiang, they naturally seized the opportunity to trample Cheng Zhao into the mud.","The Second Madam was half-dead with anger.","Belittling Cheng Zhao was a slap in the Second Madam's face. She was absolutely enraged.","She even took her anger out on Cheng Zhao.","The Second Madam was not bad at heart, but when her temper flared, she could be quite exasperating. \"Did you not know to send a maid to look for someone? Now look what's happened! Both mother-in-law and daughter-in-law have become a laughingstock, and you've dragged me down with you.\"","Cheng Zhao's attitude remained gentle.","She respectfully apologized to the Second Madam. \"It was all your daughter-in-law's lack of consideration that caused trouble for Mother.\"","The Second Madam said, \"Look at them, this is exactly how they bully people. It infuriates me. I can't hold my temper, and I was counting on you to have some self-restraint. Who knew it would be a case of 'birds of a feather flocking together'?\"","Her tone was poor, but her words implicitly treated Cheng Zhao as family.","Cheng Zhao dropped the formalities, stepped forward, and took her arm. \"Mother, please do not be angry.\"","The Second Madam was stunned for a moment.","She felt very surprised, and a bit odd.","Her fiery temper extinguished.","She felt extremely awkward.","She had never acted affectionately toward her own mother or mother-in-law. Since she had no daughter of her own, no one had ever been this intimate with her either.","The Second Madam wasn't exactly \"at a loss,\" but her attitude did soften momentarily.","\"Mother, this is a good opportunity. You must help your daughter-in-law and have them spread these rumors even further and wider,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam's eyes went wide. \"Have you lost your mind?\"","People usually tried to avoid scandals. Who would deliberately pour dirty water on themselves?","Cheng Zhao explained, \"Once the matter spreads out of control, I will go cry and complain to Her Majesty the Empress. When that time comes, to prevent the Duke from gaining a reputation for 'favoring the concubine and destroying the wife,' the Old Madam will have to compromise. They will have to request an imperial title for me.\"","The Second Madam froze.","\"Will that actually work?\" she asked hesitantly.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"If you kill a thousand enemies but lose eight hundred of your own, you still profit by two hundred. A narrow victory is still a victory. 'Duchess' is an ultra-ranked imperial title. Even if it is just an empty name, it is highly useful.\"","The Second Madam was speechless.","The female members of the Zhou clan all had imperial titles, but the Old Madam was a Duchess, as was the First Madam. Their status was entirely unshakable.","If Cheng Zhao received one too, the Second Madam would finally have room to breathe.","\"Gossip is hard to listen to. Don't go crying when the time comes,\" the Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao said, \"Thank you, Mother, for your care.\"","The Second Madam snorted.","She felt a strange sensation in her heart—a little sour, yet a little soft. Just a few words from Cheng Zhao had made her want to reward the girl with something nice.","Mu Jiang was indeed belittling Cheng Zhao everywhere.","\"...In the Duke's estate, she is completely powerless to fight back. She shouldn't think that an imperially bestowed marriage allows her to throw her weight around. I will make her learn her place early on,\" Mu Jiang said.","As a concubine, she wanted to completely overshadow Cheng Zhao to the point of irrelevance.","The First Branch was also discussing the matter.","The First Madam said, \"Madam Cheng is too young and too impatient. If she had just been obedient and kept to her place, she might not have lost so much face.\"","She added, \"Mu Jiang certainly has some skills, forcing Madam Cheng into such a desperate corner in such a short time that she completely abandoned her dignity.\"","The Eldest Young Madam, Huan Qingtang, however, was deep in thought.","\"Mother, will trampling Madam Cheng like this backfire? Mu Jiang is not in the right here,\" Huan Qingtang said.","Mu Jiang had monopolized the Duke, and Madam Cheng, as the legal wife, had to go snatch him back. If word of this spread, both the Duke and Mu Jiang would be viewed unfavorably.","Madam Cheng only lost face. But in terms of broader moral principles, she might actually draw sympathy.","\"Mu Jiang doesn't need to be in the right. She has the Old Madam's backing, the Duke's favor, and the Emperor as her patron. By stepping on Madam Cheng to build her own prestige, she is guaranteed to win,\" the First Madam laughed.","Watching the Second Branch make a fool of themselves was also quite entertaining.","However, things gradually spiraled out of control.","Several titled madams went to pay their respects to the Empress, and it was unknown who among them brought up the matter.","The Empress was furious.","She didn't dare summon the Old Madam of the Zhou clan, but she did summon the First Madam of the Zhou clan into the palace to ask if it was true.","\"...Does Duke Chen disregard all moral principles? Does he wish to favor his concubine and destroy his wife?\" the Empress demanded.","Prime Minister Cheng used the incident to ask Duke Chen when he planned to request an imperial title for his granddaughter, since they were, after all, already married.","Knowing she was in the wrong, the Old Madam did not step forward to stop it.","In less than half a month, Qiubai fully recovered and was as lively as ever. At the same time, the imperial decree granting the title arrived at the Duke of Chen's estate.","The Zhou clan now had three ultra-ranked titled madams: the Old Madam, the First Madam, and Cheng Zhao.","The servants were momentarily stunned."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Kneel Down","paragraphs":["In Dowager Madame's Shou'an Courtyard, Mu Jiang was crying her eyes out.","\"I've told you countless times to be steady and composed. You must think thrice before acting.\" Dowager Madame pulled a long face, looking at her sternly.","\"Grandmother, I didn't spread rumors; she really did come knocking on my door in the middle of the night,\" Mu Jiang said, feeling wronged.","She was stunningly beautiful, especially those eyes, which were charming, dazzling, and seemed capable of stealing one's soul. Her eyelids were swollen from crying, making her look exceptionally pitiful.","She was like a little pet kept by Dowager Madame. Dowager Madame could scold or beat her when angry, but she would never allow anyone else to lay a finger on Mu Jiang.","When she caused trouble, Dowager Madame was furious; when she cried so pitifully, Dowager Madame's heart ached.","\"...You still don't know you're wrong.\" Although Dowager Madame's words were harsh, her attitude had softened.","\"Teach me, then,\" Mu Jiang said, resting her head on Dowager Madame's knee. \"I suffered a great loss this time, making a wedding dress for her.\"","\"She is the Duchess. If she comes to your door in the middle of the night, you should at least act 'flattered' and ask for the reason. Even if she really came to snatch someone, you should give her some face. This isn't out of respect for her, but for the Duke,\" Dowager Madame said.","Mu Jiang: \"...\"","Wouldn't that suffocate her to death?","The Zhou family didn't have any girls in this branch. Mu Jiang was the only \"adopted daughter,\" and she had been raised in the Shou'an Courtyard since childhood, only moving out to live on her own at the age of thirteen.","She was the most esteemed young lady of the Duke's estate.","In the future, she would also become the true, powerful mistress of the Duke's estate; the Duchess would merely be a figurehead and a decoration, at her disposal.","She would have her own son.","Her son could be registered under the Duchess's name, but he would definitely be raised by her side and have a deep bond with her.","When her son became the Duke, she would move into the Shou'an Courtyard, the place where she grew up.","She could foresee all the glory and wealth of her life, which was why she had such a big temper.","Telling her to tolerate Cheng Shi was impossible for her.","\"You threw a little tantrum and almost caused trouble for the Duke. We had to use the title of Duchess to suppress the charge of the Duke 'favoring a concubine and destroying his wife,'\" Dowager Madame said.","Mu Jiang cried even harder.","She wasn't regretful, but full of hatred and jealousy; these emotions churned within her, burning her insides.","Dowager Madame wiped away her tears and told her not to be sad.","\"The empty title of a titled lady is worth nothing. Our family doesn't lack titled ladies,\" Dowager Madame said.","She added, \"Hurry up and give birth to a son; that's the real business.\"","Mu Jiang said yes.","She lowered her eyelashes to hide her guilty conscience.","Offspring, how could it be that easy?","The eldest branch's mother-in-law and daughter-in-law, along with the servants, were just as shocked.","They never expected Cheng Zhao to sacrifice her reputation in exchange for such practical benefits.","\"...She comes from the Cheng family of Wu Commandery. How could she ruin her reputation for the title of 'titled lady' and tolerate such a shameful thing?\" First Madam was very surprised.","For a noble lady, reputation was more important than life.","If no one had fanned the flames, Mu Jiang's cursing would never have reached the Empress.","Cheng Zhao had married Zhou Yuanshen; she would get the title of titled lady sooner or later. Why ruin herself to get it now?","First Madam then said, \"Cheng Shi is actually mercenary and short-sighted. She doesn't seem like someone from a scholarly family, but rather like a merchant's daughter.\"","The eldest young madam, Huan Qingtang, also didn't approve of Cheng Zhao going to such lengths.","But she had to re-evaluate whether Cheng Zhao's desperate ruthlessness would win her more.","\"Mother, she's got her title. In the future, she'll also have the chance to go out and socialize. Perhaps she's more formidable than we imagined,\" Huan Qingtang said.","First Madam: \"You're flattering her too much. She's been married for less than two months and has caused quite a bit of trouble. Her 'three axes' must be almost used up, right?\"","Huan Qingtang still said, \"Mother, let's just wait and see.\"","First Madam didn't respond.","Only after Huan Qingtang left did First Madam say to her trusted servant, \"Lady Huan is talking without feeling the pain. Cheng Shi just married in and can already share the same title as me. How can I tolerate this?\"","First Madam had been the heir's wife for seventeen years before her father-in-law passed away and her husband inherited the title.","After her husband inherited the title, because he had to observe three years of mourning for his father, First Madam had waited twenty years after marrying in to get the title of \"Duchess.\"","Before she had held it for long, her husband and legitimate eldest son passed away one after another—they were both refined, quiet, and had suffered hardships with Dowager Madame in the borderlands in their early years, leaving them weak and sickly.","In contrast, the second branch was as strong as calves.","First Madam had endured twenty years of hardship to get her title, while Cheng Zhao easily got it by riding Mu Jiang's coattails.","Mu Jiang wasn't brainless; she was just too smooth-sailing and arrogant. Cheng Zhao stepped on Mu Jiang to \"climb to the high platform\" and stand shoulder to shoulder with First Madam.","Cheng Zhao hadn't experienced any of the hardships First Madam had suffered. How could her heart be balanced?","\"Lady Huan cannot understand my bitterness,\" First Madam said.","Cheng Zhao's success made First Madam's sacrifices seem worthless. For someone who had lived half her life, \"value\" was her roots; how could she allow it to be shaken?","Two days later, Dowager Madame hosted a banquet to celebrate Cheng Zhao receiving her title.","Although only female relatives of the Zhou family's close and branch families were invited, it still provoked the eldest branch and Mu Jiang.","At the banquet, Cheng Zhao was poised and well-mannered, and because of her good background and her current status as a first-rank titled lady, everyone praised her.","Second Madam saw it all and was somewhat moved.","She had never received such treatment; Cheng Zhao really had some skills.","When the banquet ended, Cheng Zhao saw off the guests one by one and exchanged a few pleasantries with Dowager Madame.","Just as they were talking, Mu Jiang arrived.","Mu Jiang wasn't qualified to attend today's banquet; she was only a \"concubine.\"","\"...Young Madam, congratulations,\" Mu Jiang said.","She wore a crimson long dress. The hem was embroidered with peonies, the embroidery so exquisite that the petals looked lifelike, like fresh flowers pinned to her hem, cold and fragrant.","She wore ruby jewelry. The vibrant color complemented her face, and her dazzling eyes outshone even the evening glow in the sky.","Compared to her flamboyant luxury, Cheng Zhao's sky-blue long dress, gold ornaments, and pearl earrings seemed very low-key and plain.","Second Madam sneered.","No matter how brightly Mu Jiang dressed up, her appearance was still thirty percent inferior to Cheng Zhao's.","\"Thank you, sister,\" Cheng Zhao smiled and turned to Dowager Madame. \"Sister has perfect manners; it's all thanks to Grandmother's good upbringing.\"","\"She's like a cat, wild and untamable,\" Dowager Madame chuckled. \"You two must be harmonious in the future and not argue anymore.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","Mu Jiang looked at Cheng Zhao again, her hand moving slightly under her sleeve.","Cheng Zhao sensed something was wrong. Just as she was about to dodge, Second Madam waved her hand and knocked down a small knife.","The hidden weapon injured someone; Second Madam's palm was cut.","The sudden turn of events caused the expressions of the Zhou family women to change drastically. The eldest branch's mother-in-law and daughter-in-law both looked at Dowager Madame's expression.","Dowager Madame had a kind face, as if she hadn't seen what happened clearly: Second Madam gasping in pain, the crisp sound of the knife falling to the ground—she seemed not to have heard any of it.","\"You...\"","Second Madam pointed angrily at Mu Jiang, then looked at Dowager Madame.","Just as she was about to make a scene, she saw Cheng Zhao take a few steps forward and slap Mu Jiang across the face.","With a hard slap, Mu Jiang's face was turned to the side; she was stunned.","Dowager Madame's eyes flashed, her gaze falling sharply on Cheng Zhao's face like a falcon's.","When no one spoke, Cheng Zhao opened her mouth: \"Kneel!\""]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: An Eye for an Eye","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao's shout of \"Kneel!\" commanded everyone's hearts.","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the eldest branch exchanged a glance, both seeing the shock in each other's eyes.","How dared Cheng Shi?","It would be a piece of cake for Dowager Madame to crush her and destroy her maiden family. The ignorant were fearless; Cheng Shi actually dared to hit Mu Jiang in front of Dowager Madame.","Wasn't this a direct slap in Dowager Madame's face?","The Second Madame also understood this. Her hand trembled, and she subconsciously reached out to block Cheng Zhao, wanting to protect her.","\"You dare to act fierce?\" Mu Jiang finally came to her senses after a long while, her voice sharp and piercing.","\"What's all this noise?\"","Suddenly, a young male voice came from the door.","Like everyone else, Cheng Zhao turned around following the voice and saw Zhou Yuanshen.","Before her wedding, she had looked down at him from a teahouse. He rode a horse through the street, and she saw his upright posture sitting on horseback; she didn't see him at the wedding.","The next two times, she only saw a back and a silhouette.","Until this moment.","It had not yet snowed in Kyoto in October, but it was cold in the mornings and evenings. Everyone wore thick clothes, yet Zhou Yuanshen only wore a dark robe embroidered with dark patterns, walking slowly and heavily to the bright hall of the Shou'an Courtyard.","It had been half a year since she last saw him at the teahouse. His skin was slightly paler, and he had added the nobility of a young master of an aristocratic family, losing some of the fierceness of a military general.","He was very tall, his shoulders and back straight and level, which made him look as deep as an abyss and as towering as a mountain, with extraordinary bearing.","When Mu Jiang saw him, her eyes instantly turned red, and tears rolled down: \"Third Brother, I was bullied.\"","Zhou Yuanshen examined her, swept a glance around, and turned his gaze to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao exchanged a glance with him, then lowered her eyelashes and gave him a curtsy: \"Concubine Cheng Shi, greets the Duke.\"","Before Zhou Yuanshen could speak, Mu Jiang rushed to say: \"She just got the title of a lady of rank, and she's throwing her weight around, daring to act fierce in front of Dowager Madame!\"","She kept saying that Cheng Zhao was disrespectful to Dowager Madame, but didn't mention why Cheng Zhao was so reckless.","\"You're turning black into white. Do you still have any rules?\" The Second Madame said angrily, \"It was clearly you who ambushed Cheng Shi and even hurt me.\"","She stretched out her hand to Zhou Yuanshen, \"Look, your mother was hurt by your Secondary Wife.\"","A scratch, with beads of blood seeping out, wasn't too serious.","The Second Madame got excited as soon as she argued. Her voice raised three pitches, and even if she was right, she lost the momentum.","Zhou Yuanshen withdrew his gaze, didn't answer the Second Madame, but looked at Dowager Madame: \"Grandmother, seriously speaking, this matter is a private affair within your grandson's room.\"","Dowager Madame was silent for a long time, and only now sighed faintly: \"You young people, your tempers are so big!\"","Then she said, \"Ah Jiang was a bit rude, it's all my fault for indulging her. I'll reflect on myself.\"","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the eldest branch immediately apologized: \"We wouldn't dare.\"","\"Grandmother doesn't need to blame herself, it's the younger generation's unfilial piety.\"","\"Mother constantly worries about her children and grandchildren. How can you be blamed for the children throwing tantrums?\"","Dowager Madame's \"self-reflection\" was actually putting pressure on them.","The Second Madame had seen this kind of trick for over twenty years, and every time she was confused: You said you wanted to reflect on yourself, but you should reflect! Why did one sentence suppress all the unfairness in the end, making the suffering people swallow the bitter fruit themselves?","This was power.","Dowager Madame's coercion, the mother-in-law's power.","The Second Madame turned her head to the side, not following the \"sincere fear and trepidation\". She really wanted to rebel.","\"Making Grandmother reflect on herself is all your grandson's fault. I deserve ten thousand deaths.\" Zhou Yuanshen's tone was very light.","His words were earnest, but his attitude was very cold.","He didn't wait for Dowager Madame to say anything, and changed the subject: \"This matter started because of Concubine Mu. Make her kneel in the courtyard for an hour to apologize to Grandmother.\"","Not to the Second Madame or Cheng Zhao, but to Dowager Madame.","Dowager Madame said she wanted to reflect on herself, forcing everyone to let this matter pass, but Zhou Yuanshen wanted to strike back by punishing Mu Jiang.","If Mu Jiang dared to resist or refuse the punishment, it would mean she was disrespectful to Dowager Madame.","Dowager Madame raised her eyes and looked at this grandson.","Zhou Yuanshen's eyes were pitch-black, his gaze quiet. He had practiced martial arts since childhood and didn't suit Dowager Madame's temper. Moreover, he was a man of few words but had sharp eyes, so Dowager Madame disliked him even more.","Choosing him to inherit the title was a helpless move.","Like the late emperor, the emperor inherited the genetic disease of the Helian royal family. He went mad at the age of forty, his paranoia reached a paranoid level, and his methods were cruel.","In the past two years, the emperor hadn't been rational very often, and old feelings were somewhat unreliable. If someone instigated him and the emperor took back the Zhou family's title when he went mad, Dowager Madame's lifelong efforts would come to nothing.","Besides the Second Master, the only grandson who had come of age was Zhou Yuanshen. He was Dowager Madame's forced choice.","\"Ah Jiang, go kneel in the courtyard.\" Dowager Madame finally spoke.","The room was frighteningly quiet.","Mu Jiang stared blankly at Dowager Madame, then looked at Zhou Yuanshen.","Meeting Zhou Yuanshen's eyes, which were as deep as a cold pool, she felt timid.","With thousands of grievances, Mu Jiang could only endure it.","She went to kneel in the courtyard.","\"It's getting late. Grandmother, please rest first. Your grandson will take his leave.\" Zhou Yuanshen bowed.","The Second Madame didn't react, and Cheng Zhao gently poked her waist.","And Cheng Zhao herself also said she was leaving and pulled the Second Madame's arm; the Second Madame was smart this time and left with her son and daughter-in-law.","After they left, the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the eldest branch also took their leave. Their mother-in-law and daughter-in-law were the best at reading people's expressions and would never touch a bad omen.","Dowager Madame was about to die of anger, and Mu Jiang was punished again. Staying at this time would make them a punching bag.","\"Qingtang, did you hear that? The Duke called Mu Jiang 'Concubine Mu'.\" The Eldest Madame lowered her voice.","The Eldest Young Madame, Huan Qingtang: \"Yes, daughter-in-law heard it.\"","\"He's so mean, actually saying this in front of Dowager Madame.\"","\"It seems that Mu Jiang has lost the upper hand.\" Huan Qingtang said.","After a pause, she added, \"Perhaps Mu Jiang and Dowager Madame didn't take Cheng Shi seriously, underestimated the enemy, and temporarily lost the upper hand. The second branch has a good show to watch.\"","The Eldest Madame: \"That's good too. Wait until they fight to the death, then bring up the matter between you and the Duke.\"","Huan Qingtang's expression was a bit unnatural.","The Eldest Madame comforted her: \"You are a lady of a pure family, and you can't accept sharing a husband for a while. But think about Cheng Shi. She got a title by being shameless. Sometimes we have to put down some airs for the sake of our future.\"","Huan Qingtang didn't say anything.","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law walked back slowly.","Cheng Zhao, Zhou Yuanshen, and the Second Madame walked back to the Jiangyun Courtyard.","The Jiangyun Courtyard was far from the main courtyard, and even further from Dowager Madame's Shou'an Courtyard. It took less than half an hour to walk.","The Second Madame wanted to complain, but the farce just now really shocked her, and she couldn't care less about complaining about the old, stale matters.","\"... You contradicted your grandmother.\" The Second Madame said to her son.","Zhou Yuanshen walked in front, not turning his head: \"It's okay. Grandmother is very fair. I'm just telling the truth.\"","The Second Madame: \"Isn't it because she looks down on your wife?\"","Then she asked, \"Where are you resting tonight?\"","The Secondary Wife was still kneeling in the Shou'an Courtyard.","Like Cheng Zhao, the Second Madame actually didn't know where Zhou Yuanshen usually slept.","He had been back from the border for two years. Before that, he had been living in his general's mansion and didn't return to the Duke of Chen's mansion to live; suddenly he was asked to inherit the title and was granted a marriage. He temporarily lived in the outer study of the Duke's mansion.","Now that he was married, he should have moved back to the inner courtyard to live.","It wasn't that the Second Madame didn't want to care, but this son had too strong an opinion, and she couldn't control him at all.","\"I will rest at Nonghua Courtyard,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Second Madam cast a glance at Cheng Zhao.","Nonghua Courtyard was the very courtyard where Cheng Zhao resided.","Was he merely joking, or was he being serious?"]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: The Couple","paragraphs":["Inside the Nonghua Courtyard, it was so quiet that one could hear a pin drop.","The maidservants all held their breath, their footsteps light and slow as they served tea and water.","Zhou Yuanshen sat upright on a chair in the main hall, lifting his teacup to take a couple of sips. He wore a dark robe, looking as if the night had extended from the doorway to drape over him.","The main hall suddenly felt much colder.","Perhaps the night wind blowing in was too chilly.","\"Tell them to withdraw,\" he finally spoke after a long pause. His voice was steady and flat, as cold as frost.","Cheng Zhao gave Suyue a meaningful glance.","Her dowry maids were all well-trained and immediately retreated silently outside the curtains.","\"...I originally told you to stay here with peace of mind, and wait until the situation becomes clear in the future,\" Zhou Yuanshen said slowly, holding his teacup.","His meaning was ambiguous.","Cheng Zhao sat in the seat next to him, turning her face slightly to look at him. \"Lord Duke, the Cheng family has no daughters who remarry. The idea of 'helping you divorce and remarry' truly feels like a bolt of lightning from the blue.\"","She understood the underlying meaning of Zhou Yuanshen's words.","Cheng Zhao had received her imperial mandate and had clashed with Mu Jiang in the Shou'an Courtyard; she was now too deeply involved in the Zhou family. It would be somewhat difficult for her to leave quietly in the future.","She had disrupted the arrangements Zhou Yuanshen had made for her.","Zhou Yuanshen raised his eyes and looked into hers.","\"So, you have accepted your fate?\" he asked.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"To be the 'Wife of a Super-rank Duke' is an excellent fate. It is something I could only dream of.\"","A trace of mockery seemed to flash in Zhou Yuanshen's eyes.","Cheng Zhao had no intention of playing games during their first proper conversation. Even if the truth was unpleasant to hear, she wanted her words to match her actions, to be accountable to herself.","The highest point a woman could seek in her life was to become the wife of a super-rank duke, and Cheng Zhao had achieved this before she was even twenty.","While she wouldn't say she went through \"untold hardships,\" it was something the vast majority of noble ladies could never attain in their entire lives. She could not possibly give it up.","Zhou Yuanshen's eyes returned to a state of calm.","He let out a soft sigh.","Setting down his teacup, he reached his hand out to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao was taken aback.","She was very surprised and froze for a moment. However, she reacted quickly; the hesitation lasted only a split second before she gently placed her hand in his palm.","Zhou Yuanshen led her into the bedroom.","The next day, when Cheng Zhao woke up, Zhou Yuanshen had already left.","\"...The Lord Duke got up at the beginning of the Yin hour. He woke up so early. You were still sleeping soundly,\" Suyue said in a low voice.","Nanny Li looked at Suyue. \"Do not speak out of turn. You must be more careful from now on.\"","Suyue complied.","Cheng Zhao got out of bed, washed up, and changed her clothes. Nanny Li combed her hair, dismissed the young maids, and whispered to Cheng Zhao, \"Congratulations, Madam.\"","Nanny Li collected the virginity cloth; she would deliver it to the Second Madam later.","They had consummated their marriage last night.","It was an unexpected joy.","Nanny Li had thought that the Lord Duke would insist on waiting until the Secondary Wife conceived an heir before coming to the Nonghua Courtyard.","Just like the request for the imperial mandate, when an opportunity comes, it cannot be stopped.","Cheng Zhao gave a soft hum of acknowledgment.","Nanny Li looked at her in the mirror and felt that she wasn't being shy, but rather a bit depressed.","\"...Are you unhappy, Madam?\" Nanny Li asked.","\"He won't come to the Nonghua Courtyard often in the future, will he?\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li was stunned for a moment, then smiled. \"Is it because it hurt? Are you scared? I told you last time, you suffer a bit the first time, but it won't be like that afterward.\"","Cheng Zhao shook her head.","Facing the mirror, she fell into another long silence.","Regarding the consummation last night, she had initially been somewhat apprehensive, her heart inexplicably racing.","His large hand had scooped up her waist.","Cheng Zhao's heart sank.","Then she became very flustered. She wanted to turn her head to look at him, but Zhou Yuanshen lifted her hair, covered her exposed face with it, and pressed her head down onto the pillow.","The oil lamp inside the bed curtains was dim. With her vision blocked by her own black hair and her head pressed into the pillow, all she could see was pitch black.","The sense of humiliation in that moment cut into her heart like a knife.","She only remembered his hands.","The hand holding her waist, the hand pressing down on her head—they were clearly large and scorching hot, yet they felt colder and more indifferent than ice.","The joy Cheng Zhao had felt from receiving her imperial mandate and hosting the banquet at the Shou'an Courtyard was instantly wiped away.","The path of wealth and honor that came with the mandate was unexpectedly so difficult to walk. If she wasn't suffering here, she was being humiliated there.","Yet, Cheng Zhao did not cry.","That little bit of uneasy shyness in her heart was shattered to pieces by this \"consummation.\"","After finishing her washing, Cheng Zhao went to the Jiangyun Courtyard to pay her respects to her mother-in-law.","The Second Madam was very happy.","The virginity cloth had been sent over beforehand.","Dismissing all the servants, the Second Madam smiled and said to Cheng Zhao, \"From now on, your status is perfectly clear.\"","The Lord Duke had publicly punished Mu Jiang, spent the night in the Nonghua Courtyard, and consummated the marriage with Cheng Zhao. This was an acknowledgment of Cheng Zhao's status as his \"official wife.\"","Without these rituals, a wife wouldn't be like a wife, a concubine wouldn't be like a concubine, and the inner chambers would be a mess. That was why the scandalous farce at the Shou'an Courtyard had occurred.","Every man hoped for peace in his inner chambers.","Seeing that Zhou Yuanshen had accepted Cheng Zhao, the Second Madam also felt a weight lift from her mind.","From now on, everyone could live their days in peace.","\"If you are lucky, you might even give birth to the legitimate eldest son,\" the Second Madam added with a smile.","At that point, everyone would truly \"return to their rightful places,\" and Mu Jiang wouldn't be able to stir up any trouble.","Cheng Zhao looked at the Second Madam and couldn't help but smile.","The Second Madam asked, \"What are you smiling so foolishly about?\"","Cheng Zhao replied, \"Because Mother said I am 'lucky,' rather than telling me to 'try hard and win glory'.\"","The Second Madam said, \"...You girls from noble and scholarly families just love to nitpick words. You mustn't do this in the future; I really hate it.\"","She often spoke her mind freely and was picked on by her eldest sister-in-law because of it; then, when she complained, her mother-in-law would use the opportunity to assert her authority.","The Dowager Madame even said that she hoped she could rid herself of the roughness of a general's daughter and properly behave like a highborn madam—that she was cultivating her.","If she resisted, she was considered ungrateful and unable to appreciate good intentions.","In reality, they just disdained her.","Now Cheng Zhao was also nitpicking her words, but... it didn't seem to annoy her.","\"My mother-in-law and eldest sister-in-law really weren't educating or cultivating me; they were simply mocking me with pure malice,\" the Second Madam suddenly realized in a moment of clarity.","With the contrast of Cheng Zhao's \"nitpicking,\" the uncomfortable feeling the Second Madam had never been able to clearly articulate finally became clear.","Nitpicking words also carried an attitude; there was a clear boundary between goodwill and malice.","\"Yes, I will listen to Mother from now on,\" Cheng Zhao said sincerely.","The Second Madam breathed a sigh of relief.","She had breakfast together with Cheng Zhao.","The Second Madam was very optimistic.","This was because she underestimated Mu Jiang, and because she did not know that the Dowager Madame wanted Zhou Yuanshen to carry on the lineage for two branches of the family.","The reason the Dowager Madame didn't let the Second Master inherit the title, but chose Zhou Yuanshen instead, was because she had intended from the very beginning for Zhou Yuanshen to leave descendants for both branches.","—The Second Master could not do this. If he were to carry on both lineages, it would mean choosing the Eldest Madam. That would be truly unseemly, and the Eldest Madam might not even be able to bear children anymore.","The Second Madam might never be able to hope to live in the Chengming Hall in her entire life.","Of course, Cheng Zhao had just as little hope; she was even worse off than the Second Madam.","\"Mother, how did you marry into the Zhou family back then?\" Cheng Zhao suddenly asked.","The Second Madam said, \"Your father-in-law served under my father, and he never won against me in a spear duel. Later, he finally won once and told me to marry him. I kept my promise and accepted my defeat in the bet.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","No wonder the Dowager Madame doesn't like you; it turns out you weren't chosen by the Dowager Madame herself either.","As mother-in-law and daughter-in-law, we can truly be called \"fellow sufferers pitying each other.\""]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: Just let Zhou Yuanshen go","paragraphs":["The news of Mu Jiang being beaten and punished by kneeling spread throughout the Chen Duke's estate; the fact that the Duke stayed the night at Nonghua Courtyard also got out.","The servants began to gossip again.","\"The Third Young Madam has received her imperial mandate, she is now the 'Duchess'.\"","\"She even dealt with the Secondary Wife, and even the Old Madam couldn't do anything about her.\"","\"The Duke is clearly showing his support for her. It's hard to say who will be the true master of the inner chambers from now on.\"","The managing older female servants delivered high-quality silver charcoal for the winter to Cheng Zhao, their attitudes respectful.","The quality of the silver charcoal was excellent, without a single defective piece.","Cheng Zhao accepted her goodwill and rewarded her with a silver ingot.","As soon as the managing servant left, she praised Cheng Zhao, \"She acts with magnanimity, is gentle and knows etiquette; she is truly a well-bred lady from a prominent family.\"","The tone of the conversations changed with the situation, as everyone knew how to steer according to the wind.","Cheng Zhao decided to forget the humiliation behind the bed curtains that night and only remember the benefits she gained from it.","In the words of Nanny Li, after that night, Cheng Zhao had boarded the ship.","Her status as a titled lady, because of that night with Zhou Yuanshen, had become a reality, and she could now fight for her honor.","Two days later, it was heard that the Duke bought Mu Jiang a luxurious screen and stayed in her Lijing Courtyard for three consecutive nights.","With this ebb and flow, Mu Jiang actually rose up again.","The Second Madam was extremely furious.","She complained to the Second Master, \"At Madam Cheng's banquet that day, Mu Jiang went in dressed radiantly and luxuriously. After saying only two sentences, she used hidden weapons to hurt someone.","Mother dislikes women practicing martial arts the most, yet she hired someone specifically to teach Mu Jiang how to use hidden weapons for self-defense. Her openly hurting people is also indulged by Mother.","I really can't stand it, but your son is useless and has indulged in her gentle embrace again. Our daughter-in-law is clearly much prettier than her!\"","The Second Master listened, nodding in agreement.","The Second Madam was puzzled again, \"Where did our daughter-in-law lose? She looks like a heavenly fairy.\"","The Second Master didn't reply; he couldn't very well discuss with his wife whether their daughter-in-law was beautiful.","After the Second Madam scolded for a long time, the Second Master finally said, \"Perhaps your son just doesn't like girls from scholarly families. He takes after his roots in this regard.\"","The Second Madam: \"...\"","She sent people to inquire about where exactly Zhou Yuanshen usually rested.","The managing servant said, \"The Duke doesn't need people to serve him; sometimes he rests in the outer study, sometimes in Chenhui Courtyard. It's uncertain.\"","Chenhui Courtyard was the old Duke's inner study, located between the main courtyard, Chengming Hall, and Lijing Courtyard, separated by a few other courtyards.","It was closer to the First Branch because that was the center of power in the Duke's estate, making it convenient to meet with the managers; it was very far from the Second Branch.","Hearing this, the Second Madam felt particularly uncomfortable.","\"My son is about to become the First Branch's son,\" the Second Madam said.","The Second Master: \"...\"","Cheng Zhao had heard about the \"dual-inheritance\" matter, and so had the Second Master, but they kept it from the Second Madam.","The Old Madam wasn't afraid of the Second Madam making a fuss. Not telling her was purely because she felt these matters had nothing to do with \"irrelevant personnel\" like her.","The marriages of the clan's descendants were decided by the lady of the house; the Second Madam couldn't interfere.","If he often lived in Chenhui Courtyard, Zhou Yuanshen's true wives and concubines might be Huan Qingtang and Mu Jiang; Cheng Zhao, like the Second Madam, was \"marginalized\" by the Old Madam, having the title but no real power.","\"The children are all grown up, do you want to move out?\" the Second Master asked his wife again.","They had married in the northern borderlands. At that time, the court situation was a mess, and the Zhou family was hiding from disaster, as was the Second Madam's maiden family, Madam Fan.","Zhou Yuanshen was also born in the borderlands.","At that time, their family of three lived in the Fan family's courtyard, which was the Second Madam's maiden home. The conditions at the border were harsh, so they didn't care much about these formalities; having a place to live was good enough.","After returning to the capital, the Second Master often asked the Second Madam if she wanted to split the family and move out.","The Old Madam did not agree to split the family.","She said that as long as she was alive, splitting the family was impossible. If they insisted on doing so, they could, but they would have to buy their own house, receive no family property, and only collect a small monthly allowance.","Only after the Old Madam died could the property be divided. But if they left now, voluntarily giving up the property, they would have nothing in the future.","The Second Madam might not mind, but she had three sons.","Growing up in the Duke's estate gave the children more confidence, and the teachers at the Zhou clan school were more knowledgeable. She also needed to fight for the property, otherwise, her sons would have to \"start from scratch\" in the future.","Why should she give up what the Second Master deserved?","As for the Second Master, without a noble title, he had no noble estate, and a military officer's meager salary was not even enough to cover one banquet at the Duke's estate.","Compromising with reality, they had to endure it. The Second Madam also lacked the socializing skills of noble ladies and suffered a lot of grievances.","Now that Zhou Yuanshen had inherited the title, she didn't have to worry about the children. The Second Master asked her again if they should just move out and live a quiet life as a couple from then on.","They might as well leave Zhou Yuanshen to the Old Madam and the First Branch, as they couldn't win against them anyway.","As for the family property, the First Branch had no children or grandchildren, and Zhou Yuanshen would not mistreat his two biological younger brothers.","\"...My son is now the Duke. I've endured all these years, and good days are right before my eyes. You want me to move out at a time like this?\" the Second Madam refused.","The Second Master: \"...\"","What good days were there?","Days of suffering even more grievances were fast approaching.","The Second Master sighed. He could not disobey his mother, as that would be unfilial; yet he couldn't bear to see his wife suffer.","Being granted a title required not only ability but also luck. The Second Master was born many years too late, and there was no longer such an opportunity for him.","He said no more.","In October, the capital city saw its first snow, falling thick and fast.","Cheng Zhao and her maidservants gathered around the stove, roasting chestnuts to eat.","Zhou Yuanshen came to Nonghua Courtyard again.","He wore a black cloak with a fur collar. As he walked into the courtyard, he added a stroke of dark ink to the snow-white world.","It was only mid-afternoon.","Cheng Zhao was wearing a half-new, light-colored short jacket and a white-collared skirt, her hair casually tied into a low bun. She dressed simply and wore no makeup.","She rarely met outsiders looking so \"careless,\" and felt quite uncomfortable.","Cheng Zhao greeted him, served him by taking off his outer cloak, and ordered the maids to bring hot water for him to wash his hands.","After bustling about, she invited him to drink tea in the eastern side room where she lived.","\"The day after tomorrow is Grand Princess Fukang's birthday. You will accompany me to congratulate her,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao agreed.","She added, \"I know Grand Princess Fukang. Her eldest son often comes to the Cheng family to ask for academic advice; when my grandmother was alive, Grand Princess Fukang also came to the New Year's spring banquet.\"","\"That is very good,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","He didn't speak much.","Cheng Zhao didn't know what to talk about with him, so she asked toward the door, \"What time is it?\"","The maid at the door replied, \"It is exactly the hour of Shen.\"","It was time to prepare dinner.","As Cheng Zhao was thinking, Nanny Li came in. After bowing to Zhou Yuanshen, Nanny Li smiled and asked, \"Duke, will you stay at Nonghua Courtyard for dinner?\"","This question was actually asking: Will you rest here tonight?","If he was resting here, they would need to make the bed again and prepare hot water.","\"That is fine,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Nanny Li went out.","Cheng Zhao turned her head to look at the snow scenery outside the window, suppressing the fleeting emotion of anger in her heart. Only when her expression was calm did she turn her face back.","Zhou Yuanshen was looking at her."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: Couple's Chess Game","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao's fingers tightened slightly.","Her face showed no expression, but her tone was cheerful: \"Duke, dinner is still being prepared. Would you like to play chess?\"","\"Alright.\"","Cheng Zhao called Su Yue to take out the chessboard. She played the white pieces and played against Zhou Yuanshen.","She was good at chess, and Zhou Yuanshen was not bad either. Until Nanny Li said dinner was ready, they still hadn't decided the winner.","\"How about we eat first?\" Cheng Zhao suggested.","Zhou Yuanshen stood up.","He looked back at the chessboard, as if he had a sudden inspiration, or as if he had deliberately controlled the situation to this point, and casually placed a piece.","He won.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","He looked at Cheng Zhao: \"Your layout is very steady.\"","Cheng Zhao smiled: \"It's the Duke who is modest.\"","After dinner, the snow outside fell heavier, and the underfloor heating in the bedroom was burning very warmly.","Cheng Zhao went to wash up first.","She let down her hair, put on a brand-new silver-red small jacket, wore a plain white inner shirt and trousers, and sat on the kang near the window.","The chessboard was moved over from the east room.","Cheng Zhao was repeatedly studying the endgame just now, trying to figure out which step she started to lose from.","She was quite confident in her chess skills. Where exactly did he deliberately stalemate and not win against her, only waiting to give her the fatal blow at the end?","She had a good memory and still remembered the last few moves of Zhou Yuanshen, so she retreated five steps.","When it was the third to last step, Zhou Yuanshen came in.","He had washed up and changed into inner clothes and trousers, which were very thin. He leaned forward slightly, and heat radiated from his collar.","He helped make a move.","\"...So that's how it is.\" Cheng Zhao was enlightened, \"This chess game is very interesting. I will study it slowly later.\"","Zhou Yuanshen didn't say anything.","Inside the bed curtain, he told Cheng Zhao to rest inside, because he was going to put a long sword on the footstool.","\"Don't be afraid, it's just in case.\" His tone was distant.","Cheng Zhao: \"I'm not afraid. When I was a girl, I often hung a sword at the head of my bed to ward off evil.\"","She also had a sword.","Zhou Yuanshen covered the horn lantern, leaving only a corner that emitted a faint light.","Cheng Zhao lay on the inside.","When a pair of large hands reached over and picked her up by the waist, her body instantly tensed.","Her breathing was tight, and sweat seemed to slide down from her temples but didn't fall. The underfloor heating was burning too warmly tonight, and it was too hot inside the bed curtain.","The man's broad palm reached over from under her armpit. His arm was very long and touched her face. His fingers were like swimming snakes, gently stroking her lips.","Cheng Zhao was extremely restless. When a drop of sweat finally fell from her forehead, she forcefully bit the finger he placed on her lips.","She lay softly on the pillow, and the man behind her didn't say a word, nor did he make a sound.","He massaged her left leg for her.","Just now, her leg had been curled up for too long and it was too strenuous. When she couldn't help but put it down, her knee was lifted by him, and then she got a cramp.","The moment she got the cramp, she gasped in pain and tightly contracted her waist and abdomen.","Fortunately, he also stopped at that moment.","Cheng Zhao lay on the pillow and fell asleep just like that. Hazy, a warm towel wiped her, and someone dressed her.","She woke up but didn't dare to open her eyes. She continued to pretend to sleep, but soon fell asleep for real.","When she woke up the next day, there was no one in the bed as usual.","The thigh that had cramped in the night still hurt in the morning. Cheng Zhao frowned frequently, and wrinkles were about to form between her eyebrows.","She asked Qiu Bai to loosen her muscles.","\"You have to pick up the horse stance again. If your legs are not strong enough, it's easy to get cramps,\" Qiu Bai said.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Who would have thought that effort had to be put in this area?","When she got married, Nanny Li showed her picture books and explained them to her in detail.","According to the words of Nanny Li and her mother, when the couple had been together for a long time in the future, they would have other ways to keep it fresh and interesting.","Zhou Yuanshen, however...","Cheng Zhao thought of him and frowned again.","After Zhou Yuanshen left that day, he didn't return to Nonghua Courtyard again.","Cheng Zhao received an invitation.","Grand Princess Fukang's birthday banquet invited the three titled madams of the Chen Duke's Mansion.","This was her first time attending a banquet as a daughter-in-law and a titled madam of the imperial court. Cheng Zhao took it very seriously and asked Nanny Li to comb her hair.","\"Wear gold jewelry,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Grand Princess Fukang likes gold jewelry the most and doesn't like gems and pearls.\"","Nanny Li pondered: \"Will it be too old-fashioned?\"","\"Take out the set of gold jewelry that my eldest sister sent back when I got married. It was made by Master Wan. Grand Princess Fukang also likes Master Wan very much,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li: \"Then the princess should also have many such jewelry. What if it clashes with the princess's, will it make her unhappy?\"","\"Then we'll have to take a gamble on luck,\" Cheng Zhao said.","If the status is high and solid, naturally everything should be mainly safe; but it's Cheng Zhao's first time attending a banquet. If she doesn't stand out, she will always be suppressed.","Attending a banquet is socializing.","Nanny Li didn't continue to persuade.","Her fifth miss had always dared to take risks and never feared wind and waves. In the past, when she followed the master in office, she dared to take her maid to play on a sea ship and only came back a month later, scaring the adults and madam half to death.","Nanny Li dressed Cheng Zhao according to her request.","Because she was going to celebrate a birthday, Cheng Zhao wore a crimson kesi long jacket with auspicious cloud patterns embroidered on the sleeves, the patterns complex and exquisite; outside, she wore a silver satin cloak with a white fox fur collar, the color elegant.","She wore a gold buyao on her head, and the gold earrings in her ears had a small lotus flower pendant.","The golden light was brilliant and very moving.","The confidants were used to seeing her, but they were still dazzled and praised her beauty.","\"It's this gold jewelry that's beautiful,\" Cheng Zhao said.","It was cold, so Cheng Zhao took a small oil carriage to the front gate of the Duke's Mansion and went out together with the Old Madam and Eldest Madam Song.","She got down from the small oil carriage, and just then Zhou Yuanshen also walked to the covered corridor.","The maid Su Yue accompanied Cheng Zhao out and supported Cheng Zhao's hand.","The weather after the snow was clear, the blue sky clear and cloudless; there was still residual snow in the corners of the walls, and the wind carried the coldness of winter. And the sunlight was excellent.","The golden sunlight fell on Cheng Zhao's gold jewelry. She turned her face slightly, the golden light overflowing, dyeing her eyes brightly.","Perhaps more dazzling than her gold jewelry was that bright face.","Su Yue felt that her madam was extremely beautiful today, but the Duke clearly saw her, didn't look twice, turned around, stepped over the high threshold, and went out.","Then the Old Madam and Eldest Madam also came out.","Eldest Madam Song looked at Cheng Zhao and smiled gently: \"This dress is really grand.\"","The Old Madam smiled: \"It is indeed beautiful.\"","They were praising Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao was born into a prominent family. Her aunts, sisters-in-law, etc., never argued or fought. When they were angry, they would make sarcastic remarks and trip people up.","She was used to hearing it, familiar with it, and habitually turned a deaf ear, pretending not to hear.","\"Thank you, Grandmother, Eldest Aunt.\" Cheng Zhao smiled sweetly, holding the well-behaved expression of a junior dealing with an elder.","The three people each got into the carriage.","Zhou Yuanshen rode a horse and walked at the very front.","The group soon arrived at the Grand Princess Fukang's mansion.","Hearing that the Old Madam of the Zhou family was coming, the princess braved the cold after the snow, held a small hand warmer in her hand, and personally waited at the gate.","\"Is this the new Duke's Madam of your mansion?\" The Grand Princess smiled and looked at Cheng Zhao. \"She really is a beauty.\"","When Grand Princess Fukang went to the Cheng family as a guest, Cheng Zhao was still a child, hadn't grown up, and didn't have the chance to perform in front of the distinguished guest. She didn't remember much.","They exchanged a few polite words with each other before entering the door.","Meanwhile, Eldest Madam Song's gaze fell upon the princess's dangling hairpin, and she stared at it for a long while."]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: Countering Every Move","paragraphs":["The birthday banquet at the Princess's estate invited distinguished guests from noble and meritorious families, seated in two separate rows.","The Zhou family's seats were at the very front, close to the Princess. Cheng Zhao sat just below Eldest Madam Song; directly opposite them was the Duke of Chen, Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen barely glanced at Cheng Zhao; he was engaged in constant conversation with the Prince Consort beside him.","The Prince Consort was very amiable. Zhou Yuanshen did not show the slightest smile, but he wasn't overly stern either, showing a good deal of respect toward the Prince Consort.","The banquet featured singing and dancing, creating a lively and bustling atmosphere.","Halfway through, the Princess left her seat to change clothes and instructed the guests that they were free to admire the plum blossoms in the estate's back garden.","\"Are the wintersweet blossoms already blooming at this time of year? They haven't bloomed at our estate yet,\" someone remarked.","\"The Princess's estate has skilled gardeners, and since it is the Princess's birthday, how could there not be early-blooming wintersweets?\"","Cheng Zhao had been sitting for quite a while, and the leg that had cramped the day before yesterday was aching a bit, so she also rose from her seat to stretch her legs.","Right next to the banquet hall was a small courtyard specifically designated for female guests to change and freshen up.","Eldest Madam Song went there as well.","Three or four other female guests also arrived at this resting courtyard.","For convenience, the Princess was also changing her clothes here.","The main room of the courtyard was warmed by the underfloor heating. A few women stood around chatting. Upon seeing Cheng Zhao, they grew curious about her and pulled her into their conversation.","When the Princess emerged, everyone curtsied in greeting. Following behind the Princess was the Zhou family's Eldest Madam Song.","\"...This buyao hairpin of yours, Princess, looks as though it was crafted by the same hands as the golden hairpin worn by our Duke's wife,\" Eldest Madam Song said with a smile.","Everyone looked over.","\"This kind of gold jewelry looks far more dignified and elegant when worn by you, Princess,\" the Eldest Madam smiled again. \"I have never seen anyone who suits this jewelry better than the Princess.\"","By elevating the Princess, the implication was clear: only you are worthy of wearing such gold jewelry; anyone else imitating you is stealing your thunder and showing disrespect.","Moreover, the fact that this person was young and beautiful made the gold jewelry crafted by a famous artisan seem common, as if anyone could wear it.","What was so rare about gold jewelry?","Compared to precious gemstones, it was truly too ordinary. What made it valuable was the craftsmanship of a renowned master.","Grand Princess Fukang looked at Cheng Zhao.","The other ladies did the same.","Some sensed that something was amiss and felt a bit uneasy, wishing to leave the area to avoid getting caught up in the drama.","Of the people present today, the majority could afford to offend neither the Princess nor the Zhou family.","Without waiting for the Princess to say anything, Cheng Zhao smiled and chimed in: \"Yes, the Princess's buyao is truly beautiful. Its luster is exquisite, just like the bright moon.","The brighter and more dazzling the moon shines, the more the stars can borrow a bit of its radiance to illuminate the night sky. If it weren't for the Princess's favor, Master Wan would not have been able to create such fine jewelry, and we wouldn't have been able to benefit from his work.","Master Wan often tells people that if not for the Princess's appreciation, his talent would have been a pearl covered in dust, and back then, he and his wife and children would have starved to death.\"","Grand Princess Fukang burst into a chuckle.","She said to Cheng Zhao, \"This clever mouth of yours, has it been smeared with honey?\"","\"It's the truth!\" Cheng Zhao said earnestly. \"Who doesn't know of the Princess's keen eye for talent regarding Master Wan back then?\"","Cheng Zhao then recounted to everyone the story of how the renowned jewelry artisan, Master Wan, first met the Princess in his early years.","Many people knew this past event, but Cheng Zhao knew it in greater detail. Furthermore, by telling it again in front of everyone, she was essentially praising the Princess once more.","Why would Grand Princess Fukang care about some piece of jewelry?","This grace of recognizing talent and elevating a globally renowned goldsmith was her true glory.","The smile on the Princess's face was radiant as she listened to Cheng Zhao finish her story with a smile.","That kind of delight was evident to anyone who looked.","\"...Look at this eloquence, she has simply inherited the true teachings of Chancellor Cheng,\" Grand Princess Fukang said with a smile.","She casually took off her own dangling hairpin, not caring whether it messed up her hair, and pinned it into Cheng Zhao's hair at the temples. \"This is from a set of jewelry that Master Wan specially crafted for my birthday. This hairpin is my absolute favorite, and your eldest aunt also praised its beauty. It looks even more beautiful on a young person, and it brings me joy just looking at it.\"","Cheng Zhao curtsied gracefully and generously, \"Thank you, Your Highness. A gift from the Princess can never be declined. I will certainly save it for my future daughter's dowry.\"","Everyone burst into laughter.","The Princess was even more delighted.","Eldest Madam Song, who was standing to the side, maintained a smile the entire time. However, when people looked at her, they all felt her smile was too forced.","Her slight stiffness could not be concealed.","Grand Princess Fukang did not look at her again. She instructed a maid to fetch her another gold hairpin and redo her hair.","She then called out to Cheng Zhao, \"Come here. I enjoy listening to you speak; come sit beside me.\"","Cheng Zhao accompanied her to the side room.","Grand Princess Fukang chatted with her extensively, and Cheng Zhao took the opportunity to praise her son: \"The Heir Apparent often consults my grandfather on academic matters. My grandfather praises his handwriting.\"","\"Is that so?\" The Princess was pleasantly surprised.","The Heir Apparent was not cut out for scholarly pursuits and had made quite a few jokes of himself in academic circles because of his superficial knowledge, often misquoting classical allusions and confusing facts.","\"Yes, grandfather said the Heir Apparent's calligraphy is elegant and free-flowing, showing he is a man of a free and unconstrained nature. He doesn't care much for worldly fame; he is a rare, transcendent figure,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Princess was even more overjoyed.","Of course, she knew Cheng Zhao was flattering her. But as the Emperor's only biological sister, she held a high position and was surrounded by flattery every day.","She had grown tired and annoyed of hearing the same complimentary words.","Yet Cheng Zhao's two compliments today perfectly suited her temperament without being overly exaggerated; they sounded fresh, and it had been a long time since anyone had spoken so pleasingly to her ears.","She patted Cheng Zhao's hand and asked with a smile, \"It's hard being a new daughter-in-law, isn't it?\"","How could the Princess not hear the obvious fault-finding in Eldest Madam Song's words earlier?","Even if Cheng Zhao hadn't reacted so astutely, the Princess wouldn't have made things difficult for her; after all, she was Chancellor Cheng's granddaughter.","But Cheng Zhao's performance not only made the Princess look at her with new respect, but also fostered a sense of affection. She felt that Cheng Zhao was very considerate and understood her well.","Therefore, her words became much more intimate.","Cheng Zhao slightly lowered her eyelids and seemed to sigh softly.","She did not complain, but smiled and said, \"A new daughter-in-law is an outsider. To go from an outsider to a family member always takes a bit of time and patience. I am not in a hurry, Your Highness.\"","The Princess gladly patted her hand: \"So perceptive.\"","She did not complain about her husband's family, nor did she deny her difficulties.","The Princess then thought that when her son married in the future, they might also seek a bride from the Cheng family.","Beautiful, well-educated, with a kind and open-minded disposition.","When the Princess returned to the banquet hall, she was holding Cheng Zhao's hand.","And on Cheng Zhao's head, she wore the dangling hairpin the Princess had just given her.","Everyone's eyes fell on her, including the Dowager Madame of the Zhou family.","The Eldest Madam had already returned to her seat, looking gloomy; the Dowager Madame looked at her, wanting to ask what had happened, but the Eldest Madam was immersed in her own emotions and did not react.","The Dowager Madame had no choice but to smile.","\"How did Your Highness's hairpin end up with her? How can a child like her bear such a precious gift?\" the Dowager Madame said with a smile.","Opposite them, Zhou Yuanshen also raised his eyes and looked over.","The Princess smiled: \"A hairpin is merely a piece of jewelry; it only has value when worn on the head of someone beautiful.\"","Everyone praised her words.","Every madam and young lady from the noble families in attendance committed Cheng Zhao to memory.","She was a prominent noblewoman from an illustrious family, as well as an honored guest of the Grand Princess.","The Dowager Madame looked amiable, smiling with a sense of shared pride.","On the journey back, Zhou Yuanshen did not ride his horse. Instead, he boarded Cheng Zhao's carriage, while her maid, Suyue, moved to the trailing carriage.","He had something to ask Cheng Zhao."]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: Let Down Hair","paragraphs":["\"Why did the princess give you the hair accessory?\"","Zhou Yuanshen's expression was cold, asking straightforwardly.","Cheng Zhao told him everything that had just happened, in detail.","After listening, Zhou Yuanshen remained expressionless.","He tilted his head slightly, wanting to look at her hair accessory. Cheng Zhao planned to take it off and give it to him, to spare him from staring at it like that.","Being stared at by him made her very uncomfortable.","She casually pulled it out.","But she accidentally touched her own hair bun, loosening the hairpin that held her hair in place, just as the carriage hit a bump.","Cheng Zhao's hair was thick and smooth.","It was very difficult to style it into a beautiful bun because her hair was too thick and smooth to secure easily.","It required Nanny Li's skillful hands.","Cheng Zhao was caught off guard. By pulling the hair accessory out like that, half of her hair bun fell apart, and her black hair cascaded over her shoulders.","Her hand froze.","Faced with such a sudden turn of events, she didn't know how to react for a moment. Since there was nothing she could do and it was beyond saving, she didn't react at all.","Therefore, in Zhou Yuanshen's eyes, she looked stunned.","He supported her head and took out the hairpin from the remaining half of the bun, causing all her hair to fall down.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"You can tie a bun.\"","There were several times when his mother went to her maternal grandfather's house, wearing her hair ornaments properly. But when she was preparing to spar with her brother and maternal grandmother, she would neatly remove the hair ornaments and tie her hair into a low bun.","It was very easy, a casual thing to do, done in a few strokes, fixed with a single hairpin.","\"...How do I tie it?\" Cheng Zhao asked him in return. \"Do you know how?\"","Zhou Yuanshen: \"...\"","He just assumed that any woman with hands would know how.","\"I can't be seen by anyone now,\" Cheng Zhao sighed. \"Having my hair down in the carriage and walking back to the Nonghua Courtyard from the gate is almost the same as not wearing clothes.\"","Zhou Yuanshen remained silent.","Cheng Zhao handed him the hair accessory: \"Does the Duke still want to look at it?\"","Zhou Yuanshen took it, looked at it carefully for a few glances, and returned it to her.","Cheng Zhao was very depressed and stopped talking; Zhou Yuanshen just thought about something and didn't speak again either. The carriage returned to the Duke Chen's Mansion.","He said to Cheng Zhao: \"Don't move.\"","Cheng Zhao didn't know why, but she really couldn't move either.","Riding in a carriage with the Duke, her hair disheveled, who knew what kind of gossip would spread once she got out of the carriage.","Zhou Yuanshen went to the Old Madam's carriage and said to her: \"Grandmother is tired today, don't get out of the carriage. Let the servants lower the threshold and drive straight in.\"","Without waiting for the Old Madam to react, he had already gone to give instructions.","The servants lowered the threshold and laid wooden boards at the same time, allowing the carriages to drive smoothly up the steps.","The three carriages drove directly into the Duke's Mansion.","The Old Madam was puzzled but didn't ask much; the Eldest Madam Madam Song was half dead with anger and didn't have the mood to worry too much.","Cheng Zhao benefited from this, as the carriage arrived directly at the gate of the Nonghua Courtyard.","Nanny Li and Qiubai came out to welcome her, and Cheng Zhao almost trotted into the courtyard, with no one else around.","Seeing her hair, Nanny Li and Qiubai were both stunned.","\"How, how did you get so messy?\" Nanny Li asked worriedly.","Qiubai: \"Who bullied you?\"","Cheng Zhao shook her head: \"No one.\"","After returning, washing her hands, and changing into a set of casual clothes, Cheng Zhao sat in front of the dressing table, allowing Nanny Li to put her hair up simply.","It's not hard for someone who knows how. Nanny Li indeed casually put her hair into a simple low bun.","Suyue rode in the servants' carriage and couldn't drive into the mansion, returning to the Nonghua Courtyard a little later.","Nanny Li and the others wanted to ask her about today's situation, so Cheng Zhao said: \"I'll go to the Jiangyun Courtyard and tell Mother about today's events, so she won't worry.\"","\"That makes sense, the Second Madam has probably been worrying all day,\" Nanny Li said.","As a new daughter-in-law going out to socialize for the first time, the Second Madam must be very concerned about the situation. And she couldn't go herself.","Sure enough, when Cheng Zhao entered the Jiangyun Courtyard, the Second Madam was instructing a maid to go see if Cheng Zhao had returned.","The Second Master had also returned home from the government office, changed into casual clothes, and was drinking tea; the Fifth Young Master Zhou Yuanqi came over to have dinner after finishing his studies.","Cheng Zhao told them everything that happened at Princess Fukang's mansion.","When the Second Madam heard that the Eldest Madam Madam Song publicly found fault with her, anger rose from her heart: \"It's one thing for her to bully me, but to bully a younger generation, it's simply clumsy. These scholarly families...\"","The Second Master coughed.","The Second Madam came to her senses: if she cursed scholarly families again, she would be cursing Cheng Zhao too.","\"...Her character is despicable, and she is short-sighted. You are just a niece-in-law, how do you get in her way? She is living perfectly well in the Chengming Hall!\" the Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao: \"Don't be angry, Mother. I didn't lose to her. Among the titled ladies, no news can be hidden. The Eldest Aunt's expression was extremely ugly at the time, and she couldn't recover no matter what. Others will inevitably discuss her. In a few days, this matter will spread, and she will make a fool of herself.\"","\"She deserves it!\" the Second Madam said.","She repeatedly praised Cheng Zhao for doing a good job.","Cheng Zhao was indeed very capable.","It's still better to read more books. A woman who has read books like the Eldest Madam Madam Song needs Cheng Zhao, who has the same background, to put her in her place.","The dinner was rich, and the Second Madam even served soup for Cheng Zhao, telling her to eat more.","\"You can't get full at banquets, eat more, no one will laugh at you,\" the Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao: \"It was too cold today, and I really didn't eat much at noon. Thank you for your consideration, Mother.\"","She unceremoniously dug in.","The Second Master and Zhou Yuanqi also had good appetites, and no one would show a strange look just because they ate a little more. Cheng Zhao ate very comfortably.","Eating well at the dining table, the Second Madam's mood improved a lot.","After the meal, they chatted about trivial matters again.","Although there was only one more person, Cheng Zhao, it seemed much livelier, with many topics.","When the Duke was mentioned, the Fifth Young Master Zhou Yuanqi suddenly said: \"The boor changed his deputy general. The dark, long-faced deputy general beside him was replaced by a dark, round-faced one.\"","Cheng Zhao was amused by the child's mature yet vivid description.","The Second Madam: \"The previous one was Deputy General Wu, who had been with him since he was seven or eight years old. He shouldn't have been replaced. Was he sent out on some errand?\"","The Second Master drank his tea in silence.","He had been replaced, and he had noticed it too.","He even asked Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen said he sent Deputy General Wu to his uncle to gain experience for a while.","How could one's right-hand man be sent out casually?","Wasn't it because, in the Shou'an Courtyard, he touched the Old Madam's \"favorite pet\"?","The Emperor said he would give Mu Jiang to Zhou Yuanshen as a concubine, and the whole mansion called her that, but Zhou Yuanshen called her \"Concubine Mu\" in front of the Old Madam.","He even made Mu Jiang kneel as punishment.","This was using Mu Jiang to challenge the Old Madam's authority.","How could the Old Madam's prestige be shaken by a grandson? Not to mention the fledgling Zhou Yuanshen, even the scheming Chancellor Cheng had to yield to her.","If Deputy General Wu didn't leave, he would die, so Zhou Yuanshen had to make a painful decision.","But the Second Master wouldn't bring these things to the inner courtyard, let alone tell the Second Madam.","The Second Madam wasn't interested, and she didn't quite understand it either. The Second Master didn't want to taint the inner courtyard either.","These storms could just stay in the outer courtyard, just like the previous twenty-odd years.","However, the eight-year-old Zhou Yuanqi understood it and deliberately said it out loud.","He seemed to be saying it for Cheng Zhao to hear.","The Second Master sometimes thought that bloodlines were still very terrifying.","The brothers Zhou Yuanshen and Zhou Yuanqi were simply standard Zhou bloodlines: cold, mean, and sharp-eyed enough to see through everything.","More like the Old Madam.","The Second Master glanced at Cheng Zhao again.","Cheng Zhao looked thoughtful for a moment, then lowered her lashes and took a sip of her tea. She understood."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: Quietly Eclipsed","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao ate her fill at Jiangyun Courtyard.","It had been a long time since she had eaten so heartily.","She had a good appetite when she was young. When she turned twelve, her mother told her that her face was getting round, which lacked the refined elegance of a young lady from a noble family, and assigned someone to keep an eye on her during meals.","She was not allowed to chew loudly or eat her fill.","She had to take small bites, eat slowly, and stop when she was 70% full. She was to avoid strong flavors, and only take a small taste of dishes with heavy oil and dark soy sauce.","Now, in Nonghua Courtyard, Nanny Li would occasionally advise her to eat less to avoid \"indigestion,\" subtly reminding her not to get fat.","Currently, thinness was considered the ideal figure, and none of the noble ladies were fat.","The Second Madam practiced the spear year-round, so she wasn't afraid to eat more. Cheng Zhao hadn't felt the satisfaction of a full stomach for a long time.","Satisfied at the time, she suffered from indigestion that night, and her stomach burned terribly.","\"I want to take a walk in the courtyard,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li brought her a thick coat and warned her, \"Don't go out of the courtyard. If the old women on night patrol see you, they'll surely gossip.\"","\"I won't go far, just walk around the courtyard twice,\" Cheng Zhao replied.","Nanny Li asked Qiubai to accompany her, carrying a horn lantern.","Qiubai agreed.","The master and servant strolled slowly, chatting about trivial matters.","A dark figure flashed past.","Cheng Zhao glanced back at Qiubai.","Qiubai shook her head at her and whispered, \"Just a passerby, it's fine.\"","It was the same path as the slow-moving snake last time; it was someone belonging to the Duke.","Cheng Zhao said nothing more, smiling bitterly. \"This Duke Chen's mansion is so strange.\"","She had already received the title of a noble lady of Duke Chen's mansion and consummated her marriage with Zhou Yuanshen; she no longer had the chance to \"jump ship.\"","Cheng Zhao could only comfort herself that although the Duke's mansion was strange, at least her parents-in-law were good people, and her brother-in-law was cute and clever.","After strolling twice around the courtyard, Cheng Zhao went back to sleep. It was quite cold outside, but once she returned to the warm inner bedroom, she felt sleepy and finally slept soundly.","The next day, the maid serving the Old Madam came early to Nonghua Courtyard and said to Cheng Zhao, \"The Old Madam invites you for breakfast.\"","Cheng Zhao smiled and replied, \"Thank you for the trouble, Sister.\"","She told Suyue to tip her.","After the maid left, Cheng Zhao washed and changed her clothes. The maid serving the Second Madam also came and told her, \"The Old Madam has invited you and our Madam for breakfast.\"","She added, \"The Madam asks you to go to Jiangyun Courtyard and ride in her small oil carriage; you two can squeeze in.\"","The small oil carriage was a green-curtained carriage with oiled sides, drawn by a single horse or mule, usually used for traveling within the inner courtyards of noble families.","Duke Chen's mansion occupied an entire street, and the back garden couldn't be fully explored in an hour. Nonghua Courtyard and Jiangyun Courtyard were located at the east and west ends of the mansion, respectively, far from the Old Madam's Shou'an Courtyard. Whether it was cold or hot, they had to take a carriage to get there.","Cheng Zhao dressed neatly and went to Jiangyun Courtyard.","The Second Madam was also ready. The small oil carriage was parked at the door, with a sturdy old woman holding the horse, waiting.","\"...Why did she suddenly call us over for a meal?\" Cheng Zhao asked the Second Madam.","The Second Madam replied, \"She only calls me to pay my respects on the first and fifteenth of the month; usually, it's the eldest daughter-in-law and granddaughter-in-law who serve her. Today is the tenth, not a day for paying respects. Since she called us, she must have something to tell us. It might not be a bad thing.\"","If it were a bad thing, she would have called them in the mid-afternoon, not early in the morning.","Punishing daughters-in-law and granddaughters-in-law early in the morning was truly bad luck, and the old lady was very superstitious about it.","\"Does it have something to do with the banquet yesterday?\" Cheng Zhao asked again.","The Second Madam replied, \"Don't ask me; I can't guess the Old Madam's thoughts. She has never liked me.\"","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","When they arrived at Shou'an Courtyard, they saw Mu Jiang had already arrived and was feeding millet to the birds under the eaves.","Seeing Cheng Zhao and the Second Madam, a look of arrogance appeared on her face first; then, she reluctantly walked down the steps and curtsied to them.","The Second Madam ignored her. She had never considered her a concubine of the second branch, only treating her as someone belonging to the Old Madam; Cheng Zhao didn't mind either.","Entering the main room, they heard voices coming from the inner bedroom.","A maid went in to announce their arrival.","The Eldest Young Madam, Huan Qingtang, came out.","She was wearing a lilac brocade long jacket and had her hair combed into a round bun. Her face was lightly powdered, her eyebrows drawn, and she wore a thin layer of lip rouge, looking gentle and elegant.","She had never given birth, and since she was young, she exuded a strong youthful aura. The Second Madam felt she had more temperament and charm than Mu Jiang—though, of course, she couldn't compare to her own daughter-in-law.","\"Second Aunt, Sister-in-law, please sit for a moment; Grandmother will be ready soon,\" Huan Qingtang smiled.","The Second Madam immediately stopped finding her charming.","Huan Qingtang's attitude of treating herself as the master and the mother and daughter-in-law of the second branch as outsiders, even if she tried hard to hide it, still leaked out a bit.","Her words seemed to be welcoming them, but in reality, they were blocking them from the Old Madam's bedroom.","They were all daughters-in-law, all outsiders, yet they were divided into different classes; it was simply ridiculous.","\"Go about your business; we will sit by ourselves,\" the Second Madam said.","Huan Qingtang smiled slightly, turned, and went back inside.","After Mu Jiang finished feeding the birds, she also entered the main room. As if she couldn't see the Second Madam and her daughter-in-law, she turned and went into the inner bedroom as well.","The Second Madam whispered, \"Calling us over early in the morning just to watch their family be affectionate.\"","Cheng Zhao took the opportunity to squeeze the Second Madam's hand. \"We can be affectionate too.\"","The Second Madam couldn't help but laugh.","Cheng Zhao released her hand and smiled, \"Mother, don't mind them. When others put on a show for us, it's deliberately to make you angry. As long as you don't take it to heart, you win.\"","The Second Madam cared a lot about winning or losing. Cheng Zhao's words hit the nail on the head, and she took two deep breaths, indeed relaxing a lot.","When the Eldest Madam, Madam Song, helped the Old Madam out, Cheng Zhao and the Second Madam were full of smiles and respect, curtsying to the Old Madam.","A hint of surprise flashed in Madam Song's eyes.","Being left out in the cold for so long, the Second Madam, Madam Fan, didn't pull a long face, which surprised her a bit.","\"Calling you over, you don't blame this old woman for being meddlesome, do you?\" the Old Madam chuckled.","Cheng Zhao spoke up before her mother-in-law, smiling at the Old Madam, \"It is only right to pay respects every morning and evening. However, Mother said that Grandmother gets up early to worship Buddha and was afraid of disturbing you. Serving you is filial piety, and being considerate is also filial piety. Mother and this granddaughter-in-law are full of filial piety for you, but we were afraid you didn't know. Being called here this morning, we can finally show our filial piety, and there is only joy left.\"","The Second Madam thought: ...How good at flattering. Daughter-in-law, how much suffering did you endure in your maiden home to develop such a glib tongue?","If it were the Second Madam, even if she were made to memorize these words, she would be too ashamed to say them.","The Old Madam chuckled, \"The Cheng family girl indeed has a clever tongue. No wonder the Eldest Princess also likes you and gave you precious jewelry upon your first meeting.\"","\"The orioles under the eaves are the ones with clever tongues; why didn't the Eldest Princess reward them? The Eldest Princess was only showing you respect by favoring this granddaughter-in-law,\" Cheng Zhao replied.","The Old Madam's smile deepened. \"You child, you really have some insight. That's why they say, when choosing a daughter-in-law, you must choose one from a prestigious family; their perspective doesn't need to be taught.\"","Huan Qingtang also smiled along.","The Eldest Madam, Madam Song, smiled forcedly; Mu Jiang rolled her eyes and turned her gaze away.","The Second Madam thought: Belittling me again? Forget it, at least you praised my daughter-in-law.","Just standing there for a moment, the Second Madam felt exhausted, her head aching.","Fortunately, the Old Madam didn't continue to torment her, and ordered them to sit in the flower hall for the meal.","While the Old Madam ate, Huan Qingtang and Cheng Zhao stood by to serve; the Eldest Madam, Madam Song, and the Second Madam, Madam Fan, sat as companions; as for Mu Jiang, she sat boldly beside the Old Madam, enjoying the treatment of a \"younger sister-in-law.\"","Huan Qingtang seemed completely oblivious, and Cheng Zhao likewise pretended not to notice."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: Delegating Authority to Cheng Zhao","paragraphs":["Breakfast at Shou'an Courtyard was fraught with tension.","The Dowager Madame's veiled warnings and First Madam Madam Song's attempts to sow discord had secretly gone back and forth several times, yet Cheng Zhao's mother-in-law, the Second Madam, completely failed to pick up on them.","Cheng Zhao remembered her mother saying: \"You must know how to read between the lines, and even more importantly, how to play deaf. These two are essential skills in the inner chambers, comparable to a general's spear-wielding and archery; they are the true secrets to survival.\"","She held her mother's teachings as the golden rule.","Looking back at her mother-in-law, she didn't need to play deaf; she simply couldn't understand the hidden meanings. Yet, hadn't she lived perfectly well for over twenty years?","True, she might suffer some grievances, and many benefits didn't come her way.","But it didn't stop her from eating and sleeping.","With a broader mind, what other major things were there in life besides eating and sleeping? She was about the same age as First Madam Madam Song, yet she looked ten years younger than her.","What did gains and losses really matter?","For the first time, Cheng Zhao re-evaluated the words her mother had taught her in her heart.","Cheng Zhao also looked at Mu Jiang.","Although Mu Jiang feigned calmness, disdain and anger coexisted in her eyes, and she occasionally shot a glance at Cheng Zhao.","The breakfast finally concluded. After everyone rinsed their mouths and washed their hands, they sat down to drink tea.","Only then did the Dowager Madame state her purpose for summoning the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the second branch today: \"Cheng Shi is an imperial-mandated 'Duchess'.","Madam Song and I are both getting old, and in the future, Cheng Shi will need to manage the household. Let her take charge of a few things first, slowly get familiar with them, and then hand the household over to her.\"","First Madam Madam Song didn't seem to have received any advance notice. Upon hearing the Dowager Madame's words, surprise uncontrollably surfaced on her face.","Mu Jiang didn't know either.","She looked at the Dowager Madame in astonishment, parting her lips slightly as if wanting to say something, but saw the Dowager Madame looking at her, staring with a sharp gaze.","The words reached Mu Jiang's lips, but she didn't dare speak.","The Second Madam was both shocked and a little uneasy. She looked around, but ultimately said nothing.","Eldest Young Madame Huan Qingtang's attitude remained unchanged. After the Dowager Madame finished speaking, the room fell silent, and she was the first to chime in: \"Congratulations, younger sister-in-law.\"","Cheng Zhao stood up: \"This granddaughter-in-law is so overjoyed that my reaction is a bit slow.\"","The Dowager Madame chuckled: \"You're just a child, lacking shrewdness. Practice slowly, there's no rush. It's not like this old woman is going to die right away. I have time to teach you.\"","Pausing for a moment, the Dowager Madame's smile faded, as if deep in thought, \"I'll let you manage the main kitchen.\"","As soon as this was said, the entire room was stunned, everyone's surprise written plainly on their faces.","The main kitchen was the most lucrative place in the inner chambers, and also where the managing madam placed her trusted aides.","Telling Cheng Zhao to manage the main kitchen, what did this mean?","Did the Dowager Madame truly accept Cheng Zhao as the Duchess and want to cultivate her, or was she trying to trip her up and teach her a lesson?","That was the main kitchen, after all.","Would the Dowager Madame really use the main kitchen for Cheng Zhao to practice on?","Cheng Zhao bowed respectfully: \"Thank you for your profound love, Grandmother. This granddaughter-in-law is overwhelmed by the favor. If there are any shortcomings in the future, I beg Grandmother's tolerance.\"","She then turned to First Madam Madam Song, \"Eldest Aunt, this niece-in-law will certainly assist you well in managing the household. If there are any areas where I fall short, I hope Eldest Aunt will be more forgiving, and I will be endlessly grateful.\"","\"If there's anything you don't understand, just come and ask me,\" the First Madam smiled.","She couldn't really smile; it was a forced expression. It looked rather ferocious and a bit pathetic.","After First Madam Madam Song finished smiling, she couldn't help but say: \"You have a better fate than your eldest sister-in-law. She has been married for five years and still hasn't grasped the basics of managing a household.","Her maiden family is the Huan clan of Lujiang, and her father is the Chancellor of the Hanlin Academy. She has read more books than anyone. Sometimes, it just comes down to fate.\"","The Second Madam: \"...\"","She almost couldn't control her temper.","This wasn't the first time First Madam Madam Song had blatantly tried to sow discord.","Whenever things didn't go her way, she would use \"praise on the surface, criticize in secret\"; she was very familiar with this trick.","Having suppressed the Second Madam for a lifetime, she was now starting to suppress Cheng Zhao.","The Second Madam wanted to step forward and say a few words.","But she knew very well that she wasn't good with words. Words spoken couldn't be taken back, and she always ended up handing a weapon to First Madam Madam Song.","Now that her daughter-in-law had secured the job of managing the kitchen, First Madam Madam Song was probably coughing up blood in anger. Just thinking about it made the Second Madam feel great.","She needed to hide her weaknesses and not give First Madam Madam Song any leverage, lest she and Cheng Zhao end up at a disadvantage again.","She held back again and again, and truly managed to restrain herself.","As soon as First Madam Madam Song's voice faded, no one responded.","Huan Qingtang seemed not to have heard, and neither did Cheng Zhao. The Dowager Madame picked up her tea to drink, gently blowing on the floating leaves as if it were none of her business; Mu Jiang had a strange expression, but was just enjoying the show and didn't chime in.","At this moment, the lack of response was like a slap right back in First Madam Madam Song's own face.","Her complexion visibly turned pale and green.","\"So it can be done this way?\" The Second Madam seemed to have learned something.","Finally, she wasn't the one being deflated.","The room was so quiet you could hear a pin drop. The Dowager Madame finally set down her teacup.","As if nothing had happened, the Dowager Madame said in her usual tone: \"Starting tomorrow, Cheng Shi will also go to the Chengming Hall to handle affairs. You all should do a handover of duties tomorrow morning.\"","She added, \"You all have things to do, so you may disperse.\"","She stood up and, supported by Mu Jiang's hand, went to the small Buddhist hall.","Everyone stood up to see her off.","Watching her back disappear behind the curtain, Cheng Zhao said to the Second Madam: \"Mother, shall we go back?\"","The Second Madam agreed.","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law left Shou'an Courtyard first.","Sitting in the small carriage, the Second Madam felt as if in a dream: \"Are you really going to manage the main kitchen? This is like delivering a piece of fat meat right to your mouth.\"","She added, \"There must be some trap. This is not an easy job.\"","Cheng Zhao smiled: \"Wait until I take over the management tally and the account books of the main kitchen; then I will slowly investigate. Once I figure out the reason, I will explain it to you in detail, Mother.\"","\"You must tell me,\" the Second Madam said. She was dying of curiosity.","Cheng Zhao agreed.","The Second Madam couldn't help but feel delighted again: \"Did you see your Eldest Aunt's face? She has been married into the family for over twenty years, and the Dowager Madame has always favored her. This is the first time I've seen her get deflated.\"","Cheng Zhao smiled and said: \"Mother, I was so afraid you would start arguing with her and fall into her trap. Fortunately, you held back.\"","The Second Madam was a bit proud: \"I thought about it. At the time, I wondered if I should scold her back for you. But then I realized it might do more harm than good, so I kept quiet.\"","\"It wouldn't have done more harm than good. Helping is helping. Only those who lack ability themselves blame their helpers for causing trouble,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"I fully understand your heart in wanting to protect me, Mother.\"","The Second Madam turned to look at her: \"No wonder the Dowager Madame praised you; you really have a sharp tongue.\"","For daughters of scholarly families, their mouths are the spears in their hands.","They can just as easily kill without leaving a trace.","The Second Madam suddenly understood why she had suffered grievances in front of her mother-in-law and sisters-in-law for so many years: because they used different weapons.","And on the \"battlefield of the inner chambers,\" their weapons were the most effective.","Since Cheng Zhao married into the family over two months ago, it was as if a lightbulb had gone off for the Second Madam, making her understand truths she hadn't grasped in the previous decades.","\"...In short, be careful,\" the Second Madam said. \"From now on, you'll have to forge your own path. When it comes to the affairs of the inner chambers, my spirit is willing but my flesh is weak.\"","\"You have helped me a lot, Mother. Without the jade bracelet you gave me when I was newly married, I wouldn't have been able to show my skills no matter how capable I am. Mother, you don't need to underestimate yourself. This daughter-in-law will still rely on you in the future,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam was instantly filled with fighting spirit.","She had to help, and help well, to be worthy of her daughter-in-law's trust."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: Zhou Yuanshen's Study","paragraphs":["Inside the Jiangyun Courtyard, Cheng Zhao did not come over to serve Second Madam during dinner, but eight-year-old Zhou Yuanqi did.","Second Madam recounted the events of the day to the Second Master, while Zhou Yuanqi sat nearby listening.","\"Isn't that quite good?\" the Second Master said in a mild tone.","He had always been aloof from worldly strife and was uninterested in most household matters. Second Madam, on the other hand, was not one to fret over things. She never forced her husband to be more ambitious and never resented his indifference.","The older couple's relationship was stable and solid.","\"...'Good' is only on the surface. Who knows how many traps are hidden in the dark,\" Second Madam said.","The Second Master replied, \"Our daughter-in-law can handle it; she is quite clever. Even if she can't, living in the Nonghua Courtyard at least guarantees her a meal.\"","Second Madam agreed, \"I also think our daughter-in-law can handle it. She really knows how to speak.\"","She even repeated Cheng Zhao's words for the Second Master to hear.","The Second Master laughed out loud upon hearing them.","Beside them, Zhou Yuanqi chimed in, \"Cunning and hypocritical.\"","Second Madam glared at him. \"What nonsense are you spouting?\"","\"In her eyes, Mother, you are no different from Grandmother and First Madam. You are all outsiders. She curries favor with them, and she curries favor with you. Her words make no distinction between close and distant relations. They are not 'distant,' and you, Mother, are not 'close,'\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam rolled her eyes. \"You only know how to pick apart words. You can't just look at what she says; you have to look at her expression at the time. You don't need to worry about it, I know what I am doing.\"","Cheng Zhao certainly did not mean it like that.","\"Mother, just don't be too disappointed in the future,\" Zhou Yuanqi said. \"Her temperament is no different from Grandmother's or First Madam's.\"","\"At such a young age, slandering your sister-in-law behind her back. Is this how Mother taught you?\" Second Madam pinched his cheek.","Zhou Yuanqi's cold, scholarly facade instantly crumbled. \"Ouch! You can't pinch my face, I am a big kid... I am an adult now!\"","\"Adult my foot!\" Second Madam laughed.","Zhou Yuanqi's face flushed with anger. \"Mother, you are vulgar, you...\"","Second Madam simply used both hands to vigorously rub his fair, tender little face, making him squawk in frustration.","Only when he finally acted like a child of his age did she let go.","The Second Master remained sitting nearby, chuckling.","Mid-afternoon, Zhou Yuanshen returned from the government office and also heard about the matter.","He sent someone to summon Cheng Zhao to the Chenhui Courtyard.","Cheng Zhao thought, \"Dowager Madame had matters to instruct and called me to the Shou'an Courtyard, which I can understand. Why can't he take a few steps himself? Why must I go over?\"","Complaints aside, Cheng Zhao still changed her clothes, put on a cloak, and once again took a small oil-cloth carriage out.","The Chenhui Courtyard was located to the east of the Chengming Hall, separated from it by only two courtyards. Those two courtyards were uninhabited and served as places for the Zhou family to host banquets.","It was Cheng Zhao's first time visiting the Chenhui Courtyard.","She knew this was the inner study of the ducal estate. The courtyard gate looked just like any ordinary courtyard, with no discernible difference. Verdant bamboo was planted in the corners, lush and green this time of year, unfurling in the cold wind.","Upon knocking, a young servant boy came to open the door.","\"Madam, please come in. The Lord Duke has been waiting for you for a while,\" the servant boy said.","Cheng Zhao followed him inside, walked along the left corridor, and arrived beneath the eaves of the main house.","The servant boy did not announce her again; he simply lifted the heavy winter door curtain and invited Cheng Zhao inside.","The central hall of the main house was also like that of an ordinary courtyard, adorned with hanging calligraphy and paintings. There were two main rooms on both the left and right, all with curtains drawn.","\"Lord Duke, Madam has arrived,\" the servant boy said in a low voice, walking to the doorway on the left.","\"Come in.\"","The servant boy lifted the curtain.","Cheng Zhao had no time to look around further and stepped into the room.","The interior was warm, and a cozy aura brushed against her face. Red plum blossoms in the corner exuded a faint, elegant fragrance, accompanied by a light scent of sandalwood.","It was a sitting room, much like an ordinary sitting room, except the shelves in the corner did not display antique ornaments, but books.","Half a wall was filled with books, some wrapped in silk cloth, looking quite precious.","Zhou Yuanshen sat on the heated brick bed by the window, a Go board placed on the small table in front of him.","Cheng Zhao greeted the Lord Duke again. Seeing no senior maidservants attending in the room, she took off her cloak herself, hung it up, and then walked over to sit down.","\"...I heard Grandmother asked you to manage the main kitchen,\" he said.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"Yes, Dowager Madame instructed as such. I will go take over the duties tomorrow.\"","\"The main kitchen has been a bit chaotic lately,\" he said.","Cheng Zhao sat up straight. \"Please enlighten me, Lord Duke. I am currently completely in the dark and planned to slowly figure things out after going there tomorrow. With your guidance, I can avoid taking many detours.\"","Zhou Yuanshen raised his eyes to glance at her.","His gaze was pitch-black, and this glance seemed to carry a cold glint.","He did not seem to like Cheng Zhao's polite pleasantries.","Cheng Zhao returned a smile and did not speak again.","Zhou Yuanshen withdrew his gaze. \"Let's play a game.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","As the two played Go, Zhou Yuanshen explained the personnel disputes of the main kitchen to Cheng Zhao.","Simply put, Dowager Madame's steward wanted to retire and return to his hometown as he was getting old, and First Madam's people had taken control of the situation. Meanwhile, Dowager Madame and that steward both hoped their own trusted aides would take over, yet they found no way to intervene.","Dowager Madame's solution was to introduce a third party, shifting the conflict onto First Madam and Cheng Zhao, thereby reaping the benefits without lifting a finger.","\"...First Madam has managed the household for so many years, yet she doesn't have much real power. Everything is still decided by Grandmother,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"It is good that you understand.\"","\"What are your thoughts?\" Cheng Zhao asked. \"What do you want me to do?\"","Should she help Dowager Madame and sell her a favor, or help First Madam and break Dowager Madame's control over the inner quarters?","\"Keep to yourself. Do not become someone else's blade, nor make yourself a target,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao interpreted this to mean: the household management rights of the ducal estate have nothing to do with you from now on, and there is no need for you to get involved.","Who was the female master of the house in his heart?","Huan Qingtang, who wanted a dual-lineage marriage, or Mu Jiang?","Cheng Zhao felt it was Huan Qingtang.","No matter how you looked at it, Mu Jiang was not suited to be the female master of the ducal estate.","A female master not only had to run the household but also socialize. Mu Jiang was not a noble lady from a prominent family; many titled noblewomen looked down on her, and she would be unable to fit in.","Once ostracized, it would affect the entire ducal estate.","Huan Qingtang, however, was different. Like Cheng Zhao, she came from a scholarly family, which was the most respectable background for meritorious and highly titled noble families. Wherever they went, they carried dignity.","\"Yes, I will keep that in mind,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen placed another piece on the board.","The two played quietly; Cheng Zhao could even hear the sound of someone knocking on the courtyard gate.","The servant boy went to answer the door.","Soon, the servant boy spoke from the doorway, \"Lord Duke, the Secondary Wife has arrived.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Zhou Yuanshen put down his Go piece. Without saying anything to Cheng Zhao, he went out.","Holding a Go piece, Cheng Zhao wondered, was she just supposed to wait here?","Would Zhou Yuanshen personally bring Mu Jiang inside?","A moment later, Mu Jiang left, and Zhou Yuanshen returned to the room.","He looked at the Go board and said to Cheng Zhao, \"Let's continue.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","She did not say anything more.","In this game, neither Cheng Zhao nor Zhou Yuanshen won; it ended in a draw.","Zhou Yuanshen then said, \"There is one more thing I need to discuss with you.\"","Cheng Zhao was truly afraid of them discussing matters.","It was never anything good anyway.","\"Please give your instructions,\" she said."]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: Husband's Thoughtfulness","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen told Cheng Zhao that she could rest at Chenhui Courtyard at noon.","\"...You have duties to attend to in the morning, and the same goes for the afternoon. It would be quite a trek for you to return to Nonghua Courtyard for your midday rest.\" Zhou Yuanshen's expression remained very cold, and his tone could hardly be called gentle.","He added, \"If you prefer to go back, it is up to you.\"","The First Madam, Madam Song, lived right in Chengming Hall. The managers would come to report to her, so it was no trouble for her to eat and rest after handling affairs.","But Cheng Zhao would have to rush back and forth.","Now that winter had arrived, it would snow frequently. Even with a small horse-drawn carriage, going back would be troublesome.","\"...Would this disturb you, My Lord Duke?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"Since I brought it up, I'm naturally not just being polite.\"","\"Then thank you,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"A side room will be fine for me.\"","\"There is still an empty main room on the east side,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao glanced at him.","So, he didn't go to Nonghua Courtyard but specifically called her over just to give her a place to rest.","If the \"Duchess\" had to rush back and forth during her midday rest, the servants would inevitably mock her when they saw it, and Cheng Zhao would lose her prestige.","Once she lost her prestige, it would be difficult to convince the masses no matter what she managed.","Cheng Zhao accepted his kindness and asked, \"Will you assign one of your servants to attend to me, or should I bring one of my own maids over?\"","\"I won't be here during the midday rest. Bring your own person,\" he said.","Cheng Zhao agreed.","She assured him that she would not snoop around or wander aimlessly, nor would she dirty Chenhui Courtyard. Her maid would also be loyal and devoted, absolutely never prying into the Duke's secrets.","Zhou Yuanshen did not respond to her words.","He stood up and led Cheng Zhao to the room on the east side.","Of the two main rooms on the east, the outer one was a sitting room. The bookshelves against the wall were filled with books, and there was also a rack of long swords.","The inner room was vacant, with a few miscellaneous items scattered about.","Zhou Yuanshen told her, \"Come directly here for your midday rest tomorrow. Nanfeng will open the door for you.\"","That meant he would make the proper arrangements on his end, saving Cheng Zhao from worrying about it.","After everything was settled, Cheng Zhao returned to Nonghua Courtyard.","Everyone gathered around to ask about the situation.","\"The Duke was worried that the servants would look down on the 'Duchess', so he specifically arranged for me to rest in Chenhui Courtyard at noon. He wanted to discuss this matter and thought it would be best for me to see the courtyard for myself, which is why he sent someone to invite me over,\" Cheng Zhao explained.","Everyone breathed a sigh of relief.","Nanny Li then said, \"The Duke is very thoughtful. It is truly not easy for him to have considered this.\"","Cheng Zhao was also quite surprised.","Zhou Yuanshen didn't seem like someone with a meticulous personality. Perhaps because it concerned changes to the managerial power of the Duke's estate's inner quarters, he paid special attention to it.","The domestic affairs of the Duke's estate were very complicated, and Zhou Yuanshen had not yet reached the point where he could completely let go and let a trusted person manage them.","In the evening, Cheng Zhao spoke privately with Nanny Li, \"I suspect the Zhou family's noble estate and properties haven't fallen into the Duke's hands either.\"","Her mother-in-law had always thought that the First Branch controlled the noble properties.","But judging from Zhou Yuanshen's tone, the noble properties were firmly in the Old Madam's grasp. The Duke himself was merely a puppet, and the mother and daughter-in-law of the First Branch were nothing more than higher-level managers.","The First Madam, Madam Song, definitely believed she would be the future mistress and was eager to seize power. Taking advantage of the fact that the head manager of the main kitchen was about to \"retire due to old age,\" the First Madam wanted to arrange for her own person to take the position.","The Old Madam disagreed, but she wouldn't openly slap the face of the \"head manager of the inner quarters,\" so she inserted Cheng Zhao into the mix.","Cheng Zhao's official title as the \"Duchess\" was quite useful at a time like this.","\"...Nanny Li, do you still remember my youngest uncle?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Nanny Li: \"Why bring up the young master's uncle all of a sudden?\"","Her mind was still on the affairs of the Duke's estate.","\"Grandfather always said that my youngest uncle was a rebellious person. He didn't study or practice martial arts, just ran blindly all over the world.","But I really liked listening to him talk. He once told me that even the Emperor is nothing special; he is equally constrained by others and cannot do whatever he pleases.","The Emperor is nothing more than a patriarch with a richer 'noble estate'. Sometimes, the Emperor cannot carelessly touch the profits gained from this 'estate'. If he wants to build a garden, the imperial censors would rather smash their heads to death in the great hall than let him.\"","Nanny Li was terrified. \"Keep your voice down. Little ancestor, is this something you can casually talk about?\"","\"The logic is sound,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Nanny, think about it. In the inner courtyard of the Zhou family, doesn't the Duke seem like a new emperor, while the Old Madam is the 'Empress Dowager' controlling the real power?\"","When the noble clans were at their peak, the Emperor was not even as wealthy or powerful as the patriarch of a Duke's estate.","When the late Emperor was alive, there was too much slaughter, and the noble clans were heavily suppressed. The current Emperor inherited a lighter burden, which is why he has a bit of real power.","This situation seemed to be spiraling out of control.","The Cheng family was willing to form a marriage alliance with the Zhou family precisely because imperial power was withering and declining, and the noble and pure families needed a more powerful backing.","The Old Madam of the Zhou family was not just the one calling the shots at home.","She also had a say in the political affairs of the court.","\"It seems the Duke and the Old Madam have always been fighting,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li: \"...The Old Madam is getting on in years, and her grandson has already inherited the title. Yet she still refuses to relinquish power. What is she after?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"If I were in my old age, I wouldn't relinquish power either. If you don't hold power in your hands, are you just going to wait and live at the mercy of your children and grandchildren's moods?\"","\"Children and grandchildren should naturally respect their old grandmother.\"","\"What does an old ancestor with no money and no power rely on to gain respect? The conscience of her children and grandchildren? Children have the least conscience,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li: \"...\"","She didn't even know if Cheng Zhao was on the Old Madam's side or the Duke's side.","Why did it seem like she could understand everyone's situation?","\"...How did you get so worried that you started talking nonsense?\" Nanny Li said helplessly.","Cheng Zhao chuckled.","She just felt that the situation in the Duke's estate was complicated.","Just like the court politics, the current situation was a complete mess.","Zhou Yuanshen was not the legitimate son of the First Branch; he probably never thought he would inherit the title.","But since the title was given to him, not giving him the corresponding noble properties was nothing more than a blatant disregard for his dignity as a person.","Even the Second Madam wanted to live in Chengming Hall, let alone Zhou Yuanshen himself?","Cheng Zhao could understand. She had married into the Zhou family and occupied the position of the Duke's legitimate wife. If she were never given her official lady's title, she would also feel aggrieved.","The taste of having only an empty title and no real power was hard to bear.","As for the Old Madam, she probably couldn't let go. She might not even think highly of this grandson, Zhou Yuanshen, and only chose him to inherit the title out of helplessness.","Entrusting all the family properties to him was absolutely out of the question.","Cheng Zhao could understand both of their thoughts, but everyone had to choose their own corner to stand in.","She was the Duchess, so she ought to stand on Zhou Yuanshen's side. The Old Madam wouldn't trust Cheng Zhao anyway; even if Cheng Zhao surrendered to her, it would be meaningless.","Cheng Zhao sorted through everything in her mind.","Once she had it all figured out, no matter how difficult things were, she could slowly feel her way forward without being in a complete mess.","The next day, Cheng Zhao went to Chengming Hall.","When she arrived, the side hall where the First Madam managed affairs was already full of people.","When the crowd saw her, they greeted her with sparse voices, lacking any warmth. They were all taking their cues from the First Madam.","The First Young Madam, Huan Qingtang, sat just below the First Madam.","It seemed she had always been assisting the First Madam in managing affairs."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: Argument","paragraphs":["First Madam Song strongly disliked Cheng Zhao.","With the Old Madam absent, she couldn't even be bothered to pretend.","\"Here are the account books and tallies for the main kitchen, along with the keys to its storehouse. Keep them safe.\" The displeasure in the First Madam's tone was evident from her slightly furrowed brows.","The managers and stewards were all stealing glances at them.","Cheng Zhao, however, maintained a respectful and polite attitude as she accepted them: \"If there is anything I fall short on in the future, please point it out clearly, Eldest Aunt. I will correct my mistakes if I have made any, and strive to do better if I haven't.\"","\"I wouldn't dare. You were appointed by the Old Madam, how could you fall short? Are you saying that the Old Madam made a poor judgment in appointing people?\" the First Madam asked.","Cheng Zhao smiled: \"Grandmother's decisions are naturally a million times perfect. It's just that I feel a bit timid in front of you, Eldest Aunt, and I'm afraid of making mistakes out of panic.\"","\"There's no need for that,\" the First Madam said. \"Just do your job well. You don't need to speak such glib words in front of me.\"","This \"reprimand\" was like a sudden downpour, completely merciless.","The stewardesses occasionally peeked at Cheng Zhao.","The young \"Duchess\" might have her eyes turn red from anger.","Today was her first day on the job. Whether she cried from anger or talked back to her aunt out of frustration, the First Madam would have an excuse to pin a crime on her.","The first day was crucial. Once trampled down, it would be very difficult to climb back up later.","Cheng Zhao, however, never changed her expression.","A faint smile lingered on her face, gentle and quiet.","For the whole morning, the First Madam ignored Cheng Zhao; Cheng Zhao didn't say a word either, sitting quietly to the side, maintaining a focused and gentle expression as she listened.","During the noon break, Cheng Zhao retreated from Chengming Hall.","Among the stewardesses, someone had already gone to Shou'an Courtyard to report everything that happened this morning to the Old Madam.","\"...She has a good temper and impressive self-restraint,\" the old servant said.","The Old Madam said: \"How could the girls of the Cheng family be pushovers? The Empress arranged for such a person to enter the Duke of Chen's mansion, who knows what her intentions are.\"","She added, \"To secure the Crown Prince's position, the Empress will resort to any extreme. Unfortunately, she has miscalculated.\"","Cheng Zhao was merely a pawn caught in the struggle.","The Old Madam didn't really take her seriously.","Let alone Cheng Zhao, the entire inner residence was in the Old Madam's palm.","First Madam Song seemed to have some power, but it was nothing more than the Old Madam still needing to use her and being too lazy to teach her a lesson.","\"Let's wait and see. If it really doesn't work out, we'll have Lady Huan manage the household affairs,\" the Old Madam said.","She had a very good impression of Huan Qingtang.","As for First Madam Song, she was cautious when she was young; now that she was older, she had become spoiled, losing her past prudence and intelligence, and becoming a bit arrogant and ignorant.","Indeed, without competition, a person will slowly become lazy and corrupt.","The First Madam had lived a good life for too long.","\"Where is Lady Cheng dining at noon?\" the Old Madam asked.","She wanted to send one of her own dishes to Cheng Zhao to secretly support her and give First Madam Song a warning.","\"She said she is resting at Chenhui Courtyard for noon,\" the stewardess said.","When this stewardess left, she specifically asked Cheng Zhao.","She was the Old Madam's confidante and often thought ahead of her.","Today was Cheng Zhao's first day on the job. The Old Madam might or might not ask where she was resting at noon. She couldn't be ignorant when her master asked; she had to prepare for a rainy day.","The Old Madam indeed asked.","Hearing the words \"Chenhui Courtyard\", the Old Madam slightly turned her face.","She was a bit surprised.","There were truly not many things that could surprise her.","\"It seems the Duke is very satisfied with Lady Cheng,\" the Old Madam said.","The old servant replied yes in a low voice, not really daring to say more.","The Old Madam pondered for a moment, called her senior maid in, and told her to set aside a dish from Shou'an Courtyard and send it to Chenhui Courtyard for Cheng Zhao to eat.","The senior maid left.","The east main room of Chenhui Courtyard hadn't been tidied much overnight.","There were just a few pieces of furniture and a small bed; on the heated brick bed by the window, there was a resting pillow and a low table; on the table were a few books.","Cheng Zhao's mother-in-law had sent her own people to deliver food to Chenhui Courtyard early on, afraid that Cheng Zhao would go hungry; the maid Qiubai went to the main kitchen to fetch Cheng Zhao's daily food allowance and was waiting in the room.","Just as she was about to eat, the Old Madam's maid arrived.","She added a dish of braised chicken with quail eggs for Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao stood up and thanked her, asked Qiubai to reward the senior maid, and saw her out.","She couldn't let people stay in Chenhui Courtyard for long.","During the noon break, she just took a casual nap on the large heated brick bed by the window.","After a whole day, Cheng Zhao found that there was almost nothing for her to do. Her tasks could be finished in half the time it takes an incense stick to burn.","But she had to spend the whole day in Chengming Hall.","Cheng Zhao wasn't afraid of waiting around.","She just listened quietly, watching how the First Madam and Huan Qingtang managed affairs, silently memorizing it all.","In three days, Cheng Zhao had figured out the general workings of the inner residence of the Duke of Chen's mansion.","It was similar to her maiden home.","Cheng Zhao's mother was the eldest daughter-in-law of the eldest branch. When she managed the household, her daughters-in-law and unmarried daughters all had to stand by and learn.","She never said anything.","Even if the First Madam intentionally suppressed her and spoke harshly, Cheng Zhao didn't argue with her, just silently kept it in mind.","On the fourth day, the First Madam felt a bit unwell when she woke up.","She told Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang that they would rest for an hour at noon, as she was very tired from holding up all morning; whether they would continue working in the afternoon depended on her condition after resting, and told them to wait for word.","Cheng Zhao returned to Chenhui Courtyard.","Since the noon break was long this time, Cheng Zhao took off her outer clothes and rested on the bed, rather than just napping on the heated bed by the window.","Qiubai slept at the foot of the bed.","Later, Cheng Zhao was nudged awake by Qiubai.","Listening closely, there were two men talking in the outer room.","It wasn't Zhou Yuanshen and a page boy, but him and his father.","Qiubai hinted to Cheng Zhao with her eyes.","The master and servant weren't quite sure if Zhou Yuanshen knew Cheng Zhao hadn't left yet, after all, the noon break had already passed.","Cheng Zhao listened carefully; her father-in-law's voice was a bit loud.","\"...The path of power is piled with white bones. Hasn't our family committed enough sins in the past? Why must you do these things?","Those families whose homes were raided and confiscated, which one wasn't made of living people? Ah Shen, you have already gained so much. Why must you do these things for the Emperor?\" her father-in-law said.","\"If I don't do it, there are plenty of others who will,\" Zhou Yuanshen said. \"It is the natural order for a minister to die if the sovereign commands it. It doesn't count as committing a sin.\"","His father then said: \"That is their business. If you don't accumulate virtue, what kind of end will you face in the future? Beneath which noble title is there not a mountain of corpses and a sea of blood?\"","Zhou Yuanshen seemed to say something.","The voices of the father and son lowered a bit.","Cheng Zhao vaguely heard her father-in-law say: \"You promised your grandmother to inherit both branches. Have a child with the daughter-in-law of the eldest branch, and return the title to them.","Ah Shen, we don't need these things. Back then, your grandfather left me enough property to ensure you three brothers live a life of comfort for the rest of your lives.\"","\"Being controlled by others, I can tolerate; but asking me to act as a breeding stud...\"","\"My Lord Duke, is the Madam awake? A sister from Chengming Hall is here,\" a page boy called out loudly.","The voices of Zhou Yuanshen and the Second Master came to an abrupt halt.","The room was terrifyingly quiet for a moment.","Cheng Zhao facepalmed.","The father and son truly had not known that Cheng Zhao hadn't left yet.","However, Cheng Zhao hadn't heard any grand secrets.","Which family's ancestral title and estate weren't built on the saying 'one general's success costs the lives of ten thousand'? They were all obtained by stepping on countless corpses.","If one really dug into it, no family's ancestors had clean hands.","As for the matter of Zhou Yuanshen taking Huan Qingtang as a co-wife, Cheng Zhao had long since heard about it from her grandfather.","\"...Are you awake?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked Cheng Zhao as he stepped up to the curtained doorway.","\"I just woke up, My Lord Duke,\" Cheng Zhao replied. \"I will get up right away.\""]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: I Help You","paragraphs":["Qiubai got up first.","She put on her small jacket and hurriedly helped Cheng Zhao put on her outer robe. Cheng Zhao's hair wasn't too messy; she had only taken out her hairpin, which Qiubai helped her put back in.","After finishing the preparations, Qiubai lifted the door curtain.","Seeing a dark figure standing in the outer room, Qiubai curtsied, \"My Lord Duke.\"","\"Are you ready?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked.","\"Yes,\" Qiubai replied, holding the curtain up for Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen entered the room.","Cheng Zhao was waiting for Qiubai to bring in water for her to rinse her mouth. Seeing Zhou Yuanshen enter first, she had no choice but to pick up the thermos on the table and pour herself half a cup of water.","After rinsing her mouth, she straightened her collar. \"My Lord Duke, I will take my leave first. I am already a bit late.\"","\"Did you oversleep?\" he asked.","There was no warmth in his voice.","\"No, First Aunt said to rest for an extra two hours this afternoon. She wasn't feeling well this morning and might not have the energy this afternoon, so she told us to wait for her message,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen nodded slightly. \"Go then.\"","He added, \"I will go to Nonghua Courtyard for dinner tonight.\"","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","Having dinner meant he would be staying the night at Nonghua Courtyard.","Recalling the conversation he just had with her father-in-law, Cheng Zhao felt he would definitely have some instructions for her tonight.","Cheng Zhao agreed, walked out of the main hall, called for the maid Qiubai who was waiting at the door, and headed toward Chengming Hall.","Qiubai said to Cheng Zhao, \"Starting tomorrow, I will wait outside during your afternoon nap. I cannot be as lax as before.\"","Cheng Zhao said, \"I thought Nanfeng was always there.\"","\"The inner study seems to be poorly guarded, and Nanfeng often disappears without a trace,\" Qiubai said.","Cheng Zhao nodded slightly. \"Then when you are on duty in the future, I will place some resting pillows in the outer room so you can lie down at noon. I won't arrange for you to take night shifts at Nonghua Courtyard anymore; I will speak with Nanny Li about it later.\"","Qiubai said yes.","The master and servant arrived at Chengming Hall as they spoke.","There wasn't much to do in the afternoon, just passing the time. The First Madam, Madam Song, lacked energy and had a bad temper. Except for one or two stewards, the First Madam listened absentmindedly when others reported to her.","Cheng Zhao memorized the stewards whom the First Madam treated differently—whether with extra courtesy or extra slight—so she could inquire about them later.","After her duties were over, Cheng Zhao took a small carriage back to Nonghua Courtyard.","She changed her clothes, let down her hair, and asked another maid to style it for her. Then she said to Nanny Li, \"The Lord Duke is coming for dinner.\"","Nanny Li went to give the orders.","Zhou Yuanshen had mentioned it in advance, so there was no need for extra reminders, which was why he arrived relatively late this time.","In winter, the sky darkened quickly, and he entered Nonghua Courtyard almost right as night fell.","Everyone served him as he changed his clothes and washed his hands.","\"Serve the meal first; it's getting late,\" he said.","Nanny Li complied and ordered two rough-work older servants to carry a low table and place it on the large heated brick bed by the window in the eastern side room.","Cheng Zhao sat opposite him and had dinner.","She didn't eat much for dinner, and neither did Zhou Yuanshen. The two finished eating quickly.","This time he didn't play chess. He took a book to bed and began reading by the light of the horn lantern at the bedside.","It was still early for bed, and Cheng Zhao couldn't sleep yet, so she took a sewing basket and sat on the heated brick bed by the window to do some needlework.","From where she sat, she could just see Zhou Yuanshen through the side of the folding screen. She glanced over occasionally; he remained motionless, turning the pages of his book at a steady pace.","The embroidered pouch in Cheng Zhao's hands, which she had been working on for nearly half a month, was almost finished. She yawned, feeling a bit of soreness in her eyes, and decided it was time to rest.","Zhou Yuanshen finally put down his book.","He got up and walked over, watching Cheng Zhao pack up her sewing basket, and leaned in slightly to embrace her from behind.","Cheng Zhao was a bit unsteady and held onto the low table. \"My Lord Duke...\"","Zhou Yuanshen undid her hair bun.","The maid had casually tied it up for her, so it was loose, and her black hair instantly cascaded down.","Zhou Yuanshen's face drew closer, and through the curtain of her hanging hair, Cheng Zhao could feel the burning heat of his breath.","His hands fumbled for her sash.","The bedroom had underfloor heating and was warm and cozy, but with her shoulder skin exposed without clothing to cover it, it still felt a bit chilly.","When Cheng Zhao realized what he was about to do, she gave a violent shiver.","\"No!\" Afraid the maid on night watch in the outer room would hear, she resisted with a suppressed voice. \"No, this isn't...\"","This wasn't the bed!","She and he were a proper married couple, bestowed by the Empress, with gifts prepared by the Ministry of Rites, a couple married with the Three Letters and Six Rites. She wasn't a mistress for him to toy with.","A wife's duty was to be filial to her parents-in-law, respect and love her husband, raise children, manage the household, and handle everyday affairs.","She wasn't a sweet treat for his amusement either.","Her mother had told her that for a main wife to compete for favor was a very lowly act.","He couldn't go hunting for novelty on her.","On the large heated bed by the window, a single horn lantern could cast their silhouettes onto the window lattice, and every movement might be seen by the maids and older servants.","Cheng Zhao could not accept this.","She wasn't short, but Zhou Yuanshen was simply too tall, with long arms and legs. Based on these advantages, he could easily subdue her without using brute force.","Her body was too tense. Zhou Yuanshen firmly grasped her waist with his other hand and whispered, \"Don't struggle too hard.\"","Cheng Zhao's black hair blocked her vision.","She closed her eyes.","Perhaps it was tears falling, or perhaps it was sweat.","Cheng Zhao was sitting in the bathtub, and it was already past midnight. Stung by the hot water, her elbows and knees felt a burning pain.","Especially her knees; the left one had the skin rubbed off.","And the pain wasn't just in those two places.","Cheng Zhao leaned back against the edge of the bathtub and thought to herself that if she became pregnant, gave birth to the eldest son, and had an heir, she might be able to be a bit more assertive.","Right now, she didn't dare.","If she truly offended him deeply, and he stopped spending the night at Nonghua Courtyard in the future, Cheng Zhao would be put in a passive position.","The situation within the Duke Chen's estate was unclear, and the matter of Zhou Yuanshen taking a concurrent wife for another branch seemed set in stone. How could the Old Madam's decision allow him to resist?","Once he truly married Huan Qingtang concurrently, and she had a child first, Cheng Zhao and the second branch would be extremely disadvantaged.","As soon as Cheng Zhao married in, she won over her mother-in-law, promising that she would definitely help her turn her fortunes around and hold her head high.","Without a child, Cheng Zhao wouldn't even have a bargaining chip. Not only would she suffer grievances herself, but she would also break her promise to others.","Therefore, whether it was the difficulties she faced in Chengming Hall or the deliberate humiliation he inflicted in the bedroom, Cheng Zhao had to swallow it all.","\"...Are you done washing?\" someone suddenly spoke.","Cheng Zhao subconsciously crossed her arms over her chest. \"You go out first!\"","There was no respect at all; her tone was cold and forceful.","Zhou Yuanshen was very tall, blocking the light in the washroom. He said to her, \"You've been washing for a long time. Be careful not to catch a cold.\"","Hypocritical concern.","If he had even the slightest bit of care for her in his heart, the scene from just now would never have happened.","Cheng Zhao turned her head away.","After he went out, she called the night-watch maid in to dry her body and help her change into clean inner garments and trousers.","Zhou Yuanshen was not asleep yet.","Cheng Zhao got into bed, and Zhou Yuanshen turned up the bedside horn lantern a little. He then poured hot water from the thermos into a copper basin and washed his hands meticulously.","Drying the water with a clean towel, he took a box of ointment and entered the bed curtains.","\"Apply some ointment, or it will hurt tomorrow morning,\" he said.","Cheng Zhao said, \"I'll do it myself.\"","Her elbows and knees did indeed hurt a lot.","But Zhou Yuanshen said, \"I'll help you. You can't see.\"","Cheng Zhao froze for a moment.","An uncontrollable flash of anger surfaced on her face.","\"You...\""]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22: Not Used to Sharing a Bed with Her","paragraphs":["If possible, Cheng Zhao hoped she would not have to see Zhou Yuanshen for a very long time.","Unfortunately, he was free for the next few days.","And Cheng Zhao had no way to avoid taking her afternoon naps in the Chenhui Courtyard.","Every time she woke up from her nap, Zhou Yuanshen was there. He used to read and play chess in the western side room, but now he had moved to the eastern one.","When Cheng Zhao came out of the inner room, he would be sitting right there.","\"Lord Duke,\" she lowered her eyelashes, \"I am going to Chengming Hall now. You don't need me to serve you here, do you?\"","Zhou Yuanshen raised his eyes to look at her.","His eyes were pitch-black. When he looked at people, they were calm and rippleless, like thousand-year-old ice. His incomparably handsome face seemed covered in a layer of frost because of those eyes.","It was as if he would fly into a violent rage in the very next second.","In reality, however, Zhou Yuanshen had never lost his temper. He rarely even spoke loudly.","He had been back in the capital for some time. With his naturally fair skin, much like the Second Madam's, a period of rest had washed away the ruggedness of a military man, making him look more like a scholar.","Yet, the toughness and coldness of a general remained completely undiminished in him.","Cheng Zhao's impression of him had always been that he was rough. But thinking about it carefully, his speech and manners actually showed the noble upbringing of a young master from an aristocratic family.","The only rough and vicious behavior of his was probably in the bedroom.","\"Go on ahead,\" he said.","Cheng Zhao complied and left for Chengming Hall.","That day, Zhou Yuanshen also went out.","He went to visit his maternal grandmother.","At the same time, he met up with his youngest uncle, Fan Xiao, to discuss the recent political situation at court.","Fan Xiao worked in the Dali Temple. He hadn't yet reached the rank of Deputy Minister, but he was on very good terms with both the Minister and Deputy Minister, so he knew many inside details.","Also present today was his youngest uncle's close friend, Helian Jian, the heir of Prince Rong's Estate.","\"...Of course the Empress wants to make the Seventh Prince the Crown Prince. But there are many opponents. The Seventh Prince is only nine years old; he's too young and there are too many variables. Furthermore, the Empress's maiden family has a massive clan influence, leaving no room for the court officials,\" his youngest uncle said.","Helian Jian added, \"The court officials also keep harping on the fact that the Empress is not His Majesty's first wife, bringing it up time and again.\"","At this point, both men looked at Zhou Yuanshen.","His Majesty's first wife had been Zhou Yuanshen's aunt.","His aunt had passed away many years ago without leaving behind a son or daughter. The less there was to entrust his grief to, the more the Emperor missed her.","Zhou Yuanshen merely listened quietly.","\"...It's been three months since your grand wedding. Is there any good news from the Duchess?\" Fan Xiao asked suddenly.","The uncle and nephew were similar in age and had grown up together on the frontier, so their bond was different from others. Fan Xiao dared to ask him anything.","\"What about your concubine?\" Helian Jian also asked. \"She was handpicked by the Emperor. If she gets pregnant first, it would be more beneficial to you, right?\"","Zhou Yuanshen frowned.","He did not want to talk about these matters.","Seeing his displeasure, Fan Xiao steered the topic back to the court situation.","By evening, Helian Jian took his leave, but Fan Xiao still couldn't help showing concern for Zhou Yuanshen.","Now that he was married, the issue of an heir was quite urgent, especially given the situation of the Zhou family.","Zhou Yuanshen's maternal family all advised him to let his lawful wife give birth to the eldest son. If the concubine had a child first, he might be controlled by the Old Madam forever.","His youngest uncle, Fan Xiao, even told him a story.","\"...In the past, there was a General of Valiant Cavalry under my father's command. He and his wife had been married for seven years without a legitimate son, though he did have several children with his concubines.","His wife spent her days seeking medical advice and praying to the gods. Later, a barefoot doctor, who possessed some real skill, went to check her pulse.","The doctor said that neither husband nor wife had any major health issues. Unless their ancestors had committed grave sins, they shouldn't be lacking a legitimate child.","That barefoot doctor told them to 'return to their primal nature.' Have you ever seen cattle and horses mate? Humans essentially suppress their natural instincts, which might be why an heir is always so hard to conceive.","In less than half a year, that general's wife was with child, and subsequently gave birth to four in a row. The story spread all over the garrison.\"","Fan Xiao jokingly told Zhou Yuanshen not to be overly delicate and to hurry up and produce a legitimate son. Humans needed to learn from beasts; inside the bed-curtains, husband and wife shouldn't care about worldly statuses.","Zhou Yuanshen had done exactly that.","He originally hadn't wanted to drag Cheng Zhao into this. It was she herself who insisted on causing a fuss.","Zhou Yuanshen had also put in effort regarding the request for her imperial title; that was why the title of \"Duchess\" was granted so quickly.","Now that she had the title and claimed she was willing, giving birth to a child sooner rather than later would only benefit Zhou Yuanshen without causing any harm.","He didn't want to have too deep a bond with Cheng Zhao. His goal was clear, so every time he went to the Nonghua Courtyard, he would remember what his youngest uncle said about \"returning to their primal nature.\"","But he could feel that his Duchess was very unhappy.","Noble ladies from prestigious families were the most overly delicate.","Perhaps she would only understand Zhou Yuanshen's intentions after suffering through seven childless years—of course, Zhou Yuanshen himself couldn't afford to wait that long.","It had been two months since they consummated their marriage, yet there was still no good news from her.","Zhou Yuanshen couldn't ask anything. If he asked, it wouldn't come across as concern, but as an accusation.","He didn't want to accuse Cheng Zhao of anything; he wasn't even familiar with her. Perhaps the ancestors of the Zhou family had indeed committed grave sins, and they deserved to die out without an heir.","The woman from the eldest branch had been married for two years before her husband died, and didn't she also fail to leave behind an heir?","He was very reluctant to discuss this matter with anyone.","That day, Zhou Yuanshen returned very late.","He had drunk some wine and rode his horse back as usual. When he arrived in front of the residence and saw the plaque that read \"General Pingxi's Mansion,\" he was momentarily stunned.","It had been a long time since he last returned here.","It had been more than half a year since he moved into Duke Chen's Mansion.","Zhou Yuanshen dismounted, and his lieutenant went to knock on the door.","The General's Mansion had people left to guard it, but they hadn't expected the master to return so suddenly, and for a moment, they were a bit panicked and at a loss.","The servants made the bed and prepared hot water, and Zhou Yuanshen slept in a guest room in the outer courtyard.","He slept very soundly.","It had been a long time since he had a dreamless night like this, and he woke up feeling refreshed.","When he was at Duke Chen's Mansion, whether in the Nonghua Courtyard or the Chenhui Courtyard, he always felt a wave of confusion and a special kind of melancholy upon waking.","It always felt like something was weighing down on his chest.","Especially in the Nonghua Courtyard. Every time he woke up, having a woman beside him would startle him while he was still half-asleep. His instincts as a general made him feel it was dangerous, and he would subconsciously try to draw the dagger hidden under his pillow.","Unfortunately, he couldn't keep a dagger under the pillow in the Nonghua Courtyard.","Zhou Yuanshen really wanted to return to the Chenhui Courtyard to sleep after every time they shared a bed, but he was afraid the \"Duchess\" would overthink it.","It seemed that every time they had intercourse, she was extremely unhappy; if he were to leave without staying the night, Zhou Yuanshen felt she might die of depression.","After all, it was a human life.","If he had married a girl from a military family, perhaps they would be able to understand each other, and he wouldn't have to force himself to adapt.","Zhou Yuanshen found the General's Mansion comfortable, so he stayed there for six consecutive days.","Until Nanfeng came looking for him.","\"The Old Madam specifically called this humble servant over to ask where you have been sleeping these past few days. The Young Madam manages the main kitchen, and hearing that your dinner portions for the past few days were untouched, she also tactfully inquired,\" Nanfeng said.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"I will return tonight.\"","\"Where should dinner be served?\" Nanfeng pressed, as he needed to report back to the Old Madam.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"Chenhui Courtyard.\"","\"Then what about the Young Madam...\"","\"These matters have nothing to do with her,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Nanfeng complied.","When dealing with the Old Madam, the Lord Duke was probably very frustrated and irritable, though it couldn't be seen from his exterior.","He shouldn't have brought up the Young Madam at a time like this.","Nanfeng went back to report his mission.","On this day, Cheng Zhao got her monthly courses. Hearing that the elusive Zhou Yuanshen was returning to dine in the Chenhui Courtyard, she had an excuse to refuse his visit to the Nonghua Courtyard, and secretly breathed a sigh of relief."]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: Two Sets of Tricks","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao's monthly cycle had arrived, so Nanny Li used the small kitchen in Nonghua Courtyard to stew beef soup for her.","Beef bones and meat were simmered over a low fire for six hours. The meat melted into the broth, and with the addition of several tonic herbs, the soup became thick and savory.","\"...This kind of soup is the most nourishing in winter. Madam loves to drink it. You see, her complexion is always rosy,\" Nanny Li said.","The Madam she spoke of was Cheng Zhao's biological mother.","Cheng Zhao then said, \"We stewed a bit too much today. Send a pot to my mother-in-law's side.\"","Nanny Li complied and instructed a second-tier maid to wrap the soup pot in cotton cloth, place it in a food box, and carry it over to Jiangyun Courtyard.","The maid returned after quite a while.","\"...The Fifth Young Master was also there, and he drank a large bowl,\" the maid reported. \"The Second Madam also had some and was full of praise. She even rewarded this servant with a string of cash.\"","\"It seems that Mother and Fifth Brother both like it very much,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","Nanny Li asked again, \"Should we send some to the Duke? You are still using his inner study, after all.\"","Cheng Zhao immediately replied, \"He is neither a woman nor a child; he wouldn't like drinking soup. Don't send it, it will make us look too fawning.\"","Nanny Li agreed once more.","Before bed, Nanny Li combed Cheng Zhao's hair. Only after all the serving maids had withdrawn did Nanny Li ask Cheng Zhao in a low voice, \"Why are you angry with the Duke?\"","Cheng Zhao thought of what happened that night on the large heated bed by the window, and anger welled up from the bottom of her heart.","She had suffered so much, even scraping the skin off her knees, but to no avail. Her monthly cycle arrived without a single day's delay.","She had consummated the marriage with him several times, yet she still wasn't pregnant. Perhaps there was something wrong with him.","Cheng Zhao had a rosy complexion and was in excellent health. Her mother had given birth to two sons and three daughters. No matter how you looked at it, Cheng Zhao should be able to conceive very easily.","She had always hoped to hit the mark on the first try so that she wouldn't have to put on a false show of affection with him anymore.","After that night, Cheng Zhao saw him a few times in Chenhui Courtyard. She hardly spoke to him, and he ignored her as well.","Afterward, his whereabouts became unknown.","Hearing the servants gossip, Secondary Wife Mu Jiang was also not in the manor those few days, her whereabouts equally unknown.","Some guessed that the Duke had taken the Secondary Wife to a hot spring villa for a short stay. Others vowed confidently that the Secondary Wife would definitely be the first to give birth to the Duke's eldest son.","Cheng Zhao couldn't be bothered to pay attention and treated it all as wind blowing past her ears.","Yet Nanny Li brought it up again.","\"...I am not angry with him,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She added, \"When on earth will the Secondary Wife get pregnant?\"","Nanny Li's hands paused, looking at her face in the mirror in astonishment. \"Why are you hoping for the Secondary Wife to get pregnant?\"","Was she confused by anger?","That night... Nanny Li did know about it. She had even sent all the servants in the courtyard back to their rooms, forbidding anyone from walking around outside.","They were a young married couple; there was nothing inappropriate about it.","To fly into a great rage over this and even hope for a concubine to get pregnant first was losing the greater goal for a petty grievance.","\"Didn't you say it yourself, that I shouldn't be jealous of concubines? You said that when a man spends a long time messing around with his concubines, he empties out all his frivolous energy, and what he gives his main wife is pure gold?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Nanny Li was speechless.","Weren't those just words the madams of the inner courts used to comfort themselves?","Otherwise, if they spent all day fighting over jealousy with concubines, how would they have the mind to manage the family's daily affairs? If they lost the dignity of a main wife, which of the managers would be willing to submit to them?","Naturally, there had to be all sorts of excuses to make her feel a bit more comfortable in her heart.","But those concubines belonging to others were all fed medicine.","If the main wife hadn't given birth, they wouldn't stop the concubines' medicine.","\"I didn't get any gold. I just suffered all the hardships, both deserved and undeserved,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li said, \"Don't be impatient, Young Madam.\"","Cheng Zhao took a few deep breaths.","Perhaps because it was her time of the month, she was feeling unwell and was indeed full of complaints.","\"Pour out your grievances to this old servant, don't hold it all in,\" Nanny Li seemed to understand her harmless little temper. Instead of persuading her otherwise, she encouraged her a bit.","After Cheng Zhao vented her frustrations, she also laughed.","For the next half a month, Cheng Zhao did not see Zhou Yuanshen.","She didn't run into him at Chenhui Courtyard either.","They said Chenhui Courtyard was his inner study, but it wasn't actually that important.","It was only guarded by a twelve-year-old servant boy, Nanfeng, with two rough-work older women coming to clean. They left as soon as they finished cleaning and belonged to the outer study.","And Nanfeng would often run off without a trace. When asked, he would say that the older servant girls from the outer study had things for him to do.","From this, it was evident that this inner study was merely a place to rest one's feet.","At first, Cheng Zhao had been apprehensive, afraid that she had mistakenly entered Zhou Yuanshen's territory and disturbed his peace. She was even more afraid that if some valuable document in the inner study went missing, she wouldn't be able to explain it clearly.","She was overthinking it.","She had been going to Chengming Hall for a while now and had almost completely figured out the tasks the Eldest Madam had on hand.","The end of the year was approaching, yet not a single manager from the outer estates had come to report.","In Cheng Zhao's maiden home, starting from the tenth month, the managers of the farming estates would return to the capital one after another. What they brought back was real gold and silver.","At this time, the four first-tier maids by Cheng Zhao's mother's side would all have to use abacuses, working day and night without rest.","The end of the year was the busiest time for the main courtyard.","If anyone caused trouble during these days, her mother would sternly punish them in a foul temper. Therefore, every time the end of the year approached, Cheng Zhao would be extremely well-behaved.","During this period, Huan Qingtang didn't come to Chengming Hall.","Cheng Zhao saw her several times leading a few first-tier maids to the Old Madam's Shou'an Courtyard. The Eldest Madam herself didn't seem indignant, let alone feel any sense of urgency.","\"...The Eldest Madam's management authority is strictly limited to the inner residence,\" Cheng Zhao told Nanny Li upon returning.","Nanny Li was very surprised. \"The Eldest Madam has been managing the household affairs for quite a few years now. Has she not noticed it herself?\"","\"I am surprised as well.\"","Nanny Li still couldn't believe it. \"It can't be, can it? The Eldest Madam comes from the Marquis of Changling's manor. How could she be so ignorant?\"","\"I personally think that the Zhou family's noble estates are much richer and far exceed those of the Cheng family. Madam Song's maiden family can't even compare.","They are so wealthy that what flows into the inner courtyard is enough to make the Eldest Madam believe it is everything,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Perhaps she doesn't know the total income of the Zhou family's noble estates.\"","She added, \"When the late Emperor was alive, he was rather strict in bestowing noble estates. The Marquis of Changling's family is a scholarly lineage, and perhaps they even inherited the title at a reduced rank, so they might not have much left in their hands.\"","Except for a clean reputation.","On the other hand, for a family like the Zhous, who relied on the merit of following the dragon for two emperors, their noble estates were terrifyingly vast. What they wanted most was a clean reputation to serve as a fig leaf over their massive profits.","When the Zhou family chose daughters-in-law, they specifically picked noble ladies from clean and prestigious lineages.","Nanny Li was stunned by Cheng Zhao's analysis and still told Cheng Zhao to observe a bit more.","When Cheng Zhao went to Chengming Hall again, everything was as usual, and she didn't utter half an extra word.","The Eldest Madam said to her, \"Calling you here every day has truly been hard on you. The main kitchen only has those few tasks. How about this: starting next month, I will have the main kitchen's manager go to Nonghua Courtyard to report, saving you the trouble of running back and forth.\"","Cheng Zhao said, \"Thank you for your deep affection, Eldest Aunt.\"","\"Then perform well, so it will be easier for me to bring it up with the Old Madam,\" the Eldest Madam said.","Her tone was uncharacteristically gentle.","The next day, it snowed.","Heavy snow fell for three consecutive days, burying the streets and crushing houses, causing a moderately severe snow disaster.","Madam Song wanted to set up porridge sheds."]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: Cheng Zhao's Quick-Wittedness","paragraphs":["Whenever heavy snow fell or the summer heat became unbearable, prestigious families would always do some good deeds.","On snowy days, many people suffered from the cold and hunger. Setting up a porridge shed to distribute food was a way to accumulate virtue and do good.","First Madam entrusted this task to Cheng Zhao.","She repeatedly emphasized, \"This is a major event, so you must not make any mistakes. If anything goes wrong, neither of us will be able to explain it to Dowager Madame.\"","Cheng Zhao recalled that First Madam had just mentioned \"treating her well,\" and now this task had fallen into her lap. It was highly likely a trap.","\"Rest assured, Eldest Aunt, I will be thorough in every aspect,\" Cheng Zhao replied.","On the day the porridge shed was set up, Cheng Zhao brought Nanny Li, Qiubai, and Suyue to inspect it, overseeing everything with her own eyes.","She inspected the porridge shed at the back gate over and over again, and repeatedly checked the pots and rice used for boiling the porridge in the main kitchen.","Distributing porridge wasn't a huge undertaking; her maiden family did it as well. One year, her mother had put her eldest sister in charge and asked Cheng Zhao to assist.","Her eldest sister had learned many things from their mother and taught them to Cheng Zhao one by one.","Cheng Zhao was young and playful back then, listening to her eldest sister half-heartedly. However, she had been clever since childhood and could achieve perfect results with only half the effort.","The next day, the Chen Duke's Mansion officially began cooking and distributing the porridge.","Cheng Zhao arrived at the main kitchen early and immediately caught a whiff of a strange odor.","In the freezing winter, amidst the steaming hot main kitchen, such a smell was not easy to detect, but she still noticed it.","Cheng Zhao walked a lap around the main kitchen and left immediately.","First Madam, Madam Song, was sitting in Chengming Hall.","Today's reports were delayed by half an hour because the stewards all had to go out and supervise the servants sweeping the snow.","\"...Everything has been arranged properly, Madam,\" Madam Song's confidante, Nanny Liu, walked quietly into Chengming Hall and told her in a low voice.","First Madam took a sip of tea to moisten her throat and said after a long while, \"That is very good. Hurry and get rid of that person. She sits there all day without making a sound, playing deaf no matter how much I scold her, staring at me like a venomous snake. She is truly difficult to deal with.\"","Nanny Liu nodded.","Cheng Zhao was indeed very skilled at using the underhanded tactics typical of girls from scholarly families.","Furthermore, her self-restraint was formidable; her temper was like damp firewood—impossible to ignite, only leaving the person trying to do so full of frustration.","The methods First Madam used against the Second Madam had absolutely no effect on Cheng Zhao.","Having dominated Chengming Hall for over a decade, First Madam subconsciously felt that everything would be hers in the future, and she would be the ultimate matriarch of the Zhou family.","Cheng Zhao was an invader.","How could anyone like a wild beast that invaded their territory?","With dissatisfaction and a sense of crisis coexisting, she naturally had to clear her out as early as possible.","\"How has Lady Huan offended Dowager Madame these past few days?\" First Madam, Madam Song, took another sip of tea.","Dowager Madame had called Lady Huan to Shou'an Courtyard these past few days, asking her to lead people in helping sort Buddhist beans, which were to be donated to Jin'an Temple during the New Year.","This task was extremely time-consuming and tedious. Unless one was a devout Buddhist, it felt like torture.","Huan Qingtang had already been going there for several days.","This had never happened before.","Huan Qingtang was First Madam, Madam Song's, capable assistant. While she didn't harbor any hypocritical mother-daughter affection for her daughter-in-law, she ultimately still viewed her as a trusted confidante.","She was very protective of her own confidantes.","Therefore, by suppressing Cheng Zhao, she could divert Dowager Madame's anger and conveniently kick Cheng Zhao out of the main kitchen.","\"First Madam, do you need this old servant to go and ask around for you?\" Nanny Liu asked her.","First Madam waved her hand. \"Forget it. Lady Huan is of the younger generation; let Dowager Madame punish her to vent her anger. It's better than the old lady holding it all in for the New Year, which would make everyone miserable.\"","She added, \"Go back and keep an eye on the porridge shed. Don't let that Cheng woman pull any tricks.\"","Nanny Liu complied.","Cheng Zhao came out of the main kitchen and whispered a few words to Suyue.","Suyue, having great tacit understanding with her, went to do it immediately without the slightest hesitation.","The porridge still needed to boil for a while longer, so Cheng Zhao went to Shou'an Courtyard.","When she entered, several stewards from the outer courtyard were standing respectfully before Dowager Madame in Shou'an Courtyard.","One of them was the head steward. Cheng Zhao knew him; his wife managed the storehouse of Shou'an Courtyard—a slightly plump woman with an amiable smile.","The servants secretly called the couple \"smiling tigers.\"","\"Third Young Madam,\" everyone addressed Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao nodded slightly.","Dowager Madame sat in the main seat, smiling. \"Why have you come?\"","\"Grandmother, the snow was too heavy yesterday, and it doesn't look like it will stop today. Eldest Aunt asked me to distribute charity porridge,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Dowager Madame replied, \"You come from a prestigious family in Wu Commandery. You can handle such a small matter well. Your Eldest Aunt has a good eye for people.\"","Cheng Zhao smiled brightly. \"With Grandmother trusting me, I absolutely dare not mess things up. I checked the almanac early this morning, and today is the birthday of the Goddess of Plum Blossoms.\"","Dowager Madame was slightly surprised. \"Is that so?\"","\"Starting from this hour, the Goddess of Plum Blossoms descends to the mortal realm and will not return until the Beginning of Spring. On such a grand day, I thought that since Grandmother is a devout Buddhist, perhaps you would prefer to do some good deeds with your own hands?\" Cheng Zhao said.","Dowager Madame pondered.","She cast a quiet glance at Cheng Zhao, her expression unreadable.","Cheng Zhao added, \"I'm not asking Grandmother to go out and distribute porridge. How could you withstand such cold weather? You just need to go to the main kitchen and stir the large porridge pot. I've already sent someone out to spread the word that today, the Dowager Madame of the Duke's Mansion is personally making offerings to the Goddess of Plum Blossoms by doing good deeds.\"","Dowager Madame's gaze instantly sharpened.","Cheng Zhao met her gaze, her clear eyes blinking, looking very innocent.","\"Our Zhou family is used to keeping a low profile. From now on, you must not spread such words and cause such a commotion,\" Dowager Madame said.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"Yes, I will remember Grandmother's teachings.\"","Dowager Madame said, \"Go and keep an eye on the porridge shed first.\"","Just as she finished speaking, the steward from the gatehouse rushed hurriedly into Shou'an Courtyard.","\"Dowager Madame, word has spread outside that you are honoring the Goddess of Plum Blossoms today. The Dowager Consort of the Rong Prince's Mansion has sent some incense, candles, and modest gifts.\"","Dowager Madame slightly clenched her fingers, though a smile still floated on her face. \"We have lived next to the Rong Prince's Mansion for so many years. Whenever there is an event, the Dowager Consort is always the first to show support.\"","She stood up with a smile. \"Send someone to deliver a return gift of thanks to the Dowager Consort.\"","Only then did she look at Cheng Zhao. \"Let's go. We'll head to the main kitchen to take a look. It's been many years since I last boiled porridge.\"","Cheng Zhao complied.","Huan Qingtang walked out from the side room. She had heard everything Cheng Zhao just said.","She smiled and exchanged greetings with Cheng Zhao before saying, \"I shall also accompany Grandmother to the main kitchen.\"","She then ordered the managing women, \"Prepare a soft palanquin.\"","As Dowager Madame set off from here, Huan Qingtang's senior maid immediately went to deliver a message to Chengming Hall.","First Madam, Madam Song, was reviewing the recent invitations from the gatehouse, preparing which ones to reply to and what gifts to send, when she suddenly heard Huan Qingtang's senior maid report that Dowager Madame had gone to the main kitchen.","She was struck as if by lightning.","\"How, how did this trouble Dowager Madame?\" Madam Song stood up, her face pale with shock.","Seeing this, the senior maid smiled and said, \"You should go over and take a look too. We wouldn't want Dowager Madame to lack people serving her.\"","It was a hint for her to hurry over and quickly put away any tricks she had planned.","If this blew up, Dowager Madame would show no mercy.","First Madam, Madam Song, hurriedly ordered a maid to fetch her wooden clogs. The snowy ground outside was hard to walk on, so she needed to put on the clogs to go to the main kitchen.","She walked extremely fast, almost slipping several times, desperately trying to get there ahead of Dowager Madame.","However, Dowager Madame's group had already set off long ago. By the time she arrived, Nanny Liu from the main kitchen was already kneeling on the ground.","First Madam Song's vision went dark and her legs grew slightly weak. She only managed to steady herself by holding onto her maid's hand."]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25: Announcing Victory","paragraphs":["The atmosphere in the main kitchen was stagnant, with only the billowing steam rising from the pots.","Everyone trembled in fear.","Dowager Madame did not fly into a rage; she merely instructed indifferently, \"Drag her out, give her thirty blows with the board, and kick her out of the ducal mansion.\"","The manager, Nanny Liu, kowtowed incessantly, \"Dowager Madame, please spare my life! Please give this servant one more chance. This servant was audacious, but I will never dare do it again!\"","First Madam, Madam Song, seemed barely able to stand steady.","After she entered, both Dowager Madame and Huan Qingtang glanced back at her. Taking advantage of Dowager Madame's inattention, Huan Qingtang gave First Madam, Madam Song, an imperceptible shake of her head.","Madam Song turned pale.","\"For the rice used for charity, even if you used stale rice, it might still be forgivable, but you actually used moldy, rotten rice.","If anyone died from eating it, the entire ducal mansion would be held accountable. At best, the Duke would be fined and imprisoned; at worst, our titles would be stripped and our estate confiscated.","Are you trying to kill the entire ducal mansion? Fortunately, the Duchess was sharp and saw through your wicked tricks. And you still have the nerve to beg for mercy? Drag her away,\" Dowager Madame said.","She spoke very slowly, her tone never rising.","Yet every word carried weight, pressing heavily on everyone's hearts.","She made the dangers of this matter crystal clear, preventing the servants from thinking it was a trivial matter and leaving them with the impression that Dowager Madame was harsh and heartless.","Based on Dowager Madame's explanation of the severe consequences this could have brought, expelling Nanny Liu and giving her thirty blows with the board was already extremely lenient of the ducal mansion.","At the same time, she pushed Cheng Zhao to the forefront.","If any of Nanny Liu's cronies felt dissatisfied, the one they would hold a grudge against would not be Dowager Madame, but Cheng Zhao, who had reported the matter.","The majesty, benevolent tolerance, and fairness of a superior—Dowager Madame displayed every single one of them without fail.","Cheng Zhao stood to the side, her head slightly bowed, remaining silent.","Two rough-work older maidservants stepped forward, gagged Nanny Liu, and dragged her away.","After Dowager Madame finished handling the matter, she ignored First Madam, Madam Song, and instead said to Cheng Zhao, \"The Duchess has done very well, saving us from a great disaster.","I will reward you handsomely. Later, I will have fifty taels of gold leaves brought to you from my storehouse, so you can use them to reward others during the New Year.\"","Cheng Zhao immediately replied, \"Thank you, Grandmother.\"","Although she had been pushed into the eye of the storm and would attract the resentment of some, it also genuinely established her authority.","Elders like Dowager Madame needed to be benevolent; while young, newly-wed daughters-in-law like Cheng Zhao needed authority.","As for resentment, the truth was that even if the vast majority of people in this mansion resented Cheng Zhao, it would not be a great loss to her.","Cheng Zhao could not have both a good reputation and actual power unless Dowager Madame was willing to prop her up. When she could only choose one of the two, she chose the latter.","\"...The new rice has been swapped in, Grandmother,\" Cheng Zhao said to Dowager Madame. \"The pots have also been washed clean. We trouble Grandmother to personally add the rice.\"","Dowager Madame wanted to say something, but Cheng Zhao continued loudly, \"I have checked the storehouse repeatedly, and there is no moldy rice.","Please rest assured, in a household like ours, unless someone is intentionally causing trouble, we would never keep moldy rice in the storehouse. Even the mice in the storehouse are raised to be plump and fat.\"","Dowager Madame could not help but chuckle.","When she laughed, someone nearby immediately played along, chiming in with a few joking remarks.","This person was Dowager Madame's confidante and the sister-in-law of the chief steward. Originally, Dowager Madame had wanted her to take over the main kitchen, but First Madam, Madam Song, had disagreed and sent Nanny Liu to compete for the position.","A few others also echoed the sentiment.","The underlying implication of their words was that Nanny Liu had procured poisonous rice from elsewhere to frame the entire ducal mansion.","First Madam, Madam Song, also vainly attempted to interject a few words, but was interrupted by Cheng Zhao. She stood awkwardly on the spot, wishing she could tear Cheng Zhao to pieces.","After the new rice was put into the pot, Dowager Madame waited for the water to boil, stirred the rice porridge a few times, instructed Cheng Zhao to boil the porridge a bit thicker and not be too stingy, and then left the main kitchen.","First Madam followed suit, personally escorting Dowager Madame back to the Shou'an Courtyard, no longer able to care about her trusted aide, Nanny Liu.","For the rest of the morning, Cheng Zhao stayed in the main kitchen, accompanied by Nanny Li; her maids, Suyue and Qiubai, kept an eye on the porridge stall at the back gate.","There were many people lining up to receive porridge.","This incident quickly spread throughout the inner quarters of the ducal mansion; everyone everywhere heard about it.","Dozens of pots of porridge were distributed that day.","Cheng Zhao casually ate a little food in the main kitchen and was busy until mid-afternoon.","When she returned to the Nonghua Courtyard, Second Madam had arrived.","Cheng Zhao smiled and said, \"Why did you come over, Mother? You just needed to call for me.\"","\"You have been busy all day, how could I make you run around again?\" Second Madam said. \"Go quickly and change your clothes, and then tell me what happened.\"","Cheng Zhao finally revealed a genuine smile for the first time that day. \"Alright, Mother, please sit for a moment.\"","She instructed the maids to serve fresh tea to Second Madam, bringing out her best tea leaves and pastries to entertain her, before going to change her clothes.","After removing her hairpins and taking off her thick outer garments, Cheng Zhao finally went to sit down in the eastern side room.","Second Madam remarked to her, \"Doesn't your neck get tired wearing a whole head full of hairpins and ornaments normally? Although they do look quite pretty.\"","Second Madam's own attire was always very simple and capable.","Cheng Zhao smiled. \"I have been used to it since childhood. When I was little, heavy objects were pressed into my hair buns; when wearing long earrings, the earrings must not hit the face while walking.\"","Second Madam clicked her tongue. \"You suffered a lot in your maiden home.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","\"I am not saying your mother abused you, but in a prestigious family like yours, there are simply too many rules,\" Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao understood her meaning and smiled. \"Mother, that is because the aristocratic families and even the imperial clan in the capital all use this set of rules. Only by conforming to it can one earn respect; families that deviate from the norm cannot last long.\"","\"You don't hate it?\"","\"I'm alright with it,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","Since she was young, she had been full of energy and very active; she had to find a balance between strict etiquette and her true self.","Especially during the three years her father was posted outside the capital, when only she and her fourth brother accompanied their parents, she played around with absolute lawlessness.","Her mother was very afraid that she would not be able to adapt upon returning to the capital, that she would turn into a wild child and suffer from disparagement. Therefore, her mother suppressed her strictly, forbidding her from attending any of the Cheng family's banquets.","The madams of the aristocratic families did not know her, and she had no reputation to speak of. Consequently, after she reached her coming of age, not many prominent families came to propose marriage.","However, Cheng Zhao adapted very well.","Her two older sisters always said she was smart and knew how to please others. Even if she was rebellious in her bones, she did enough on the surface so that no one could pick out any faults.","Compared to Cheng Zhao, Second Madam suffered because she was not good at keeping up appearances, putting her true temperament right out in the open.","\"...Weren't you asking about the main kitchen, Mother?\" Cheng Zhao steered the topic back.","Second Madam sat up a bit straighter. \"I heard Nanny Liu was beaten and kicked out?\"","That Nanny Liu was part of First Madam, Madam Song's dowry and had managed the main kitchen for quite a few years.","\"Yes. Grandmother personally gave the order. If she had not spoken, how would I dare touch Eldest Aunt's person?\" Cheng Zhao said.","She recounted the incident to Second Madam in detail.","First Madam was distributing porridge but had prepared a sack of moldy, toxic rice. Of course, she wasn't going to actually distribute it; rather, she wanted to use it as a handle against Cheng Zhao, taking the opportunity to find fault and kick her out.","Who knew that Cheng Zhao would keep such a close watch.","Watching that sack of rice go into the pot, she went and invited Dowager Madame over.","She even enthusiastically invited Dowager Madame to taste the pot of porridge.","Once boiled, the porridge seemed to have nothing wrong with it. But that was Dowager Madame—who would dare let any mishap befall her? When Dowager Madame wanted to taste it, the manager, Nanny Liu, was scared out of her wits.","\"It was merely a psychological game. Nanny Liu broke under the pressure and was so terrified that she knelt down to stop Dowager Madame. In truth, after being boiled, the toxicity of the poisoned rice was quite limited,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam: \"...\""]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26: Look at Someone in a New Light","paragraphs":["Second Madam really wanted to rush to Chengming Hall and confront First Madam.","She wanted to have a huge fight with First Madam.","As an elder and the mistress managing the Duke's estate, wasn't it too despicable for her to use such underhanded methods to frame a junior?","Cheng Zhao stopped Second Madam.","\"Mother, we are in the right this time. If you make a scene, the focus will shift from the main kitchen to you. By then, even with reason on your side, you'll lose the high ground, and we'll be the ones suffering a loss again,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"How can I swallow this anger?\" Second Madam said furiously. \"How does your managing the main kitchen get in her way? You are the Duchess now. To think she would be so malicious.\"","With the slightest misstep, Cheng Zhao would not only be despised by Dowager Madame and slandered by the servants, but could even be involved in a deadly lawsuit.","This was a sin!","A person could be unkind, but to go to such lengths was truly enough to incur the wrath of both men and gods.","\"Mother, if you can't swallow this anger, why not go horseback riding and relax? The next time you see Eldest Aunt, you must be smiling. Unless you never want to live in Chengming Hall,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam was speechless.","\"Even at the border, one wouldn't wage a full-scale war over a single skirmish. When war breaks out, the goal is to conquer cities and seize territory. If you aren't fully prepared, you shouldn't tear away all pretenses on the surface,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam took several deep breaths.","Still feeling indignant, she left in a huff.","Nanny Li was somewhat worried. \"Second Madam won't actually go make a scene, will she? We finally managed to gain the upper hand.\"","Cheng Zhao thought for a moment. \"I think I managed to persuade her.\"","She added, \"My mother-in-law is actually quite easy to get along with, it's just that her temperament is too straightforward.\"","Such a blunt personality was not very suitable for living in the inner courts of any noble household.","She should have gone with Second Master to his official post. Being the wife of a local magistrate in another region, the female family members of such a small place would curry favor with her. Even if she was straightforward, no one would dare say anything, and she could live freely.","Unfortunately, they didn't choose that path.","Second Madam probably did it for the children.","The brothers Zhou Yuanshen and Zhou Yuanqi had clearly received the very orthodox scholarly upbringing of the Duke's estate.","Even though Zhou Yuanshen had been in the military for years, he could still play the part of a noble young master and quickly conceal his martial aura upon returning to the capital. He must have received this kind of education for a long time.","Cheng Zhao thus deduced that Second Madam had always known what kind of personality and temperament was acceptable among the upper-class nobility in the capital.","Of course, knowing is one thing, but being able to do it is another.","Sometimes when First Madam provoked her, she really couldn't handle her momentary impulses, which was why she repeatedly exposed her true nature.","Straightforwardness was in her bones, making it very difficult to change.","She wasn't brainless or ignorant.","Cheng Zhao sometimes felt that she herself was just a bit cunning, knowing better than others how to use tactics, and mimicking whatever she learned quite well, but in her bones, she shared the same aloof pride as Second Madam.","She really admired Second Madam.","Kind and straightforward people, no matter how many flaws they had, earned Cheng Zhao's respect.","Sure enough, Second Madam endured this matter and didn't go to make a scene at Chengming Hall.","Second Master praised her, seemingly joking, \"You've learned some shrewdness. This daughter-in-law of ours is a formidable female teacher; she can actually teach you.\"","Second Madam replied, \"She's better at teaching than you. You can talk for ages without getting to the point.\"","\"My son isn't as good as your daughter-in-law, and now I'm not as good as her either?\"","\"No one can compare to her!\" Second Madam said.","Her daughter-in-law had good looks, a good brain, and was clever and capable. Just looking at her made Second Madam feel comfortable.","For several days in a row, the Chen Duke's estate was buzzing about this matter.","First Madam was still managing the household, so the servants didn't dare discuss her casually, but they inevitably gossiped in secret. After all, Nanny Liu from the main kitchen had been beaten and driven away; such news couldn't be hidden.","The replacement of a major steward involved many minor stewards and other menial servants.","The beating had been carried out publicly in the outer courtyard.","Since this had happened, naturally everyone from top to bottom wanted to know what exactly had happened to Nanny Liu.","\"She used poisoned rice to cook charity porridge and was caught by the Third Young Madam.\"","\"That day, Dowager Madame happened to be preparing to do some good deeds and saw it with her own eyes. Nanny Liu was so scared she confessed honestly. She even dragged First Madam down with her.\"","\"I heard that First Madam has gone to Shou'an Courtyard to pay her respects these past few days, but has been turned away every time.\"","The servants didn't dare speak too harshly of First Madam, Madam Song; they only said Nanny Liu had committed a sin.","Of course, anyone with clear eyes knew what was really going on.","Second Madam's people asked around for news. Seeing First Madam suffer a setback made Second Madam very happy; she was cheerful every day and barely got angry anymore.","Hearing that First Madam was blocked at Shou'an Courtyard, Second Madam couldn't quite believe it, so she took a small carriage to Shou'an Courtyard early in the morning to pay her respects.","Sure enough, she saw First Madam standing in the courtyard.","Dowager Madame hadn't blocked her outside the courtyard—that would look like an evil mother-in-law tormenting her daughter-in-law—but she didn't let her enter the main hall either, simply leaving her to stand in the courtyard.","When Second Madam saw this, she was itching to go up and gloat with a few words.","Remembering Cheng Zhao's warning, she forcefully held herself back.","\"...My daughter-in-law's small kitchen stewed some beef soup. There is a thick kind meant for dinner, which I'll bring to you next time, Mother; this kind is light and nourishing, perfect for a bowl at breakfast to keep your body warm all day,\" Second Madam said.","Dowager Madame glanced at her.","She said pointedly, \"Second daughter-in-law, you've improved.\"","The meaning of this sentence was unclear.","Second Madam caught a hint of it, but she couldn't be bothered to figure it out: \"Being filial to my mother-in-law is what a daughter-in-law should do. It was only after becoming a mother-in-law myself that I understood many principles.\"","Dowager Madame lost interest. \"It's good that you understand. In all our years as mother-in-law and daughter-in-law, I've had to endure so many of your complaints.\"","Second Madam was speechless.","I've complained my whole life, and you haven't changed one bit. In the end, I'm the one suffering. Who is enduring whom exactly?","Second Madam held back again and again, not talking back.","After delivering the soup, she left Shou'an Courtyard.","Dowager Madame said to her trusted aide, \"She even knew to find an excuse when coming to watch a spectacle. The second daughter-in-law has indeed improved greatly. Has that Duchess from the second branch become incredibly resourceful?\"","She looked at Cheng Zhao in a new light.","Regarding the poisoned rice in the main kitchen, Dowager Madame thought about Cheng Zhao's handling of it afterward and concluded there was no method more suitable than hers.","If Cheng Zhao had brought the poisoned rice to complain, Nanny Liu might have found an excuse and perhaps even turned around to falsely accuse her.","Cheng Zhao wasn't very familiar with the main kitchen yet. If Nanny Liu had time to prepare and struck first with a false accusation, Cheng Zhao might not have been able to take her down.","Then, according to Dowager Madame's temper, whoever was in charge of the task would bear the consequences, so Cheng Zhao would have been punished no matter what.","First Madam, Madam Song, had targeted Cheng Zhao precisely because she saw this point.","Unexpectedly, they had underestimated Cheng Zhao.","\"...How much land does the Cheng family own?\" Dowager Madame suddenly asked her aide. \"The Cheng family has no noble title, though they are known as a prominent family of Wu Commandery. But how much wealth do they actually have?\"","The aide was taken aback. \"The Cheng family was a prestigious clan even in the previous dynasty. They supported the late Emperor, so their family assets didn't suffer much loss. Chancellor Cheng has served as an official for three reigns and is an old, crafty fox; the Cheng family is never seen flaunting their wealth. Outsiders aren't quite clear on exactly how much land they have.\"","She then asked Dowager Madame, \"Why do you bring this up?\"","\"Cheng's insight is deeper than I imagined. She is still so young; if the Cheng family didn't have substantial resources, how could they have raised someone like her?\" Dowager Madame said."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27: When a melon is ripe, it falls off the vine.","paragraphs":["The Dowager Madame was in a fairly good mood.","She never placed high hopes on anyone.","Whether they were her children, daughters-in-law, or managers, they were all her servants.","She always had more than one servant.","They did things for her.","When pleased, she would reward them heavily; when displeased, she would punish them severely. If anyone tried to ruin her good days or leak her secrets, she could also be ruthless enough to kill.","The First Madame, Madam Song, had some brains but no great wisdom. In recent years, she had become increasingly pampered and arrogant, going a bit too far.","Taking advantage of Cheng Zhao's hand to deal with the main kitchen's affairs also served as a warning to the First Madame, Madam Song. The Dowager Madame was quite satisfied with Cheng Zhao.","Nanny Liu of the main kitchen was quite skilled at winning people over and deceiving her superiors while hiding things from her subordinates. To deal with her, strong evidence was needed.","It had to be convincing so as not to chill the hearts of the other managers.","The inner courtyard always needed people to get things done. Every decree from the Dowager Madame had to be justified.","She sent Cheng Zhao to manage the main kitchen because Cheng Zhao had received the imperial mandate of the Duchess. Having her manage it made this decree viable.","At the time, the Dowager Madame was still considering her next move, but she hadn't expected Madam Song and Nanny Liu to underestimate their enemy so much, handing a great opportunity right into the Dowager Madame's hands.","The Dowager Madame said unhurriedly, \"I have lived a lifetime and seen that every fruit first blossoms, then slowly sets and ripens.","If you rush to eat the fruit, it will be sour and bitter. You must wait. Bide your time, and the fruit will naturally fall into your hands.\"","Using Cheng Zhao had yielded such miraculous results, and the Dowager Madame was satisfied.","She had an excuse to punish the First Madame, Madam Song, telling her to restrain herself so she wouldn't become so indulgent that she forgot the hierarchy.","Huan Qingtang was in the Shou'an Courtyard, helping the Dowager Madame manage the year-end rents sent from the farming estates.","She suddenly felt a chill of fear.","Outside, it was said that the Chen Duke's estate owned over two hundred thousand mu of land.","But judging from these rents, it was far more than that!","Now that Huan Qingtang knew these secrets, how could she guarantee to the Dowager Madame that she would never speak out of turn? Or rather, how could she convince herself to yield the Chengming Hall to Cheng Zhao in the future?","\"Perhaps this is Grandmother's idea. She wants me to agree to a dual-lineage marriage with the Duke.\"","Huan Qingtang closed her eyes slightly to soothe her inner emotions.","Sometimes, fate pushes everyone into their rightful places.","Huan Qingtang prepared to have a chat with Zhou Yuanshen.","She knew Zhou Yuanshen kept his distance from her, simply because they had been set up for a matchmaking meeting in the past.","Neither had fancied the other.","The Huan family mainly didn't like the Second Madame, believing such a mother-in-law would be difficult to get along with. The Chen Duke's estate was illustrious, but Zhou Yuanshen was not a son of the first branch; when the family eventually divided, he would become a collateral branch with little weight.","That time, using the birthday banquet at Princess Qing'an's residence, the two sides had a very simple meeting. It wasn't very formal.","It was Princess Qing'an who insisted on playing matchmaker on a whim.","The Second Madame probably thought Huan Qingtang was beautiful, and the Huan family admired the power of the Chen Duke's estate. Furthermore, neither family dared to offend Princess Qing'an, so they verbally agreed to the meeting.","Later, Huan Qingtang's matchmaking meeting with the eldest grandson of the Duke's estate was very formal: the Dowager Madame first invited a matchmaker to sound them out, and then they arranged to meet at a temple, which the Dowager Madame attended in person.","The meeting with Zhou Yuanshen was originally never mentioned by anyone. It was a noble young lady who was jealous of Huan Qingtang; she had also been at Princess Qing'an's banquet, spied on the secret, and spread it everywhere.","By the time this secret spread, Huan Qingtang had already set a wedding date with the eldest grandson of the Chen Duke's estate.","Fortunately, her mother-in-law and husband didn't believe these rumors. The Dowager Madame also said, \"It is common for those of noble character to be envied by the mediocre,\" never mentioning the matter and strictly forbidding the servants from discussing it.","The only one who brooded over it was probably the Second Madame.","Huan Qingtang felt fortunate countless times that she hadn't become the Second Madame's daughter-in-law.","The Second Madame's personality was like a wild horse. How could a noble lady from a scholarly family know how to tame a horse? The Second Madame charged about recklessly, and Huan Qingtang was truly a bit afraid of her.","But in the end, her husband passed away, and she still had to marry Zhou Yuanshen. The Second Madame would still be her mother-in-law.","The hand of fate always pushed misplaced people into the positions that belonged to them, even if it delayed time and the path was winding.","Huan Qingtang sighed.","She also thought of Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao handled this recent matter quite beautifully. Fortunately, she didn't have the Second Madame's reckless personality.","Huan Qingtang had been dealing with women of Cheng Zhao's temperament since childhood, so she was confident she could handle Cheng Zhao.","The only issue was Zhou Yuanshen. At the very least, she needed to give him a heads-up and explain the events of that year again in advance—even though he had never mentioned that meeting.","Cheng Zhao sat in the Nonghua Courtyard, counting gold leaves.","Her senior maid, Suyue, was very straightforward: \"Only fifty taels of gold leaves. The Dowager Madame is a bit stingy.\"","Cheng Zhao couldn't help but laugh. \"What a big tone you have!\"","Fifty taels of gold, in anyone's hands, was a considerable fortune.","Cheng Zhao certainly didn't disdain it.","Gold leaves were very thin. Fifty taels of gold could be beaten into a full box. Using them to reward people during festivals was both generous and presentable, and they could last a long time.","\"This servant was hoping she would give a hundred taels,\" Suyue said.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"The Dowager Madame's money doesn't just appear out of thin air. Other than you, no one would call her stingy.\"","Nanny Li then scolded Suyue, \"You girl, with your big ambitions and empty eyes, you need to change that.\"","Suyue stuck out her tongue.","Making everyone laugh.","Cheng Zhao handed the money box to Nanny Li and breathed a soft sigh of relief. \"My first assignment is finally secured.\"","A minor matter in the main kitchen had not only established her authority but also vented anger on behalf of her mother-in-law, and she even received fifty taels of gold leaves. Cheng Zhao believed she had achieved good results.","From now on, she would still have a place of influence in the main kitchen.","As Cheng Zhao slowly took root in the Chen Duke's estate, her title as the Duchess would carry more weight.","She had been in a good mood these past two days.","With the matter settled and her monthly time over, Cheng Zhao felt completely relaxed.","Just as she was planning to go out with her maids Qiubai and Suyue to check on her dowry shops and meet the head manager in charge of her dowry, Zhou Yuanshen sent someone to the Nonghua Courtyard.","\"The Duke said he will come to the Nonghua Courtyard for dinner tonight,\" the maid said.","This was an unfamiliar maid.","She was very pretty and delicate, tall and slender.","Nanny Li acknowledged it, invited her to sit down, and asked for her name and where she worked.","The maid's name was Mingyu, and she served in the outer study.","Hearing that Zhou Yuanshen was coming, Cheng Zhao's face turned quite ugly.","She returned to the inner bedroom and spent a long while trying to compose her emotions, but still felt a wave of frustration.","Thinking of this, Cheng Zhao suddenly said, \"Make sour radish duck soup again. I'm going to the Jiangyun Courtyard for dinner tonight.\"","She added, \"Tell the Duke to go to the Jiangyun Courtyard for dinner as well.\"","Nanny Li was shocked. \"How can you...\"","Her belly hadn't shown any signs of pregnancy yet, and the internal situation of the Zhou family was so complicated. How could she avoid the Duke at a time like this?","\"We haven't had dinner with my parents-in-law yet. Can't we show some filial piety? My second brother and sister-in-law occasionally accompany my parents for meals too,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She didn't intend to fall out with Zhou Yuanshen.","On such a happy day, she simply didn't want to spoil the mood.","She would just be willful this one time."]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28: A Secret Rendezvous with the Elder Sister-in-Law","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao sent a maid to Chenghui Courtyard.","Zhou Yuanshen had returned to the mansion and settled in Chenghui Courtyard. Cheng Zhao told the maid to inform him to come over earlier in the afternoon.","However, the maid was gone for a long time.","Waiting and waiting, the sour radish duck soup was ready before the maid finally returned.","This was a young maid who was usually quite playful. Suyue couldn't help but scold her, \"It took you half a day to come back. Did you go ghost hunting on the way?\"","The young maid felt a bit wronged. \"No, it's just that I didn't see the Duke.\"","Cheng Zhao called her over and asked what happened.","\"...Nanfeng wouldn't let this servant in, saying the Duke was resting. This servant said she could wait a bit, but Nanfeng strongly urged this servant to return first, saying he would pass on the message.","This servant felt something was strange about this matter, so she avoided Nanfeng and waited in the corner for half a day. Young Madame, guess what this servant saw?\"","Suyue was almost ready to curse her. \"You were told to report back, and you're keeping us in suspense? Speak up!\"","\"This servant saw the Eldest Young Madame coming out of Chenghui Courtyard. Just her alone!\" the young maid said.","She added, \"Even someone with our Young Madame's decisive personality is always accompanied by someone when she goes out.\"","Suyue, \"...\"","Nanny Li then said to the young maid, \"You did very well. No one spotted you, right?\"","\"Probably not. This servant waited until Nanfeng closed the courtyard gate before hurrying back,\" the young maid said.","Nanny Li grabbed a handful of candies for the young maid and told her to leave.","Cheng Zhao sat there, slowly combing her hair.","Nanny Li, Suyue, and Qiubai all wanted to comfort her.","The matter of serving two branches of the family hadn't spread yet; only a very few people knew about it.","And Cheng Zhao was one of the insiders.","\"Young Madame, you see...\"","\"I can tolerate others,\" Cheng Zhao interrupted Nanny Li. \"Is the soup ready? I'll go to Jiangyun Courtyard first. When the Duke arrives, tell him.\"","Nanny Li agreed.","Arriving at Jiangyun Courtyard, she saw Second Madam teaching Zhou Yuanqi how to hold a spear.","Zhou Yuanqi was holding a short spear, specially made for children to practice with. Looking at his stance, his lips pouted enough to hang a gourd; he was very unwilling to practice.","Seeing him frustrated, Cheng Zhao found it a bit funny.","\"I don't want to practice,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam, \"If you don't want to practice, you'll take ten lashes. This is what you lost to me.\"","\"If you dare hit me, I'll go tell maternal grandmother.\"","\"Complain and you'll get twenty lashes when you come back,\" Second Madam said.","Zhou Yuanqi's eyes widened. \"You're bullying a child!\"","\"Now you know you're a child? You always say you're an adult,\" Second Madam said.","Zhou Yuanqi, \"...\"","Cheng Zhao couldn't help but laugh out loud.","Zhou Yuanqi turned to her, even more displeased.","Cheng Zhao stepped forward, a maid carrying a food box. She smiled at Zhou Yuanqi, \"I brought sour radish duck soup.\"","Zhou Yuanqi gulped.","He was a bit more polite to Cheng Zhao.","\"Let me see your spear,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi handed it to Cheng Zhao.","\"A specially made crow-neck spear? Is this suitable for children to practice with? I thought everyone started with a plain spear,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi looked at her in surprise.","Second Madam was both surprised and delighted. \"You know about spears?\"","Thinking back to the second day of her marriage, when her maids used short crossbows, Second Madam suddenly realized that short crossbows couldn't be bought on the market.","Buying and selling short crossbows was illegal.","Cheng Zhao must have had a very legitimate channel to get these things.","\"My eldest brother-in-law is a military officer,\" Cheng Zhao smiled. \"He's stationed in the South Sea, specifically dealing with pirates.\"","Second Madam remembered a very famous military officer who seemed to be in the South Sea.","He was also a disciple of the Fan family.","Second Madam remembered there was such a person, but right when she wanted to say his name, she couldn't remember it; the more she wanted to say it, the more she couldn't.","Just as she was about to ask what Cheng Zhao's eldest brother-in-law's name was, Zhou Yuanqi spoke up. \"If I give you the crow-neck spear to play with, do you know how?\"","\"If I know how, what reward will you give me?\" Cheng Zhao asked with a smile.","Zhou Yuanqi, \"I'll give you a copybook.\"","\"What copybook?\"","\"Mr. Qu Lian's copybook,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao, \"Then what you've collected is definitely a fake. All twenty-four of Mr. Qu Lian's copybooks passed down in the world are in the Cheng family of Wu Commandery.\"","Zhou Yuanqi's eyes widened even more.","Saying he couldn't play with a spear didn't bother him much; saying the copybooks he treasured were fake made him unyielding.","He sneered, imitating an adult. \"You're too arrogant! The ones in your family are the fakes. The four I have are all genuine.\"","\"I'll teach you how to tell genuine from fake later,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","Zhou Yuanqi's face turned red. \"You, simply don't know what you're talking about, you wait!\"","She'd teach him!","He actually needed her to teach him!","Zhou Yuanqi turned and ran out, determined to bring his copybooks over to prove his innocence, not even caring about drinking the sour radish duck soup.","Watching him run far away, Second Madam didn't even care to ask about Cheng Zhao's eldest brother-in-law and hurriedly shouted, \"You come back here, today's two hours have just begun. Don't even think about slacking off.\"","Cheng Zhao then said, \"Mother, he clearly doesn't want to learn.\"","\"I know. But look at his skinny arms and legs; if he doesn't practice more, a gust of wind could blow him away in the future,\" Second Madam said.","She added, \"Studying and writing are just as hard; without a good physique, it's hard to achieve greatness. Ah Shen's handwriting is good, everyone praises it, isn't it because he played with spears since he was little?\"","Cheng Zhao nodded. \"Mother's reasoning is also correct. When we practiced writing since we were little, we had to hang sandbags on our wrists.\"","\"Compared to the wrist strength developed from holding a spear, the weight of a sandbag on the wrist is truly child's play, which is why I urge him to practice the spear properly,\" Second Madam said.","She also said Zhou Yuanqi was being squeamish. \"When Ah Shen was his age, he could already hold a plain spear. He's still playing with wooden sticks.\"","Cheng Zhao laughed out loud.","Her daughter-in-law was truly too beautiful; when she smiled, it was like a blooming peony. Second Madam's mood brightened by thirty percent just looking at her.","\"You seem to know how to play with a spear too?\"","\"A little bit.\"","\"Want to spar?\" Second Madam asked.","It was just a casual question, making conversation before turning to go back.","Unexpectedly, Cheng Zhao actually agreed. \"We'll both use plain spears, Mother, you have to go easy on me.\"","Second Madam, \"...\"","Cheng Zhao asked Second Madam for some ribbons and tied her pant legs tightly in a proper manner. Since her father-in-law hadn't returned yet, it didn't matter how much they fooled around.","She didn't even take off her outer long skirt, unafraid of it being cumbersome.","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law dueled with spears.","Cheng Zhao had quite some skill, which pleasantly surprised Second Madam.","As they sparred, Second Madam discovered after a few moves that she was truly just putting on a show. She had learned, but hadn't practiced hard, so posing looked very intimidating and beautiful.","Second Madam probably liked beautiful things, whether it was appearance or moves.","However, towards the end, Cheng Zhao might have struggled a bit; when she stepped forward, her foot slipped, and she almost ran into Second Madam's spear point herself.","Even if it was a plain spear, this collision would have been enough to make her hurt for half a day.","Second Madam could only quickly lift the spear point.","It didn't hurt her, but it messed up her bun.","\"Oh my!\"","Second Madam saw her hair cascade down like a waterfall, like a length of black silk unfurling. Snow-white skin and black hair, instantly breathtakingly beautiful.","Only then did she exclaim.","Cheng Zhao probably misunderstood, quickly waving her hand. \"It's fine, I felt the bun was going to come loose just now.\"","Glancing out of the corner of her eye, she saw the courtyard gate open, and two people standing at the doorway.","One tall and one short.","The taller one was Zhou Yuanshen.","The shorter one was Zhou Yuanqi.","Night had not yet fallen. A lingering trace of the sunset's afterglow fell upon Cheng Zhao's face, making her eyes shimmer with a captivating light.","Zhou Yuanshen remained silent.","Eight-year-old Zhou Yuanqi, however, spoke up, \"Where did this female ghost come from?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\""]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29: Want to Kick Zhou Yuanshen Out","paragraphs":["Second Master had not yet returned to the manor.","He hadn't sent word that he wouldn't be back for dinner, so everyone sat waiting for him in the flower hall of Jiangyun Courtyard.","Second Madam's maid did Cheng Zhao's hair. There were no extra hair ornaments, just a single jade hairpin to hold it in place.","Cheng Zhao touched it twice, finding it quite interesting. She was even better at doing hair than Nanny Li.","Zhou Yuanqi was currently making a grand speech about why he shouldn't practice the spear.","First, he accused Second Madam of being tyrannical, saying this was wrong and that a mother should be kind and affectionate.","Then he threatened Second Madam, claiming he would not only complain to his maternal grandmother but also to Dowager Madame; furthermore, he would spread Second Madam's bad reputation.","Second Madam merely asked him faintly, \"Are you my son?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"You don't have to be,\" Second Madam said.","Zhou Yuanqi choked with anger. Unable to reason with her, he felt like pulling his hair out.","Cheng Zhao laughed from the sidelines.","Zhou Yuanqi turned his attention to her: \"You wield a spear like a madwoman. If the managing nannies see you, will they ever submit to you in the future?\"","Cheng Zhao smiled and said, \"You should first think about how to deal with those fake calligraphy copybooks of yours.\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\"","The child had his heart pierced twice in one evening, just short of vomiting blood.","He wished he could drop his little old scholar disguise and throw a massive tantrum right in front of Cheng Zhao and Second Madam to regain some face.","Today, he had lost both his dignity and his pride.","When Cheng Zhao taught him how to distinguish between genuine and fake calligraphy copybooks, he unexpectedly discovered that the five thousand taels of silver his maternal grandmother had given him had all been swindled by unscrupulous merchants.","Heartache!","\"Where did you get those copybooks?\" Cheng Zhao asked again.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"Someone gave them to me.\"","\"These look like they were printed by booksellers from Zhouhai; it's the ink they use,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"If that 'someone' spent money on them, you can tell me. I can find someone to ask around for you and see if we can get the money back.\"","\"Really?\" Zhou Yuanqi was surprised.","Then he realized he had almost been tricked by Cheng Zhao into telling the truth. Feigning nonchalance, he waved his hand, \"Forget it.\"","\"Forget it? Such realistic fakes must have cost hundreds of taels of silver, right? Wouldn't it be a pity to just forget it?\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\"","No, he couldn't catch his breath. He was about to die of anger.","Second Madam saw through it and deliberately teased him, \"Maybe more than hundreds of taels. Tell your sister-in-law and ask her to think of a way. The Cheng family is familiar with the booksellers over in Zhouhai.\"","Zhou Yuanqi was about to cry.","He was even angrier.","Fortunately, Second Master returned at this time.","While Second Madam and Cheng Zhao, mother-in-law and daughter-in-law, echoed each other to tease Zhou Yuanqi, Zhou Yuanshen sat to the side, not saying a word.","Cheng Zhao ignored him, and Second Madam also treated him as if he didn't exist.","Since he didn't speak, no one asked him anything.","The sour radish duck soup for dinner finally soothed Zhou Yuanqi's bleeding heart.","He decided to heartily drink two large bowls of soup and throw the matter of buying fake copybooks and losing a huge sum of five thousand taels to the back of his mind.","However, The Brute had come, so there might not be enough soup to go around.","Zhou Yuanqi cast a resentful glance at him, wondering what on earth he was here for.","To act as a door god?","The sour radish duck soup was delicious, and Cheng Zhao felt that today's tasted even better.","Her father-in-law and mother-in-law both praised it; Zhou Yuanqi buried his head in his bowl, expressing his satisfaction and delight; only Zhou Yuanshen very cautiously drank three mouthfuls.","Just three mouthfuls.","He set it aside and didn't touch it again.","By the time dinner ended, he hadn't taken another taste, causing Zhou Yuanqi to glance at his bowl several times.","Zhou Yuanqi was very dissatisfied with such a waste of good food.","But he didn't dare act rashly; The Brute would really hit him.","It would be great if there was no The Brute in the family.","Zhou Yuanqi remembered last time his father was talking with a strategist in the outer study, saying that the First Branch also wanted The Brute, so why not adopt him out to the First Branch?","Anyway, his maternal grandmother was very rich, so Zhou Yuanqi didn't need to spend the Duke's estate's money. The Brute could be anyone's older brother.","An older brother who wouldn't even drink perfectly good duck soup—Zhou Yuanqi didn't want him!","After dinner, Zhou Yuanqi couldn't wait to ask this question: \"Father, when are you going to adopt Third Brother out to the First Branch?\"","Second Madam was stunned.","Second Master desperately winked at Zhou Yuanqi and even kicked him under the table.","Zhou Yuanqi suddenly realized that his mother didn't know yet.","He had to tell his mother.","His mother would definitely be eager to kick The Brute away.","\"...Mother, Grandmother wants to adopt Third Brother into the First Branch,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam's face darkened.","\"Even if there's an adoption, it would be you. You haven't come of age yet. Lord Duke is already an adult. Where is the logic in adopting an adult?\" Cheng Zhao laughed from the side.","Second Madam's face looked terrible: \"What is going on?\"","\"Nothing is going on.\" Zhou Yuanshen, who hadn't opened his mouth all night, finally spoke. \"Just some ridiculous rumors that only a child would take seriously.\"","Second Madam: \"Are you hiding something from me? Hiding it just from us mother and daughter-in-law?\"","Cheng Zhao suddenly felt guilty.","They are only hiding it from you, Mother-in-law. I am aware of it.","\"No,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Second Master remained silent.","That day, when Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen left Jiangyun Courtyard, and Zhou Yuanqi also left, Second Madam interrogated Second Master.","Second Master had no choice but to tell her about the matter.","Second Madam was so angry her eyes turned red.","\"They want to hog all the good things; they are so greedy.\" Second Madam was furious to the extreme, her chest heaving violently, almost bursting into tears.","It wasn't out of sadness, but out of such intense anger that she couldn't control her tears.","Second Master hurriedly rubbed her back to soothe her.","\"Yuanshen hasn't agreed yet,\" Second Master said.","Second Madam: \"Did you agree?\"","Second Master: \"...\"","\"If you dare agree, I won't live with you anymore,\" Second Madam said.","\"Alright, I won't agree,\" Second Master said. \"Yuanshen is grown up; we can't make decisions for him anymore.\"","Second Madam thought for a moment, \"The other children can't either!\"","\"They don't want the other children,\" Second Master said.","\"Does Zhaozhao know?\" Second Madam asked again.","For a moment, Second Master didn't realize who she was talking about.","\"Cheng Shi, of course.\"","Second Master: \"...\"","He paused and said tactfully, \"Perhaps the couple discussed it, or perhaps he didn't tell her. It's not my place to pry into that.\"","\"If she knew, how wronged would she feel?\" Second Madam ached for her. \"They bully me, and then turn around and bully my daughter-in-law.\"","She wished she could march to Shou'an Courtyard and argue it out with Dowager Madame.","Second Master told her not to make a fuss. Once Dowager Madame caught hold of a weakness, Zhou Yuanshen would have to agree just to smooth over the conflict, even if he didn't want to.","They had to stay steady for now.","Second Madam thought of Cheng Zhao's cleverness and decided to swallow her anger.","She had never learned how to endure in her entire life, and she had never gained any benefits either. She might as well learn this skill now and see how it turns out.","When Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen came out of Jiangyun Courtyard, she stood at the door and asked, \"Where will Lord Duke rest tonight?\"","Zhou Yuanshen: \"...Nonghua Courtyard.\"","\"I am not feeling very well today. I'm a bit sore and tired from practicing the spear with Mother, and I ate too much, so I'm afraid I cannot serve you,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen glanced at her.","\"How about I send someone to escort you to Lijing Courtyard?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","That was Mu Jiang's courtyard.","Zhou Yuanshen turned and walked away without saying another word to her.","He headed straight for Nonghua Courtyard.","Cheng Zhao did not chase after him; she followed him back to Nonghua Courtyard at a leisurely pace.","Along the way, she had already sorted out her feelings."]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30: The Showdown in the Bedroom","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen entered Nonghua Courtyard first.","Nanny Li was slightly taken aback. She looked behind him but did not see Cheng Zhao.","She held back her questions, however, and bowed to Zhou Yuanshen.","\"Qiubai, go help the Duke change his clothes,\" Nanny Li instructed.","Qiubai complied.","But Zhou Yuanshen said in a deep voice, \"There is no need.\"","He stopped Qiubai outside the door and went into the inner bedchamber alone.","Cheng Zhao returned a moment later with a young maid. Nanny Li looked at her inquiringly, but Cheng Zhao merely shook her head, signaling Nanny Li not to interfere.","\"The Duke is in the inner bedchamber,\" Nanny Li said.","Cheng Zhao acknowledged this and lifted the curtain to enter the inner chamber.","Zhou Yuanshen had taken off his thick outer coat himself. He sat on the heated kang by the window, fiddling with the Go board.","Seeing him, Cheng Zhao immediately recalled what had happened here that night. Irritation and unease filled her almost instantly.","She involuntarily paused at the doorway.","Zhou Yuanshen raised his eyes.","His gaze was bone-chillingly cold.","Cheng Zhao found it familiar.","When the Dowager Madame was displeased, she had the exact same look.","It was filled with scrutiny, displeasure, and coldness.","But looking closely, Zhou Yuanshen resembled both the Second Madame and the Second Master; he didn't look much like the Dowager Madame. This was because the Second Master hadn't inherited much of the Dowager Madame's looks either.","Cheng Zhao's parents-in-law must have been a stunning couple in their youth. Both possessed excellent features, making the brothers, Zhou Yuanqi and Zhou Yuanshen, very handsome.","While Zhou Yuanshen didn't resemble the Dowager Madame in appearance, his temperament was strikingly similar.","\"Go wash up first. Come back and play a game of Go,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao voiced her agreement.","After washing up, she left her hair down, put on her inner garments, and draped a silver-red short jacket over her shoulders.","By the time she returned from the washroom, Zhou Yuanshen had gone to wash up as well.","She waited for a while, her emotions mostly settling down, before Zhou Yuanshen walked in wearing thin inner garments.","The inner chamber was very warm; the underfloor heating was burning exceptionally strong.","Zhou Yuanshen was probably a little hot, as the collar of his inner robe was slightly open, allowing Cheng Zhao to see a bit of his skin.","Meanwhile, Cheng Zhao was still wearing her short jacket.","Cheng Zhao thought he was thick-skinned and unafraid of the cold, while he probably thought she was overly delicate.","His gaze lingered on her face for a moment before shifting away.","He glanced at her hair.","Cheng Zhao's black hair was cascading down.","Neither spoke again. They played Go in silence, with Zhou Yuanshen taking the white stones this time.","As the game stabilized, Zhou Yuanshen suddenly asked, \"You heard what my father said last time?\"","Cheng Zhao was still pondering her next move. Hearing this, she looked at him. \"...That time at Chenhui Courtyard? Yes, I heard it.\"","Zhou Yuanshen placed another stone.","While they were talking, Cheng Zhao lost her focus for a second, and he instantly wiped out a large section of her pieces.","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","She had worked so hard to defend that territory. This damn brute!","She quietly let out a breath.","Zhou Yuanshen seemed completely indifferent to winning the game and continued, \"Today, why was your maid peeking outside Chenhui Courtyard?\"","Cheng Zhao was startled once again.","\"I failed to manage my people properly. It won't happen again, My Lord,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She thought to herself, you were secretly meeting your widowed sister-in-law—such a shameful thing—and my maid saw it. Are you planning to take your anger out on me?","Regardless, my maid's actions represent my intentions.","Just treat it as if I was the one peeking.","If Cheng Zhao hadn't been curious, the maid would never have stayed to watch before leaving. Of course, she was acting on what she guessed were her master's wishes.","Cheng Zhao had no intention of punishing the maid, let alone driving her away.","She pretended not to understand the underlying meaning of Zhou Yuanshen's words.","\"If there is anything you want to know, you can ask me,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao placed a stone.","This move should stabilize the situation in this area and also capture a bit of Zhou Yuanshen's territory. She was temporarily satisfied with this layout.","Only after making this move did she have the mind to speak: \"My Lord, you and I are both of the younger generation. I understand that there are many things we cannot control.\"","A young tree trunk is simply not as thick and sturdy as an older one. When facing fierce winds and torrential rain, a young tree might snap in half or be uprooted completely.","Accumulating strength takes time.","Faced with the Empress's bestowed marriage and the Dowager Madame's deliberate difficulties, Cheng Zhao had no power to resist, but she was not disheartened.","She knew very well that she was merely young and therefore weak in influence.","Her path had only just begun.","The same went for Zhou Yuanshen.","He was also young and equally needed time to grow stronger.","Cheng Zhao had heard her grandfather say that Zhou Yuanshen was carrying out the slaughters for the Emperor, so the Emperor wouldn't leave behind a bad name.","Who would willingly seek out infamy?","Zhou Yuanshen simply understood that with the deaths of the men in the eldest branch, the heavy burden of the family was forced onto his shoulders. His military path was cut short, and to find a new path for himself, he had to do what others dared not or were unwilling to do.","And the Dowager Madame was someone who could influence the Emperor.","If she told Zhou Yuanshen to take on dual lineage duties, what could he do?","Cheng Zhao had already pondered this issue.","She had already received the imperial mandate as a Duke's wife; she was walking this path a bit faster than Huan Qingtang.","A woman's ultimate achievement was to become a revered matriarch: possessing a top-tier imperial mandate, having flocks of children and grandchildren, and securing the family's noble titles, properties, and status.","Huan Qingtang had a similar background to hers and shared the same goals. As long as she also married Zhou Yuanshen, the two of them would inevitably be unable to tolerate each other.","Two tigers cannot share one mountain. It wasn't something that could be reconciled just by Cheng Zhao being magnanimous.","Huan Qingtang could tolerate countless Mu Jiangs, but she would absolutely never tolerate a Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao and she would definitely have a showdown, and the one who took the first step held the advantage.","Of course, Huan Qingtang had her own advantages: she was the eldest grandson's wife personally selected by the Dowager Madame. Whether it was her family background or character, the Dowager Madame preferred her.","Cheng Zhao did not ask Zhou Yuanshen too many questions.","In her heart, Zhou Yuanshen wasn't necessarily her ally; he had no personal affection for her.","He might even favor Huan Qingtang.","If she discussed everything with him now and revealed her bottom line, only for him to turn around and betray her, what could she do?","Cheng Zhao's future situation would be even more difficult.","She had to be prepared to fight alone.","Cheng Zhao didn't expect Zhou Yuanshen to favor the eldest branch; she was just making the worst-case preparations first, forcing herself not to slack off.","\"...My Lord, is there anything you want to tell me?\" Cheng Zhao asked him in return.","She wanted to fish for information from him, too.","Zhou Yuanshen's face was completely expressionless. His gaze fell on the Go board, and he wiped out another huge section of Cheng Zhao's stones, effortlessly destroying the layout she had just set up.","Cheng Zhao looked at the board speechlessly, only to hear him say, \"No.\"","He had nothing he wanted to talk to her about.","Cheng Zhao suffered a crushing defeat this time.","Since she started learning Go, this was the first time she had been completely annihilated. For a moment, she was almost furious.","She stood up. \"I am tired and will go to rest now. Please make yourself comfortable, My Lord.\"","She took off her short jacket and tossed it at the foot of the bed, wrapped herself in the brocade quilt like a silkworm chrysalis, and rolled over to sleep facing the inside of the bed.","Then, the light inside the bed curtains dimmed.","Zhou Yuanshen got into bed, let down the curtains, and lay down as well.","The night passed in silence.","When Cheng Zhao woke up the next morning, he had already left for court.","She changed her clothes. The Go board was still on the kang table, the endgame a horrible sight. Cheng Zhao casually swept the stones onto the floor.","As a result, Nanny Li spent the entire morning coaxing her.","As Nonghua Courtyard gradually lost the lingering traces of Zhou Yuanshen, Cheng Zhao finally felt a bit happier. The Go board in the inner bedchamber was cleaned up, and Cheng Zhao went to Chengming Hall to handle her duties."]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31: Cheng Zhao Must Strive","paragraphs":["The capital of Shangjing had seen several consecutive days of clear skies following the snow.","Cheng Zhao received some wonderful news.","Her mother had sent someone over with winter tonics, bringing along the message that her eldest brother-in-law was returning to the capital to report on his duties, and her eldest sister would be coming back with the children.","Her eldest sister, Cheng Han, was the person who treated Cheng Zhao best in this world.","\"...Every time my fourth brother and I got into a fight, Eldest Sister always took my side,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Her eldest sister was twelve years older than her; they shared the same Chinese zodiac sign and the exact same birthday. Any gifts relatives gave to her eldest sister could easily be passed down for Cheng Zhao to use.","Out of the five siblings, because of this special bond, Cheng Zhao was closest to her.","Their mother was always too busy, so before her eldest sister married, she was the one who played with Cheng Zhao and taught her how to read. Because her eldest brother-in-law had to observe a mourning period, her eldest sister's wedding was delayed for three years, giving her three extra years to keep Cheng Zhao company.","Nanny Li couldn't help but laugh. \"Are you still holding a grudge against the Fourth Young Master?\"","\"I'll hold it for a lifetime,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She added, \"I need to make a trip home. Since Eldest Sister is back, Third Sister should be coming home too, right?\"","Cheng Zhao's third sister, Cheng Ying, had married into the estate of the Prince of Jingnan four years ago.","The Prince of Jingnan was the only prince of a different surname in the current dynasty, wielding immense power and prestige. Third Sister had married Zhang Yunqi, the youngest son of the princely estate.","Elders naturally doted on their youngest sons, and marrying him meant she wouldn't have to manage the household chores. The Cheng family had been extremely satisfied with this marriage.","Unexpectedly, Zhang Yunqi ran away the very month after the wedding, his whereabouts unknown.","This matter was covered up for a long time, until a year later when he returned to the capital with the daughter of a condemned official, who was already pregnant.","The princely estate refused to let her enter the household but didn't force the issue too harshly, allowing Zhang Yunqi to settle the woman and child in an outer residence.","When this scandal broke, Cheng Zhao's third sister became the laughingstock of the entire capital.","Because of this, Third Sister lived in seclusion, rarely seen all year round. She didn't socialize or attend banquets, completely fading into the inner courtyard.","Their mother couldn't just run over to the princely estate to see her every single day.","Last January, in front of Cheng Zhao's parents, their grandfather asked Third Sister if she wanted a divorce. Third Sister refused and distanced herself even further from the Cheng family ever since.","It seemed she was afraid that her bad luck and misfortune would taint the family, bringing shame upon her grandfather, parents, and siblings.","At that time, Cheng Zhao made up her mind that she had to strive for excellence.","If she married well, bringing pride to her mother and glory to the family, perhaps Third Sister would be willing to divorce, return home, and escape her sea of bitterness.","Her own marriage was only average, and Zhou Yuanshen hadn't even accompanied her on the traditional third-day visit home. However, she wasn't as aloof and proud as Third Sister, who refused to fight for anything.","Less than four months into her marriage, Cheng Zhao had managed to secure the title of a first-rank Duchess. This alone put her above many others.","Nanny Li took the opportunity to say, \"The government offices have been quite idle lately, and the Duke doesn't need to keep an eye on the Capital Garrison all day long. He is often at home.\"","She was hinting for Cheng Zhao to bring Zhou Yuanshen along when she visited her family.","Cheng Zhao remained silent for a long time.","Nanny Li probed gently, advising her again, \"Young Madam, you cannot become arrogant over a single victory. The road ahead is still difficult to navigate, and you will at least need the Duke's support...\"","\"...Isn't the New Year approaching? We will go back in January to pay New Year's greetings. If he is willing, I will naturally ask him,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li said no more.","Because Cheng Zhao was serving at Chengming Hall, she went to the Old Madam's Shou'an Courtyard to inform her of her visit home; she also told the Second Madam.","The Second Madam ordered someone to prepare gifts.","The Old Madam also arranged a few gifts, which were mostly for show; the Second Madam's gifts, on the other hand, were genuinely valuable.","Cheng Zhao took her maids, Qiubai and Suyue, and headed out early the next morning.","She even ran into Zhou Yuanshen at the door.","She curtsied in greeting.","\"Where are you going?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked.","Cheng Zhao told him truthfully.","Zhou Yuanshen gave a slight nod, didn't ask another word, and rode off on his horse.","Cheng Zhao hurried back to the Cheng family estate early, just as her parents had finished breakfast.","\"Rushing like this, aren't you afraid others will laugh at you?\" her mother scolded her. \"Sit down first. I'll send someone to see if your eldest sister is up yet.\"","Upon returning to the capital, her eldest sister was temporarily staying at the Cheng family home.","Her eldest brother-in-law was not a native of the capital. He was the sole heir for three generations, his parents had both passed away, and he had no relatives or friends in the capital. He did own a residence, but it had been vacant for years with only one old servant looking after it, so returning there would be highly inconvenient.","Her grandfather had given the word for her eldest sister and her husband to stay at the family home until the New Year was over. Her mother had cleaned up her eldest sister's old maiden quarters for them to live in.","\"She should be up by this hour,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","Not wanting to wait, she turned to leave but was stopped by her mother's sharp command.","\"Sit down, I have something to ask you,\" her mother said.","Cheng Zhao had no choice but to sit properly.","\"I heard that Grand Tutor Wu offended Zhou Yuanshen and has been thrown into prison?\" her mother asked.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"With your background, how can you ask about such gossip?\"","Her mother raised a hand as if to hit her.","Who was the Grand Tutor? He was the Emperor's teacher.","The Emperor had only been the Crown Prince for a year before ascending the throne, but his teacher had accompanied him for over a decade.","Now he had walked down his father's old path, growing annoyed with his nagging teacher and wanting to get rid of him.","What was the difference between killing one's teacher and killing one's father?","This matter definitely had to go through someone else's hands, and Zhou Yuanshen had become that blade.","This was already the third issue Zhou Yuanshen had handled for the Emperor.","\"...How will the historians write about him? Which of those notoriously treacherous villains didn't leave behind a torrent of infamy after their deaths?\" her mother worried. \"You should advise him not to be too greedy.\"","He was already the Duke of Chen.","The highest rank of nobility—what else could he seek? The Zhou family was like flowers added to brocade, possessing both power and influence.","\"I can't persuade him,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Mother, do you think that as a wife, I must constantly 'advise' my husband to do the right thing? If you feel that doing so is better for me, I will do it.\"","Her mother choked on her words, unable to speak for a long while.","Cheng Zhao stood up. \"I'm going to see Eldest Sister and the children. I'll take my leave first.\"","Without waiting for her mother to stop her again, Cheng Zhao ran off.","Suyue was carrying a small bundle, which contained the gifts Cheng Zhao had personally prepared for her eldest sister and the children. When they arrived at the gate of her eldest sister's courtyard, Qiubai went to knock, and a maid quickly came to open the door.","Cheng Zhao didn't really recognize this maid, but the maid knew Cheng Zhao.","\"Fifth Young Lady, please come in. Our Madam has been looking forward to seeing you,\" the maid said.","Cheng Zhao entered the courtyard.","Before even stepping through the door, she called out loudly, \"Eldest Sister!\"","A six-year-old girl, wearing a light green padded jacket and cotton trousers, ran out of the room. She was dressed so thickly that she looked perfectly round and plump.","\"Fifth Aunt?\"","Cheng Zhao scooped her up in her arms. \"Heng'er still remembers me! She actually remembers me!\"","Her eldest sister walked out of the room.","She looked at Cheng Zhao and smiled, but as she smiled, tears welled up in her eyes.","The wet nurse took the child away, and her eldest brother-in-law walked out from the inner bedroom.","Cheng Zhao exchanged greetings with him. He told the sisters to catch up and then took his leave.","\"You've grown taller again,\" her eldest sister said with a smile.","The tears in her eyes rolled down her cheeks.","Cheng Zhao threw herself into her arms and cried too. \"I missed you every single day. Are you going to leave again?\"","\"I'm not leaving. Now that we're back, your brother-in-law is going to secure a position in the Ministry of War. We won't be going away again.\" Her eldest sister cried as well.","The two sisters had endless things to talk about.","Her eldest sister was now a mother of three. Aside from six-year-old Heng'er, she also had a pair of three-year-old twin boys.","She had set off while pregnant back then, so Cheng Zhao had never even met her nephews.","However, she had already prepared gifts for them.","Mid-morning, Third Sister Cheng Ying also returned.","Second Brother, his wife, and Fourth Brother also arrived at the courtyard.","It had been a long time since the siblings had all gathered together like this.","\"I've booked a private room at the Drunken Immortal Pavilion. Let's head out for a meal,\" said Second Brother, Cheng Yan."]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32: Did I Humiliate Myself","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao ran into Zhou Yuanshen at the entrance of Zuixian Restaurant.","Zhou Yuanshen had also come to eat with a group of people.","Originally, they wouldn't have met.","Just as they were about to enter the private booth on the second floor, someone suddenly called out, \"Senior Brother Du?\"","Cheng Zhao's eldest brother-in-law was named Du Anli.","Hearing this form of address, Cheng Zhao, who was walking at the very back arm in arm with her eldest sister, turned her head first and caught sight of Zhou Yuanshen.","The person speaking wasn't Zhou Yuanshen, but a tall young man behind him.","The young man had wheat-colored skin. At a glance, one could tell he was a military officer, tall and straight.","Seeing young women, he didn't avoid suspicion. He smiled brightly, revealing a small canine tooth.","The eldest brother-in-law walked over, both surprised and eager: \"Junior Brother, why are you here?\"","He said to Cheng Zhao's eldest sister, \"This is Junior Brother Fan Xiao from the Fan family, whom I've mentioned to you.\"","He also introduced, \"This is my clumsy wife.\"","They greeted each other.","Cheng Zhao stood to the side.","After they finished talking here, Fan Xiao and Zhou Yuanshen's group were about to enter the private room when Zhou Yuanshen beside them suddenly spoke.","He said, \"Little Uncle, this is Lady Cheng.\"","Fan Xiao looked at him in confusion.","Zhou Yuanshen continued, \"She is the Duchess of Chen.\"","Fan Xiao: \"...\"","The private room reserved by Cheng Zhao's second brother was bustling with noise and excitement.","She met Fan Xiao, Zhou Yuanshen's little uncle.","Her mother-in-law had such snow-white skin, but her little uncle had a wheat-colored complexion. He didn't look much like Cheng Zhao's mother-in-law. Perhaps one looked like the father and the other like the mother.","Cheng Zhao also met Helian Jian, the heir of the Prince of Rong's Residence.","And Cheng Zhao's sisters finally saw Zhou Yuanshen himself.","Cheng Zhao's brothers all knew him. After the marriage was granted, the second brother and fourth brother went to inquire about him separately, but he just didn't know them.","Fan Xiao looked at Cheng Zhao's third sister, Cheng Ying, several times.","Every girl in the Cheng family had an uncommon appearance. Cheng Ying was thinner and more fragile, like a person made of snow, cold and arrogant, more otherworldly than Cheng Zhao and her eldest sister.","Cheng Ying was inherently cold and arrogant, unsuitable to be the principal wife of the eldest son, so the family chose the youngest son of the Prince of Jingnan for her.","Who knew they had also misjudged.","\"...Adding ties of marriage to ties of blood, let's go play polo together another day,\" Fan Xiao said with a smile. \"You all should be good at playing polo, right?\"","Polo was inherently more fun with more people.","The eldest brother-in-law answered for them, \"Let's wait until after the New Year. Everyone is busy with various things at the end of the year.\"","The young waiter added a table in the private room, and the two groups gathered together to eat.","They also drank some wine.","Fan Xiao said to Zhou Yuanshen, \"You are the youngest brother-in-law, quickly toast your brother-in-law and brothers-in-law.\"","Zhou Yuanshen didn't have any bashfulness, standing up nimbly to pour wine.","He toasted the three of them separately.","Cheng Zhao's second brother Cheng Yan and fourth brother Cheng Chao exchanged a glance, both having dissatisfaction towards Zhou Yuanshen in their eyes.","They then forced Zhou Yuanshen to drink.","Zhou Yuanshen accepted everyone who came.","Therefore, he drank the most.","Later, it was the eldest brother-in-law who came out to stop them: \"We're going to be relatives for a lifetime, we don't lack this meal of wine, don't be greedy for too much.\"","The eldest brother-in-law had quite a bit of prestige, so Cheng Yan and Cheng Chao withdrew.","Zhou Yuanshen sat down as if nothing had happened, but Cheng Zhao's second brother seemed a bit drunk.","The meal was lively.","After the meal, everyone stood up to take their leave.","At the entrance of Zuixian Restaurant, a carriage with an ornate canopy had been waiting for a long time.","Seeing everyone come out, a young servant went forward and whispered something.","The carriage curtain was lifted, revealing a young and handsome face.","Romantic features, luxurious clothing.","He jumped out of the carriage, his posture unrestrained and elegant, bowing to everyone: \"Brother-in-law, Second Brother, Fourth Brother.\"","Then he greeted his second sister-in-law and sisters.","No one in the Cheng family paid attention to him.","It was still the eldest brother-in-law Du Anli who smoothed things over: \"Yunqi, why didn't you come up?\"","Zhang Yunqi then said, \"I just arrived, thinking you should have finished eating. Ah Ying, it's time to return to the residence, Mother asked me to come pick you up.\"","Cheng Ying nodded slightly.","She bid farewell to everyone and got into the carriage with Zhang Yunqi.","Fan Xiao watched this young and beautiful young couple walk away, then looked at the Cheng family members, a bit curious, but he didn't ask anything.","The carriages drove over one by one.","Zhou Yuanshen's carriage pulled over, the coachman put down the horse stool, and he looked at Cheng Zhao: \"Are you returning to the residence?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Okay.\"","She also said to her eldest sister, \"Tomorrow I will send you an invitation, you bring the children to the Chen Duke's Residence as guests.\"","The eldest sister agreed.","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen went back.","In the carriage, he closed his eyes and dozed off, seeming a bit drunk.","Cheng Zhao also didn't speak.","Upon returning to the Chen Duke's Residence, Zhou Yuanshen then said, \"You go back first, I'm going to the outer study.\"","Cheng Zhao said okay.","Her maidservants hadn't followed her to the restaurant, estimating they would return a bit later, Cheng Zhao walked back to Nonghua Courtyard alone.","It was very far, she walked for a long time.","Midway she also ran into Mu Jiang.","\"Third Young Madam, where have you been?\" Mu Jiang greeted her.","Seeing no one around Cheng Zhao, Mu Jiang didn't bow, her attitude very arrogant.","She even looked Cheng Zhao up and down out of the corner of her eye, \"Dressed so shabbily, could it be you went back to your maiden home?\"","Compared to Mu Jiang, Cheng Zhao's clothing and jewelry were steady, valuable, and not flashy, looking less brightly colored and dazzling than her attire.","Cheng Zhao looked back at her quietly: \"Who is asking me?\"","\"You can't see me? In broad daylight, could it be you're blind?\" Mu Jiang sneered.","Cheng Zhao: \"My eyes are set high, of course I can't see things that are too small and too short.\"","She turned to leave.","Mu Jiang's expression changed drastically: \"You're humiliating me? You're humiliating the Old Madam, humiliating His Majesty!\"","\"What are you to the Old Madam, and what are you to His Majesty? If I remember correctly, you are merely the Duke's concubine,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She added, \"If you want me to humiliate you, kneel down and beg me.\"","Mu Jiang changed color in anger.","The hidden weapon in her hand was thrown out again.","Cheng Zhao knew how to practice swordplay, wield a spear, and also use a short crossbow, but she wasn't very good at defending against hidden weapons.","However, Cheng Zhao had sharp eyes and had always been vigilant against Mu Jiang hurting people.","Seeing she was about to suffer a loss, before her wrist was even raised, Cheng Zhao took a few steps forward and bumped into her.","Bumping her so she staggered, the hidden weapon shot off target.","Mu Jiang didn't stand firm and fell to the ground.","The maidservant exclaimed: \"Concubine.\"","\"What's all this fuss?\" Zhou Yuanshen stood not far away at an unknown time, quietly watching this scene.","Mu Jiang complained in extreme anger: \"Third Brother, she pushed me, and also humiliated me.\"","\"Did you kneel down and beg her?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked.","Mu Jiang looked at him in astonishment.","\"Did you kneel down and beg her to humiliate you? If not, did she have nothing better to do?\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","A hidden weapon was thrown at her feet, \"If I see you use this kind of thing again, I will break your wrist. Did you hear me?\"","Mu Jiang refused to get up.","She stubbornly looked up at Zhou Yuanshen: \"She bullied me.\"","She waited for Zhou Yuanshen to pick her up.","Zhou Yuanshen looked at Cheng Zhao, \"Let's go, go back.\"","After saying that, he walked forward, and Cheng Zhao followed him.","Mu Jiang was stunned in place.","For a long time, the figures of the two of them disappeared at the end of the path, and Mu Jiang was still in a daze.","She seemed unable to believe it.","The maidservant wanted to support her: \"Concubine, the ground is cold...\"","Mu Jiang raised her hand and slapped her across the face: \"What happened just now, do you know how to tell the Old Madam?\"","\"It was the Third Young Madam who bullied you, this servant heard it all, and the Duke also took sides,\" the maidservant endured the burning pain on half her face and answered in a low voice.","Mu Jiang pulled her arm and stood up herself.","She straightened her lapel and went to Shou'an Courtyard to complain."]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33: Call Her Name","paragraphs":["Dowager Madame did not help Mu Jiang vent her anger.","Instead, she sent a maid to Nonghua Courtyard to deliver some pastries to Cheng Zhao.","\"Dowager Madame asks, since you returned to your maiden home today, is your family all well?\" the maid said.","Cheng Zhao glanced toward the inner bedchamber.","Zhou Yuanshen was quite heavily drunk. He had just thrown up once in the washroom. It wasn't until he vomited that Cheng Zhao realized he had truly been forced to drink too much by her two older brothers.","After throwing up, he washed up, changed his clothes, and went to rest.","Cheng Zhao sat in the eastern side room drinking tea until the maid from Shou'an Courtyard arrived.","She had planned to wait for Zhou Yuanshen to wake up so they could go pay their respects to Second Madam together.","Seeing this, Cheng Zhao said to Nanny Li, \"Prepare a small carriage for me; I am going to Shou'an Courtyard.\"","When Cheng Zhao arrived at Shou'an Courtyard, Mu Jiang was in Dowager Madame's small Buddhist hall copying scriptures; Dowager Madame did not mention a single word about Mu Jiang blocking the way.","To bring it up would mean acknowledging Mu Jiang was in the wrong, and that whatever punishment Cheng Zhao gave her was justified.","\"...I would like to invite my eldest sister over as a guest tomorrow,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Dowager Madame smiled cheerfully. \"Relatives should visit each other often; harmony brings prosperity. Go ahead and invite her, and it's perfectly fine to have her stay for a few days.\"","\"Everyone is busy near the end of the year. Once the new year has passed and things are more leisurely, I will invite her for a short stay,\" Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Dowager Madame gave a slight nod and told Cheng Zhao to send someone to inform the main kitchen to add a few more dishes for the guest tomorrow; she also told Cheng Zhao to go to the wine cellar to pick out a few jars of good wine.","\"...Speaking of drinking, during lunch, Lord Duke was made drunk by my two older brothers,\" Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Dowager Madame: \"Is that so? Ah Shen has always been restrained.\"","\"Perhaps he was just happy. They are of similar age and compatible temperaments, so they drank without restraint,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Dowager Madame: \"Prepare some hangover soup and let him get a good rest.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","After chatting for quite a while, she finally left Shou'an Courtyard.","Since she already had the small carriage, Cheng Zhao made a side trip to Second Madam's Jiangyun Courtyard.","She recounted the day's events to Second Madam once more.","Second Madam had more points of concern, so Cheng Zhao chatted with her for quite a while, right up until dinnertime.","\"I'm not very hungry, I'll just have some rice porridge tonight; Lord Duke is probably awake by now, and he likely won't have much of an appetite either,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam: \"Go on back, I don't need you to serve me during the meal here.\"","When Cheng Zhao returned, Qiubai and Suyue had already arrived home.","\"Madam has prepared return gifts and left them at the porter's lodge. They will be sent to Dowager Madame and Second Madam first thing tomorrow morning,\" Suyue said.","\"My mother is very thoughtful.\"","\"Madam has always been thorough,\" Suyue said.","Nanny Li asked Cheng Zhao what she wanted to eat and where the meal should be set.","Just then, Zhou Yuanshen woke up.","Cheng Zhao entered the inner bedroom and asked him, \"What would Lord Duke like for dinner?\"","\"Some rice porridge.\"","It coincided perfectly with Cheng Zhao's thoughts.","Dinner was plain rice porridge paired with side dishes. Cheng Zhao casually took a few bites.","She had gone out today and ate very little for dinner, so Cheng Zhao planned to take a bath right after eating and go to bed early.","She still had to host her eldest sister tomorrow.","After dinner, when Cheng Zhao ordered the maids to prepare hot water, Zhou Yuanshen raised his eyes and glanced at her.","Cheng Zhao was solely focused on thinking about her eldest sister and did not notice his expression.","Inside the washroom, as she soaked in the warm water, planning tomorrow's arrangements, a hand landed on her shoulder. She just assumed it was Nanny Li.","Whenever Cheng Zhao spent too much time doing needlework, reading, or practicing calligraphy, Nanny Li would massage her shoulders and neck while she bathed.","However, when the hand slid further down, Cheng Zhao was suddenly startled.","She subconsciously turned her head, and the man leaned in slightly to look at her.","Cheng Zhao avoided his hand. \"Lord Duke, do you want to take a bath too? I will order the maids to come...\"","Zhou Yuanshen untied his inner garments.","Cheng Zhao had barely ever seen his body and turned her face to the side.","The bathtub was spacious. When he stepped in, the water almost overflowed past Cheng Zhao's shoulders. She wanted to get up and leave.","\"I'll let you have it!\" She was about to go.","Her waist was already caught in an embrace.","Cheng Zhao smelled the faint scent of alcohol on him. After vomiting in the afternoon, he had brushed his teeth with tooth powder, and he had rinsed his mouth again after dinner, so the smell of alcohol had mostly dissipated.","The water was a bit hot, but his body was even more scorching.","Cheng Zhao was like a cat that had fallen into the water, flailing and struggling to escape.","Zhou Yuanshen was behind her, practically caging her in his arms. Her black hair hung over the edge of the tub and into the water.","It felt a bit wet and heavy.","Zhou Yuanshen spoke: \"Cheng Zhao.\"","He called her by her name.","Cheng Zhao felt slightly surprised that he actually remembered her name.","She always thought that when addressing her, he would call her Cheng Shi, just like how he introduced her to his uncle at the restaurant.","\"...If you don't want to, tell me directly. Once you say it, I absolutely won't force you. Just don't regret it later.\" His voice was very slow.","His hands were underwater, gripping her waist neither lightly nor heavily, his thumbs gently rubbing the skin on the side of her waist.","Cheng Zhao stopped all her movements.","\"I don't mean that.\" Cheng Zhao's throat felt stiff, the words squeezed out one by one.","She waited for his reply.","But he didn't say anything else.","Cheng Zhao wanted to turn around, but his hands applied a slight pressure, forbidding her to move.","Following the force of the water, she was pushed by him until she was leaning over the edge of the bathtub.","Cheng Zhao felt like she was seasick; as the water rippled around her, she felt a bit dizzy, her consciousness turning hazy.","\"Can, can you... the water has gone cold...\"","She muttered this sentence like she was sleepwalking.","Just a moment ago, there was an instant where her breathing tightened so much she couldn't catch her breath, her whole body was burning hot, yet suddenly a flower bloomed.","She began to drift and float, feeling somewhat dazed.","She really felt the water had gone cold; she was freezing.","The man behind her also seemed very frustrated.","\"I drank alcohol.\" His voice was low. \"I didn't expect it to be this difficult either.\"","He forcefully gripped her waist again, one hand climbing up to gently touch her face. \"You can use some strength this time.\"","Fearing she wouldn't understand, he explained, \"Last time when your leg cramped, you used a lot of force. Try exerting strength like that again.\"","Cheng Zhao tensed her waist and abdomen.","She was very tired, and in such a posture, when she exerted force again, she only felt like she was going to collapse from exhaustion.","His hands, one gripping her waist, the other holding her shoulder, suddenly applied force together.","It hurt a lot. Cheng Zhao felt as if her bones were going to be crushed by him.","In Cheng Zhao's line of sight, she saw the veins suddenly bulging on his arm.","Cheng Zhao was in a lot of pain, but she endured it and didn't speak, because he released his grip in the very next instant.","A complete mess everywhere.","She fell asleep in a daze, feeling someone applying ointment to her, just like last time.","She did not open her eyes.","When she woke up early the next morning, she saw the bruises on the side of her waist.","They were finger marks, firmly imprinted on her body.","Zhou Yuanshen had left early in the morning again. Cheng Zhao didn't see him when she woke up.","She was very tired, and knowing she had already woken up late, she couldn't be bothered to move.","\"Is there any hope of getting pregnant this time?\" she thought with frustration as she lay in bed.","Why was getting pregnant so exhausting?","Not only was she not pregnant, but there was no sign from Mu Jiang either.","Cheng Zhao calculated the days; the number of times Zhou Yuanshen spent the night at Mu Jiang's place was far greater than at Nonghua Courtyard.","\"If he really has a problem, could we invite a doctor to prescribe medicine?\" Cheng Zhao thought.","Would he fly into a rage?","It would be better to wait.","Wait until Mu Jiang couldn't stand it anymore and suggested calling a doctor for him first, and then Cheng Zhao could play along and offer some supporting remarks."]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34: Seen by Him","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao took her time getting out of bed.","She did not call anyone in to serve her, but looked at herself in the mirror.","There were indeed bruises on her waist and shoulders. They were not too severe, much like the bumps and scrapes from childhood.","She gently rubbed the blue marks and sighed.","A cough sounded from behind her.","Cheng Zhao slowly turned her head.","She saw Zhou Yuanshen entering the inner bedroom holding a book.","Cheng Zhao hurriedly pulled her inner garments together. However, he had already seen her with her top off, admiring herself in the mirror.","She felt extremely embarrassed.","\"With a figure like yours, Madame Duke, there is no need to sigh,\" he said.","It sounded like a joke, yet also a genuine attempt to comfort her.","Cheng Zhao frowned.","He had already stepped forward.","Her hastily wrapped inner garment still revealed a bit of skin. He casually lifted it and saw her waist.","Cheng Zhao swatted his hand hard.","A loud slap echoed.","\"Has the Lord Duke not gone to work?\" After hitting him, she felt a bit of regret and spoke up to cover it up.","Looking up at him, his expression was completely placid, showing neither joy nor anger.","Zhou Yuanshen took two steps back and said indifferently, \"I am on leave today.\"","\"Would the Lord Duke like to move to another place? My Eldest Sister is coming to visit today.\"","\"Invite brother-in-law to come as well,\" he said. \"We brothers-in-law can play chess, it won't delay your chatting.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Brother-in-law has no time. He has a lot of official business after returning to the capital.\"","Zhou Yuanshen took a book from the small shelf next to the kang table in the inner bedroom: \"I will go to Chenhui Courtyard to read. Send someone to find me if there is anything.\"","He turned and left.","Only then did Cheng Zhao call people in to serve her.","Remembering how he had seen her looking in the mirror without clothes just now, Cheng Zhao was so frustrated she wanted to bang her head against the wall.","\"...Have someone distribute the gifts brought back yesterday to Dowager Madame and my mother-in-law, and tell them that I am receiving my Eldest Sister as a guest today,\" Cheng Zhao ordered after washing up.","Suyue complied.","Mid-morning, her Eldest Sister arrived.","Cheng Zhao waited for her at the main gate.","She led her to see Dowager Madame first.","Eldest Sister brought gifts for Dowager Madame, including a box of sea pearls, each one perfectly round. Even in the capital, in a prominent family like the Zhou family, it would not be easy to find such large and plump sea pearls.","Dowager Madame said, \"You are too polite, Madame.\"","\"These are just some worldly items to show my filial respect, please do not disdain them. My youngest sister is a clever and smart child; with your guidance, she will surely have a great future. I respect and thank you from the bottom of my heart,\" Eldest Sister smiled.","Dowager Madame praised her repeatedly.","Accompanying them was the First Young Madame, Huan Qingtang.","Huan Qingtang felt that when Cheng Zhao's Eldest Sister socialized, her approach was the same as Cheng Zhao's: she was good at flattering others while also elevating herself.","Neither haughty nor humble.","The person who raised them must have a profound background.","This demeanor was worth learning, and Huan Qingtang admired it.","It was a pity that Cheng Zhao's Eldest Sister had a very ordinary marriage. As the legitimate eldest daughter of an aristocratic family, she only married a third-rank Cavalry General with no family background.","After sitting at Dowager Madame's place for a while, they went to Second Madame's courtyard.","They also gave some local specialties.","All were rare and expensive.","Second Madame was overjoyed and asked a lot about the garrison at the East Sea defense line.","Cheng Zhao's Eldest Sister was very cautious in this regard, almost claiming ignorance to every question.","\"...Last time, my youngest sister asked the family to help inquire with the booksellers in Zhouhai whether they had swindled Young Master Zhou's money.","Those booksellers are all familiar with my fourth brother. Upon being asked, they admitted it was unethical and their fault. The banknotes have been returned.\" Eldest Sister handed another small box to Second Madame.","Seeing that she used a box to hold it, Second Madame was stunned for a moment.","How much money must this be?","Opening it to take a look, Second Madame almost fainted: \"This little brat, spent thousands of taels to buy a calligraphy copybook?\"","\"Five thousand taels,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","Second Madame: \"...I must break his legs tonight. No wonder he went to his grandmother for money last time and kept it from me.","His grandmother even said that a child asking for some money is harmless; and buying a calligraphy copybook is a scholarly pursuit, so any amount of money is worth spending.\"","She couldn't help but want to spit, \"No matter how scholarly it is, it's not worth five thousand taels.\"","Cheng Zhao and Eldest Sister were both amused.","\"As for the booksellers...\"","\"They seek my grandfather's calligraphy and paintings, and my fourth brother is friends with them. They usually make a lot of money from the Cheng family. To get them to spit the money out, my fourth brother treated them to a meal with wine,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","Second Madame: \"Then I must thank the Fourth Master. Later, I will have Yuanshen invite his brother-in-law for a drink.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","Speaking of Master Qu Lian's calligraphy copybooks, they can now sell for a thousand taels a copy on the market, but unfortunately, there is demand but no supply.","Forgeries are disastrously common.","Cheng Zhao's fourth brother stole the authentic works from home and gave them to the booksellers, allowing them to pass off fakes as genuine.","Of course, as to how much benefit the fourth brother gained from this, he would not say a word to outsiders, and even their grandfather was unaware.","When the fourth brother asked them to refund the money, they did so straightforwardly.","Leaving Jiangyun Courtyard, Eldest Sister said, \"Your mother-in-law has a rather straightforward personality.\"","\"She is very direct.\"","\"That is very good, it makes getting along easy,\" Eldest Sister said.","Cheng Zhao nodded.","She led Eldest Sister back to Nonghua Courtyard.","Because Eldest Sister gave a gift that pleased Dowager Madame, the banquet sent from the main kitchen at noon was truly rich.","There were also four additional dishes added by Dowager Madame for Nonghua Courtyard.","Second Madame also added dishes.","The meal was very enjoyable.","In the afternoon, Cheng Zhao saw Eldest Sister off.","After Eldest Sister returned to the capital, Cheng Zhao was a bit absent-minded while handling affairs at Chengming Hall.","First Madame, Madam Song, having suffered a minor setback, was also a bit more clear-headed and much more polite to Cheng Zhao, maintaining a superficial harmony.","However, having lost a key subordinate, she harbored even more resentment toward Cheng Zhao in her heart.","Being busy with various matters recently, Madam Song clearly had her own calculations, and she was just as absent-minded as Cheng Zhao.","The tasks at the main kitchen were simple, so Cheng Zhao asked her for a leave of absence.","\"Dowager Madame has already said that after the New Year, the managers of the main kitchen will go to Nonghua Courtyard to report,\" Madam Song said to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao: \"It is hard on the managers to run so far, it would be better if I continue to come over. If you do not mind, Eldest Aunt, I will still come to Chengming Hall to bother you.\"","First Madame: \"...\"","She probably hated Cheng Zhao lingering around her very much, and her expression changed uncontrollably.","Seeing this, Cheng Zhao took the opportunity to say, \"The main kitchen does not need to report every day. I would like to manage the affairs once every three days, do you think that is acceptable?\"","Coming only once every three days made First Madame feel a bit more comfortable.","\"This is your task. As long as you guarantee there will be no trouble and explain things clearly to the managers, you can naturally do as you please,\" First Madame said.","Cheng Zhao: \"Then I will do it once every three days.\"","This way she could just rest for two days.","She returned home again.","Third Sister also came back often.","Second Sister-in-law brought pastries over, and the four women played cards together happily.","A maid from her grandfather's side came: \"The Chancellor heard that the Fifth Young Lady has returned to the estate, and asks you to go to the outer study.\"","Cheng Zhao figured it must be about the Zhou family, so she got up and went.","\"In the Imperial Study, the Emperor told the Duke of Chen that his eyes resemble his aunt's; and he also said that Mu Jiang's nose and mouth resemble hers,\" her grandfather said.","Cheng Zhao: \"So that was the reason he picked up Mu Jiang back then. But he didn't keep Mu Jiang by his side, and even let her become a concubine to Zhou Yuanshen.\"","\"The Emperor's thoughts are extremely chaotic now. He told the Duke of Chen to hurry up and have a son with Mu Jiang. If the child resembles Empress Xuancheng, he will crown that child as the Crown Prince.\"","Empress Xuancheng was Zhou Yuanshen's aunt. The emperor had only ascended the throne after her death, posthumously granting her an empty title.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","The courtiers would absolutely tear Zhou Yuanshen to pieces."]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35: Believe It or Not","paragraphs":["When Cheng Zhao returned from her grandfather's outer study, her sister and sister-in-law both asked her what she had gone to do.","\"Those matters concerning the Duke Chen's Mansion,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Don't ask, they're all unlucky matters.\"","Her eldest sister looked at her with heartache.","Her second sister-in-law then asked, \"Besides the main kitchen, does the Zhou family have any other matters for you to manage? It would be good if you could get the position of the steward at the gatehouse.\"","The gatehouse was a know-it-all, knowing everything.","When her second sister-in-law married in, the first task her mother gave her was to manage the gatehouse.","This was much more important than the storehouse and the kitchen.","It was equivalent to letting her familiarize herself with the family's network of connections first.","Cheng Zhao's second sister-in-law was named Yin Linlang, who also came from an aristocratic family in Wu Commandery. Her grandmother was the Grand Princess of Rong'an, but she had passed away in her early years.","\"Don't even think about the gatehouse. I only make a brief appearance at the main kitchen. The one who really makes the decisions is Nanny Qin. She is a trusted aide of the Old Madam and also the wife's younger sister of the general steward,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"It's hard to make a breakthrough when they are doubly related,\" her second sister-in-law said.","Cheng Zhao nodded.","\"Don't be anxious either. Wait a bit and the opportunity will come. What's important for you now is to give birth to the Duke's legitimate eldest son,\" her second sister-in-law said.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Her eldest sister smiled, \"Offspring is the most unhurried thing.\"","She then said to Yin Linlang, \"Zhao Zhao understands. Don't worry too much about her. You're almost catching up to my mother's nagging. As the old saying goes, 'An eldest sister-in-law is like half a mother'.\"","Cheng Zhao couldn't help but laugh.","Her third sister, Cheng Ying, also laughed beside her.","Her second sister-in-law smiled and changed the topic, chatting about the latest silks and satins.","\"... You seemed to really like the enamel hairpin I gave you last time. I recently got another set of enamel jewelry and an enamel rouge box. They are all quite interesting. You can take them back later,\" her second sister-in-law said to Cheng Ying.","Cheng Ying thanked her, \"Thank you, Second Sister-in-law.\"","\"If you're happy, Mother won't have to worry all the time,\" her second sister-in-law said.","Cheng Ying: \"I'm not unhappy.\"","Cheng Zhao gave her second sister-in-law a look, telling her not to say any more.","But her second sister-in-law couldn't help it, \"When Father and Mother mention you, they are always full of guilt. You've had a great reputation since you were young, and the madams of noble families all praise you. When you reached the age of marriage, the matchmakers broke down the threshold. But in the end, Father and Mother misjudged...\"","Before the marriage, they had also inquired about Zhang Yunqi.","There was nothing wrong with the Prince of Jingnan's Mansion, and Zhang Yunqi was famously handsome.","Cheng Ying was proud and aloof. How could ordinary men match her? Among all the noble young masters in the capital, only Zhang Yunqi's appearance, talent, and family background could match hers.","Who knew the result would be so unsatisfactory.","Zhang Yunqi not only trampled Cheng Ying's face on the ground, but also trampled the Cheng family's face.","The Cheng family had their own confidence and advised the girl to divorce and return home to seek another future.","\"There's nothing bad about me,\" Cheng Ying said. \"It's the same as at home. The food and clothing are just as good, and the servants are the same people from before.","The false reputation before marriage wasn't spread by our family, but by others flattering me. I don't care about these things.\"","\"But Zhang Yunqi...\"","\"He is no different from ordinary people. Every day he is here, I am restrained for a day. Fortunately, he is not often here,\" Cheng Ying said.","Cheng Zhao looked at her eldest sister and second sister-in-law, not knowing what to say.","Perhaps, none of them understood Cheng Ying.","There was no bitterness on Cheng Ying's face.","Cheng Zhao looked closely at her and felt that she was like someone living on an isolated island. She wouldn't come out easily, and others couldn't get in.","Cheng Ying never cared about the bustling disputes in the world.","When she returned to the Duke Chen's Mansion that day, Nanny Li asked about the situation at home, and she gave a brief account.","She also mentioned Cheng Ying.","\"Third Sister never practices Zen, but I feel she has thoroughly understood the secular world. It's not that she was forced to understand, but she is extremely talented,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li said, \"Third Miss is a heavenly fairy, not like someone who eats whole grains. She indeed has good talent.\"","\"But she is not cold-hearted. She remembers everyone's preferences. Every year, the birthday gift she gives me is what I want the most. She just needs to observe a little to know what I hope for. It's like she can see through me,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Seeing through everything, including the human heart.","But Cheng Ying was not disappointed, nor did she look down on anyone. She just kept a little distance from the secular world.","However, there were always people who couldn't adapt to her sense of distance.","Either they worried about her with good intentions.","Or they maliciously wanted to pull her down, making her roll in the mud and no longer be noble.","\"I really envy my mother. How could she give birth to such excellent children? Every one of them is good,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Except for Fourth Brother. Was he picked up?\"","Nanny Li was amused by her.","Mentioning Cheng Ying, Nanny Li remembered something, \"That Master Dai, is she still following Third Miss?\"","A distant relative from Cheng Zhao's mother's maiden family came to seek refuge. Her husband died, and the clan wanted to force her to remarry, and also confiscate her dowry and her husband's property into the clan's property.","Madam Dai brought her son and daughter, abandoned the land, packed up gold, silver, and valuables, and fled to the capital overnight to seek refuge with her distant aunt, who was Cheng Zhao's mother.","The mother sent people to inquire about it after hearing about it. After confirming it was true, she let Madam Dai stay.","Madam Dai had good sword skills. She was originally going to teach the Fourth Young Master Cheng Chao, and then Cheng Ying and Cheng Zhao followed to practice.","Cheng Chao was not interested in practicing the sword and quickly disappeared. However, Cheng Zhao and Cheng Ying continued to learn.","Cheng Zhao learned everything quickly, but she liked many things. Once she became familiar with the sword skills, she stopped going. Instead, Cheng Ying kept learning.","Later, Madam Dai became Cheng Ying's exclusive master, and the mother even paid Master Dai a monthly allowance.","When Cheng Ying got married, she also chose Madam Dai as a dowry maid.","Nanny Li didn't know what happened after that.","\"She follows Third Sister,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Master Dai is not only Third Sister's teacher but also her 'guard'.\"","\"Then at least Third Miss doesn't have to worry about her life in the Zhang family,\" Nanny Li said.","\"If the Zhang family dared to kill a wife, wouldn't they be giving the Emperor an excuse to attack them? I heard the Emperor has been dissatisfied with this 'Prince with a Different Surname' on several occasions,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li said she made sense.","Then she quietly asked Cheng Zhao, \"I heard the Emperor highly values the Duke. Have you heard about this?\"","Cheng Zhao shushed her.","\"These matters have nothing to do with us. There's no need to say more in the future,\" Cheng Zhao said.","In a blink of an eye, it was the first day of the twelfth lunar month.","As the end of the year approached, some stewards who returned from outside places finally came to Chengming Hall to deliver rent.","Madam Song was secretive and didn't let Cheng Zhao know; while Cheng Zhao, who only went once every three days, was very obedient and didn't ask much.","When she went to the Second Madam's Jiangyun Courtyard, she met Zhou Yuanqi.","Zhou Yuanqi's copybook was fake, his silver notes were confiscated by his mother, and he received two lashes. His emotions towards Cheng Zhao were extremely complicated.","He was cold and aloof, ignoring Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao asked him, \"How is your learning?\"","He turned his head to the other side, showing that he was at odds with Cheng Zhao.","\"During the New Year, how about you go to the Cheng family with me to pay New Year's greetings? My grandfather likes children with good learning. If you don't make mistakes in answering his questions, I will ask him to give you two copybooks of Master Qu Lian,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi suddenly turned his head back.","The movement was so quick that Cheng Zhao was afraid he would sprain his neck.","\"Are you just talking big?\" he asked tentatively.","He coveted the copybooks very much, but he didn't want to reconcile with Cheng Zhao easily.","\"Believe it or not,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\""]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36: By Imperial Decree","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao was teasing Zhou Yuanqi when Zhou Yuanshen arrived.","Since the last time, the two of them hadn't seen each other for several days.","Cheng Zhao hadn't seen him in Chenhui Courtyard either.","However, she knew that he often rested in Lijing Courtyard. This was because the main kitchen would send his dinner there.","Coupled with the Emperor's frequent mention of the past, Zhou Yuanshen couldn't neglect Mu Jiang.","\"Where's Mother?\" he asked.","Cheng Zhao thought he was asking Zhou Yuanqi, and Zhou Yuanqi thought he was asking Cheng Zhao, so neither answered, letting the Duke's question fall flat.","The room was briefly awkward.","Fortunately, the clever senior maid bringing in tea chimed in, \"The Old Madam called the Madam to Shou'an Courtyard.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, the Second Madam returned.","She didn't look very happy.","Cheng Zhao quickly stood up, helped the Second Madam take off her cloak, and handed her the hand warmer from the maid.","After she sat down and ordered the maid to serve tea, Cheng Zhao asked, \"What did Grandmother call you for?\"","\"Nothing much. Laba is the Dharma Treasure Festival, and she wants us to accompany her to Jin'an Temple to burn incense and listen to the monks chant,\" the Second Madam said.","She added, \"We have to go every year, attend the evening and morning sessions, and stay overnight.\"","She looked very annoyed.","The Second Madam didn't believe in Buddhism.","Cheng Zhao said, \"She didn't call me.\"","\"Lady Huan isn't going either,\" the Second Madam said, as if to comfort Cheng Zhao. \"She just called Madam Song and me to go with her.\"","Cheng Zhao understood.","Zhou Yuanqi couldn't interject, so he sat obediently to the side.","Zhou Yuanshen spoke up, \"Grandmother called me to go too.\"","Second Madam: \"Then you go too.\"","Annoyed, she ordered the maids to pack for the trip to Jin'an Temple with the Old Madam tomorrow.","The Second Master returned home in the mid-afternoon.","The government offices were busy before the New Year. The only one not busy was probably Zhou Yuanshen, whose status was unusual now, being the Emperor's favorite.","After dinner, the Second Master called Zhou Yuanshen to the outer study; father and son had matters to discuss.","Zhou Yuanqi, curious, wanted to join the fun. Given that he had previously revealed the secret that Zhou Yuanshen might take on two branches of the family, the Second Master forbade him from following and shooed him away.","Cheng Zhao returned to Nonghua Courtyard.","Since Zhou Yuanshen hadn't said in advance that he was coming, Cheng Zhao didn't wait for him, eating and resting on her own.","The next day, the Second Madam went to Jin'an Temple.","She didn't return until the ninth day of the twelfth lunar month.","With the First Madam, Madam Song, away, Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang held down the fort at Chengming Hall.","This time, the sisters-in-law talked for quite a while, seemingly getting along well; in reality, they were probing each other.","Cheng Zhao didn't know what Huan Qingtang had found out, but she hadn't uncovered Huan Qingtang's true situation. After all, they couldn't talk too deeply.","On the mid-afternoon of the ninth, the Old Madam's party returned to the manor.","Huan Qingtang went to the gate to welcome them, and Cheng Zhao followed.","Unexpectedly, Mu Jiang also got out of the carriage.","Huan Qingtang observed Cheng Zhao from the corner of her eye.","Cheng Zhao's expression didn't change at all.","When Huan Qingtang stepped forward to support the Old Madam's hand, flanking her with Mu Jiang, Cheng Zhao didn't try to compete.","She went to receive her own mother-in-law.","When Huan Qingtang turned around, she saw her mother-in-law, Madam Song, getting out of the carriage alone, with no one to help her.","With Cheng Zhao as a contrast, Huan Qingtang's behavior of crowding the Old Madam despite knowing Mu Jiang was there, while neglecting her own mother-in-law, was seen by many.","Her face paled slightly as she said something to the Old Madam, then turned towards Madam Song.","To everyone's surprise, Madam Song lost her temper on the spot and shook off her hand.","Huan Qingtang froze.","Mu Jiang couldn't help but smile.","Huan Qingtang looked wretched and embarrassed, her face turning from pale to red.","\"Let's go in quickly, it's so cold outside.\" The Old Madam turned back, looking at Madam Song with a smiling face.","Madam Song forced a smile: \"Mother, take your time.\"","She personally went over to help the Old Madam step over the threshold.","The Second Madam watched the drama, feeling somewhat pleased.","Zhou Yuanshen stood to the side, saying nothing and showing no expression from start to finish.","Everyone got into their own small oil carriages. As Cheng Zhao was helping the Second Madam, Zhou Yuanshen walked over and said to Cheng Zhao, \"I will dine at Nonghua Courtyard tonight.\"","The Second Madam frowned.","She seemed to want to say something.","But Cheng Zhao had already agreed.","On the way back, the Second Madam's expression was dark and very displeased.","\"Mother, what happened? You look very unhappy,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam: \"It's nothing.\"","\"Why keep it from me? Does it concern me?\" Cheng Zhao asked with a smile.","Second Madam: \"Not really. I'm just afraid it will disgust you.\"","Cheng Zhao thought for a moment. What could be disgusting?","\"Last night in the guest room at Jin'an Temple, did the Duke sleep with the Secondary Wife?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Second Madam: \"How did you...\"","Cheng Zhao: \"What's the big deal? Mother, both the Secondary Wife and I belong to the Duke.\"","Second Madam: \"...\"","She still found it disgusting.","Jin'an Temple was bustling with incense offerings, so guest rooms were hard to book, and the courtyards were small.","The Second Madam had assumed Zhou Yuanshen would stay at the front and squeeze in with the monks.","Unexpectedly, he shared a room with Mu Jiang.","Staying together was one thing, but they caused a commotion in the middle of the night. The courtyard was too small, and the windows and doors were too thin.","It was the first time the Second Madam realized how shameless Mu Jiang was; the way she called out \"Third Brother\" was simply unbearable to hear.","If the Second Madam heard it, who among the Old Madam, the First Madam, and the other maids and servants didn't?","It was mortifying.","In a sacred Buddhist place, no less.","When she got up in the morning, the Second Madam had a long face, intending to reprimand Zhou Yuanshen.","But the Old Madam was smiling, looking to be in a good mood.","So the Second Madam didn't dare to act out of line.","If Cheng Zhao knew her husband and his concubine had such a merry night in a temple guest room, right in front of the family elders, she would be disgusted too.","She hadn't wanted to say anything.","But since Cheng Zhao had guessed it, and she was a married woman, the Second Madam spoke without restraint.","\"...Even the top courtesans in the brothels aren't as wanton as her.\"","Cheng Zhao didn't laugh or change her expression, but said seriously, \"Mother, just telling me is enough. Don't go spreading this around.\"","\"Do I even need to? Don't those maids and servants have mouths?\" the Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao: \"I heard from my grandfather that His Majesty told the Duke to have a child with Mu Jiang as soon as possible. This is consummation by imperial decree.\"","\"What?\"","Cheng Zhao then told the Second Madam what her grandfather had heard in the imperial study.","The Second Madam was horrified: \"Absurd! Does Yuanshen actually believe such words? The Emperor is clearly out of his mind.\"","\"Even if the Duke doesn't believe it, he has to put on a show,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"At the very least, he has to show the Emperor that he tried.\"","The Second Madam was stunned.","For a moment, she felt both angry and heartbroken for her son.","The Emperor and the Old Madam were forcing Zhou Yuanshen to be a lapdog for imperial power and the family, not treating him like a human being at all.","No wonder it was so awkward; Zhou Yuanshen had no choice but to do it, at least to let the Old Madam hear.","And no wonder the Old Madam was satisfied.","The Second Madam felt a bitter ache in her heart: \"Yuanshen never even wanted the Zhou family's title.\"","\"Mother, things have come to this point. Who can jump ship now? We're already tied together,\" Cheng Zhao said.","In the evening, when Cheng Zhao returned from Jiangyun Courtyard to Nonghua Courtyard, the maid said the Duke had arrived.","\"Set the table,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She turned and went into the inner bedroom.","The maid followed, intending to help Cheng Zhao change her clothes, but Zhou Yuanshen stepped forward, picked Cheng Zhao up in his arms, and placed her on the bed.","Cheng Zhao was slightly startled.","His hand lifted her skirt."]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37: Don't Hold a Grudge Against Me from Now On","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao pressed her hand over Zhou Yuanshen's.","She heard the sound of the maid hastily retreating and closing the door; she remembered her mother-in-law describing what happened last night.","Cheng Zhao knew she had a decent marriage, and she ought to cherish it.","Unlike her third sister's aloofness, she wanted these worldly honors.","She also tried her best to cooperate with Zhou Yuanshen.","But she couldn't.","Not right now.","She couldn't accept it.","She stared at him intently, restraining the flames of anger in her eyes, wanting to say something reasonable, but then she heard him speak.","He said, \"Cheng Zhao, I gave you a chance. Don't blame me in the future.\"","He added, \"And tell your family not to resent me either.\"","He turned to leave.","Cheng Zhao understood what he meant.","Last night, he must have put all his effort into performing his duties with Mu Jiang, perhaps even using some more effective methods; Mu Jiang would likely end up pregnant.","This concubine, due to her connection with the Emperor, was already the center of attention, unlike other concubines; she was also highly regarded by the Old Madame.","If Mu Jiang were to get pregnant first, it would benefit everyone.","After the Emperor said those words, Zhou Yuanshen complied, and he would earn the Emperor's satisfaction; the Old Madame had been waiting for Mu Jiang to give birth first, and she would be pleased too.","As for Mu Jiang, having the eldest son would allow her to suppress Cheng Zhao at every turn in the future; with the Old Madame backing her, the eldest son might not even be called a concubine-born eldest son.","Zhou Yuanshen could do nothing and just reap the benefits.","The only one at a disadvantage was Cheng Zhao.","When that time came, her situation would become even more difficult.","But if Cheng Zhao were to get pregnant at the same time, she might just manage to give birth first if she tried hard enough.","Giving birth even a moment earlier meant getting ahead; if she was even luckier, and Mu Jiang had a girl while she had a boy, bearing Zhou Yuanshen's legitimate eldest son would result in a win-win for both her and Zhou Yuanshen in the future.","When Zhou Yuanshen told her family not to resent him, he had probably seen the Cheng family's attitude toward Zhang Yunqi.","Zhang Yunqi had kept a mistress outside, trampling on the Cheng family's dignity, and the Cheng family didn't even bother to maintain a facade of politeness.","If Mu Jiang got pregnant and Cheng Zhao didn't, outsiders would definitely belittle Cheng Zhao. Cheng Zhao would suffer grievances when socializing, and how would her maiden family view Zhou Yuanshen then?","At that point, it wouldn't be as simple as just getting him drunk.","These considerations were truly for Cheng Zhao's sake.","Cheng Zhao quickly understood. She took a few steps forward and grabbed his hand.","\"Duke, I was wrong just now,\" she said. \"You... please don't go...\"","Zhou Yuanshen turned his head.","Cheng Zhao gripped his hand tightly, but her eyes felt terribly dry and sore.","Zhou Yuanshen's finger gently wiped away a tear that had fallen from her eye.","\"Cheng Zhao, what are you feeling wronged about?\" he asked, though his voice was not cold.","His breath was somewhat scorching.","Someone who was usually as cold as ice now breathed with a scalding heat, like a burning brazier.","\"Have I not tried my best to be a good husband to you?\" he asked. \"You are not pregnant, do you blame me?\"","Cheng Zhao shook her head.","\"I don't feel wronged, and I don't blame you,\" she said.","It was just that this was not the kind of marriage she approved of.","Her parents, her eldest sister and brother-in-law, her second brother and sister-in-law, they didn't live like this.","Her third sister's marriage was terrible, but outsiders knew of her hardships and sympathized with her.","What about Cheng Zhao?","On their first night of consummation, her husband had covered her face with her hair as if she were unbearably ugly, and pressed her face into the pillow.","He had never faced her directly.","Cheng Zhao was treated like livestock being bred.","Wasn't she his wife?","But Cheng Zhao couldn't take matters of the boudoir outside to complain about.","She had been granted this marriage by imperial decree, and she had received an official title; this was already better than most. The stabbing pain she felt in her marriage could not be confided to anyone.","This was a matter between her and Zhou Yuanshen alone.","\"Please don't go.\" Cheng Zhao raised her eyes, the moisture in them fading away. \"I promise, from now on you will never see a wronged expression on my face. I am not unwilling.\"","Just as she had told him before, it was exactly what she wanted.","Cheng Zhao reached out and untied his sash.","Zhou Yuanshen watched her without moving.","The floor heating had not yet warmed up, and the bedroom was a bit cold; Cheng Zhao was cold too, seemingly trembling the whole time, so she tried hard to suppress it.","Her stomach cramped in waves, and she immediately forced herself to forget what her mother-in-law had described about the guest room at Jin'an Temple last night. She told herself she was probably just hungry.","Lying on her stomach again.","This time, Zhou Yuanshen's movements were a bit more brisk.","After it was over, he actually left.","Cheng Zhao did not get out of bed; she couldn't be bothered to wash up.","She didn't sleep either. Covered in blankets, she felt the bedroom's floor heating finally warm up, slowly bringing some heat.","In the second half of the night, she finally called the maid to bring in water for a simple wipe-down.","After that day, Cheng Zhao never saw Zhou Yuanshen again, nor did he come to Nonghua Courtyard to spend the night.","With the busy end of the year approaching, Cheng Zhao slowly pushed him to the back of her mind.","In the blink of an eye, it was New Year's Eve.","The New Year's Eve ancestral sacrifice was another grand drama, because the Old Madame told the First Madame, Madam Song, and Huan Qingtang to stand at the front, which displeased the Second Madame.","The Second Madame had endured it for nearly half a year and finally couldn't help but lash out.","\"Why do my daughter-in-law and I still have to stand in the back?\" the Second Madame asked.","The Old Madame didn't speak to her, but instead said to the Second Master, \"Teach your wife what rules are.\"","\"Mother, you don't need to make things difficult for us. If your rules were clear and strict, I wouldn't be saying this. You have to give us a reason,\" the Second Madame said.","\"Is contradicting the Old Madame reasonable? No reasoning can surpass filial piety,\" Mu Jiang, standing to the side, said coldly.","She was standing right next to the Old Madame.","Concubines generally did not participate in the New Year's Eve ancestral sacrifice. But with Mu Jiang attending, who dared to say a word of objection?","Huan Qingtang glanced at Mu Jiang and then lowered her gaze again.","\"Yes, filial piety is paramount.\"","As everyone fell silent, Zhou Yuanshen spoke up.","He affirmed Mu Jiang's words.","A smile immediately floated onto Mu Jiang's face.","\"Grandmother, if we are not dividing the household, please allow my mother to stand at the front. As a son, I cannot be unfilial,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Old Madame looked at him.","Zhou Yuanshen quietly looked back at her without blinking.","Just as the Old Madame was about to flare up, Zhou Yuanshen took a few steps forward and said softly, \"Grandmother, the sacrificial offerings from the palace have not yet been bestowed this year.\"","Every New Year's Eve, the Emperor would bestow sacrificial offerings upon noble families to show imperial favor.","In previous years, the Old Madame was the one called to receive the imperial decree for these offerings.","What about this year?","Zhou Yuanshen had put in a lot of effort for the Emperor this year, and he had already inherited the title. According to old customs, only he was qualified to receive the decree.","The rewards hadn't arrived yet, and it was still undecided who would receive them.","It was a psychological battle at this moment.","\"Madam Fan, you stand here,\" the Old Madame finally spoke after exchanging a few glances with Zhou Yuanshen.","She had compromised.","The Second Madame was slightly stunned. Without showing joy, she simply asked, \"What about my daughter-in-law?\"","\"If you continue to nitpick, you can go back,\" the Old Madame said.","Cheng Zhao squeezed the Second Madame's hand, urging her to step forward. Regardless, winning one position for now was acceptable; they could take it slowly in the future.","Just as the Second Madame took her place, the sacrificial offerings bestowed by the imperial court arrived.","This time, the Emperor still called for the Old Madame to receive the decree.","The Old Madame breathed a sigh of relief; she then looked at Zhou Yuanshen, her gaze unreadable.","It seemed to say: \"You are still a bit too young to challenge me. Before the Emperor, I will always be the first person.\"","Yet it also seemed to say, \"You are very good at playing with people's minds; you actually bluffed me. A person of my age showing timidity in front of you.\"","The grandparent and grandchild met each other's gaze, neither of them saying a word."]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38: The Concubine Is Pregnant","paragraphs":["The Zhou family's New Year's Eve was very lively.","After the ancestral worship at the Duke's estate concluded, there was another ceremony at the main Zhou family shrine.","The main shrine accommodated hundreds of men and women.","After the ceremony, the Old Madam invited the collateral branches over to stay up together for New Year's Eve.","The collateral branches consisted of the descendants of Zhou Yuanshen's grandfather's brothers and cousins.","There were many of them; some had even lived in the Chen Duke's estate before moving out.","Thus, among these people, some watched like tigers eyeing their prey, their eyes filled with greed and wildness, making Cheng Zhao feel uneasy just looking at them.","But the Old Madam's gaze upon them was like a master teasing naughty kittens; everything was firmly under her control.","Meeting the Old Madam's eyes, those people immediately became docile.","Cheng Zhao sat with the members of the Second Branch.","Zhou Yuanshen, however, did not share a table with them. He sat beside the Old Madam, accompanied by Mu Jiang, First Madam Madam Song, and Huan Qingtang.","Mu Jiang enjoyed every privilege, yet no one dared utter a single word.","The only one who dared to speak was the Second Madam. She was about to open her mouth again.","Cheng Zhao held her hand: Mother, these rose melon seeds smell so good. How are they roasted?","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law listened to the opera and discussed food. The Second Madam did not look over there anymore to avoid getting annoyed.","She understood what Cheng Zhao meant.","Earlier during the ancestral worship at the Duke's estate, Zhou Yuanshen and the Old Madam had a silent contest, and Zhou Yuanshen won. But the Emperor still trusted the Old Madam the most.","Zhou Yuanshen had narrowly won a round; if the Second Madam made a fuss now, it would give the Old Madam an excuse to lash out at Zhou Yuanshen.","...Come, kowtow to your great-aunt. Amidst the chatting and laughing over there, a woman in her thirties led a child over.","Seeing this child, First Madam Madam Song showed a bit of tender affection in her eyes.","The little boy was about five or six years old. He had lost his front baby teeth, making his smile look endearingly silly and very cute.","He bowed respectfully.","What a smart and lively boy. The Old Madam chuckled and patted the child's head, instructing a maid to hand him a purse.","The purse contained silver ingots, the Old Madam's New Year's reward for the children.","The child was led away, and a woman in her fifties, likely one of Zhou Yuanshen's great-aunts, smiled and asked the Old Madam, Sister-in-law, do you like that child very much?","He is very cute.","He looks a bit like Yuancheng, the great-aunt said.","Yuancheng was Zhou Yuanshen's eldest cousin, the original heir of the Zhou family.","First Madam Madam Song's eyes grew a little moist upon hearing someone mention her son.","The Old Madam, however, smiled, I am getting old and can't quite remember. I only recall what Yuancheng looked like when he got married.","She then said to Madam Song, Does he look like Yuancheng when he was little? I don't think they look very much alike.","First Madam Madam Song replied, He does, Mother.","The great-aunt then asked, Sister-in-law, are you planning to adopt this child for the First Branch?","As soon as this was said, the entire venue fell silent, leaving only the sound of gongs and drums from the opera stage.","The stage was a bit far away, lively but not noisy.","Cheng Zhao looked over.","For a moment, she couldn't figure out who was actually directing this scene.","This great-aunt, who could sit beside the Old Madam, wouldn't possibly say something foolish.","Every word and action had underlying conflicts of interest.","The Old Madam's expression did not change.","First Madam Madam Song looked at her eagerly, as if waiting for an answer.","An adopted child's bloodline is distant. Talking about the First Branch or Second Branch is flattering them. They are all juniors, all part of the Duke's estate. From now on, let's just be one close family, the Old Madam said.","The great-aunt seemed very surprised: One close family? Sister-in-law, I don't quite understand. How will we be one close family?","The Old Madam smiled, Figure it out yourself.","The great-aunt thought for a moment: I'm thinking, could it be that the Duke will assume dual inheritance? If so, both branches would be fulfilled, and we would never be separated.","Cheng Zhao understood this time.","This great-aunt was the Old Madam's person. She was speaking on behalf of the Old Madam, using New Year's Eve to convey what the Old Madam wanted to say.","The collateral relatives present were all shocked to hear this.","Perhaps in their eyes, dual inheritance was something only merchants or poor families did, and it wasn't quite honorable; a Duke shouldn't stoop to such a thing.","But the Old Madam had spoken, and who dared to disobey her?","Everyone looked at the sisters-in-law, the First and Second Madams.","They thought the Second Madam would fly into a rage.","Yet the Second Madam sat quietly.","First Madam Madam Song paled: Aunt, don't make wild guesses. What kind of joke is this? It's truly frightening.","The Old Madam looked at her quietly.","First Madam Madam Song's hands trembled in disbelief.","Huan Qingtang sat there quietly, enduring the scrutinizing gazes. She was quiet and dignified, perfectly holding the demeanor of a noble family's matriarch.","Just as unfazed as her was the Duke's wife, Cheng Zhao.","These two young daughters-in-law truly made people look at them with new respect; neither was a pushover.","There was another person who was greatly shocked, and that was Mu Jiang.","Mu Jiang suddenly lost her temper at the great-aunt: What nonsense are you talking about? At your age, have you gone senile?","Her voice was fierce.","The Old Madam seemed to sigh: Ah Jiang, apologize to your great-aunt. Shouting and yelling, what does that look like.","Mu Jiang was like a cat raised by the Old Madam. She extended her sharp claws to scratch people, and the Old Madam, seemingly thinking she wouldn't understand a lecture, just reached out and tapped her lightly on the forehead.","She told her in a casual tone not to run wild.","As for the others, who dared to argue with the Old Madam's people?","The great-aunt smiled: The Secondary Wife is right, I am truly old. Sister-in-law, I will come around more often in the future. If you don't move around when you get old, your brain doesn't work well.","The Old Madam smiled: Come often, I always hope to have someone to share intimate chats with. We have been sisters-in-law for decades, and you suit my temper the most.","Mu Jiang's face was full of anger, yet she still had to apologize: Great-aunt, I was rash just now. Please don't hold it against a junior.","Of course, of course, the great-aunt smiled.","With this commotion, the entire Zhou clan knew that the Duke's estate's pie would not be shared with the clansmen, and they shouldn't harbor any crooked ideas.","The Old Madam was going to stuff the whole pie into Zhou Yuanshen's arms.","Zhou Yuanshen had never been well-liked since he was a child. It was said that when he studied at the clan school, he outshone his eldest cousin, causing a rift between the brothers.","Later, it was said he didn't want to study anymore and went to the frontier.","It seemed like he was yielding to his cousin, and the Old Madam even praised him for being humble.","Unexpectedly, after the second young master died prematurely, the eldest young master's health also failed, and he passed away within two years, leaving the First Branch without an heir.","Zhou Yuanshen was older than his two younger brothers, making him suitable to inherit the title and the dual inheritance.","The Zhou family's wealth and status all fell onto his shoulders alone.","To put it bluntly, so did the women.","Huan Qingtang was exceptionally beautiful and came from a noble background; Mu Jiang was charming and lovely with an extraordinary background. They both belonged to Zhou Yuanshen, which was tacitly approved by the Old Madam.","The Empress had also bestowed upon him a legitimate wife as exquisite and beautiful as jade.","There was no need to guess; throughout the spring banquets of the first lunar month, everyone would be discussing this matter of the Chen Duke's estate.","The Old Madam wanted to build momentum for Huan Qingtang.","Cheng Zhao knew she might be slandered. Only by stepping on one could another be elevated.","The Second Madam also worried for Cheng Zhao.","It's fine, I have my imperial mandate, Cheng Zhao remained relatively optimistic.","She held no grievances.","However, things did not go as the Second Madam and Cheng Zhao had anticipated, with Huan Qingtang stealing the spotlight at the New Year spring banquets.","Because Mu Jiang stole all the thunder.","She was pregnant."]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39: Having Money Is a Good Thing","paragraphs":["As a titled lady, Cheng Zhao attended the spring banquets hosted by the aristocratic families of the capital.","She always attended these banquets with the Second Madam. Under normal circumstances, the hosts would also invite Huan Qingtang and the First Madam.","Outsiders were all eager for a good show, as the matter of the \"dual inheritance marriage\" had already caused a huge uproar.","However, both Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang displayed the refined upbringing of scholarly families. Their words and actions were elegant and graceful, leaving no room for anyone to find fault.","On the surface, they appeared perfectly harmonious.","With the two younger women saving face for the family, the First and Second Madams, as sisters-in-law, seemed afraid of being outshone by their daughters-in-law and vied to present themselves well too.","This picture of peace and amiability created the exact situation the Old Madam desired most.","Even though Huan Qingtang failed to overshadow Cheng Zhao, the Old Madam was still pleased.","What pleased the Old Madam even more was that Mu Jiang started showing signs of pregnancy, vomiting incessantly in the mornings. An imperial physician was summoned to check her pulse, confirming that she was indeed expecting.","Overjoyed, the Old Madam personally entered the palace to report the good news to the Emperor.","The Emperor rewarded Mu Jiang with many fine gifts and even ordered the Empress to send two senior maids experienced in caring for pregnant women to the Zhou family, specifically to look after Mu Jiang.","\"Even a princess would only receive such treatment.\"","The servants of the Chenguo Duke's estate gossiped among themselves.","Cheng Zhao, however, thought to herself, \"If she were truly treated like a princess, she would have been given a title long ago. Even if she couldn't be named a princess, wouldn't they at least give her the empty title of a commandery princess or a county princess? Would they let a princess be a concubine?\"","From this, it was clear that the Emperor had other intentions and did not care about Mu Jiang at all.","The Old Madam was merely using this to add prestige to the Zhou family.","Outside, those with ulterior motives had their own varied opinions on the matter.","Cheng Zhao counted the days; her monthly courses were delayed by five days.","Her heart skipped a beat.","She tried her best to suppress her joy, planning to wait another two days before calling for a doctor.","\"I don't feel like vomiting,\" Cheng Zhao only told her three trusted confidantes. \"Calling for a doctor at this time would look like I'm trying to compete with the Secondary Wife.\"","Qiubai was very nervous. \"Then you must be careful. Starting today, you cannot practice your swordplay in the mornings.\"","Suyue suggested, \"How about I secretly inform the Second Madam and ask her to send for a doctor to come in through the side gate to take a look?\"","Nanny Li stopped the two of them.","\"Don't panic just yet. The Young Madam's concerns are correct. At a time like this, even if she is pregnant, we must be wary of someone trying to frame or harm her, let alone when it's not even certain,\" Nanny Li said.","Cheng Zhao nodded in agreement.","After speaking, Nanny Li could not help but ask with concern, \"Do you feel any tightness in your chest or bloating in your stomach?\"","Cheng Zhao carefully felt her body for a moment.","She shook her head. \"No, I feel no different than usual.\"","She did not go to Chengming Hall to handle affairs that morning. Instead, she sat at the desk in the eastern side room practicing calligraphy, gently touching her stomach from time to time.","It didn't feel like she was pregnant at all.","Cheng Zhao's luck always seemed rather ordinary. Every time she hoped for something, it generally didn't go her way; what she wanted, she usually only got when she wasn't paying attention.","She truly hoped to get pregnant quickly so she could ignore Zhou Yuanshen for a year or half.","But the more she hoped, the more likely she was to be disappointed.","That day, Zhou Yuanshen came to Nonghua Courtyard again.","After dinner, the couple sat on the large heated brick bed by the window, playing chess.","The spring banquets were very lively this year, and he had visited many households as well.","He had also accompanied Cheng Zhao back to her maiden home to pay New Year greetings.","Cheng Zhao had even brought Zhou Yuanqi along. She led Zhou Yuanqi to her grandfather, and sure enough, her grandfather gifted him two copybooks of Master Qu Lian's calligraphy.","Her grandfather even said, \"If there are any other books or copybooks you like but don't have, just come and ask me for them.\"","Zhou Yuanqi was so moved he almost cried.","Cheng Zhao teased him a few times. Because of this, the two who went to the Cheng family for New Year greetings had a very pleasant time, and consequently, Zhou Yuanshen seemed to be in a good mood as well.","During the New Year banquet, no one in the Cheng family forced him to drink.","They didn't even mention the matter of the \"dual inheritance marriage.\"","Sitting on the heated bed by the window playing chess at this moment, both Cheng Zhao and he were preoccupied with their own thoughts, making a complete mess of the chessboard.","\"From my monthly allowance, I will subsidize Nonghua Courtyard with one hundred taels every month,\" Zhou Yuanshen suddenly said.","Cheng Zhao asked, \"Will you have enough for yourself then?\"","As the Duke's wife, the Zhou family's public account gave her a monthly allowance of two hundred taels.","Cheng Zhao couldn't spend it all.","She also had her own dowry, the dowry rewarded to her by the Ministry of Rites, and so on.","However, if Zhou Yuanshen was willing to subsidize her, she had no reason to refuse.","She just didn't know what sudden madness had taken hold of him.","\"It's enough,\" Zhou Yuanshen said. \"I also need to subsidize Lijing Courtyard a bit every month; her monthly allowance isn't much.\"","Cheng Zhao understood.","\"It's only right, as she is pregnant,\" Cheng Zhao said.","After saying that, she looked at Zhou Yuanshen's face.","Coincidentally, Zhou Yuanshen was looking at her too.","Both sets of eyes held a probing look, and their gazes met squarely.","Seeing that his expression was fine, Cheng Zhao said, \"Congratulations, Your Grace.\"","Although he had to be manipulated by the Old Madam, he had ultimately completed the task given by the Emperor and could gain more imperial favor.","Imperial favor was his opportunity to climb higher and break free from constraints.","Choosing the lesser of two evils. If it weren't for the Emperor, Mu Jiang would never have gotten pregnant so easily; Zhou Yuanshen had compromised on this matter.","\"...What about you?\" he asked. \"I haven't deliberately neglected you.\"","Cheng Zhao understood what he meant. He was saying that around the Laba Festival, he had done his duty as a husband with both women, giving Cheng Zhao a chance as well.","Just as she was about to speak, she felt a sudden, heavy ache in her lower abdomen.","It felt exactly like this every time her monthly courses arrived, and her heart sank.","It wasn't that she was afraid of losing to Mu Jiang; she simply didn't want to go through the torment with Zhou Yuanshen again.","She didn't answer him, getting up and heading to the washroom.","Her menses had arrived.","When Cheng Zhao didn't come out for a long while, Zhou Yuanshen walked to the door of the washroom and asked, \"Are you unwell?\"","\"I'm fine,\" Cheng Zhao replied.","Only when she came out did she tell Zhou Yuanshen that her time of the month had come again.","She wasn't pregnant.","Zhou Yuanshen remained expressionless.","He merely said, \"Then let's rest early.\"","Lying in bed, Cheng Zhao thought that her delayed period might have been caused by his torment, which left her body somewhat weak; and his methods on her were truly ineffective.","How was Mu Jiang so lucky?","\"It's not really luck. He spends more days at Mu Jiang's place. With more time, the chances of getting pregnant are naturally higher.\"","Cheng Zhao instantly stopped feeling envious.","She couldn't withstand that kind of grinding torment.","The next day, the manager from the accounting room indeed came to Nonghua Courtyard, informing Cheng Zhao that Nonghua Courtyard could collect three hundred taels of monthly allowance, with the Duke personally subsidizing one hundred taels.","Cheng Zhao thanked him, tipped him with a purse, and asked, \"Has the subsidy for the Secondary Wife been arranged as well?\"","\"Yes, the Secondary Wife gets an additional fifty taels,\" the manager replied.","Cheng Zhao had someone see him out.","She said to her confidantes, \"It's a good thing we didn't call for a doctor. If word had gotten out, I would have slapped my own face today and made a huge joke of myself.\"","Nanny Li felt a bit heartbroken for her.","She comforted her, \"It's good to be cautious. The days are still long, Young Madam.\"","Cheng Zhao nodded.","Suyue added, \"The Secondary Wife is pregnant, but you also gained an extra one hundred taels in your monthly allowance. In short, you didn't come away empty-handed.\"","\"Money is just as good. A child might not be as reliable as money when it comes to knowing when you're cold or hot,\" Qiubai also chimed in.","Cheng Zhao burst into laughter.","Seeing her laugh, Nanny Li breathed a sigh of relief. \"What kind of soup would you like to drink?\"","\"Black chicken soup with red dates, and some red date cakes,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Make some extra to send to my mother-in-law and Fifth Brother. The weather is still cold, so eating more of these nourishing foods is good for the body.\"","Nanny Li hurried off to prepare them.","When Cheng Zhao delivered the soup and pastries to Jiangyun Courtyard, the Second Madam was currently fuming over the news of Mu Jiang's pregnancy."]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40: Zhou Yuanshen's Punishment","paragraphs":["Second Madam had been angry since New Year's Eve, holding in a belly full of fire.","\"...Why does he still subsidize her with fifty taels of silver every month?\" Second Madam scolded Zhou Yuanshen to Cheng Zhao. \"Dowager Madame has money to subsidize her.\"","\"Mother, the Duke also subsidizes me,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam did not know about this yet.","Mu Jiang had shouted about it until the whole courtyard knew, but Cheng Zhao had not mentioned it.","\"How much does he subsidize you?\"","\"One hundred taels a month.\"","Second Madam could not help but laugh. \"Yuanshen is quite an interesting person. If you say he is mature and old-fashioned, he can do that kind of thing in a temple; but if you say he is dissolute and frivolous, he keeps the rules of wives and concubines very strictly. I really do not know him.\"","Giving Mu Jiang fifty taels, he gave Cheng Zhao one hundred taels.","No matter how much merit a concubine achieved, she must be beneath the primary wife.","\"Tell me, if he really takes on the dual-lineage heir duty, how will he settle you and Lady Huan? How will the two of you divide the senior and junior roles?\" Second Madam asked.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","On New Year's Eve, Dowager Madame revealed the intention of a dual-lineage heir, which was like a muffled thunder striking everyone's heart, shocking everyone into a loss for what to do.","Second Madam initially thought it was just a casual remark.","Since Dowager Madame brought it out into the open, the matter was set in stone.","Second Madam's heart ached for her daughter-in-law, feeling that Cheng Zhao was very pitiful. Of course, all the women in the inner courtyard were pitiful; everyone was in a sorry state, including Second Madam herself.","What was the point?","On second thought, being pitiful was not unique to the women of their family.","From top to bottom, which woman did not suffer?","In poor families, women had to work in the fields and leave the solid rice for the men and children while drinking thin porridge themselves; if slightly wealthy, the family would have flocks of wives and concubines.","The women of the Zhou family fought back and forth, but at least they had noble titles, estates, and imperial mandates. What did the women of ordinary families have? Just a few pieces of fabric, and didn't they still have to break their heads fighting for them?","Living was truly a suffering.","Second Madam decided that she would neither make things difficult for herself nor for her daughter-in-law.","They had so many difficulties; they always had to treat themselves a little better.","\"...Mother, I have the title of an imperial mandate lady. If the Duke handles things according to the rules, I am still the highest,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam was lost in her own thoughts, unable to return to her senses, and her tone was a bit depressed: \"What is the use of being the highest? Isn't it still living a stifling life for a lifetime?\"","\"If I am stifled, others are just as stifled. Anyway, I am the highest,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She only pursued glory.","When she reached the age of Dowager Madame, the imperial court rewarding New Year's Eve sacrificial items directly to her, bypassing the children and grandchildren, would be the highest achievement of an imperial mandate lady.","That was also Cheng Zhao's goal.","She would definitely have to suffer some grievances.","She would inevitably succeed.","Second Madam reached out and touched her hair. \"You child! I really cannot understand the thoughts in the heads of you girls from scholarly families.\"","Cheng Zhao held her hand, and the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law smiled at each other.","The red date black chicken soup was very delicious; the red date cake was sweet but not cloying, and Second Madam loved it very much, leaving only a little for Zhou Yuanqi.","After Mu Jiang became pregnant, Zhou Yuanshen stopped staying at Lijing Courtyard.","He spent half a month at Chenhui Courtyard and the other half at Nonghua Courtyard. That he stayed at Chenhui Courtyard was judged by Cheng Zhao based on where his dinner was served.","During the early stages of her pregnancy, Mu Jiang vomited so much that the sky spun and the earth went dark. She tormented the people in the main kitchen all day long, demanding all sorts of different things to eat.","And it was Cheng Zhao who managed the main kitchen.","\"The Duke subsidizes me with fifty taels of silver. Can I set up a small kitchen for myself?\" Mu Jiang asked Dowager Madame.","It just so happened that Cheng Zhao, the First Madam Madam Song, and Huan Qingtang were all reporting at Shou'an Courtyard.","Hearing this, Huan Qingtang glanced at Mu Jiang but did not say anything.","Dowager Madame smiled and said, \"You have to ask the Duchess; she manages the main kitchen now.\"","\"Grandmother, this matter should be handled as a special case. If you and the Duke agree, naturally a small kitchen can be added for Secondary Wife,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She refused to take the bait.","Concubines could not have their own small kitchens.","Under normal circumstances, apart from Dowager Madame and the lady of the house, no one could open their own private stove.","Some things represented status and position. For example, what clothes to wear and what jewelry to wear in the palace all had to be based on rank; it was not something you could do just because you had money.","Without that status, no matter how much money you had, you could not do it.","Cheng Zhao did not have a small kitchen. On her side, she set up a stove in the wing room to stew soup and make some small snacks. Full meals could also be made, but she did not touch them; this was about following the rules.","Mu Jiang was a concubine. If she wanted privileges, no one had the qualifications to agree except Dowager Madame and Zhou Yuanshen.","\"The child A-Jiang is carrying is the first of my great-grandchildren. With her starting things off, the descendants will flourish. Logically speaking, giving her a small kitchen is also permissible?\" Dowager Madame asked the First Madam.","The First Madam, Madam Song, smiled: \"Mother, if you agree, tell Cheng Shi to go to the main kitchen and give the order, and Secondary Wife's allowance will be separately allocated to Lijing Courtyard.\"","She did not get involved either.","Dowager Madame agreeing and Cheng Zhao handling the matter had nothing to do with her.","Mu Jiang tossed and turned for a few days, and seeing them making excuses, she became a bit annoyed.","\"I will go and tell the Duke myself,\" she said.","Cheng Zhao: \"Then I will wait for the Duke's instructions. Grandmother, do you think that is okay?\"","Mu Jiang wanting to bypass Dowager Madame herself was exactly what Cheng Zhao wished for.","She was very clever and knew how to chime in at the right time. If Mu Jiang had no one to protect her, it would be very difficult for her to have a good life under her hands.","Dowager Madame forced a smile. \"Then we will wait for the Duke to decide.\"","It was estimated that it would not work out. Zhou Yuanshen would not be willing to give anyone in the inner courtyard the opportunity to overstep the rules.","On this day, Mu Jiang specially waited for Zhou Yuanshen at Chenhui Courtyard.","Zhou Yuanshen rejected it without a second word.","\"If you do not like to eat, then take medicine. If you do not want to give birth, then do not give birth,\" he said lightly.","Mu Jiang was stunned. \"Third Brother, this is also your flesh and blood.\"","\"Then do not cause trouble, and nourish your pregnancy properly,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Mu Jiang felt extremely wronged, tightly clenching her fingers, very much wanting to have an argument with Zhou Yuanshen.","But she thought about it and held back.","If they argued, it would only benefit Cheng Zhao. Perhaps even Huan Qingtang.","Between the two of them, one was more sinister than the other.","Mu Jiang swallowed this breath of anger.","However, enduring until the evening, she broke her composure and rushed to Nonghua Courtyard to settle the score with Cheng Zhao.","Her servants had heard from elsewhere that because of her pregnancy, Zhou Yuanshen subsidized Lijing Courtyard with fifty taels of silver, but subsidized Nonghua Courtyard with one hundred taels.","She was the one suffering, and Cheng Zhao got to benefit from it. She did not object to that, but Cheng Zhao could not get twice as much as her.","This was simply humiliating her.","Cheng Zhao did not let her enter the courtyard gates.","\"Go and tell Dowager Madame. If Secondary Wife goes crazy, she must be sent to the estate to nourish her pregnancy,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Mu Jiang's managing old maidservant persuaded her to go back.","Zhou Yuanshen grounded her.","She cried and complained that he was heartless and ungrateful, but Zhou Yuanshen remained unmoved.","\"She is pregnant...\" Dowager Madame felt a bit powerless, wanting to say a few good words.","Zhou Yuanshen then said, \"Having a pregnancy makes her hot-headed. Once she does something wrong, you and His Majesty will lose face along with her. Lock her up for two months first. Wait until she passes the early stages of pregnancy and her mood stabilizes, then let her out.\"","Dowager Madame: \"...\"","With the pregnant Secondary Wife being grounded, the prestige brought by her pregnancy was instantly shattered.","Dowager Madame had nothing to say.","This was Mu Jiang handing over the knife herself; Dowager Madame could not blame anyone else.","\"How did A-Jiang know about Nonghua Courtyard getting an extra one hundred taels of monthly allowance?\" Dowager Madame asked. \"Did Cheng Shi deliberately provoke her and tell her? Go and investigate.\""]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41: It Was Cheng Zhao Who Was Stirring Up Trouble","paragraphs":["Mu Jiang was grounded.","The Old Madam needed a \"protocol\" for doing things; everything had to follow the rules. Simply put, when beating or scolding servants or juniors, an excuse was required.","Zhou Yuanshen turned her own weapon against her, using the excuse of \"considering the heirs\" to place Mu Jiang under house arrest in Lijing Courtyard.","The Duke's estate was once again buzzing with discussion.","The servants were confused for a moment.","The concubine's status was extraordinary, and she was pregnant with a child, so how could the Duke treat her so indifferently?","The Eldest Young Madam, Huan Qingtang, came to Chengming Hall.","From the end of the year until the Lantern Festival, Chengming Hall did not handle official estate duties. The First Madam, Madam Song, sat in the eastern side room drinking tea and chatting about trivial matters with her trusted confidante.","\"Mother, your daughter-in-law has something to say to you,\" Huan Qingtang said.","Madam Song dismissed her confidante.","\"Why the troubled face?\" Madam Song slowly sipped her tea.","Huan Qingtang asked, \"Mother, why did you tell Mu Jiang about the Duke subsidizing the monthly allowances of the two places?\"","Madam Song set down her teacup, her face darkening. \"You are questioning me?\"","\"The Old Madam already knows,\" Huan Qingtang said.","Madam Song's expression twisted slightly. \"You are of one mind with the Old Madam now, do you even respect me anymore?\"","Huan Qingtang looked at her in confusion. \"What do you mean by that, Mother?\"","\"Did you know about the dual-lineage inheritance beforehand?\"","Huan Qingtang looked at her, her gaze calm and composed. \"Mother, you advised me several times to have a child of my own.\"","\"Lady Huan, you are playing dumb!\" the First Madam said resentfully.","Madam Song had known about the dual-lineage inheritance for a long time and thought it was an excellent idea. However, making it public in front of the clan members on New Year's Eve without telling her in advance was a different matter.","The First Madam always believed that her prestige in the Duke's estate was significant, second only to the Old Madam.","For such an important matter, they should have certainly communicated and discussed it properly before making it public.","As for how to announce it, they should have picked a more suitable time, instead of bringing a child who looked very much like her son to pay New Year's greetings on New Year's Eve, using that as an excuse to bring it up.","Madam Song had no choice but to quickly pretend she knew nothing about it.","The Old Madam had not only bypassed Madam Song, completely ignoring her, but had also used her deceased son to make a point: \"Even looking like Yuancheng doesn't qualify one to be the heir,\" forcing the clan members to give up their hopes.","At that moment, the First Madam was furious.","She was treated like a deaf and foolish person, and her deceased son was exploited. It was not only a show of contempt for her but also a rejection of her son.","And Huan Qingtang definitely knew.","The First Madam used to think that the dual-lineage inheritance was excellent, much better than adoption, because Huan Qingtang was on her side and utterly loyal to her.","Having a child of Lady Huan's own bloodline would better secure the First Madam's wealth and glory.","During the New Year, Huan Qingtang went to Shou'an Courtyard a few times, and she changed.","She became closer to the Old Madam.","With the comparison of the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law from the Second Branch, Madam Song grew suspicious of Huan Qingtang.","Once trust was broken, this dual-lineage inheritance would completely sideline the First Madam, just like on New Year's Eve, and she would reap no benefits.","Her husband and son were both gone, yet she was still hurriedly acting as a stepping stone for others.","She was absolutely resentful.","Having had to pretend she knew nothing on New Year's Eve, the indignation and embarrassment made Madam Song want to tear someone to pieces just thinking about it.","She did not dare disobey her mother-in-law, so she could only vent her anger on this widowed daughter-in-law.","\"...I actually think now that adoption would be better,\" Madam Song said coldly.","Huan Qingtang looked back at her, neither servile nor overbearing. \"Mother, these matters are decided by the elders. If you think it is good, then it is very good.\"","Madam Song choked on her words.","\"Are you talking back to me?\" Madam Song asked coldly.","Huan Qingtang's expression remained tranquil, like a willow swaying in a gentle breeze—slightly stirring but still gentle, without any great waves.","\"I wouldn't dare,\" Huan Qingtang said softly. \"Mother, your daughter-in-law just feels that Cheng Shi seems to have some capability.\"","Madam Song's chest tightened with anger. \"Don't drag others into this!\"","\"Mother, if you dislike your daughter-in-law, I won't dare to be an eyesore in front of you in the future. But I have a few words; would Mother be willing to listen?\" Huan Qingtang asked.","Madam Song only glared at her hatefully.","Huan Qingtang slowly began to speak.","\"Mother always told me to get close to the Old Madam. Only by gaining the Old Madam's favor can our mother-in-law and daughter-in-law pair securely hold our place in Chengming Hall forever.","Everything in the Duke's estate is in the Old Madam's hands, and we can only inherit from her. But on the Laba Festival, Cheng Shi merely supported our aunt, and Mother became angry.","I always thought Mother wouldn't take such a small matter to heart. Cheng Shi doesn't have the right to serve by the Old Madam's side, but Mother couldn't see that; you only saw that I didn't support you at that moment.","Mother used to say that an adopted son would always worship his biological parents after a hundred years, and it would have nothing to do with Yuancheng. Only a child I bear myself will worship my father-in-law, you, Yuancheng, and me.","But in such a short time, Mother has forgotten all of this and even deliberately tried to undermine me. You even attempted to spread rumors in my name, making the Old Madam think that I was the one who instigated Mu Jiang to cause trouble.\"","The First Madam calmed down a bit.","Huan Qingtang had mentioned the ancestral worship.","Asking Huan Qingtang to agree to the dual-lineage inheritance and have a child was not just for the management rights of Chengming Hall, but also for future ancestral sacrifices.","Huan Qingtang's son, in terms of bloodline, would not depart from the First Branch.","The First Madam was still angry, but her stance softened somewhat.","She had been blinded by anger.","\"...Mother, Cheng Shi truly has some capability. If she hadn't received an imperial mandate, you wouldn't care about her this much. The more you care about her, the easier it is to fall into her trap,\" Huan Qingtang said.","She continued, \"The title and properties of the Duke's estate should rightfully be yours. The Second Branch should live separately just like our granduncles, relying on whatever benefits slip through your fingers in the future to get by.","It is perfectly normal that you cannot stand Cheng Shi. However, before you have even done anything to Cheng Shi, you first suspect your own daughter-in-law. This pains me deeply.\"","Madam Song felt a wave of shame, followed by an inexplicable surge of annoyance. \"Are you accusing me?\"","\"I wouldn't dare,\" Huan Qingtang said, kneeling before her.","Tears quickly welled up in her eyes. \"Mother, we are the ones who depend on each other for survival. Without you, why would the Old Madam even pay attention to me? Without you, how could I ever compete with Cheng Shi and Mu Jiang?","You say I am accusing you, but I only want to wake you up. If you continue to be deceived, I will have no way out but death.\"","Seeing her cry, the irritation in Madam Song's heart dissipated significantly.","She sighed in silence.","After a long while, she finally said, \"Get up and wipe your tears. What do you look like crying and weeping like this? It makes it seem as if I have mistreated you.\"","Huan Qingtang stood up and wiped away her tears.","Madam Song fell silent for another moment before saying, \"In the future, when you go to the Old Madam, you must tell me early on if anything happens.","You cannot hide things from me. In this family, without me, you are nothing. It is good as long as you understand this principle.\"","Huan Qingtang murmured her agreement.","She left Chengming Hall and went to the Old Madam's Shou'an Courtyard.","She admitted that she was the one who found out about the matters of the public accounts and accidentally let it slip, which was how it reached Mu Jiang's ears.","\"You are a good child willing to take responsibility,\" the Old Madam said calmly. \"Ah Jiang is arrogant and willful; it's good to temper her character a bit. Besides, this is the Duke punishing her. It's just young people flirting and quarreling; we don't need to worry about them.\"","Huan Qingtang murmured her agreement.","The Old Madam went on to say that she would seek an imperial decree without delay, asking the Emperor to bestow a marriage and command Zhou Yuanshen to take Huan Qingtang as his concurrent primary wife.","\"I will leave everything for Grandmother to decide,\" Huan Qingtang replied.","Whenever this matter was brought up in the past, she had always remained completely silent. This was the very first time she had explicitly relented."]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42: Zhou Yuanshen's Invitation Was Rejected","paragraphs":["Once a person's heart changes, no matter how much sweet talk is used to make amends, cracks will always remain.","Eldest Madam's distrust of Huan Qingtang, once born, planted a seed. Even though she tried desperately to suppress it, the seed sprouted at the first sign of wind and rain, growing into a lush vine that climbed over her heart.","On the fourteenth day of the first lunar month, Cheng Zhao returned to her maiden home again.","Her siblings were discussing going to see the lanterns the next evening, planning to walk a large circle along the moat and not return until dawn the following day.","Fourth Brother said, I have booked Zuixian Restaurant. The seats on its second floor are perfectly situated to see this year's Lantern King.","Cheng Zhao did not have much interest in viewing lanterns along the river, but she did like seeing the Lantern King.","Tell Third Sister to restrain herself a bit this year. When she guesses lantern riddles along the street, she exposes all the gimmicks the merchants deliberately set up to stump scholars and attract tourists. There is not a single lantern riddle she cannot guess, Fourth Brother added.","Everyone laughed.","Cheng Zhao said, I like being with Third Sister. Whatever lantern I want, she can guess the riddle with just a glance. Whenever I go out with her, I never return empty-handed.","I do not like going out with her, Fourth Brother said.","Cheng Zhao replied, That is because she steals your thunder.","On the fifteenth day of the first lunar month the year before last, several girls from Cheng Zhao's relatives gathered together. Second Brother picked up Third Sister, and the large, lively group went to the lantern festival.","Fourth Brother Cheng Chao originally wanted to show off. But the lantern riddles that had him scratching his head in confusion, Cheng Ying knew the answers to with just a lift of her eyes.","The girls all ran after Cheng Ying, including Cheng Zhao.","Fourth Brother Cheng was so angry his teeth itched.","...This year I will remind Third Sister to restrain herself a bit, Eldest Sister said with a smile, then added to Fourth Brother Cheng, Aren't you just asking for trouble by comparing your knowledge with hers?","Everyone laughed.","Eldest Sister continued, Ask the Duke if he wants to view the lanterns with our family on the fifteenth.","Cheng Zhao's smile faded.","Seeing this, Eldest Sister smiled and said, If he is busy, bring your brother-in-law. That child is truly amusing.","Cheng Zhao said, I will ask him later.","She added, I might not be able to come out. Every family has different rules. Prince Jingnan's Mansion is willing to let Third Sister spend the holiday with her maiden family, but Duke Chen's Mansion might not.","Once you become someone's wife, you have to abide by their rules. Go back and ask first. If you really cannot come out, do not be upset; there will always be opportunities in the future, Eldest Sister said.","Cheng Zhao agreed.","She returned to Duke Chen's Mansion early that day and went straight to Jiangyun Courtyard.","She told Second Madam about going to see the lanterns the next evening.","Second Madam readily agreed, Just go, have a good time all night, and catch up on sleep on the sixteenth.","She added, When we were young, we also loved going to see the lanterns, but now we cannot stay up through the long night. However, your father-in-law and I will still go out to look at the lanterns, stroll for half an hour, and then come back.","Cheng Zhao smiled and said, That is very nice. I do not like strolling all night either. But with everyone urging me on, it is inconvenient to be a spoilsport. If I ruin the fun, no one will want to play with me in the future. Throughout the whole year, the Lantern Festival is the only time one can be this indulgent.","That makes sense.","Who is Yuanqi spending the holiday with? Cheng Zhao asked.","Who would be willing to take him to the lantern market? He is too good at guessing lantern riddles. The merchants wish they could cover his mouth; he casually guesses the Little Lantern Kings they have so carefully prepared.","How is he going to see the lanterns? He is clearly going to crash the party. When I take him, the merchants look at me with condemnation, and I wish I could find a hole to hide in. Second Madam sighed.","Cheng Zhao could not help but laugh.","She also mentioned her Third Sister, Cheng Ying.","Yuanqi definitely cannot compare to my Third Sister. After all, he is young and not as experienced. Let me take him along and see who wins more between the two of them, Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam agreed without hesitation, Alright. Let him know that there is always someone better out there, so he does not become arrogant just because he is smart.","Cheng Zhao agreed.","Second Madam, however, hesitated to speak.","Cheng Zhao seemed to guess what she wanted to say.","She was probably going to ask about Zhou Yuanshen.","Cheng Zhao did not pick up the conversation.","After returning from Jiangyun Courtyard, she sent Suyue to tell Zhou Yuanqi, inviting him to view the lanterns together the next evening.","Zhou Yuanqi did not have much interest in this matter and shook his head, It is meaningless, I am not going.","Suyue then said, Our Third Young Miss has read many books, and there is no lantern riddle in the world she cannot guess. The Young Madam asked you to go take a look and broaden your horizons.","Zhou Yuanqi was dizzy with anger and said coldly, What a big boast. Then I must go and experience this for myself.","His competitive spirit was instantly aroused.","It was too easy for Cheng Zhao to play him.","When Suyue came back and relayed his words, Cheng Zhao smiled, Children are so easy to manipulate, how cute.","But he would not be cute for many more years.","Once he grew a bit older, he would probably understand these tricks and not be easily fooled.","It was still early, so Cheng Zhao planned to check the account books of the main kitchen for the past few days. The official seals would be opened on the sixteenth, and she could not afford to make mistakes in a rush.","But Zhou Yuanshen arrived.","...Are you going out to the lantern festival tomorrow night? he asked Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao, Yes. I have already told Mother. Mother agreed and even asked me to bring Yuanqi.","She added, Everyone in our family is going, and we will bring guards. Rest assured, we will not lose Yuanqi.","Zhou Yuanshen paused.","Then he nodded slightly, That is fine too.","He did not have dinner at Nonghua Courtyard. After finishing his words, he made an excuse that he had other matters and left first.","Nanny Li said to Cheng Zhao, The Duke wanted to spend the Lantern Festival together with you, right? Perhaps he even wanted to invite you to the lantern festival.","He did not say that.","He...","If he did not say it, then he did not mean it. Cheng Zhao interrupted Nanny Li, Serve the meal, I am a bit hungry.","Nanny Li said no more.","The next day was the Lantern Festival. Lanterns were hung at the main gate of Duke Chen's Mansion, the gates of various courtyards, and the treetops. Tonight, huge bright horn palace lanterns would be placed on the paths to illuminate them, making the entire garden as bright as day.","Dinner was held at Yixia Pavilion, which was specially used for banquets and watching fireworks.","Old Madam was in very high spirits.","The stewards had also prepared a few lantern riddles for Old Madam to guess.","Everyone guessed a few one after another and asked Old Madam for rewards.","Old Madam indeed handed out pouches to them one by one. Each pouch was heavy, containing gold ingots.","The gold ingots were forged into various auspicious shapes, each weighing about two taels, with two placed in each pouch.","Send a decorative lantern and some food to Lijing Courtyard as well. Tell Ah Jiang not to cry and to have a good holiday, Old Madam said with a chuckle.","Huan Qingtang chimed in, Grandmother, should we call Secondary Wife over for the holiday? On a day of reunion, it is only prosperous when everyone is present.","Old Madam looked at Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen, wearing a black robe embroidered with gold thread in an auspicious cloud pattern, had a bland expression, Sister-in-law, what kind of prosperity do you want? Say it out loud and let Grandmother hear it.","Huan Qingtang's face turned pale.","Old Madam smiled and said, It seems you still have not cooled your anger?","Grandmother, I am not angry, and I do not act based on personal likes or dislikes. Punishing Concubine Mu was in accordance with family rules. If there are no rules, wouldn't this household fall into chaos in the future? Zhou Yuanshen said.","He called her Concubine Mu again, not Secondary Wife.","Right in front of the whole family.","Old Madam's smile faded, That is true. The Duke's rules are indeed greater than the heavens.","Zhou Yuanshen stood up and bowed to Old Madam, I would not dare. Grandmother's rules are the greatest. If you wish to bring Concubine Mu out, your grandson would absolutely not dare to object.","Old Madam was counterattacked by him.","For a moment, she was stuck in an awkward position, unable to advance or retreat.","She scanned the room and looked at Cheng Zhao."]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43: Cheng Zhao's Silver Tongue","paragraphs":["The Old Madam cast her gaze toward Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao did not want to be a target. Vigilant in her heart, her mind raced to come up with a countermeasure.","The Old Madam was not without flaws. Her flaw was that she wanted every matter to be handled beautifully.","It had to be reasonable and well-founded, possessing authority while not losing a sense of kindhearted leniency.","Zhou Yuanshen had quickly figured out her temper. He made sure she couldn't pick out any faults in everything he did, yet he would not allow her to manipulate him.","In the entire Chen Duke's Estate, only Zhou Yuanshen barely had the qualifications to contend with the Old Madam.","Of course, this wasn't because he held a noble title, but because he had a way out.","If provoked, he could tear away all pretenses with the Old Madam. At worst, he could discard his title, and he could even argue a few words with the Old Madam before the Emperor.","Others could not do this.","Their status could not compare, they had no leverage to threaten the Old Madam, they lacked financial power, and they had no voice before the Emperor.","The Old Madam wanted to let Mu Jiang out; after all, Mu Jiang was pregnant.","Perhaps Huan Qingtang had received the Old Madam's instructions to step forward and say a few words; or perhaps she wanted to show off and test Zhou Yuanshen's attitude toward her.","In short, Huan Qingtang was rebuffed. Zhou Yuanshen did not give her any face.","Zhou Yuanshen didn't give the Old Madam face either, even bringing up the rules.","The Old Madam looked at Cheng Zhao.","If Cheng Zhao did not speak, she would offend the Old Madam; if she opened her mouth, she would only share Huan Qingtang's fate and offend Zhou Yuanshen.","It was a dilemma.","What the Old Madam and Zhou Yuanshen were contesting over was the right to speak.","Whose words were the family rules that brooked no argument, and who was the true master of this household.","A large family was like a small country. There could only be one head of the household, one person supreme above all.","The Old Madam wanted Cheng Zhao to speak, not allowing her to stay out of it.","Living in the inner courtyard, the Old Madam had countless ways to torment Cheng Zhao.","Just one method alone, not allowing her to leave the house, didn't require much of a reason. As long as she wished to do so, she could place Cheng Zhao under house arrest within the estate doors.","The underhanded tactics of the inner courtyard sometimes struck so painfully that one couldn't even cry out.","...Grandmother, Lord Duke, please do not be angry over a single sentence from eldest sister-in-law. Secondary Wife was taught by Grandmother; she understands the rules best.","Both the Lord Duke and Grandmother are doing this for her own good, telling her to rest peacefully and nurture her pregnancy. She knows how to be grateful. I believe Secondary Wife would absolutely not be so ignorant of etiquette as to insist on coming out for the festival.","If she did that, wouldn't she be wasting Grandmother's teachings and letting down the Lord Duke's protective affection? Cheng Zhao smiled.","Huan Qingtang's face turned another shade paler.","The Old Madam had not personally said to let Mu Jiang come out for the Lantern Festival.","She merely hinted at the idea, waiting for a clever junior to pick up the cue.","Huan Qingtang had offered this flattery because, to her, this matter carried merit and no fault.","But she never expected to hit such a snag, being directly rejected by Zhou Yuanshen and even causing the Old Madam and Zhou Yuanshen to butt heads.","Cheng Zhao even directly ignored the Old Madam's intentions, solely seizing upon Huan Qingtang's words: the suggestion to lift Mu Jiang's grounding was spoken by Huan Qingtang, leaving a handle for Cheng Zhao to grab.","Cheng Zhao's mind was too sharp; she immediately found this loophole.","She praised the Old Madam without offending Zhou Yuanshen. By sacrificing Huan Qingtang alone, she brought the situation under control.","Huan Qingtang understood very well in her heart that whether it was the Old Madam or Zhou Yuanshen, every contest was merely a probe without completely tearing away pretenses.","This time, the probing went a bit too far when it was Huan Qingtang's turn to speak.","Cheng Zhao's words provided the perfect way out.","The Old Madam laughed first: Ah Jiang indeed understands etiquette. She is sometimes arrogant and willful only because she is innocent. She has no bad intentions and puts everything out in the open.","It is because Grandmother dotes on her that she acts this way. Secondary Wife is also striving; she is pregnant with Grandmother's great-grandchild. This is the best repayment to Grandmother, making Grandmother's affection worthwhile, Cheng Zhao said.","I dote on all of you as well. You mustn't say I am biased, the Old Madam laughed.","Cheng Zhao hurriedly said she wouldn't dare.","Zhou Yuanshen called for a managing older female servant: Deliver a lantern and two dishes of food to Lijing Courtyard. Say they are from me, and tell her to spend the festival peacefully. Both Grandmother and I remember her contributions.","He did not refute Cheng Zhao, nor did he continue to clash with the Old Madam.","Although he did not refer to Mu Jiang as Secondary Wife or Ah Jiang, he at least sent food and a lantern, which would soothe Mu Jiang's heart.","This contest dissolved into nothingness just like that.","Zhou Yuanshen glanced at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao smiled lightly at him; he gave a slight nod.","To onlookers, the young couple exchanging glances truly seemed somewhat affectionate.","Huan Qingtang lowered her gaze.","Eldest Madam Song looked at this one, then at that one, unable to conceal the mockery in her eyes.","The family banquet ended, and everyone prepared to go out to admire the lanterns.","The Chen Duke's Estate was not restrictive about this matter. During the Lantern Festival, even people from the palace would come out to admire the lanterns; it was one of the few festive days of the year.","The crowd departed one after another.","Eldest Madam Song deliberately fell a few steps behind to wait for Huan Qingtang.","...Have you made arrangements with anyone to go admire the lanterns? Song asked her.","Huan Qingtang shook her head: I have no mood to admire lanterns this year, Mother.","Song: You should go out for a walk. If Cheng Shi wasn't so good at causing trouble, you could have gone with her.","Speaking of Cheng Zhao again, That mouth of hers is truly vicious. Seeing the situation going wrong, she stepped on you to gain merit in front of the Old Madam and the Lord Duke.","Huan Qingtang's eyes grew a little red.","You were very right, this Cheng Shi has some tricks up her sleeve. And she has a kind face but a cruel heart, Song added.","Huan Qingtang sighed softly. She didn't shed tears, but seemed very dispirited: It was also my own thoughtlessness in speaking that allowed her to gain the upper hand.","You spoke first, and she spoke later. The person walking in front will definitely leave footprints; it is not your fault. There will be many more times she steps on you in the future, Song said.","Huan Qingtang remained silent.","Eldest Madam Song thought for a moment and told her: We mother-in-law and daughter-in-law must be of one mind for you to win. Only then will our position in Chengming Hall be secure.","Mother, Chengming Hall belongs to us to begin with, Huan Qingtang said.","Song smiled faintly: It is a good thing that you have such determination.","The people of the second branch were the first to leave Yixia Pavilion.","They returned to change their clothes before heading out.","This time, they did not ride in the small oil carriages; the group strolled back.","The Second Madam then said to Cheng Zhao: You are truly clever. I was sweating for you at the time.","Cheng Zhao: I was sweating for myself too.","The Second Madam couldn't help but laugh.","The Second Master also felt that his daughter-in-law was eloquent and possessed some wicked brilliance.","Actually, this daughter-in-law of mine is suited to preside over Chengming Hall, the Second Master thought to himself.","The Second Master respected his eldest sister-in-law Song and pitied her for losing her husband and son, but he did not think she could live in Chengming Hall forever.","Chengming Hall was no ordinary courtyard; it was the main residential quarters of the Duke's Estate, the residence that came with the noble title, symbolizing status and position.","For example, if the late Emperor passed away without leaving an heir, and his younger brother happened to inherit the throne, must the late Emperor's Empress monopolize the central palace and refuse to vacate Kunning Palace for her sister-in-law?","Even if the Empress Dowager tacitly consented, this matter would still be wrong.","A misalignment of status would make many people feel wronged.","Where there is grievance, there is unwillingness and anger, which in turn sparks disputes.","If the Old Madam were wise, having chosen Zhou Yuanshen to inherit the title, she should have vacated Chengming Hall, which came with the title, for Zhou Yuanshen.","Only then could a family truly live in peace and avoid the kind of dispute that had happened tonight.","Of course, the Old Madam couldn't care less."]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44: It Was Cheng Zhaoxian Who Started It","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao returned to Nonghua Courtyard first; she needed to change her clothes before going out.","The two brothers, Zhou Yuanshen and Zhou Yuanqi, also returned to their respective courtyards.","The spring chill was lingering, and the night wind was slightly biting. The Second Master and the Second Madame walked rather slowly, the old couple chatting while strolling.","The floor-standing palace lanterns along the path were very bright, some adorned with brilliant and vivid paintings.","\"...Do you think Mother will hold a grudge against Zhaozhao?\" the Second Madame suddenly asked.","\"Our daughter-in-law is very smart and handles things appropriately. Mother won't blame her,\" the Second Master said.","\"Mother wanted Mu Jiang to come out, and Lady Huan was speaking in accordance with Mother's wishes, but Zhaozhao disrupted the situation,\" the Second Madame said.","The Second Master smiled: \"You have become much wiser lately. Becoming a mother-in-law has made your worldly wisdom advance by leaps and bounds.\"","The Second Madame: \"...\"","It was a bit cold, so he took off his cloak and draped it over his wife.","The Second Madame hurriedly said there was no need, fearing he would catch a cold; the Second Master said he had drunk a little wine during dinner, and the heat from the alcohol was making him feel restless, so he wanted to get some fresh air.","The couple slowly walked back to Jiangyun Courtyard, changed their clothes again, and prepared to go out.","Huan Qingtang returned to her own courtyard, took off her outer garment, changed into casual clothes, and sat on the large heated brick bed by the window in a daze.","Her personal senior maid served her tea and advised her: \"Why not go out for a walk to relax?\"","Huan Qingtang just shook her head.","The senior maid couldn't help but curse Cheng Zhao. She had also been serving at Yixia Pavilion at the time and heard Cheng Zhao's words.","\"...She trampled you in the mud to curry favor with Lord Duke. Her methods are despicable,\" the senior maid said.","Huan Qingtang remained silent.","\"If you don't show her some color, she'll just think you're easy to bully,\" the senior maid added.","She couldn't help but continue, \"She just has good luck. If the Eldest Young Master were still alive, their entire second branch would just be a 'collateral branch', and moving out of the Duke's mansion would mean they leave the noble family and are nothing!\"","Huan Qingtang slowly closed her eyes.","She didn't speak, and after a long while, she let out a slow sigh.","\"I thought I could get along peacefully with her,\" Huan Qingtang said.","\"She is petty, vicious, and selfish. You never stepped on or belittled her. She attacked first,\" the senior maid said.","Huan Qingtang thought, yes, Cheng Zhao started it first.","She blew the horn of war.","Cheng Zhao was an \"outsider.\" She was bestowed a marriage by the Empress and forced upon the Zhou family, not someone the Zhou family sought to marry.","She invaded the Duke's mansion.","Huan Qingtang always thought that Cheng Zhao would know what belonged to her and what didn't, and that she would have a sense of propriety. But she didn't expect her to be so ambitious.","Perhaps Cheng Zhao really wanted to live in Chengming Hall?","Did she have such an unrealistic idea?","Dowager Madame would not hand over the power and wealth in her hands to an \"outsider.\" Since this person was not chosen by Dowager Madame, she had no right to take over the Duke's mansion.","Huan Qingtang sighed again: \"I have no other choice but to accept the challenge.\"","How could her dignity and status be trampled upon?","Cheng Zhao finished getting ready and took a small oil carriage to the main gate of the Duke's mansion.","Her brother-in-law, Zhou Yuanqi, had been waiting for a long time. When he saw her, he complained: \"You dawdled and made me wait bitterly.\"","\"My courtyard is far away,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"Hurry up. In a while, the streets and the riverside will be full of people, and we won't be able to squeeze in.\"","\"My fourth brother has booked a private room at Zuixian Restaurant,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi looked at her and asked: \"Do you know who the owner behind Zuixian Restaurant is?\"","Zuixian Restaurant had an excellent location, unique in Shangjing City, and had a good reputation. The dishes were rich, the wine was precious, and a meal cost a fortune.","\"Could it be that you know?\"","\"It's my youngest uncle,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao: \"A restaurant is indeed a good place to gather information and pass on messages. Not bad, your youngest uncle has quite an eye.\"","She added, \"You've revealed his secret.\"","Zhou Yuanqi glared at her angrily: \"You don't need to show off your cleverness.\"","\"Let's encourage each other,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\"","His first defeat of the day, unconvinced both in words and in heart, waiting to turn the tables later. Zhou Yuanqi sat up straight indignantly, and the carriage waited to depart.","They waited for a little while because a carriage in front hadn't been adjusted yet.","The lantern light at the door was bright, and the frost-like moonlight spilled all over the ground, making everywhere as bright as day. Lifting the carriage curtain, she saw Zhou Yuanshen getting onto a carriage.","\"So we were waiting for The Brute,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","When he said \"The Brute,\" his voice was relatively soft, but Zhou Yuanshen glanced over.","Zhou Yuanqi then said to him: \"You're blocking the way.\"","Zhou Yuanshen ignored him and got onto the carriage by himself.","\"Let's go to Zuixian Restaurant, we might even run into The Brute. He's definitely enjoying the lanterns with youngest uncle. Other than youngest uncle, who would want to talk to him?\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao: \"If you don't restrain yourself, in less than five years, no one will want to talk to you either. He still has youngest uncle, do you have any close friends?\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\"","He didn't.","He looked down on everyone. His peers were all little brats in his eyes, and giving them an extra glance was already flattering them.","He indeed had no playmates.","Cheng Zhao's words made him reflect.","When he was a bit older, he wouldn't study in the clan school anymore and would go to Hengshan Academy.","Perhaps he could condescend to get to know a few peers and have companions to go out with during festivals.","\"Do you have any close friends?\" His mind worked very fast, and he immediately asked Cheng Zhao back.","Cheng Zhao: \"I have sisters and sisters-in-law. I also have female cousins. I have plenty.\"","\"...You're cheating, family members don't count.\"","\"Lord Duke's close friend is also his youngest uncle. Why doesn't it count?\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"The relatives my age are all appallingly stupid. You and The Brute just have good luck.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Everyone is stupid in front of you. You are a genius with unparalleled talent, a rare hero throughout the ages. Heroes are all lonely.\"","Zhou Yuanqi was stunned.","The words were true, and he deserved them. But why did it always carry a hint of teasing when it came out of her mouth?","\"...If you keep doing this, I'll put you in the same category as The Brute, both annoying,\" Zhou Yuanqi warned seriously.","Cheng Zhao smiled hurriedly: \"There's no need for that. I just won't say it.\"","Once they left the street of the Duke's mansion, the road was indeed very congested.","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanqi had a \"battle of words,\" neither gaining the upper hand, and both were tired of talking when they finally squeezed their way to Zuixian Restaurant.","Cheng Chao's servant boy was waiting at the door.","Zuixian Restaurant was strictly guarded tonight. Only distinguished guests came, and casual customers were not allowed to wander in. The Cheng family's servant boy, like the other servant boys, was waiting for guests.","\"Fifth Aunt, you are the last to arrive,\" the servant boy said, \"They are all here, please go upstairs.\"","Cheng Zhao led Zhou Yuanqi upstairs.","The private room was lively.","It was the best private room in the entire Zuixian Restaurant, directly facing the Lantern King.","Cheng Zhao thought, Cheng Chao really knows how to snatch a spot. Just as she was thinking about how he managed to choose such a good private room, the curtain was lifted, and she saw a large group of people.","Including Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanqi also saw him and looked at Cheng Zhao in confusion.","Cheng Zhao avoided his gaze.","\"Third Brother, Youngest Uncle.\" He went forward to greet the people he knew first, \"Brother Shizi.\"","Then he greeted the people from the Cheng family.","The arrogant little peacock was still fully courteous when facing relatives.","Cheng Zhao glanced at her fourth brother.","And Zhou Yuanshen, his seat was turned sideways to Cheng Zhao, and he was turning his head to look at the lanterns outside, ignoring her."]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45: Stunning Talent","paragraphs":["The private booth was bustling with activity.","A large group from the Cheng family was gathered on one side. Over by Zhou Yuanshen's side were Fan Xiao and Helian Jian, along with two young girls who shared some facial resemblance to Helian Jian, likely children from Prince Rong's estate.","Cheng Zhao shot her fourth brother a look.","The siblings went out to the corridor to talk.","\"...How did so many people end up together?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Cheng Chao replied, \"We ran into Fan Xiao, and he invited us over. The Lantern King was moved to a different spot this year, so the booth we booked was facing the wrong way.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"You didn't ask around beforehand? What use are you?\"","Cheng Chao: \"You didn't contribute money or effort, so what are you picking at? If you don't want to sit here, go out and play by yourself.\"","He added, \"Besides, there are no outsiders here.\"","Centered around Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen, everyone present was indeed family or friends: the Fan family were close relatives, and Prince Rong's estate were close neighbors.","Since things had already come to this, Cheng Zhao couldn't say much more. She silently noted another strike against Cheng Chao in her heart, deciding never to entrust him with important matters in the future.","Fan Xiao even invited a songstress into the private booth to play the lute and sing.","After sitting for a short while, the Lantern King downstairs began to light up.","It was a massive lantern equipped with mechanical gears that allowed it to rotate on its own. It had twenty-four panels featuring beautiful women, flowers and birds, and landscapes, so beautiful it was dazzling.","It could be seen right from the window of the private booth. Visually, it felt closer and more breathtaking than being downstairs.","\"This year's Lantern King was made by the Liao family workshop. the Liao clan is the best at making lanterns.\"","\"It is indeed beautiful. However, I wonder who was hired to paint the lantern panels? It lacks the simple elegance of last year's,\" someone said.","Fan Xiao said, \"It was still painted by the scholars of Hengshan Academy; it's them every year. Perhaps a different group did it this year, as they used much richer and vibrant colors.\"","Cheng Zhao, however, said, \"Last year's was too plain. This year's is just right. On such a wonderful day, it should be heavily colored to reflect the lively and prosperous atmosphere.\"","The eldest sister laughed, \"My little sister is a person of worldly tastes.\"","Fan Xiao said, \"The Duchess's opinion coincides with mine. I also think vibrant richness is auspicious.\"","Zhou Yuanshen glanced at him.","Fan Xiao took the opportunity to say, \"Isn't that right, Yuanshen?\"","Several members of the Cheng family looked over.","Zhou Yuanshen had no choice but to say, \"Yes.\"","\"He's saying one thing but meaning another. He actually liked last year's. He painted the 'Fishing in the Snow' piece from last year. A teacher at Hengshan Academy used to be his private tutor and specially invited him to paint that picture,\" Fan Xiao said.","Hengshan Academy was the largest academy in the current dynasty, yearned for by many scholars.","This topic was interesting, and everyone chimed in eagerly.","Zhou Yuanshen did not join in the replies.","He looked straight ahead, not glancing sideways.","Cheng Zhao had no interest in this; she wanted a rotating lotus lantern.","Vendors didn't sell lanterns equipped with mechanical rotating gears. Instead, they required solving very difficult riddles to win them, serving as an attraction for tourists.","Some people, unable to solve them, had to settle for the next best thing and buy other lanterns.","\"...You must win one for me later,\" Cheng Zhao said to Zhou Yuanqi. \"Call my third sister to come along. If you get it before she does, I will give you a reward.\"","\"What kind of reward?\"","\"My grandfather still has many books and calligraphy copybooks, as well as precious inkstones and brushes. What do you want?\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi's eyes brightened significantly.","Cheng Zhao walked toward her third sister, who was sitting in the corner.","Cheng Ying sat there alone, silent but not gloomy.","On the contrary, quite a few people in the private booth would secretly steal glances at her.","Her outstanding appearance and noble temperament made her resemble a magnolia blossom on a branch. Even sitting quietly, she possessed a strength of character that made her impossible to ignore.","Cheng Zhao called her, brought Zhou Yuanqi along, and then downstairs called for the maidservant Qiubai, along with the Cheng family guards, and headed toward the lantern market.","She linked her arm with Cheng Ying's.","\"...Win three lanterns for me. One for Mother, one for my mother-in-law, and another one for myself,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Cheng Ying replied, \"Rotating lotus lanterns are not easy to come by; only one out of ten lantern stalls has them. There will definitely be many Hengshan Academy scholars lining up for them.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Just do your best. It's fine if we don't get them.\"","She added, \"Show Yuanqi what it means to possess immense talent and profound knowledge.\"","Cheng Ying turned to look at Zhou Yuanqi and told him, \"Don't listen to your sister-in-law. There is a trick to guessing lantern riddles; it's nothing more than using a key to open a door.\"","\"I know how to open doors too,\" Zhou Yuanqi said coldly.","Cheng Ying: \"Yes, we have the keys.\"","The implication was that there was no need to be arrogant.","Zhou Yuanqi had always felt that his sister-in-law's beauty was otherworldly, unmatched by ordinary people; yet this 'Third Sister' was not inferior to his sister-in-law at all. They were like two fairies descended from the heavens, equally flawless and ethereal.","Walking through the lantern market with the two of them, Zhou Yuanqi inexplicably felt very honored.","Anyone following fairies would feel joyful.","Soon, they spotted a rotating lotus lantern.","Sure enough, the entrance was surrounded by scholars, all dressed elegantly and looking quite learned.","The riddle was a line of characters.","It wasn't a character-guessing riddle, but a character-dismantling riddle.","This kind was relatively difficult. Cheng Zhao was the worst at guessing character riddles, let alone this type that required dismantling, analyzing, and then guessing.","This kind of character riddle was like fortune-telling.","A character, its meanings and strokes, the allusions contained within after it's dismantled, and then guessing a related one; and in this sentence, which character was the central one that hinted at the answer?","Cheng Zhao took one look and was completely baffled.","Cheng Ying did not guess it immediately this time.","She glanced at the rotating lantern and said to Cheng Zhao, \"The painting on this lantern is the work of Old Master Cui, the headmaster of Hengshan Academy. It bears his small seal.\"","Zhou Yuanqi looked at her in surprise.","Guessing a riddle also required looking at the painting—he had learned another trick.","\"Is that of any use?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Cheng Ying explained, \"Since the painting has an origin, the allusion contained in the riddle's answer naturally has an origin as well. Old Master Cui is most fond of the 'Bamboo Grove School'...\"","She spoke softly, her voice not loud.","Outsiders couldn't hear clearly; only Zhou Yuanqi could hear.","He listened, completely stunned.","Cheng Zhao: \"You don't need to teach me how to make a key, I wouldn't know how. Just guess the answer directly. Hurry, don't let anyone else snatch it away. This rotating lantern is exquisitely made; it'll probably be hard to find a better one later.\"","Cheng Ying's analysis was interrupted, but Zhou Yuanqi had already guessed it.","He stepped forward and said loudly, \"The answer is 'Zhuangzi Dreaming of a Butterfly'.\"","Another scholar hurriedly answered, \"The answer is 'Drumming on a Basin and Singing'.\"","Cheng Zhao's heart leaped into her throat as she whispered to Cheng Ying, \"Which one is it?\"","Cheng Ying gently patted the back of her hand.","The shopkeeper came out, saw the two people who had answered, and looked at Zhou Yuanqi in surprise.","\"This young gentleman has guessed the riddle correctly.\"","A chorus of gasps erupted all around.","The scholars all looked at Zhou Yuanqi in amazement; some also saw Cheng Zhao and Cheng Ying, their gazes lingering, unwilling to look away.","Suyue and the guards blocked them from the front.","\"Young gentleman, please come in and sit for a while, and leave some of your calligraphy for our humble shop,\" the shopkeeper warmly invited.","Zhou Yuanqi frowned.","He didn't want to.","The shopkeeper tried to pull him, and the others, for whatever unknown purpose, started cheering to urge him and the Cheng sisters to go into the shop.","Things got a little chaotic, but then someone spoke up: \"There's no need. Just give him the lantern.\"","A man stood in the shadows against the light. His posture was tall and straight, his presence intimidating, instantly dissolving the commotion of the crowd.","For the first time, Zhou Yuanqi looked his brother square in the eye.","A brute was still of some use after all."]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46: The Thoughtfulness of the Duke","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen arrived.","He carried an aura of aloofness and chill. Some of the scholars seemed to recognize him, while others were intimidated by his presence, whispering among themselves.","The shopkeeper was a good judge of character, knowing exactly who could be offended and who could not. He swiftly took down the lantern and handed it to Zhou Yuanqi.","The small lantern was exquisite and ingenious. Its light and shadow fell upon the child's face, making his fair and delicate features look like someone out of a painting.","Zhou Yuanqi handed the lantern to Cheng Zhao.","\"Here, I got it first,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","He thought Cheng Zhao would tease him a bit; he also thought Cheng Ying would be unconvinced and try to argue that her ideas had enlightened him.","However, the fairy-like ladies merely looked at him quietly, their eyes full of joy.","No one wanted to be a killjoy at this moment.","Cheng Zhao said, \"Yuanqi indeed has great knowledge. Whatever treasure of my grandfather's you want, just tell me. I will go ask for it.\"","Cheng Ying also added, \"To have such a quick mind at such a young age, you must have put a lot of hard work into your studies and possess true knowledge. Yuanqi will become a great scholar of his generation in the future.\"","Zhou Yuanqi felt like he was floating.","His heart was like boiling water, with little bubbles tumbling and rising, impossible to suppress.","His joy must have shown on his face, because his teeth felt a bit cold—he was smiling so broadly that his teeth were showing.","Realizing he had lost his composure, he immediately shut his mouth and adjusted his expression. \"The answer to this riddle was very simple. Given a little more time, you could have guessed it too.\"","\"I couldn't have guessed it anyway,\" Cheng Zhao laughed. \"This lantern is too beautiful. I'll give it to my mother-in-law later.\"","Zhou Yuanshen walked slightly ahead and to the side of them. Hearing the two sisters flatter the child, he caught a glimpse of his younger brother's silly smile out of the corner of his eye, but he showed no reaction.","The lantern was held in Cheng Zhao's hand.","Her hands were slender and fair like scallion roots. Illuminated by the lantern's light, her nails appeared almost transparent.","Zhou Yuanshen didn't turn his head to look again and just kept walking forward.","As expected, spinning lotus lanterns were not easy to find. They walked down most of the street without encountering another one.","\"There definitely must have been more than one shop. Were they won by other people?\" Cheng Zhao said.","Cheng Ying replied, \"The adjacent street isn't as bustling and lively as this one. If this street doesn't have any, it's likely there won't be any more.\"","Looking at the lantern in her hand, Cheng Zhao smiled, \"Having even one is great. When I give it to my mother-in-law later, she will definitely be happy.\"","\"Since there's only one, you can keep it for yourself,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","There was no need to constantly please others.","She was so beautiful and came from a good background. Why did she have to be so humble as a daughter-in-law?","It was because of the brute.","The brute didn't like her.","The brute not only had a beautiful concubine, but also two pretty maids given to him by their grandmother in Lijing Courtyard. On top of that, he was going to marry that cunning and beautiful widowed sister-in-law from the eldest branch.","The brute's side was stuffed with people, but his mother only had one daughter-in-law.","Pleasing his mother seemed more advantageous.","It was a bit humble, but she knew how to grasp the crucial point. His sister-in-law was not only beautiful but also smart.","Except that she didn't know how to guess lantern riddles.","It was fine if she couldn't guess; Zhou Yuanqi could, and he could help her.","Zhou Yuanqi once again felt that it would be better if the brute wasn't in the family. Let the eldest branch and their grandmother have him, and let him never come back.","Didn't his sister-in-law need a husband too?","They could find a better one outside and have him marry into the family. This way, his parents would gain a son-in-law, and they could still kick the brute out.","As Zhou Yuanqi let his imagination run wild, the brute suddenly turned his head and glanced at him, startling Zhou Yuanqi.","\"What?\"","\"Are you thirsty?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked.","\"No,\" Zhou Yuanqi replied.","\"There's a rice milk stall ahead. Do you want to quench your thirst?\" Zhou Yuanshen then asked Cheng Zhao and Cheng Ying.","Cheng Zhao wasn't thirsty, but she was a little hungry. Rice milk was sweet, filling, and wouldn't cause indigestion.","\"I'm not thirsty,\" Cheng Ying said.","Cheng Zhao, however, said, \"I want some.\"","She handed the lantern to Cheng Ying to hold, and walked forward with Zhou Yuanshen, telling Cheng Ying and the others to wait where they were.","The two of them stood before the stall, waiting to buy the rice milk. A parade carrying lanterns passed by, and Cheng Zhao shifted inward a bit, moving closer to Zhou Yuanshen.","The lanterns being carried on poles happened to shine on her profile, bathing her features in an orange glow.","Zhou Yuanshen turned his head to speak and happened to catch sight of this scene.","He silently turned his head back.","He told the vendor he wanted two bowls of rice milk.","He handed one bowl to Cheng Zhao and downed his own in one gulp. Then he said to the vendor, \"Give me another bowl.\"","\"Is the young master this thirsty? Drink slowly, this milk can be intoxicating,\" the vendor laughed.","This time, Zhou Yuanshen drank it slowly, sip by sip, unlike his previous thirst.","Cheng Zhao didn't quite like the taste of the rice milk; it was a bit sticky on her teeth. She took three sips and put it down.","When she turned around, she didn't see Zhou Yuanqi and Cheng Ying; Suyue and the guards were nowhere to be seen either.","Cheng Zhao felt inexplicably nervous. \"Where are they?\"","Zhou Yuanshen finished his bowl before answering her, \"I saw our young uncle just now. With another parade passing by and the crowd getting dense, they probably went back with him.\"","Cheng Zhao thought that her third sister was the most reliable and wouldn't lose Zhou Yuanqi, and since Suyue and the guards were skilled in martial arts, nothing would happen to them. She felt relieved.","\"Let's head back too,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"We still have to walk a big circle along the river later, so we shouldn't make them wait for me.\"","Zhou Yuanshen nodded.","As Cheng Zhao turned around, a vendor carrying a shelf of lanterns on a shoulder pole passed by. It was piled high, and when pushed by two playing boys, it almost crashed into Cheng Zhao.","The Lantern Festival market was just this crowded.","Cheng Zhao dodged, but her hair still got snagged by a bamboo strip on the shelf, and her hairpin became tangled in the lantern rack.","The vendor didn't notice and kept walking forward. Cheng Zhao couldn't keep up, and her hairpin was pulled out.","With quick reflexes, Zhou Yuanshen retrieved the hairpin.","When he turned back, half of Cheng Zhao's hair bun had come undone.","She wished she could find a place to hide.","\"So unlucky!\" she muttered.","She came out to see the lanterns every year.","Every time, some little incident would happen—losing an earring or jewelry, getting her clothes dirty, or getting into a conflict with someone—but this was the first time her hair bun had been ruined.","\"...In the past, when I was at home, I wore my hair in a double bun, which was easier to secure,\" Cheng Zhao still tried to explain.","She had messed up her hair in front of Zhou Yuanshen several times already.","Zhou Yuanshen probably thought that Cheng Zhao's servants were unskilled at doing hair.","But that wasn't the case.","Cheng Zhao's hair was too thick and smooth. The double bun she wore as a young unmarried girl divided her hair into two sections, making it easier to manage.","Now married, she had to wear a married woman's hairstyle, and her hair simply wouldn't stay securely in a single bun.","\"Last time, there was a maid serving my mother-in-law who did hair very tightly. I'll go ask for her later,\" Cheng Zhao thought.","While she was at a loss for what to do, Zhou Yuanshen pulled her.","The two retreated beneath the eaves of a street shop, into a shadowed area.","He told Cheng Zhao to turn around and then completely undid the rest of her bun.","Cheng Zhao gasped.","Zhou Yuanshen used his fingers to comb through her hair, attempting to pin it up for her.","He didn't control his strength well, pulling Cheng Zhao's hair so hard it hurt.","Cheng Zhao didn't move.","She really had no other choice.","Zhou Yuanshen seemed to actually have some skill. In just a moment, he managed to twist Cheng Zhao's hair into a round bun and insert her hairpin.","It was a bit low and too tight, making Cheng Zhao's scalp burn with pain.","But at least her hair was fixed.","She touched it.","It was far too tight; if she wore such a round bun often, her scalp would peel right off.","\"Thank you, Lord Duke,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen did not speak.","He hadn't bothered to speak to Cheng Zhao all night. It seemed he was still angry about her rejecting his invitation yesterday.","\"Let's go.\" He turned around first.","Cheng Zhao had no choice but to hurry after him."]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47: Staying Over Again","paragraphs":["Returning to the Zuixian Pavilion, Cheng Ying and Zhou Yuanqi were already sitting in the private booth.","\"...We were pushed to the side of the road just now. Some stall over there was selling something with a smell so strong that Yuanqi couldn't stand it, so we came back first,\" Cheng Ying explained to Cheng Zhao.","With the crowded and chaotic streets, and the child growing a bit impatient, Cheng Ying was terrified he might accidentally wander off. They happened to run into Fan Xiao, so they all came back together.","Safety first.","Every year during the Lantern Festival, children went missing, so one had to be vigilant.","They hadn't waited for Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen.","\"I know Third Sister is reliable. I figured you must have returned first,\" Cheng Zhao said.","This year, Cheng Zhao didn't stroll through the Lantern Festival all night because she felt dizzy.","That bowl of rice wine had quite a kick. Cheng Zhao's alcohol tolerance was usually decent—she could normally drink a few ounces of liquor—but today she felt drowsy.","She told the group, \"I'm going back first, I can't hold out any longer.\"","She looked a bit listless, which her Eldest Sister had already noticed. \"You've been exhausted by all the busy affairs of the New Year. Go back early and get some rest,\" she said.","Cheng Zhao agreed and then asked Zhou Yuanqi, \"Are you going back?\"","Zhou Yuanqi replied, \"No!\"","It had been a long time since he had this much fun at a festival, and he had no desire to go back early.","Cheng Zhao looked around at everyone, considering who to entrust Zhou Yuanqi to.","Her Fourth Brother, Cheng Chao, should have been the most suitable, but considering he couldn't even book a private booth correctly, Cheng Zhao didn't trust him.","Third Sister spoke up, \"I'll take Yuanqi.\"","She then asked Zhou Yuanqi, \"Are you willing to be obedient and stay by my side?\"","Zhou Yuanqi felt her tone was a bit arrogant, treating him almost like a servant; yet, coming from Cheng Ying, it sounded very natural.","She didn't usually like paying attention to people, but she was willing to let him tag along, which put Zhou Yuanqi in a good mood.","He nodded, giving an equally arrogant nod in return. \"I can protect you. You are a woman.\"","A child claiming he was going to protect a woman...","Cheng Zhao held back her laughter. She left Qiubai behind so there would be an extra person to look after Zhou Yuanqi, and only then prepared to return to the manor.","Zhou Yuanshen then said, \"I'll head back first as well.\"","The husband and wife rode in the same carriage. There were too many people on the street, and the carriage couldn't squeeze its way out for a long time. Amidst the stop-and-go motion, Cheng Zhao nearly fell fast asleep.","The alcohol had gone to her head.","Zhou Yuanshen was also in the carriage. In her drowsy state, she vaguely felt him support her head to prevent her from bumping into the carriage wall.","Cheng Zhao shifted a bit to the side and told him, \"I'm not asleep, just resting my eyes.\"","Zhou Yuanshen made no sound.","When she felt the person in the carriage move, she opened her eyes to find Zhou Yuanshen's face right next to hers.","She froze for a moment.","Zhou Yuanshen looked at her quietly, saying nothing.","The light in the carriage was dim, and Cheng Zhao couldn't clearly see his expression, but she could feel his scorching breath.","He had drunk two bowls of that rice wine.","Cheng Zhao had felt uncomfortable after just three sips; having drunk two bowls, he was perhaps far more intoxicated than she was.","She didn't want to serve a drunkard. She thought she shouldn't have returned with him, let alone shared the same carriage.","Zhou Yuanshen held her face, his fingers gently stroking her cheek. His fingertips brushed against her skin and traced over her lips.","Slowly, yet with a bit of force, he rubbed against her lips.","Cheng Zhao's drowsiness cleared up by a fraction.","She simply sat up and moved to the other side.","Zhou Yuanshen didn't move again. He sat in the shadows, not saying a word.","Cheng Zhao turned her head to the other side. Thinking about the earlier clash at the Duke's estate in the Yixia Pavilion, and still feeling the touch of his fingers on her lips, she felt exceptionally irritable.","This irritability felt like being forced to wear a padded cotton coat in the sweltering heat of midsummer.","Not only was it hard to breathe, but her whole body felt wrapped in dampness.","She tried hard to calm her emotions.","The carriage returned to the Duke's estate, and Zhou Yuanshen instructed the driver, \"Go directly to Nonghua Courtyard.\"","The driver went to pass on the word, and the servants immediately removed the door sill so the carriage could smoothly enter the estate.","Once inside the estate, Cheng Zhao sobered up a bit more. \"My Lord, are you resting in Chenhui Courtyard tonight?\"","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"Nonghua Courtyard.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Unless they were going to share a bed, he rarely ever stayed in Nonghua Courtyard.","Every time he went there, it was as if he was on a mission, and Cheng Zhao would suffer through another ordeal.","Since they returned quite early, Nanny Li was a bit surprised. \"You didn't stay out for long.\"","\"I'm a bit tired,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She had taken a nap in the carriage. The slight drowsiness brought on by those three sips of rice wine had all but vanished. She realized she was completely awake now.","Then what did she come back for?","Not only did she come back herself, but she had also brought Zhou Yuanshen along.","Skipping the lantern festival just to come back and suffer his humiliation?","Cheng Zhao was filled with regret and frustration.","After washing up, she lay down, vainly attempting to pretend to be asleep to get through the night.","Carrying the faint scent of water vapor, Zhou Yuanshen climbed into bed wearing his inner garments.","He sat there and after a long while, spoke: \"Cheng Zhao?\"","Cheng Zhao had her eyes closed, pretending to sleep. Hearing him call her, she simply rolled over, turning her back to him. \"I won't regret tonight, nor will I resent you.\"","Every time she showed the slightest reluctance, he would use \"heirs\" to pressure her: if she dared to refuse him, they might as well cut ties going forward.","He wanted to keep Cheng Zhao cornered.","Cheng Zhao was usually very rational, but when she was exhausted, she just wanted to throw a tantrum.","Especially after Mu Jiang got pregnant, she always felt that even though they shared the same man, Cheng Zhao was not treated as well as Mu Jiang.","Perhaps that one time she said she was \"willing,\" it had placed a shackle on her, making him feel he could humiliate her at will.","A hand fell onto her shoulder, neither light nor heavy.","He turned Cheng Zhao's body to face him.","Cheng Zhao was stunned.","She thought she understood Zhou Yuanshen. As long as she was unwilling, he would definitely respond with coldness and might even leave Nonghua Courtyard in the middle of the night.","The last time she cried, he left right after finishing.","\"Cheng Zhao, why are you always unhappy?\" he asked. \"What have I done wrong this time?\"","Cheng Zhao looked at him in astonishment.","Did he actually think he had done something right?","Did he have so little self-awareness?","\"My heart is the same as yours. I also want you to have a child. We are fundamentally striving in the same direction, so why does it always seem like I am bullying you?\" he demanded, almost aggressively. \"If you have any dissatisfaction, can you just tell me?\"","All of Cheng Zhao's spite and anger dissipated in that instant.","Yes, why should she be angry with him?","Acting out of spite was meant to achieve a purpose.","Being angry now, aside from venting her emotions, was entirely meaningless and would only block her path to wealth and status.","Mu Jiang was already pregnant, and the dual-lineage marriage with Huan Qingtang was imminent. Was she going to wait until both of them had children before she bowed and scraped to beg for mercy?","Her posture then would be far more pathetic than her current state in the bedroom.","To forever be a titled lady in name only? She couldn't accept that either.","Life in the inner chambers meant enduring hardship. She couldn't suffer all this bitterness and end up with nothing.","If she wanted to be the primary wife of the household, besides a royal title, she needed to at least have an heir. This was the established condition of the world, as well as the family rule.","Cheng Zhao sat up.","The small horn lantern on the bedside table inside the bed curtains illuminated a tiny space, leaving his eyes pitch-black in the shadows. And Cheng Zhao unexpectedly noticed that his gaze was a bit dazed.","He was always calm and restrained...","\"I don't want to be on my stomach. I find it very humiliating,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen frowned slightly.","\"Besides, the results aren't good. Look, Concubine Mu is already pregnant, and she probably didn't use the method I do, right?","Not only is my body uncomfortable and my heart stifled, but I've gained nothing from it. Could you... treat me in a different way?\" Cheng Zhao said."]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48: Cheng Zhao Refuses to Admit Fault","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao felt much more relaxed.","When it ended, his body pressed against hers. Cheng Zhao could feel his burning breath spraying on the side of her ear, as well as the violent heaving of his chest.","A slight sheen of sweat, not sticky, but carrying a certain warmth.","\"No wonder he has a better relationship with Mu Jiang and is more willing to stay at her place.\"","So, with this kind of merging, they were closer to each other.","She could feel his breath, his heartbeat.","His lips were almost pressed against the side of her face, and the hot air he exhaled was a little ticklish. Cheng Zhao tilted her head slightly to the side.","Zhou Yuanshen seemed to freeze for a moment.","He rolled over and got up.","After washing up, the couple went to bed. Cheng Zhao was truly exhausted this time, and she quickly fell asleep.","When she woke up the next morning, Zhou Yuanshen was predictably not in bed.","Cheng Zhao woke up, and a maid served her as she washed up. Suyue told her, \"Qiubai came back at dawn and brought your lantern.\"","The lantern was placed on the kang table in the eastern side room.","Cheng Zhao combed her hair and changed her clothes, then picked up the lantern. \"I'm going to Jiangyun Courtyard to serve my mother-in-law breakfast.\"","And she would eat there while she was at it.","At this hour, her father-in-law had already gone to court. The imperial court also resumed work today, so it would be very busy.","Seeing her arrive so early, the Second Madam was slightly surprised. \"Why don't you sleep a little longer?\"","\"I came back to the manor at the end of the Xu hour yesterday. We didn't stroll for long,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Of course, she actually went to sleep quite late, almost at the Zi hour.","\"...The lantern Yuanqi won.\" Cheng Zhao handed it to the Second Madam.","She then vividly recounted Zhou Yuanqi's performance last night to the Second Madam.","The Second Madam beamed with joy. \"He is indeed quite clever.\"","As the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law were talking, Zhou Yuanqi arrived.","After paying his respects to the Second Madam, he sat down to wait for breakfast, with some bruising under his eyes.","\"I only slept for a shichen. I have to go to the academy to check in this morning, and I'll sleep more this afternoon,\" he said to the Second Madam.","The Second Madam said, \"Go ahead. Children can handle staying up.\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\"","Cheng Zhao winked at the Second Madam, silently urging her to praise Zhou Yuanqi. After all, it wasn't easy to guess that lantern riddle.","The Second Madam then said, \"This lantern is very nice. If we went to the Liao family's workshop to buy this kind, we'd have to order it half a year in advance.\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"It's a gift for Third Sister-in-law. Mother is just benefiting from the association.\"","The Second Madam: \"How rare. It saved me a few taels of silver and half a year of waiting.\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\"","Cheng Zhao laughed out loud.","The three of them had breakfast, and Zhou Yuanqi dawdled, reluctant to go to the clan school.","Cheng Zhao asked him, \"If you're late, won't the teacher scold you?\"","\"The teacher is counting on me to make a name for him. He wouldn't dare scold me,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","In the future, when Zhou Yuanqi's fame shook the world, his enlightenment teacher would also become famous.","The Second Madam couldn't stand his arrogance and wanted to say a few more words, but Cheng Zhao changed the subject.","\"Did anything interesting happen while you were admiring the lanterns last night?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Zhou Yuanqi thought of something and seemed a little annoyed. He flatly said, \"No,\" stood up, and left.","The Second Madam felt he needed a good beating.","On his way to the clan school, Zhou Yuanqi recalled an incident from last night.","When they went downstairs to admire the lanterns, they encountered an extremely handsome young master, accompanied by a gentle and charming woman.","The man was dressed luxuriously and formally, and because of his good looks, he stood out in the crowd.","Zhou Yuanqi looked down on everyone, but he thought this man was quite outstanding and could be \"recruited as a live-in son-in-law\" for his sister-in-law.","He took a liking to this man.","But then he saw someone greet him.","Zhou Yuanqi was confused. He listened from the side for a long time before he finally understood that this man was Zhang Yunqi, the husband of Third Miss Cheng.","The woman accompanying Mr. Zhang was his outer room.","His outer room was slender and delicate, possessing a certain frail beauty. But compared to Third Miss Cheng, whose skin was whiter than frost and snow, she was both vulgar and infuriating.","Zhou Yuanqi had heard that Mr. Zhang had redeemed a sold daughter of a convicted official. Fearing his family's disapproval, he hid it from everyone and ran away, abandoning his family and wife.","Many people mocked Third Miss Cheng because of this.","She was originally the most outstanding noble lady in the entire capital, and even the Empress praised her endlessly. Suddenly suffering such a fate, those who were jealous of her all stepped forward to kick her while she was down.","How wretched she must have been at that time!","Zhou Yuanqi knew all about these past events. He just found it hard to match the person in the rumors with the person he saw in reality.","Moreover, they didn't match at all.","Cheng Ying was elegant and noble, talented but not arrogant, and not pitiful at all. She didn't look like someone who was covered in disgrace. And Zhang Yunqi's outer room didn't have a beauty capable of toppling cities that could crush Cheng Ying.","On the contrary, Cheng Ying and Zhang Yunqi's appearances complemented each other perfectly.","When Zhou Yuanqi thought about how he had taken a fancy to this man's good looks and vainly attempted to recruit him as a son-in-law for his sister-in-law, he felt as disgusted as if he had eaten a fly.","At the time, many people were looking at Zhang Yunqi and his wife, deeply interested in their secrets.","His young uncle, Fan Xiao, watched with even greater relish.","\"To make a beauty suffer such humiliation, that Mr. Zhang truly deserves death by a thousand cuts!\"","Recalling it, Zhou Yuanqi was still full of anger as he puffed his cheeks and went to school.","The Second Madam was also confused when she saw Zhou Yuanqi suddenly lose his temper and leave.","It was the sixteenth day of the first lunar month, and Chengming Hall also resumed work. After finishing breakfast at Jiangyun Courtyard, Cheng Zhao took a small oil carriage and rushed to Chengming Hall.","The morning was very busy.","Huan Qingtang didn't need to go to Shou'an Courtyard. She still followed Madam Song.","The same went for Cheng Zhao.","It wasn't until close to noon that the tasks were distributed, and they had already missed lunchtime.","The First Madam kept Cheng Zhao behind. \"You two sisters-in-law will both eat here with me, so you don't have to go back and forth. I've already instructed the main kitchen to send your portions over.\"","It wasn't a discussion at all.","She had something to say.","Cheng Zhao recalled yesterday's confrontation at Shou'an Courtyard and had a feeling in her heart. She smiled and nodded. \"Then I'll trouble First Aunt.\"","They had a simple lunch.","After the meal, the three of them sat down to drink tea and chat. The First Madam asked Cheng Zhao about her lantern viewing last night.","Cheng Zhao gave a brief account.","The First Madam smiled and said, \"Cheng-shi, as an elder, there is something I must say to you.\"","Cheng Zhao sat up straight. \"Please enlighten me, First Aunt.\"","\"As a daughter-in-law in the Duke's mansion, you cannot monopolize all the benefits. We all respect the Old Madam and the Duke, but it is inappropriate to casually use others' mistakes to claim credit,\" the First Madam said.","She was referring to how Cheng Zhao had used the loophole in Huan Qingtang's words yesterday to resolve the conflict between the Old Madam and Zhou Yuanshen.","Cheng Zhao smiled. \"First Aunt is absolutely right. I share the same view as you.\"","She added, \"Interfering in someone else's private matters and causing discord between a wife and a concubine, I also consider that a 'mistake'.\"","Huan Qingtang froze.","Madam Song was stunned.","It turned out that Cheng Zhao didn't feel any guilt at all.","She even believed that when Huan Qingtang publicly suggested bringing Mu Jiang out for the Lantern Festival, she was interfering in the private matters between her and Zhou Yuanshen, and that Huan Qingtang had provoked her first.","But in the eyes of the First Madam and Huan Qingtang, Mu Jiang wasn't a concubine in Cheng Zhao's room at all, and she didn't fall under Cheng Zhao's jurisdiction.","The First Madam had intended to teach Cheng Zhao a lesson.","A person who had used someone else should logically feel embarrassed.","She hadn't expected to be picked apart by Cheng Zhao instead.","Huan Qingtang drank her tea in silence, seemingly not hearing anything.","The First Madam, however, grew angry. \"Cheng-shi, by picking faults like this, have you studied in vain?\"","Cheng Zhao didn't get angry, nor was she embarrassed or apprehensive. Her expression remained unchanged as she simply said, \"First Aunt, neither of us has made a mistake, so why do you seem to be 'flying into a rage out of humiliation'?\"","The First Madam: \"...\"","Huan Qingtang, standing to the side, gave a soft smile.","It seemed a little helpless, yet also remarkably magnanimous and unbothered."]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49: We Must Pay More Attention to Cheng Zhao","paragraphs":["The first dispute of the new year broke out in the Chengming Hall.","There was no loud quarreling, but the words were sharp and unsparing.","Huan Qingtang used the words of the First Madam to accuse Cheng Zhao of stepping on her to climb up yesterday, saying she was vicious.","Cheng Zhao, however, stated that Huan Qingtang started it first and that she had crossed the line.","If Huan Qingtang's words were accepted by the Old Madam, and Mu Jiang came out to celebrate the Lantern Festival, whose reputation would be damaged, Cheng Zhao's or Huan Qingtang's?","Of course, it would be Cheng Zhao's.","Since she had provoked her first, she shouldn't expect her to show mercy.","Huan Qingtang didn't act pitifully or try to defend herself. She just remained silent, as if she hadn't heard Cheng Zhao's words. When the situation was unfavorable to her, she just pretended nothing had happened.","Cheng Zhao's mother had also taught her this trick, to be used when there was no other choice.","The First Madam, Madam Song, was very angry, but she was awakened by Cheng Zhao's words. Cheng Zhao didn't say anything about her, it was only Huan Qingtang who had made a mistake.","Cheng Zhao would not speak ill of others.","If the winner insists on showing off, it will only expose their own shortcomings, and the prestige they have won will be greatly reduced.","The smell of gunpowder was so strong, but the East Secondary Room was quiet.","Except for the First Madam, Madam Song, no one spoke loudly.","\"... You all go back and rest for a while, I also need to take a nap,\" the First Madam said.","Her face didn't look good.","Cheng Zhao said yes.","She and Huan Qingtang went out. The two walked out of the East Secondary Room, their attitude as relaxed as if nothing had happened.","The First Madam was still very angry: \"This Cheng Shi, is simply...\"","She didn't know how to describe Cheng Zhao.","She looked down on her, yet felt that she was very slippery and difficult to deal with.","She wished she could step on her and crush her to death.","The First Madam's trusted old servant said, \"Madam, this old servant actually thinks that the Third Young Madam's words are not wrong. It was indeed the First Young Madam who provoked her first.\"","\"Why are you siding with an outsider?\"","\"This old servant means that you should restrain the First Young Madam. If she keeps handing knives to others, she will suffer a crushing defeat.","You and she clearly occupy the high ground, easy to defend and hard to attack. For the Third Young Madam to try to fight her way into the Chengming Hall is tantamount to ascending to heaven.","But if the First Young Madam makes mistakes and falls down herself, dragging you down with her, that is truly giving the Third Young Madam an advantage.\"","The First Madam's expression restrained.","\"Do you think Cheng Shi is easy to deal with? She has no respect for hierarchy in her eyes, we can't allow her to be complacent,\" the First Madam said.","She didn't really listen.","The managing servant, however, felt that they should pay more attention to Cheng Shi.","Treat Cheng Shi as an opponent to study.","Cheng Shi not only has ambition but also means. As long as there is a stepping stone, she will fight desperately to climb up. She clearly wants to live in the Chengming Hall.","A daughter-in-law without desires and demands would not behave like Cheng Shi.","If they are not smart enough to beat Cheng Shi down, then the only way for the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the first branch is to remain completely still.","No matter how Cheng Shi provokes, do not respond.","Occupying their position without moving, and having the Old Madam backing them up, Cheng Shi would have no way at all.","Unfortunately, the First Madam and the First Young Madam seemed to be exceptionally confident in themselves.","Even when Cheng Zhao didn't provoke them, they still had to jump around a bit.","The gunpowder in the Duke's Mansion had already been ignited. Without fighting to a victory or defeat, neither side would beat the drums and withdraw their troops.","The servants would be tossed about along with them, and the managing servant trembled in her heart.","Cheng Zhao went to the Chenhui Courtyard for her afternoon nap.","Nanny Li sent a young maid to deliver a bowl of bird's nest porridge to nourish Cheng Zhao.","Qiubai was waiting to serve Cheng Zhao as she rested.","Cheng Zhao didn't sleep, she just leaned on the large heated brick bed by the window in the secondary room and finished the bowl of bird's nest porridge.","\"... The First Madam actually blames you for stepping on the First Young Madam?\" Qiubai asked.","Cheng Zhao: \"That mother-in-law and daughter-in-law are still of one mind. However, this unity is not strong enough, they will fall out sooner or later.\"","\"The First Young Madam was actually able to persuade the First Madam to stand up for her, she is quite something,\" Qiubai said.","Cheng Zhao nodded.","Qiubai lowered her voice: \"Once the Emperor 'bestows a marriage' and she also becomes the Duke's wife, your life will not be easy.\"","If Zhou Yuanshen were to marry two wives, it would definitely be a marriage bestowed by an imperial edict.","This is much more honorable than a marriage bestowed by the Empress.","The Old Madam had long thought about \"dividing power\". The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the first branch would manage the household affairs, and Zhou Yuanshen would inherit the title. This way, the title would not be lost, and the Duke's assets would be firmly in the old lady's hands.","Within the Duke's Mansion, no one could obtain real \"power\" and outshine the Old Madam.","The older she got, the more she only trusted the power and money in her own hands.","If they wanted the \"dual marriage\" matter not to be criticized by high-ranking noble families, the best way was a marriage bestowed by the Emperor.","This was not to elevate Huan Qingtang, but to preserve the dignity of the entire Duke's Mansion, as well as the Old Madam's status.","If the dual marriage really happened, Cheng Zhao's life would indeed be very difficult.","\"... Fate is just like this. If I had gotten pregnant first, this path would have fewer thorns, but unfortunately, the concubine got pregnant first,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Qiubai quietly asked her: \"Should we ask Madam to invite a Guanyin who sends children for you?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Would it be useful?\"","\"Do you believe in Guanyin or the Duke?\" Qiubai asked.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Then the Guanyin who sends children is more reliable.","\"Although there's nothing wrong, I still want a doctor to take my pulse,\" Cheng Zhao said.","To ensure she is healthy.","Cheng Zhao added: \"I also heard that there were some rumors about the Duke and his widowed sister-in-law before. Roughly, they had some affection when they were young, but it ended up as nothing.\"","Qiubai: \"Didn't Madam inquire about this? You said you didn't care at the time. How about you ask Madam carefully next time you go back?\"","If Zhou Yuanshen and Huan Qingtang had a good relationship, and the two had \"separated\" for these years, once they had a dual marriage, wouldn't they desperately try to make up for it?","Qiubai felt sorry for her young lady just thinking about it.","\"Marrying into any family wouldn't be as frustrating as the Zhou family,\" Qiubai said.","Cheng Zhao: \"No one wanted to marry into the Zhou family, neither me nor my parents, it was a marriage bestowed by the Empress.\"","She added, \"Although the inner courtyard of the Zhou family is frustrating, I am already a super-grade titled madam. Marrying into which family could give me such an opportunity? Some people struggle all their lives and don't even get a title before they die.\"","Qiubai couldn't help but laugh.","Besides the young male servant Nanfeng, there was no one else in the Chenhui Courtyard, and the master and servant spoke softly, chatting freely without any restraint.","After the afternoon nap ended, Cheng Zhao had to go to the Chengming Hall again, and a maid came.","Cheng Zhao had seen this maid before. She served in Zhou Yuanshen's outer study and was named Mingyu.","Mingyu was slender and elegant, with a delicate appearance. She bowed respectfully, \"Madam, I will deliver some of the Duke's documents inside first, he will read them this evening.\"","Cheng Zhao nodded slightly: \"Go in and put them down.\"","She went to the Chengming Hall.","Cheng Zhao handled affairs once every three days, and after finishing today, she could rest for two days.","There were no disputes in the afternoon, and matters were quickly sorted out, so Cheng Zhao returned to the Nonghua Courtyard.","After coming back, she first practiced swordsmanship, then took a bath, and sat on the large heated brick bed by the window to dry her hair.","\"... The Duke said he will have dinner in the Nonghua Courtyard tonight.\" The maid named Mingyu came again.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","He rested here yesterday, why is he coming again?","Cheng Zhao made up her mind and instructed Qiubai, \"Go back to the Cheng family tomorrow and tell my mother to quickly invite a Guanyin who sends children for me.\"","Quickly get pregnant to completely interrupt this matter of \"the Duke coming for dinner.\"","She wanted some peace and quiet.","Zhou Yuanshen hadn't arrived yet, and Cheng Zhao's hair was dry. Nanny Li taught her how to put up her hair.","Cheng Zhao's hands were quite deft, but she wasn't good at fiddling with hair, and after a long time, it was still a mess.","Seeing that it was getting late and Zhou Yuanshen was about to arrive, Cheng Zhao asked Nanny Li to put it up for her, and she would slowly learn later."]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50: Zhou Yuanshen Proactively Extends an Olive Branch","paragraphs":["In the evening, Zhou Yuanshen arrived at the Nonghua Courtyard.","Seeing him enter, Cheng Zhao stood up to greet him before they both sat down.","\"...Today, the Emperor went mad and slashed a minister with a sword,\" Zhou Yuanshen suddenly said to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao was stunned. \"Who? My grandfather?\"","Zhou Yuanshen paused. \"It has nothing to do with your family.\"","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","Then why are you telling me?","Wait, no.","She raised her eyes, looking at Zhou Yuanshen, and after a long moment, she tentatively asked, \"Is My Lord chatting with me about court affairs?\"","\"Yes.\"","Cheng Zhao was speechless again.","She felt it was very strange and was a bit confused, but she still went along with his words.","\"Why did the Emperor attack someone in public?\"","Convicting a scholar-official required a very strict process; even severe torture was not allowed. There had to be sufficient evidence.","By slashing someone right in the court, the Emperor would face attacks from all his subjects. They would rise up in resistance and refuse to work, causing the entire government apparatus to come to a standstill.","Government affairs needed officials to handle them.","Not only that, but it would also leave a heavy mark in the historical records: the court historians were also scholar-officials, and they would record this matter in detail, leaving the Emperor with a legacy of infamy for thousands of years.","\"The Emperor wanted to rebuild the imperial mausoleum, which was opposed by Grand Preceptor Guo. They had been discussing this matter since before the new year.","After the new year, Grand Preceptor Guo's disciples used this to stir up trouble and said some very unpleasant things. In a fit of rage, the Emperor drew his sword and slashed him,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao listened carefully to his words.","When the Emperor attended court, he would occasionally carry a long sword. However, this item was mostly for decoration; courtiers, whether civil or military, were not allowed to bring swords into the hall.","\"...The Emperor's sword was sharpened?\" she asked.","Zhou Yuanshen looked back at her. \"It shouldn't have been.\"","\"Then someone deliberately played a dirty trick. They first angered the Emperor, and also had his sword sharpened?\" Cheng Zhao said.","Otherwise, even if he drew his sword, it would only be to frighten the courtiers.","Once blood was drawn, it was completely different.","This incident would affect the political situation and implicate many people, including the Duke of Chen's estate.","A storm was coming.","\"Someone must have tampered with it,\" Zhou Yuanshen said. \"It is the doing of the Guo family.\"","The Guo clan was a prominent family from Yingzhou, renowned throughout the world, and the current Empress was born into the Guo clan. The influence of top-tier noble families in the court was much greater than that of the Emperor himself.","The Guo family had always wanted to win over the Duke of Chen's estate, as well as the Cheng family, which was why Empress Guo had bestowed the marriage between Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen.","Of course, if this caused the Zhou and Cheng families to turn against each other and engage in internal strife, it would also benefit the Guo clan.","Killing two birds with one stone.","\"My Lord, does the Emperor want you to exert yourself and resolve this matter for him again?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"Yes.\"","\"Do you need my grandfather's help?\" Cheng Zhao asked again.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"I will go and speak to the Prime Minister myself.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Then tomorrow I can accompany you to the Cheng family.\"","\"There's no need,\" Zhou Yuanshen said. \"It's just a casual chat; you don't need to show up. This matter isn't too complicated. As long as the Emperor relents and names the Seventh Prince as the Crown Prince, this issue will be easily resolved.\"","\"The Seventh Prince's maternal family is too powerful; the Emperor will not be willing,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"What are My Lord's thoughts?\"","\"The Seventh Prince is weak and cowardly. If he becomes Emperor, it will be a fatal blow to the imperial clan. But for the noble families, it is an excellent opportunity,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao glanced at him.","When he said opportunity, he didn't just mean the opportunity for the Guo clan of Yingzhou, but also his own.","Nowadays, the power of the imperial clan had withered severely.","The Emperor's murderous actions would inevitably lead to the weakening of imperial power. Absolute power could never be achieved through slaughter; it would only alienate the scholar-officials from the Emperor even more.","The late Emperor had planted the seeds of disaster, and the current Emperor was walking down his father's old path. The court was in utter chaos at this time.","At the beginning of last year, the Prince of Xingyang set up his own banner and wanted to raise an army to rebel.","For such a treasonous act, the courtiers were actually divided on whether to send troops to attack him. When Cheng Zhao heard about it at the time, she found it unbelievable.","At that moment, she realized just how dissatisfied the courtiers were with the Emperor!","Fortunately, the Prince of Xingyang was soon assassinated, and the matter was left unsettled.","Now, just at the start of the year, the Emperor slashed a minister in the main hall. This action would inevitably stir up massive waves.","She wondered how it would ultimately be resolved.","Cheng Zhao suddenly realized that perhaps one day, war would break out everywhere.","Court politics was not just a contest within the main hall; it could also cause the disaster of war. This had happened in the late Emperor's later years, but at that time, the Helian clan still had luck on their side, and several rebellions were quelled.","And now?","Did the Helian clan still have such luck?","Cheng Zhao looked at Zhou Yuanshen.","She suddenly realized that if the world fell into chaos, Zhou Yuanshen might not be without a chance, because he himself was a military general, and his maternal family, Madam Fan, also held military power.","\"...Does My Lord feel that an heir will definitely be established this year?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","\"It is imminent,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The husband and wife chatted about court politics for quite a while.","Cheng Zhao understood the situation very well.","Her eldest sister was very good at managing the household, and her third sister was brimming with literary talent, but she alone liked to read history books and listen to her grandfather talk about political affairs.","After dinner, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen played chess and continued chatting about this matter.","They had been married for almost half a year, and this was the first time they had conversed so smoothly.","Right before going to sleep, Cheng Zhao suddenly asked, \"Why did My Lord talk to me about these things today?\"","\"Your eldest sister said that you really like listening to your grandfather talk about these things. Therefore, you are very favored by your grandfather,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","\"When did Eldest Sister tell you?\"","\"When you all went downstairs to guess lantern riddles,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","\"You said that you are willing to be this Duke's wife. Cheng Zhao, I have no intention of tormenting anyone, and I am not deliberately being distant with you,\" he added.","Cheng Zhao thought of what happened last night.","The two of them were indeed very much strangers; even the days they had shared a bed added up to less than a month.","Before Mu Jiang got pregnant, he always rested in the Lijing Courtyard, where there were beautiful concubines and maids.","Cheng Zhao didn't have much interest in chatting. But being able to understand him as a person was beneficial to her.","If he showed her a bit of favoritism, Cheng Zhao's path would be easier to walk.","She also relied on him for children.","\"Of course, I want to be closer to My Lord,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen pulled her into his arms.","During their intimacy that night, his movements were much gentler.","Cheng Zhao once again felt the scorching heat from last time, and her breathing became so tight she could barely catch her breath. And when he leaned down, wanting to cover her lips, Cheng Zhao hurriedly avoided him.","She was about to run out of breath, how could she let him block her mouth?","Zhou Yuanshen's movements paused again.","He hadn't fully enjoyed himself yet, but he hastily wrapped things up. After washing up with water, the couple went to sleep.","He left before dawn.","When he left, Cheng Zhao was still thinking, \"Is there an early court session today too? The Emperor slashed a minister, won't Grand Preceptor Guo make a fuss for a few days?\"","Her thoughts were not wrong.","That day, Zhou Yuanshen was indeed at home; he was reading in the Chenhui Courtyard and even sent someone to tell Cheng Zhao that he would come to the Nonghua Courtyard for lunch.","Cheng Zhao didn't have to go to the Chengming Hall today, and she thought to herself, why is he being so endless?","\"...Suyue, make a trip back and tell my mother to quickly get a statue of the Child-Giving Guanyin for me,\" Cheng Zhao said.","After Mu Jiang got pregnant, he stopped going to the Lijing Courtyard, and Cheng Zhao also hoped she could gain some peace and quiet soon."]},{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51: Another Farewell to Zhou Yuanshen","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen had said he would come over for lunch.","As noon approached, he sent the young servant boy, Nanfeng, to Nonghua Courtyard to inform Cheng Zhao: The Duke has some business to attend to outside and will not be dining here.","Cheng Zhao grabbed a handful of coins to reward Nanfeng, glanced at Suyue, and asked Suyue to see the boy out.","Soon, Suyue returned.","She whispered to Cheng Zhao, The First Madam sent someone to deliver furniture to Chenghui Courtyard, saying she wanted to replace two chairs for the Duke, and sent Nanfeng away. When Nanfeng returned, someone had trespassed into Chenghui Courtyard by mistake. The Duke lost his temper and immediately went to Chengming Hall. He had Nanfeng come over to our side to drop a word, and then he left.","Cheng Zhao asked, Trespassed by mistake? Who was it?","It couldn't be Huan Qingtang.","Huan Qingtang came from a prestigious family and had the Old Madam paving the way for her; she wouldn't be so desperate.","It was a visiting cousin, a young lady, Suyue said. As for who exactly, Nanfeng didn't know either.","Cheng Zhao let out a cold sneer.","The First Madam, Madam Song, truly looked down on Cheng Zhao and was far too arrogant, constantly using these underhanded methods to disgust people.","Taking advantage of Mu Jiang's pregnancy, did First Madam Song also want to send someone to reel in Zhou Yuanshen?","All the women in the inner courtyard used this trick on him. It seemed like scheming and plotting, but in reality, it was just rewarding and flattering him. Cheng Zhao thought he had rather good luck.","Serve the meal. I am a bit hungry, Cheng Zhao said.","Suyue complied.","She went out to give the orders and returned to ask Cheng Zhao, Young Madam, should we go and inquire about that young lady?","Ask around, just so we know what is going on, Cheng Zhao said. Have Qiubai go ask Nanfeng; she is more familiar with him.","Qiubai took on the task.","Cheng Zhao then instructed Suyue to make a trip back to the Cheng family estate around noon.","By dusk, Qiubai had figured out the situation at Chenghui Courtyard, and Suyue had also returned from the Cheng family.","...The girl who intruded into Chenghui Courtyard is named Hu Zhiwei, living in the courtyard near the back street. She is a relative from the First Madam's maiden family who came to seek refuge, Qiubai said.","What kind of relative from her maiden family?","I think she is the daughter of her younger female cousin, calling the First Madam aunt, Qiubai said.","Cheng Zhao pondered, The Marquis of Changling's estate is right here in the capital. Since she is the daughter of a cousin, why didn't she seek refuge with the Song family, but instead came to the Duke of Chen's estate?","Perhaps the Marquis of Changling's estate does not accept outside relatives seeking refuge? Qiubai suggested.","These noble families still looked glorious and prominent on the outside, but their insides were actually quite empty. Just feeding their own servants was a struggle.","It was fine for relatives to occasionally come for a handout, but long-term refuge required assigning a courtyard, arranging meals, and even subsidizing them with hundreds of coins every month. A clean family like the Marquis of Changling's estate might not be able to afford it.","Young Madam, do you need to reveal this matter to the Old Madam? Qiubai asked.","Cheng Zhao replied, I am only inquiring so I know what is going on, lest my Eldest Aunt treats me like a fool. It is not to stop anything.","She added, The harder my Eldest Aunt tries, the easier it is for her to make mistakes. Once she hands me an opportunity, I will have more authority to manage affairs.","Qiubai hesitated, Then the Duke...","This kind of thing requires mutual consent. Could the girl hold him down? If he wants it, what does it have to do with us?","Qiubai was speechless.","Cheng Zhao turned to ask Suyue, What did my mother say?","Madam said she is very gratified that you, Young Madam, are taking the matter of heirs so seriously. She will bring you back for a visit, invite a doctor to check your pulse first, and then use the excuse of visiting the Duke's estate to bring you a Guanyin statue, Suyue reported.","Cheng Zhao nodded slightly.","Her mother handled things flawlessly.","Sure enough, the next day the Cheng family sent a managing older female servant to the Zhou family, saying that Cheng Zhao's mother had a nightmare yesterday and was very worried about Cheng Zhao, so she sent someone to check on her.","Cheng Zhao took the opportunity to tell the First Madam, My mother occasionally suffers from nightmares, and I am not very at ease. I want to go back and see her.","She quietly watched the First Madam.","Yesterday, the First Madam had sent someone to trespass into Chenghui Courtyard by mistake. Many people already knew about this, and she felt inexplicably in the wrong.","Facing Cheng Zhao, the First Madam's smile was even more attentive, You are a filial child. Have the gatekeeper prepare some gifts for you. Go early and return early.","The gatekeeper prepared several common gifts for her.","Cheng Zhao also went to tell the Second Madam.","The Second Madam prepared precious tonics like ginseng and bird's nest, instructing Cheng Zhao to attend to the sick carefully, and added, Staying overnight is also fine. Send a maid back to tell me, and I will go to Shou'an Courtyard to speak on your behalf.","Cheng Zhao smiled, Thank you, Mother. I shouldn't need to stay overnight.","The Second Madam didn't yet know about the incident at Chenghui Courtyard yesterday, otherwise she would have exploded with anger again.","Cheng Zhao didn't tell her, to avoid causing her grief.","Returning to the Cheng family, she first went to see her grandfather.","Grandfather indeed had not gone to court.","The Emperor had slashed a court official, and the impact of this incident was terrible. For the past few days, ministers had claimed illness and refused to attend court. Yesterday, the Emperor even invited several trusted aides into the imperial study to discuss the matter.","...Establishing a crown prince is also troublesome, Grandfather said.","Grandfather did not want to establish a crown prince.","Once a crown prince was established, the entire political situation would fall into the hands of Grand Tutor Guo, which would be detrimental to the Cheng family.","Of course, the Guo family had the upper hand this time.","Grand Tutor Guo even secretly threatened the Emperor: This matter is too terrible. For the sake of the Emperor's dignity, the historians can choose not to record it, Grandfather said.","Cheng Zhao's expression changed, That is truly terrifying.","The role of historians is to clearly record historical facts.","Once it was not recorded, this event would have no historical evidence to support it. In the future, folk rumors and unofficial histories would adapt it into something outrageous.","Outrageous enough to go down in infamy for thousands of years.","For example, unofficial histories might say the Emperor skinned a minister alive in court, and even roasted human flesh to eat.","—And that wouldn't even be the most bizarre. Cheng Zhao couldn't even imagine the more outrageous versions.","In short, the incident had happened. Grand Tutor Guo saying do not record means there would be no evidence to refute the claim that the Emperor ate human flesh, which would scare the Emperor to death.","A mistake was fine if it was wrong; if properly recorded, it was merely a stain, rather than a blank canvas for rumors to spread.","The blank canvas was the most terrifying.","A crown prince must be established, Cheng Zhao affirmed.","Grandfather nodded.","Cheng Zhao asked, What about Zhou Yuanshen? What effort is he going to put in for the Emperor this time?","He is in the palace today. The Emperor will definitely entrust him with a heavy responsibility, Grandfather said. The Emperor currently trusts the Zhou family very much.","The Emperor has always relied heavily on the Zhou family. Back then, it was the Zhou family who protected him, and it was the Zhou family's military power that helped him secure his rule over the empire, Cheng Zhao said.","The grandfather and granddaughter talked for quite a while.","Only then did Cheng Zhao go to her mother's courtyard.","Her mother asked her what she and her grandfather had chatted about.","Grandfather told me about some court affairs, Cheng Zhao said.","The doctor her mother had invited for her was from Wu Commandery, skilled in medicine and tight-lipped.","After checking her pulse, the doctor said Cheng Zhao had a heavy heart, causing her qi to stagnate, but her body was otherwise fine.","Relax your mind, Madam, the doctor advised. A person is like driftwood; let the water support you, and perhaps you will rise. If you keep struggling, you will keep sinking to the bottom, which is counterproductive.","Cheng Zhao agreed vocally, but smiled bitterly in her heart.","If she fell into the water, she would definitely be the one scratching and struggling desperately.","She could not let fate arrange things for her. She seemed to believe more in hard work than in destiny, unlike how water naturally supported driftwood.","Her mother saw the doctor out and then chatted with Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao then asked about the past, You previously inquired about it. What old history is there between Zhou Yuanshen and Lady Huan?"]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52: The Kiss","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao asked her mother about the old romance between Zhou Yuanshen and Huan Qingtang.","\"The Huan family has an excellent reputation. When outsiders speak of their daughters, it is mostly with praise. As for the events of the past, it's no longer possible to find out the exact details; it's a mix of truth and falsehood,\" her mother said.","\"Did Zhou Yuanshen admire her from a very early age?\"","Her mother looked at her quietly. \"Zhaozhao, of my three daughters, you are the most beautiful. But compared to your beauty, what you excel at even more is scheming.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"I just asked you a little question, why are you scolding me?\"","\"'He who steals a hook is executed; he who steals a state becomes a feudal lord.' If you fail, you are deeply manipulative; if you succeed, you are far-sighted in strategy. I am saying that you are resourceful,\" her mother explained.","Cheng Zhao: \"...What are you trying to say?\"","\"What does it matter what happened in the past between the Duke of Chen and the Huan woman, Zhaozhao? Will you lose?\" her mother asked.","Cheng Zhao fell silent. \"It's hard to say.\"","\"Then let me tell you this. The Huan family has a pure and noble reputation. As long as your cousin-in-law defeats you, her past with the Duke of Chen will naturally be a beautiful legend. Even if it is false, it will become true.","\"If you win, a noble lady from an aristocratic family in Wu Commandery, pure-hearted and intelligent, makes a perfect youthful match with the Duke of Chen. Then, even if the past is true, it will become false.","\"Zhaozhao, you are already married to the Duke of Chen. If you have no intention of backing out, the truth or falsehood of the past is meaningless. Your persistence is nothing more than prying into privacy,\" her mother said.","Cheng Zhao was silent for a long time before she finally said, \"I understand, Mother.\"","Her mother gave a slight nod. \"If you really want to pry, when you visit Princess Qing'an's residence in the future, you can ask indirectly.","\"It was Princess Qing'an who acted as the matchmaker back then, though she rarely mentions it now. She should know some of the inside story.\"","She added, \"Of course, you could just ask the Duke of Chen directly. He knows best.\"","Cheng Zhao nodded.","Mid-afternoon, Cheng Zhao returned to the Duke of Chen's estate.","She first went to Shou'an Courtyard to pay her respects to the Dowager Madame, bringing back several tonics her mother had prepared.","Then she went to Jiangyun Courtyard. Besides the return gifts the Cheng family prepared for the Second Madam, there was also a set of the Four Treasures of the Study intended for Zhou Yuanqi.","It just so happened that Zhou Yuanqi had returned from the clan school.","Upon seeing the set of the Four Treasures of the Study, obvious surprise flashed in his eyes, but he held it back. \"You didn't need to bring me a gift. I'm not a child.\"","The Second Madam could hardly bear to look at him.","Cheng Zhao smiled and said, \"You guessed the lantern riddle right last time, and it was agreed that my grandfather would give you something. I even mentioned that riddle to my grandfather today.\"","\"What did Chancellor Cheng say?\" Zhou Yuanqi asked.","In just these few short days, Zhou Yuanqi had already gained some reputation.","His performance at the Lantern Festival had been astonishing, and given his young age, the students of Hengshan Academy praised him everywhere. His reputation for talent had finally caught the attention of the scholarly circles.","\"He praised your quick thinking. When you study, you don't just read blindly. However, your thinking is a bit shallow and still needs my third sister's guidance. He suggested that when you are a few years older, you should go out on a study tour,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi looked like he was humbly accepting the teaching, listening attentively and asking Cheng Zhao to tell him more.","But regarding the topic of Zhou Yuanqi, Cheng Zhao hadn't actually talked too much with her grandfather.","\"In a few days, you can come visit my maiden home again. If you have any questions, you can ask my grandfather in person,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"We'll see.\"","\"He really appreciates you.\"","Zhou Yuanqi almost let his joy show on his face, but he forced himself to hold it in, though his eyebrows still lifted in delight.","The Second Madam was absolutely amused to death by him.","\"How is your mother's health?\" the Second Madam asked out of concern.","Cheng Zhao: \"She is very well, just missing me a little. She had a nightmare, but it was nothing serious.\"","She smiled and added, \"She also said she was sorry for disturbing you all and would like to come visit in a few days.\"","She quietly told the Second Madam, \"It's mainly because she wants to invite a statue of the Child-Giving Guanyin for me.\"","The Second Madam was slightly surprised. \"This... you don't need to rush. How old are you, anyway?\"","\"She has this intention, and I cannot disobey her. As children, obedience is filial piety,\" Cheng Zhao said.","For a moment, the Second Madam felt very envious.","If only she had a daughter.","Back when she was pregnant with Zhou Yuanqi, she had wholeheartedly hoped for a daughter. In the end, the one she gave birth to was as delicate as carved jade, even prettier than a girl, but unfortunately, he had the stuffy air of an old pedant—neither affectionate nor cute.","But it didn't matter. Now someone else's good daughter was her daughter-in-law. From now on, they would be mother and daughter for a lifetime.","\"When is she coming? When she does, we will host the meal on our side,\" the Second Madam said.","\"When she sends someone to let me know, I'll tell you,\" Cheng Zhao replied.","In the late part of the first lunar month, it actually snowed again in the capital.","A spring snow fell, and the weather that had finally warmed up a bit turned freezing once more.","Cheng Zhao's mother sent a letter, saying she was coming to the Duke of Chen's estate to visit her daughter.","Upon receiving the letter, Cheng Zhao routinely notified the Dowager Madame and Chengming Hall.","Then she told the Second Madam.","When her mother arrived, just like Cheng Zhao's eldest sister, she had prepared gifts for every part of the Duke of Chen's estate.","For the Dowager Madame, it was a string of precious Buddhist prayer beads. For the First Madam and Huan Qingtang, there were two sets of tourmaline and ruby hair ornaments. As for the Second Madam, she received tribute silk that had been awarded by the Empress.","The Second Madam liked it very much and sent Nanny Fan to quietly spread the word, letting the servants of the ducal estate know just how wealthy and generous her in-laws were.","When the First Madam and Huan Qingtang's maiden families came to visit, they only brought superficial, inexpensive, common gifts.","They were supposed to dine in Jiangyun Courtyard, but because the weather was cold, the Second Madam, being considerate of her in-law and daughter-in-law, had it arranged in Nonghua Courtyard.","\"...It is all my fault. After the marriage was bestowed, I didn't inquire carefully and was full of resentment. Of course, I wasn't resenting you, but rather this marriage.","\"Before the wedding, I didn't visit your esteemed residence, and it is only today that I finally meet my in-law. I have offended you greatly, and I will drink three cups of wine with you later as an apology,\" the Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao's mother couldn't help but smile.","The Second Madam was truly straightforward, speaking whatever was on her mind with a heart full of sincerity.","\"You are too polite. With you taking care of Zhaozhao, I am very much relieved,\" Madam Cheng said.","While they were talking, Nanny Li had already led the maids to settle the Child-Giving Guanyin statue in the warm pavilion on the east side.","Cheng Zhao sat down to converse.","There was some noise from the inner bedroom. Cheng Zhao heard it and glanced over curiously.","Nanny Li went in to check.","She quickly came out and whispered a few words to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao frowned slightly.","\"You should go take a look quickly,\" Nanny Li said.","Cheng Zhao stood up and said to her mother and mother-in-law, \"Excuse me for a moment.\"","Stepping out of the eastern secondary room, she then asked, \"What is going on?\"","\"I don't know. The Duke's expression doesn't look quite right; it seems like he's drunk,\" Nanny Li said.","Cheng Zhao: \"His mother-in-law and mother are both here, yet instead of coming to pay his respects, he's hiding in the inner bedroom?\"","When did he even come to Nonghua Courtyard?","Filled with questions, she entered the bedroom.","She didn't see Zhou Yuanshen at first, but she heard his somewhat rapid breathing.","As she walked past the folding screen, she saw him leaning against the dressing table, his head slightly lowered.","Just as Cheng Zhao was about to step forward, he grabbed her and pulled her over.","She felt the scorching heat of Zhou Yuanshen's palm.","The snow outside hadn't completely melted yet, and the cold wind was biting, but the skin of his cheeks and neck was flushed red, like red-hot iron.","\"My Lord Duke, you are...\"","She was a bit frightened.","Before she could finish her sentence, Zhou Yuanshen pulled her hair loose.","Cheng Zhao looked at him in astonishment.","She was already pinned against the dressing table by him. He leaned down, and with scalding breath, he kissed her lips.","Cheng Zhao's eyes widened sharply."]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53: Tonic","paragraphs":["A gentle breeze blew outside the window, carrying the chill of peach blossom snow as it sneaked into the inner bedchamber like a mischievous child.","Cheng Zhao's hair hung loose. Zhou Yuanshen held the back of her neck with one hand and wrapped his other arm around her, trapping them together in a small, intimate space.","Dark tresses obscured a bit of her vision as he kissed her. Cheng Zhao felt as though she were dreaming; nothing felt quite real.","His breath was scalding.","Hotter than the sparks of a heating stove.","Yet Cheng Zhao felt cold, her senses exceptionally heightened in this moment.","The intertwining of their lips and teeth made her tremble, and with the chilly wind blowing against the skin of her hand, she shivered and snapped back to her senses.","She pushed against Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen pressed in closer, nearly pinning Cheng Zhao against the dressing table.","Cheng Zhao's back bumped against the bronze mirror.","She tried in vain to grab onto something, knocking a rouge box down with her hand and causing a clatter.","\"Young Madam...\" Nanny Li stood outside the door curtain, her voice slightly hesitant. \"Young Madam, shall I serve the meal?\"","The door was not closed tightly.","And Zhou Yuanshen's hand had already hooked onto the sash of her skirt.","He looked as if he wanted to swallow Cheng Zhao whole.","Cheng Zhao's mind gradually cleared.","There was something wrong with his state. Her mother-in-law and her own mother were both sitting in the eastern side room. At a time like this, she absolutely could not let him do as he pleased.","Taking advantage of a moment when his grip loosened, she bit down hard on his lip.","Her teeth were sharp, drawing blood instantly, and Cheng Zhao tasted the faint metallic flavor of rust.","Zhou Yuanshen gasped in pain, his grip loosening a fraction, and Cheng Zhao seized the chance to break free.","Her thigh slammed into the corner of the dressing table. The corner was bound in iron, and the heavy impact made Cheng Zhao double over uncontrollably, tears of pain welling up in her eyes.","When she raised her eyes, a tear slipped down her cheek.","Zhou Yuanshen stared at her.","His eyes cleared up a fraction.","\"Prepare some cold water for me,\" he ordered in a deep voice.","Cheng Zhao called out to Nanny Li: \"Nanny, come in.\"","Nanny Li walked in and saw Cheng Zhao with her hair disheveled and her eyes red, feeling a wave of shock in her heart.","\"Have someone bring in cold water,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li complied.","\"After giving the order, come back and comb my hair,\" Cheng Zhao added.","Nanny Li went to carry out the tasks.","The commotion on this side could hardly be hidden from the two mothers sitting in the eastern side room.","Second Madam thought about it for a moment and vaguely understood what was going on: the only one who would dare make such a scene in Cheng Zhao's bedchamber was undoubtedly Zhou Yuanshen.","With his mother-in-law here, it was already highly improper for Zhou Yuanshen not to come and pay his respects; if he were to further...","Using all the wisdom she had accumulated over half her life, Second Madam said to Madam Cheng, \"In-law, there is a beautiful blood coral in Jiangyun Courtyard. Would you care to go and have a look?\"","She regretted it as soon as she said it.","Since when was blood coral considered a rare treasure? The Cheng family had plenty of them.","And among Second Madam's own treasured collection, blood coral did not even rank.","It was mainly because she had mentioned gift-giving with Second Master that morning and happened to bring up blood coral. In her moment of panic, it was the only thing she could think of.","Madam Cheng smiled gently. \"I am most fond of blood coral; its color is festive and auspicious. Please, lead the way.\"","Given a way out, she immediately took it.","Second Madam and Madam Cheng walked out with quick steps, even bumping into a rough-work maidservant carrying water at the door.","\"Absolutely absurd!\" Second Madam was furious inwardly.","How could this put her in-law's mind at ease?","Putting herself in the other's shoes, Second Madam felt she could strangle Zhou Yuanshen herself.","He was usually the most rigid and observant of propriety. How could he act so frivolously today?","What would his mother-in-law think of him?","Second Madam glanced at Madam Cheng's face.","Madam Cheng possessed excellent composure. As if she had noticed nothing, her smile did not falter for a second as she followed Second Madam out.","Second Madam made small talk all the way, feeling extremely guilty.","She also felt her behavior was inappropriate, like a guilty person protesting too much, further blackening Zhou Yuanshen's reputation. But she simply could not pretend nothing had happened.","Fortunately, Madam Cheng did not find fault and merely went along with her words.","Lunch was served in Jiangyun Courtyard, having been temporarily relocated.","Cheng Zhao did not go to keep them company during the meal.","Her lips were slightly swollen, and she was currently having Nanny Li apply a cold compress to them; she had changed her clothes and redone her hair.","Cheng Zhao sat on the large heated brick bed by the window in the eastern side room, feeling deeply depressed.","Zhou Yuanshen was still in the washroom.","Nanny Li served Cheng Zhao tea. \"Would you like to go to Jiangyun Courtyard to eat?\"","They probably had not finished eating yet.","Cheng Zhao shook her head. \"I have no appetite.\"","\"If you don't go, Madam will be worried,\" Nanny Li said.","She added, \"Later, ask Lord Duke what exactly happened. If you explain it to the Madams, they will surely understand.\"","Cheng Zhao lowered her eyes and said nothing.","Nanny Li knew she wanted to throw a temper tantrum right now and needed time to calm her nerves. She was still young after all; sometimes her endurance crumbled, and she could not maintain her composure.","Two hours later, Zhou Yuanshen arrived in the eastern side room.","He had changed into casual wear, a quilted black long robe embroidered with gold thread in an auspicious cloud pattern. The heavy garment made his face appear even paler.","The flush across his body had faded.","His lip was a little swollen. The place Cheng Zhao had bitten was the inside of his lower lip. It had swelled up and hurt terribly, but fortunately, it was not very visible from the outside.","\"...I was out of line just now,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao remained silent.","She was the Duke's wife. Even at the risk of offending him, she could not blindly indulge him and show no temper of her own.","\"Has mother-in-law returned home?\"","\"You still remember that my mother is here?\" Cheng Zhao retorted.","Zhou Yuanshen's dark eyes were serene, and his face held no extra expression. He merely let out a soft sigh. \"The tonic Dowager Madame had someone send over...\"","Cheng Zhao looked at him sharply.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"It likely wasn't Dowager Madame's person. She occasionally sends me some soups and broths.\"","Dowager Madame had a habit of rewarding him with tonics, so he had been off his guard.","After drinking it, he immediately felt a burning heat all over his body.","Zhou Yuanshen had planned to finish his current tasks and then enter the inner courtyard to visit his mother-in-law; he knew she was visiting today.","In the side room of Chenhui Courtyard, the large heated brick bed by the window grew increasingly hot. A drop of sweat rolled down his temple, and Zhou Yuanshen suddenly lowered his head.","When he was sixteen, he also experienced sudden, restless urges, but he rarely felt like this nowadays.","Then someone knocked on the door.","He heard the voice of a young woman.","\"Miss, why are you here again? Lord Duke was very angry last time.\" Zhou Yuanshen heard Nanfeng's voice.","He lifted the window lattice and caught sight of a flash of crimson skirts.","The dress was very beautiful.","Zhou Yuanshen rarely found other people's clothes beautiful.","His composure was completely shattered.","Before Nanfeng could send the person away, Zhou Yuanshen left Chenhui Courtyard like a gust of wind. At the door, he ran head-on into the young woman and caught a whiff of a rich fragrance.","It was so fragrant it made one's mouth water.","In truth, Zhou Yuanshen usually disliked heavy incense. Even though he had spent years at the frontier, the upbringing of the Duke's estate had taught him the ability to appreciate fine things.","Heavy scents were too vulgar.","He originally did not like it.","All his senses were betraying him, so he sprinted frantically to Nonghua Courtyard.","Running too fast made his whole body burn.","When he reached the courtyard gate, his remaining shred of reason told him that his mother-in-law was present.","He feared that his current state would frighten people and leave a bad impression on his mother-in-law.","Zhou Yuanshen had scaled the wall to enter Nonghua Courtyard, climbing directly into the inner bedchamber through the back window.","Now, with the husband and wife sitting alone, Zhou Yuanshen could not excuse himself.","He simply said, \"It is all my fault. I lost my composure.\""]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54: Zhou Yuanshen's Apology","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao did not accept Zhou Yuanshen's apology.","It was her mother's first time visiting the Nonghua Courtyard as a guest, yet Zhou Yuanshen had let such a thing happen. Cheng Zhao could not find any excuses to absolve him.","She stood up, not looking at him. \"I am going to the Jiangyun Courtyard. My Lord Duke, you can have your meal by yourself; there is no need to follow me.\"","She turned and left.","Her senior maid Suyue followed her.","Nanny Li absolutely did not dare to persuade her. If she said one more word, her mistress would probably harshly scold the Duke. She was trying her best to hold back her temper.","Walking out of the Nonghua Courtyard, the cold wind blew against Cheng Zhao, finally calming her down a bit.","She did not go directly to the Jiangyun Courtyard, but instead took a walk along the small path for a while.","Letting the cold wind blow over her, she thought about what had just happened and how to resolve the matter.","As her mind cleared, that surge of emotion also faded away.","\"...Young Madam, what do you plan to do?\" Suyue asked.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"We will talk about it this afternoon.\"","She finally headed to the Jiangyun Courtyard.","Madam Cheng had drunk a couple of extra cups of wine, bringing a flush of color to her cheeks. The Second Madam had a good tolerance for alcohol; she drank even more but remained completely clear-headed.","The two women looked at Cheng Zhao.","The Second Madam did not know what to say, nor could she ask too much.","Madam Cheng spoke up, \"Zhaozhao, come and eat something. It is cold, do not starve yourself.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","\"I went back to my room to change clothes. How come you came to the Jiangyun Courtyard to eat?\" she asked with a smile.","Madam Cheng replied, \"It is cold, and I am too lazy to walk back and forth. I am saving my energy, as I am not like you young folks anymore. You are all like little cats, full of energy to toss about.\"","Cheng Zhao smiled.","The Second Madam smiled along.","After the meal, they sat for a little longer. Cheng Zhao and the Second Madam accompanied Madam Cheng to bid farewell to the Dowager Madame, and then she left the Chen Duke's Mansion.","Cheng Zhao and the Second Madam saw her off at the main gate.","Once the carriage had gone far, the Second Madam asked Cheng Zhao, \"What happened just now?\"","Cheng Zhao linked arms with her, and only after the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law got into the small carriage did she say, \"The Duke is feeling a little unwell.\"","The Second Madam frowned, \"What on earth is wrong with him?\"","Cheng Zhao did not want her mother-in-law to act on impulse and stir the matter up until it was unmanageable, so she said, \"Rest assured, Mother, my mother will not blame the Duke.\"","She added, \"Besides, no one saw the Duke enter the Nonghua Courtyard, so it is fine. Just pretend we do not know.\"","The Second Madam was speechless.","She still felt indignant, blaming Zhou Yuanshen for failing to live up to expectations.","Zhou Yuanshen did not rest in the Nonghua Courtyard that night.","The next day, the imperial court finally resumed morning assemblies, and he was away from home for the entire day.","Cheng Zhao called Nanfeng over to ask.","Nanfeng told Cheng Zhao, \"The old woman who delivered the soup has a round face and is slightly plump. I looked around everywhere but did not run into her. If I ever meet her, I will definitely recognize her.\"","Cheng Zhao said, \"I suspect they will not let you run into her again.\"","First Madam Madam Song had managed the household for many years; she still possessed some cunning methods.","The old woman who delivered the medicine was certainly someone Nanfeng and Zhou Yuanshen did not know. With an unfamiliar face and no distinctive features, she would be hard to remember. If she was secretly sent away afterward, it would be done without anyone noticing.","According to the First Madam's plan, once Zhou Yuanshen drank the tonic, he would definitely take in her niece.","Once the deed was done, her niece could only become Zhou Yuanshen's concubine. With her around, Zhou Yuanshen's relationship with the eldest branch would become closer.","It would also serve as a warning to Huan Qingtang that the First Madam did not rely entirely on her.","Today was also the day his mother-in-law came as a guest. Zhou Yuanshen would absolutely not dare to make a scene and would have to quietly suppress the matter.","Although risky, the First Madam would indeed grasp a vulnerability of Zhou Yuanshen, giving her a leash to control him in the future.","But Zhou Yuanshen was a military general. Even with his last breath on the battlefield, he could hold on and ride his horse back to camp.","Let alone a mere bowl of drugged medicine.","If he did not want to be manipulated, he could have gone to Mu Jiang's Lijing Courtyard. The Lijing Courtyard was closer to the Chenhui Courtyard.","Although Mu Jiang was pregnant, the Lijing Courtyard had two beautiful maids arranged by the Dowager Madame. These two were officially recognized and meant to be given to Zhou Yuanshen as bed-attendants.","The First Madam calculated everything, but she solely misjudged Zhou Yuanshen as a person.","He was not the type of weak, scholarly young master who looked impressive on the outside but was ruined on the inside.","\"The Duke ordered this lowly one to keep investigating,\" Nanfeng said.","Cheng Zhao said, \"If you find out anything, let me know as well.\"","Nanfeng complied.","Cheng Zhao made a trip to the Dowager Madame's courtyard.","She said to the Dowager Madame, \"Grandmother, the tonic you sent someone to deliver to the Duke yesterday, what medicinal ingredients were used in it?\"","The prayer beads in the Dowager Madame's hand paused slightly as she smiled and asked, \"Why do you ask?\"","\"I do not know which ingredient in the tonic was wrong, but the Duke suffered from an upset stomach all night. This granddaughter-in-law thinks that Grandmother has a heart full of care for the Duke, but because the imperial court has been chaotic and he is exhausted from dealing with it, he is a bit overworked and actually cannot handle such strong tonics,\" Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","The Dowager Madame replied, \"I will ask the manager about it later.\"","She added, \"Tell Yuanshen to come to me after the morning assembly. I will see how he is doing.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","In the mid-afternoon of that day, as soon as Zhou Yuanshen returned to the mansion, he was called over by the Dowager Madame.","The Dowager Madame asked him what tonic it was.","Zhou Yuanshen recounted everything to her in detail.","\"The old women in my courtyard are only these few. You can take a look and see who it was,\" the Dowager Madame said.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"Grandmother, there is no need to look. This grandson knows it was not your people.\"","\"In this household, for someone to dare falsely pass on my words, they truly do not take me seriously anymore,\" the Dowager Madame said lightly.","Zhou Yuanshen said, \"This grandson feels the same. Why not call Eldest Aunt over to investigate this matter thoroughly?\"","He added, \"Eldest Aunt's health might be poor, and her energy cannot keep up. Why not hand over the management of the gatehouse to my wife Cheng Shi, letting her share Eldest Aunt's burdens?\"","The Dowager Madame looked at him.","\"Handing it over to Huan Shi would be the same,\" the Dowager Madame said.","Zhou Yuanshen said, \"Grandmother, if I make a fuss, not only will the eldest branch look bad, but you will also get angry. Why bother?\"","Just one sentence, spoken not loudly, yet the Dowager Madame felt a dull ache in her chest.","\"The household is indeed a bit messy,\" the Dowager Madame said. \"Allow me to consider this matter further.\"","Zhou Yuanshen was unusually obedient; this time he was not aggressive and simply left.","He went to the Nonghua Courtyard.","Cheng Zhao curtsied in greeting, helped him take off his fur-collared crane cloak, and instructed the maids to serve tea and water.","\"...Nanfeng has already told me. Everyone knows it in their hearts, but unfortunately, we have not caught any evidence,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"However, I told Grandmother.\"","Zhou Yuanshen said, \"Grandmother called me over to ask about it.\"","\"What did she say?\"","\"She might give you the management of the gatehouse to appease me,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao paused.","She should have been happy. After all, her eldest sister and second sister-in-law had both suggested she obtain the management rights of the gatehouse, so that she could have a clearer view of the social engagements of the Chen Duke's Mansion.","But Cheng Zhao had never thought of exchanging for it in this way.","For Zhou Yuanshen, yesterday's incident was very humiliating.","He could have made a huge fuss.","\"My Lord Duke...\"","\"This is for you.\" Zhou Yuanshen handed Cheng Zhao a small box.","Cheng Zhao took it.","She assumed it was jewelry, but upon opening it, she found a small crossbow.","Cheng Zhao looked at him in astonishment.","\"The mechanism of this small crossbow allows it to fire four short arrows in succession,\" Zhou Yuanshen said. \"It is more sensitive than an ordinary small crossbow, so you must be extremely careful when wearing it.\"","Cheng Zhao looked at him fixedly, unable to speak for a moment.","\"If you do not like it, I will exchange it for ten thousand taels of silver notes for you,\" he added. \"Cheng Zhao, yesterday was my fault, making you lose face.\""]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55: Cheng Zhao Gets Another Benefit","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao was not a capricious person.","Once she felt respected, she could handle things calmly.","\"Thank you, Duke. I really like the small crossbow,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She added, \"Secondary Wife knows how to use hidden weapons, but I don't. The next time she dares to use a hidden weapon against me, I will shoot her with the small crossbow.\"","\"Concubine Mu,\" he said. \"You don't need to call her Secondary Wife.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","With the topic reaching this point, Cheng Zhao formally discussed some matters with Zhou Yuanshen for the first time.","\"Duke, you could have gone to Lijing Courtyard yesterday,\" she said.","Lijing Courtyard was closer and fully justifiable. His concubines and bedmaids were already there.","He certainly knew that his mother-in-law was a guest at Nonghua Courtyard.","If one said he was out of his mind, he still knew enough to climb in through the rear window; if one said he had some reason left, he deliberately abandoned the near for the far.","\"...The matters of Lijing Courtyard have nothing to do with you,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Her anger almost flared up again.","\"I mean, Lijing Courtyard is solely my own affair; it has nothing to do with you as the Duchess. You don't need to worry about it.\" Sensing that his words might be ambiguous, he explained further.","Cheng Zhao caught that hint of guilt in him.","Taking advantage of this slight apology and the topic of Lijing Courtyard, Cheng Zhao planned to bring up something she had been considering for a long time.","\"Alright, I assure you that I will never interfere in the affairs of Lijing Courtyard,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"However, speaking of Lijing Courtyard, there is something I want to tell you as well. It's about Nonghua Courtyard.\"","Zhou Yuanshen looked at her and nodded slightly: \"Speak.\"","\"I have six dowry maids in total, and none of them are prepared to be your bedmaids. Although my place here is not the main courtyard, back in my maiden home, my mother's courtyard did not have any bedmaids either,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She would also become pregnant in the future.","Cheng Zhao did not want Zhou Yuanshen to subconsciously think that, just like at Mu Jiang's side, there would always be someone here to serve him.","Once Cheng Zhao became pregnant, Zhou Yuanshen would not be able to spend the night at Nonghua Courtyard.","Cheng Zhao did not want to leave things ambiguous and let Zhou Yuanshen misunderstand. If one day he insisted on having her maids, tearing face then would be even uglier.","Regardless of whether he was displeased or not, Cheng Zhao wanted to make it clear in advance.","Some rules of the Duke Chen's Estate were different from those of the Cheng family.","The Cheng family's reputation in the capital was better than that of the Duke Chen's Estate, and their rules were more in line with secular conventions. This was why Cheng Zhao dared to tell him so directly.","If he disagreed, it would mean that his Zhou family was vulgar and ignorant of etiquette, which would be despised.","Cheng Zhao secretly applied pressure to resolve this matter first.","Zhou Yuanshen looked at her steadily: \"Cheng Zhao, the mistress's maids are all literate. They were cultivated to be managers in the first place.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Yes.\"","\"Do you think I don't understand that?\"","\"No, I was just afraid there might be a misunderstanding,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She explained further, \"I am not looking down on you.\"","\"It's good for husband and wife to speak clearly when there's an issue. I didn't take offense,\" Zhou Yuanshen said. \"You were afraid I wouldn't behave, and I was also afraid you would force someone on me.\"","Cheng Zhao burst into a laugh.","The cold aura surrounding Zhou Yuanshen melted away with her laugh.","His posture and demeanor visibly relaxed quite a bit.","Cheng Zhao even felt that he was secretly sighing in relief.","Regarding yesterday's incident, the person who had truly lost all face was him. He had embarrassed himself in front of his mother, mother-in-law, and wife.","When many people face embarrassment, they use anger to cover it up, first treating themselves as the victim and recklessly venting their resentment.","But Zhou Yuanshen did not fly into a rage out of humiliation. Not only did he fight for the household management rights for Cheng Zhao, but he also earnestly apologized to her.","He dared to face his own ugly state directly—this was easy to say but very hard to do.","Zhou Yuanshen might not be a good husband, and she might not be able to share mutual affection with him, but he was indeed a good family head.","He had principles.","Even covered in mud, he would still grasp the maximum benefits.","If he remained unchanged, the two of them walking forward hand in hand wouldn't be a bad thing for Cheng Zhao.","Zhou Yuanshen could not only defeat his opponents but also conquer himself. Cheng Zhao needed such a powerful and rational ally.","Therefore, reaching this point, all of Cheng Zhao's dissatisfaction and anger completely vanished.","She even showed concern for Zhou Yuanshen: \"Duke, how are you feeling today? Is that drug still bothering you?\"","Zhou Yuanshen: \"I'm alright.\"","He added, \"I asked the imperial physician for some detoxifying medicine and have already taken a dose.\"","Cheng Zhao told him to take care of his health.","After finishing these matters, Zhou Yuanshen left Nonghua Courtyard and did not stay the night.","Cheng Zhao carefully put the small crossbow away and breathed a sigh of relief.","\"I told you there was no need to rush, just wait for First Aunt to deliver the management rights to me,\" Cheng Zhao said to her trusted aides.","Her aides were all very irritated, feeling that the First Madam was truly unpresentable.","Cheng Zhao, however, had a different view from theirs.","\"You only think her methods are clumsy, but in reality, she looks down on me, and she also looks down on the Duke,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Cheng Zhao did not believe that the First Madam would use such methods to deal with the Old Madam.","She had suppressed the second branch for decades and was used to it. The Second Master and his wife could not get even a bit of respect from her, let alone the younger generation.","She was even too lazy to bother thinking of a more complex and long-term method to win over Zhou Yuanshen.","She wanted to have a close relationship with the Duke, yet she looked down on Zhou Yuanshen, which was why she wanted to put a leash around his neck.","She almost succeeded.","Because she utilized the relationship between the Old Madam and Zhou Yuanshen.","The Old Madam frequently sent tonics to Zhou Yuanshen. Such small favors were most suitable for an elder to do; it required no effort, and Zhou Yuanshen was obliged to accept the sentiment.","The grandmother's affection was bestowed very well, and the relationship between the two was harmonious.","The First Madam, however, severed this relationship.","From now on, the Old Madam could no longer casually send food to Zhou Yuanshen. With what face could she show her concern for her grandson?","This concern had to be out in the open, for Zhou Yuanshen and everyone else to see.","\"First Aunt didn't offend me, but Grandmother is probably furious,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Just as Cheng Zhao guessed, a violent storm occurred in Shou'an Courtyard.","Madam Song knelt before the Old Madam, a large patch of her skirt wet, and her cheek burning with pain.","The Old Madam had first thrown a teacup at her, the tea soaking her long skirt. After scolding her a few times, she actually argued back and talked back, so the Old Madam slapped her.","Madam Song was stunned by the slap.","Having been married into the family for over twenty years, she had never been beaten.","The Old Madam's furious rage was vented through this slap.","\"You really don't know how the word death is written, daring to even use me,\" the Old Madam said. \"If I find a fault, having the Marquis of Changling's estate stripped of its title and confiscated would be as easy as lifting a finger.\"","Madam Song was scared pale, trembling all over.","She began to cry bitterly and defend herself.","\"...I have spoiled you too much over the years, spoiled you so much that you don't know your limits,\" the Old Madam said.","Without committing a major mistake, a mother-in-law generally would not beat or scold her daughter-in-law.","This matter was extremely serious.","The Old Madam ordered Madam Song to claim illness for a month and stop managing affairs.","\"Let Lady Huan manage things in your stead. Let you see whether this Duke's Estate will starve without you,\" the Old Madam said.","She added, \"I never thought of handing the gatehouse tallies over to Cheng Shi. Now I must give them to her. You truly care for Cheng Shi; those who don't know better would think you are Cheng Shi's proper mother-in-law.\"","Madam Song lay on the ground, weeping bitterly.","The Old Madam watched her quietly.","The Old Madam completely refrained from mentioning the matter of driving away the niece from Madam Song's maiden family.","She had other plans in mind."]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56: Kiss Her Bruises","paragraphs":["The news of Eldest Madam Song’s illness spread through the Duke of Chen’s estate in no time.","The Dowager Madame summoned Huan Qingtang and Cheng Shi to the Hall of Chengming to oversee household affairs together.","“...Cheng Shi, you’ve been managing the main kitchen for some time now, and you’ve handled matters steadily—I’m satisfied.","Now that your eldest aunt-in-law has fallen ill from overwork and exhaustion, the capable shoulder more. You must share her burdens.” The Dowager Madame said this in front of all the household stewards and Huan Qingtang.","Huan Qingtang smiled as she watched Cheng Shi.","Cheng Shi stood up: “Thank you, Grandmother. I will not disappoint your expectations.”","The Dowager Madame then said: “The gatekeeping duties will be handed over to you.”","She asked further, “Do you know how to manage the gatekeeping?”","In some noble families, the inner and outer courtyards were managed separately. The inner court was run by the mistress, while the outer court was handled by an idle elder of the household overseeing administrative affairs.","Gatekeeping matters involved not just entry management, receiving guests, and relaying messages, but also handling all incoming and outgoing correspondence, as well as etiquette.","The personnel at the gate had to be sharp, intelligent, and absolutely loyal.","Because the gate essentially held the secrets of the entire mansion.","At the Zhou estate, the inner and outer courtyards were not separated. The Eldest Madam managed everything, though the chief steward shared much of the burden on her behalf.","Originally, the gatekeeping duties would never have fallen to Cheng Shi.","But Zhou Yuanshen had proposed it.","“...I’ve learned a little from my mother. For specific matters, if I’m unsure, I’ll consult the chief steward; for anything more important, I will always ask Grandmother first,” Cheng Shi said.","She showed no signs of timidity.","Eldest Madam Song gave her the opportunity, and through the contest between the Dowager Madame and Zhou Yuanshen, Cheng Shi once again benefited.","And Cheng Shi—she was not only skilled at seizing chances but also clever and sharp, with a bit of insight.","She was practically the spear in Zhou Yuanshen’s hand, striking wherever he pointed.","The Dowager Madame scrutinized her several times.","“Your mother raised you well,” the Dowager Madame said meaningfully. “The traditions of the Wu Commandery noble clans run deep—more impressive than I imagined.”","“Grandmother flatters me. When it comes to deep traditions, none rival our own Duke of Chen’s estate,” Cheng Shi replied.","The Dowager Madame smiled faintly.","The token for the gatekeeping duties was handed over to Cheng Shi.","Cheng Shi managed the gate the same way she had handled the main kitchen: she reviewed the logs and records daily, met with the minor stewards, listened carefully to their reports, but did not disturb the existing personnel.","When minor stewards tried to test her or overstep their bounds, she would point it out.","She avoided changing the overall framework, lest she cause trouble due to inadequate preparation. She didn’t yet have enough trusted subordinates to rely on.","But she remained vigilant, noting every subtle movement and calling attention to it when necessary, so the stewards knew she was aware of everything.","No one dared to deceive her.","In the following days, Huan Qingtang and Cheng Shi managed affairs in the small antechamber beside the Hall of Chengming, while Eldest Madam Song ‘recuperated’ in her main quarters.","Occasionally, sounds came from Eldest Madam Song’s bedchamber.","Sometimes a bowl was smashed, sometimes she cursed the maidservants.","Huan Qingtang paid no attention; Cheng Shi too was skilled at feigning ignorance.","“...She holds things together well,” Huan Qingtang’s senior maid said anxiously. “Cheng Shi has managed both posts competently.”","Huan Qingtang pondered: “It’s not just because she was well-bred by her family. It’s also because of her noble background.”","The stewards all knew that Cheng Shi came from a prestigious family.","A noble lady of a prominent clan had her own capabilities, and Cheng Shi was also aware that they instinctively respected her.","Even when they tried to test her or deceive her, she would quickly call them out, earning their increasing respect.","Respect from others—this gave her authority.","Cheng Shi’s authority wasn’t something she had built herself; it came from her family background.","In terms of pure lineage, the Huan family was second to none. But when it came to heritage and wealth, the Cheng family held the upper hand.","That was one reason why, despite Cheng Shi marrying late and not being particularly favored by the Dowager Madame, the stewards still feared her.","“Mu Jiang thinks she can take her place—she’s dreaming. She was a Secondary Wife; in the eyes of the stewards, she’ll never have that kind of prestige,” Huan Qingtang added.","Whether it was Mu Jiang or Cheng Shi, both were thorny issues.","Huan Qingtang had to stay fully alert to manage them.","Having taken on two responsibilities, and with the Eldest Madam claiming to be ill, Cheng Shi had to go to the Hall of Chengming almost every day.","One day, after finishing her duties, Cheng Shi was about to return to Ronghua Courtyard for the evening meal when she encountered Zhou Yuanshen at the crossroad leading to Chenhui Courtyard.","He was wearing soft armor.","The armor made him look tall and martial, sharpening his features into something more stern and imposing than usual.","Cheng Shi rarely saw him in soft armor, so she glanced at him in surprise.","“Just returned from the Capital Garrison Camp,” he explained.","He hadn’t been home for a few days.","Cheng Shi wasn’t familiar with his daily movements, so she said, “Then you should rest early, my lord.”","“Come play a game of chess,” he said.","Cheng Shi: “It’s almost time for the evening meal.”","“Eat at Chenhui Courtyard, then go back afterward,” he said.","Cheng Shi thought it acceptable and could also take a walk to aid digestion.","Since there was still time before dinner, Zhou Yuanshen changed into his everyday long robe and sat with Cheng Shi in the side chamber to play chess.","He told her, “The decree for establishing the heir apparent has been drafted. It will be announced to the court in a couple of days.”","Cheng Shi’s hand, holding a piece, paused.","“Lord Duke, will you be promoted again?” Cheng Shi asked.","If the Zhou family didn’t gain anything, the Guo family wouldn’t have it all to themselves.","This was the result of bargaining.","“His Majesty has appointed me as the Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Shi: “Congratulations, Lord Duke.”","Zhou Yuanshen placed a piece, expressionless. Neither pleased nor disappointed.","She couldn’t tell what calculations were running through his mind.","But she knew that with the establishment of the heir apparent, Zhou Yuanshen’s power at court and his standing with the Emperor would greatly increase.","It would no longer be so easy for the Dowager Madame to suppress him.","But manipulating power—this path was still not easy.","While Cheng Shi’s mind wandered, Zhou Yuanshen won the game.","“I won,” he said.","“Oh.”","“I want to come to Ronghua Courtyard tonight,” he said, looking at her.","Cheng Shi: “...Alright.”","She agreed, and Zhou Yuanshen stood up and walked over to her.","He lifted her chin and placed a light kiss on her lips.","A gentle, unhurried kiss.","Cheng Shi’s eyelashes fluttered; it felt strange to her, a little uncomfortable, and she wanted to turn her face away.","He noticed and pressed his hand to the back of her neck, deepening the kiss.","Cheng Shi felt herself being pushed back, about to fall, until he finally let go, his breathing growing heavy: “Cheng Shi, let me check that injury you got the other day.”","Cheng Shi tried to dodge.","He pulled her onto the wide kang by the window.","“It doesn’t hurt.”","“Let me see,” he insisted.","Cheng Shi refused.","She had bumped her thigh, leaving a deep bruise that still ached. It had been a hard hit.","But how could she show him that spot?","This wasn’t a place for him to look.","His hand found the sash of her skirt again, just like that day in Ronghua Courtyard.","“Let’s go to Ronghua Courtyard first! I’ll show you there,” Cheng Shi said hurriedly, trying to stop his hand.","“It’s the same here,” he said, kissing her lips again. “Cheng Shi, I want to... take a look.”","His last few words came out with a burning breath.","Cheng Shi turned her head to the side.","He lowered himself and kissed the bruised spot. She couldn’t help trembling slightly.","When she finally put her leg down, her limbs felt weak.","She had no strength to move, held as she was in Zhou Yuanshen’s arms.","At some point, the chessboard beside them had been pushed to the floor, the pieces scattered all over. Cheng Zhao leaned over slightly to look, and her dark hair brushed against Zhou Yuanshen's chest.","He steadied her shoulders.","\"Don't move,\" his voice came from his throat. \"It tickles.\"","If she kept this up, he wouldn't even have time for dinner tonight.","Cheng Zhao immediately lay still, not daring to move an inch."]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57: The Composure Cheng Zhao Desires","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao was held tightly in Zhou Yuanshen's arms.","Usually, when looking at him, he always seemed cold. His eyes were cold, his demeanor was cold, yet his skin was scorchingly hot.","Cheng Zhao felt as if she were holding a warm stove and wanted to pull away.","She leaned forward to reach for her clothes, only to find them tossed to the other end of the large heated bed by the window.","As she moved, her dark hair brushed against Zhou Yuanshen again.","Zhou Yuanshen rolled over and pinned her beneath him.","Cheng Zhao glanced at the sky outside. My Lord Duke, it is getting late. It is time for dinner. Are you hungry?","Broad daylight, in the side room of Chenhui Courtyard...","Thinking of the management authority over the gatehouse and then of having an heir, Cheng Zhao forcefully swallowed all her discomfort.","Indulging his madness once in a while would not make the sky fall.","Just as she finished speaking, Zhou Yuanshen blocked her lips with his own.","Cheng Zhao's eyes widened slightly.","Was he going to do it again?","I am very hungry... Zhou Yuanshen answered her, his voice incredibly hoarse.","Cheng Zhao wanted to say something, but he kissed her again.","Later, she did not know when she fell asleep. In her daze, she could still feel someone wiping her clean and changing her clothes.","When Cheng Zhao completely woke up, it was the Yin hour of the next day.","A small horn lantern flickered in the room, and she heard Zhou Yuanshen's voice: Have the clothes and cosmetics been brought over?","Yes, My Lord Duke, the maid Qiubai answered in a low voice.","Wait until the Young Madam wakes up to help her dress and wash, Zhou Yuanshen said.","He went out.","By the dim light, Cheng Zhao saw the lilac fine cotton bed curtains and realized this was the main room of Chenhui Courtyard.","Yesterday mid-afternoon, when they came in, he had said they would play chess.","They only played one game, yet he had tossed her about twice.","Cheng Zhao might have been a bit tired these past two days, and unable to withstand his fondling, she eventually fell asleep.","She had not even eaten dinner.","Waking up, it was already time for him to attend the morning court.","Cheng Zhao sighed softly.","She closed her eyes again and did not move.","A moment later, she called her maids in.","Qiubai and Suyue came in together.","Have my breakfast sent to Nonghua Courtyard. Do not have it brought here, Cheng Zhao said.","Wherever the meal was set, the main kitchen would know where the person was.","Cheng Zhao did not want others to know she had rested in Chenhui Courtyard last night.","It was normal for Zhou Yuanshen to stay in Nonghua Courtyard; but for Cheng Zhao to stay with him in Chenhui Courtyard was a bit strange.","What Duke's wife would abandon her perfectly good courtyard to sleep in the inner study with her husband?","A study, after all, was a place of elegance and the husband's exclusive domain.","Even if she were just burying her head in the sand, Cheng Zhao had to hide away.","She figured she would eat some pastries to fill her stomach.","Even though she was a bit hungry.","When she was hungry, pastries would not be enough to satisfy her.","She would endure it and eat more at noon.","The Duke's breakfast has already been delivered, Qiubai said. He did not touch it. He said he would eat outside and told us to save it for you.","Nanfeng also brought a small stove in. The breakfast is being kept warm and has not gone cold. If you get up to eat now, it will not need to be reheated.","Cheng Zhao: ...","After washing up, Cheng Zhao ate her breakfast first before doing her hair and makeup.","Cheng Zhao was a bit surprised that Zhou Yuanshen had thought this far ahead.","He probably knew that a woman of Cheng Zhao's background valued rules highly and would be reluctant to spend the night with him in Chenhui Courtyard.","He knew, yet he insisted on doing it anyway...","Cheng Zhao slowly finished her breakfast, rinsed her mouth again, and then sat down, letting her maids comb her hair and apply her powder.","Once they were done, it was still early. Chengming Hall was close by, so Cheng Zhao casually picked up a book, unhurried.","If you lived here, it would indeed be convenient to handle your daily duties, Suyue said.","Everything could be done unhurriedly.","Although hurrying over from Nonghua Courtyard was not considered far, there was still the process of rushing, which made one feel pressed for time.","Cheng Zhao laughed. You have no ambition. Do we handle duties just to live in Chenhui Courtyard? This is merely the inner study.","The best would be to live in Chengming Hall.","That would be true ease.","Because she was full and had time to read, Cheng Zhao cast aside any lingering discomfort from last night and went to Chengming Hall in a fairly good mood.","Only upon arriving did she learn that the Eldest Young Madam, Huan Qingtang, had slept in the eastern main room of Chengming Hall last night.","Because Madam Song had asked her to attend to her illness.","Huan Qingtang had her own courtyard, not far from Chengming Hall. It was the courtyard from her wedding, and she had continued to live there after becoming a widow.","To stay in the main room of Chengming Hall, the principal courtyard, signified a different status and position.","The managers seemed to have all heard about this, and they looked at Huan Qingtang with more prudence.","Upon hearing this, Cheng Zhao's expression remained completely unchanged, and she even showed concern for Huan Qingtang: Sister-in-law, you must be tired from attending to the sick, right?","In front of the managers, Huan Qingtang said with a smiling face, It is fine. Mother favors me greatly; she only asked me to keep her company and did not make me serve tea or fetch water.","On one hand, this was telling the managers that she had moved into Chengming Hall.","Without the approval of the Old Madam and Madam Song, it would have been impossible for her to move in. This was a demarcation of status and position.","On the other hand, it elevated Madam Song, letting people know she was a lenient and kind mother-in-law.","The managers looked at her, and they also looked at Cheng Zhao.","Smiling, Cheng Zhao praised the Eldest Madam a bit and added, I hope Eldest Aunt recovers soon. Without her here to take charge, I feel very panicked.","Mother will be well soon, Sister-in-law, do not worry, Huan Qingtang smiled.","It was a scene of peace and joy.","The managers carefully savored Cheng Zhao's words and could not detect a hint of sarcasm or hidden bitterness.","With Cheng Zhao's background, it was impossible for her not to know what her sister-in-law moving into Chengming Hall meant. Yet she managed to remain completely composed, her words devoid of any emotion, which was truly formidable.","Mid-morning, some managing older women gathered together and chatted about this matter.","The two Young Madams of our estate are actually more shrewd than the two Madams.","When discussing distinguished scholarly families, Cheng Shi and Lady Huan are both at the top. The Old Madam has a good eye.","Cheng Shi's marriage was decreed by the Empress. The Empress is trying to curry favor with the Duke, deliberately choosing a universally excellent Young Madam for him.","The Third Young Madam did not even make a fuss! She holds the imperial mandate of a Duke's wife, comes from a good background, yet she can swallow this grievance. She truly has refinement.","Once she has an heir, her situation in the future will be different. She does not fight over a momentary advantage and leaves behind a good reputation; she is quite capable.","Being so young, they truly live up to being ladies of noble families. Their upbringing is truly remarkable.","Towards Huan Qingtang, the managing women gained some respect; but they did not belittle Cheng Zhao because of it. Instead, everyone felt that Cheng Zhao was steady, shrewd, and not to be underestimated.","Huan Qingtang's maid eventually heard these discussions and was very irritated.","She said to Huan Qingtang, The mouths of these managing women are the most venomous. Cheng Shi lost the upper hand, yet they still praise her!","Huan Qingtang smiled bitterly. This, I really did not expect.","Do you need me to send someone to speak up for you? We cannot just let Cheng Shi gain such a reputation.","Huan Qingtang pondered and shook her head: The more we do, the more mistakes we might make. Let us wait. We have won a step; for now, let us not get distracted."]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58: Promotion","paragraphs":["The news about Chengming Hall spread quickly.","The servant boy Nanfeng reported the matter to Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen remained expressionless, as if he had not heard a thing.","Over in Nonghua Courtyard, Nanny Li and the others were also discussing it.","The one most indignant was Suyue.","Suyue had a fiery temper and a straightforward manner. Moreover, she was extremely biased toward Cheng Zhao and could not stand seeing her suffer even the slightest grievance.","\"...The Old Madame is determined to elevate Lady Huan. Once the decree for dual-lineage inheritance is issued, they might even request the title of Duchess for her,\" Suyue said.","She added, \"In other households, having a noble concubine is frustrating enough, but the Duke Chen's Mansion has another official wife! If it were not for Her Majesty the Empress bestowing this marriage, why would our lady have to swallow such an insult?\"","Nanny Li agreed, \"It is indeed quite stifling.\"","Cheng Zhao, however, smiled calmly. \"Do not be anxious. The Old Madame will soon ask her to move out. She is only there to tend to the sick.\"","\"I am just afraid that tending to the sick is an excuse to let her stay there permanently. The First Madame has also compromised, wanting to ease relations with Shou'an Courtyard,\" Suyue said.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"It does not depend on them, but on the Duke.\"","The others looked at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao said, \"Do not panic. Let us just wait and see.\"","That day, when Zhou Yuanshen came to Nonghua Courtyard for dinner, Cheng Zhao felt a bit nervous.","He had tossed her about twice last night, leaving her quite uncomfortable; she would not be able to handle him acting up again tonight.","Besides, if she wanted to get pregnant, she could not afford to be too exhausted.","Facing Zhou Yuanshen, Cheng Zhao maintained her composure, quietly waiting for his next move without speaking up preemptively.","After the meal, Cheng Zhao brought up the matter of Chengming Hall.","She probed, \"Sister-in-law has moved into the eastern main room.\"","Zhou Yuanshen remained expressionless and said indifferently, \"Did they not say she is tending to the sick? That is her filial piety.\"","When dealing with Mu Jiang, he always referred to her as Concubine Mu; but toward Huan Qingtang, his tone was much more polite.","Perhaps it was because of their different backgrounds, or perhaps his feelings for them differed.","Cheng Zhao thought to herself that with the establishment of the Crown Prince approaching, Zhou Yuanshen would soon become the Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince. Seeing this connection, the Old Madame would definitely rebalance the statuses of Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang.","Of course, before rebalancing, the Old Madame would still test Zhou Yuanshen's attitude.","Cheng Zhao had also tested the waters, but could not make out his intentions.","She could not be bothered to ask any further.","After dinner, the husband and wife each went about their own business.","Zhou Yuanshen took a book to read in bed, while Cheng Zhao continued with her needlework.","This time, she was embroidering a handkerchief.","Zhou Yuanshen walked over to the table to pour himself some water.","Feeling a bit thirsty, he did not call for a maid. Instead, he poured himself a cup of tea, sipped it slowly, and naturally strolled over to Cheng Zhao's side.","Cheng Zhao continued her needlework.","\"...That butterfly is embroidered a bit fat,\" he could not help but say.","Cheng Zhao's embroidery skills were quite excellent. She had embroidered a butterfly—chubby and endearingly clumsy, yet vividly lifelike and exquisite.","This showed her masterful craftsmanship, though it was a wonder why she chose to embroider such a butterfly.","\"I embroidered it like this on purpose, to give to Heng'er,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"Children like cute and amusing things, and I promised her last time.\"","She then explained, \"Heng'er is my niece, my eldest sister's daughter.\"","\"She should like it very much,\" Zhou Yuanshen said. \"What other needlework do you usually do?\"","\"Just small things,\" Cheng Zhao replied.","\"Last time I saw you making a sachet.\"","Mentioning the sachet reminded Cheng Zhao of the time he had pressed her down on this very window-side heated brick bed, scraping her knees. Her face darkened slightly.","She did not reply.","\"...Let us rest, it is getting late.\" Without waiting for her to speak, Zhou Yuanshen set down his teacup.","Cheng Zhao was almost done tying off the thread, so she murmured an agreement and only went to bed after finishing her stitching.","He lay there quietly.","Seeing that he had no other intentions, Cheng Zhao quietly breathed a sigh of relief.","When she woke up early the next day and tidied up her sewing basket, Cheng Zhao could not find the handkerchief. She asked Nanny Li in surprise, \"Did you see it?\"","\"The Duke took it when he left,\" Nanny Li said. \"Did you not know?\"","Cheng Zhao was speechless. \"...What did he take it for? I embroidered that for Heng'er.\"","Nanny Li chuckled. \"Perhaps he likes it. You should embroider something for him. After all, he gave you a short crossbow last time.\"","\"That was his way of apologizing,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"Make him a sachet, embroider something a bit more grand so he can hang it on his belt. Courtesy demands reciprocity; consider it a thank you for his short crossbow?\" Nanny Li suggested softly, observing Cheng Zhao's expression.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"Wait until he returns my handkerchief first.\"","She felt a bit annoyed. \"I told him it was embroidered for Heng'er. Why is he snatching a child's thing? It is not like he is three years old.\"","Taking her eyes off it for just a second, she had tragically lost a handkerchief.","Cheng Zhao decided that she would ask for it back when he returned to the estate in the afternoon.","That butterfly was extremely cute; she had spent seven or eight days embroidering it. It was vibrant and chubby, full of childlike charm. Heng'er would definitely love it.","Cheng Zhao had only come up with the idea by a stroke of sudden inspiration.","With these thoughts in mind, she finished breakfast and went to Chengming Hall to handle her duties.","The day passed peacefully.","By mid-afternoon, Sun Fenghui, the head steward of the Duke Chen's Mansion, came to Chengming Hall to report. He specifically smiled at Cheng Zhao and said, \"Congratulations, Third Young Madame. Today the imperial court established the Crown Prince, and the Seventh Prince has moved into the Eastern Palace. The Duke has been appointed as the Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince.\"","The political decree from the morning had not even been announced to the world yet, but the Duke's Mansion already knew about it by the afternoon.","Everyone was both surprised and delighted.","The wealth and status of the Duke Chen's Mansion had gained another layer of security.","When the next reign arrived, they would still be close ministers to the Emperor, their prestige growing heavier by the day.","Huan Qingtang smiled, \"Congratulations to the Duke, and congratulations to you too, sister-in-law.\"","Cheng Zhao smiled back. \"I heard the Duke mention this matter before. It is indeed worthy of celebration.\"","Huan Qingtang's smile faded slightly, though she remained beaming.","All the compliments from the crowd were directed at Cheng Zhao.","No matter what the outside world said or how the Old Madame arranged things, Zhou Yuanshen's only official wife right now was Cheng Zhao, and Cheng Zhao also held an imperial mandate.","This grand occasion for Duke Chen was solely related to Cheng Zhao.","\"The winds are changing.\"","\"The Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince must be a highly respected veteran official. Yet the Emperor appointed the Duke to the position; this shows extreme trust in him.\"","\"Even the Old Madame will have to weigh things carefully now, right?\"","The stewards did not have much political insight, but they clearly understood the weight of the title of Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince.","This was an undeniable position of honor, a massive bestowal of wealth and status by the Emperor: it guaranteed their standing not only in this reign, but in the next one as well.","The Old Madame probably never expected that the Emperor would bypass her and reward Zhou Yuanshen so heavily.","In the evening, when Zhou Yuanshen returned to the estate, he was invited directly to Shou'an Courtyard by the porters—Cheng Zhao was informed of this.","Zhou Yuanshen's servant boy, Nanfeng, came to Nonghua Courtyard to tell Cheng Zhao to wait for him for dinner.","Cheng Zhao naturally waited.","A moment later, he arrived.","\"What did Grandmother say?\"","\"Establishing the Crown Prince is a major event, and the political landscape will become turbulent as a result. Grandmother asked about a few things,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","\"With the Seventh Prince named Crown Prince, the Guo family's status in this dynasty will now surpass that of the Duke Chen's Mansion,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The most prominent household in the current dynasty was, of course, the Zhou family of the Duke Chen's Mansion.","When it came to rewards from the Emperor and Empress, the Zhou family always received the first and best share; no one surpassed them.","But the Guo family already had prestige, and as the maternal family of the Crown Prince and the Empress, their influence would surge immensely from now on.","The Old Madame was probably panicking a little.","\"...Grandmother also asked me if there were any official transfers. I said no, just the addition of the Grand Tutor title,\" Zhou Yuanshen added.","He was now holding multiple posts simultaneously.","Cheng Zhao asked, \"Besides that? Did she say anything else?\"","If she wants to pursue the dual-lineage inheritance now, would she not have to ask for your opinion first?","Did she probe you about it?"]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59: The Sister-in-Law Moves Away Again","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao was quite interested in the matter of the dual inheritance.","After all, Huan Qingtang had already moved into Chengming Hall.","From the implications of this event, Cheng Zhao could tell that the Old Madam was likely planning to arrange the dual inheritance soon.","This was directly tied to Cheng Zhao's own interests.","\"...Nothing else was said.\" Zhou Yuanshen raised his eyes, his dark, quiet gaze falling upon her face. \"And there is absolutely nothing else, Cheng Zhao.\"","Cheng Zhao lowered her eyelashes.","She murmured an acknowledgment and asked no more.","The couple had their dinner.","While playing chess after dinner, Cheng Zhao brought up her handkerchief.","\"...How could you just take it? That was for Heng'er,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"It looks very cute.\"","\"You are the Duke of Chen, and now the Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince. It is inappropriate for you to carry such a handkerchief. If anyone were to see it, it would be utterly absurd,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She waited for Zhou Yuanshen to return it.","She knew that as long as she asked, Zhou Yuanshen would definitely give it back to her.","However, to her complete surprise, he said in a very mild tone, \"I want it, Cheng Zhao. You can embroider a new one for your niece.\"","He added, \"Your eldest brother-in-law needs a position in the Ministry of War, doesn't he? I will help with that. Consider it my gift to our niece.\"","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","It was true that the new year had just passed, and her eldest brother-in-law's position was still unsettled.","Trading a single handkerchief for such a great favor was certainly worth it.","Still, Cheng Zhao found it bizarre.","He possessed the noble elegance of an aristocratic scion, and when donning soft armor, the imposing majesty of a military general. Tucking away a handkerchief embroidered with a chubby butterfly was truly unfitting.","It was too weird. It didn't suit him at all.","\"Let me embroider another handkerchief for you, with a color and pattern that suits you better. I'll also make you a sachet,\" Cheng Zhao offered. \"As for my eldest brother-in-law's post, I will have to trouble Your Grace for your assistance.\"","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"Just the sachet will do. I already have a handkerchief.\"","He insisted on having that specific handkerchief.","Cheng Zhao was speechless again.","Seeing that he genuinely wanted it, she had no choice but to relent and agree to let him keep it.","However, the sachet would have to wait. She needed to embroider a new piece for her niece first; it was a promise made to the child, and she had to bring it back on her next visit.","Cheng Zhao stopped playing chess. She fetched her sewing basket and began cutting fabric.","This time, Zhou Yuanshen did not go to bed to read. He sat on the heated kang bed by the window, facing Cheng Zhao across the small table.","She busied herself with needlework while he read.","Occasionally, he would lift his gaze to glance at her before returning to his book.","After working for a while, Cheng Zhao's eyes felt a bit sore.","When she rubbed her eyes for the third time, Zhou Yuanshen put down his book. \"Rest now. It is getting late.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","Inside the bed curtains, he pulled her into his embrace.","Thinking about how late it was, and how much time he usually spent on such matters, Cheng Zhao reached out and pressed her hands against his chest. \"I want to sleep.\"","\"Mhm,\" he murmured in response.","He gently kissed her lips.","The kiss gradually deepened, plundering her senses like a conquering army. His hand had already slipped under the hem of her inner garments, softly caressing her skin.","As his breathing grew heavier, the strength of his hands increased as well.","With a slight force and his palms burning hot, Cheng Zhao trembled softly. She wanted to pull away.","Zhou Yuanshen whispered to her, \"You are very delicate, Cheng Zhao.\"","Cheng Zhao retorted, \"You are being rough, yet you blame me for being delicate?\"","The accusation carried no weight whatsoever, as her voice was trembling slightly.","It sounded less like a reproach and more like an endearing pout.","Frustrated, Cheng Zhao shut her mouth, but her reaction successfully amused him.","That night, Cheng Zhao did not get to sleep until midnight, her body feeling so soft it could melt.","Perhaps it was the excitement of his promotion to Grand Tutor, or perhaps Cheng Zhao's responses had pleasantly surprised him, but he completely let loose that night.","The gentle facade of an aristocratic gentleman was entirely gone, and his usual coldness was completely burned to ashes. He was like a fierce beast just awakening, ravenously devouring his prey with a hunger that had slumbered through the winter.","Much like the bed, Cheng Zhao felt as though she had almost been dismantled.","As she drifted into a hazy sleep, Cheng Zhao suddenly remembered Zhou Yuanqi's evaluation of him and mumbled softly, \"Brute.\"","He seemed to have heard it. He cast a glance at her, but Cheng Zhao had already rolled over and fallen asleep.","He wrapped his arms around her from behind.","Lacking the strength to push him away, Cheng Zhao let him hold her.","The next day, Cheng Zhao woke up late.","She hurriedly ate her breakfast. While sitting before the mirror to dress up, she noticed her lips were a bit swollen.","She had no time to worry about it and rushed to Chengming Hall to attend to her duties, barely making it on time.","The morning's tasks concluded quickly.","At noon, Huan Qingtang went to Shou'an Courtyard for lunch, seemingly to help the Old Madam sort Buddha beans.","By mid-afternoon, as the duties wrapped up and the managers were about to disperse, Huan Qingtang smiled and said, \"Mother's health is recovering. After a few more days of rest, the household management will be handed back to her.\"","The managers all voiced their acknowledgment.","Cheng Zhao listened quietly.","Huan Qingtang continued, \"Since Mother is fine and no longer needs my care, I will move back to Cuiyun Courtyard tomorrow.\"","The managers exchanged various glances, looking at Huan Qingtang and then at Cheng Zhao.","However, the two young madams maintained completely normal expressions, revealing not a single hint of their true thoughts.","Still, the news spread, creating a far greater stir than when Huan Qingtang had originally moved into Chengming Hall under the pretext of nursing the sick.","That day, Zhou Yuanshen did not visit Nonghua Courtyard.","The imperial edict establishing the Crown Prince was proclaimed to the world today, and Zhou Yuanshen's appointment as Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince sent shockwaves through the court and the public. Aside from him, the Grand Preceptor and the Grand Protector to the Crown Prince were all veteran officials around fifty years old.","\"If they absolutely must use him, they could have made him the Junior Protector to the Crown Prince.\"","That would have been a much more suitable position.","Not only would it fit his age, but the duties would align properly as well.","Yet, against all odds, he was made the Grand Tutor.","Zhou Yuanshen had previously handled a few matters for the Emperor, which had already provoked dissatisfaction among the court officials. In the streets and alleys, malicious rumors about him were also circulating.","It was as if he had been grouped together with those unforgivably wicked and treacherous ministers.","With the addition of this Grand Tutor title, his reputation worsened yet another degree.","Whispers of these rumors eventually drifted into the inner quarters of the Duke of Chen's estate, though the servants and managers dared not speak of them in front of their masters.","On this day, Huan Qingtang moved out of Chengming Hall.","The next day, a subtle shift occurred in the attitudes of the managers.","Both Huan Qingtang and Cheng Zhao sensed it.","After the daily duties were completed, the Second Madam sent someone to invite Cheng Zhao to Jiangyun Courtyard for a meal.","\"...Quick, tell me what happened!\" the Second Madam blurted out all at once.","Cheng Zhao asked, \"Mother, which matter are you referring to?\"","\"Lady Huan, of course,\" the Second Madam said.","The Second Master had already informed her about the affairs of the royal court.","She was a bit worried for her son.","Zhou Yuanshen's reputation had grown quite unpleasant due to his ruthless killings and his unconventional promotion. However, the Second Madam could not afford to dwell on that; she had no control over matters outside the estate.","She was far more concerned with the affairs of the inner courtyard.","\"Eldest Sister-in-law moved into the main chambers of Chengming Hall earlier, claiming she was there to nurse the sick. Eldest Aunt wasn't even ill, so naturally, it was just an excuse.","I suspect the imperial edict for the dual inheritance was about to be issued, and Grandmother was building up momentum for her in advance, intending for her to share Chengming Hall equally with Eldest Aunt.","However, the Duke has just been promoted. Perhaps during this critical juncture, it is inappropriate to stir up further rumors and add to the burden on His Grace's reputation.","Grandmother is thoughtful and prudent. The dual inheritance matter will likely be postponed, which is why Eldest Sister-in-law moved back out of Chengming Hall,\" Cheng Zhao explained.","The Second Madam was momentarily stunned.","\"They... they actually...\"","Cheng Zhao held her hand and smiled. \"Mother, this is a good thing! Moving in and then moving back out—there's no way to pretend nothing happened. The managers and servants are all watching.\"","Moving into Chengming Hall might not have necessarily boosted Huan Qingtang's prestige, but moving out has utterly swept away her dignity."]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60: Have Found a Suitable Man for Cheng Zhao","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao talked a lot with Second Madam.","She said to Second Madam, \"Mother, my grandfather and my mother used to say that one should never rush into anything. Without absolute certainty, rushing only leads to mistakes. I didn't listen to this advice before, but thinking about it now, they were very right.\"","Dowager Madame was anxious. Having heard that Cheng Zhao was performing very well in Chengming Hall and had earned the respect of the managers, she feared Huan Qingtang wouldn't be able to suppress her, so she told Huan Qingtang to move into Chengming Hall ahead of schedule.","Huan Qingtang was also anxious. Wanting to secure her status as the main wife of Chengming Hall and backed by Dowager Madame, she agreed and moved in.","But unexpectedly, after the imperial court established the crown prince, Zhou Yuanshen was promoted.","Dowager Madame certainly knew about the establishment of the crown prince, but she hadn't caught wind of Zhou Yuanshen's promotion.","The importance of the Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince position was obvious to all, and it was also a layer of guarantee for the Zhou family's long-lasting wealth and status.","Dowager Madame could not possibly oppose it.","Had she known in advance, she would never have arranged for Huan Qingtang to move into Chengming Hall.","She was caught completely off guard.","Because of this impatience, Huan Qingtang moving in and then moving back out caused her reputation to suffer greatly.","The loss outweighed the gain.","\"...How were they just anxious? They clearly had crooked intentions and malicious motives. You silly child, you are just as silly as I used to be, still trying to make excuses for them,\" Second Madam said.","After Cheng Zhao married into the family, Second Madam never blamed herself again.","The doubts that had troubled her for over twenty years were all answered.","She had simply been plotted against, targeted, and ostracized by her mother-in-law and sisters-in-law all along.","When evaluating Dowager Madame, her words were sharp; she disregarded filial piety and couldn't be bothered to be tactful or subtle.","When she directly called Dowager Madame malicious, Cheng Zhao stepped forward and covered her mouth.","Second Madam was speechless.","\"Mother, beware of eavesdroppers. Unfilial conduct is a grave offense; do not leave anyone with something to use against you,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam said, \"You are right.\"","She then smiled and added, \"You won without fighting this time, entirely because you managed to stay composed. You deserved this.\"","If Cheng Zhao had made a fuss when Huan Qingtang moved into Chengming Hall, the outcome might not be what it is now.","Now, as the managers secretly mocked Huan Qingtang, they would also naturally sigh in admiration at Cheng Zhao's prudence.","Some even said, \"The Third Young Madam is a master strategist and shares a deep affection with Lord Duke. She must have known about Lord Duke's promotion long ago and just held her ground.\"","With Cheng Zhao's shrewdness and Lord Duke as her backing, the managers would all look up to her.","No matter how formidable Dowager Madame was, she was nearing the end of her days. In the future, the entire ducal estate would belong to Zhou Yuanshen. Cheng Zhao and Lord Duke had a deep relationship; the bond of a young married couple carried significant weight, not to mention she was so wise.","As for who would be the true mistress of the ducal estate in the future, the managers would have to place their bets anew.","Cheng Zhao won this round beautifully.","She did nothing, yet achieved a total victory. Even Second Madam cheered for her.","\"Perhaps in a year or half, you will move into Chengming Hall,\" Second Madam smiled.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"Mother, it is you who will move into Chengming Hall. When the time comes, I will be like First Sister-in-law, going to your side every day to run errands.\"","Second Madam couldn't help but chuckle, \"That troublesome?\"","\"It's not troublesome; you deserve it,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madam was not skilled at managing a household and had no desire to live in Chengming Hall at all; she just couldn't swallow her anger.","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law talked for a long while before Second Master returned from court and Zhou Yuanqi came home from school.","In recent days, the liveliest topic of conversation was all about Zhou Yuanshen.","\"...Mother, let's quickly kick Third Brother out. He's going to go down in history in infamy and drag our ancestral graves down with him.\" Zhou Yuanqi's finely sculpted, jade-like face looked entirely serious.","Cheng Zhao chuckled.","Zhou Yuanqi also looked at her earnestly, \"Third Sister-in-law, don't panic. I have arrangements for your matters too.\"","He had already scouted several handsome men and was testing them on Cheng Zhao's behalf, planning to observe the situation for a year or two.","Second Madam tapped Zhou Yuanqi on the forehead. \"All day long, you're full of nonsense. I'll have you adopted out first!\"","\"It's not like I'm doing evil. Last time, Third Brother killed Grand Tutor Wu. That was the Emperor's grand tutor; how is it any different from killing someone's father? Now he has become the new Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince. People outside are calling him a treacherous official,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Generally, treacherous officials who incur public wrath are cursed for hundreds or thousands of years. Zhou Yuanshen was very daring in his killings; he wasn't far from inciting public anger.","Cheng Zhao smiled and asked Zhou Yuanqi, \"Which treacherous officials do you know of?\"","Zhou Yuanqi named two. One was Zeng Bo, and the other was Huang Zhilin.","Cheng Zhao asked, \"Do you know when they died and why they died?\"","Zhou Yuanqi choked on his words, then argued a moment later, \"I don't like them, so I couldn't be bothered to learn about them. I have many books to read, I don't have the time.\"","\"I know them all, let me tell you.\"","Cheng Zhao explained to him in detail: Zeng Bo lived a thousand years ago. He died of consumption before he was forty, yet his family continued to thrive for another hundred years before falling.","It wasn't until the entire era collapsed that Zeng Bo was dragged out to be cursed, blamed as the cause for the ruin of the entire court.","As for Huang Zhilin, his reputation was indeed poor, but he served as an official under two dynasties and lived to his eighties, dying a natural death. It was later his grand-daughter-in-law's husband who, for the sake of his own career prospects, dug up thousands of crimes against him and had his corpse exhumed and flogged.","\"You see, those you think are treacherous officials, one was forced to take the blame for the entire court a century later, and the other was a sacrificial lamb and a stepping stone in political struggles. To call a person treacherous, you must look at what they did, who instructed them, and who benefited. In the imperial court, the winner is king and the loser is the villain. However, the families of these two men lived very stable and wealthy lives,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi said, \"You are just making sophistries.\"","\"People are not black or white. Even the most upright court official has his faults,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi replied, \"You are speaking up for a brute. No matter how you argue, that brute's reputation is indeed poor right now.\"","\"Once he gains real power, he will repair his reputation,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi asked, \"Reputation can be repaired?\"","\"Reputation is like a city wall; it requires money, effort, and power to repair. It doesn't grow naturally from the ground. Generally speaking, a person who desires nothing will not have a bad name, but neither will they have a good one; they will simply remain obscure,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi told her, \"These are all just fallacies.\"","Second Madam also felt that Cheng Zhao was making excuses for Zhou Yuanshen, but seeing Zhou Yuanqi at a loss for words made her quite happy.","\"Listen to your sister-in-law,\" Second Madam said. \"If you dare say you'll have your third brother adopted out again, I'll throw you out.\"","\"You're biased!\"","\"He is the Duke of Chen, of course I am biased. When you earn an official rank, I will be biased towards you too,\" Second Madam said.","Zhou Yuanqi puffed his cheeks in anger.","Second Master listened from the side.","After a long while, he finally said, \"Zhaozhao is indeed very knowledgeable. These words have also given me something to reflect upon.\"","Cheng Zhao cast him a surprised glance.","Her own parents and grandfather all called her Zhaozhao, and she didn't mind the nickname. It was just a bit surprising that her father-in-law would address her like this.","It gave her the illusion that he was treating her like his own daughter.","\"Zhaozhao is absolutely right,\" Second Madam smiled.","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","She had gone from being Cheng Shi to her parents-in-law's Zhaozhao.","Zhou Yuanqi was suppressed and stopped throwing a tantrum, and the family happily ate their meal together."]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61: Master of the Manor Is Not Easy to Use","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao had dinner at Jiangyun Courtyard and sat down to chat for a long time.","Zhou Yuanshen also came.","The Second Master and his wife were both a bit surprised.","Zhou Yuanqi disdained to pay attention to him.","\"...Have you gone to the Eastern Palace to handle official duties?\" Second Master asked him.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"Just like at the Capital Garrison, it's just clocking in.\"","Second Master: \"You now hold three official posts.\"","Cheng Zhao didn't expect that his post at the Capital Garrison was also a sinecure.","When the marriage was bestowed, the family all said he was serving at the Capital Garrison.","He was also frequently away from home a while ago.","Recently, he had spent more days at home.","\"I'm merely acting as the Emperor's eyes,\" Zhou Yuanshen said lightly.","His pupils were pitch black, and in the dim candlelight of the night, his gaze was tinged with the coldness of a deep pool. Even when sitting quietly and chatting, he carried an innate aloofness.","Zhou Yuanqi rolled his eyes: \"Not just his eyes, but also the Emperor's knife.\"","His voice hadn't broken yet, and Cheng Zhao always felt he spoke with a \"milky\" voice. Saying such sharp things in a child's voice was particularly amusing.","Zhou Yuanqi was very sensitive about being \"laughed at,\" so Cheng Zhao had to hold it in.","\"Only the sharp and precious are qualified to be the Emperor's knife. A famous blade. The Emperor would look down on ordinary scrap iron,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi also rolled his eyes at her.","Cheng Zhao smiled at him, indicating that the two of them were on the same side.","Zhou Yuanqi seemed to secretly curse her as a \"traitor\" and turned his head to the other side.","Second Madam was a bit worried: \"Ah Shen, you need to take it easy and consider yourself. Killing Grand Tutor Wu last time was truly going too far.\"","She then cursed the Emperor, \"He can't even tolerate a Grand Tutor, so narrow-minded!\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...Mother, these words are treasonous and will get our heads chopped off.\"","Second Madam: \"Then I'll say it at the execution ground too.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","\"I know what I'm doing, Mother doesn't need to worry,\" Zhou Yuanshen spoke up.","His tone had no fluctuations, his dark eyes were silent and still, and no one knew what he was really thinking. He always remained impassive, neither joyful nor angry.","Good things, bad things, flowed past him without leaving a trace. He didn't change for anything, remaining steadfast.","Perhaps, his attitude towards women was the same.","Whether towards Cheng Zhao, Mu Jiang, the two beautiful bedmaids, or Huan Qingtang, Zhou Yuanshen equally didn't take anyone to heart.","He would just do what he should do at the appropriate time.","The Emperor wanted him and Mu Jiang to have a child, so Mu Jiang got pregnant; the Duchess needed an heir, so he worked very hard on Cheng Zhao.","In the future, when he took Huan Qingtang as a co-wife, he would probably treat her the same way.","Thinking of this, Cheng Zhao felt there was nothing bad about him.","Zhou Yuanshen was a very rational person, albeit very ruthless. But his eyes could see the value of others, he would handle matters more fairly, making him more suitable to be the head of the family.","For a large family to prosper for a long time, the head of the family needs to abandon personal likes and dislikes, putting the family's interests first in everything.","Cheng Zhao didn't expect him to favor her, only that he wouldn't favor anyone else.","As long as he wasn't biased, Cheng Zhao was confident she could win.","\"...You are now also a Grand Tutor. Don't you find it ironic? You killed the Emperor's Grand Tutor, yet the Emperor made you the Crown Prince's Grand Tutor. Isn't he just waiting to deal with you in the future?\" Second Madam said.","Her words pulled Cheng Zhao's thoughts back.","Cheng Zhao was probably a bit distracted, causing her thoughts to be less profound.","She casually said, \"Since you've become a knife, be the sharpest knife. Everyone else is just meat on the chopping block. Dealing with the knife in the future? That also requires skill and opportunity.\"","Everyone looked at her.","Including Zhou Yuanshen.","Cheng Zhao instinctively bit her lower lip, wanting to cover up her slip.","Zhou Yuanqi sneered: \"What a big tone, what big ambition! What, do you want to be a rebellious subject and traitor along with the brute?\"","Zhou Yuanshen: \"So that's how it is.\"","\"What 'so that's how it is'?\" Second Madam asked.","Zhou Yuanshen didn't answer.","His words were out of nowhere, only Cheng Zhao understood.","Cheng Zhao had called him a \"brute\" in the bedroom, and he definitely heard it.","He probably wondered in his heart why Cheng Zhao would evaluate him like that.","He found the source of this word today, which was why he said \"so that's how it is.\"","Because Zhou Yuanqi and Second Madam were always bantering, the topic couldn't stay on one track, and it soon went off course.","Unknowingly, the night grew late.","It had been a long time since the family chatted for so long, even though the chat was a mess.","However, this was life. No family's casual chat stuck to just one topic; it was usually all over the place.","\"It's getting late, and we all have things to do tomorrow. You should all head back,\" Second Master said.","Zhou Yuanshen and his wife, along with Zhou Yuanqi, stood up to take their leave.","They parted at the fork in the road.","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen walked back slowly, stepping on the thin moonlight of the crescent moon.","\"...Weren't you originally commanding the Capital Garrison?\" Cheng Zhao asked him. \"When the marriage was bestowed, you seemed to still be in the Capital Garrison.\"","\"Now I serve as the Grand General of the Left Martial Guard. When the Zhou family handed over military power, I served in the Capital Garrison, which was nothing more than to pacify the border troops.","The Left Martial Guard is my actual duty; there is someone else for the Capital Garrison, and I just hold an empty title,\" Zhou Yuanshen said lightly.","Cheng Zhao: \"You hold quite a few empty titles.\"","\"The head of the Zhou family can also take a lot of the blame,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Emperor still needed the Zhou family.","Just like in his early years when his position was unstable and he needed the Zhou family's support, now he also wanted to make the most of the Zhou family.","Hearing this, Cheng Zhao paused slightly: \"You are also surrounded by danger in the court.\"","\"Danger is also opportunity,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","\"Then you must be careful everywhere,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"Even if you become a widow, you will still be a top-rank titled lady. What are you afraid of?\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao: \"...There is no heir yet.\"","Under the faint moonlight, Zhou Yuanshen's face showed no emotion.","He turned to look at Cheng Zhao, \"Is the Child-giving Guanyin not effective?\"","Cheng Zhao really wanted to say, it's you who isn't useful!","But then she thought of the pregnant Mu Jiang in Lijing Courtyard...","He was just not useful with Cheng Zhao; Mu Jiang had already borne fruit.","Wait!","Cheng Zhao raised her eyes to look at him: \"Did Nanfeng eavesdrop on my chat with Qiubai?\"","Zhou Yuanshen walked forward without answering this.","Cheng Zhao decided not to bring delicious pastries for Nanfeng in the future; that kid actually eavesdropped. She also needed to speak more quietly in Chenhui Courtyard.","No wonder Zhou Yuanshen was a bit clingy these past few days; it turned out he was competing with the Child-giving Guanyin.","At night, Zhou Yuanshen wanted to toss about again.","Cheng Zhao's scalp went numb.","How did he have endless brute strength?","\"No, the doctor said it's very hard to conceive if you're too tired,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"I'm really tired. I need to rest for a few days.\"","\"Alright,\" Zhou Yuanshen agreed.","Thinking about an heir, Cheng Zhao felt his mood was okay tonight and tried to discuss with him: \"From now on, can we do it twice a month?\"","Zhou Yuanshen seemed to find it dull, his tone very light: \"Whatever you want.\"","He was also preparing to lie down.","Hearing Cheng Zhao's words, he got up to change clothes: \"I still have some things to do. You rest, don't wait for me.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","She pulled Zhou Yuanshen's hand and whispered, \"I'm discussing it with you, aren't I? If you don't agree, we can talk about it.\"","\"I didn't disagree,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","He looked down at her hand.","Her slender, pale fingers were neatly trimmed at the ends, the light pink nails seeming to have a pearlescent sheen, healthy and full.","It tightly grasped his sleeve.","Cheng Zhao gripped tighter: \"If you say that you will make the decisions for everything from now on without discussion, I will just let you order me around and say no more.\"","\"I didn't mean it like that. I just suddenly remembered something.\" His tone was cold as he lay back down. \"Go to sleep.\"","Frowning, he added, \"You read too much, Cheng Zhao. You always overthink things.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\""]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62: Zhou Yuanshen completed this month's errand.","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen had not visited Nonghua Courtyard for several days.","Everything in the Chen Duke Estate remained the same.","The First Madam, Madam Song, had not yet \"fully recovered\" and was still resting; Huan Qingtang's orders were not as effective as before; some stewards were now taking their cues from Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao remained steady, continuing to observe more and speak less at Chengming Hall.","Her duties were relatively relaxed. She woke up early to practice swordplay and practiced calligraphy in the evening, letting the days pass at a leisurely pace.","After the arrival of spring, a late spring snow melted, and the weather grew warmer day by day.","The Chen Duke Estate had already begun tailoring summer clothes for the masters and servants.","Cheng Zhao's maid brought out her spring clothes to air them in the sun.","In the mid-afternoon sunlight, she returned to Nonghua Courtyard to find the yard filled with fluttering dresses in vibrant and fresh colors, a sight that greatly lifted her spirits.","After dinner, Cheng Zhao sat under the lamp doing her embroidery.","She was embroidering a fat cat.","The chubby little cat took a lot of time to embroider, but it also perfectly explained why Cheng Zhao had delayed giving it to her niece for so long—she had to rush the work.","Spending a long time on embroidery allowed her mind to wander over various matters.","Since Zhou Yuanshen had not come for several days, Cheng Zhao guessed that with the newly appointed Crown Prince and the complex political situation, he was too busy to get away.","Regardless of whether the Emperor was friendly towards Zhou Yuanshen, he needed him.","Zhou Yuanshen was currently the most useful weapon; and Zhou Yuanshen, in order to escape his constrained situation, was willing to sacrifice his reputation in exchange for real power.","They both got what they needed.","\"...Except for his parents-in-law, everyone else has ulterior motives toward him,\" Cheng Zhao thought, \"including me.\"","She didn't think Zhou Yuanshen was pitiful.","In this world, being schemed against by others meant that the person had value.","If it were Cheng Zhao, she would need to have value. She would rather be calculated against than be completely useless.","Moreover, Zhou Yuanshen still had parents who truly loved him; his younger brother constantly showed disdain for him, but in a way, it was just another form of worrying about him.","He was better off than the vast majority of people.","Cheng Zhao admired Zhou Yuanshen for being able to find his own way out in such a situation, rather than being flattered into arrogance or wallowing in self-pity and grievance.","Most of the time, he was like a dormant leopard, lying quietly in wait as he hunted.","He had also gained some rewards.","In his contest with the Old Madam, he was not completely controlled.","It was only in his struggle against the Emperor that he temporarily held the lower hand, which was why he tried so hard to make Mu Jiang pregnant with his child.","Cheng Zhao suddenly thought, \"Does he want me to get pregnant?\"","She was his official wife bestowed by Empress Guo. What role did Cheng Zhao play in this situation?","\"He probably does, right?\"","Zhou Yuanshen did not reject sharing a bed with her; the Cheng family had no conflict of interest with him.","In fact, the Cheng family's good reputation and the stability of his marriage with the Cheng family brought him no harm whatsoever.","Unknowingly, nearly half a month passed.","By February in Shengjing City, the weather had warmed up. Wild grass sprouted in the suburbs, willow branches budded, and many people arranged to go on spring outings.","Cheng Zhao's new handkerchief was finished.","She had embroidered a plump, adorable kitten with pale yellow patterns.","\"I'll visit my maiden home tomorrow and go out to play with my eldest sister,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"I heard my brother-in-law's position has been finalized as the Vice Minister of War.\"","She also wanted to know where her eldest sister and brother-in-law would live next.","Would they move back to their own residence, or continue staying at the Cheng estate?","She also needed to give the handkerchief to her niece, Du Heng.","As she was planning this, she felt an anxious ache in her lower abdomen.","Cheng Zhao hadn't been worrying about having children lately, so she hadn't paid much attention to her menstrual cycle.","Startled by the sudden sensation, she paused and immediately went to the washroom.","Sure enough, her period had come again.","This time, it was only delayed by two days.","She felt a little discouraged when she came out.","\"...How on earth did the Secondary Wife get pregnant?\" Cheng Zhao held a warm cup of ginger tea, feeling somewhat disheartened.","Mu Jiang was lively and healthy, but Cheng Zhao wasn't sickly either. Why couldn't she match up to her?","\"Don't worry, Young Madam. Didn't the doctor advise you to relax a bit?\" Nanny Li said.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"But this is just too unfair.\"","She and Zhou Yuanshen had shared a bed several times this month.","The doctor said she only had some stagnant qi and was otherwise perfectly fine and healthy.","Her mother had even invited a Guanyin statue for granting children for her.","\"Have you all been burning incense for me lately?\" Cheng Zhao asked Suyue and the others.","Her Guanyin statue was placed in the east room, and the maids offered incense every day.","Because Cheng Zhao was sometimes too busy, she would forget about it.","\"You should offer the incense yourself; we will remind you every day,\" Suyue said. \"Your heart is not sincere enough. If we offer incense on your behalf, the Bodhisattva won't accept it.\"","Cheng Zhao thought this made sense.","\"Once my period is over, I must offer incense to the Bodhisattva every day,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li couldn't help but smile: \"None of you are sincere enough.\"","She repeatedly urged Cheng Zhao not to be anxious.","Blossoming and bearing fruit both require the right timing.","\"Why hasn't the Duke come over these past few days?\" Nanny Li also asked.","Cheng Zhao thought to herself that they had already been together several times, so it didn't matter much whether he came or not.","If he missed a month and the gap was too long, only then would she need to worry. This month, Zhou Yuanshen's duty was already fulfilled.","\"The court has many matters; he is busy,\" Cheng Zhao replied.","The next day, Cheng Zhao went to Chengming Hall to \"ask for leave,\" as she needed to go out.","Huan Qingtang naturally agreed readily; the head steward wouldn't restrict her either, and didn't dare ask what she was going out to do.","Cheng Zhao then informed the Old Madam and the Second Madam before heading to the Cheng family.","Her mother told her that her eldest sister and brother-in-law had already moved back to the Du family's residence.","The Du family's residence was not far from the Chen Duke Estate, about five or six miles away. The entire house was not large, but it was fully equipped and very comfortable to live in.","After her eldest sister returned to the capital, her mother had instructed her second brother to quickly start renovating the house from the inside out and replace all the furniture with new pieces.","Having been unoccupied for years, there were always places the servants had neglected.","By the time her eldest sister and brother-in-law moved in, her brother-in-law would definitely have to go to work at the government office, and her eldest sister would have to manage the household and take care of three children. How would she have the time to repair the house?","They would just be making do.","Cheng Zhao's mother couldn't stand making do; life had to be refined.","Her second brother handled things properly and had asked friends for help, so the house renovations were completed last month.","Her eldest sister had only moved in three days ago.","Cheng Zhao wanted to visit, and her mother wanted to take a look along the way, so the mother and daughter set off together.","\"...Your grandfather said that we originally needed to call in more favors; your brother-in-law was also using his superior's connections, striving to stay in the Ministry of War.","The court has been busy with appointing the Crown Prince recently, and everything is chaotic. We all thought it would drag on until at least June or July. We didn't expect the appointment letter to come down so quickly,\" her mother said to Cheng Zhao.","She was probing Cheng Zhao with her words.","Cheng Zhao nodded: \"The Duke said he would help. Eldest brother-in-law is his relative by marriage, and will be of assistance to him in the future.\"","\"Next time, tell your father and your second brother to invite the Duke home for drinks,\" her mother said. \"Also, tell your eldest sister and brother-in-law to keep the Duke's favor in their hearts.\"","\"Brother-in-law and the Fan family share the same master, and the Fan family is the Duke's maternal family. They already have a relationship, so they should interact more,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Her mother nodded in relief.","As they talked, they arrived at the Du residence.","However, at the entrance, they ran into Fan Xiao, as well as her brother-in-law, Zhou Yuanqi.","Cheng Zhao was slightly surprised.","She wasn't too surprised that Fan Xiao was here, but why had Zhou Yuanqi also come?","She looked at Zhou Yuanqi in confusion.","Zhou Yuanqi came over to pay his respects. Proper and well-behaved, and exceptionally handsome, he made Cheng Zhao's mother nod repeatedly: \"Has the Fifth Young Master been busy with his studies lately?\"","She liked him very much.","\"Not too busy, Auntie,\" Zhou Yuanqi replied respectfully.","He looked absolutely nothing like his usual self at home, where he would roll his eyes at the drop of a hat.","Cheng Zhao could not help but smile.","Just as the group was about to head inside, a voice suddenly called out from behind them, \"Brother Fan!\""]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63: The Prince's Miss","paragraphs":["Everyone turned around and saw a young man wearing a lake-green cloak.","He looked to be about twenty years old, with a pair of peach-blossom eyes that held a watery tenderness when he looked at people. His brows and eyes carried a smile, making him appear very approachable.","Fan Xiao was taken aback at first: \"It is the Heir Apparent... wait, we should call you the Prince of Andong now, right?\"","\"It has been a few years, but Brother Fan is still as dashing and straightforward as ever,\" Helian Xuan, the Prince of Andong, said with a smile.","\"It must be three years now. We heard about your father's passing, but we were too busy during the New Year to offer our condolences. Please do not take offense,\" Fan Xiao said.","Helian Xuan smiled. \"You all sent condolence money, for which my mother and I are very grateful. Thank you for your concern.\"","Cheng Zhao stood to the side, listening.","Helian Xuan seemed to have just noticed her and Madam Cheng. He stepped forward to bow. \"Madam Cheng...\"","Seeing Cheng Zhao, his tone hesitated for a moment before his smile returned. \"Fifth Miss.\"","Cheng Zhao immediately replied coldly, \"I am the Duchess of Chen. If the Prince does not respect me, he must at least respect my husband.\"","Zhou Yuanqi and Fan Xiao immediately looked over.","The curiosity and inquiry in the eyes of the uncle and nephew were exactly the same.","Madam Cheng patted the back of Cheng Zhao's hand and said with a smile, \"What kind of madam brings up her official title all day long? You really have a child's temper.\"","She then smiled and asked the Prince of Andong, \"Is the Dowager Princess well? She used to have some leg ailments in her earlier years and could not stand dampness. Your fiefdom is drier; has she recovered?\"","\"There is a renowned doctor in our fiefdom who cured my mother. She rarely suffers from flare-ups now. She even mentioned wanting to visit the capital when she has time, but she dare not enter without an imperial edict,\" the Prince of Andong said.","\"What orders brought the Prince to the capital this time?\" Madam Cheng asked with a smile.","\"It is regarding the official horses. His Majesty summoned me to the capital to report,\" Helian Xuan said.","While they were talking, Cheng Zhao's eldest sister and brother-in-law walked out from the inner courtyard.","They exchanged greetings.","\"...I didn't expect us to run into each other. No wonder the lamp wick kept popping last night,\" the eldest brother-in-law, Du Anli, said.","Everyone entered the courtyard.","The doors, windows, corridors, and pillars of the courtyard were all brand new. It was small, elegant, and exquisitely decorated.","The men went to the main hall of the outer courtyard to talk, while Cheng Zhao and her mother followed her eldest sister into the inner courtyard.","She first took out a handkerchief for Heng'er.","\"...How adorable.\" Her eldest sister's eyes lit up. \"Not only are your embroidery skills good, but your painting skills are also impressive.\"","Her mother also took it to look and praised her, \"You have improved. I was always worried you would be too impatient for needlework, but to think you have practiced it to such proficiency.\"","Cheng Zhao forced a smile.","Heng'er was even more overjoyed.","She looked at it again and again, then threw herself into Cheng Zhao's arms. \"Fifth Aunt, Heng'er likes you the most.\"","Cheng Zhao chuckled and pinched her little nose.","The wet nurse took her out to play.","Cheng Zhao's face darkened.","\"Are you still angry?\" Her eldest sister walked over and put an arm around Cheng Zhao's shoulders. \"Life and death are determined by fate. His parents and sister have all forgiven him, so why must you hold onto it?\"","\"Wenliang was my guard; he sold himself into servitude. When he died, the Prince of An's estate played a trick, bringing Wenliang's parents over to play the victims, forcing Mother to return his indenture contract to them.","\"They took the benefits from the Prince of An's estate and settled the matter. Wenliang's perfectly good life was just thrown away on Helian Xuan,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Madam Cheng sighed.","Cheng Zhao continued, \"What makes me even angrier is that the Prince of An's estate was dishonest. Instead of apologizing to us, they went straight to Wenliang's family.\"","Madam Cheng then said, \"I heard that the Heir Apparent was in a coma for three months at the time. It was the Prince and Princess of An who made the decision to seek out Wenliang's parents.\"","The Heir Apparent she mentioned was Helian Xuan.","Helian Xuan's father was the Prince of An.","After his father passed away, he inherited the title at a lower rank and was titled the Prince of Andong.","He and the current Emperor were cousins.","\"They treated me like a fool,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"I told the Heir Apparent of An over and over again that the old fishermen said there would be strong winds and the boat would capsize. He refused to listen. So many people died, and he was the only one who survived, taking my guard down with him.\"","Cheng Zhao's father was an official in Fengzhou; the Prince of An was the Emperor's biological uncle, sent by him to Fengzhou to oversee the transportation of official salt.","The two government offices were very close, so Cheng Zhao and Cheng Chao used to play together with the Heir Apparent of An.","They fell out within a couple of days because neither would yield to the other.","At home, relying on her grandfather's doting and being her parents' youngest daughter, Cheng Zhao thoroughly dominated her fourth brother, Cheng Chao.","Upon arriving in Fengzhou, Cheng Chao colluded with Helian Xuan. The two fools actually managed to turn the tables on Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao could not stand their smugness.","The two self-righteous boys always wanted to boss Cheng Zhao around, rushing ahead of her in everything and forbidding her from doing this or that.","Meanwhile, Cheng Zhao felt that they lacked both intelligence and foresight, and were not even qualified to be her followers. Paying attention to them was a pure waste of time, yet they still hung around her all day.","Just looking at them was annoying.","In short, Helian Xuan led Cheng Chao in a rebellion against Cheng Zhao, and from then on, Cheng Zhao was at odds with them.","Wenliang was Cheng Zhao's attendant, a Fengzhou local who was a strong swimmer and very enthusiastic. Whenever Cheng Zhao took her maids out to play, Wenliang always led the way.","Helian Xuan wanted to go look for sea pearls, and secretly used Cheng Chao to poach Wenliang away.","The boat capsized that very day.","Wenliang and seven attendants from the Prince of An's estate all died; Helian Xuan barely escaped with his life.","One of the deceased was a servant of the Cheng family, yet the Prince of An's estate did not first visit to apologize or discuss compensation. Instead, they sought out Wenliang's parents and had them step forward.","Madam Cheng was also furious at the time.","This matter was handled very poorly.","It showed neither self-respect nor respect for the Cheng family.","Madam Cheng went to the Prince and Princess of An and righteously reprimanded them.","The Princess of An cried, saying that the Heir Apparent, Helian Xuan, had not yet awakened and his life hung in the balance.","As a result, Madam Cheng, who should have been in the right, ended up looking like she was throwing a tantrum.","Madam Cheng valued her demeanor the most. After returning to the manor, she found herself in an awkward position, unable to advance or retreat, feeling incredibly stifled.","A few years later, Madam Cheng was no longer angry. She would even ask about Helian Xuan's mother and comfort Cheng Zhao a little.","\"...Forget it, it is all in the past,\" her eldest sister gently hugged Cheng Zhao. \"I heard that Wenliang's sister is still in the Prince of Andong's estate today.\"","\"I do not want to care about that.\"","Cheng Zhao stood up and went out for some fresh air, taking the opportunity to find her niece to play with.","After she left, Madam Cheng whispered to her eldest daughter, \"When the Prince of An passed away, the imperial court granted the Princess of An special permission to return for her investiture.","\"She met with Her Majesty the Empress and even had lunch in the Empress's palace. Not long after, the Empress bestowed a marriage upon Zhao-zhao.\"","She added, \"I was always afraid that Zhao-zhao was too wild and would ruin her reputation as a noble lady, so I did not let her socialize. How did the Empress know about Zhao-zhao? It is hard for me not to suspect the Dowager Princess of An.\"","Cheng Han smiled.","Madam Cheng sighed, \"Back then, I thought the two of them were a good match. I almost made a misstep, but fortunately, I did not let anything slip.\"","Cheng Han lowered her voice, \"My little sister is competitive and has not yet opened her heart to romance. The Dowager Princess of An really overthought things.\"","She continued, \"Losing the Cheng family as an in-law, she will not even have time to cry before realizing she can never find anyone better than the Chengs. It shows how narrow-minded she is. Mother, do not stoop to her level.\"","She also said, \"Our little sister married quite well now. The Duke of Chen is handsome and elegant. In terms of looks, family background, and bearing, he does not lose to the Prince of Andong in any way.\""]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64: Are You Childhood Sweethearts","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao took a tour of the inner courtyard of her eldest sister's mansion by herself.","No one followed her.","After she had walked enough, she returned to her eldest sister and mother.","\"...The sightseeing pavilion in the west is built so well. The window lattices were made by the Xu family's workshop again. Furniture from the Xu family's workshop always requires a wait,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Her mother smiled, \"Your second brother put a lot of thought into it.\"","\"Second Brother is reliable. If it were Fourth Brother, he would definitely fool you and Eldest Sister,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Her eldest sister laughed, \"You and A'Chao weren't this bad when you were young. It's just those few years in Fengzhou that made the two of you as incompatible as fire and water now.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"He ganged up with an outsider to bully me, and he still expects me to treat him well?\"","When they were in Fengzhou, her fourth brother Cheng Chao always brought Helian Xuan to wander in front of her.","In Cheng Zhao's eyes, two tigers cannot share one mountain. Those two refused to lower themselves and listen to her orders, yet they dared to constantly hover around her. It was pure provocation.","It was like foreign tribes harassing the borders.","It would have been one thing if Cheng Chao provoked her himself, but he even brought an outsider.","It was not merely a threat to Cheng Zhao's territory, but also a rebellion against the family. Not docile, not loyal—Cheng Zhao felt irritated just thinking of him.","\"Don't let an outsider ruin your sibling bond,\" her eldest sister said. \"Our little sister is the most magnanimous, just forgive him. Why care so much about an outsider and give him such face?\"","Cheng Zhao took a deep breath. \"Eldest Sister is right.\"","Her mother said, \"You only like to listen to your eldest sister's words. Whenever I try to persuade you, you never listen.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Lunch was eaten separately. Her eldest brother-in-law was entertaining guests in the outer courtyard and did not come in to accompany his mother-in-law.","After Cheng Zhao had lunch with her mother and eldest sister, she prepared to return to her estate.","A servant boy went to inform him, and the eldest brother-in-law came out to see off his mother-in-law and sister-in-law.","Fan Xiao and Helian Xuan also took the opportunity to say their goodbyes.","They met again at the doorway.","\"...Come visit our estate another day,\" Zhou Yuanqi suddenly said to Helian Xuan.","Helian Xuan's peach-blossom eyes looked exceptionally friendly and handsome when he smiled. \"Alright, I will definitely come to bother you. I happen to have some matters to discuss with Duke Chen.\"","Fan Xiao also exchanged a few pleasantries, inviting Helian Xuan to visit his home another day.","Helian Xuan was also acquainted with the Fan family's old matriarch. He asked about the old madam's health and promised to visit another day.","Only then did they part ways.","Since Cheng Zhao was returning to the Duke Chen's estate, Fan Xiao entrusted Zhou Yuanqi to her.","\"This saves me from having to escort him back separately,\" Fan Xiao smiled. \"Thank you for the trouble, Madam Duke.\"","When he called Cheng Zhao Madam Duke, there was a hint of teasing in his tone.","\"Uncle is making fun of me,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"I will take him, Uncle can rest assured.\"","Fan Xiao: \"Come play at our house another day, and bring Yuanshen along.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","They each got into their carriages. Cheng Zhao did not spare another glance at Helian Xuan.","Inside the carriage, Zhou Yuanqi looked at her curiously several times.","\"Why did you follow Uncle to visit my brother-in-law's house?\" Cheng Zhao asked Zhou Yuanqi.","\"Little Uncle has a military book compiled by Du Anli. I had never met someone with such insight, so I was curious and asked Little Uncle to bring me to meet him,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","He added, \"Little Uncle deliberately teased me. It wasn't until we were almost at the door that he told me Du Anli is your brother-in-law. I've met him before.\"","During the New Year, he had followed along to pay New Year's greetings at the Cheng family and had met Du Anli.","He only knew him as the eldest brother-in-law but hadn't remembered his name.","This time, he finally got his name, background, and official title all sorted out.","\"My eldest brother-in-law is indeed very talented and learned, and his martial arts are excellent. He is also quite worldly-wise,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Cheng family children all respected their eldest brother-in-law very much.","\"Compared to The Brute?\" Zhou Yuanqi asked.","Cheng Zhao: \"Don't even think about catching me making a mistake.\"","\"Then you must think The Brute doesn't compare. By saying that, you've just exposed your own mistake,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","She desperately wanted to reach out and pinch his cheeks.","But she didn't dare.","Zhou Yuanqi always fancied himself an adult; he could not accept others teasing him like a child. He couldn't do anything about verbal teasing, but getting physical would be going too far.","Cheng Zhao was afraid he would fly into a rage out of humiliation.","\"Are you and the Prince of Andong childhood sweethearts?\" Zhou Yuanqi asked again.","Cheng Zhao whipped her head around. \"Who started that rumor?\"","Zhou Yuanqi observed her. \"Are you feeling guilty?\"","\"No!\"","\"But you have quite a temper. With such a huge reaction, it's hard to say there's no past between you two,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","There was indeed a lot of past history, but she simply could not accept the term childhood sweethearts. This term was not only ambiguous but also carried a hint of fond memories.","Cheng Zhao and Helian Xuan definitely did not have that kind of relationship.","Cheng Zhao would often think of her estate guard, Wen Liang.","Not only was this guard loyal and attentive, but he also had a very good relationship with Qiubai. After he died, Qiubai secretly cried several times.","There was no opportunity to avenge his death. His parents and sister took the opportunity to defect to Prince An's estate, using his remains to seek high positions.","They suppressed everything. Cheng Zhao wanted to seek revenge, but in their eyes, she was just stirring up trouble, making her look bad from all sides.","Cheng Zhao didn't know who to hate.","And this human life, that friendship, and Qiubai's pain were all connected to Helian Xuan.","\"I don't have any past with him.\" Cheng Zhao turned her head to the side.","She forcefully clenched her back teeth.","However, Zhou Yuanqi kept looking at her.","After watching her for a long while, Zhou Yuanqi came to a conclusion: The Empress's bestowed marriage had broken up a pair of lovebirds.","Zhou Yuanqi had just tactfully inquired about it. Helian Xuan's father had passed away before Cheng Zhao's marriage was bestowed. He guessed that Helian Xuan was observing a strict mourning period, which delayed the wedding.","And through a twist of fate, Cheng Zhao became Zhou Yuanqi's sister-in-law.","\"Can this person marry into our family as a live-in son-in-law?\" Zhou Yuanqi thought.","It was unlikely. Helian Xuan was the Emperor's cousin, had inherited a noble title, and had been conferred the title of Prince.","A Prince could never become a live-in son-in-law.","Zhou Yuanqi clicked his tongue, feeling a bit unwilling to give up.","He had scouted quite a few candidates for a live-in son-in-law for his sister-in-law. In terms of conversational skills, appearance, and temperament, Helian Xuan ranked at the very top; no one could surpass him.","His background was also excellent.","Only someone with such a noble status was qualified to match his Fairy Sister-in-law.","Before meeting Helian Xuan, it seemed like anyone would do; after meeting him, everyone else felt like just making do.","Zhou Yuanqi disliked making do the most; he pursued the best in everything. Even for practicing calligraphy, he would buy Mr. Qu Lian's copybooks at a high price.","\"How can I force a Prince to become a live-in son-in-law?\"","This would probably be one of Zhou Yuanqi's primary tasks for a long time to come; he had to conquer this difficult problem.","Aside from Helian Xuan being outstanding in every aspect, it was also because his appearance could barely compete with The Brute.","Zhou Yuanqi felt that The Brute was very lucky to have been born extremely handsome. And it was precisely because he was handsome that he attracted so many women around him, making his Fairy Sister-in-law suffer grievances.","His imagination ran wild, a massive battle raging in his brain, bustling with intense activity in silence.","Meanwhile, Cheng Zhao was also quietly lost in thought.","When the carriage parked at the entrance of Duke Chen's estate, the two of them were completely unaware.","Until someone lifted the carriage curtain.","Outside the curtain was a clear mid-afternoon. Sunlight crashed in from outside, and both Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanqi subconsciously squinted their eyes.","\"...Fell asleep?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked. \"You haven't gotten out of the carriage for ages. What are you two dawdling for?\"","The sunlight spilled onto his face. His prominent brow bones cast a slight shadow under his eyes, making his excellent bone structure appear even more striking.","Helian Xuan was still not as good-looking as him.","Zhou Yuanqi let out a deep sigh.","Trying to find a live-in son-in-law who surpassed The Brute in every aspect was so difficult.","\"Getting off right now,\" Cheng Zhao snapped back to reality.","She and Zhou Yuanqi stepped through the grand doors of the Duke of Chen's estate, their minds weighed down by heavy thoughts.","Though young in age and possessing exquisitely delicate features, the two of them wore the profound, solemn expressions of the elderly. It was quite an amusing sight, Zhou Yuanshen thought to himself as he, too, stepped over the threshold."]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65: The Duke's Urgency","paragraphs":["The three of them walked back.","Two of them were utterly dejected.","\"Let's go sit in Chenhui Courtyard for a bit,\" Zhou Yuanshen spoke up from behind.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"Not going.\"","\"I wasn't talking to you.\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\"","Cheng Zhao then went with Zhou Yuanshen to Chenhui Courtyard, where the servant boy Nanfeng served them tea.","\"What were you doing?\" he asked.","Cheng Zhao told him the truth.","Zhou Yuanshen had thought Cheng Zhao took Zhou Yuanqi out, never expecting it was their young uncle.","\"...Then who upset you two? Also our young uncle?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked again.","His young uncle, Fan Xiao, always loved to tease cats and dogs; he was very mischievous.","\"No,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She drank her tea in silence, her emotions having already calmed down.","After finishing a cup of tea, Cheng Zhao saw it was getting late. Needing to return for dinner, she said, \"My Lord Duke, I will head back first.\"","\"I'll go over too,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao glanced at him, hesitating slightly before saying, \"My monthly time has come, and I fear it might be unclean. You cannot stay in Nonghua Courtyard tonight.\"","She wasn't negotiating.","She rejected him concisely and clearly.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"I am not afraid of it being unclean.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","These men, every single one of them loved to provoke her. Why were they all so disobedient?","Was it because she was too weak?","Probably.","When could she become an old matriarch, having the final say like the Old Madam? That way, everyone would be respectful when standing before her.","But it would be soon.","Cheng Zhao had already received the imperial mandate of a Duchess. As long as she kept walking down this path, with her power, status, age, and experience slowly increasing, she would gain authority.","The couple returned to Nonghua Courtyard.","After dinner, Cheng Zhao prepared to practice calligraphy to calm her mind.","Zhou Yuanshen still held a book to read.","Cheng Zhao had seen his books; they were all about local customs and old traditions of various places, or about water conservancy, which she found very boring.","They were neither history books nor storybooks.","They remained silent as the night gradually deepened.","Cheng Zhao wrote a few pages of characters.","When Zhou Yuanshen stood up, he looked at her writing and casually remarked, \"You don't put enough strength into your writing.\"","\"I am known for being graceful and elegant, so I don't need to exert too much effort,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"I thought you preferred a handsome and spirited style, with vigorous strokes that penetrate the wood.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Not really. Why would you think so?\"","\"You are very competitive.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","She argued that she wasn't.","Seizing the opportunity, Zhou Yuanshen grasped her hand and guided it to write two characters: Cheng Zhao.","The calligraphy was elegant and free, with sharp and strong strokes; it was indeed beautiful.","However, he gripped Cheng Zhao's hand so tightly that it hurt.","\"These two characters must be kept,\" Cheng Zhao said, ignoring the slight pain in her hand. She picked it up to admire it carefully, finding it more beautiful the longer she looked.","She then said to him, \"When the New Year comes, please write the couplets for Nonghua Courtyard.\"","\"It is still early for the New Year,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","He didn't promise anything in advance.","The couple went to rest.","Before Cheng Zhao went to wash up, she drank a bowl of brown sugar ginger tea.","Zhou Yuanshen suddenly leaned over, kissed her lips, and whispered, \"A bit sweet and a bit spicy.\"","Cheng Zhao avoided him.","Unsure if it was because of the ginger tea, a wave of heat inexplicably flushed her cheeks: \"Too much ginger juice was added.\"","Zhou Yuanshen kissed her again.","Cheng Zhao tried to dodge, but he wrapped his arm around her waist.","\"My Lord Duke, my monthly time is still here.\" Cheng Zhao pushed him, her breathing a bit hurried.","Now, not only were her cheeks hot, but she felt her palms were burning too—just how much ginger juice did Nanny Li put in the tea?","Was ginger free this year?","Yet Zhou Yuanshen did not let go.","He held her tightly, pulling her soft waist close to him.","His dark, placid eyes became chaotic. He kissed her lips, then went to kiss her earlobe.","Cheng Zhao wanted to hide even more; she was ticklish.","The tickling made her whole body uncomfortable.","Zhou Yuanshen grasped one of her hands.","Her pale, slender hand, illuminated by the lantern light, looked like transparent white jade without a single flaw. She had such a competitive personality, yet her body was as if made of jade.","Sometimes Zhou Yuanshen was afraid she would bump into things, because she was so perfect that a slight accident would leave a mark on her.","\"Cheng Zhao, touch me...\" he said.","\"No!\"","Her collar was pulled loose by him, and he leaned down to kiss her collarbone.","His breath burned her.","Cheng Zhao twisted, trying to escape, but her hand was already being guided by him toward his body.","She was truly anxious this time, fighting with all her might to shove him away.","His arms were like iron hoops; the more Cheng Zhao moved, the closer she pressed against him.","Cheng Zhao's hand touched his chest and was guided all the way down by him...","\"Zhou Yuanshen, don't go too far!\"","Cheng Zhao bit at him.","As if anticipating this, he took the opportunity to press her onto the bed, gripping her jaw with his hand.","Her lips were slightly parted, her breath like orchids.","Zhou Yuanshen kissed her again.","Just as Cheng Zhao was about to cry, he finally let go.","His breathing was extremely heavy as he strode to the washroom.","Cheng Zhao had struggled until her clothes were in disarray, and she hurriedly straightened them.","After a long while, when Zhou Yuanshen returned from the washroom, Cheng Zhao was already lying down to sleep with her back to him.","She did not look at him.","He looked at her in silence.","\"I will go back to Chenhui Courtyard to sleep,\" he said. \"Do you want me to stay?\"","\"No need!\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen left.","After he went out, Cheng Zhao kept feeling that her inner trousers were soiled, so she got up to change her clothes again.","Having lost her sleepiness, she washed her hands meticulously, freshened up simply, and sat dazed under the lamp.","She felt that Zhou Yuanshen in that moment just now didn't seem like himself.","He wasn't aloof or rational.","He was like a starving beast that had to devour flesh and blood to satisfy its burning appetite.","It had only been half a month since they last shared a bed. During this half month, had he not visited Lijing Courtyard?","Cheng Zhao took a few deep breaths, suppressed her chaotic thoughts, put away the two characters he wrote, and then finally went to sleep.","Mid-afternoon the next day, Zhou Yuanshen returned, bringing some pastries.","He stood quietly in front of Cheng Zhao, his dark eyes placid: \"From the palace. When they were rewarded to us before, Mother said they were quite delicious. Try them and see if you like them.\"","He added, \"I have some matters to attend to tonight, so you don't need to wait for me.\"","Cheng Zhao said yes.","He came in a hurry and was leaving in a hurry.","He still wore his black robe and a cold expression, showing absolutely no emotion when he spoke.","Cheng Zhao couldn't tell if he felt apologetic either, and accepted the pastries: \"Thank you, My Lord Duke.\"","Zhou Yuanshen gave a slight nod and then left.","The pastries were indeed very delicious. Paired with brown sugar ginger tea, Cheng Zhao found it quite enjoyable.","The slight unpleasantness from last night dissipated.","In the end, nothing really happened; he just grabbed her hand and held it. She was almost angered to tears, and when his breathing became erratic, he let go of her hand.","Cheng Zhao decided to turn the page.","Two days later, her monthly time ended. Cheng Zhao earnestly went to offer incense to Guanyin, praying to conceive early.","In mid-February, the weather grew warmer, and the noble households began preparing for peach blossom banquets.","Eldest Madam Song's grounding was lifted, and she was still the one managing the household.","The first thing she did upon coming out was to organize a banquet. She led Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang to the Old Madam to ask for instructions.","Inside Shou'an Courtyard, however, there was a woman with a son and daughter, chatting with the Old Madam.","\"Cousin-in-law,\" Eldest Madam Song greeted."]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66: Face-to-Face Instigation","paragraphs":["The niece-in-law, grandnephew, and grandniece from the Qingyuan Marquis Manor, Dowager Madame's maiden home, came to visit.","They greeted each other.","Cheng Zhao had met them during the New Year. She stepped forward, called out to her cousin-aunt, then to her younger cousin-brother and cousin-sister, and stood to the side.","They were much more familiar with Huan Qingtang.","\"...Cousin-in-law, why do you look a bit thinner?\" Dowager Madame's grandniece, Sun Zhiya, held Huan Qingtang's hand and asked affectionately.","The grandnephew, Sun Zhisheng, also glanced at Huan Qingtang. \"Cousin-in-law must be tired, right? Managing the household is not easy and takes a lot of hard work.\"","\"It's not too bad,\" Huan Qingtang smiled, then added, \"The calligraphy copybook you asked me to write last time is finished. I was planning to send it to you soon. Since you are here, you can just take it back with you.\"","Sun Zhiya was very happy. \"Thank you, Cousin-in-law.\"","They started chatting about calligraphy copybooks.","Sun Zhiya said, \"Cousin-in-law, does your maiden family have any calligraphy copybooks by Mister Qu Lian? Last time, County Princess Xizhen brought one out and showed it off everywhere.\"","\"Aya, what kind of talk is that!\" the Marchioness of Qingyuan immediately chided.","Cheng Zhao listened quietly without changing her expression.","Huan Qingtang smiled and spoke up to bail Sun Zhiya out, \"Cousin-aunt, I didn't take offense.\"","She continued, \"Mister Qu Lian's copybooks haven't been seen for many years. I don't know who collected them. Over the past two years, many convincing fakes have appeared. They are all forgeries.\"","Sun Zhiya's eyes lit up. \"Cousin-in-law, next time you can go and expose County Princess Xizhen.\"","The Marchioness of Qingyuan was quite helpless. \"Aya...\"","\"Aya is innocent and pure; she cannot tolerate falsehoods. This is what makes her lovable,\" Huan Qingtang smiled.","She added, \"Next time we visit Princess Qing'an's residence, if we see County Princess Xizhen, perhaps I can help her appraise the copybook.\"","The group chatted about calligraphy.","Cheng Zhao stood by the side the whole time, quietly listening to them talk without interrupting.","Madam Song, seeing that everyone from the Qingyuan Marquis Manor liked Huan Qingtang, also flattered her with a few words.","\"...The Huan family daughter is a true lady of a noble and pure lineage. When it comes to talent, no one in the entire capital can match her,\" Madam Song said.","Sun Zhiya, however, looked at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao acted as if she didn't notice.","When her eyes met Sun Zhiya's for a moment, Cheng Zhao only smiled faintly.","Sun Zhiya's expression changed slightly.","She was a bit displeased.","\"Third Cousin-in-law seems unconvinced. After all, the Cheng family is also a scholarly family,\" Sun Zhiya said.","The Marchioness of Qingyuan spoke up again, \"Aya, don't talk nonsense.\"","She smiled at Cheng Zhao, \"Please don't take offense.\"","Madam Song took the opportunity to say, \"Madam Cheng won't take offense. She is the most tolerant and generous, and never fusses over anything.\"","She couldn't help but add, \"Since she married into the family, our manor has become much livelier. Indeed, a large family brings prosperity.\"","In the less than half a year since Cheng Zhao married in, Madam Song had suffered setbacks twice.","The first time was the poisoned rice in the main kitchen, which caused her trusted aide to be beaten and driven out; the second time was sending \"tonic\" to the Duke, which was also related to Cheng Zhao, resulting in her being grounded.","Whenever Madam Song saw Cheng Zhao, an inexplicable anger would flare up inside her.","She held it in again and again, but still said, \"Since Madam Cheng married in, she has been excellent in every aspect, making the rest of us look inferior. Look, Qingtang has lost so much weight these days; she was also forced into a helpless situation.\"","Dowager Madame remained silent, glancing at her lightly with a hidden warning.","The Marchioness of Qingyuan felt a bit helpless.","\"Did she bully Cousin-in-law?\" Sun Zhiya asked from the side.","Her brother, Sun Zhisheng, immediately shot an unfriendly glare at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao merely looked back at Dowager Madame. \"Grandmother, do you also feel that I haven't shared Eldest Sister-in-law's burden?\"","Dowager Madame: \"...\"","Her underlying meaning was: Grandmother, do you need to give me more household management tallies?","Madam Song harbored ill intentions, and Sun Zhiya was purely naive; they were practically handing Cheng Zhao a knife to use against them.","Dowager Madame had ten thousand ways to deal with Cheng Zhao, but currently, she did not want to tear all face with Zhou Yuanshen.","\"...Mother, you've misunderstood Sister-in-law. She has always worked very hard,\" Huan Qingtang spoke up, then said to Sun Zhiya, \"Cousin, come with me to fetch the copybook.\"","She added, \"Cousin-brother, you come along too. The Cuiyun Courtyard has very delicious pastries, Peach Blossom Crisps rewarded by the palace.\"","The three of them bowed to Dowager Madame and left the Shou'an Courtyard first.","On the way, Sun Zhiya still asked Huan Qingtang, \"Cousin-in-law, is that sister-in-law of yours deeply scheming and always working against you?\"","Huan Qingtang remained silent.","Sun Zhisheng was more impulsive. \"It looks like it. Her marriage was bestowed by the Empress. She has backing, so she bullies people everywhere.\"","At the mention of the Empress's maiden family, the Guos, the two Sun children were filled with resentment. They had conflicts with several young masters and misses of the Guo family.","The Guo family had a very domineering young miss. Everyone had suffered at her hands, yet no one dared to clash with her head-on.","Sun Zhiya had also been lectured by Miss Guo before.","Since Cheng Zhao was bestowed upon the Zhou family by Empress Guo, and Huan Qingtang tacitly acknowledged her arrogance, Sun Zhiya immediately transferred her anger onto Cheng Zhao.","\"At the Peach Blossom Banquet three days from now, I will teach her a lesson,\" Sun Zhiya said.","She glanced at her brother.","Sun Zhisheng gave a cunning smile.","Huan Qingtang said, \"Cousin, don't be angry anymore. With your beautiful face, getting angry easily makes you pale, and then you won't look pretty.\"","The three headed toward the Cuiyun Courtyard.","Cheng Zhao and Madam Song also left the Shou'an Courtyard.","Madam Song walked very fast.","Cheng Zhao still caught up with her. \"Eldest Aunt, do you feel no guilt at all for drugging my husband last time?\"","Madam Song froze.","Her face instantly turned ugly. It was a mix of resentment and feeling utterly ashamed.","When facing their own disgraceful behavior, ordinary people could not remain as rational and calm as Zhou Yuanshen, so Madam Song's voice raised a few pitches. \"Madam Cheng, you dare to question an elder like this?\"","\"Elders should be loving, and juniors should be filial. If an elder has not a shred of self-respect and dignity, do not expect the junior to be completely obedient,\" Cheng Zhao said quietly. \"I still want to ask First Madam Zhou one sentence: have you reflected on the drugging incident?\"","She no longer called her Eldest Aunt, but First Madam Zhou.","When Cheng Zhao said this, she even took a step forward, forcing Madam Song to retreat two steps in a row, almost falling over.","Her maid supported her.","Intimidated by Cheng Zhao, Madam Song's trusted maid did not dare to say a single word.","\"Sooner or later, you will have to apologize to the Duke and me.\" Cheng Zhao's gaze fell unblinkingly on her. \"Grandmother let you out to resume managing affairs, not to stir up trouble out of nothing again.\"","With that said, Cheng Zhao turned and left.","When she spoke, the maids beside Madam Song and the maids from the Shou'an Courtyard who were seeing them out were all present.","The news reached Dowager Madame's ears.","After the people from the Qingyuan Marquis Manor left, Dowager Madame leisurely drank her tea.","\"A bunch of little monkey cubs, chattering away quite livelily,\" Dowager Madame smiled.","She had seen mountains of corpses and seas of blood.","These petty scratching tricks against each other weren't even enough to fill the gaps between Dowager Madame's teeth.","Everything was under the old lady's control.","Dowager Madame was even more willing to see them fight amongst themselves.","Only by competing with each other would they realize who the true master of this household was, preventing them from forming cliques based on petty cleverness.","Dowager Madame, just like the Emperor, did not like her \"courtiers\" to be too united.","The court was most stable when the courtiers kept each other in check. Whichever side grew weak, she would lend a hand, ensuring that no one could dominate alone."]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67: Praising Cheng Zhao","paragraphs":["The Duke of Chen's mansion was hosting a peach blossom banquet, and the invitation cards had to be sent out through the gatehouse.","Cheng Zhao thus knew who the First Madam and the Old Madam had invited.","Replies came back one after another.","\"...Princess Qing'an's estate is not included,\" Cheng Zhao said to her trusted aides.","The reason she paid special attention to Princess Qing'an's estate was not only because the Old Madam's grandniece had mentioned the calligraphy copybook last time, but also because Princess Qing'an had previously acted as a matchmaker for Zhou Yuanshen and Huan Qingtang.","Cheng Zhao was curious about this past event, though her mother said she was prying into privacy.","Secrets were indeed fascinating, making one want to uncover the truth behind them.","She even planned to ask Princess Qing'an about it indirectly.","However, she never expected that the Zhou family no longer interacted with Princess Qing'an's estate; during the New Year, the gatehouse had clearly received gifts from Princess Qing'an's estate and had returned them as well.","\"No one dares not to curry favor with the Zhou family, so it's likely that Princess Qing'an offended the Old Madam. They still send gifts to each other to maintain a final shred of dignity without tearing each other's faces, but in reality, they no longer associate,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"That's quite interesting,\" Suyue said. \"Young Madam, you should check the gatehouse's account books to see if she was only excluded starting this year.\"","Cheng Zhao replied, \"That's a good idea. I'll look into it after we finish our current tasks.\"","With the banquet approaching, Cheng Zhao also had some errands on hand. Both she and Huan Qingtang had to help the First Madam welcome the guests.","A banquet was the ultimate test of a matriarch's abilities, and Cheng Zhao could not afford to make any mistakes.","Following what her mother and eldest sister had taught her, Cheng Zhao first ranked the guests: she needed to grasp firmly who was the most important and ensure absolutely nothing went wrong with them.","Among the Zhou family's guests, the only one who had the best relationship with the Old Madam and was highly respected by her was Grand Princess Fukang.","The others, to varying degrees, were the ones currying favor with the Old Madam.","And as it happened, Grand Princess Fukang also liked Cheng Zhao very much.","\"...Bring out the hair stick the Princess gave me last time. I will only wear this one piece of gold jewelry for this banquet,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li hurriedly went to prepare it.","As they were talking, a little maid outside said that the young servant Nanfeng was looking for Qiubai.","Nanfeng was not yet thirteen years old, but he was highly valued by Zhou Yuanshen. He often ran between the inner and outer courtyards and didn't need to avoid anything, which was very convenient.","Qiubai, not knowing what it was about, went out for a moment.","After returning, she said to Cheng Zhao, \"The Duke has something to remind you about, regarding the Marquis of Qingyuan's estate.\"","Last time, Madam Sun from the Marquis of Qingyuan's estate, along with the Sun family's young master and miss, came as guests and almost caused a quarrel between Cheng Zhao and her eldest aunt. Zhou Yuanshen had probably heard about it.","\"What is it?\"","Qiubai lowered her voice and relayed Zhou Yuanshen's words to Cheng Zhao.","After hearing this, Cheng Zhao frowned slightly: \"Miss Sun dares to cause trouble at the Duke of Chen's peach blossom banquet?\"","\"The Old Madam highly values her maiden family's grandnephew, and Miss Sun is spoiled and arrogant. She has been betrothed to the Fifth Prince and will be a princess consort in the future, which adds to her arrogance. She dares to do anything,\" Qiubai said.","She added, \"She might not necessarily cause trouble, but he just wanted to remind you to be careful.\"","This information was also gathered by Nanfeng and told to Qiubai.","Cheng Zhao then said, \"The Duke knows everything that happens in the inner courtyard.\"","She continued, \"How is Nanfeng just a young servant? He is practically the Duke's eyes, observing the inner and outer courtyards all day long. Yet everyone just treats him as an inconspicuous child, and no one guards against him.\"","Last time, when Cheng Zhao and Qiubai were discussing the Child-giving Guanyin in the Chenhui Courtyard, Nanfeng was also there.","\"Reward him with some money, and grab some candies for him,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Although this child tattled in secret, Cheng Zhao still liked him quite a bit, and even hoped he could help her gather information in the future.","Qiubai agreed.","In the blink of an eye, it was the day of the Duke of Chen's peach blossom banquet.","Guests also arrived from the Second Madam's maiden family: an aunt, bringing along two cousins-in-law.","\"Zhaozhao, come here.\" The Second Madam specifically called Cheng Zhao over to introduce them.","Having seen them during the New Year visits, Cheng Zhao remembered them and could greet each of them by name.","This made the Second Madam even happier.","Her daughter-in-law was not only as beautiful as a fairy but also smart and clever. Moreover, she took the affairs of the Second Madam's maiden family to heart, making the Second Madam feel completely satisfied inside and out.","\"Mother, please sit with them for a while. I still need to go and welcome the guests,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She then instructed the servants, \"Serve Aunt the Tieguanyin tea. I remember Aunt said she only likes this kind of tea.\"","The Second Madam was even more delighted.","The aunt also smiled slightly, her face glowing with pleasure.","\"The Duke's Madam is truly thoughtful,\" the aunt said.","\"Zhaozhao is indeed filial,\" the Second Madam said.","Their words were filled with immense warmth and affection.","Cheng Zhao smiled and whispered to the Second Madam, \"Grand Princess Fukang hasn't arrived yet. She is the most honorable guest today, so I must go and greet her.\"","\"Go on with your work.\"","Only then did Cheng Zhao leave.","Because she explained everything clearly, the Second Madam naturally understood her, and the aunt also praised Cheng Zhao for being considerate.","Soon, the guests arrived one after another.","A little maid came to report, and the Old Madam stood up to welcome the guest. Undoubtedly, Grand Princess Fukang had arrived.","The Second Madam also followed to the door of the flower hall and sure enough, she saw her daughter-in-law supporting the Grand Princess's arm, walking towards the hall.","Huan Qingtang and the First Madam, Lady Song, both trailed behind.","\"She's so showy, showing off all by herself!\" Suddenly, the Second Madam heard someone beside her say.","The Second Madam did not turn her head, so as not to alert the snake by beating the grass, but out of the corner of her eye, she caught a glimpse of Sun Zhiya, the Old Madam's grandniece.","The Second Madam dared not offend anyone from the Sun family. But hearing her words, which were clearly aimed at Cheng Zhao, the Second Madam felt a hidden sense of vigilance.","When she snapped back to reality, the Second Madam was a bit surprised. She hadn't expected herself to think so much in that split second.","If it had been before, she definitely would have turned her head to look immediately.","Since the other party hadn't named names, if she insisted on turning around to look, she might be falsely counter-accused.","As the Second Madam was thinking this, Grand Princess Fukang had already entered.","Everyone stood up to pay their respects.","Only after Grand Princess Fukang and the Old Madam took their seats did the others sit down.","\"...The embroidery on the Duke's Madam's dress today is truly excellent.\"","After saying a few words, Grand Princess Fukang made sure to praise Cheng Zhao.","This was because Cheng Zhao had just praised Grand Princess Fukang's son at the door.","Grand Princess Fukang's son had mediocre talents, yet he insisted on mingling in scholarly circles to earn the title of a gifted scholar. It was unknown what sort of obsession he had.","He often made a fool of himself.","Grand Princess Fukang knew this as well, but there was nothing she could do. He was her only son, filial and obedient, usually gentle and polite. If one part of him was bad, the other nine parts were excellent. The Grand Princess loved this son dearly.","Cheng Zhao repeatedly praised him, calling him a free spirit, which struck right at the Grand Princess's heart: if his handwriting wasn't good, it was considered elegant and untamed; if his poetry was ordinary, it was considered unconventional.","What the scholarly circles valued was strength of character.","Of course, it was useless for the Grand Princess to boast about him herself. It required someone like Prime Minister Cheng, who was highly respected and had immense prestige in scholarly circles, to praise him in order to elevate the heir's status.","And Cheng Zhao was Prime Minister Cheng's favored granddaughter.","Grand Princess Fukang naturally had to support her.","Aside from these selfish motives, Cheng Zhao was indeed experienced and endearing.","When Grand Princess Fukang praised Cheng Zhao for the fourth time, First Madam Song's expression turned a bit unsightly.","She nudged Huan Qingtang, gesturing for her to step forward so the Grand Princess could see her too.","However, Huan Qingtang remained completely serene.","At this moment, Sun Zhiya walked over and warmly paid her respects to Grand Princess Fukang.","She was not only the grandniece of the Old Madame, but she was also destined to marry into the imperial clan in the future. Even the Grand Princess had to show her some respect.","Just as she was about to speak, a dark shadow suddenly darted past.","With quick reflexes, Cheng Zhao pulled some white powder from her pouch and scattered it around the Grand Princess.","The crowd froze for a moment before noticing a black creature. Startled by the powder, it was desperately trying to scurry away.","\"A scorpion!\"","\"What an enormous scorpion!\"","Sun Zhiya was stunned for a second before she hurriedly chased after it, crying out, \"Gale!\"","Madam Sun almost blacked out."]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68: Zhou Yuan's Devoted Protection of His Wife","paragraphs":["The flower hall was thrown into a momentary chaos.","Over at the main table, however, it was terrifyingly quiet.","The Dowager Madame and Grand Princess Fukang didn't say a word; Madame Sun's expression changed time and again; the First Madame, Madam Song, the Second Madame, Madam Fan, and Huan Qingtang all remained silent.","Only the sight of Sun Zhiya chasing after the scorpion caught the eyes of the guests.","The guests couldn't hold back and began to whisper among themselves.","\"Is that a scorpion?\"","\"Did Miss Sun name it?\"","\"She's so bold, daring to chase a scorpion?\"","\"It might be a pet she keeps that suddenly got out.\"","\"That's too terrifying. Who would dare to keep a scorpion around?\"","Sun Zhiya certainly dared.","Yesterday, Nanfeng had gathered some information and told Cheng Zhao: Sun Zhiya had a pet scorpion, as long as an adult man's palm, sleek and pitch-black.","It was a gift from someone, non-venomous and harmless, but those who didn't know would be frightened by such a large scorpion.","A few days ago at the Shou'an Courtyard, there had been a minor conflict, and the matter had reached Zhou Yuanshen's ears.","Since it involved the young miss and young master of the Sun family, and today was the Peach Blossom Banquet, Zhou Yuanshen sent Nanfeng to tell Cheng Zhao to be careful of Sun Zhiya's \"pet.\"","She might play a trick on Cheng Zhao, causing her to lose her composure in public.","She might also play a trick on a distinguished guest Cheng Zhao cared about, disrupting Cheng Zhao's plans and thereby damaging her prestige.","Cheng Zhao had brought some sulfur powder in her purse.","Insects and scorpions all fear sulfur powder. However, the smell of sulfur powder wasn't considered strange; it was normally sprinkled during the Dragon Boat Festival, so the guests were familiar with it and wouldn't panic upon smelling the powder.","\"...What play shall we listen to today?\" After a long while, the Dowager Madame smiled and asked Cheng Zhao.","She didn't ask the First Madame, Madam Song, nor Huan Qingtang, but Cheng Zhao.","This was to show the guests that Cheng Zhao, the Duchess, was the future mistress of the Duke of Chen's estate.","Cheng Zhao smiled and said, \"The playbill has been brought to you. Grandmother, you choose the play, and it will begin right away.\"","\"Let the Grand Princess choose the play.\"","\"The Dowager Madame should choose first,\" the Grand Princess smiled. \"I am a guest, I cannot overstep my bounds.\"","She then praised Cheng Zhao, \"The Duchess is the most well-versed in etiquette and truly has good breeding. The most favored household in the entire capital is the Duke of Chen's estate, which is why the Empress chose the most outstanding noble lady for the marriage.\"","These words elevated both the Dowager Madame and Cheng Zhao.","The Dowager Madame probably didn't want anyone to steal the show at the Peach Blossom Banquet. If Sun Zhiya hadn't made a scene, she would have spoken up to suppress it.","Even the Grand Princess had to bow her head a bit before the elderly lady.","But this moment wasn't suitable.","The Dowager Madame just smiled, chose a play, and Cheng Zhao went to give the orders.","Sun Zhiya's mother, the Marchioness of Qingyuan, found an excuse to go out and look for her daughter, and only brought her back after a long while.","She specially picked a basket of flowers and presented them to the Dowager Madame and the Grand Princess.","\"...This child wanted to pick some flowers, but was a bit clumsy. Grand Princess, please don't take offense,\" the Marchioness of Qingyuan said.","Grand Princess Fukang accepted this graceful exit: \"The flowers are truly beautiful. Peach blossoms, pear blossoms, and winter jasmine. It's so thoughtful of you.\"","Sun Zhiya's smile was very forced.","After presenting the flowers, she finally went to sit down, but many people around her whispered in discussion.","Halfway through the banquet, many guests wanted to go out to freshen up, or go to the back garden to relax.","\"The back garden of the Duke of Chen's estate is unique in the entire capital. Second only to the Imperial Garden,\" someone said.","In the area close to the imperial city, where land was worth its weight in gold, the Duke of Chen's estate occupied an entire street, and the back garden was as large as an ordinary family's entire residence.","Some guests who hadn't seen it wanted to take a stroll.","The guests invited today included not only female relatives but also unmarried noblemen from various families—most banquets in the capital were for socializing; and one of the purposes of socializing was \"matchmaking.\"","Unmarried noblemen with good reputations were often invited to the Peach Blossom Banquet and the Spring Exploration Banquet.","Of course, this wasn't for the noble young ladies to look at, but for the titled madames to observe.","To look at their character, appearance, conversational skills, and so on.","The Grand Princess's son also came today.","The Grand Princess even asked Cheng Zhao, \"Are there any sisters from your family coming as guests?\"","\"I was busy today and didn't invite my cousins,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","Cheng Zhao had four uncles in her family.","She didn't have any younger sisters from concubines, but she had several younger cousins, two of whom had already reached the age of hairpinning and were in the process of discussing marriage.","\"Another day, I'll invite them to play at the Princess's estate, and you should come too,\" the Grand Princess smiled.","She had already set her sights on the girls of the Cheng family, thinking she could pick one to be her daughter-in-law.","Cheng Zhao joked with her for a few words.","Then, as others wanted to stroll in the back garden, Cheng Zhao continued to accompany them.","Feeling a bit tired, the soles of her shoes had stepped on the mud in the back garden and felt very heavy, so she ordered the maid Qiubai to fetch a pair of shoes to change into.","While Cheng Zhao was resting in the pavilion by the lake, the siblings Sun Zhiya and Sun Zhisheng rushed over.","\"...You made my Gale run away. Send someone to find it right now!\" Sun Zhiya pointed angrily at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao blinked: \"Cousin, are you talking about that scorpion?\"","\"Exactly!\"","\"As a noble lady, you bring a scorpion when you go out as a guest. I suppose your mother must be very happy about that?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Her younger brother Sun Zhisheng took a step forward: \"Stop threatening my sister! You harmed my sister's beloved pet, you have to pay for it.\"","\"I didn't see any beloved pet.\"","\"That kind of scorpion is hard to buy even with ten thousand pieces of gold. If you don't find it, don't even think I'll let you off,\" Sun Zhiya said.","Cheng Zhao was about to say something when she saw the brothers Zhou Yuanshen and Zhou Yuanqi walking into the back garden.","They probably just came back, and their grandmother asked them to entertain guests in the back.","Zhou Yuanshen saw Cheng Zhao first and strode over; Zhou Yuanqi hurriedly trotted to keep up, his short legs making him look a bit awkward in front of his brother.","\"You bully your own sister-in-law, and you bully your relatives. Your character is malicious!\" Sun Zhisheng said. \"If you don't find my sister's beloved pet, I'll go out and say you stole my sister's thing. We'll see how...\"","\"What did you say? Who stole something?\" Behind them, Zhou Yuanqi frowned and asked.","The Sun siblings were facing away from the pavilion entrance, and when they turned around together, their legs instantly gave way.","\"Cousin.\"","\"Cousin, we just...\"","\"Call him the Duke!\" Zhou Yuanqi's tender little face was stern. \"No manners, making a fool of yourselves.\"","Without waiting for them to answer, \"What were you saying just now? You bullied my third sister-in-law, and you want to slander her?\"","\"...She let my sister's beloved pet escape.\" Sun Zhisheng wasn't one to be pushed around easily either. After a momentary panic, he immediately puffed out his chest.","He had heard his parents say that the second branch of the Duke of Chen's estate only inherited the title through good luck. If the people of the first branch were all alive, they would have been separated and become a collateral branch, and in the future, they wouldn't have the right to associate with a noble house like the Sun family.","What was Zhou Yuanqi so proud of?","\"What beloved pet?\" Zhou Yuanqi asked. \"Explain clearly, how did it escape, and what is it?\"","Sun Zhiya's face stiffened: \"Forget it, I won't pursue it.\"","\"You won't pursue it and that's it? You spoke wildly in front of my sister-in-law, did you apologize?\" Zhou Yuanqi asked.","He then looked at Zhou Yuanshen, \"Third Brother, did you hear that?\"","Cheng Zhao had been holding back her laughter all along.","The child was so beautiful, and his aggressive appearance was particularly amusing.","\"Kneel down and kowtow, and this matter will be dropped,\" Zhou Yuanshen said slowly.","Sun Zhiya and her younger brother, Sun Zhisheng, were completely stunned.","\"Why should I? Don't push things too far!\" Sun Zhisheng snapped back to his senses, flying into a rage.","The moment the words left his mouth, Zhou Yuanshen realized the boy had no intention of quietly apologizing. Grabbing him by the collar, Zhou Yuanshen hurled him straight into the nearby artificial lake.","Sun Zhisheng was fifteen this year. Though skinny, he was quite tall. Yet, Zhou Yuanshen tossed him as easily and smoothly as if he were throwing a pillow.","Sun Zhiya watched, dumbfounded.","Then, Zhou Yuanshen shifted his gaze to her. His pitch-black eyes were downright terrifying, closing in on her like the chilling edge of an unsheathed blade."]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69: Call Me Duchess","paragraphs":["Sun Zhiya backed away in fear.","She leaned against the pillar of the pavilion, trembling uncontrollably, \"You, you dare to push me down. Great-Aunt will not spare you.\"","Zhou Yuanqi snapped back to his senses.","He was just shocked by the reckless fellow's casual wave of the hand.","When the reckless fellow was showing off, he actually had the heroic bearing of a military general.","Not bad, fit to be his brother.","—Temporarily cross off a few from the list of live-in sons-in-law for his fairy-like sister-in-law, leaving only the Prince of Andong. The reckless fellow still needed to be observed for future performance.","\"If I pushed you down, and you clung to the Lord Duke, who would be at a disadvantage?\" Cheng Zhao smiled and spoke up. \"Hurry up and pull your brother up, the water is cold.\"","She added, \"He's too playful, actually falling into the water.\"","Sun Zhiya bit her lip fiercely.","She didn't dare to glare at Zhou Yuanshen, so she stared at Cheng Zhao, bullying the weak and fearing the strong.","The artificial lake wasn't deep, but it was almost submerging Sun Zhisheng's head.","He shouted loudly, \"Help!\"","Cheng Zhao then said to Zhou Yuanshen, \"Lord Duke, let's retreat, lest we be seen and people gossip that you didn't save someone in danger, which would be detrimental to your reputation.\"","\"Mm.\"","The three of them left by another path, turned past a rockery, and disappeared from the side of the artificial lake. Only shouting could be heard from afar.","Zhou Yuanqi was still dissatisfied. \"Third Brother, why didn't you throw that woman down too? She's so arrogant.\"","Not only arrogant, but also unyielding.","Cheng Zhao then said, \"If she gets all wet and we see her in a disheveled state, can you take responsibility or can I? Only the Lord Duke can take responsibility.\"","Zhou Yuanqi, \"Who wants to look?\"","\"The world wants to look. People love to watch this kind of wicked spectacle. You are still young and don't understand the sinister nature of human hearts,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi, \"...\"","The most sinister human heart is probably tucked in your own chest, right?","The three of them walked back along another path. Zhou Yuanqi and Cheng Zhao bickered, neither admitting defeat. Zhou Yuanshen walked behind them, listening in silence.","\"...In short, they are the maternal relatives of Grandmother. Yielding to them a little is out of respect for Grandmother,\" Cheng Zhao educated Zhou Yuanqi.","Zhou Yuanqi rolled his eyes. \"You didn't yield to them either.\"","\"I did. But they pushed their luck,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi, \"If we didn't come, could you have handled them?\"","\"Naturally.\"","\"Be careful not to bite your tongue making big boasts,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao, \"You are not even nine years old, yet so long-winded. How will you turn out in the future? You probably won't even be able to get a wife.\"","Zhou Yuanqi, \"...\"","Hearing his wife defeat his younger brother twice in a row, Zhou Yuanshen finally spoke up, \"Go back to the flower hall to entertain the guests, lest Grandmother sends someone to look for you if you're gone too long.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","Zhou Yuanshen added, \"Come to Chenhui Courtyard later, rest a bit before going back.\"","A lot of things instantly flashed through Cheng Zhao's mind.","But with her brother-in-law right in front of her, and this child being too sharp, she agreed without hesitation, \"Alright.\"","She then asked Zhou Yuanqi, \"Do you want to go with me?\"","\"No. I have already seen Grandmother, and now I need to go back and practice calligraphy,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","They really just came to find Cheng Zhao.","It was Zhou Yuanshen who wanted to find Cheng Zhao, and Zhou Yuanqi tagged along.","By the time Cheng Zhao returned, the Dowager Madame had already heard about the incident in the back garden.","Sun Zhisheng was taken away to change clothes, and the Marchioness of Qingyuan hurriedly went to check on her son.","The room was full of guests, and some had already heard rumors, after all, Sun Zhiya had shouted loudly for people to pull her brother up.","But no one said anything.","When the Dowager Madame's grandnephew came as a guest, whether he playfully fell into the water himself or was pushed down by someone, it was not appropriate to bring it up and ruin the Dowager Madame's mood.","Except for the minor commotion caused by the two Sun children, the entire banquet was very lively, and both hosts and guests enjoyed themselves.","The titled ladies all praised the two young madams of the Zhou family.","Someone mentioned Cheng Zhao and tentatively asked the Dowager Madame, \"In the future, will this be the Third Young Madam, or the Second Young Madam?\"","During the New Year, rumors had spread from the Chen Duke's estate about a dual-lineage inheritance.","Cheng Zhao was currently the Third Young Madam because Zhou Yuanshen was the Third Young Master; if the dual-lineage inheritance took place, Huan Qingtang would be the primary, and Cheng Zhao would rank second, so she could also be called the \"Second Young Madam,\" following Huan Qingtang's ranking.","This question could be taken in different ways.","If the Dowager Madame was displeased, she could say the ranking remained unchanged, and stability was best; if the dual-lineage inheritance was to become a reality, they could pretend to congratulate Cheng Zhao on moving up a rank.","The Dowager Madame's expression was unreadable, showing neither joy nor anger.","But Cheng Zhao spoke up before her, \"I am the Duchess.\"","She smiled and added, \"Madam Feng, you can just call me 'Duchess'. You are busy with important matters and don't need to trouble yourself with remembering rankings.","I am the Duchess bestowed by Her Majesty the Empress. You will absolutely not go wrong addressing me this way.\"","She then asked the Dowager Madame, \"Isn't that right, Grandmother?\"","The Dowager Madame smiled amiably, \"Look at her, so eloquent, smart, and quick-witted. Of course, she is the Duchess titled by the imperial court.\"","Many titled ladies heard these words.","Upon leaving the Chen Duke's estate, it was inevitable that they would discuss Cheng Zhao.","\"She speaks very well. At first glance, the two young madams seem similar, equally beautiful and equally worldly-wise. Looking closer, Lady Huan is in favorable circumstances while Cheng Shi is in adverse ones, yet the two are evenly matched, with Cheng Shi even being slightly superior.\"","\"Cheng Shi is also a bit more beautiful. They all say Lady Huan is a beauty, and her reputation is widespread. She is indeed pretty, but standing next to Cheng Shi, she falls short.\"","\"How many families in the whole city can compare to the foundation of the Cheng family of Wu Commandery? She is also bestowed marriage by Her Majesty the Empress. Now that the Eastern Palace has a master, the status of the Empress and the Crown Prince is stable, and Cheng Shi's status rises along with it.\"","After this banquet, Cheng Zhao's position in the hearts of the titled ladies became a bit more solid.","Compared to the noble and elegant demeanor of the aristocratic Lady Huan, Cheng Zhao was more like a typical high-born noble lady, worldly-wise, sharp, and excellent at reading people.","High-born ladies found it easier to interact with someone like Cheng Zhao.","As for people like Huan Qingtang, the noblewomen felt a bit of awe and a bit of intimidation towards her. They were afraid of being polite to her face only to be despised as \"vulgar\" behind her back, always feeling inferior in front of her.","Over time, they wouldn't want to associate with her.","And among prominent families, frequent interaction and socializing were necessary.","The noblewomen still hoped Cheng Zhao would be the \"First Madam\" of the Chen Duke's estate, making it easier to deal with her in the future. They were all people of the same kind.","After the guests left, the Dowager Madame kept Madam Song, Cheng Zhao, and Huan Qingtang behind.","\"What happened with the falling into the water?\" the Dowager Madame asked Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao told the truth.","The Lord Duke threw him down.","The Dowager Madame silently drank her tea.","Madam Song and Huan Qingtang held their breath, not daring to make a sound.","After Cheng Zhao finished speaking, she also stood silently to the side.","\"...I will speak to the Lord Duke about this matter. Cheng Shi, you may go back first,\" the Dowager Madame said.","Cheng Zhao agreed and turned to leave briskly.","The Dowager Madame then said to the First Madam, Madam Song, \"You may go back too.\"","Only Huan Qingtang was left behind.","Madam Song glanced at Huan Qingtang.","This glance carried a hint of warning: no matter what the Dowager Madame said to her, she must report back to her mother-in-law and not overstep her bounds.","Madam Song bowed and took her leave, departing from Shou'an Courtyard together with Cheng Zhao.","The First Madam ignored Cheng Zhao, but Cheng Zhao spoke up, \"In front of Grandmother, neither First Aunt nor I have much face.","It's a pity the Duke's estate is too large and there are too many trivial matters, otherwise, Sister-in-law alone would be enough to manage the household. Why would our help be needed?\"","\"Cheng Shi, stop trying to sow discord...\"","\"Aunt, please take your time. I will be heading back now.\" Without waiting for her to finish, Cheng Zhao strode away.","She gave the First Madam no opportunity to retort.","The First Madam's words caught in her throat. Unable to swallow them down or spit them out, she felt utterly stifled.","Her anger burned furiously."]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70: Cheng Zhao Wants a Divorce","paragraphs":["Shou'an Courtyard was located at the westernmost part of the entire Duke's estate. One had to pass through Chengming Hall on the central axis to reach Chenhui Courtyard.","Cheng Zhao wore a rose-red short jacket woven with gold floral vines, paired with a long white silk skirt. Two jade pendants weighed down her waist, and she wore only a gold hairpin on her head.","To call her attire luxurious would be inaccurate, as it was simple in every aspect; yet to call it plain would also be wrong, for it was so dazzlingly beautiful that one could hardly look away.","As she walked into Chenhui Courtyard, it was as if she had brought the evening glow into the side room. The sunlight reflected off her gold hairpin, bathing the room in a brilliant radiance.","Zhou Yuanshen lifted his eyes to look at her, set down his book, and said to Nanfeng outside the curtain, Serve tea.","Nanfeng complied.","Soon, he brought in two cups of hot tea.","Cheng Zhao picked up one cup and handed it to Zhou Yuanshen first before taking the other for herself.","...How was the banquet today? Zhou Yuanshen did not drink the tea; his quiet gaze fell upon her face.","Cheng Zhao replied, Just as you saw, it was only those two ignorant children from the Sun family who were provoked into causing trouble. Nothing else happened; everyone was very polite.","She added, All the guests, except for Grand Princess Fukang, came to curry favor with the Zhou family. Who would dare to cause a scene?","Zhou Yuanshen picked up his tea and began to drink.","He seemed to finish it in one gulp.","Seeing that his teacup was empty, Cheng Zhao asked, Would the Duke like some more tea?","The side room featured a large heated brick bed by the window, with several chairs arranged nearby. There was also a folding screen that blocked the view from outside the curtain. Behind the screen stood a table and a long couch for resting.","Usually, a thermos of hot water would be placed on the table.","Cheng Zhao glanced in that direction.","There was a window behind the screen, but it was closed. The light there was dimmer compared to this side, making it hard to see clearly if there was a thermos on the table.","The servant boy Nanfeng ran around all day; his main duty wasn't serving tea and water here anyway.","As these thoughts flashed through Cheng Zhao's mind, Zhou Yuanshen spoke, Alright.","He pushed his teacup toward her.","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","Sometimes a wife had to pour tea for her husband; it was nothing out of the ordinary, just a standard duty.","Thinking this, Cheng Zhao slipped on her shoes, stepped down from the brick bed, and walked around the screen.","Sure enough, there was a thermos on the table.","To her surprise, it actually contained hot water.","Before her hand could touch the thermos, a dark shadow loomed behind her.","Cheng Zhao instinctively turned her head. Zhou Yuanshen had actually followed her and was standing silently right behind her.","She furrowed her brows slightly.","She thought, if you were going to pour the tea yourself, why did you order me to do it?","Looking closely at him again, she noticed something was different.","His eyes were very bright, especially in the dim light. There was no extra expression on his face, but his eyes seemed to be tinged with fire.","In their half-year of marriage, Cheng Zhao had seen this look on him twice before.","He was like a furnace about to erupt. When untouched, it was a quiet stove; but upon contact, one would realize how scalding hot it was, burning fiercely on the inside.","Panic gripped Cheng Zhao, and she turned to dodge away.","She instinctively tried to hide, but just as she turned, Zhou Yuanshen had already trapped her in his arms.","Cheng Zhao braced her hands against the tabletop to keep from falling back onto it, while he leaned in and captured her lips.","...My Lord Duke, it's the middle of the afternoon! Cheng Zhao was pinned so tightly she couldn't move.","If she shoved him, her arms would lose their support, and he would press her onto the table. If she kept supporting herself, he would just press against her and kiss her, leaving her at his mercy.","She turned her head away and barely managed to utter a word before he cupped her face again.","Unable to care about anything else, Cheng Zhao freed one hand to push him.","In her desperation, she blurted out, Zhou Yuanshen, you can't do this here again...","He caught her hand, his body continuously pressing down on hers, determined to bend her backward over the edge. Why can't I? Cheng Zhao, you can try to convince me.","This is the study! Cheng Zhao gritted her teeth, but she felt her waist growing weak.","As he kissed her, waves of warmth washed over her. Her hands, her waist, everything felt like it was melting into water, unable to hold out against the current situation.","I want to, he said in a low voice. His brows and eyes remained still, and there was no smugness at the corners of his lips. Amidst this calm, his eyes burned even brighter, like a cluster of flames.","His breath grew even more scorching.","He held onto Cheng Zhao's hand and moved to untie her sash.","Cheng Zhao still wanted to struggle, but he had already loosened her hair bun. The gold dangling hairpin was removed, and her dark hair cascaded over her shoulders, with one strand falling across her eyes.","The arm supporting her lost its strength, and her defenses completely crumbled.","Zhou Yuanshen supported the back of her head, pressing Cheng Zhao down onto the table. With a loud crash, the thermos and the teacups all fell to the floor.","The water from the thermos trickled down from the table, and Cheng Zhao could hear the pattering sound of it.","Zhou Yuanshen...","Hmm? He stroked her cheek and lowered his head to kiss her lips again.","Can you... she tried to speak between their touching lips.","Suddenly, there was a knock on the door.","It was a woman's voice, somewhat familiar. My Lord Duke.","It was the maid from Zhou Yuanshen's outer study. Cheng Zhao remembered her; her name was Mingyu.","My Lord Duke, your subordinate has something to report. It is an urgent message from the Northwest, Mingyu's voice came from outside the door.","Cheng Zhao dared not move an inch. She held her breath, waiting for Zhou Yuanshen to leave her.","Zhou Yuanshen straightened up slightly, his lips leaving hers, but his feet did not move a single step.","Shockingly, he said, Come in and speak.","Cheng Zhao abruptly widened her eyes.","She sat up, but couldn't sit completely straight, propping herself up halfway with both hands.","Her dark hair cascaded down her back like a waterfall, draping over her smooth shoulders and revealing skin as white as snow.","The stark contrast between her black hair and snowy skin made Zhou Yuanshen's breathing grow significantly heavier.","Outside the screen, Mingyu seemed to hesitate for a moment. My Lord Duke?","Speak, Zhou Yuanshen commanded.","Cheng Zhao dared not move.","A buzzing sound filled her ears.","The window by the large brick bed was open, and the sunlight streamed in from there. From behind the screen, Cheng Zhao could see Mingyu's shadow.","Mingyu stood at the doorway, still some distance away from the screen.","She was reporting something about official horses, but Cheng Zhao couldn't hear a single word clearly because the noise in her own ears was too loud.","Zhou Yuanshen had not stopped.","His breathing, her own racing heartbeat—Cheng Zhao heard them with absolute clarity.","My Lord Duke, your subordinate has finished reporting. Should I ask the advisors to wait at the General's Manor for you to discuss this? Mingyu asked.","Alright, go... make the arrangements first. I will head over after dinner, Zhou Yuanshen said.","Mingyu left. Cheng Zhao didn't even hear the sound of the door closing; she could no longer hear any noises from the outside.","For a moment, Cheng Zhao's mind went completely blank.","Zhou Yuanshen carried her to the long couch. Just as he tried to straighten her clothes, Cheng Zhao reached out and slapped him across the face.","Her hand carried quite a bit of force, leaving her palm numb.","Zhou Yuanshen froze for a moment. He slowly raised his eyes, his dark gaze landing on her face.","Tears were already streaming down Cheng Zhao's face.","I want a divorce! she told him in a calm voice, letting her tears flow freely."]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71: Kiss Her Hand","paragraphs":["The side room fell quiet for a moment.","Cheng Zhao's tears flowed even more fiercely, blurring her vision.","Zhou Yuanshen froze for a moment, then forcefully grabbed her hand.","Cheng Zhao tried to pull her hand back.","What right did he have to fight back, what right did he have to try and break her hand?","Instead, he gently kissed her hand.","Cheng Zhao suddenly widened her eyes.","Outside, the sun was shifting westward. The light inside the room was already dim, and it was even darker behind the folding screen.","This man was rigid, cold, and had an unreasonable aloofness about him; those eyes held no warmth whatsoever.","Yet, the things he did contradicted this completely.","Cheng Zhao's anger also peaked at this very moment.","\"I want a divorce!\" Her voice rose. \"It works out perfectly since you are about to take on the duty of marrying your widowed sister-in-law. You can just marry another woman who will let you manipulate her as you please, and everyone will be happy.\"","The only person she felt sorry for was her mother-in-law.","Cheng Zhao had confidently promised her mother-in-law, telling her to stand by her side and that she would help her turn her life around.","Her mother-in-law had kept her promise and taken good care of Cheng Zhao recently.","Her father-in-law was also a good person, gentle, kind, and amiable. Her brother-in-law could be infuriating at times, but fortunately, he was still young, and Cheng Zhao could easily handle him.","If it weren't for Zhou Yuanshen, perhaps Cheng Zhao would have hit the jackpot and found herself a wonderful marriage.","Alas, fate never allowed anyone to have it all perfectly.","\"Cheng Zhao.\" Zhou Yuanshen pinched her chin, lifting her face with a slight force. \"If you want a divorce, why are you crying?\"","\"Those are two different things.\"","\"Our marriage was bestowed by the Empress. If you divorce, will the Ministry of Rites agree? Will the Empress be willing? And what about your maiden family, will they agree?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked softly.","Cheng Zhao forcefully shook off his hand. \"You can't threaten me. Don't think that only your Zhou family is powerful; the Cheng family isn't to be trifled with either!\"","She stood up to leave.","As she walked past the folding screen, she realized her clothes were still messy and her hair was disheveled.","A sense of grievance overwhelmed her once more.","Standing there, she felt her life was just as wretched as this moment.","Wretchedness was present at every moment. She wasn't living much more decently than her third sister; she was just better at pretending.","Zhou Yuanshen followed her and adjusted her sash. Using his fingers as a comb, he gathered her hair into a low bun and pinned her gold buyao ornament in place.","His movements were not entirely skilled, pulling at Cheng Zhao's scalp until it hurt, but at least she was presentable enough to go outside.","Cheng Zhao pulled open the door of the side room.","Reaching the doorway, she said to Zhou Yuanshen, \"I don't want to see you ever again. You don't need to treat me as the Duchess, and I don't want any heirs.\"","She walked out.","Cheng Zhao walked all the way back to Nonghua Courtyard without any maidservants following her.","The evening glow was beautiful, hanging over the distant rooftops and treetops. Sparrows were startled into flight, rustling the newly budded branches.","Cheng Zhao strolled along.","Nightfall descended right at this moment.","As pitch-black darkness enveloped her, she was startled to realize there was a light behind her.","She immediately turned her head.","Zhou Yuanshen was carrying a lantern, following her from a moderate distance.","Cheng Zhao then thought about how her grandfather used to lament the unpredictability of the world and how things often went contrary to one's wishes. She hadn't understood it back then, being young and having limited experience.","Even being bestowed a marriage didn't quite go against Cheng Zhao's wishes, as she had always hoped to earn a noble title and marry into a prestigious family.","But in reality, what could she control?","The sun rose in the east and set in the west. No matter how angry or unwilling she was, the setting sun went down without any alteration, and the dark night took over.","Her feelings and dignity from before were very important; nothing was worth sacrificing them.","Cheng Zhao decided she needed to get far away from the Duke of Chen's mansion.","She would have to break her promise to her mother-in-law. In the future, when her two brothers-in-law were ready for marriage, Cheng Zhao might help out and choose two good daughters-in-law for her mother-in-law.","Her mother-in-law was so straightforward and kind; she deserved to enjoy her twilight years in peace.","Other than that, this place was not worth Cheng Zhao lingering around.","She didn't look back again.","The light behind her kept illuminating her path. She walked faster and faster, trying to shake him off, but the man was tall with long legs and could easily keep up with her.","When Cheng Zhao returned to Nonghua Courtyard, the light behind her disappeared.","She ordered the courtyard doors to be closed.","A maid took a glance, seemingly unable to make out who the retreating figure was, and simply shut the doors tight.","Nanny Li and the others were about to ask questions, but Cheng Zhao told them to prepare hot water first.","After her bath, Suyue wiped her down. Seeing the red marks on her back, she felt both heartache and worry. \"Were you bitten by something?\"","Disbelievingly, she added, \"Could it be that scorpion?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","The surface of the desk in the study had been too hard; even with clothes cushioning her, she had suffered quite a bit.","She shook her head. \"Don't worry, I wasn't bitten.\"","Suyue: \"Should I get some ointment to rub on it? And perhaps brew some medicine to clear out internal toxins for you to drink?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"Neither is necessary.\"","She added, \"Hurry and order the meal to be served. I'm so hungry.\"","Once she had sorted out her thoughts, Cheng Zhao felt completely relaxed, and suddenly her stomach began to rumble with hunger.","Leaving the Duke's mansion and giving up her title as a noble lady, who was to say she wouldn't have a bright future? Even if she didn't, she might at least be saving her own life.","Fate was preordained.","The year before last, she had taken Qiubai and Suyue out to play. At a temple fair, they came across a rather deserted fortune-telling stall, and she had her fortune told.","The fortune-teller said she was destined for immense wealth and honor, a nobility beyond words, even boasting that she was the reincarnation of a golden phoenix.","Her mother had said the fortune-teller only spouted nonsense because he saw Cheng Zhao's fine clothes and figured she would give him a good tip.","Cheng Zhao had retorted, asking which fortune-teller didn't spout nonsense? She liked what this man had to say, so she was happy to reward him. She had given him a two-tael gold ingot.","For dinner, Cheng Zhao ate more than half a bowl of rice. She then took a stroll in the courtyard, chatting with Nanny Li about the various events of the day's banquet, before finally going to sleep.","Exhausted, Cheng Zhao fell fast asleep.","The next day, Cheng Zhao woke up early and went to Chengming Hall as usual to ask for leave from the First Madam, Madam Song, and Huan Qingtang, saying she needed to visit her maiden home.","The atmosphere in Chengming Hall was unpleasant.","The First Madam, Madam Song, was unhappy, though it wasn't directed at Cheng Zhao.","She just said sarcastically, \"Always thinking about going back, your heart has gone wild. Where is your real home?\"","Cheng Zhao replied, \"A place where we can be the masters of our own house is the true home for noble ladies like us, isn't that right, First Aunt?\"","Madam Song's face twisted slightly.","She was the Duchess, but she couldn't call the shots, even though she had been married into the Zhou family for over twenty years.","Her emotions were too complicated; the First Madam waved her hand, telling Cheng Zhao to go on ahead.","Huan Qingtang sat to the side, not saying a word.","Cheng Zhao then went to inform the Old Madam.","This time she didn't see the Old Madam in person. A maid said the Old Madam was praying to Buddha and that Cheng Zhao only needed to inform the First Madam.","Only then did Cheng Zhao head out.","The gatekeeper arranged a few gifts for her. Upon arriving back, Cheng Zhao went straight to see her mother.","A steward was reporting to her mother.","Waiting until noon, after having lunch with her mother, Cheng Zhao finally said, \"I want a divorce.\"","Her mother slowly raised her eyes. \"I heard many people praised you at the Duke of Chen's peach blossom banquet yesterday. What, you won and you're still not happy?\"","\"It has nothing to do with that,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Her mother replied, \"Admitting defeat isn't like you. Tell me about it.\"","\"I don't want to talk about it. Anyway, I want a divorce. I'll go talk to Grandfather and ask him to mediate for me,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Her mother nodded slightly. \"Go ahead.\""]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72: Smooth to the Point of Being Unpleasant","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao waited for her grandfather to return from the morning court session.","She got straight to the point and brought up the matter.","Her grandfather chuckled while sipping his tea. Have you thought it through?","Yes.","Let us first discuss the difficulty of this matter. Your marriage was bestowed by the Empress. If you seek a divorce, it would be a slap in her face and a blow to her dignity, her grandfather said.","He added, The Empress is the Emperor's wife, which means this also concerns the dignity of the imperial family. Not only would the Empress have to agree, but the Emperor must also give his nod of approval.","You have read so many books, and the imperial censors have never won a debate against you. You can quote the classics and cite historical precedents, drawing from legal codes, folk customs, and worldly wisdom. You can find the reasoning to help me, as long as you want to, Cheng Zhao said.","Her grandfather smiled. This matter is indeed difficult, and not just because of the Emperor. For a bestowed marriage, if you want a divorce, you must offer them a way to save face.","A way to save face?","The elders of both families must submit memorials to the throne, requesting the Emperor and Empress to approve your divorce. The head of the Duke of Chen's estate is the Duke of Chen. Would he be willing to submit this memorial on your behalf? her grandfather asked.","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","This matter is fraught with difficulties. If there is a second solution, I do not approve of you taking this path, her grandfather said.","He then asked her, Has it truly come to this? Tell me what happened. Is it about the dual inheritance?","No.","Rest assured about the dual inheritance. I will block it at the front; I will not let the Emperor issue an imperial decree to bestow a marriage for that. If the Emperor really does so, this time I can quote the classics on your behalf and make the imperial censors argue for more than three months, her grandfather said.","Cheng Zhao smiled.","You can still smile, so it does not seem like you are at a dead end, her grandfather said.","He sighed, At your age, you have not experienced much. A small cut on your finger feels like the sky is falling. When you get a little older, if your right hand is broken this morning, you will learn to eat with your left hand by tomorrow morning.","Cheng Zhao was horrified. That is a terrifying way to put it.","Ask your parents if this is not how all adults get through life. How many storms have you weathered? Let alone anything else, you have not even gone hungry, her grandfather laughed.","Cheng Zhao sighed.","Her grandfather asked, You will not tell me? If you have been wronged, you should speak up.","It is useless to say it. Did you not just say that even a broken hand is useless? Cheng Zhao said.","Her grandfather smiled. Even so, you should try to solve whatever can be solved.","Cheng Zhao remained silent.","She did not say anything else and returned to the Duke of Chen's estate.","Later, her grandfather summoned his eldest son and eldest daughter-in-law to ask about Cheng Zhao's situation.","Cheng Zhao's father had not seen his daughter and did not know; her mother had heard about it but was also completely baffled.","...Zhao Zhao has always been resourceful. She would not ask for a divorce unless she was truly suffering. She did not tell you, perhaps because it is something too difficult to speak of. Ask her again, her grandfather said to Cheng Zhao's mother.","First Madam Cheng said, She will not tell me either. I will have her eldest sister go ask; the two sisters can talk more easily.","Her grandfather gave a slight nod.","Cheng Zhao returned to the Duke of Chen's estate, paid her respects around the household as if nothing had happened, and then returned to her room.","She sent someone to deliver a message to the palace.","Two days later, Her Majesty the Empress indeed summoned her to the palace.","The maids at Nonghua Courtyard brought out Cheng Zhao's formal mandate attire. Dressed and made up according to her rank, she took a carriage into the palace.","At Kunning Palace, she ran into the Empress's niece from her maiden family, Guo Hanzhang.","Guo Hanzhang did not have a good reputation in the capital. She was famously fierce and unruly, and many noble ladies had suffered at her hands.","Cheng Zhao had not met Guo Hanzhang when she was little; later, she followed her father to his official post for a few years. After returning to the capital, her mother kept her at home, forbidding her from socializing in order to temper her character and teach her etiquette.","This was her first time meeting Guo Hanzhang.","However, they had both heard of each other.","...What made you think of visiting me? the Empress asked Cheng Zhao with a smile. Is there something the matter?","She added, It is not appropriate for me to interfere much in the affairs of the Duke of Chen's estate. His Majesty has always respected and loved the Dowager Madame above all others.","The implication was clear: if you are trying to stop the Duke of Chen from taking a dual-inheritance wife, do not come to me. I cannot help you. The Dowager Madame has more face before the Emperor than I do.","I made a scented pouch and prayed for a peace amulet at Jin'an Temple, which I wished to present to Your Majesty. Spring has arrived, and as the deities descend to the mortal realm, I feared Your Majesty might accidentally offend a spirit while admiring the flowers. This item can ensure your safety. I brought it especially as a small token of my devotion, Cheng Zhao said.","Empress Guo was a little surprised. You are very thoughtful.","She looked closely at Cheng Zhao's embroidery and praised it repeatedly, even showing it to her sister-in-law and her niece, Guo Hanzhang.","Madam Guo also praised it.","If Hanzhang spent some time on needlework, I would be relieved, Madam Guo added.","Guo Hanzhang's face instantly darkened.","Madam Guo was still dissatisfied and continued, Her stitches are not even steady.","Empress Guo just smiled and did not chime in.","But she also did not like hearing her sister-in-law complain about her niece.","My mother also rarely does needlework; managing the household always keeps her exceptionally busy. When my grandmother was alive, she never criticized my mother's embroidery, Cheng Zhao said.","She did not say her mother's embroidery was bad, only that being good at needlework was not particularly meaningful.","No matter how much society demanded women to be skilled in needlework, there were actually very few occasions where it was truly needed.","Your grandmother was tolerant, Madam Guo smiled.","With your excellent judgment and keen eyes, and with Her Majesty the Empress keeping watch, the in-laws chosen for Miss Guo in the future will surely have a very tolerant and gentle mother-in-law, Cheng Zhao smiled.","She was signaling to Madam Guo to look at the Empress's expression and stop talking.","Upon hearing this, Madam Guo indeed looked at the Empress and immediately smiled. The wife of the Duke of Chen truly has a clever tongue. Her words have made me feel much more at ease, and I am not so worried anymore.","Everyone outside says she has a clever tongue; Grand Princess Fukang loves listening to her speak the most, the Empress said. Do not worry too much. Children have their own destinies.","The topic was successfully changed.","Guo Hanzhang glanced at Cheng Zhao.","This glance carried a hint of interest.","Cheng Zhao really knew how to speak and read the room, managing to control the situation perfectly.","Such a person was considered very slick and not particularly likable. At least, Guo Hanzhang did not quite like her.","But with her around, the atmosphere was indeed very pleasant. Therefore, she was popular most of the time and could reap the benefits.","Is not the Cheng family a scholarly household? How come her glib tongue makes her seem like she comes from a merchant background? Guo Hanzhang thought to herself.","She lazily shifted her gaze away.","Empress Guo had received Cheng Zhao's pouch, and her mood, which had nearly been ruined by her sister-in-law's complaining, had been salvaged by Cheng Zhao.","Therefore, after the Guo mother and daughter left, Empress Guo kept Cheng Zhao behind alone and asked her the purpose of her visit.","I just wanted to see you, Cheng Zhao said.","She had a request, but she could not say it outright; she needed the Empress to guess it.","Those in power do not like being made demands of; they only like to figure things out themselves and bestow favors as a reward.","If you do not tell me, then I will not be able to help you, Empress Guo smiled.","It is really nothing. It is because of your bestowed marriage that I was able to become a duchess. I dare not forget this kindness and ought to come serve you often. But I also feared disturbing you, so I have not dared to come pay my respects frequently, Cheng Zhao said.","Empress Guo said, You are a first-rank duchess. Requesting an edict to visit me is proper etiquette. Come often in the future.","Cheng Zhao said yes.","She did not say anything else.","She was merely observing, looking for an opportunity.","Just as her grandfather had said, the root of the problem lay in the bestowed marriage.","As for how to proceed, Cheng Zhao would have to play it by ear. At this stage, the path to a divorce was completely blocked, without a sliver of hope in sight.","She would have to plan it slowly and carefully.","With the heir to the throne officially appointed and her husband serving as the Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince, the political landscape was much clearer than before. Cheng Zhao's growing closeness to Empress Guo was no longer considered a sensitive matter; rather, it was a relationship she now needed to carefully cultivate."]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73: Don't Let Mother Know","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao emerged from the Kunning Palace and returned to the Duke of Chen's mansion.","Nanny Fan, her mother-in-law's trusted servant, was sitting idly in the Nonghua Courtyard.","Seeing her return, Nanny Fan smiled, \"Young Madam, it's good that you are back. Did something happen in the palace? The Second Madam has been worried all day.\"","Cheng Zhao replied, \"Nothing happened. I just went to visit Her Majesty the Empress and offer a peace charm. Nanny, please go back first and tell my mother to rest assured. I will come over after changing my clothes.\"","Nanny Fan checked her expression a few times.","After making sure she was fine, she went back to report.","The fact that Cheng Zhao took the initiative to submit a visiting card and request an audience with the Empress was known only to her and her confidants. It was not something to be broadcasted to everyone.","\"...Young Madam, why did you go to see the Empress?\" asked Nanny Li.","She knew Cheng Zhao had requested to enter the palace, but she didn't know her purpose.","Cheng Zhao hadn't even told her confidants about the conflict that erupted in the Chenhui Courtyard; as for her desire for a divorce, she hadn't breathed a word of it either.","It wasn't worth making everyone worry and feel down over something that hadn't even taken shape yet.","\"My marriage to the Duke of Chen was bestowed by the Empress. Going to pay my respects occasionally is the right thing to do. If I am living well, she will naturally feel gratified and might even reward me,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She added, \"It's not a bad thing to have another person to rely on. The Empress did help me get my title of mandate.\"","\"Then if you are not doing well, could you go and complain?\" Suyue asked with a smile.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"No. If the Empress truly felt guilty, I would be in trouble. Her guilt would only make her help me once. Over time, she would rather I didn't exist.\"","To maintain a long-lasting and good relationship, \"guilt\" cannot exist; it would be a thorn. Therefore, Cheng Zhao didn't go to complain.","Her grandfather had analyzed the many difficulties of getting a divorce with her.","If she couldn't link this matter to what the Empress feared most, the Empress would never slap her own face and agree to Cheng Zhao's divorce.","Cheng Zhao had to slowly look for an opportunity.","The maids helped her change clothes. She put on a casual pale lotus-root colored upper garment embroidered with interlocking branches and a plain white skirt. They simply tied her hair into a low bun, and Cheng Zhao went to the Jiangyun Courtyard to see her mother-in-law.","\"...During the Peach Blossom Banquet, Young Master Sun fell into the water. Grandmother is probably unhappy about it in her heart. I went to the Empress to find some backing,\" Cheng Zhao told the Second Madam.","The Second Madam said, \"The status of the Empress and the Crown Prince is only average; it is Grand Preceptor Guo who holds power over the court. Against the Old Madam, the Empress might not have a winning chance.\"","\"I'm not trying to go against the Old Madam,\" Cheng Zhao smiled. \"In social relations, you have to water the plants and pull the weeds regularly. You can't just beg her when you desperately need a favor.\"","The Second Madam was relieved.","She sighed, \"I am most afraid of social interactions, but you handle them with ease.\"","\"Everyone has their strengths and weaknesses,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","While the mother and daughter-in-law were talking, the porter outside announced that the maternal uncle had arrived.","The Second Madam said, \"It's your young uncle. Last time I sent someone with a message, asking him to look into something for me. He's probably here to report back.\"","She added, \"Quickly, invite him in.\"","Soon, Fan Xiao entered.","After greeting each other, the Second Madam ordered the maids to serve tea and hurriedly asked, \"Quick, tell me, what exactly happened to Yuanjin?\"","Fan Xiao smiled, \"Congratulations, Eldest Sister. Yuanjin did not become a captive.\"","The Second Madam let out a huge sigh of relief.","She said to Cheng Zhao, \"A few days ago, I received a letter saying Yuanjin went missing while on night patrol. They couldn't find him anywhere, and thought he might have been abducted by the Northern Di people.\"","Cheng Zhao said, \"Fortunately, that's not the case.\"","Fan Xiao said, \"Not only is it not the case, but the twelve men he led encountered a sneak attack unit. They fought against the odds but were then surrounded by hundreds of the enemy. To escape, he and his men fought fiercely for eight days and repelled them. Second Brother requested a merit reward, and the imperial court appointed Yuanjin as a Commandant.\"","The Second Madam seemed in disbelief, a mix of surprise and joy: \"Really?\"","\"It's the news Yuanshen found out. Second Brother requested the merit, and Yuanshen exerted effort in the court to secure this reward for Yuanjin,\" Fan Xiao said.","Tears of joy welled up in the Second Madam's eyes: \"Yuanshen didn't tell me.\"","\"He probably got the news a few days ago, but he might have been busy these past few days,\" Fan Xiao said.","After saying that, he glanced at Cheng Zhao, \"What has Yuanshen been busy with these days?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","The Second Madam also looked at Cheng Zhao.","\"The Duke of Chen has not been resting in the Nonghua Courtyard these past few days, and his whereabouts are unknown,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam said, \"He's probably resting in the outer study. Someone, go find the Duke.\"","Nanny Fan instructed a maid to pass the message.","Cheng Zhao really wanted to leave.","Taking advantage of the gap when the Second Madam and Fan Xiao were talking, she said, \"Mother, I just returned from the palace, and I'm quite exhausted right now. I'll go back and lie down first.\"","\"Eat before you go back. If you are tired, go to the kang in the side room and rest for a while. Drink some ginseng soup to replenish your energy,\" the Second Madam smiled. \"Dinner will be ready in half an hour.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","Fan Xiao looked at her curiously and smiled, \"Madam Duke, do you have time to visit the Pillar of State General's Mansion another day? My mother has been talking about you.\"","The Second Madam said, \"We can go back together. Zhaozhao, you come too. Your spearmanship is too flashy. Have your grandmother give you some pointers, and you will definitely benefit a lot.\"","Fan Xiao was a bit surprised: \"Madam Duke knows how to use a spear? I couldn't tell. Do the girls in your family have to learn spearmanship too?\"","Cheng Zhao smiled forcedly: \"I only learned a little bit of the basics.\"","\"Does every girl have to learn?\" Fan Xiao asked again.","Cheng Zhao: \"No, just me.\"","Because of this interruption, Cheng Zhao couldn't find an opportunity to decline visiting the Fan family, and the Second Madam and Fan Xiao finalized the matter.","Fan Xiao added, \"Bring Yuanqi along too. Mother only thinks about him. Out of all the children and grandchildren in the family, Yuanqi is her precious darling.\"","The Second Madam said, \"He is extremely boring. Only Mother still thinks about him. Who else likes him?\"","\"Yuanqi is quite interesting. He has read a lot of books and can scold people without using dirty words. Eldest Sister, you really can't imagine how he mocked me last time...\"","The siblings were solely focused on complaining about Zhou Yuanqi, and Cheng Zhao had no way to steer the conversation back.","She didn't even have a chance to stand up and take her leave.","Soon, a maid brought ginseng soup to Cheng Zhao. This was what the Second Madam drank every day, and she casually gave her a bowl.","After Cheng Zhao finished drinking, the Second Madam was very considerate: \"Go lie down and rest. You don't need to stand on ceremony in front of me.\"","Having accepted her hospitality, Cheng Zhao had no choice but to go to the side room.","Then, she heard that Zhou Yuanshen had arrived.","Cheng Zhao leaned against the bolster, keeping her head suspended to avoid messing up her hair bun, and closed her eyes to rest her spirit.","Someone gently touched her cheek.","She opened her eyes. Zhou Yuanshen was standing nearby. He wore a sky-blue kesi robe embroidered with cloud patterns and floral medallions, his face expressionless.","Cheng Zhao frowned and immediately shifted inward.","She wanted to distance herself from him, but it coincidentally made room for Zhou Yuanshen to sit down.","Zhou Yuanshen took the opportunity to sit.","Cheng Zhao immediately tried to get up.","Zhou Yuanshen said, \"I apologize to you. Don't let Mother know, or she will worry.\"","Cheng Zhao didn't want to say a single word to him.","\"What do you want me to do for you to let go of your anger?\" he asked again. \"Should I also go and burn incense to your Guanyin the Child-Bringer every day?\"","Cheng Zhao glared at him.","Bringing up the Guanyin the Child-Bringer again.","She didn't even care about having children anymore; she was currently looking for a chance to get a divorce."]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74: Zhou Yuanshen Seeks Peace","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao turned her head toward the window, remaining silent.","Zhou Yuanshen sat beside her and did not speak again either.","The two sat in silence.","Second Madam called from outside the curtain, Zhaozhao, do you have any dietary restrictions?","Restrictions on what?","Do you eat pork lung soup? Second Madam asked again.","Cheng Zhao: I do. I don't avoid that.","Only the brothers Yuanshen and Yuanqi don't eat it. Let's ignore them and make the soup as usual, Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao: ...","While speaking, she had turned her head back this way, and when she refocused, she met Zhou Yuanshen's gaze.","She looked away.","Zhou Yuanshen asked, What are your dietary restrictions?","We won't be dining together anyway, so the Lord Duke doesn't need to care, Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen fell silent.","After a long while, he finally said, Cheng Zhao, you cannot get a divorce.","Cheng Zhao could not help but feel a surge of fury.","I don't need to analyze it for you. You are a smart person and know the difficulties involved, he added. You will have to continue being the Duchess.","Nothing is impossible in this world. Do not underestimate me, Cheng Zhao said coldly.","Zhou Yuanshen: We can work together. Perhaps with our combined efforts, the Emperor will agree.","Cheng Zhao slowly turned her face toward him.","Zhou Yuanshen's eyes remained completely unrippled: This bestowed marriage was Grand Preceptor Guo's scheme to begin with. Now that Grand Preceptor Guo monopolizes the court, the Emperor hates him to the bone. When the net is finally drawn in the future, this marriage can serve as one of Grand Preceptor Guo's crimes, and then you will be free.","Cheng Zhao turned her face back.","She wasn't a little fool.","Annihilating a powerful noble faction was much harder than getting the Empress to go back on her word.","Eliminating such a behemoth could drag down the entire Chen Duke's estate, and even the Cheng family.","Cheng Zhao was unwilling to take that risk.","The Cheng family of Wu Commandery had an excellent reputation, and her grandfather enjoyed immense prestige throughout the world. Even if there truly was a change of dynasties, the new emperor's first act would be to curry favor with the Cheng family, needing her grandfather to endorse his legitimacy.","Cheng Zhao would not drag the entire Cheng clan into the struggle between the Emperor and the Guo family.","If Zhou Yuanshen was willing to be a blade, that was his business.","Cheng Zhao was neither stupid enough to be sweet-talked into forgetting herself, nor would she hypocritically humor him.","Therefore, she said, The Cheng family has no grudge against the Guo family, nor with the Emperor. Divorce is a private matter between you and me. I never agreed to conspire with you...","What divorce? someone suddenly asked from outside the window.","The voice was childish and milky.","Startled, Cheng Zhao subconsciously pushed open the window and saw Zhou Yuanqi standing beneath it, listening to their conversation.","She made a shushing gesture at him. Mother is in the outer room.","Zhou Yuanqi had pink, tender cheeks and pitch-black eyes, as exquisite as a carved porcelain doll. With the same cold and aloof expression as his older brother, he looked at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao whispered, Come inside quickly, Young Uncle is here too.","She closed the window again.","She let out a soft sigh.","Zhou Yuanshen hadn't said anything the whole time; he just watched her.","Cheng Zhao ignored him.","Zhou Yuanqi came in. Fan Xiao was teasing him, and the uncle and nephew were talking and laughing.","Cheng Zhao remained seated on the window-side kang. She pulled a resting pillow a bit closer and leaned back against it; she closed her eyes to doze off, paying no more attention to Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen pulled over another pillow and mimicked her posture, leaning back as well.","The two were silent.","Cheng Zhao, in a few days Concubine Mu will have her grounding lifted, Zhou Yuanshen suddenly said.","Cheng Zhao opened her eyes.","Mu Jiang's pregnancy was stable now. Carrying the first child of the Zhou family's next generation in her belly, she had the capital to stir up trouble; meanwhile, those two in Chengming Hall were very good at using others to do their dirty work, especially Lady Huan.","Cheng Zhao could well imagine that her situation was going to become increasingly difficult.","Without a divorce, she was still the Duchess.","Cheng Zhao could not accept herself being a downtrodden Madam; she needed to pull herself together.","Is the Lord Duke trying to say that from now on, you will frequently stay in Lijing Courtyard to accompany Concubine Mu, ensuring she safely gives birth to this child? Cheng Zhao asked.","Without waiting for Zhou Yuanshen to answer, she said, That is fine. You don't need to discuss this matter with me. I have no objections.","Zhou Yuanshen turned his head slightly to look at her: I have no intention of staying in Lijing Courtyard.","That is between you and her, Cheng Zhao said.","Cheng Zhao wanted to be the Duchess, wanted to live in Chengming Hall. Mu Jiang and her child were never stumbling blocks.","If pushing Zhou Yuanshen away could buy Mu Jiang's peace and quiet, Cheng Zhao was more than willing to do it.","Not having an heir for the time being didn't matter.","Zhou Yuanshen was silent for another long while before saying, How should I apologize to you? Can you tell me clearly?","Cheng Zhao did not want to forgive him.","If she told him how to apologize, it would be as if the matter was resolved and behind them.","In Cheng Zhao's heart, this hurdle could not be crossed. She did not want to silently accept the harm and pretend it didn't exist.","The Lord Duke does not need to apologize. Just get me the divorce papers, and we will be even, Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen stood up and walked out.","Cheng Zhao: ...","A breath caught in her throat; she was almost furious.","A moment later, her father-in-law returned, and the meal was set in the flower hall.","The pork lung soup was prepared very well, with two types of medicinal herbs added, making it refreshing and tender.","It's delicious, Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanqi looked disgusted. You are someone who has tasted black-bone chicken soup and sour radish duck soup. How can you bring yourself to praise such a vulgar thing?","It's not vulgar. It's very delicious, Cheng Zhao said. You should try some.","Even if I died, and had to choose between going to the eighteenth level of hell and drinking pork lung soup, you could come visit me in the eighteenth level of hell, Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao: You'd still care about vulgarity after dying? Truly a scholar, a great talent.","She added, My third sister would probably like it. She loves this kind of flavor the most.","Zhou Yuanqi looked at her.","Fan Xiao quietly raised his eyes but didn't answer, continuing to drink his soup.","Second Madam initially wanted to remind the two of them that bickering at the dining table was forbidden; but finding their banter amusing, she let it slide.","I don't believe she likes it, Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao: In a few days, we're all going out for a spring outing to fly kites in the suburbs. You can ask my third sister then.","Alright, Zhou Yuanqi said. We'll have people protect us. Call your fourth brother, and I'll arrange for others.","Fan Xiao chuckled. Yuanshen and I can protect you. There's no need to find anyone else.","We don't want you two! Zhou Yuanqi immediately retorted.","Zhou Yuanshen glanced at his younger brother.","His gaze was deeply meaningful.","Zhou Yuanqi thought that since his sister-in-law wanted a divorce, he better quickly kick this brute away so as not to lose her. Recruiting a live-in husband was an urgent matter.","If they brought the brute on the spring outing, what if his sister-in-law got upset?","Young Uncle was even worse. The man had a glib and wicked tongue; he would surely offend his sister-in-law and the heavenly talented lady.","...I have my own candidates, Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam was curious. Who are you choosing?","Mother, don't worry about it. You will thank me in the future, Zhou Yuanqi said.","Second Madam was completely baffled, thinking to herself, what kind of wretched son is this, spouting such nonsense?","Second Master didn't understand either, but he didn't need to understand.","Zhou Yuanshen said to the maid serving dishes beside them, Serve me a bowl of pork lung soup.","Everyone looked at him.","Including Zhou Yuanqi.","Zhou Yuanqi: You don't like drinking it.","I can try, Zhou Yuanshen said.","Zhou Yuanqi curled his lip: If you try it, I'll be the only one not drinking it, giving Mother another excuse to scold me.","Traitor!","When the soup was brought to him, Zhou Yuanshen picked it up. He sniffed it and put it down. A moment later, as if mustering his courage, he brought it to his lips but then put it down again.","Zhou Yuanqi sneered, If you don't like it, don't ask for it. What a waste.","Second Madam never forced her children, so she also said, If you don't want to drink it, then leave it.","Zhou Yuanshen, however, looked at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao refused to meet his eyes.","This was just a meal, not a test or a punishment from her. He could drink it or not as he pleased.","\"It is fine if you do not drink it,\" Fan Xiao said with a smile. \"You and the Duchess can agree to disagree and respect each other's dietary preferences. You can still grow old together just the same.\"","Zhou Yuanshen picked it up and took a sip."]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75: The Purchase of the Duke","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen finished the bowl of soup.","Showing no expression of distaste, he seemed to find it palatable after a taste and easily finished it all.","He even cast a glance at Zhou Yuanqi.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"Don't even think about persecuting me. I won't drink it.\"","\"You don't like drinking soup, and you don't like talking nonsense either, right?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked mildly.","Zhou Yuanqi thought to himself, he is actually threatening me!","What good would it do me to expose the fact that my sister-in-law wants a divorce?","And what harm would it do to The Brute?","He has plenty of women, but there is only one heavenly sister-in-law.","Zhou Yuanqi snorted.","Second Madam looked at one, then the other. \"What secrets are you two hiding, playing riddles right in front of me?\"","\"Nothing,\" the two brothers said in unison.","Second Madam: \"...\"","The bumps in her life were all birthed by her own womb. What a sin.","Fan Xiao loved this kind of liveliness the most, watching from the side with great interest; Second Master didn't care much about the children's conflicts, letting them bicker among themselves.","After the meal, the few of them chatted.","They mainly talked about the Fourth Young Master, Zhou Yuanjin, being promoted to Captain.","Cheng Zhao then said, \"Congratulations to Father and Mother. With this title, Fourth Brother's promotion to a general is just around the corner.\"","The rank of Captain was considered a watershed; it was incredibly difficult to cross this threshold.","The promotion of soldiers, without major military merits, would be stuck below the rank of Captain. Once appointed as a Captain, even without further military merits, one could eventually become a general just by accumulating seniority.","At such a young age, Zhou Yuanjin practically had his future secured in the bag.","Second Master and his wife were naturally very happy.","\"He had really good luck this time, a blessing in disguise,\" Second Master said.","Cheng Zhao: \"It is because he is brave and composed that he has such good fortune.\"","\"He does have some capability,\" Second Madam said.","Zhou Yuanqi didn't like his third brother, and he equally disliked his fourth brother.","He said, \"The Zhou family's ancestral graves must be smoking green, exclusively prospering military generals. the Hothead just picked up a huge bargain.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","One brother is The Brute, and the other is the Hothead. This younger brother is indeed very good at giving nicknames.","Second Madam knocked him on the forehead. \"Show some respect!\"","She added, \"Your fourth brother has established himself and achieved great things. What about you?\"","\"I'm still young,\" Zhou Yuanqi said. \"In the future, my fortune will be higher than both of theirs. Just you wait, Mother.\"","Second Madam was disdainful. \"Could you also become a Duke?\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...That was an inherited title, not something he earned himself. He is just a General Pacifying the West.\"","Fan Xiao laughed, \"Being the General Pacifying the West is not easy either. It was exchanged with a narrow escape from death.\"","Speaking of this, he looked at Cheng Zhao. \"Has the Duchess ever been to the General's Manor?\"","Cheng Zhao shook her head.","Zhou Yuanshen chimed in, \"I'll take you to see it next time. The place is quite small.\"","With everyone sitting there, Cheng Zhao had no choice but to agree.","It was getting late, and the various gates of the Chen Duke's Manor were about to be locked. Fan Xiao stood up to take his leave. Zhou Yuanshen walked Fan Xiao to the door.","Zhou Yuanqi, on the other hand, was going to walk Cheng Zhao back.","\"...Why did you and The Brute mention divorce?\" Zhou Yuanqi asked.","Cheng Zhao realized that she had no way to pour out her grievances to anyone.","Even in front of Zhou Yuanshen, she couldn't freely accuse him of his misdeeds, because she simply couldn't say the words out loud.","For the first time, Cheng Zhao was like a mute eating bitter herbs—suffering in silence.","It could be considered a new experience of hardship.","\"It was a joke,\" Cheng Zhao said to Zhou Yuanqi.","Zhou Yuanqi snorted, showing his disbelief. \"Forget it if you don't want to tell.\"","Arriving at the entrance of the Nonghua Courtyard, Zhou Yuanqi turned and left, clean and decisive.","Zhou Yuanshen walked Fan Xiao to the main entrance, arranged a carriage to send him off, and urged him not to ride a horse.","\"Are you and the Duchess at odds?\" Fan Xiao asked him.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"Yes.\"","\"Have you thought about how to resolve it?\" he asked.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"No.\"","\"Get in the carriage. Let's find a place to drink, and I will carefully strategize for you,\" Fan Xiao laughed.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"Little Uncle cannot help with this matter.\"","\"You underestimate me.\"","\"Little Uncle has no wife in his room. When it comes to marital affairs, all you give are terrible ideas,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Fan Xiao: \"...\"","He scolded Zhou Yuanshen for being unfilial, dropped the carriage curtain, and ordered the driver to head back.","Fan Xiao was twenty-five years old this year. He had been married when he was sixteen.","His wife passed away from illness. Even before marrying over, her health had not been good. She was thin and frail, unable to stand a gust of wind. Additionally, she had been somewhat reluctant to marry into a military family, and eventually died of melancholy.","Fan Xiao had never remarried.","The Fan family did not make arrangements for him to take a second wife either.","However, his superior was currently acting as a matchmaker for him. Perhaps in a year or half a year, he would take a wife again.","Zhou Yuanshen stood at the doorway for a moment.","The mid-spring wind was chilly, blowing a cold draft up his sleeves, and he thought of Cheng Zhao again.","Zhou Yuanshen pondered alone for a long time.","The next day, he made a trip to the Du family, the home of Cheng Zhao's eldest brother-in-law.","Another day passed, and Cheng Zhao's eldest sister sent her an invitation card, inviting her over as a guest.","Cheng Zhao went immediately.","\"Yesterday, the Duke came to drink with your brother-in-law,\" her eldest sister smiled.","Cheng Zhao was stunned, then frowned. \"Did he say anything?\"","\"You guessed wrong this time. He told me everything; Mother told me too,\" her eldest sister laughed.","Cheng Zhao stood up to leave.","Her eldest sister pulled her back. \"But no one told me exactly how the Duke offended you, not even the Duke himself. I figured that besides me, you probably have no way of telling anyone else about this. Keeping it bottled up is uncomfortable. Want to chat with me?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...I can't even tell you.\"","\"You can say, 'Once upon a time, there was a young married couple...'\"","Cheng Zhao was amused and laughed out loud.","Her eldest sister patted the back of her hand. \"Let's drink some wine too.\"","They didn't drink in the side room, but hid inside the green gauze cabinet. In that tiny square of space, a few dishes and a jar of good wine were laid out.","The two sisters huddled in the green gauze cabinet chatting.","After downing three cups of wine, Cheng Zhao's chatterbox gradually opened.","She briefly told her eldest sister about the matter.","Her eldest sister couldn't help but laugh.","\"...In many prominent households, when the master and the main wife are consummating, the maidservants have to hold water and serve outside the curtain. You should know about this, right?\" her eldest sister asked.","Cheng Zhao had almost forgotten about this.","When she and Zhou Yuanshen shared a bed, they always called the maids in only after the deed was done.","\"Therefore, although it was very excessive of him to call the maid in to await orders, it isn't an unforgivable sin,\" her eldest sister said.","Cheng Zhao frowned.","Her eldest sister leaned in closer and asked her softly, \"Zhao Zhao, how do you two communicate regarding this matter?\"","Cheng Zhao didn't understand. \"What communication?\"","\"Just like how we are chatting now. I say a sentence, you say a sentence; I ask a question, you answer. A married couple's intimate acts in the boudoir are also like a conversation. When he spoke, did you answer?\" her eldest sister asked again.","Cheng Zhao was stunned.","She was supposed to \"answer\"?","She was his legitimate wife. Being dignified was her duty. How could she...","\"What if he was hoping for you to give some response? Just as the maid knocked on the door, he noticed you were exceptionally nervous, not your usual 'indifference.' He might have been instantly captivated by this response, thereby making a mistake?\" her eldest sister continued.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\""]},{"number":76,"title":"Chapter 76: Zhou Yuanshen is an exceptional person","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao's eldest sister put in a lot of good words for Zhou Yuanshen.","She said, \"Zhaozhao, the Duke of Chen is a perfect match for you. I used to wonder what kind of man could ever be worthy of my little sister. When I saw him, I knew he was the one.\"","\"You flatter him too much,\" Cheng Zhao replied.","Her eldest sister pinched her cheek and poured her another cup of wine.","Cheng Zhao drank it, her stubborn temper softening a bit, and resumed her conversation with her eldest sister about Zhou Yuanshen.","Her eldest sister explained that Zhou Yuanshen had received a highly traditional aristocratic upbringing and was accustomed to a life of luxury and service.","To him, it was perfectly normal to have servants standing by to attend to him even while bathing or sharing a bed.","\"...Did Nanny Li not teach you these things before you were married?\" her eldest sister asked.","\"She did,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"She even mentioned that among my maids, aside from Suyue and Qiubai, someone might have to serve as a bedmaid.\"","It was just that she had eventually forgotten about it.","Whenever she was with Zhou Yuanshen, he never called her maids in to serve them.","Furthermore, Cheng Zhao's maids were all well-behaved and knew their place; none of them ever tried to throw themselves at him. Cheng Zhao had also made it clear to him that she would not give any of her own people to him.","Because of this, Cheng Zhao subconsciously came to believe that the private intimacy she shared with Zhou Yuanshen was the normal way of things.","She simply hadn't thought about that particular custom.","And on that day, Mingyu had not come in to serve them, but merely to report back on an errand—which was likely why Zhou Yuanshen knew he was in the wrong.","\"Zhaozhao, men can be quite foolish sometimes. It was the Duke of Chen's fault for giving in to his greed in that moment,\" her eldest sister continued.","\"It was entirely his fault,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"But to demand a divorce over this and give up your status as a first-rank titled lady... isn't that a pity?\"","Cheng Zhao remained silent.","\"Perhaps he simply loved your 'response' in that moment too much,\" her eldest sister added. \"He had never tasted such a delicacy before, and upon encountering such fine fare, his table manners slipped.\"","Cheng Zhao shot her sister a look. \"Do you really believe he hasn't tasted 'delicacies'? Over at Mu Jiang's place, aside from herself, there are two incredibly beautiful maids.\"","\"You are acting like a child again,\" her eldest sister laughed.","She pointed out that Cheng Zhao was simply being competitive, feeling as though she had lost the upper hand in the matter.","But in a marriage, winning and losing were not calculated that way.","Her eldest sister shared a great deal more with her.","\"I know a woman, a former courtesan who bought her freedom years ago. Now, she is exclusively hired by various brothels to train their girls. Shall I have her speak with you?\" her eldest sister asked in a hushed tone.","Cheng Zhao was taken aback. \"You actually know people like that?\"","\"I manage my own household and estate now; naturally, I have to know a little bit of everyone. Mother knows all sorts of people too, she just couldn't let you young girls know about it,\" her eldest sister explained.","She added, \"When you eventually become the true mistress of the ducal estate, with all internal and external affairs in your hands, you too will have to deal with all shades of life.\"","Cheng Zhao remained silent for a moment before shaking her head.","Her eldest sister gently patted her head again. \"You are still young. There is no rush.\"","She continued, \"Make peace with him. The Secondary Wife is pregnant with a child, and his widowed sister-in-law might be taken in as a co-wife to continue the family line. By holding onto this grudge, you are only hurting yourself.\"","Cheng Zhao let out a heavy sigh.","\"He already knows he was wrong. He begged me to plead on his behalf and even sent me several generous gifts,\" her eldest sister laughed.","\"You let him bribe you?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","\"Of course, I only willingly accepted his bribes because I can see what a perfect match he is for you,\" her eldest sister replied.","Cheng Zhao leaned in a little closer. \"What exactly did he give you?\"","Her eldest sister listed them out in detail for Cheng Zhao: \"Two blood coral sculptures, a box full of gold leaves, and a fine horse; along with an absolutely exquisite folding screen.","\"This kind of folding screen would make a very decent gift for any Dowager Madame's birthday celebration in the future. Even the screen in my dowry isn't as fine as the one he sent.\"","Cheng Zhao felt that he had put genuine thought into these gifts; they weren't just randomly picked from the storehouse.","He truly intended to make peace.","\"Eldest Sister, since you've pleaded for him, I won't hold it against him anymore,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Eldest Sister breathed a sigh of relief. \"Mother, Father, and Grandfather will be at ease now too.\"","She added, \"Since you two have reconciled, you should come home for a meal so our parents can see for themselves.\"","She pinched Cheng Zhao's nose. \"Making such a big fuss over a trivial matter, you really are a child.\"","\"It was a major matter.\"","\"Yes, yes, a major matter,\" Eldest Sister said with a smile.","To a child, any little thing was a major matter.","However, everyone's maturity accumulates with the passing years. After experiencing many things in the future, looking back at today, she would probably feel a sense of happiness.","Cheng Zhao rested at her eldest sister's place for two days.","The next day, Eldest Sister also brought over their second sister-in-law and third sister.","The four of them gathered around to play tiles, bringing up the upcoming Shangsi Festival. They talked about going for a spring outing in the suburbs, flying kites, washing by the river, and wearing flowers in their hair.","Cheng Zhao's second sister-in-law, Yin Linlang, said, \"I've already had someone reserve a spot early and set up curtains. I've also invited quite a few relatives and friends. You all must come together when the time arrives.\"","\"I'll bring Yuanqi along.\"","\"Excellent, he's very amusing,\" Second Sister-in-law said.","Cheng Zhao laughed. \"Everyone thinks he's amusing, except for my mother-in-law. And his least favorite thing is for others to praise him as 'amusing'.\"","The women all burst into laughter.","In passing, they mentioned Cheng Zhao's other brother-in-law, Zhou Yuanjin.","He had been appointed as a commandant, which wasn't a huge event; many court officials probably didn't even know.","Cheng Zhao had told her sisters about it.","\"If your Second Branch takes the path of military merit, it might not be worse than how things are now,\" Second Sister-in-law remarked. \"Now that the Duke of Chen has abandoned the martial path to establish a firm foothold in the court, he has sacrificed a lot. His reputation isn't exactly pleasant to the ears.\"","Eldest Sister shot her a meaningful glance.","\"I'm not looking down on him, I'm just worried for him,\" Second Sister-in-law quickly clarified. \"My little sister's honor and glory are entirely tied to him.\"","Third Sister chimed in, \"He kills for the Emperor, so he must have left himself a way out. As long as he can produce evidence that the Emperor ordered him to do it, and hands that evidence over to the historians, the historians will clear his name.\"","She paused, then added, \"I think he's kept a backup plan; he seems quite calculating. The title of 'General Pacifying the West' wasn't just picked up off the street.","Perhaps his younger brother will remain in the position of 'commandant' until he's thirty, but he was appointed General Pacifying the West at the age of twenty.\"","\"He is indeed very outstanding,\" Eldest Sister agreed.","Cheng Zhao realized that her sisters all quite admired Zhou Yuanshen.","Her sisters were quite wise and were not the type to follow others blindly.","\"Could it be that I am prejudiced against him?\" Cheng Zhao reflected.","Her sisters didn't know about the wretched internal affairs of the Zhou family.","But when Cheng Zhao looked at Zhou Yuanshen, he always carried the shadows of the Dowager Madame, Mu Jiang, and Huan Qingtang. She had never looked at him purely as his own person.","When she occasionally praised him, it was for her mother-in-law's ears, or she was praising the patriarch of the Zhou family, rather than praising him as a man.","And it certainly wasn't praising a man who had any real relationship with her.","Cheng Zhao couldn't be blamed for this.","On their very first night as newlyweds, he had presented Cheng Zhao with a massive problem; the first time they consummated their marriage, he had humiliated her again.","Even up to this day, Cheng Zhao had never felt at ease around him.","Cheng Zhao still felt that he had nothing to do with her.","After this incident, Cheng Zhao realized she had to continue playing her role as the Duchess, which meant the issue of producing an heir could no longer be ignored.","She had been tempted to just throw caution to the wind and give up, but her lifelong habit of striving for the best meant she simply could not allow herself to sink.","Therefore, after this brief detour, she had to get back on the right track.","This meant Cheng Zhao would have to swallow the harsh words she had lashed out at Zhou Yuanshen with just a few days prior, a realization that left her feeling rather awkward.","Then again, she reasoned, the path to wealth and status required one to be adaptable and know when to yield.","At the very least, venting her frustrations meant her grievances would not stay bottled up inside to hinder her future schemes.","That was what truly mattered."]},{"number":77,"title":"Chapter 77: Cheng Zhao Stirring Up Trouble Again","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao stayed at her eldest sister's place for two days before returning to the Duke of Chen's mansion.","Her eldest sister had prepared gifts for her, so Cheng Zhao first went to Dowager Madame's Shou'an Courtyard.","\"...Eldest Sister was paying respects to the Floral Goddess, and I also offered a prayer, wishing for the Zhou clan to enjoy everlasting wealth and honor. That is why I returned late, please do not blame me, Grandmother,\" Cheng Zhao said.","This was not a lie. Her eldest sister had indeed been making offerings to the Peony Goddess these past few days, and Cheng Zhao had also paid her respects.","Dowager Madame smiled.","Cheng Zhao was very good at using grand pretexts to suppress people. Dowager Madame felt that among the little monkeys in their backyard, she was the most mischievous and the cleverest.","\"You are very thoughtful,\" Dowager Madame said. \"It is not that you are forbidden from returning to your maiden home, but there are simply too many matters to attend to. The main kitchen has been very busy these past few days, you should go about your duties.\"","Cheng Zhao did not talk back.","The porter's lodge and the main kitchen were both running smoothly; even if she didn't manage them for half a month, nothing would go wrong.","Dowager Madame was also using chores to suppress her, using the same tactic as her. This was called an eye for an eye.","Cheng Zhao then went to Chengming Hall.","First Madame, Madam Song, did not say much, only telling her, \"In a few days, the Secondary Wife will be released from her grounding. Tell the main kitchen to put more effort into her meals.\"","It turned out that Madam Song was in a good mood because she was gloating.","Mu Jiang was already very good at causing trouble, and she had Dowager Madame backing her. Now that her early pregnancy had passed and her health had improved, the Duke of Chen could, as usual, spend the night at Lijing Courtyard. Her status was truly unique.","The one who would suffer the most was undoubtedly Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao lowered her gaze and, after a long moment, smiled. \"Eldest Aunt is right. I will certainly take good care of the Secondary Wife.\"","She added, \"The Duke has many descendants, which must make Grandmother very happy. There is a way forward and backward; with more children, one can be allocated here, another there. Perhaps the first branch might even get one. It is all thanks to her grace.\"","Madam Song's expression changed.","Her gloating was stuck in her throat, unable to be swallowed or spat out, making her feel extremely stifled.","Cheng Zhao was telling her that Mu Jiang's pregnancy did not only affect Cheng Zhao alone, but the entire Duke's mansion.","Because Mu Jiang was Dowager Madame's person.","Madam Song and Huan Qingtang were both widows. Whether Mu Jiang's child would be raised under Cheng Zhao's name or adopted into the first branch in the future was truly hard to say.","It all depended on Dowager Madame's decision.","If that really happened, adopting Mu Jiang's child to the deceased Zhou Yuancheng would be far more awkward for Madam Song than a dual-lineage marriage with Huan Qingtang.","At that point, Madam Song would become a completely useless chess piece.","She would have to be like widows from other households, dressing plainly and living in seclusion.","As for Cheng Zhao, backed by a prominent family from Wu Commandery and bestowed marriage by the Empress, she might turn the most disadvantageous situation into a win-win-win for herself, Mu Jiang, and Dowager Madame, only needing to sacrifice the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law of the first branch.","For Madam Song to think she could stay out of it and watch Cheng Zhao make a fool of herself at this time was truly foolish.","She should have a stronger sense of crisis than Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao had pointed it out to her, making her clearly feel the crisis, and her face turned extremely ugly.","Huan Qingtang watched as Cheng Zhao won with just a few words and was secretly alarmed.","Cheng Zhao's glib tongue was indeed a bit difficult to deal with.","\"This is truly the first time I have encountered someone like her,\" Huan Qingtang thought to herself.","Even noble ladies from scholarly families were not like Cheng Zhao.","The Zhou family had considered many things about Cheng Zhao, but they never expected her to be so articulate and her words to have such a sharp edge.","Cheng Zhao did not stay long in Chengming Hall, turning and leaving.","Seeing Madam Song trembling slightly, Huan Qingtang gently held her hand. \"Mother, we will live in Chengming Hall forever, please do not worry too much.\"","She added, \"Even if Mu Jiang's child is adopted into the first branch, it will be raised by us. Besides, Grandmother has never had this intention; it is all Cheng's wild guessing. She is just scaring you.\"","Madam Song looked at her.","She wanted to say something, but then felt that Huan Qingtang would also benefit from this matter and was no longer on the same page as her.","Madam Song shook off Huan Qingtang's hand and entered the inner bedroom without a word.","Huan Qingtang was stunned for a moment.","She smiled bitterly.","Cheng Zhao's sowing of discord hit the First Madame's sore spot every time, and she no longer quite trusted Huan Qingtang.","It was very helpless.","Cheng Zhao's destructive power was much stronger than Huan Qingtang had imagined.","Huan Qingtang felt that she should do something and could not let Cheng Zhao continue to scheme against Chengming Hall like this.","Before Cheng Zhao married in, everything in the Duke of Chen's mansion had clearly been very normal. Chengming Hall was also fine; Huan Qingtang was a widow, but her days had never been clouded.","\"She is so tricky.\"","Huan Qingtang still wanted to see Zhou Yuanshen.","Last time she went to Chenhui Courtyard, she went alone.","The servant boy Nanfeng did not stop her, so she went in. She had clearly seen Zhou Yuanshen return to Chenhui Courtyard, but she did not see him in the inner room.","She sat alone and waited for a moment.","Cheng Zhao even sent a maid to pass a message. Huan Qingtang heard the voice of Cheng Zhao's maid, who was sent away by Nanfeng.","After waiting for quite a while, with no other choice, Huan Qingtang finally left Chenhui Courtyard.","She had a very important matter she wanted to tell Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen should be very interested in this matter.","Once Zhou Yuanshen knew, the dual-lineage marriage would go more smoothly.","Of course, it would be smooth now too; a dual-lineage marriage with her had ten thousand benefits for Zhou Yuanshen and no drawbacks whatsoever.","Huan Qingtang still hoped that she could become somewhat familiar with Zhou Yuanshen before the marriage was bestowed.","A few days later, Mu Jiang came out.","The weather was still cold and clothes were thick, so Mu Jiang's three-month pregnancy was not too obvious.","But she constantly supported her waist and held her belly, so it could still be seen.","She sat in Shou'an Courtyard, wearing a thin Kesi silk cloak and a golden-red dress, looking as bright and luxurious as fire.","Dowager Madame ordered everyone to go to Shou'an Courtyard for breakfast.","On the way there, Second Madame was very irritable. \"She is released from grounding, she should just come out and live her life properly. Yet Dowager Madame specifically called us to go take a look. Isn't this teaching her to be arrogant and domineering?\"","She added, \"This behavior of the Secondary Wife is entirely spoiled by Dowager Madame.\"","Cheng Zhao said, \"She was raised by Dowager Madame, so it concerns Dowager Madame's authority.\"","She didn't say dignity, but authority.","Dowager Madame let Mu Jiang show off with the purpose of establishing authority.","The old matriarch's prestige was reflected in major matters; usually, she was lenient and gentle. But there needed to be something to make people understand who was truly the master of this house.","That was why Mu Jiang existed.","\"Mother, you must endure it later,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Second Madame patted her hand. \"Don't worry.\"","She added, \"You silly child, the only one suffering grievances is you.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"I am not aggrieved. I have never lost.\"","Second Madame: \"...\"","She cared about feelings, while Cheng Zhao cared about winning and losing.","Cheng Zhao was the most qualified mistress of the house. Her eyes only focused on authority, and she could ignore all the thorns along the way.","Thinking carefully, her personality was somewhat similar to Dowager Madame's.","When the small oil carriage arrived at Shou'an Courtyard and the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law stepped out, they saw everyone surrounding Mu Jiang.","Cheng Zhao stepped forward, first paying her respects to Dowager Madame, then to First Madame, Madam Song, before sitting down to speak.","\"The Secondary Wife looks very well,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"Thank you, Young Madame. You look well too,\" Mu Jiang smiled.","As they were talking, a maid announced that the Duke had arrived.","Cheng Zhao caught a glimpse from the corner of her eye; everyone was looking at him.","This room full of women, this overwhelming wealth and honor, all rested on him alone, yet he rarely showed complacency.","This was perhaps his most commendable trait, right?","If it were Cheng Zhao, she might not even be able to do it.","Zhou Yuanshen stepped into the main hall. His gaze first fell upon Cheng Zhao and his mother before turning toward Dowager Madame. \"Grandmother.\"","\"Did you not go to morning court?\" Dowager Madame asked with a smile.","\"Today is a day of rest,\" Zhou Yuanshen replied."]},{"number":78,"title":"Chapter 78: Zhou Yuanshen Held Her Hand","paragraphs":["The chair next to Dowager Madame was empty.","She instructed Zhou Yuanshen, \"Sit down and speak.\"","She pointed to that seat.","However, Zhou Yuanshen sat in the seat below Cheng Zhao. \"I just came to see Grandmother. I have matters to attend to later.\"","Dowager Madame's smile remained unchanged.","But the atmosphere suddenly tightened.","Zhou Yuanshen acted as if he didn't notice.","Mu Jiang wanted to speak very much, but did not dare to act rashly. She looked at Zhou Yuanshen with deep affection, waiting for him to look back at her and look at her belly.","She was pregnant with a child.","Yet Zhou Yuanshen never looked at her, only focusing on sitting there. The atmosphere gradually grew taut, and everyone's heartstrings tightened, their breathing slowing down.","A maid served him tea.","Zhou Yuanshen picked up the tea. The lid gently clinked against the teacup, making a slight sound. Along with the rising aroma of the tea, it broke the temporarily strange atmosphere in the room.","Everyone secretly breathed a sigh of relief.","\"...Ah Jiang, how have you reflected on the mistake you made last time, after being grounded for so long?\" Dowager Madame deliberately asked Mu Jiang in front of Zhou Yuanshen.","Mu Jiang supported her waist and stood up, \"My Lord Duke, it was my fault last time. I shouldn't have compared myself with the Young Madam. By subsidizing my monthly allowance, you showed me great favor, and it was my own greed.\"","She added, \"It was only right for the Young Madam to show off, as what she received was also a reward from My Lord Duke. I should yield to her.\"","Hearing her words, Zhou Yuanshen slowly put down his teacup.","Expressionless, he quietly looked at Dowager Madame. \"Grandmother.\"","Just one word, and he did not speak again, waiting for Dowager Madame to respond.","Everyone felt this oppressive aura once more.","Second Madam felt a layer of sweat form on her palms.","Even Mu Jiang, who was standing there, straightened her body a bit.","\"Does Ah Shen feel that she hasn't reflected well?\" Dowager Madame smiled.","Still as amiable and kind as ever.","\"Grandmother, she was grounded back then only because she was hot-headed and shouting, which might have harmed the fetus in her womb.","Looking at her now, she has no remorse at all and even attempts to smear the Duke's wife. Lock her up for another month to let her completely sober up.","She should understand just how important the fetus in her womb is to us. Once something happens to the child, chopping off her head will be of no use.\"","Zhou Yuanshen spoke slowly, word by word.","When he spoke, no one dared to interrupt.","And the meaning of his words was baffling. Let alone Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang, even Second Madam looked at him in surprise.","Was the fetus in her womb really that important?","Although it was said that the Emperor ordered Zhou Yuanshen to have a child, and the firstborn was precious, what right did this child have to threaten Dowager Madame?","Zhou Yuanshen was clearly using this matter to force Dowager Madame to compromise.","The smile on Dowager Madame's face faded.","She looked back at Zhou Yuanshen, and the grandmother and grandson's eyes met for a moment.","Then, Dowager Madame spoke. \"Ah Jiang, from now on you must focus on resting and nourishing your pregnancy. You cannot join in any excitement, lest you disturb the fetus. Do you understand?\"","Mu Jiang complied, \"I understand, Grandmother.\"","She then turned to Zhou Yuanshen, \"My Lord Duke, I will definitely strive to give you a healthy and lively eldest son.\"","Zhou Yuanshen ignored her words and picked up his tea again.","After finishing his drink, as if nothing had happened, he looked at Dowager Madame. \"Grandmother, Maternal Grandmother sent someone to fetch Mother and the Cheng family daughter to the Fan residence as guests. If Grandmother has no other matters here, I will escort them over.\"","He added, \"We might stay overnight at Maternal Grandmother's house.\"","He respectfully stood up and bowed to Dowager Madame.","His attitude was docile.","A smile returned to Dowager Madame's face. \"Go then. Relatives should visit each other often. Your maternal grandmother is getting old, and her desire for children and grandchildren to reunite is the same as mine.\"","Cheng Zhao and Second Madam hurriedly stood up.","After bowing to Dowager Madame, they followed Zhou Yuanshen and left.","The small oil-cloth carriage was still parked at the door.","Zhou Yuanshen squeezed in with the two of them.","Cheng Zhao's shoulder was pressed against his, and she tried her best to shrink back.","\"...What were you two sparring over just now? I didn't understand,\" Second Madam said.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"The fact that Mother can tell it was 'sparring' makes me see you in a new light.\"","Second Madam made a motion to hit him. \"You dare to make fun of your old mother?\"","Cheng Zhao turned her head and saw that his eyes were a bit bright.","When he was happy, he rarely smiled, but his eyes would be a third brighter than usual—of course, this might just be Cheng Zhao's illusion.","Cheng Zhao looked at him, and he looked at Cheng Zhao.","Being so close, the couple's breaths were mere inches apart. Cheng Zhao turned her face back.","\"Your grandmother seemed to be somewhat deflated. What exactly did you say?\" Second Madam asked again.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"I didn't say much.\"","\"Zhao Zhao, did you understand what they were saying?\" Second Madam asked.","Cheng Zhao shook her head. \"I didn't really understand either.\"","This time, she truly didn't understand what kind of riddles Zhou Yuanshen and Dowager Madame were playing.","Logically speaking, the child in Mu Jiang's womb should be what Zhou Yuanshen hoped for and wanted the most, yet he used it to threaten Dowager Madame.","It seemed that Dowager Madame was the one who cared the most.","Dowager Madame did not turn around and use this matter to intimidate Zhou Yuanshen.","\"My Lord Duke, what exactly were you talking about?\" Cheng Zhao asked him directly.","It was rare for her to initiate a conversation with him.","Disregarding the fact that Second Madam was still there, Zhou Yuanshen grasped Cheng Zhao's hand.","Cheng Zhao was stunned and tried to pull her hand back, but Zhou Yuanshen held it tight.","He said, \"Let the matters of the Shou'an Courtyard stay in the Shou'an Courtyard. Don't worry about it.\"","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","If you want to talk properly, why must you hold my hand?","Mother is still here.","Seeing this, Second Madam couldn't help but smile. \"Alright, since you tell us not to worry, we'll rely on you. If there's trouble, you solve it.\"","\"Alright!\"","Zhou Yuanshen's voice was firm, carrying a rare hint of emotional fluctuation.","Second Madam said, \"Don't boast. What will you do if the Concubine provokes Zhao Zhao next time?\"","\"She wouldn't dare,\" Zhou Yuanshen said. \"If she provokes her, she will be grounded again.\"","Second Madam didn't say anything more.","She just thought to herself that grounding wouldn't solve the problem.","This concubine was given to Zhou Yuanshen by Dowager Madame, and she had the Emperor's backing behind her; moreover, she had striven to get pregnant first.","Grounding was merely a temporary fix.","Forget it, she would think about such troublesome matters later. Asking Zhou Yuanshen to come up with a plan now was also making things difficult for him.","\"Did your maternal grandmother really send someone to invite us?\" Second Madam asked.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"No. We can just visit directly, Maternal Grandmother will be happy.\"","Second Madam was speechless.","While they were talking, they arrived at the entrance of the Jiangyun Courtyard, and Second Madam got off first.","Cheng Zhao also wanted to get off, but Zhou Yuanshen had already instructed the older female servant driving the carriage to head to the Nonghua Courtyard.","\"Let go of me,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen asked, \"Still angry?\"","\"If you don't let go, I'm going to get mad,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen released her hand.","The couple entered the Nonghua Courtyard.","Nanny Li didn't expect Cheng Zhao to return so quickly. Hadn't she said she was going to the Shou'an Courtyard to accompany Dowager Madame for breakfast?","\"My Lord Duke, Young Madam, have you had breakfast?\" Nanny Li asked.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"No.\"","She added, \"Just prepare something simple. We have to go out later.\"","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen had breakfast together.","Although the two did not converse, Nanny Li felt that the atmosphere between them was fairly harmonious.","The Duke hadn't visited the Nonghua Courtyard for several days, and now he was here again, right on the day the Concubine was ungrounded. This was a good thing.","After the meal, Cheng Zhao went to change her clothes.","Since she was going out as a guest, she needed to dress more elegantly.","She stepped into the inner chamber with her maids Suyue and Qiubai trailing behind her, only to hear Zhou Yuanshen's voice call out, \"Wait outside the door for now.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\""]},{"number":79,"title":"Chapter 79: You Need to Be Gentle with Her","paragraphs":["Inside the bedroom, Cheng Zhao's spine stiffened.","She couldn't help but recall that day in the Chenhui Courtyard, when he had also stepped around the folding screen to find her just like this.","Her eldest sister had counseled her a lot, and Cheng Zhao had come to accept the reality of what happened at the Chenhui Courtyard.","She could not change the current situation.","She didn't plan to continue arguing with him.","But she didn't want to be intimate with him either.","She took two steps back. \"Does the Lord Duke have something to say?\"","Zhou Yuanshen stopped in his tracks. \"Are you still angry about what happened last time?\"","\"It's all in the past,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"You asked my eldest sister to intercede, and I must give her face. We will let this matter go.\"","She only said \"let this matter go,\" but she didn't say she wasn't angry.","Zhou Yuanshen was dressed in a dark robe, its lapels embroidered with golden auspicious clouds, but the faint golden gleam could not dilute the coldness and detachment radiating from him.","Cheng Zhao always felt that he had nothing to do with her, probably because of this attitude of his: he had no intention of getting close to anyone.","He only sought what he needed.","Whatever he wanted, he would stop at nothing to get it, whether it was his status in the royal court or those fleeting moments of pleasure with Cheng Zhao.","He didn't let anyone get close to his heart.","Even with his parents, who defended and accommodated him at every turn, there was a certain barrier; they were never truly close.","There was nothing wrong with this attitude; at the very least, it meant Mu Jiang wouldn't be able to enjoy any special treatment either.","\"I need to change my clothes. Let's not keep Mother waiting,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"Cheng Zhao, you are the Duchess,\" he spoke up.","\"Yes.\"","\"If I were no longer the Duke of Chen, would you still want to be the Duchess?\" he asked.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"My bestowed marriage was to the Duke of Chen. If you no longer hold the title, I will simply live my days like the women of the eldest branch. You do not need to worry about me.\"","Zhou Yuanshen's gaze fell upon her face.","Cheng Zhao met his eyes without backing down.","\"If you say so, I will take it as the truth, Cheng Zhao,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","\"I am speaking from the heart,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"Then I want to tell you that Concubine Mu's child is very important to the Chen Duke's estate. If you only wish to be the Duchess, you must yield to her somewhat regarding her affairs,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","He added, \"At the very least, this child must be born safely.\"","Every word and sentence from the recent confrontation in the Shou'an Courtyard echoed in Cheng Zhao's mind.","\"Yes, Lord Duke,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen turned and walked out.","With his departure, Cheng Zhao felt the heavy pressure dissipate significantly, and her spine slowly relaxed.","She sat alone for a while, silently pondering the words he had just spoken and what he had said in the Shou'an Courtyard.","Cheng Zhao instructed her maid to help her change and comb her hair. When she stepped out of the inner bedroom fully dressed, she found Zhou Yuanshen sitting in the main hall, drinking tea as he waited for her.","She resumed her usual demeanor and smiled at him. \"Lord Duke, apologies for keeping you waiting.\"","\"Let's go.\"","\"Wait just a moment,\" Cheng Zhao said.","Nanny Li quickly gathered a few gifts, taken from the storehouse containing Cheng Zhao's dowry.","\"These are gifts for Grandmother and Aunt. There's an aged ginseng root and a set of tourmaline jewelry,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"...You've spent too much. I will compensate you with ten thousand taels of silver,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","\"It didn't cost that much,\" Cheng Zhao replied.","Last time, when he gave Cheng Zhao a small crossbow, he had also said that if she didn't like it, he could give her ten thousand taels as compensation.","\"Keep the extra. Whenever you want to have new jewelry made, just call the manager of the goldsmith's shop to the estate,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao voiced her compliance.","The couple left together. Waiting for them at the main gate were the Second Master and Zhou Yuanqi.","They each boarded their carriages.","Zhou Yuanshen and Cheng Zhao shared a carriage. Neither spoke; they simply sat in silence.","They soon arrived at the Pillar of State General's Manor.","Cheng Zhao had visited during the New Year, dined with the Fan family, and remembered quite a few people.","Coming again this time, she was familiar with the way.","The group went to the main courtyard.","The Old Dowager resided in the Fan family's main courtyard.","\"Grandmother,\" Zhou Yuanqi greeted her with a bow.","The grandmother beamed with joy. \"Out of all of you, only Yuanqi's bow is the most proper and pleasing to the eye.\"","The Second Madam's mouth twitched. \"Mother, you spoil him too much.\"","\"Nonsense, a child should be praised when he does well. His manners are perfect, and he is smart and eager to learn. I can never praise him enough,\" the grandmother laughed.","It was a lively scene.","After exchanging greetings, the aunt arranged for the meal, and the youngest uncle, Fan Xiao, also came in.","After sitting idly for a moment, Fan Xiao said to Zhou Yuanqi, \"I recently got a new foal. It's incredibly beautiful. Do you want it?\"","\"What color is it?\" Zhou Yuanqi was clearly interested but deliberately played hard to get.","\"Pure white all over.\"","Zhou Yuanqi immediately stood up. \"I'll go take a look.\"","He added, \"I'll just look first. If the breed is good, I might reluctantly accept it.\"","The Second Madam was almost angered to death by him. \"You have no respect for your elders! Are you asking for a beating?\"","Fan Xiao ruffled Zhou Yuanqi's hair. \"Did your uncle say I was giving it to you for free? If you like it, trade me five thousand taels of silver for it.\"","He added, \"If you don't have enough silver, borrow it from someone.\"","The grandmother chimed in with a laugh, \"Go take a look. If you like it, Grandmother will pay for it.\"","\"Then hurry up and go, your grandmother is rich,\" Fan Xiao laughed.","The group headed to the training grounds.","Cheng Zhao also followed along to join the fun.","The Second Madam didn't go. She stayed behind to complain to the Old Dowager, \"By spoiling him like this, he doesn't know his limits. Have you forgotten the time he was scammed out of five thousand taels buying a calligraphy copybook?\"","\"The money was recovered, and he even got two authentic works out of it. Look at how good his luck is. With such good fortune, he doesn't need to practice asceticism; he is destined to live a life of wealth and honor. What are you worrying about?\" the Old Dowager asked.","The Second Madam was speechless.","Her mother hadn't been like this when she was younger. Whenever the Second Madam and her siblings lost focus for even a second while practicing the horse stance, a horsewhip would crack against their bodies.","Now, with her grandsons and maternal grandsons, her indulgence knew no bounds.","The Second Madam lamented that she hadn't been born at the right time and shook her head helplessly.","There were many horses in the stables at the training grounds, including quite a few fine steeds.","Cheng Zhao didn't know much about horses. Judging purely by their appearance, she praised them all the way.","The snow-white foal was tied up separately.","When it was led out, it even kicked up its hind legs.","\"...This is a wild horse. It's too untamed and not suitable for Yuanqi. Tame it for half a year before giving it to him,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Fan Xiao laughed, \"It just has a slightly fierce temperament, it's fine. It's not a wild horse. How could a wild horse have such a fine coat?\"","\"It is a wild horse,\" Zhou Yuanshen said with certainty. \"Its coat is indeed very fine, shiny and smooth, looking as if it were meticulously cared for. This proves that it truly possesses a wild nature, allowing it to fight for the best water and grass.\"","Fan Xiao replied, \"It's already been trained for a few days, it'll be fine.\"","\"I want to ride it.\" Zhou Yuanqi was already captivated, wishing he could leap onto its back immediately.","Fan Xiao ordered someone to saddle the horse.","\"Look, it allows itself to be saddled, don't worry,\" Fan Xiao added.","Zhou Yuanshen merely frowned but did not try to stop them again.","Once the snow-white foal was saddled, Zhou Yuanqi stamped his feet in delight. \"Youngest Uncle, quickly lift me onto the horse.\"","Cheng Zhao stood to the side, smiling.","At this moment, Zhou Yuanqi was very much a child. His words, actions, and expressions were all those of a young boy who hadn't grown up yet, full of innocent charm.","All his pretenses were cast aside.","Fan Xiao led the horse, and Zhou Yuanqi took the reins. He tentatively tapped the horse's belly with his heels, and the foal began to trot.","Everything was normal.","After running half a lap around the training grounds, just as everyone let their guard down, the foal suddenly began to gallop wildly and buck, desperately trying to throw Zhou Yuanqi and the saddle off its back."]},{"number":80,"title":"Chapter 80: The Skill of the Duke","paragraphs":["Such an unexpected change made Cheng Zhao and Fan Xiao turn pale.","Cheng Zhao clenched her back teeth, not letting herself cry out in alarm, afraid of frightening Zhou Yuanqi; and Zhou Yuanqi on horseback also didn't say a word, holding on to the reins tightly.","The pony was actually playing with him, constantly tossing him around at a very fast speed.","Cheng Zhao even suspected that when Zhou Yuanqi landed, the pony would step on his head.","\"Quick, prepare bows and arrows!\" Fan Xiao ordered immediately, \"Call someone to help!\"","Fortunately, it was in the Fan family's drill ground, not in the wild.","Just as everyone was going crazy with anxiety, Zhou Yuanshen had already rushed out.","He mounted a horse nearby and galloped towards the drill ground. When he got close to the pony, there was some distance between the two sides, but he actually stood on the horse's back.","Cheng Zhao covered her mouth, her eyes wide open, still not daring to make a sound.","Fan Xiao was also surprised, looking at this scene as if he had seen a ghost.","Zhou Yuanshen seemed to make a leap and landed on Zhou Yuanqi's horse.","He didn't miss.","The pony was not tall and strong, and couldn't bear the weight of two people. Its legs immediately went weak, and it didn't run as freely and easily as before.","But it was also fierce, wanting to throw both of them off its back, so it simply bounced on the spot.","Zhou Yuanshen pinched his brother's shoulder. While the pony was spinning, they had already reached several guards. Zhou Yuanshen easily threw Zhou Yuanqi down.","He had a lot of strength in his hands.","Two guards lent a hand and caught Zhou Yuanqi.","Zhou Yuanqi was dizzy and didn't move for a long time, obediently clinging to the guard's arms.","Cheng Zhao ran over there.","Zhou Yuanshen's hands had already tightened the reins and even wrapped around the horse's neck.","The pony galloped anxiously for several laps.","Fan Xiao was extremely tense.","Zhou Yuanshen's hands tightened, and the pony fell to its knees as if unable to breathe. He was not thrown off, but landed steadily.","After such a toss, the pony lay on the ground panting heavily, foaming at the mouth, and was really tired out.","Zhou Yuanshen's footsteps swayed slightly, and he stood steadily next to it, patting the dust off his clothes.","Zhou Yuanqi burst into tears with a \"wa\" sound.","Cheng Zhao couldn't care less about looking at Zhou Yuanshen and ran to Zhou Yuanqi: \"Fifth Brother, how are you?\"","Zhou Yuanqi could only stand steadily by leaning on the guard, crying bitterly: \"I almost died, Little Uncle harmed me!\"","Fan Xiao, who followed: \"...\"","Cheng Zhao gently patted his back: \"It's fine, you're alive and well, not dead yet.\"","Zhou Yuanqi was still crying.","He had suffered a great fright, and after recovering his senses at this moment, he was somewhat unable to control himself.","Fan Xiao also coaxed him.","Zhou Yuanshen walked over and said to the guard: \"Take him down. Order someone to call a doctor and give him some soothing medicine.\"","Afterwards, everyone in the Fan family knew that an accident had happened at the drill ground.","Fortunately, Zhou Yuanshen had excellent riding skills and was good at controlling horses, so no major disaster occurred.","The Old Dowager scolded Fan Xiao: \"I told you before, this pony needs to be trained for a few more days, it looks restless.\"","Fan Xiao muttered: \"It's beautiful. When it grows up, it won't look so good.\"","Showing off should be done early.","When it's a pony, it's the cutest and most beautiful, almost a bit like Zhou Yuanqi.","No matter how naughty it is, it's just a pony.","Fan Xiao had seen too many horses and didn't take it seriously. After all, a pony's endurance is limited. He didn't expect this horse to be so clever and understand human nature.","Usually, when adult guards trained it, although it was not docile, it wouldn't go crazy; when it found out that there was a child on its back, it started to make trouble and act badly.","\"Slaughter it.\" The Old Dowager said.","Fan Xiao hurriedly said: \"There's no need, right? It can still be raised.\"","\"Must a life be lost before you listen to advice?\"","Zhou Yuanshen, who was standing aside, spoke up after a long time: \"Maternal Grandmother, keep it. Someone among the lieutenant generals at home understands horses, hand it over to him to train.","This horse is very clever. As long as it is tamed, it will be a rare good horse in the future. Maybe it can be given to Yuanqi.\"","The Old Dowager sighed: \"You young people, one by one, don't believe in evil. Forget it, I'll give it to you. You lead it to the Pingxi General's Mansion. I can't bear to look at it.\"","Zhou Yuanshen said yes.","Zhou Yuanqi cried for a while, drank the soothing medicine, and fell asleep heavily.","Lunch was not very pleasant.","The Second Madam felt sorry for her son and didn't know who to scold; she also felt a bit embarrassed in front of her daughter-in-law, feeling very depressed.","After the meal, the group returned to the mansion.","The next morning, when Cheng Zhao went to Jiangyun Courtyard to pay her respects, she heard that the Second Madam had gone to see Zhou Yuanqi.","\"...What's wrong with the Fifth Young Master?\" Cheng Zhao asked the maid.","\"He had a fever in the middle of the night. The people around him didn't dare to call a doctor, and just waited until morning to say it.\" The maid said.","It was almost as Cheng Zhao expected.","The child was frightened yesterday.","Rumor has it that a child's soul is unstable, and it's easy to get a fever when excessively frightened.","Even if he drank some soothing medicine yesterday.","When Cheng Zhao arrived, the Second Madam was ordering people to pack things: \"Move him to Jiangyun Courtyard and let him live in my warm pavilion.\"","The maid said yes.","Zhou Yuanqi had already woken up.","Cheng Zhao went forward and touched his forehead. He just looked at her softly. At this time, he was completely a child, without the adult expressions he usually disguised, a bit fragile, making people feel particularly distressed.","Her heart also twitched.","\"The fever is not too high.\" Cheng Zhao said, \"Mother, don't worry.\"","The Second Madam was anxious in her heart, but not directed at anyone. She sighed, \"Children will all have headaches and brain fever, it's fine.\"","She was relatively optimistic and didn't make a fuss, because she hadn't had a child die prematurely.","Therefore, she was still calm at this moment.","On the one hand, she ordered the older female servants to go out and call a doctor, and on the other hand, she told people to move Zhou Yuanqi's courtyard.","Cheng Zhao accompanied her.","After settling Zhou Yuanqi, it was getting late. The Second Madam asked her: \"Don't you need to go to Chengming Hall?\"","\"Here on your side...\"","\"You can come back after you finish your work. It's useless for us all to guard him. He needs to recover slowly, you go ahead.\" The Second Madam said.","Cheng Zhao agreed.","Walking out of Jiangyun Courtyard, Cheng Zhao ordered the maid Suyue beside her: \"Go tell Nanny Li to go home and ask my mother what medicine to use when a child is frightened, and whether there are any peace charms or the like.\"","Suyue agreed.","When Cheng Zhao finished her errand at Chengming Hall and returned, Zhou Yuanshen and the Second Master had both returned home from the government office.","The doctor had already been there.","Medicine was being boiled in the small side room of Jiangyun Courtyard, and there was a strong smell of medicine upon entering the door.","\"How is it?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","The Second Madam told her to go take a look.","She entered the warm pavilion in the inner bedroom and saw Zhou Yuanqi holding a book to read.","Cheng Zhao couldn't help laughing and reached out to touch his forehead.","He avoided it: \"Oh, you can't, it's not proper.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","She had already touched his forehead. It was still a bit hot, but not too hot to the touch.","\"You're still reading, aren't you dizzy?\" Cheng Zhao asked him.","Zhou Yuanqi: \"I just caught a cold. I sweated at the time and was blown by the cold wind. It wasn't from fright, why would I be dizzy?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"A cold and fever will also make you dizzy. I didn't say you got a fever from fright. You're trying to hide it but making it more obvious.\"","Zhou Yuanqi was so angry that he quietly blew out a breath, and said in a childish voice: \"I decline your sick visit!\"","Cheng Zhao came out of the warm pavilion.","\"His spirits are okay.\" Cheng Zhao said to the Second Madam.","The Second Madam: \"He's just a child, a headache and brain fever is nothing serious.\"","Zhou Yuanshen accompanied them and sat for a while.","After Cheng Zhao finished looking, she returned to Nonghua Courtyard. Nanny Li had already returned from the Cheng family.","\"Madam said that since he suffered such a fright, he needs some spiritual healing. She knows a doctor who is skilled in it. Additionally, a strong person needs to sleep beside him for a few nights to help settle the child's soul,\" Nanny Li said.","Cheng Zhao replied, \"Let's wait and see. I don't think Yuanqi would be willing to drink talisman water, nor could he accept someone else sleeping beside him.\"","That night, Zhou Yuanqi ran a high fever again.","He was tormented like this for four consecutive nights, suffering from a low-grade fever during the day and a high fever late at night. He grew visibly weaker; even when sitting idly, he lacked the strength to read.","Second Madam was frantic with worry.","Cheng Zhao immediately sent someone to inform her mother, asking her to bring the doctor skilled in spiritual healing to Duke Chen's Estate."]},{"number":81,"title":"Chapter 81: Cheng Zhao's Good Fortune","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao informed Chengming Hall and Shou'an Courtyard about Zhou Yuanqi's illness.","She sent someone to invite her mother, asking her to bring a doctor over.","The Old Madam personally came to Jiangyun Courtyard and asked the Second Madam, \"How did he get so sick? You must take good care of him.\"","The Second Madam felt a lump in her chest.","Cheng Zhao held the Second Madam's hand and answered for her, \"Grandmother, you and Mother are both anxious. Illness comes like a landslide and goes like pulling silk. Let's not panic and take it slowly.\"","The Old Madam sighed.","\"Yuanqi is a child whose intelligence borders on the supernatural. I hope he can survive this ordeal,\" the Old Madam said.","The First Madam, Madam Song, and Huan Qingtang also came.","\"He must get well soon. When Yuancheng was dying, he also had frequent fevers.\" Madam Song had tears in her eyes.","She wasn't distressed for Zhou Yuanqi, but pitying her deceased son.","The Second Madam's anger surged.","Cheng Zhao handled them one by one, asking them to sit idly in the east secondary room.","Cheng Zhao's mother arrived quickly.","She brought a doctor in his fifties. After taking the pulse, the doctor prescribed cinnabar and talisman paper, asking people to prepare them as he wanted to draw a talisman for Zhou Yuanqi.","Madam Cheng came to the east secondary room again and met the Old Madam and the others.","Hearing that it was Zhuyou, Madam Song said, \"I hope it works. These days, there are many doctors who are good at Zhuyou, but few who truly have medical skills.\"","Many doctors claimed to know Zhuyou, but it wasn't very effective.","The Second Madam felt that her in-laws had taken trouble, yet Madam Song was still picking faults, which annoyed her to the extreme.","Madam Cheng had a very good temper, seemingly unable to hear the disgust in Madam Song's words: \"Good doctors are hard to find. We have also suffered enough. Some doctors just cheat people out of their money.\"","\"Isn't that so,\" Madam Song said.","She was naturally led by Madam Cheng to talk about quack doctors.","The doctor quickly drew two talismans and took his leave.","Madam Cheng also wanted to leave.","She gave a small box to the Second Madam: \"The Prime Minister heard that Yuanqi has a fever and specially asked me to bring the 'Ziyang Pill'. You keep it first. If the fever doesn't break tonight, give it to the child.\"","The Old Madam looked over.","This glance was meaningful, but she said nothing.","Huan Qingtang felt slightly surprised.","The Ziyang Pill was used to save lives. The materials were exquisite and the price was high. Many medical families could only make twenty pills in ten years.","Its alias was also \"Huanyang Pill\".","It was said to be a rejuvenating medicine for the elderly when they were seriously ill, which could save their lives for a few years; some doctors also said that the Ziyang Pill was actually a fever reducer.","It did have the effect of reducing fever, but very few people used it solely for that purpose. It was like using a sledgehammer to crack a nut, too wasteful.","Huan Qingtang looked at the Old Madam again.","The Old Madam definitely had two Ziyang Pills too. At her age, it was impossible for her not to prepare this kind of medicine.","But whether it was the eldest legitimate grandson Zhou Yuancheng who was ill a few years ago or Zhou Yuanqi who had a fever today, the Old Madam didn't take out this medicine.","Prime Minister Cheng, however, asked Madam Cheng to bring it over.","For a moment, Huan Qingtang felt not touched, but intense jealousy: a wealthy and generous family, too sincere, had won over people's hearts too steadily.","Wouldn't the Second Madam be grateful to death to the Cheng family?","Even if Cheng Zhao made a big mistake in front of her mother-in-law in the future, the Second Madam would think of today's Ziyang Pill and wouldn't argue with her.","The Cheng family spared no effort to support the child and pave the way for Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao was really lucky.","\"...I can't take this!\" The Second Madam was overwhelmed by the favor and hurriedly declined.","She was too shocked.","Cheng Zhao pressed her hand: \"Mother, accept it first. We might not need it. When Fifth Brother is better, we can return it.\"","The Second Madam had tears in her eyes: \"Thank the Prime Minister for thinking of Yuanqi.\"","\"The Prime Minister really likes Yuanqi and says this child will become a great scholar in the future,\" Madam Cheng smiled.","The Second Madam took out a handkerchief to wipe her tears.","Madam Song, the First Madam, asked in a very low voice, \"What is the Ziyang Pill?\"","Huan Qingtang glanced at her, her heart pausing slightly.","Had the Changling Marquis's Mansion never even heard of the Ziyang Pill?","This kind of famous medicine was passed down within families, and pharmacies indeed wouldn't sell it over the counter. It was reasonable for some small families outside not to know, but Madam Song of the Changling Marquis's Mansion actually...","\"A precious fever-reducing medicine,\" Huan Qingtang said.","Madam Song curled her lips.","Madam Cheng left. The Old Madam gave a few instructions, telling the Second Madam to take good care of Zhou Yuanqi, and led the others back.","On the way back, Madam Song also said, \"Jiangyun Courtyard is really far. It's exhausting to run over.\"","Huan Qingtang didn't speak.","She felt the same.","Jiangyun Courtyard was a distance from Chengming Hall. Going from here to Shou'an Courtyard every day was like a court official living in the south of the city going to court; they would be looked down upon by their colleagues.","\"I absolutely cannot move out,\" Huan Qingtang thought.","The Cuiyun Courtyard she lived in was the courtyard for the eldest legitimate son's wedding, linked to Chengming Hall.","Once the first branch left Chengming Hall, she would have to leave too.","Living in places like Jiangyun Courtyard and Nonghua Courtyard, even if the courtyards looked fine, because they were far from the Old Madam, the servants would look down on them.","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law went back with their own thoughts.","In Jiangyun Courtyard, Nanny Fan personally boiled the talisman water and brought it to Zhou Yuanqi.","Zhou Yuanqi refused to drink it.","He helplessly said to his mother and sister-in-law, \"You don't read books normally! What talisman paper? It's just drawn with cinnabar. What's useful is the cinnabar. Cinnabar does reduce fever, but it will also damage my brain.\"","He didn't want to become a boor or a reckless youth; he was smart.","Cheng Zhao said, \"If you burn for another night, you'll burn stupid anyway.\"","She also said, \"There is also cinnabar in the Ziyang Pill. A small amount is not poisonous. Be obedient. Also, if you belittle Zhuyou, me, and Mother again, I'll have to beat you.\"","The depressed Second Madam beside them laughed out loud.","Zhaozhao from a scholarly family was becoming more and more like her.","She used to think that scholarly families were hypocritical and full of tricks, but the Cheng family treated people sincerely.","Under Cheng Zhao's suppression, Zhou Yuanqi reluctantly drank the talisman water.","After finishing it, he said to Cheng Zhao, \"If I become a fool in the future, you have to listen to me.\"","\"If you're stupid, how will you remember my promise?\"","Zhou Yuanqi: \"...\"","The two bickered for a while.","The Second Master went to the government office to check in and quickly returned. Cheng Zhao then withdrew from the inner bedroom; mid-morning, Zhou Yuanshen also returned home.","Zhou Yuanqi was fine during the day.","After drinking the talisman water, his low fever seemed to have lessened a bit, but he didn't sweat.","\"...Youngest Uncle also asked about Yuanqi's illness,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Second Madam said, \"We must hide it. Your grandmother is old. If she hears about it, she will definitely blame herself.\"","\"I told Youngest Uncle that he was fine, just busy these days, and I'll invite him as a guest later,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Second Madam nodded.","Cheng Zhao stayed in Jiangyun Courtyard all day.","After dinner, the Second Madam asked the Second Master to go to the warm pavilion to sleep with Zhou Yuanqi.","Zhou Yuanqi refused.","The Second Master told him to be obedient.","Zhou Yuanshen beside them said, \"Didn't you say you need a strong person to suppress it?\"","\"I'm not good enough?\" the Second Master said.","\"You have white hair.\"","The Second Master: \"...\"","Zhou Yuanshen then said, \"I'll do it.\"","Cheng Zhao glanced at him in surprise.","Zhou Yuanqi's eyes widened: \"No! Absurd!\"","He rarely had such a horrified expression, successfully amusing the Second Madam and Cheng Zhao.","\"I don't want to, I don't want to sleep with a boor!\" Zhou Yuanqi protested strongly.","However, no one cared."]},{"number":82,"title":"Chapter 82: Call Me \"Third Brother\" Again","paragraphs":["That night, Second Madam rested on the long couch in the secondary room of Jiangyun Courtyard, leaving the inner bedroom to the father and his two sons.","The brothers Zhou Yuanqi and Zhou Yuanshen stayed in the warm pavilion; Second Master slept on the bed.","Zhou Yuanqi was extremely disgusted by the arrangement, but after night fell, he had no energy left to fuss, because his fever flared up again.","He drank another dose of talisman water.","Groggy, he was about to fall asleep.","Second Master and Zhou Yuanshen spoke for a good while across the warm pavilion.","\"The Crown Prince is too young and in poor health. The men of the Helian clan go mad when they reach a certain age; the Crown Prince may not turn out to be a wise ruler,\" Second Master said.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"We will talk about the future when it comes.\"","\"You have done so much for the Emperor, yet you still can't refuse your grandmother's arrangement for you to carry on two family lines?\" Second Master asked again.","Zhou Yuanshen said, \"I have my own plans.\"","\"Yuanshen, you have always brooded over the matchmaking matter at Princess Qing'an's manor back then, haven't you?\" Second Master asked.","Zhou Yuanshen remained silent.","Second Master did not know how to comfort him either.","After Zhou Yuancheng of the eldest branch passed away, many things did indeed change, leaving Zhou Yuanshen in an awkward position.","Actually, when he was first asked to inherit the title, Zhou Yuanshen had refused it.","It was the Emperor who told him to inherit the title.","The Emperor always treated the Zhou family's affairs as his own.","Second Master felt that his son hated many people. He hated all those who mocked him and wantonly treated him as a pawn.","He clearly had his own bright future; he was doing quite well on the path of a military general.","\"...However, Zhaozhao is a very good person,\" Second Master said, bringing up something happy. \"The Cheng family is also not bad.\"","\"Yes,\" Zhou Yuanshen replied.","\"Then treat Zhaozhao better, and be filial to your father-in-law and mother-in-law,\" Second Master said.","\"I know.\"","\"Have children early and spread the family branches with Zhaozhao,\" Second Master added. \"If it really comes down to it, we can move away from the capital in the future.\"","\"Father, where in this world is there a pure land?\"","Second Master sighed.","They talked about a few other things.","Zhou Yuanshen suddenly said, \"Father, Yuanqi is sweating.\"","Second Master immediately got up.","He walked over to the warm pavilion and touched Zhou Yuanqi; his forehead was indeed wet.","\"Don't move him yet, let him sweat it all out,\" Second Master said. \"If he can break a sweat, he will probably get better.\"","The father and son waited for another hour, then called a maid to bring hot water to wipe Zhou Yuanqi down and change his clothes.","Zhou Yuanqi woke up but felt tired again, groggily closing his eyes.","Second Madam couldn't sleep in the secondary room and came in to look when she heard the commotion.","\"His fever has finally broken.\" Second Madam touched Zhou Yuanqi's forehead, feeling a wave of relief.","As she spoke, the corners of her eyes grew damp.","Her child being sick almost broke her heart; it also reminded her of the torment she felt when Zhou Yuanshen was injured in the past.","The next day, when Zhou Yuanqi woke up, his low-grade fever was completely gone, and his forehead felt cool.","He even said he was especially hungry.","Second Madam hurriedly sent someone to prepare breakfast and another to inform Cheng Zhao.","After washing up, Cheng Zhao came to Jiangyun Courtyard.","Seeing that Zhou Yuanqi had regained his spirits, she was also happy.","She even teased him, \"The Duke's wealth and nobility suppressed your illness. Hurry up and say, 'Thank you, Third Brother, Third Brother is truly a good person.'\"","Zhou Yuanqi was so annoyed; he bit the tip of his chopsticks and ignored her.","Zhou Yuanshen, however, glanced at her.","\"The Duke must be tired from last night, right? Are you resting today?\" Cheng Zhao asked him.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, \"I'll rest for a day, I've already asked for leave.\"","\"Then are you going to Nonghua Courtyard?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Zhou Yuanshen said yes.","Her taking the initiative to invite him to Nonghua Courtyard meant that the previous incident was completely behind them.","After Zhou Yuanqi finished his breakfast, he muttered a \"Thank you.\"","Cheng Zhao still didn't let him off: \"Thank you who?\"","Zhou Yuanqi turned around and ran off; he had to go to the clan school.","Second Madam shouted from behind, \"You just recovered and you're going to the clan school? Rest a bit more.\"","\"I'm already fine.\"","\"Let him go. Children have strong constitutions; once the fever breaks, it's no big deal. If he stays here all day, I'll get annoyed with him too,\" Second Master said.","Second Madam: \"...\"","Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen returned to Nonghua Courtyard.","She instructed the maids to make the bed again. Zhou Yuanshen had watched over his brother last night and hardly slept.","Of course, he wasn't too sleepy at the moment.","\"Aren't you going to Chengming Hall?\" he asked her, seeing that Cheng Zhao had changed into casual clothes after returning from Jiangyun Courtyard.","\"I also asked for leave. Three days of leave,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She added, \"I thought that if Yuanqi didn't get better, I would have to go back to my maiden home and ask my mother for a solution; I was also afraid that Mother might need help here, so I simply asked Eldest Aunt for leave.\"","Zhou Yuanshen nodded slightly.","He said he couldn't sleep in the morning and would rest a bit after lunch.","\"Want to play chess?\" he asked Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao agreed.","The couple played chess and chatted about trivial matters.","They didn't mention Mu Jiang, only talking about his general's manor. He said the residence wasn't large, but it was decorated quite nicely, and they could go see it next time.","Cheng Zhao then said she would go see it when she had time.","\"How will that horse be handled?\" Cheng Zhao asked again.","\"It's being kept at the general's manor. The lieutenant will tame it,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","He added, \"It was because Yuanqi is young that he was bullied by the horse. It's in an animal's nature to bully the weak and fear the strong; it's not a major fault. It has a well-proportioned build and a beautiful coat; it will be a fine steed in the future.\"","Cheng Zhao said, \"Will you still give it to Yuanqi later?\"","\"Depends on whether he likes it.\"","The two continued talking.","Seeing that he was still in good spirits, Cheng Zhao said, \"How about we go to the Cheng family for lunch? We can return the Ziyang Pill to Grandfather while we're at it.\"","\"You shouldn't have brought such a precious thing for Yuanqi.\"","\"My grandfather takes a detached view of life and death. Children are the hope and future,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","Zhou Yuanshen looked at her deeply again.","Cheng Zhao was thinking that since she had gone home last time making a fuss about a divorce, she should let her parents know; her eldest sister also told her to reconcile with Zhou Yuanshen and bring him home for a meal.","Zhou Yuanshen agreed to go back with her.","Cheng Zhao sent a maid ahead to the Cheng family to inform them, then went to change her clothes.","Zhou Yuanshen went to the storehouse to pick out a few gifts.","The young couple returned and had lunch with her mother; then they waited until mid-afternoon when her grandfather and father returned home from court.","Grandfather asked about Zhou Yuanqi's condition.","\"He's already well. He went to school bright and early this morning,\" Cheng Zhao smiled.","\"Indeed eager to learn, and talented too,\" Grandfather smiled.","Cheng Zhao's father was rather stern and taciturn; Cheng Zhao and her sisters didn't dare misbehave in front of him.","Zhou Yuanshen, however, was able to chat with him about the political situation.","After returning Grandfather's Ziyang Pill and having dinner at the Cheng family, the couple finally returned to the Chen Duke's Manor.","That night, Zhou Yuanshen stayed at Nonghua Courtyard.","After bathing, Cheng Zhao got into bed wearing her inner garments.","Perhaps because she had experienced quite a few things recently, her awkwardness from last time had faded a lot.","When Zhou Yuanshen embraced her, she fell softly into his arms.","\"You called me 'Third Brother' this morning. Call me that again,\" his voice was hoarse.","Cheng Zhao: \"When did I?\"","It took her a moment to remember that she had said it while teasing Zhou Yuanqi.","No wonder Zhou Yuanshen had glanced at her at the time.","Cheng Zhao turned her head away.","She ignored him.","Zhou Yuanshen gently turned her face back and kissed her lips. \"Cheng Zhao, say it for me to hear.\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\""]},{"number":83,"title":"Chapter 83: Do You Get Nervous","paragraphs":["The atmosphere inside the bedcurtains was enchanting and intimate.","Cheng Zhao remembered what her eldest sister had said about responding. When he kissed her, she gently sucked on his lower lip. Even though she didn't call him Third Brother.","Zhou Yuanshen felt slightly surprised.","Therefore, that night, Cheng Zhao felt as if she was going to be taken apart by him all over again.","After it was over, Cheng Zhao went to bathe. Then, enduring her aching waist and weak legs, she went to the side room to offer a stick of incense to Guanyin, the Goddess of Mercy who brings children.","She knelt down devoutly and kowtowed.","Zhou Yuanshen had also finished washing up. Dressed in plain white inner garments, the usual coldness about him had lessened considerably. He stood at the door, quietly watching Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao knew he was there. She didn't turn around, earnestly bowing to Guanyin before finally standing up.","Zhou Yuanshen looked at her and said, I will offer a stick of incense too.","Cheng Zhao didn't refuse; having children was something they both had to work at together.","She lit three sticks of incense and handed them to him. Please, My Lord.","Zhou Yuanshen earnestly bowed three times and inserted the incense into the censer.","It was as if he had just accomplished something monumental.","Back in the bedroom, Cheng Zhao was just about to fall asleep when he pulled her into his arms again.","Cheng Zhao pushed against him. My Lord, it's very late.","She didn't want to do it again.","She had been tossed about enough. No matter how greedy he was, he needed to show some restraint. Cheng Zhao was not someone he could just toy with.","I can't sleep. Let's talk, he said.","Cheng Zhao was also not sleepy.","But if they were just going to talk, why did he have to hold her in his arms?","Pressed against his chest, she could feel his heartbeat and smell his breath, which carried a hint of cooling tooth powder.","Enveloped by the man's scent, she felt rather uncomfortable.","Let me lie down properly, and we can talk slowly. She broke free from Zhou Yuanshen's embrace.","Zhou Yuanshen didn't force her.","...March 17th is Grandmother's sixty-second birthday. For her sixtieth birthday, Eldest Cousin had just passed away, and the Emperor was in poor health and hadn't named an heir, so it wasn't celebrated grandly. This year, it should be made up for. The Emperor even mentioned this to me before the New Year, Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao frowned slightly. Are you saying this, or is Grandmother? I haven't heard anything about this from Chengming Hall.","Perhaps they will tell you in the next few days.","For a major birthday celebration, a proper household would prepare half a year in advance; even just for a lively gathering, it requires three months of preparation. If they only mention it 'in the next few days,' how will there be enough time? Cheng Zhao said.","Grandmother likes to give people urgent tasks to test their abilities, Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao fell silent.","Are you nervous?","I manage the gatehouse and the main kitchen. When hosting a banquet, the first tasks are sending out invitations and receiving gifts, which fall under the gatehouse's duties. The second is the food and wine, which is the main kitchen's responsibility.","If a birthday banquet is organized in a rush, the two most important and demanding tasks are both mine. How can I not be nervous? Cheng Zhao said.","She felt a trace of resentment, almost gritting her teeth.","But on second thought, the Old Madame loved to play with power and people's minds, so it made sense for her to give such orders.","Perhaps the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law at Chengming Hall had already heard the news and were just keeping it from Cheng Zhao.","The next head of Chengming Hall would be Huan Qingtang; this was the Old Madame's very clear stance. To elevate her, she would tell her in advance, allowing her to handle her duties methodically and flawlessly.","When the time came, the only one scrambling in a panic would be Cheng Zhao.","The slight feeling of pleasure Cheng Zhao had just experienced vanished in an instant.","She had to rouse her fighting spirit.","Cheng Zhao quickly thought back to how her mother and eldest sister handled things when her own grandmother was alive and celebrating her birthday.","At that time, her eldest sister kept her and her third sister close by. She had been entirely focused on fried milk cakes, while her third sister kept complaining that the calligraphy on the couplets wasn't elegant enough. Neither of them had listened to their eldest sister's instructions.","But it didn't matter; she could cram at the last minute and go ask her mother and eldest sister for advice.","Do you need my help? Zhou Yuanshen asked her in the darkness.","Cheng Zhao returned to her senses. If I run into difficulties, I will definitely ask My Lord for help.","Zhou Yuanshen gave an affirmative hum.","His tone revealed neither joy nor anger.","Just as Cheng Zhao was about to start making a plan, she heard Zhou Yuanshen speak again. Cheng Zhao, if Grandmother holds a birthday banquet, you must be prepared. The Emperor and the Crown Prince might both attend.","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","She inexplicably felt nervous again.","First, she had never met the Emperor. Second, she had heard that the Emperor's mental state had been very poor these past two years, and he sometimes became delirious.","Cheng Zhao didn't want to cause a massive disaster.","...If the Crown Prince really does come to offer birthday greetings, there can be no fireworks. During the New Year, the Crown Prince set off fireworks to please His Majesty but injured his hand in an explosion. There is still a burn scar on the palm of his left hand to this day, Zhou Yuanshen added.","Cheng Zhao was astonished. I haven't heard about this either.","The news was suppressed. Not only did the Emperor and Empress forbid anyone from speaking of it, but Grand Preceptor Guo also didn't want it to reach the court, as it would be detrimental to the Crown Prince, Zhou Yuanshen said.","The Crown Prince's injury wouldn't earn him sympathy; it would only make the court officials feel he was unreliable and distrust him even more.","I will remember that, Cheng Zhao said.","The two talked for quite a while longer before finally going to sleep.","Waking up early the next day, Cheng Zhao went to pay her respects to her mother-in-law as usual and asked about her brother-in-law, Zhou Yuanqi.","Once his fever broke, it didn't return, the Second Madame said. Don't worry, just focus on your duties with peace of mind.","Cheng Zhao said yes.","She sent a maid to tell Zhou Yuanqi that he should just let her know whatever he wanted to eat. Since she managed the main kitchen, even if she had to pay out of her own pocket, she would make sure Zhou Yuanqi ate well.","By mid-afternoon that day, Cheng Zhao had finished her duties. The servant boy Nanfeng was waiting for her at the entrance of Chenghui Courtyard.","Seeing Chenghui Courtyard made Cheng Zhao's scalp tingle with anxiety, but she didn't allow herself to feel fear. She had to slowly find her power and couldn't just let Zhou Yuanshen do as he pleased.","Young Madame, Nanfeng bowed to her. My Lord is going to drink with the Maternal Uncle tonight and won't be home. He prepared something for you and asked you to take it yourself.","Cheng Zhao asked, What is it?","It looks like bank notes.","It took Cheng Zhao a moment to remember that on the day they went to visit the Fan family, Zhou Yuanshen had said he would give her ten thousand taels in bank notes.","Because she had brought expensive gifts to the Fan family, Zhou Yuanshen was afraid she would suffer a loss.","She entered the western side room.","Sure enough, she saw a black lacquered box on the low table on the kang. Inside were bank notes, each worth one thousand taels, ten of them in total.","I'll take them, Cheng Zhao said. Do I need to sign a receipt?","Nanfeng was momentarily stunned and then laughed. Why would you need to sign for something My Lord is giving you? I've seen you take it, and that's enough.","Cheng Zhao was speechless.","She took the box and went back.","In the blink of an eye, it was March. Cheng Zhao's sister-in-law from the Cheng family sent her an invitation to celebrate the Shangsi Festival.","There was only half a month left until the Old Madame's birthday celebration. When Cheng Zhao went to pay her respects along with the First Madame, Lady Song, and Huan Qingtang, the Old Madame still didn't mention it.","Lady Song also showed no reaction.","Only Huan Qingtang had been somewhat busy these past few days, going out twice.","Lady Song even muttered, Huan usually doesn't like returning to her maiden home. What's been going on with her these past few days?","Cheng Zhao listened quietly.","During the Shangsi Festival, Zhou Yuanshen accompanied Cheng Zhao, and Zhou Yuanqi tagged along as well.","But Cheng Zhao had no mind for sightseeing.","She and her eldest sister were washing by the river, simply dipping their handkerchiefs in the water.","...First, dig out the account books from previous New Years to see which guests were invited, so you have a good idea. Also, make a mental note of which theater troupes performed, what dishes were served, and what wine was poured in the past, her eldest sister told her. As for the rest, you'll just have to see what sudden instructions the Old Madame gives and adapt to the situation.","What about the fireworks? How should that be handled? Cheng Zhao asked.","Because it was uncertain whether the Crown Prince would attend.","It was impossible to host a birthday banquet without arranging a fireworks display. However, if the Crown Prince were to attend, this activity would have to be canceled, leaving an empty gap in the schedule.","\"Go ask Ah Chao,\" Eldest Sister said. \"He is full of clever ideas. Have him come up with a solution for you.\""]},{"number":84,"title":"Chapter 84: A Heavy Burden, Also an Opportunity","paragraphs":["On the third day of the third lunar month, Cheng Zhao didn’t play much; she spent most of her time talking with her eldest sister and her fourth brother.","Zhou Yuanqi, meanwhile, followed Cheng Zhao’s third sister, Cheng Ying. Both of them wore peony hairpins, drawing quite a few admiring glances.","One was as beautiful as freshly fallen snow, the other as delicate as a jade carving—together, they were the most captivating sight of the entire Shangsi Festival.","Zhou Yuanqi was used to being the center of attention and paid it no mind; Cheng Ying remained indifferent, unaffected by the praises or criticisms of the mundane world.","They were content in their own bubble, flying kites for a while and composing several poems.","Cheng Ying wrote a long poem, roughly fifty-four lines. Remarkably, Zhou Yuanqi remembered every single line and found each one exquisite, leaving a lingering fragrance on his tongue when he recited them.","“I’ll copy it out neatly for you later. I’ve been practicing Master Qu Lian’s calligraphy copybook recently, and my handwriting has improved a lot. You must treasure it,” Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Ying didn’t find his words amusing.","She nodded seriously, “I definitely will treasure it.”","The two had plenty to talk about.","Cheng Zhao’s fourth brother, Cheng Chao, noticed them and said to Cheng Zhao, “Third sister gets along well with children. She’s a bit talented but also somewhat naive.”","“Are you praising her, or criticizing her?”","“Both.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","She needed a favor from her fourth brother, so she didn’t argue, just rolled her eyes at him.","In her eyes, the third sister was the most free-spirited and bold—both learned and sincere.","Such admirable qualities seemed rare to the adults, who always acted surprised and tried to taint Cheng Ying with stains of worldly cynicism.","Only children truly understood her beauty and purity and enjoyed her company.","“...She likes children so much, she really should have one of her own,” Cheng Chao added.","Cheng Zhao: “You love eating roast beef so much; do you want to become a butcher?”","Cheng Chao: “...”","Their eldest sister quickly stepped in to separate them.","Both meant well and cared for Cheng Ying, but somehow their conversation was heading toward an argument.","If they were five years younger, they probably would have ended up fighting, which was quite a headache.","On this day of the Shangsi Festival, Zhou Yuanshen sat together with Cheng Zhao’s eldest sister’s husband and her second brother. The three chatted about trivial matters, which wasn’t boring at all.","On the way home, Zhou Yuanqi was still a bit excited and enthusiastically recited the poems he and Cheng Ying had composed to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao listened but couldn’t help drifting off, thinking about the matriarch’s birthday celebration. Her literary skills were limited, and the long poem made her drowsy.","“...You really are like a cow chewing on peonies,” Zhou Yuanqi noticed her distraction and couldn’t help but complain.","Cheng Zhao could only smile awkwardly.","Zhou Yuanshen sat quietly beside them, saying nothing.","That day, Zhou Yuanshen stayed again at Nonghua Courtyard.","“...I heard from your brother-in-law that your fourth brother was once rejected from an engagement?” Zhou Yuanshen suddenly asked.","Cheng Zhao snapped back to attention.","“Yes,” she replied.","“Why?”","“They were betrothed when they were eight years old. The bride was Seventh Miss Chu from the Feng’en Duke’s Chu family. They had been in contact for many years. When they were thirteen and the wedding date was set, Seventh Miss Chu announced at my grandmother’s birthday banquet that she wanted to break off the engagement,” Cheng Zhao explained.","At this point, Cheng Zhao frowned slightly. “In short, both families lost face. At that time, my grandmother’s health was already poor, and she passed away within half a year.”","My Fourth Brother said he would observe the mourning period and not delay the Seventh Miss, so he agreed to call off the engagement. The elders of the Feng’en Bo Mansion tried hard to salvage the situation, but in the end, it was a slap in the face to the Cheng family.","Not long after, the Seventh Miss was married off to a distant place. What their family’s true circumstances were, we had no idea.”","He added, “And frankly, I didn’t bother to find out. The whole matter left me quite displeased. My Fourth Brother was blameless in all this; no one spoke ill of the Cheng family. Over the years, many have sought to matchmake for him, but none were deemed suitable.”","After Cheng Zhao came of age, no immediate marriage arrangements were made because Cheng Chao stood in the way.","In a prominent family, respect for seniority is paramount. As long as Fourth Brother’s marriage remained unsettled, Cheng Zhao could not proceed with marriage talks—at least not until she turned eighteen.","Once she reached eighteen, even if Cheng Chao remained a bachelor, Cheng Zhao’s marriage had to be arranged.","However, the Empress intervened with a bestowed marriage, solving the dilemma of Cheng Zhao’s marriage prospects.","“Are you thinking of matchmaking for my Fourth Brother?” Cheng Zhao asked.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “...I’ll keep an eye out for him, though I’m not sure which family has a suitable young lady waiting to be wed.”","He added, “You do have some friction with the Chu family of Feng’en Bo Mansion. But at Grandmother’s birthday banquet, the Chu family should send guests. If you’re displeased, have the main branch handle their reception; you don’t have to deal with them yourself.”","“I understand. The Chen Guogong Mansion and Feng’en Bo Mansion are old friends,” Cheng Zhao said. “I’ll adapt as the situation demands. Rest assured.”","Zhou Yuanshen nodded.","Taking advantage of the moment, he pulled Cheng Zhao close and kissed her lips.","Cheng Zhao: “...”","He kept teasing her well into the night. The next morning, when she went to Chengming Hall to attend to official duties, she kept nodding off.","The Eldest Madam sent someone to summon the three officials from Chengming Hall to visit Shou’an Courtyard.","Sure enough, the topic turned to the birthday banquet on March 17.","The matriarch casually said, “Just a simple gathering of family and friends for a meal. I’m putting up five thousand taels of silver myself for the celebration, so the public funds won’t be overly strained. It’s easier for those managing the household to explain.”","Eldest Madam Song was utterly shocked.","“Mother, is this to make up for the sixtieth birthday banquet?” she asked bluntly.","The cost of a birthday banquet was usually only a few hundred taels of silver; anything over a thousand was already extravagant. Yet the matriarch mentioned five thousand taels.","This five thousand taels came from her own pocket; the public funds would cover additional expenses.","Cheng Zhao thought that Eldest Madam’s question was unnecessary, making her seem less tactful and refined, losing face in front of the younger generation.","Since the amount had been stated, this was clearly a make-up sixtieth birthday banquet, to be celebrated in the most lavish manner.","Compared to Eldest Madam Song’s slip, both Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang remained composed.","Especially Cheng Zhao, who focused her gaze intently on the matriarch.","She didn’t speak out rashly because Eldest Madam and Eldest Sister-in-law were present; it wasn’t her place to take the lead. She waited quietly for instructions.","“...You all remember that the sixtieth birthday banquet was never held last time. Each of you has been dutifully filial,” the matriarch smiled.","Eldest Madam Song didn’t press further.","This was indeed to make up for the sixtieth birthday banquet.","“Mother, there’s not much time left. Is it still possible?” Eldest Madam Song asked worriedly.","Nanny Sun, standing beside her, smiled with a sharp edge: “Eldest Madam, what do you mean by ‘not much time left’? That’s an unlucky thing to say.”","The Eldest Madam hurriedly stood up: “Mother, my daughter-in-law misspoke.”","She was always respectful and cautious before the matriarch. Though she had her grievances, she feared the matriarch greatly.","\"Alright, alright,\" the matriarch said with a warm smile, \"No need to nitpick.\"","She went on, \"It's just a birthday banquet. Everyone who can come is connected to the Zhou family by fate. Those who can't make it simply aren't meant to be here—no need to force it.\"","She spoke with ease.","But it wasn’t just about relatives and friends; there were countless preparations to handle.","A mid-March birthday banquet naturally called for fresh peonies, since they were in season. Yet the orders for peonies had been placed well before the New Year.","Where else could they get any now?","That was just one of the challenges the matriarch could think of.","There were more.","The main kitchen’s supplies, some rare and precious ingredients—they simply couldn’t be gathered in time. Plus, there were birthday peaches, and the special clothes, shoes, and socks for the birthday celebration.","Less than half a month left—who could survive this kind of pressure?","Mrs. Song clenched her palm so tightly her nails dug into her flesh.","At a time like this, who could come to her rescue?","Who would willingly take on this heavy burden and, by doing so, shoulder the blame?","The matriarch spoke again: “Mrs. Song, if you’re feeling overwhelmed, hand this over to Lady Huan. She’s young and needs the chance to gain experience. You and Mrs. Cheng can assist her.”"]},{"number":85,"title":"Chapter 85: Zhou Yuanshen's Guarantee","paragraphs":["The news of the old madam's birthday celebration spread that very day.","The entire Duke of Chen's estate knew about it.","By mid-afternoon, Cheng Zhao had drafted the guest list and submitted it for Huan Qingtang's review.","Her speed left the eldest madam dumbfounded; Huan Qingtang merely smiled, read it carefully, then crossed out a few names and added a few more.","There were about three hundred guests, both male and female.","Afterward, Cheng Zhao returned to the Nonghua Courtyard. The second madam sent for her.","Cheng Zhao changed into her house clothes and went to the Jiangyun Courtyard for dinner.","Her father-in-law and Zhou Yuanqi were both there.","Shortly after, Zhou Yuanshen also returned.","The second madam urged Cheng Zhao to explain quickly what was going on.","Cheng Zhao recounted everything in detail.","The second madam was stunned: \"A grand birthday feast like this, and they're only giving you half a month to prepare?\"","\"Both my eldest aunt and I have only half a month, but my eldest sister-in-law may not,\" Cheng Zhao said with a smile. \"She's been at the Shou'an Courtyard since the twelfth lunar month.\"","\"This is favoritism at its worst!\" the second madam exclaimed.","\"Mother, I think Grandmother is quite strategic. She wants our eldest sister-in-law to take command at the Chengming Hall.","Look at it this way: with such a rushed birthday event, even our eldest aunt would want to shy away from such a thorny task. When Grandmother proposed letting our eldest sister-in-law manage things, the resistance from that side vanished.","Our eldest sister-in-law has been preparing for a long time. She will certainly handle everything properly. Even if something goes wrong, Grandmother will cover for her.","By using this birthday banquet, the tally tokens will fall into our eldest sister-in-law's hands, and it will be very hard for our eldest aunt to reclaim them,\" Cheng Zhao explained with a smile.","The second madam stared blankly. All these twists and turns—even if she could return to her mother's womb and have her brain re-formed, she still wouldn't figure them out.","\"You girls from scholarly families really know your stuff!\" the second madam sighed.","She used to look down on daughters from scholarly households, but now she was convinced.","With such scheming, if you lacked a little foresight or had shallow experience, you'd end up being someone else's pawn without realizing it.","The second madam felt lucky she hadn't sought the power to manage the household—otherwise, she wouldn't even know how she died.","Zhou Yuanshen remained expressionless, lifting his tea to take a sip, then another.","Zhou Yuanqi nodded in agreement: \"It's just as you predicted.\"","\"So this birthday banquet is a way to hand over the household management?\" the second master asked.","As he said this, he glanced at Zhou Yuanshen.","Since they were letting Lady Huan take charge, the matter of dual inheritance was already a done deal.","The emperor had probably approved it as well.","Lady Huan was indeed beautiful, clever, and from a good family, but Zhou Yuanshen hadn't chosen this willingly. The second master felt his son was being wronged.","And then there was the matter involving Princess Qing'an's mansion back then...","The second master looked at Cheng Zhao as he thought this. With a daughter-in-law as sharp and perceptive as she was, how could she not have thought of it?","And it directly affected her interests.","Yet, there was no sign of dismay or defeat on her face.","Aside from the second madam, who hadn't considered that angle, everyone present likely understood it clearly.","But Zhou Yuanqi, though he knew the situation, had no ability to keep things to himself. He said outright: \"After the birthday banquet, we'll have an elder sister-in-law added to the family.\"","The second madam was taken aback.","Cheng Zhao instinctively reached to cover Zhou Yuanqi's mouth.","This gesture amused the second madam; Zhou Yuanqi's eyes went wide with anger as he pushed her hand away.","The second madam wanted to laugh but also felt like scolding. In the end, laughter came before anger.","Zhou Yuanshen set down his teacup and said calmly, \"There won't be an extra elder sister-in-law, don't worry.\"","\"You don't get to decide that,\" Zhou Yuanqi retorted.","Luckily, he had backup plans. His fairy-like sister-in-law would stay in their household.","Zhou Yuanqi felt the family couldn't function without him. He needed to eat well, grow up strong, be their leader, and guide them through life.","As for that reckless fellow—he should just go to the main branch!","Unfortunately, at this year's Shangsi Festival, he hadn't encountered the Prince of Andong.","He had heard that the Prince of Andong hadn't gone to his fiefdom but was staying in the capital, handling affairs for the emperor.","Slowly, step by step, the Prince of Andong would belong to the second branch.","\"...Besides the gatekeepers and the main kitchen, I'm also in charge of the fireworks,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She glanced at Zhou Yuanshen.","Zhou Yuanshen had guessed this; he knew the Duke of Chen's estate inside and out. Cheng Zhao was grateful for his reminder.","However, neither the second master nor the second madam understood, and Zhou Yuanqi was equally confused.","\"What about the fireworks?\" the second madam asked.","Cheng Zhao looked to Zhou Yuanshen for permission, asking silently if she could speak.","Zhou Yuanshen nodded.","Cheng Zhao dismissed the attendants and, in a low voice, told the second madam.","The second madam was both alarmed and angry: \"Isn't this setting a trap for you?\"","\"Both Grandmother and the Duke only anticipate the possibility. The emperor and the crown prince may not actually come,\" Cheng Zhao said.","\"If they do come, then just don't set off the fireworks. It's better to skip one thing than to make a mistake by doing too much,\" the second madam advised.","Cheng Zhao agreed.","The second madam felt that Cheng Zhao probably wanted to compete with Huan Qingtang. Now telling her to hold back was like asking her to admit defeat.","Cheng Zhao had always been very concerned about winning and losing. She had once said she didn't feel wronged around Mu Jiang because she had never lost.","\"Zhao Zhao, did you hear what I said?\" the second madam asked, worried.","Cheng Zhao smiled. \"Mother, rest assured. I will not lose face, nor will I cause any major trouble.\"","The second madam sighed.","That dinner weighed heavily on everyone's minds.","After the meal, the children left, and the second madam and the second master sat by the window-covered bed, chatting idly.","\"Maybe we should just separate from the household and live on our own,\" the second madam suddenly said.","For the first time in over twenty years, she relented.","The property could be forfeited; the children would have to suffer somewhat in the future without the estate's backing—never mind. They could attend the Fan family's clan school.","The second master gave a helpless smile. \"It's too late for you to come around now. Last time, Ah Shen told me, 'All lands under heaven belong to the king.' If the emperor wants him to inherit the title, where can we possibly go?\"","The second madam sighed again.","The second master added, \"Don't lose heart. I think our daughter-in-law is brimming with confidence.\"","\"How can she possibly win against them? Lady Huan has the old madam behind her, and the old madam has seen everything in her life,\" the second madam said.","The second master replied, \"A young, sharp mind is a powerful tool. As they say, 'You can't make mud stick to a wall.' Even with support, Lady Huan needs to have a clever mind herself. I don't think she's as smart as Zhao Zhao.\"","\"That's true—Zhao Zhao is indeed intelligent,\" the second madam agreed. \"And she has a strong will to win.\"","A person with a strong will to win has endless drive, isn't afraid of setbacks, and is full of energy. Cheng Zhao was like a general charging into battle, fully armed.","Lady Huan lacked this kind of relentless resilience.","She may have pride, but her actions don't match her ambitions. The lofty airs of a daughter from a scholarly family still clung to her; she wasn't as bold as Cheng Zhao, who held nothing back.","Take the title of lady, for example. Cheng Zhao had deliberately harmed her own reputation by spreading negative news about herself just to obtain it.","Huan Qingtang, constrained by social standing, could not do such a thing.","Having that title or not having it—it made all the difference in the world. Cheng Zhao's sacrifice at the time was well worth it.","\"Just wait—Zhao Zhao will bring you honor and comfort,\" the second master said.","The second madam felt his words weren't empty.","Perhaps she really could enjoy the blessings her daughter-in-law would bring."]},{"number":86,"title":"Chapter 86: Want to steal the credit","paragraphs":["For the Dowager Madame’s birthday, Cheng Shi swiftly arranged her own share of duties.","The menu was finalized and, as usual, submitted to Huan Qingtang for review.","There were eighteen dishes, four of which were vegetarian, as the Dowager Madame observed a vegetarian diet for religious reasons.","Cheng Shi selected Braised Vegetarian Chicken, Arhat’s Delight, Vegetarian Ham, and Lotus Cream Soup.","“Arhat’s Delight and Lotus Cream Soup are the grand dishes among the vegetarian offerings; the Braised Vegetarian Chicken and Vegetarian Ham are simpler,” Huan Qingtang remarked approvingly. “Sister-in-law, the Lotus Cream Soup is no easy task. Grandmother once had it at Jin’an Temple. If it’s not done well, it might be better to replace it with something else.”","Lotus Cream Soup, also known as Snow-Clearing Sunset, requires picking lotus flowers, removing the pistils and bases, then boiling them with tofu. The petals must not lose their color, and the tofu must be tender without falling apart.","It seems like a simple dish, but it is actually extremely difficult, testing one’s mastery of heat-control and skill.","Yet it is beautiful, like sunset clouds resting on petals after snow—vivid and brilliant.","If it could be made successfully, it would surely add luster to the birthday banquet.","After speaking, Huan Qingtang waited for Cheng Shi to ask for her help.","The kitchen of Jin’an Temple had a chef skilled in this dish, and it was also a signature vegetarian offering at the temple. He could be invited down from the mountain under the name of the Marquis of Chen’s Mansion.","Of course, neither Cheng Shi’s nor Huan Qingtang’s status sufficed—they would need the Dowager Madame’s involvement.","Cheng Shi was in charge of the main kitchen, and naturally she wanted to shine. She certainly wouldn’t want to replace this dish.","Huan Qingtang could persuade the Dowager Madame to help.","“...Sister-in-law, without the Lotus Cream Soup, these vegetarian dishes would be plain and unremarkable. Grandmother’s such a special occasion—how could we make do?” Cheng Shi said.","Huan Qingtang replied, “That’s true.”","“Rest assured, I’ve already asked my mother to send a letter to Jin’an Temple. They will send the head chef of their kitchen to the mansion,” Cheng Shi said with a smile.","Huan Qingtang was speechless for a moment.","She said nothing, but nodded with a smile. “Excellent, then.”","The menus and guest lists were drawn up and sent to the Dowager Madame for approval.","The Dowager Madame immediately noticed the Lotus Cream Soup among the vegetarian dishes.","“This dish is hard to make well. I’ve never seen it done properly anywhere except at Jin’an Temple,” the Dowager Madame said with a laugh.","“If the lotus petals aren’t discolored, they’re either steamed to mush.”","She then looked at Huan Qingtang. “Didn’t you warn Cheng Shi?”","“Cheng Shi said her family knows someone at Jin’an Temple and can invite the chef,” Huan Qingtang replied with a smile.","The Dowager Madame chuckled. “The Cheng family has such connections?”","The reserves of the Cheng clan were, in truth, far deeper than the Dowager Madame had imagined.","She had thought the Chengs were at most on par with the Huans, slightly more respectable than the Marquis of Changling’s House, the Song family.","Now it seemed that the combined resources of the Huans and Songs could barely match the Chengs.","“Grandmother, Sister-in-law said she can handle it. We can trust her,” Huan Qingtang said.","The Dowager Madame nodded. “Then let her manage it.”","After Huan Qingtang left, the Dowager Madame gazed at the dish list, lost in thought.","Her trusted steward, Nanny Sun, who knew her thoughts and intentions best, asked quietly, “Dowager Madame, aren’t you worried that Cheng Shi might outshine the eldest young mistress? I am a bit concerned.”","If Cheng Shi succeeded in bringing in Jin’an Temple’s head chef, she would indeed shine at the birthday banquet.","And Cheng Shi was exceptionally skilled at seizing opportunities, almost grasping in her ambition. This streak of competitiveness, Huan Qingtang lacked entirely.","“Don’t worry,” the Dowager Madame said with a smile. “Everything at the banquet will be credited to Huan Qingtang’s arrangements.”","Nanny Sun was taken aback.","Then she understood: as long as the Dowager Madame willed it, no matter how much Cheng Shi did, it would only add to Huan Qingtang’s glory.","No one would ask about the chef. As long as the Dowager Madame praised the Lotus Cream Soup in front of the guests and expressed satisfaction with Huan Qingtang’s handling of affairs, the honor would belong to Huan Qingtang.","“You’re right. Cheng Shi is too eager for advancement. She caught me off guard for a moment,” Nanny Sun said.","The Dowager Madame smiled faintly.","Indeed, Cheng Shi, though so young, proved far more troublesome than she had imagined.","The Dowager Madame was used to having the final say, yet Cheng Shi repeatedly crossed her boundaries.","On the second day after entering the household, during the morning tea ceremony, she had threatened the Dowager Madame. Then came a series of incidents that left the Dowager Madame deeply displeased.","Moreover, she had been married into the family by imperial decree from Empress Guo.","The Guo family and the emperor were in a state of mutual restraint, and the Dowager Madame stood on the emperor’s side. As a result, she also resisted anyone granted by Empress Guo.","If Cheng Shi wanted to shine, well, it would depend on whether the Dowager Madame gave her that opportunity.","The Marquis of Chen’s Mansion was bustling day and night. All other matters took a back seat, everything centered on the Dowager Madame’s birthday.","Soon, the day of the birthday arrived. Cheng Shi rose at dawn.","One round of guests was expected at noon, and even more distinguished guests in the evening. Cheng Shi would have to work from morning till late.","Throughout the entire year, the Marquis of Chen’s Mansion held night banquets only three times: on Mid-Autumn Festival, New Year’s Eve, and Lantern Festival, all for clan members.","But this time, a night banquet was specially held for the Dowager Madame’s birthday. Besides clan members, close friends and long-standing family acquaintances were also invited. Special caution was needed regarding fire hazards and security.","“...I heard there will be a crane dance show and fireworks tonight?” Cheng Shi’s maid Suyue asked.","“The cranes were tribute birds, normally raised in the imperial gardens. They’ve been borrowed specifically for the Dowager Madame’s birthday,” Cheng Shi said.","Suyue replied, “Then we’ll all get to witness something extraordinary.”","“That crane dance was Sister-in-law’s idea,” Cheng Shi added.","Suyue immediately said, “This servant won’t watch!”","Cheng Shi laughed.","Mu Jiang had also heard about the banquet.","A few days ago, at the Shou’an Courtyard, she had narrowly escaped being confined to her room again, so she had been keeping out of trouble.","But she felt bitter.","She was carrying his child, so why was Third Brother still so cold to her?","Thus, she suspected that Cheng Shi was behind the falling-out.","“Do you think Third Brother could ever come to like Cheng Shi?” Mu Jiang asked the old matron beside her.","The matron, originally from the palace, had expected a life of comfort in the marquis’ mansion, thinking she would enjoy the perks of being with a favored concubine. But instead, the marquis had ignored even the emperor’s goodwill and had directly placed Mu Jiang under house arrest.","The matron quickly understood the reality: regardless of how the outside world called Mu Jiang a “Princess in all but name,” inside the marquis’ mansion, she was nothing more than a concubine.","If the marquis doted on her, she could soar on sheer background and the Dowager Madame’s influence. But if the marquis decided to suppress her, it was well within his rights.","When Mu Jiang pressed her about the marquis, the matron did not dare stir trouble and only said, “Cheng Shi was granted by Empress Dowager Guo’s decree.","With the Guo family currently so powerful at court, the marquis must at least keep up appearances. In terms of beauty, she can’t match you, Madam. And besides, you are with child.”","Mu Jiang beamed, gently caressing her belly. “I carry Third Brother’s child.”","Then she lowered her voice, “Now that the pregnancy is stable, can Third Brother spend the night at the Lijing Courtyard?”","“It might be better to wait another month or two for greater safety,” the matron advised.","Mu Jiang pouted.","Soon, she heard that Huan Qingtang was hosting the birthday banquet and that Cheng Shi was helping.","“They’re just trying to show off,” Mu Jiang said. “Maybe Grandmother doesn’t even want to celebrate—she’s never liked grand occasions. It’s just Huan Qingtang and Cheng Shi using her birthday for their own glory.”","The matron did not reply.","Mu Jiang had already heard various rumors about the banquet from the outside.","She sent the matron away and called in her trusted maid, whispering instructions before telling her to act.","“But—”","“Just do as I say,” Mu Jiang said. “Even if something goes slightly wrong, it won’t harm Grandmother’s prestige. It just can’t let Huan Qingtang and Cheng Shi have all the credit.”","The maid steeled herself, thinking that the Secondary Wife knew the Dowager Madame well and wouldn’t dare offend her outright, and so she left to carry out the task."]},{"number":87,"title":"Chapter 87: Excluding Cheng Zhao","paragraphs":["By the time March seventeenth arrived, it was the day of the Chen Duke’s estate birthday banquet.","The weather was fine—a vast blue sky without a single cloud, golden sunlight spilling over tender new branches, everywhere fresh greenery and vibrant life.","The Second Madam was also helping to receive guests that day.","Zhou Yuanshen had requested leave from his duties and was at home managing affairs as well.","At dawn, a long string of firecrackers was set off, echoing through the entire street. The air hung thick with haze for a while, all the smell of gunpowder from the firecrackers.","With that, the birthday feast began.","All the maids and servants in the household had changed into brand-new blue cotton clothes, brighter in color than usual by three shades.","As for the masters, needless to say, even the widowed First Madam, Lady Huan Qingtang, was decked out in gold and silver, adorned with pearls and jade, dressed in resplendent luxury.","Though they did not wear mourning clothes on ordinary days.","Led by the Second Master, over a hundred members of the Zhou clan gathered early in the morning to offer birthday greetings to the Grand Madam.","Among the throng of women, Mu Jiang was dressed the most opulently.","On her head, Mu Jiang wore an intricate gold hairpin with an oversized tail, hung with a dozen gold tassels, dotted with tiny rubies; her earrings were set with two rubies, each the size of a pigeon’s egg, the pinnacle of extravagance.","Her gown was of kesi silk embroidered with gold-thread crabapple blossoms, each step she took shimmering with golden light.","In comparison, Huan Qingtang’s clothes and jewelry were not as delicate and dazzling, but she still held her own in presence, because she wore a set of jadeite ornaments gifted by the Grand Madam.","Cheng Zhao’s jewelry was of gold matched with pearls. Compared to the two of them, it might be less valuable, but its quality was not inferior.","Among the three, Huan Qingtang was steady and composed, exuding the dignity of a leading mistress; Mu Jiang was arrogant, flashy, and beautiful, and being pregnant gave her a unique privilege.","As for Cheng Zhao, she was not outshone. Her features and figure were even more superior. Even if her clothes and jewelry were not as fine, she was still dazzling and eye-catching.","“The Duke truly is blessed with good fortune,” someone deliberately remarked.","The words were vague, not singling anyone out, yet it seemed to praise all three women at once.","Mu Jiang glanced at Huan Qingtang, then at Cheng Zhao. She saw both of them looking straight ahead, their expressions unchanged, which made Mu Jiang’s own furtive glances seem petty.","Indignation welled up inside her.","But on such an occasion, she dared not cause trouble. She silently stood still.","“Nonsense—my daughter-in-law is clearly the true beauty,” the Second Madam thought to herself as she also looked at them.","In her opinion, neither Huan Qingtang nor Mu Jiang was as attractive as Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao had good skin and good bone structure; no matter how she dressed, she was beautiful.","The other two, if they insisted on comparing with her, would always fall short somehow.","“Don’t flatter yourselves by trying to match Zhaozhao. You can’t,” the Second Madam thought further.","Luckily, she had gained some tact now.","In the past, she would have said it out loud.","After the birthday greetings, several clan relatives gathered around the Grand Madam, sitting with her and making small talk. The daughters-in-law and granddaughters-in-law had to go attend to their duties.","Mu Jiang sat nearby.","Great-Aunt kept praising her: “Secondary Wife is truly a peerless beauty, and she even looks a bit like Grandaunt. No wonder the Grand Madam dotes on her.”","As she spoke, she cautiously observed the Grand Madam’s expression.","The Grand Madam looked at Mu Jiang with affectionate indulgence, showing no sadness.","Great-Aunt continued, “She’s even more graceful than before. That belly must surely be carrying a son. The pregnancy signs are good, and she’s steady.”","She cited examples of the signs when she had given birth to sons to affirm Mu Jiang’s condition.","The Grand Madam indeed beamed with joy: “May your kind words come true.”","Mu Jiang’s smile grew even more radiant: “I’ve had several dreams, and in every one, I dreamed of a boy.”","“That’s a pregnancy dream—it can’t be wrong,” Great-Aunt said.","The Grand Madam sighed with emotion: “Among all the children in this house, Ah Jiang pleases me the most. And now we also have Huan Qingtang; she is considerate and thoughtful, and has deep refinement. When I chose her back then, she was selected from hundreds—truly unique among scholarly families.”","Mu Jiang’s smile faded a few degrees.","Huan Qingtang again!","Great-Aunt chuckled, “Speaking of scholarly families...”","She paused there, glancing at the Grand Madam.","She wanted to bring up Cheng Zhao.","Seeing the Grand Madam’s expression turn instantly cold, Great-Aunt shifted her words, “Indeed, among all the families in the world, the Huan family stands supreme.”","The Grand Madam’s face returned to normal.","So Great-Aunt thought to herself: Before the Grand Madam, Cheng Zhao doesn’t even rank. Today, she would have to flatter Huan Qingtang more.","Huan Qingtang was the legitimate eldest daughter-in-law.","Compared to Huan Qingtang, Mu Jiang was barely a favored concubine.","And that favored concubine only had a slight edge because she was pregnant.","“Cheng Zhao is somewhat unlucky. With beauty like hers, and having been granted marriage by the Empress, she would have had an easy life marrying into any other family,” Great-Aunt thought.","But she had to marry into the Zhou family.","Among all the nobles at court, only the Zhou family could stand against the Empress’s maternal family, the Guo clan.","A person’s fate, truly hard to say.","In Great-Aunt’s eyes, Cheng Zhao was exceptionally beautiful and socially adept. Leaving aside personal preferences, it was hard not to steal a few more glances at her.","Within the Shou’an Courtyard, everyone had their own thoughts.","Taking the opportunity to get some air, Mu Jiang sought out her trusted maid and instructed her to carry out properly the tasks she had ordered a few days prior.","The trusted maid acknowledged the order.","Cheng Zhao was receiving guests. The vast majority of the guests were very warm toward her, not treating her as inferior to Huan Qingtang.","In fact, the guests got along with her even better.","Cheng Zhao was sharp-tongued, quick-witted, and could laugh and joke easily, making her much more approachable than Huan Qingtang.","Huan Qingtang was elegant, noble, and proper, but some of the honored ladies came from military families and recognized only a few characters, not being fond of reading. Talking to Huan Qingtang was an ordeal for them.","Cheng Zhao was different.","Young as she was, she knew a little about everything under heaven and earth. When it came to common folk humor, as long as it wasn’t too vulgar, she could keep up.","Of course, the honored ladies who came as guests to the Chen Duke’s estate wouldn’t dare say anything too crude.","Regardless of how people outside compared the two, the honored ladies clearly preferred Cheng Zhao—that was plain for all to see.","The only one who paid little attention to Cheng Zhao was Lady Chu of the Feng’en Bo Estate.","The Chu family’s daughter had taken the initiative to break off an engagement with Cheng Zhao’s family, without even giving a proper reason. In short, the two families were now at odds. Cheng Zhao didn’t bother with her either, leaving her entirely in Huan Qingtang’s hands to entertain.","Accompanied by Huan Qingtang, Lady Chu went to the Grand Madam’s courtyard.","On the way, Lady Chu said, “From now on, you should visit our home often. Our family is related by marriage to the Grand Madam, but we have no wish to see anything foul.”","The “foul thing” she meant was Cheng Zhao.","Huan Qingtang pretended not to understand and simply smiled: “I will certainly come to visit often, madam. Please don’t mind me being a nuisance.”","“Of course not. My daughter is just like you—well-read and well-mannered,” Lady Chu said.","In the Shou’an Courtyard, Lady Chu kept praising Huan Qingtang.","Cheng Zhao’s mother, three aunts, and her eldest sister also arrived to offer birthday congratulations. Her third sister came with her mother-in-law, the Princess of Jingnan.","The Princess of Jingnan seldom took her youngest daughter-in-law out in society, afraid people would gossip, but she treated Cheng Ying very well and was protective.","At the midday banquet, eighty percent of the guests had arrived.","There were also eighteen dishes, one of which was hibiscus soup.","“This hibiscus soup is truly excellent.”","“It’s been a long time since I saw such a splendid vegetarian dish. It really opened my eyes.”","“Which chef made this?” the Lady of Feng’en Bo asked.","The Grand Madam smiled and said to Huan Qingtang, “It’s from the head chef at Jin’an Temple, isn’t it? Huan Qingtang, you were in charge of the banquet. Tell them.”","Huan Qingtang was startled for a moment.","But she quickly understood the Grand Madam’s intent.","She stood up: “Yes, it’s from the head chef at Jin’an Temple.”","All the guests were full of praise.","Some people praised Huan Qingtang for her filial piety, thinking of such a vegetarian dish; others admired her resourcefulness for being able to invite the chef from Jin’an Temple. The Princess of Jingnan, however, seemed to hesitate, as if she had something to say. Seated at the main table beneath the Dowager, she paused for a moment before finally speaking with a smile: “This is not the Furong Soup made by the chef of Jin’an Temple.”"]},{"number":88,"title":"Chapter 88: Slapped in Public","paragraphs":["The Zhang family of Jingnan Prince’s Mansion were the only non-imperial clan to hold the title of prince in Shengjing.","During the late emperor’s reign, he had shown almost indulgent favor toward the Zhangs; moreover, the Zhangs had sided with the current emperor when he was made crown prince, earning them some merit.","The present emperor was now greatly dissatisfied with this princely house of a different surname, but he still dared not act rashly against the Zhang family.","As for landholdings, the Zhangs’ estates were perhaps the only ones that could rival the Zhous’, though outsiders had no real idea of how much land either family owned.","The Princess Consort Jingnan was usually modest and unassuming, and the noble ladies generally thought well of her. Even those who disliked her could find no open fault with her.","Just as everyone was praising Huan Qingtang, she spoke up and contradicted Huan Qingtang—this was a direct slap at the Grand Lady’s face.","The Zhou family had no quarrel with the Zhangs, so the Princess Consort’s words surprised everyone; a momentary hush fell over the gathering.","Even Grand Princess Fukang cast a curious glance her way.","At that very moment, the Grand Princess had a bite in her bowl. She savored it—the tofu was indeed more tender and delicate, and there was some extra flavor to it.","“...On the first and fifteenth of each month, I also observe a vegetarian fast. We have a cook in our household whose uncle is a head chef in the kitchens of Goldpeace Temple. He has mastered some true techniques and invented several vegetarian dishes of his own.","A few days ago, the head chef of Goldpeace caught a chill and didn’t dare come to cook. That’s why the Duchess asked about borrowing our cook, isn’t it? When our cook makes the Lotus Skin Broth, he adds a bit of homemade peanut paste to enhance the tofu’s aroma. Grand Lady, do taste it again—doesn’t it taste different from what you’ve had at Goldpeace Temple before?”","For a moment, the entire hall fell perfectly silent.","Huan Qingtang’s face drained of color. Calm as she prided herself on being, her eyes trembled slightly.","Cheng Shi sat together with the Second Madam; at those words, she did not move at first.","All the female guests were watching her, but she neither stood up to speak nor showed any particular expression. She simply sat in silence.","Grand Princess Fukang took another taste and laughed, “Indeed, the tofu is richer; I sensed it too just now.”","“Does it feel too heavy, Grand Lady?” the Princess Consort Jingnan asked again.","“Not really. Old folks’ tastes tend to be stronger—I didn’t notice any richness,” the Grand Lady said with a smile.","Huan Qingtang could not let the Grand Lady take the blame, and the Princess Consort had deliberately pointed this out to credit Cheng Shi. She had to say something.","Steadying her expression, Huan Qingtang forced a smile and said, “I’ve been very busy these past few days. A while ago, my sister-in-law gave me the main kitchen’s menu and told me she intended to invite the chef from Goldpeace Temple.","Goldpeace Temple is quite familiar with our household, so I sent over my name card too. I just didn’t expect the chef had been swapped halfway. I trust my sister-in-law with managing the main kitchen and didn’t make further inquiries.”","With that, she looked at Cheng Shi.","Cheng Shi rose slowly to her feet and responded with composure.","“I knew my sister-in-law was busy, which is why I didn’t trouble her with such a trivial matter. Grandmother put me in charge, so of course I have to take responsibility for everything. Whatever turns up, I handle it myself—only that way can I live up to Grandmother’s trust.”","“Cheng Shi has done very well. Today’s Lotus Skin Broth is both lovely to look at and delicious to eat,” the Grand Lady said with a warm smile. “I have always had confidence in the way you handle things.”","The atmosphere relaxed.","The earlier incident—where Huan Qingtang had been elevated only to be slapped down—seemed as if it had never happened.","One careless enough would have missed this whole game of raising up and putting down.","But unfortunately, every titled lady present was a shrewd expert, and the noble young ladies were sharp too. No one had forgotten.","“Thank you, Grandmother,” Cheng Shi replied with a laugh. “Since Grandmother has entrusted me with the gate and the main kitchen, and tonight’s fireworks display as well, I certainly won’t disappoint your high expectations.”","Through this matter, she made it clear to the guests: the credit for the main kitchen and the gate matters belonged all to her. The fireworks at the night banquet were also her responsibility.","Any excellence in these tasks was due to Cheng Shi’s ability; any mistakes would be her failure as well.","She did not covet others’ merits, nor would she let anyone steal her own.","She was neither overbearing nor overly self-effacing.","At the last Peach Blossom Banquet, the noble ladies had already formed a good impression of her. This time, they found her even cleverer and more quick-witted.","Huan Qingtang, however, fell short.","When the guests looked at her, her discomfort was nearly written on her face. She lacked the Grand Lady’s poise in the face of embarrassment.","When the midday meal ended, the guests stayed on to listen to opera and await the night banquet.","Some went to stroll in the Chen Duke’s mansion’s rear garden.","For this occasion, the Chen Duke’s estate had put out over two thousand pots of peonies.","There were many in the flower hall, and even more in the rear garden.","A senior maidservant deliberately announced, “Her Ladyship the senior young mistress prepared all these. Every peony from the Xu family’s nursery is here.”","The guests murmured among themselves, careful not to offer casual praise.","“Could it be that someone else did the work, but it’s being credited to her again?”","“Is the Grand Lady trying to back her up? With the Grand Lady’s support, she’ll become the mistress of this house one day. What a pity for Cheng Shi.”","“Still young and immature—she snatched credit in public without preparing for the counterattack, and now she’s made herself look so awkward. Her skills are poor.”","These were deliberately biting remarks.","The guests knew these peonies were the work of Huan Qingtang, because Cheng Shi had already stated that she wasn’t in charge of that task.","Lady Chu of the Feng’en Earl’s Mansion remarked, “These peonies are truly stunning, in such full bloom. It really takes the young mistress’s influence to lease the entire peony stock of the Xu family’s nursery.”","At that, one lady nearby couldn’t help snorting coldly. “No wonder the Xu family’s nursery canceled my order for a hundred peony pots.","I had placed a deposit last winter for my Spring Gathering Banquet. It turns out they were chasing after the rich and powerful—taking my peonies for this event without a word.”","The atmosphere froze instantly.","No one responded.","If even a merchant could dare cancel her peony order, her family’s clout clearly wasn’t much. The titled ladies certainly weren’t about to stick up for Huan Qingtang or defend her.","But it gave others gossip ammunition against her.","After the midday meal, Cheng Shi invited all the relatives from the Fan and Cheng families to her Courtyard of the Crimson Clouds.","The room was filled with people, lively and warm.","“Aunt, I thank you for speaking up on my behalf just now,” Cheng Shi said to the Princess Consort Jingnan.","The Third Sister, Cheng Ying, had a worthless husband, but the Princess Consort was a decent woman. She felt guilty over her youngest son’s marriage to Cheng Ying and treated her generously.","Every time Cheng Ying came home, she said her parents-in-law had no fault, and the matter of Zhang Yunqi shouldn’t make the Zhang family a target.","When preparations for the Lotus Skin Broth had been underway, Cheng Shi had guessed the Grand Lady would give the credit to Huan Qingtang.","She had spoken about it with her mother.","Her mother happened to know that the Jingnan Prince’s Mansion had such a cook, who was the nephew of the head chef at Goldpeace Temple and inherited his secret recipes.","“Better be safe than sorry. If nobody brings it up, don’t say anything,” her mother had said.","When the mother asked the Jingnan Mansion to borrow the cook, the Princess Consort agreed without hesitation.","Not only that—she also testified on Cheng Shi’s behalf at the critical moment.","Cheng Shi naturally had to express her gratitude.","“We are all kin—it was just a small favor,” the Princess Consort replied.","Second Madam looked from one to the other.","She reflected that human relationships were truly complicated.","The Chengs all detested Cheng Ying’s husband, Zhang Yunqi, yet they genuinely respected his mother, the Princess Consort. It seemed they had long accepted that a marriage alliance was about the bond between two families, separate from the relationship between husband and wife.","Not only the elders thought this way; the sisters Cheng Shi and Cheng Ying seemed to feel the same. One respected the Princess Consort, the other cherished her mother-in-law. Neither held any grievances against the Princess Consort.","As long as the elders honored each other, a marriage was considered good.","Second Madam used to dislike this way of thinking among scholarly families, seeing it in matters like this one with the Jingnan Mansion.","Now, however, she saw it might make sense after all.","She had truly become much more enlightened."]},{"number":89,"title":"Chapter 89: Want to Overthrow the Duke","paragraphs":["Inside Jiangyun Courtyard, the conversation was lively and far more engaging than at the banquet.","Everyone present was either family or closely related.","“...Zhao Zhao, why didn’t you invite Princess Qing'an?” Princess Consort Jingnan suddenly asked.","Cheng Zhao replied, “She wasn’t invited to the previous gatherings either. This time, I tried to include her, but my elder sister-in-law crossed her name off the list.”","Cheng Zhao suspected that Second Madam was unaware of the behind-the-scenes matchmaking Princess Qing'an had arranged between Zhou Yuanshen and Huan Qingtang, but Princess Consort Jingnan certainly knew.","If Second Madam had known, given her personality, she would have told Cheng Zhao long ago.","Cheng Zhao realized that her younger brother-in-law, Zhou Yuanqi, inherited his inability to keep secrets from his grandmother.","“...Did you used to invite Princess Qing'an?” Cheng Zhao asked, directing the question to the princess consort.","The princess consort only smiled, “This is only my second visit to the Chen Guogong residence, so I’m not very familiar with the customs here.”","She added, “Next time you come to our residence, I’m fairly close with Princess Qing'an. I’ll introduce you.”","Fairly close...","Introduce me...","She definitely knows!","Cheng Zhao glanced at her mother.","Her mother smiled helplessly, resigned to Cheng Zhao’s habit of prying into secrets.","This matter concerned Cheng Zhao’s future, and she truly wanted to uncover the past between Huan Qingtang and Zhou Yuanshen. But from what she knew of Zhou Yuanshen, asking him would be pointless—he wouldn’t say a word.","Amid the lively chatter, Zhou Yuanshen arrived.","After changing his clothes, he came forward to pay his respects.","“Why are you here? Aren’t you supposed to be attending to guests?” Second Madam asked him.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “There are honored guests inside Jiangyun Courtyard as well. I came back especially to pay my respects, Mother.”","Second Madam was speechless.","She hadn’t put on a proud face for her son, and almost caused him to offend someone. She regretted speaking without thinking.","Cheng Zhao smiled beside them, “Guogongye is thoughtful. I’m here to entertain the guests, so you can greet them and then get back to your duties.”","Everyone else agreed, telling him to get back to work and not waste time on formalities.","Zhou Yuanshen had many matters to attend to today; the guests in the outer courtyard were being hosted by him and the Second Master.","Only then did Zhou Yuanshen leave.","Everyone was smiling, except Princess Consort Jingnan, who looked a little gloomy.","Compared to Zhou Yuanshen, her own son was simply too disappointing.","Thankfully, the in-laws were reasonable, and Cheng Ying was tolerant and magnanimous, so no one had lost face.","As Zhou Yuanshen left, he glanced at Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao saw him out of Jiangyun Courtyard.","“...I heard about what just happened,” he said.","Cheng Zhao replied, “It’s a small matter, nothing serious.”","“It was your grandmother who went too far,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","Even if the Dowager Madame was indifferent to affairs, she couldn’t be unaware that the main kitchen was managed by Cheng Zhao. Yet she stole the credit for herself.","She couldn’t even maintain this basic fairness.","It was like in the court—when the emperor showed favoritism, it bred sycophants and corrupt officials.","Once people tasted the power, they became addicted and demanded more, trampling on others’ efforts, even lives.","“Were you prepared in advance, or was it a lucky accident?” Zhou Yuanshen asked again.","Cheng Zhao said, “Guogongye, please don’t think ill of me. I was just cautious and kept a watchful eye. I didn’t expect it to come up.”","“That’s not being distrustful; it’s being prudent,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “You did well. Truly a worthy Lady of the Highest Rank.”","His words were praise, but carried a hint of something strange.","Cheng Zhao didn’t think much of it and took it as a compliment, smiling, “Thank you, Guogongye.”","Zhou Yuanshen nodded slightly and left Jiangyun Courtyard.","Halfway through, he skirted around a corridor and ran into Mu Jiang.","Mu Jiang was adorned in all her finery, her garments lavish and rich.","This made Zhou Yuanshen think of the royal family of the Northern Di.","There was once a Khan of the Northern Di who adored horses; his horses had tails braided with gemstones of every color; their saddles were inlaid with the finest woven fabrics, and their hooves were shod in gold.","Later, the soldiers captured his horses, but those horses could barely run anymore — utterly useless.","Yet the useless beasts still flaunted themselves, proud and arrogant.","Much like Mu Jiang now, her head crowned with ruby jewelry.","She was also the Dowager Madame’s carefully adorned “pet,” pitiful yet tragic. But she had not the slightest awareness of her plight, basking complacently in such splendor.","“Third Brother.” She spotted Zhou Yuanshen and stood up happily. “Third Brother, I’ve been waiting here for you. I saw you go that way and thought you’d be coming back.”","“Is there something you need?” Zhou Yuanshen asked.","“Third Brother, the child is kicking me now. Would you like to feel?” Mu Jiang leaned in closer.","Zhou Yuanshen’s face remained expressionless. “Take good care of the pregnancy.”","He brushed past her, about to leave.","Mu Jiang reached out to grab his hand but missed.","“Third Brother!” she called out sharply.","The Chen Duke’s residence was bustling with guests today, many eyes watching.","Hearing her loud call, some turned to look; not far off, Huan Qingtang, preparing to visit the main kitchen, was about to pass by. She and her maid stood there awkwardly.","Mu Jiang noticed her.","Zhou Yuanshen halted.","Mu Jiang stepped forward, wanting desperately to collapse into his arms.","But she recalled last winter, when she had deliberately flown a kite in his path to throw herself at him.","Back then, she had giggled coquettishly, hoping to soften his heart; even if he pushed her away, she would have taken it as a playful jest.","Unexpectedly, Zhou Yuanshen had outright thrown her off that time. She had fallen to the ground, her knee bruised by a stone, aching for quite a while.","Now she was pregnant, guests were everywhere, and Huan Qingtang was nearby. Mu Jiang, for once, had some sense and didn’t throw herself into his arms.","She feared he would push her away again.","Yet that night at Jin’an Temple, they had been clearly affectionate.","Mu Jiang had felt only pain and anxiety then, but she had tried hard to create an illusion of happiness. He had been breathing hard on her, deeply moved.","In the darkness, without seeing his face, lying with her back turned to him, she still made him feel a man’s pride.","And now she was pregnant again.","Why was he still dissatisfied?","Mu Jiang thought this over, feeling a little wronged: “Third Brother, you haven’t once looked at our child alone.”","Her belly was already slightly rounded, the shape becoming visible.","She felt fuller, more voluptuous.","The nursemaid had said that after three months, they could be intimate again. She should show him.","This time, she wanted the candlelight bright, to let him see their child and her beauty.","“Is now the time to talk about this?” Zhou Yuanshen asked coldly, his face unreadable.","“I don’t know when I can say it,” Mu Jiang replied. “Third Brother, when will you go to Lijing Courtyard? Or let me come to your Chenhui Courtyard? Could you give our son a name?”","Zhou Yuanshen said, “We’ll talk about it later.”","\"Third Brother, I know you're upset today. Some people stole the credit and embarrassed the Chen Duke’s household in front of the guests. Your anger is only natural,\" Mu Jiang raised her voice.","But Huan Qingtang didn’t leave.","She just stood there.","Mu Jiang spoke, and she listened—neither stepping forward nor retreating.","“Don’t be angry. You still have me and the child,” Mu Jiang said.","Zhou Yuanshen heard this and replied coldly, “If you have nothing to say to me, why keep repeating the same few words?”","With that, he walked away.","Mu Jiang called after him again, but he seemed not to hear, ignoring the curious looks from the guests.","As he passed Huan Qingtang, she bowed respectfully and said, “Your Grace.”","Zhou Yuanshen acknowledged her with a grunt and returned the greeting, “Sister-in-law.”","“Your Grace, I...” Huan Qingtang spoke again, as if she had something to say.","But Zhou Yuanshen didn’t stop; he kept walking.","In the past, he would have at least given her some dignity."]},{"number":90,"title":"Chapter 90: Intentional Mischief","paragraphs":["Mu Jiang walked over slowly.","She gazed calmly at Huan Qingtang and said, “If you have any words you wish to say to the Lord Duke, I can relay them for you.”","Huan Qingtang looked at her, then after a moment, smiled. “Secondary Wife, why do you bear me such ill will? I have no quarrel with you.”","“You know why yourself!”","Huan Qingtang leaned in closer, almost whispering in her ear: “You have your backing, and I have mine. Besides, the Lord Duke respects me. You’ll gain nothing by trying to provoke me.”","With that, she sidestepped Mu Jiang and walked away.","Mu Jiang stood frozen, still processing, as Huan Qingtang departed.","If she pressed the matter further, it would devolve into a loud argument. On such an occasion, Mu Jiang valued her dignity.","She gritted her teeth and endured.","The Second Madam’s maid was passing by on an errand and happened to witness the scene. She later reported it to the Second Madam, who in turn told Cheng Zhao.","After hearing it, Cheng Zhao thought quietly for a moment and then said, “Do you think the Secondary Wife might stir up trouble?”","“What trouble could she stir? At worst, she’ll cause some mischief—a little scratching or sulking,” the Second Madam said dismissively.","Cheng Zhao replied, “I’ll send Qiubai to check around, just to ensure nothing is overlooked.”","Qiubai was skilled in martial arts but had a delicate, unassuming appearance; she could move about without drawing attention. Being close to Cheng Zhao, she was ideal for acting as Cheng Zhao’s eyes and ears.","Cheng Zhao immediately dispatched her.","Inside Crimson Cloud Courtyard, the atmosphere was lively. The guests conversed merrily, and before they knew it, dusk had fallen. A servant from the banquet hall came to summon them.","That evening’s feast would be held in the main hall for all guests, and the stage for the opera had already been set up.","Lanterns were hung everywhere, interspersed with standing horn-shaped palace lanterns placed a few steps apart, illuminating the entire area brightly.","The horn-shaped palace lanterns came in various forms and painted designs, each one a small spectacle to admire.","As night fell, all seats beneath the head table in the banquet hall were cleared, and the guests moved to lower positions.","Cheng Zhao immediately understood: the Emperor was coming!","He truly intended to attend the Dowager Madame’s birthday celebration in person.","The Zhou family’s power and splendor had just reached another new height tonight.","Soon, armored guards took their positions.","The moment everyone in the hall realized the Emperor was arriving, silence fell. Every person held their breath.","When the Emperor ascended to the head seat, the guests knelt in obeisance.","“Rise, all of you,” the Emperor said.","Dressed in casual robes and accompanied by the Crown Prince, who was not yet ten years old, the Emperor took the seat of honor. He gestured for the Dowager Madame to sit beside him, but she politely declined, engaging in a brief exchange of deferential protest.","Afterward, the Dowager Madame summoned the Zhou family to present themselves before the Emperor.","Cheng Zhao followed behind the Second Madam.","“Which one is the Duchess of Chen?” the Emperor asked.","Cheng Zhao stepped forward: “Your subject’s wife pays respects to Your Majesty. Long live the Emperor.”","She kowtowed three times, keeping her gaze lowered.","The Emperor did not ask her to raise her head but said, “The Duchess of Chen is gentle and magnanimous—truly the hallmark of a noble household.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","Many terms existed to describe noblewomen, and the Emperor surely knew them.","Yet he chose two: gentle and magnanimous.","Gentle meant not contending or competing; magnanimous meant being able to tolerate both a pregnant concubine and a widowed sister-in-law serving as a concurrent heir.","He was indeed well-informed about every matter concerning the Zhou family.","Cheng Zhao also recalled her grandfather mentioning that the Emperor had once instructed Zhou Yuanshen and Mu Jiang to conceive a child, promising that the child would one day be named Crown Prince. That was before the heir apparent was established—almost like a mad rambling.","Tonight, however, the Emperor was perfectly lucid.","When he finished speaking, Cheng Zhao had to express her gratitude: “Thank you, Your Majesty. Your subject’s wife is deeply honored.”","The Emperor then dismissed her.","He exchanged a few more words with Zhou Yuanshen before instructing everyone to take their seats.","As she withdrew, Cheng Zhao quickly observed the Emperor and the Crown Prince.","She had visited Kunning Palace several times before, but had only met Empress Guo, never the Crown Prince.","The Crown Prince resembled Empress Guo somewhat; and like the Emperor, he was pale, thin, and possessed a sinister look in his young eyes.","Cheng Zhao often felt that her own brother-in-law acted like an adult. Compared to the Crown Prince, her brother-in-law seemed healthy and ruddy-cheeked, still full of childish innocence—truly still a child.","The Zhou family members accompanied the Emperor at the head table, while the other guests sat below.","Cheng Zhao was seated a fair distance from the Emperor and the Crown Prince. With the clang of gongs and drums from the stage, she had to strain to catch their conversation.","The Crown Prince asked, “When will the cranes dance?”","The Dowager Madame chuckled, “They will be prepared shortly.”","“I want to see the cranes dance—it’s an auspicious omen. A blessing for the Dowager Madame’s long life and a blessing for the empire’s prosperity,” the Crown Prince declared.","Those words were surely coached, but the sentiment was auspicious.","The Emperor nodded approvingly.","The Dowager Madame was delighted as well: “Your Highness, first have a sip of light refreshment. The cranes will be ready to dance soon. No need to rush.”","The Crown Prince sat up straight.","Mu Jiang, seated in the farthest corner, seemed to hear those words too.","Her expression shifted. She stood up, intending to leave.","But the Dowager Madame immediately fixed her with a warning look, signaling her to sit down.","Mu Jiang had no choice but to comply, though unease gnawed at her.","She hadn’t expected the Emperor to come, nor had she anticipated the Crown Prince’s speech. All she had wanted was to humiliate Huan Qingtang.","What should she do now?","Mu Jiang’s expression flickered several times. She glanced at Zhou Yuanshen for help, but he was busy talking to the Crown Prince, ignoring her.","The Emperor, however, cast a look her way.","His gaze was benevolent, almost fatherly.","Mu Jiang often saw the Emperor. She had been found by him and entrusted to the Dowager Madame’s care—she was practically half a daughter to him.","She always believed that once she bore the Zhou family’s eldest son, the Emperor would grant her the title of a commandery princess. Then, both Huan Qingtang and Cheng Zhao would be beneath her.","Her son would become the head of the Zhou clan, the future Duke of Chen.","The Duke’s prosperity was tied to Mu Jiang as well, and she didn’t want to cause trouble now, but it seemed too late to salvage things.","No, she needed to find an opportunity to slip away.","Just as she was thinking, she overheard the Dowager Madame saying to the Emperor, “...Lady Huan arranged it all. She’s exceptionally capable.”","Mu Jiang was stunned.","Hadn’t Huan Qingtang just embarrassed herself over the vegetarian meal? Yet here the Dowager Madame was praising her before the Emperor—could it be that she too was seeking an honorary title?","Mu Jiang was the one pregnant, so why did others reap all the benefits?","Would Huan Qingtang truly be married into a concurrent branch?","Mu Jiang wavered, wanting to remedy the situation, but hesitated.","The feast began, and the stage grew lively. Dances followed the opera.","Then, Nanny Sun from Longevity Court quietly approached Huan Qingtang and whispered a few words. Huan Qingtang’s expression shifted dramatically, disbelief spreading across her face.","Mu Jiang noticed and felt a secret satisfaction.","She was pregnant—who could punish her? Even if trouble arose, it would be a minor matter, not a court affair.","She let herself feel at ease.","Huan Qingtang rose and walked to the Dowager Madame’s side.","She murmured something to her.","But the Dowager Madame replied, “You and Lady Cheng go check it out.”","Huan Qingtang acknowledged and summoned Cheng Zhao. The two sisters-in-law left the head table.","“What’s wrong, Sister-in-Law?” Cheng Zhao asked.","“Come with me,” Huan Qingtang said, striding forward.","Cheng Zhao followed, and they headed to a yard beside the banquet hall.","In the yard, someone was weeping.","“I don’t know what happened—I was watching them the whole time. I only went inside for a cup of tea...”","Before the maid could knock, Huan Qingtang pushed open the yard gate herself.","She and Cheng Zhao saw what lay inside and froze.","All the cranes lay dead in their cages."]},{"number":91,"title":"Chapter 91: Cheng Zhao's \"Show\"","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao saw the situation in the courtyard and quietly stood at the entrance without going further inside.","Huan Qingtang was surrounded by maids and women as she entered the courtyard. Her cheeks kept trembling, although she tried her best to stay calm.","She didn't notice Cheng Zhao.","\"...Madam, I'm wronged!\" The stewardess in charge of the cranes knelt on the ground, crying bitterly. \"I don't know how these cranes died.\"","\"Take your time and tell me. When did you notice something was wrong?\" Huan Qingtang asked.","\"They were fine this morning. You invited the masters to teach the cranes to dance. They trained the cranes at noon.","You gave the order to let the masters have a good meal, preparing for the performance later. After they went to have their meals, the cranes' legs went weak.","I thought they were just tired. Then I saw them foaming at the mouth and all of them fell down. One died, and the other seven also seemed abnormal. That's why I quickly came to tell you.","In just such a short time, the other seven also died. I don't know the reason. They were only given water once in between. The masters said not to feed them because they would use food to lure the cranes during the performance later.\"","The stewardess was crying loudly and then said, \"Could it be that they starved to death?\"","Huan Qingtang pondered and then turned around and said, \"Sister-in-law, what do you think...\"","But she didn't see Cheng Zhao.","When she turned around again, she saw Cheng Zhao standing at the courtyard entrance with her maid Suyue. Both of them covered their noses with handkerchiefs and looked like they didn't dare to enter.","Huan Qingtang was almost infuriated.","She quickly walked out and said to Cheng Zhao, \"Sister-in-law, Grandmother asked us to come and have a look. What are you doing at the door?\"","Cheng Zhao gave her a helpless look.","Suyue replied, \"Madam, our young mistress can't stand the smell of dead things. She has been afraid of dead poultry since she was a child. She has been retching just now.\"","Cheng Zhao said, \"Sister-in-law, I don't know what's going on either. If I vomited in the courtyard, it would be even more embarrassing.\"","Huan Qingtang said, \"...Sister-in-law, what do you think happened?\"","\"Sister-in-law, you arranged the birthday banquet, and you were in charge of the crane dance performance alone. Asking me is really embarrassing me,\" Cheng Zhao said.","She then added, \"Sister-in-law, have you finished the interrogation? If so, I'm going to leave. I really can't stand it.\"","She pretended to vomit again.","Suyue quickly said, \"Young mistress, take it easy. Let's take a few more steps back.\"","Cheng Zhao waved her hand, indicating that she could still endure it.","Huan Qingtang's face turned blue and white. She didn't expect such a thing to happen and didn't know how to deal with it for a moment. She wanted to shift the responsibility to Cheng Zhao, but Cheng Zhao didn't take the bait.","Apart from Cheng Zhao, it was useless to shift the blame to other stewards because she was the \"general steward\" of the entire birthday banquet.","Cheng Zhao seemed to be in great pain.","Huan Qingtang was waiting for her to give suggestions and come up with solutions, but she was weakly relying on her maid.","In order to avoid getting involved in this trouble, she didn't even enter the courtyard.","\"Sister-in-law, in my opinion, the two of us...\"","\"I can't stand it anymore!\" Cheng Zhao trotted a few steps to the side, bent down and lowered her head. When her back was turned to Huan Qingtang, she pressed her finger against the root of her tongue.","She didn't vomit anything because her stomach was always in good condition, but there was a very real retching sound.","She coughed painfully.","Suyue supported her with concern and asked, \"Young mistress, how do you feel?\"","The stewardesses and maids who came with them also came out of the courtyard later.","One stewardess said, \"Could it be that the third young mistress is pregnant?\"","Huan Qingtang looked at Cheng Zhao.","After a while, Cheng Zhao came back. The stewardess asked with concern, \"Third young mistress, how do you feel?\"","\"I just can't stand the smell of dead poultry. You may not notice it, but I can smell it,\" Cheng Zhao covered her nose with a handkerchief. \"Sister-in-law, can you stay and handle it? I'll go back first. If Grandmother wants to punish me, I'll bear it myself.\"","Huan Qingtang said, \"...\"","The stewardess sized up Huan Qingtang's expression and said, \"How about letting the third young mistress go back first? She really can't help here.\"","If Cheng Zhao was also pregnant, she would be very noble in the future. The stewardess wanted to make a good relationship with her.","Huan Qingtang said, \"Sister-in-law, you can go back first.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","She returned to the flower hall where the birthday banquet was being held.","When she walked up to the dowager lady, Cheng Zhao said in a voice that could be heard by the dowager lady, the emperor, and Zhou Yuanshen, \"Sister-in-law was in charge of the crane dance performance. I really couldn't help. Sister-in-law told me to come back first.\"","\"How's the situation?\" the dowager lady asked with a smile.","The emperor was also curious and asked, \"What happened?\"","\"Your Majesty, I didn't enter the courtyard, so I'm not very clear,\" Cheng Zhao said. Then she said to the dowager lady, \"Sister-in-law is wise and decisive. She can handle it.\"","The dowager lady still smiled and said, \"Then go and sit down and listen to the opera.\"","Cheng Zhao said yes.","The emperor and the crown prince were there. The people in the main seats didn't dare to get up or move around casually. They couldn't leave their seats without permission.","Zhou Yuanshen looked at Cheng Zhao with an inquiring look in his eyes. Cheng Zhao just waved her hand to tell him to rest assured.","Huan Qingtang didn't come back for half an hour.","The crown prince asked about the crane dance performance twice.","\"...This batch of cranes is the most spiritual. Father also said he would give me two to raise in the Eastern Palace,\" the crown prince said.","He was a little expectant.","The emperor said, \"Cranes are not something that will make one indulge in pleasure. If you like them, raise them. They will make the courtyard look auspicious.\"","The dowager lady's smile was a bit hard to maintain.","Then Huan Qingtang finally came back and whispered to the dowager lady.","The dowager lady was always very calm.","\"...It's time to set off the fireworks, right?\" the dowager lady said with a smile.","The crown prince was inexplicably nervous.","The emperor glanced at him, and he sat back obediently with a little sweat on his forehead.","Cheng Zhao stepped forward and said to the dowager lady, \"Grandmother, I have a new and interesting way to play. It's both beautiful and fun. We can just skip the fireworks.\"","The crown prince relaxed a bit. He looked at Cheng Zhao curiously.","The emperor said, \"Not setting off fireworks, isn't it a bit of a let-down?\"","\"Your Majesty, please allow me to keep it a secret for now,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The emperor seemed to be in a very good mood tonight and his emotions were stable. He said, \"If your secret isn't good enough, I'll revoke your imperial title.\"","Cheng Zhao agreed.","She was smiling on the surface, but her palm was wet with sweat.","Many times, people tell the truth in a joking way.","It seemed that Cheng Zhao's \"superior imperial title\" had already annoyed the dowager lady, and the dowager lady wanted to take it away.","And transfer it to Huan Qingtang.","Cheng Zhao sent someone to make arrangements.","Soon, colorful carrier pigeons took off into the sky above the flower hall.","The pigeons were brightly colored, and they even sparkled in the night sky.","The guests had never seen such a sight before and were all amazed.","The pigeons even formed a character \"Fu\" (happiness).","If it was just the dowager lady's birthday banquet, the character \"Shou\" (longevity) would be better, but since the emperor was also there, the character \"Fu\" had a better meaning.","\"Really good!\" the emperor said.","The crown prince clapped his hands happily.","There were thousands of pigeons, and then they scattered in the night sky, looking like stars and adding more splendor to the night view.","The guests were full of praise.","\"Why do the pigeons glow? And how did they form the character?\" the crown prince asked.","Cheng Zhao explained it to him.","\"Your Highness, our flower hall is at a lower position, and the gate tower of the main courtyard is at a higher position. At the higher position, black branches were arranged to form the character 'Fu' and pigeon food was stuck on them.","This batch of pigeons had been hungry. They immediately went to look for food, so it looked like they formed the character themselves,\" Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","He added, \"As for the glowing effect, it's achieved by grinding night pearls into fine powder and adding some powder of red obsidian. They smeared this mixture on the pigeons, and it's these powders that make them glow.\""]},{"number":92,"title":"Chapter 92: Destroyed the Dual Inheritance","paragraphs":["The most important thing was to make the pigeons glow, allowing them to replace fireworks as they burst open in the night sky.","The luminous pearls were Cheng Zhao’s own. Back when she was in Fengzhou, she had once gone out to sea with her maids Suyue and Qiubai and brought back seven such pearls.","Her mother kept them in the cellar, where they shone brilliantly at night.","The red sunstone was the work of her fourth brother, Cheng Chao. The stone was originally a dull grayish brown; only after being exposed to the sun for a period of time did it turn red and glow in the dark.","It was also quite expensive.","The pigeons themselves had an even more interesting origin—they, too, came from Cheng Chao.","Initially, Cheng Chao had tried to ask Cheng Zhao for money, but she threatened him: “If you keep stealing grandfather’s treasured calligraphy scrolls and selling them to booksellers, flooding the market with forgeries so convincing they’re nearly indistinguishable from the originals, all for a hefty profit—what do you think will happen if Grandfather finds out? Won’t Father give you a beating?”","Their father was indeed the type to hit his children.","Cheng Chao begged her to keep quiet and never asked for money again.","He could be a bit of a nuisance at times, but he was also thorough in his work, handling the tasks Cheng Zhao assigned him exceptionally well.","Cheng Zhao explained the origin of the “pigeon trick” to the Grand Matriarch, the Emperor, and the Crown Prince, then said with a smile to the Grand Matriarch: “Grandmother, these pigeons don’t come from merchants. They were sent by pigeon breeders from the nearby villages, who heard that Your Ladyship was celebrating a birthday. They offered them as a token of good fortune for you.”","The Emperor nodded with satisfaction upon hearing this and said, “This is indeed very thoughtful.”","The Grand Matriarch’s authority did not conflict with the Emperor’s in the slightest. No matter how her honor was displayed, the Emperor would not feel jealous.","Instead, he felt that Cheng Zhao had handled the matter beautifully; the gesture was full of good omens.","The Grand Matriarch beamed, not directly at Cheng Zhao, but at the Emperor: “These children don’t know their limits. I, this old woman, only managed this good fortune by borrowing a little of Your Majesty’s prestige. These pigeons are actually a prayer for Your Majesty and the realm.”","The Emperor laughed: “In that case, I must reward the Duchess of Chen.”","The Grand Matriarch replied, “That would be her great fortune.”","Cheng Zhao immediately knelt and kowtowed: “I thank Your Majesty for your boundless grace.”","The Emperor thought for a moment, then said to the eunuch beside him, “Reward her with five hundred taels of gold and a set of ruby head ornaments.”","The eunuch acknowledged the order and noted it down.","Cheng Zhao kowtowed again to express her gratitude.","Last time, the Grand Matriarch had rewarded her with golden leaves worth only fifty taels, which was already considered quite generous; now the Emperor casually gave her five hundred taels of gold.","It was an extremely heavy reward.","Many high-ranking generals who had rendered illustrious military service were only granted “five hundred taels of gold” when the Emperor bestowed titles upon them.","And that was already from a generous emperor. Some emperors, when enfeoffing a marquis, only rewarded “two hundred taels of gold.”","The Emperor had given Cheng Zhao five hundred taels of gold on a whim. Of course, it was not to elevate Cheng Zhao herself, but to honor the Grand Matriarch.","It was also meant to show all the nobles in the capital that the Zhou family’s favor would always be unique and unparalleled.","As for the source of this imperial favor, Cheng Zhao was somewhat puzzled.","After the evening banquet ended, the guests departed in high spirits, all chatting about the night’s events.","Just as everyone was about to leave, the Crown Prince was still asking about the cranes. The Emperor stared at him quietly for a few seconds, and the Crown Prince immediately shrank his shoulders, his expression dejected.","Only then did Cheng Zhao understand one of the purposes behind this reward.","As the crowd dispersed, Cheng Zhao saw off her own relatives and tidied up. She sat in the outer courtyard’s main hall until the gatekeeper had finished all his duties before returning to the inner courtyard.","By the time she got back, it was already past midnight.","“Madam, I saw the Secondary Wife’s maid making trouble, but I didn’t stop her; Nanfeng saw it too and told me not to say anything,” Qiubai reported.","Cheng Zhao said, “You did well.”","“I was scared too. If the Secondary Wife had harmed the cranes and the Emperor became furious, it could have implicated the entire Duke’s mansion, and you would have suffered as well. But that kid Nanfeng is sharper than me. I thought it best to listen to him,” Qiubai said, patting her chest.","Cheng Zhao smiled and said to her, “The Emperor values the Grand Matriarch, and the Grand Matriarch dotes on the Secondary Wife. She can do whatever she wants. Your judgment this time was correct. Everyone around the Duke is useful. From now on, observe more and learn more.”","Qiubai acknowledged the advice.","Since Zhou Yuanshen did not come over, Cheng Zhao naturally assumed he had rested elsewhere. Just as she was preparing to wash up and go to sleep, he arrived at the Ronghua Courtyard.","“...After seeing off the Crown Prince and His Majesty earlier, I talked with Father for a while,” Zhou Yuanshen said. “Then Grandmother called for me again.”","Cheng Zhao asked, “What did she say?”","“Just trivial matters. I’m tired from today. Let’s rest first,” he replied.","Cheng Zhao didn’t press further; she was indeed exhausted to the point of collapse and couldn’t hold on any longer.","She went to sleep, but the Grand Matriarch’s Shou’an Courtyard was still awake.","Mu Jiang was kneeling in the side chamber.","Huan Qingtang stood beside her, gently pleading: “Grandmother, please let the Secondary Wife rise. She is with child.”","The Grand Matriarch said, “Confine her to her quarters until she gives birth.”","Mu Jiang wept bitterly: “Grandmother, that will be unhealthy for both me and the child. I beg you to have mercy on me.”","The Grand Matriarch closed her eyes, feeling very helpless.","Mu Jiang knew exactly how to manipulate the Grand Matriarch. Since she was pregnant, the Grand Matriarch could neither hit nor scold her, nor impose any real punishment.","That was why she dared to act so recklessly.","“...Originally, tonight His Majesty was going to order the Duke to take a secondary wife to carry on the lineage. But to suppress the ‘Crane Dance,’ His Majesty had no choice but to heavily reward Cheng. The two of you fought among yourselves, and Cheng reaped all the benefits,” the Grand Matriarch said, deeply pained and furious.","Mu Jiang prostrated herself and wept, but in her heart, she felt no regret.","She had sabotaged the plan for a secondary wife.","No matter how much the Grand Matriarch analyzed the situation for her, Mu Jiang simply did not want to share her third brother.","Having Cheng Zhao in the picture was already unbearable for Mu Jiang; adding Huan Qingtang would only infuriate her to death.","Mu Jiang didn’t care about the broader situation, whether it was favorable or unfavorable to her. She only sought what made her own heart comfortable.","Huan Qingtang soothed the Grand Matriarch: “Grandmother, His Majesty’s generous reward was for the Zhou family, not for Cheng. All the glory belongs to the Duke’s mansion and to you.”","She added, “Cheng was merely acting as your agent. No matter how well she performs, others will only say that the Chen Duke’s mansion’s birthday banquet was magnificent and unparalleled.”","The Grand Matriarch sighed.","She fell silent for a long while, then finally said, “Both of you return. It’s late.”","Huan Qingtang still attended to the Grand Matriarch, helping her change clothes and let down her hair, then supporting her until she lay down before leaving.","She was meticulous and thoughtful.","“...Huan is perfect in every way, but she lacks that fierce edge Cheng has. She still needs more experience and caution in handling matters,” the Grand Matriarch said to her trusted Nanny Sun.","When it came to tasks under her charge, Cheng Zhao always prepared for every contingency.","For the vegetarian sauce in the Lady’s Honor dish, she had outright changed the cook.","The Grand Matriarch was certain that with the pigeons replacing fireworks, Cheng Zhao must have also had a backup plan. If the Grand Matriarch had tried to take the credit and give it to Huan Qingtang, it would have only brought shame upon them all.","As for Huan Qingtang, she had merely arranged a Crane Dance performance, allowing Mu Jiang to seize the opportunity and kill the cranes.","Before leaving, the Emperor repeatedly told the Grand Matriarch: “What are cranes but just wild fowl? Tributes of them come in by the thousands every year. If one dies, so be it. Don’t blame A’Jiang for this.”","With that said, the Grand Matriarch, though furious, held back from slapping Mu Jiang.","She was truly disappointed.","It wasn’t just Mu Jiang who disappointed her; it was also Huan Qingtang.","She had always thought that her carefully chosen eldest grandson’s wife, a noble lady from a pure and prestigious family, would possess the same capability and good reputation as herself.","But she never expected that, in front of Cheng Zhao, Huan Qingtang would prove so vulnerable.","As for Cheng Zhao, her overly obvious eagerness to curry favor would only worsen the Chen State Duke’s estate’s already precarious state—adding fuel to the fire. Besides, the Grand Dowager disliked her, finding fault with her no matter what she did.","“Grand Dowager, this time we had no choice but to let that Cheng woman benefit greatly in order to divert the guests’ gossip,” Nanny Sun said. “At least the estate’s reputation is preserved.”","She added, “Lady Huan is still young. You can teach her for a few more years.”","“She needs some confidence,” the Grand Dowager said.","“You mean...”","“Let Cheng suffer a little. Let Huan Qingtang see that Cheng is nothing more than someone with a bit of petty cleverness,” the Grand Dowager said.","Otherwise, Huan Qingtang would lose her nerve facing someone like Cheng Zhao.","What was so hard about dealing with Cheng Zhao? She was just a little troublemaker. The Grand Dowager simply didn’t stoop to her level.","But she really did deserve to be taught a lesson.","“This old servant understands,” Nanny Sun said. “I’ll make arrangements. Let her be a bit more restrained, give her a lesson to remember.”","The Grand Dowager nodded slightly.","Then she asked, “What about the investigation into Commandery Princess Zhaoyang? Did she flee to Wu Commandery back then?”"]},{"number":93,"title":"Chapter 93: Really Like Cheng Zhao","paragraphs":["The Dowager Madame once again brought up the matter of Commandery Princess Zhaoyang from years ago.","She had always suspected some connection between Cheng Zhao and the Commandery Princess, but she had met Cheng Zhao’s mother and sisters, and had even investigated the women of the Cheng family.","Every daughter-in-law of the Chengs came from a distinguished family, each with a clear lineage that could be traced.","Now, eighteen years had passed since those events.","Nanny Sun dared not investigate the matter too openly and said, “There’s been no progress yet. Too much time has gone by.”","“Forget it. Let’s set this aside for now,” said the Dowager Madame.","She barely managed to fall asleep as dawn approached.","In the following days, both the Duke of Chen’s mansion and the capital city were abuzz with talk of the birthday banquet.","The main topic was a comparison between the two young married women of the Zhou family.","“Wasn’t there supposed to be a crane dance? In the end, it never appeared. The eldest young madam seemed somewhat flustered.”","“Maybe Lady Su wanted to steal the spotlight. Could the crane dance have been part of her plan? That’s why the Duchess of Chen switched it to a pigeon act instead?”","“The pigeon act was truly brilliant—an ingenious idea. The Emperor himself praised it and rewarded her generously.”","“Five hundred taels of gold! Now she’s rich, won’t the servants be flocking to curry favor with her?”","The one most delighted was not Cheng Zhao’s own family, but her mother-in-law.","The Second Madam felt truly vindicated.","“...General Sheng’s wife showered you with so many compliments she got parched. She really knows how to praise. Everyone outside is singing your praises too,” the Second Madam said, beaming.","Cheng Zhao smiled and replied, “That’s because Madam Sheng holds you in high regard, Mother, so she praised me along with you.”","“Oh, you silly child!” The Second Madam couldn’t hide her grin. “She was praising you, only you!”","She added, “This time, I’ve finally let out a huge sigh of relief. I suspect there’s plenty of trouble brewing between the first branch—mother-in-law and daughter-in-law.”","Cheng Zhao just smiled.","How could there not be conflict?","Several days had passed since the birthday banquet and the incident of stealing the limelight. Everyone knew the Dowager Madame intended to elevate Huan Qingsheng.","Surely Lady Song had already figured it out by now?","The handover of household management rights between mother-in-law and daughter-in-law could have been done in countless more dignified and gentle ways.","Even if the Dowager Madame had ordered her to hand over the tally tokens, it would have been better than scheming against her like this.","Lady Song herself was not a magnanimous person. Once she mulled things over, she and Huan Qingsheng would surely become sworn enemies.","She probably also harbored deep resentment toward the Dowager Madame.","Gloating aside, the Second Madam also warned Cheng Zhao, “You need to be careful. Your eldest aunt may try to use you as a pawn and lure you in. Don’t mistake that for goodwill.”","Cheng Zhao nodded. “I understand, Mother.”","She lowered her voice to the Second Madam, “If she plays hypocrite, I can play that game too. Rest assured, I know all these petty tricks of the inner court.”","The Second Madam smiled with relief.","Then she looked at Cheng Zhao again. “Your mother seems gentle-natured. How do you know all this?”","“I have three aunts by marriage, each from a prestigious family. Below my father are twin sisters a year younger than him. As for my grandmother, she never really liked her daughters-in-law much. The rivalry between them never ceased. Now they seem meek and proper only because they’ve run out of strength to resist,” Cheng Zhao said.","She added with a laugh, “These unsavory matters must sound amusing to you, Mother.”","The Second Madam was taken aback. “They all seemed fine. Your aunts were quite pleasant.”","“When visiting as guests, of course they appear pleasant. If my sister-in-law and I went out visiting, I’d act affectionate and chatty with her too,” Cheng Zhao said.","The Second Madam: “...”","Cheng Zhao’s mother was likely exhausted by the time she chose her daughters’ marriages, wanting them to have an easier life.","The eldest daughter, who should have married into a high-ranking family, instead chose Du Anli for mutual affection, even though his family was relatively modest.","The third daughter was married to the youngest son of a high-ranking family, with the hope that she could live a life of untainted aloofness, composing poetry and admiring flowers.","When choosing daughters-in-law, temperament was her priority.","Only Cheng Zhao’s marriage, which was decreed by imperial edict, was beyond her mother’s expectations.","Still, Cheng Zhao was never one to fear hardship—she simply could not tolerate mediocrity.","After the birthday banquet, Empress Guo summoned Cheng Zhao to Kunning Palace.","“Everyone is talking about you. You handled things beautifully, and the pigeon act was brilliant,” Empress Guo said with a smile. “The Crown Prince couldn’t stop praising you.”","Since the Emperor had rewarded Cheng Zhao handsomely, Empress Guo had to know what happened that day.","Cheng Zhao first made a few modest remarks, then recounted the events of the birthday banquet.","“...Perhaps His Majesty planned to grant another titled lady to the Zhou family on this joyous occasion,” Empress Guo said with a smile.","Unfortunately, Huan Qingsheng failed to seize the opportunity. Her timing was unlucky, and she simply couldn’t rise to the occasion.","The Dowager Madame had tried to elevate her, but she didn’t succeed.","Instead, it was Cheng Zhao who earned fame and reward. Five hundred taels of gold would keep the titled ladies talking for years.","From now on, when people mention the titled ladies of the Duke of Chen’s mansion, the first will be the Dowager Madame, and the second will be Cheng Zhao.","She had even overshadowed her eldest aunt.","And she had only been married into the family for half a year.","In such a short time, Cheng Zhao had performed so brilliantly that Empress Guo regarded her with new respect.","“If His Majesty does grant another lady title to the Zhou family, you’ll need to stay vigilant,” Empress Guo reminded her with a smile.","Cheng Zhao replied, “Your Majesty, you were the one who arranged my marriage. I will never bring shame to you. No matter how good a match His Majesty might arrange, I won’t be outshone.”","Empress Guo laughed.","She told Cheng Zhao, “The one who praised you most lavishly was Grand Princess Fukang. She insisted that I select another unmarried girl from the Cheng family to betroth to her son the heir-apparent.”","Cheng Zhao said, “I do have a few unmarried cousins. But they are gentle and reserved, not nearly as cunning as me.”","She meant that if the princess valued her abilities and assumed all Cheng daughters were like her, she was mistaken.","Even her own sisters had different temperaments.","For instance, her third sister was quite detached from worldly affairs.","As for Cheng Zhao’s other cousins, every one of them were obedient—her mother had never mentioned any troublesome ones.","“I also reminded the Grand Princess of that. But she’s now dead set on asking for a Cheng girl for her son. She simply adores you too much,” Empress Guo said with a chuckle.","Cheng Zhao replied, “The heir-apparent used to visit my home often. The Grand Princess has known me for a long time. She never planned to betroth her son back then. It’s only after Your Majesty arranged my marriage and I had a chance to shine that she began to appreciate me. I think what the Grand Princess truly admires is Your Majesty’s discerning judgment.”","Empress Guo couldn’t help but laugh.","“What a silver tongue you have,” she said, patting Cheng Zhao’s hand.","They chatted for quite a while before Cheng Zhao left the palace. At the palace gate, she encountered Zhou Yuanshen.","“Duke of Chen,” Cheng Zhao stepped forward to greet him. “Why are you here?”","“I heard the Empress summoned you to the palace,” Zhou Yuanshen said succinctly. “Has something happened?”","“Nothing really. She had heard about the birthday banquet and summoned me to ask about it, and also to give me some praise. Since the Emperor already rewarded me, the Empress couldn’t pretend not to know,” Cheng Zhao explained.","It was merely a matter of social decorum.","If Cheng Zhao had failed at the banquet, the Empress would now be eager to disown her.","Zhou Yuanshen nodded slightly. “Come along. Ride in my carriage. I’m going to the Drunken Immortal Tavern with your maternal uncle for some drinks. You can join us.”","“The Drunken Immortal Tavern has a braised fish dish that’s tender and flavorful. I really like it,” Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen replied, “That’s their signature dish. They have plenty of other good food there too.”","As they spoke, the carriage soon arrived at the Drunken Immortal Tavern, where her maternal uncle, Fan Xiao, was waiting at the entrance.","He also went to the birthday banquet that day and witnessed the spectacular sight of doves flying, which filled him with admiration for Cheng Zhao."]},{"number":94,"title":"Chapter 94: Sneak a Kiss on Her","paragraphs":["Fan Xiao had not only invited Zhou Yuanshen for drinks but also a few other friends.","Seeing Cheng Zhao arrive, he arranged the others in separate seats, only sharing the table with Zhou Yuanshen and his wife.","“Duchess, your foresight is admirable. You handled matters so brilliantly in such a short time,” Fan Xiao said with a laugh.","It seemed Zhou Yuanshen had already told him about the birthday banquet’s details.","“You flatter me, Uncle. I merely did my duty,” Cheng Zhao replied.","Fan Xiao praised her again.","The three of them were quite at ease. While the two men drank and chatted, Cheng Zhao sampled several of the delicious dishes.","“...Here, take this,” Fan Xiao handed a black lacquered box to Zhou Yuanshen.","Cheng Zhao glanced at it curiously.","Before she could ask, Fan Xiao explained unprompted, “It’s banknotes. Ah-Shen told me to be prepared in case the emperor brought up ‘double inheritance,’ so I made arrangements. But the emperor didn’t mention it.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","Zhou Yuanshen took the black lacquered box and said flatly, “No need to say more.”","But Fan Xiao couldn’t help adding, “Ah-Shen, dodging the issue of ‘double inheritance’ won’t work. You need to tackle the root cause.”","Cheng Zhao interjected, “Uncle, ‘double inheritance’ is Grandmother’s tactic, a rope to bind the Duke. If we can’t drive a wedge between Grandmother and the emperor and make them fall out, there’s no way to ‘remove the firewood from under the cauldron.’”","She often thought that saying “stirring the boiling water to cool it” was foolish—a waste of effort.","Yet many times, the firewood under the cauldron was already blazing, impossible to pull away. Stirring the water was the only way to handle the immediate crisis.","One approach required long-term planning; the other was a response to current difficulties.","Either was better than doing nothing.","And Zhou Yuanshen had certainly made long-term plans.","It was like planting a tree—it takes two or three years to bloom and bear fruit.","The Grand Matriarch’s bond with the emperor had been cultivated over decades. She knew him better than anyone. Resolving this in one stroke was truly a tall order.","Under such immense pressure, Zhou Yuanshen hadn’t given up resisting. He had done everything he could.","“...It’s good that you understand his difficulties,” Fan Xiao smiled. “With you two united as one, things will get better.”","Cheng Zhao glanced at Zhou Yuanshen.","He lowered his head to drink, showing neither pride nor self-pity.","When obstacles appeared, he carved paths through mountains and built bridges across waters. He tackled problems as they arose. For deep-rooted ills he couldn’t remove, he wouldn’t indulge them either. Even if only superficial measures worked, he would buy time.","You couldn’t fell a giant tree with one axe stroke—you had to keep chopping slowly.","If it were her, Cheng Zhao would do the same.","So, she understood Zhou Yuanshen.","Having said her piece, she continued eating. Zhou Yuanshen raised his eyes, his gaze sweeping over her face before he downed a cup of wine.","Fan Xiao rambled on about many things.","He also mentioned the matchmaking by Qing’an Commandery Princess’s residence.","Cheng Zhao immediately pricked up her ears. She was very curious about this matter, wondering if Zhou Yuanshen had once pursued something in vain and then harbored resentment toward Huan Qingtang.","How deep had their old feelings been?","“If they hadn’t schemed, maybe you would have...”","Zhou Yuanshen coughed.","Fan Xiao cut himself off: “No more talk of the past.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","He had already started—why not continue?","She stared at Fan Xiao expectantly, but he just smiled and refilled her cup.","Cheng Zhao had no choice but to look away.","Regarding this past incident, those in the know were unwilling to speak; those who couldn’t keep secrets, like the Second Madam and Zhou Yuanqi, didn’t know the inside story.","To get to the bottom of it, she suspected not even asking Zhou Yuanshen would work. He wouldn’t open up.","“I’ll have to go ask Qing’an Commandery Princess herself,” Cheng Zhao thought. “Her daughter, Xianzhen County Princess, seems to have a forged calligraphy copy. Next time, I’ll use that as an excuse to visit Qing’an Commandery Princess’s estate.”","She made up her mind.","Amidst the eating, drinking, and idle talk, dusk had fallen before they knew it.","When it ended, the night drum had already sounded—it was well into the night.","At the entrance to the Drunken Immortal Tavern, they ran into Andong Commandery Prince Helian Xuan and Cheng Zhao’s fourth brother, Cheng Chao.","They exchanged courtesies.","“I’ve been hearing about the duchess’s amusing anecdotes lately,” Helian Xuan said.","He stood under the lantern by the tavern door, light and shadow enveloping him, his face even fairer, like the bright radiance of jade.","Clean, yet with a touch of austerity.","Cheng Zhao didn’t sneer, but she wasn’t eager to engage with him either, turning her head to the side.","The atmosphere grew a bit awkward.","Fan Xiao’s gaze swept between them again.","Cheng Zhao’s fourth brother, Cheng Chao, laughed, “The Duke’s mansion banquet is indeed the talk of everyone. Fifth Sister, haven’t you thanked me yet?”","“You can ask me for a reward privately,” Cheng Zhao said, her tone sharp, shooting him a warning glance.","What did he mean, saying such things in front of outsiders? Who was his flesh-and-blood relative after all?","Zhou Yuanshen’s gaze also rested on her face.","Cheng Chao felt a pang of embarrassment and wanted to say something, but nothing seemed fitting.","He inwardly fumed—he wouldn’t help her again next time. She’d gotten a little honor and now her tail was in the air.","Helian Xuan’s expression dimmed.","“I won’t forget your reward. I’ll send it home another day,” Cheng Zhao added.","Seeing him and Helian Xuan together, Cheng Zhao could hardly suppress her anger.","After all, someone from the Cheng family had died at Helian Xuan’s hands.","Cheng Zhao was angry at her own brother for being spineless and for always valuing outsiders more than her. He was so obedient to Helian Xuan but always argued with her.","The one time he did something for her, he had to ask for credit in front of outsiders.","Among the three standing there—Helian Xuan, Fan Xiao, and Zhou Yuanshen—who was appropriate for discussing private family matters?","Whose relationship with her was closer than that of siblings born from the same mother?","In front of a group of outsiders, his talk was so inappropriate, blurring the lines between close and distant. It truly infuriated her.","“...It’s getting late. Shall we call it a night?” Fan Xiao, sensing the awkwardness, smiled as he tried to smooth things over.","Helian Xuan looked at Cheng Zhao again.","Cheng Zhao immediately met his gaze.","Their eyes locked. Cheng Zhao’s expression was dark, and it was Helian Xuan who looked away first.","“We’ll head back first,” Cheng Chao said, calming down, then added to Zhou Yuanshen, “Duke, come home for a meal another day. Grandfather was asking about you.”","“I’ll drop by when I have time,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","They exchanged farewells and set off separately.","The Zhou family carriage arrived, but Zhou Yuanshen said, “The night market is ahead. Care to stroll around to sober up?”","He had drunk a bit, maybe three-tenths tipsy.","Cheng Zhao: “Alright.”","This street was the busiest and most lively, the night market bright with lights and crowds bustling shoulder to shoulder, as lively as broad daylight.","“On ordinary nights, the market isn’t as packed as it is during the Lantern Festival. But it’s still pretty good,” Cheng Zhao remarked.","Zhou Yuanshen said, “It’s been nearly a decade with no major affairs in the court. The people live and work in peace, which is why the night market thrives.”","Then he asked her, “Want to eat something?”","Cheng Zhao was already full.","She had walked with Zhou Yuanshen to digest the meal, with no intention of getting anything to eat.","“I’d like to buy some trinkets, but nothing to eat,” she said.","Two peddlers carrying their wares crossed paths. To avoid them, Cheng Zhao and Zhou Yuanshen moved to the eaves of a shop.","Right there was a street tree, casting a patch of shadow over the eaves.","Suddenly, he lowered his head and planted a kiss on her lips.","It was so fleeting she thought she had imagined it.","Cheng Zhao: “...”"]},{"number":95,"title":"Chapter 95: Misdirected Anger","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao opened her eyes wide.","She looked around, and no one was paying attention to them. As the night deepened, the people on the street gradually dispersed.","She seemed to let out a sigh of relief.","She looked at him. He was expressionless, and his burning eyes stared back at her in the dark.","Cheng Zhao turned around and was about to leave.","Zhou Yuanshen didn't pull her but followed her steps. Soon, the two of them returned to the entrance of the Drunken Immortal Tower. Cheng Zhao got into the carriage first.","As soon as she sat down firmly, Zhou Yuanshen also got in.","The carriage slowly made its way back to the mansion.","There was originally a small horn lantern, but Cheng Zhao didn't light it, so the carriage was pitch - black. Zhou Yuanshen sat there, only a faint outline.","She couldn't see his face clearly.","After a while, Cheng Zhao said, \"Duke, what you did just now was inappropriate.\"","\"Why?\" In the darkness, he asked her back. There was a faint smell of wine on his breath, mixed with the man's body heat.","Cheng Zhao could feel it. She subconsciously moved a bit to the side and bumped into the carriage wall.","\"We are a proper couple, married by the order of the Empress Dowager,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"How could you treat me lightly?\"","\"I didn't treat you lightly. You are my wife,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","He wasn't his usual silent self.","Whenever Cheng Zhao asked him a question, he would answer, not giving in a single word.","\"I'm also the Duchess, a super - grade imperial - conferred lady. If people saw us, how could I have the face to live?\" Cheng Zhao said.","She had her own dignity and status.","In the current world, the social customs were good, and women weren't overly restricted. But Cheng Zhao was determined to be the matriarch of the clan, and her prestige was very important.","\"Cheng Zhao, is the title of imperial - conferred lady really that important?\" he asked.","\"For a woman, if she doesn't strive for this status, what else can she strive for?\" Cheng Zhao asked him angrily.","Strive for the little pleasure with him?","He could be with her today and go to the Lijing Courtyard tomorrow.","Cheng Zhao's eyes followed him around every day. Wouldn't all the books she had read since childhood, the principles she had learned, and the house - managing experience taught by her mother be in vain?","Since she could remember, she had never shed tears over the romances of talented scholars and beautiful ladies when watching operas. She had never envied the young and loving couples in other families, who were well - matched in appearance and talent.","As she grew older, the girls of the same age among her relatives and friends were all discussing their betrothals.","During the gatherings in the boudoir, when they mentioned their fiancés, they would talk about what kind of person he was.","Cheng Zhao sat silently beside them, thinking, \"Don't you consider the family's ancestral property, the mother - in - law's character, and the inheritance of the title and estate?\"","Ancestral property meant a wealthy family background. In the inner - house life, the person in charge was never the husband but the mother - in - law, because the power of the household was passed down from the mother - in - law. The title was related to her own imperial - conferred status.","As for the husband, apart from helping her with procreation, what else could he do for her? Unless he was extremely unreliable and there was no elder to restrain him, he might squander the ancestral property.","Of course, this was also unacceptable.","What Cheng Zhao had envied since childhood were those old noble lords.","But today, Zhou Yuanshen asked her if the imperial - conferred title was important.","It was like asking a man if his official position was important.","If it wasn't important, what did one rely on to gain a foothold in this world?","If only she were a man. If she worked so hard, her family, parents, and wife would all strongly support her, help her become a good official, clear away internal and external obstacles for her, and assist her to rise to high positions.","They would praise her for her progress and be proud of her, allowing her to focus without distractions.","As a woman, the sad thing was that her so - called \"high position\" was only an imperial - conferred title.","But he asked her if it was important.","Cheng Zhao leaned her head against the carriage wall and suddenly lost the strength to speak.","All her annoyance disappeared in an instant. She just felt extremely disheartened.","In the darkness, Zhou Yuanshen moved over and hugged her in his arms.","Cheng Zhao didn't struggle and let him hold her.","He tightened his arms and whispered, \"I was out of control just now. Cheng Zhao, in this world, what's noble isn't just the title of the Duchess.\"","Cheng Zhao didn't say a word.","She thought he was just talking without understanding the situation.","He kissed her lips again.","She turned her head away.","\"I'm here to apologize to you,\" he said again. \"You can make a request, and I'll fulfill it for you. Or, I can help you and find a match for your fourth brother?\"","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","When he mentioned finding a match, she remembered the matter of the Qing'an Princess Mansion that she had talked about several times.","It was when she tried to matchmake Zhou Yuanshen and Huan Qingtang.","\"Forget it. A person who aims for great things shouldn't be bothered by minor details,\" Cheng Zhao comforted herself in her heart. \"I have to get what I want.\"","She rolled her eyes a few times and softened her voice. \"Then you answer me a question and explain it in detail.\"","\"Okay.\"","As soon as the words were spoken, the carriage arrived at the Chen Duke's Mansion.","Zhou Yuanshen got out first and told the servant to lower the threshold so that the carriage could directly enter the mansion and go to the Nonghua Courtyard.","Cheng Zhao went to wash up first.","When she was alone, she suddenly thought, \"Did I take my anger out on him just now?\"","Seeing Cheng Chao being so confused about right and wrong and mixing with Helian Xuan, Cheng Zhao was really furious. And in front of Zhou Yuanshen and Fan Xiao, she couldn't not save face for her elder brother and was not convenient to lose her temper.","So she was full of anger.","The kiss Zhou Yuanshen gave her on the street was in a dark corner.","Just as her eldest sister said, a couple could relax some of the rules appropriately. He wasn't some other lecher.","Cheng Zhao felt that she had transferred her anger at \"Cheng Chao's disobedience\" to Zhou Yuanshen.","She thought Zhou Yuanshen was also disobedient.","In fact, Cheng Chao was her elder brother and Zhou Yuanshen was the Duke. They were under no obligation to listen to her.","After sorting out these thoughts, Cheng Zhao adjusted her mood, changed into her nightclothes, and came out of the dressing room.","Zhou Yuanshen had already washed up. He had let his hair down and was sitting at the table, drinking a cup of tea.","Seeing Cheng Zhao come in, he lowered the curtain hanging from the gold hook, and the couple got into the bed together.","In the small space of the bed, the horn lantern was covered by a lampshade, emitting only a faint light. There was a curtain outside the bed curtain, making the bed as private as a small room.","\"What do you want to ask?\"","\"What happened at the Qing'an Princess Mansion back then?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","Zhou Yuanshen paused.","Cheng Zhao: \"Why did the Qing'an Princess suddenly want to matchmake you and the Huan family? She couldn't be that stupid to do such a thing.\"","Zhou Yuanshen seemed to take a deep breath.","\"This matter makes me a bit embarrassed, Cheng Zhao,\" he said.","Cheng Zhao was slightly stunned.","Embarrassed, not sad or disappointed.","Cheng Zhao understood that there was a hidden story in it. It was definitely not as simple as \"casually match - making\". Maybe the mother - in - law hadn't thought it through carefully.","\"... If you don't want to talk about it, let's change the topic. Tell me, why did your slow - wind snake pass by the Nonghua Courtyard?\" Cheng Zhao said.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"I chose the Nonghua Courtyard. This courtyard is convenient for communicating with the outside world. Whether it's the slow - wind snake or people, it's easy to get in and out.\"","At that time, he thought that she was like an ordinary woman, living here unawares and wouldn't discover his secret.","\"I'll take you to take a closer look at the slow - wind snake and the defense of the Nonghua Courtyard when I'm free,\" he said. \"I also want to tell you about the matter at the Qing'an Princess Mansion.\"","He was silent for a moment, then pulled Cheng Zhao over and hugged her in his arms.","He started to talk about the secret from that year.","As Cheng Zhao listened, anger welled up from the bottom of her heart, and she was extremely furious.","Those women had bullied him wantonly."]},{"number":96,"title":"Chapter 96: The Stirred-up Duke","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao listened to Zhou Yuanshen’s account and grew very angry.","She shared his indignation: “This was premeditated, sacrificing only you. You had no quarrel with them.”","Zhou Yuanshen tightened his arm around her. “It’s not exactly sacrifice; each had their own agenda.”","He had always been cautious.","The matchmaking proposal from Princess Qing’an had been sudden, catching him off guard.","Moreover, it happened at Princess Qing’an’s residence, during her birthday banquet. As the host, she held the advantage.","Zhou Yuanshen had mentally replayed the situation countless times afterward, but still found no better solution than what he had done at the time. Because he wasn’t familiar with Princess Qing’an’s household—nor did he understand the dynamics—but as a family friend spanning generations, he had no choice but to engage.","Thus, even though the matter rankled him, and those in the know—like his father and his maternal uncle—felt aggrieved on his behalf, he didn’t stew over it.","It was like war. Even with countless precedents of surprise attacks, enemies would still devise new ones.","Being defeated by a surprise attack merely added another lesson; he wouldn’t brood over the humiliation of the defeat.","War meant both wins and losses.","Even the most outstanding general couldn’t be undefeated. Zhou Yuanshen only focused on his own territory, not on the tally of victories or defeats.","As long as his territory hadn’t shrunk, and his most vital strongholds hadn’t fallen, defeat wasn’t terrifying.","His struggles with the Emperor and the Grand Madam were the same.","The incident at Princess Qing’an’s estate occasionally came up in conversation because of Huan Qingtang—his maternal uncle would sometimes mention it; Cheng Zhao, curious, would also ask.","He didn’t want to talk about it. It was meaningless.","Everyone involved in that affair was irrelevant to him.","After hearing this, Cheng Zhao was filled with righteous fury.","She suppressed her urge to curse, afraid of losing the dignified composure expected of a noblewoman’s daughter. After a long pause, she said, “When the chance comes, I’ll get revenge for you.”","She looked like a fierce little cub baring its fangs.","Soft and beautiful, yet still too young and not strong enough. Perched on the city wall, glaring down, she had no deterrent effect—like a cat, instead.","Cute and adorably naive, making one want to scoop her up into an embrace and tousle her.","But Zhou Yuanshen knew she wasn’t a tame kitten. She was clever and formidable; deep down, she was a beast of prey.","She was just like him—needing time to grow.","Time and power would gradually sharpen their claws. Once they commanded the mountains and forests, all other beasts would submit.","He kissed Cheng Zhao.","She kissed him back and murmured softly, “Hurry tonight. I’m tired and want to sleep.”","“... That’s not up to me alone; you’ll need to put in some effort,” he said.","Their clothes fell away, and he took her hand, guiding it to gently brush across his chest.","He nibbled at her lips, then bit her earlobe.","Cheng Zhao bit her lip, holding something back, her body trembling slightly.","Zhou Yuanshen coaxed her in a low voice: “Cheng Zhao, you said you wanted this to be quick. But you haven’t stoked the fire enough.”","“I— I am the Duchess of the State...”","Even in bed, she couldn’t let herself be too unrestrained with him.","“Duchess of the State, then let’s take it slow.” His voice was light, subtle in the darkness—an expressionless, yet vaguely teasing threat.","Cheng Zhao ignored him.","“Call me ‘Third Brother,’” he said gruffly, pausing and waiting.","Her hand touched the thin sheen of sweat on his chest, and a tight string snapped within her mind, leaving her suspended midair—unable to land, unable to ascend.","Her breathing grew frantic. Cheng Zhao feared she might suffocate, but he deliberately tormented her.","As he spoke, his fingers traced her chin, his thumb brushing against her lips.","Cheng Zhao was almost unbearably frustrated; the words slipped through her clenched teeth: “Third Brother.”","She remembered a waterfall once.","In deep winter, it had frozen solid, locking the entire river. In early spring, the sun thawed the ice, and the water surged down.","The roaring current sounded like a river pouring from the heavens. All other sounds drowned in the thundering cascades.","Cheng Zhao felt a little delirious.","When she regained some awareness, Zhou Yuanshen’s hands were gently stroking her spine, pulling her close into his embrace.","Cheng Zhao had discovered a new joy in life.","At this moment, she was happy; based on previous experiences, her mood would stay lifted for the next two or three days.","Like savoring an exquisite pastry—it brought her delight for quite some time.","If she tried to hoard this pleasure and cling to it anxiously, she would soon find it unbearable.","Cheng Zhao’s mind didn’t wander to anyone or anything. She simply nestled quietly against Zhou Yuanshen.","After resting, they both went to the washroom.","Cheng Zhao bathed, changed into fresh undergarments, and grew drowsy; Zhou Yuanshen came in afterward.","Suddenly reminded of something, Cheng Zhao said, “I didn’t burn incense for the Bodhisattva... Ah, never mind. I’ll do it tomorrow morning and tell Suyue to remind me.”","She was too sleepy to keep her eyes open and soon fell asleep.","The next morning, when she got up, Zhou Yuanshen had already left for court. Cheng Zhao slowly freshened up and dressed, feeling as though she had forgotten something.","After breakfast, she remembered the Guanyin statue for fertility.","She had been lazy the night before and hadn’t offered incense, hoping to make up for it this morning.","She called for a maid to prepare the offerings.","The maid who had been on night duty said, “The Duke lit incense twice last night. He offered three sticks himself and also burned another three on behalf of the Madam.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","She said nothing else and hurried to Chengming Hall to attend to business.","After the birthday banquet, Chengming Hall had taken a few days off; the stewards also rotated their leaves, as everyone had been exhausted.","Only a handful of duty stewards remained on shift.","Today, work resumed. The great hall within Grand Madam’s domain was filled with stewards, crowded inside and out.","When Cheng Zhao entered Chengming Hall, the stewards made way for her, allowing her a smooth path to the seat beside the Grand Madam.","The Grand Madam’s expression was very sour.","But when she saw Cheng Zhao, she managed a smile. “Cheng Zhao, you’re quite early today.”","Cheng Zhao had come precisely on time, neither early nor late.","It was just that Huan Qingtang had not yet arrived.","“I ought to have come earlier to serve you, Aunt,” Cheng Zhao said smiling. “But I had to pay my respects to my mother-in-law first, which delayed me.”","Her words made the Grand Madam’s face shift again in color.","Why hadn’t Huan Qingtang arrived yet? There was still an incense stick’s worth of time, but she, too, had gone to pay morning respects at Shou’an Compound.","This was something Cheng Zhao had mentioned to the Grand Madam before.","The Grand Madam had always found it grating. But after the birthday banquet incident, her displeasure had peaked.","“Let’s begin. First, call roll from the name ledger,” the Grand Madam said. “Cheng Zhao, take care of it.”","This task was usually Huan Qingtang’s.","Cheng Zhao didn’t want to be anyone’s knife. The Grand Madam was not her ally—she was merely using her to provoke Huan Qingtang.","The stewards were watching.","If Cheng Zhao allowed herself to be manipulated so easily and acted so brainlessly, would any steward respect her?","She had started off so well.","So she laughed and said, “Aunt, I know all the stewards in the household by name. I don’t need to consult the ledger.”","The Grand Madam, taking this for boasting and showing off, frowned slightly.","“Isn’t that right, Nanny Qian?” Cheng Zhao pointed to a matron. “I have a good memory—don’t you all believe me?”","She was deflecting—joking to lighten the mood.","She neither refused the Grand Madam outright, nor accepted the task meant for Huan Qingtang, which would have caused trouble.","Nanny Qian smiled. “Third Madam is still young, so indeed has a sharp memory. When this old servant was your age, I remembered everything too. Every thread and needle in the house, and how many roots of ginger I had stored—everything was clear.”","Nanny Qian was from the main kitchen and was familiar with Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao called on her, of course needing her to respond, simply to kill time.","The First Madame could not yet lose her temper.","Just as they were exchanging questions and answers, Huan Qingtang finally arrived."]},{"number":97,"title":"Chapter 97: Watching the Fire from Across the Shore","paragraphs":["A \"chaotic battle\" broke out in the Hall of Cherished Brightness.","Madam Song, the senior wife, confronted Huan Qingtang directly, demanding to know why she had made everyone wait for her.","Huan Qingtang was momentarily stunned, then explained herself with clear logic and justification: \"Mother, the appointed time for duties had not yet arrived. This daughter-in-law was not late.\"","\"You dare to argue further?\" Madam Song thundered in fury. \"Such defiance and unfilial conduct!\"","Defiance and unfilial conduct were not mere verbal accusations; they were serious offenses codified in law. Of course, strict criteria applied when determining punishment—trivial matters like disrespectful words rarely led to conviction. Even so, because \"unfilial behavior\" was enshrined in the legal code and allowed parents-in-law to file complaints at the yamen under that pretext, the term carried immense weight.","The flower hall of the Hall of Cherished Brightness fell into absolute silence.","Huan Qingtang knelt down.","Her knees touched the ground, but her back remained straight as a pole: \"This daughter-in-law dares not be unfilial. I beg Mother to calm her anger.\"","For some time, she had assisted with duties in the Hall of Cherished Brightness, cultivating a number of trusted confidants. Although she had lost some face during this birthday banquet and had not received an imperial betrothal as \"rumored,\" it was plain for all to see that the Grand Madam valued and elevated her.","Thus, many stewards counseled Madam Song, speaking in Huan Qingtang's defense.","Huan Qingtang's posture of admitting fault was somewhat reluctant; Madam Song's fury blazed unchecked. The two women, mother-in-law and daughter-in-law, found themselves locked in a stalemate.","The stewards offered a few words of advice, but none struck the right chord. Like fanning flames, their efforts only burned Madam Song's anger hotter.","Cheng Zhao stood nearby, watching the spectacle unfold.","\"Third Young Madam, you should help mediate as well. The Hall of Cherished Brightness must maintain harmony,\" a steward said.","Cheng Zhao replied: \"I am hardly a person of the Hall of Cherished Brightness, Steward Han. The burden of harmony here is not mine to bear. You are putting me in a difficult position.\"","The crowd: \"...\"","These words added yet more fuel to the fire. Madam Song hurled her teacup to the ground: \"From now on, who belongs to the Hall of Cherished Brightness remains to be seen. Let no one grow too complacent!\"","She retreated into the inner chamber.","Those left behind exchanged glances. Some sized up the kneeling Huan Qingtang, whose skirt hem was stained by a splash of tea; others sized up Cheng Zhao, whose ambition for power was obvious and who seized every chance to stir up trouble.","Who would be the future mistress of the Hall of Cherished Brightness? The stewards had once been certain, but now doubt crept into their hearts.","No matter how much the Grand Madam disliked or diminished her, the incoming Duchess of the State was advancing with formidable force.","\"Eldest Young Madam, please rise,\" a steward said, moving to help Huan Qingtang up. \"If you injure yourself kneeling, the senior Madam herself will feel remorse.\"","Another steward added, \"Mother-in-law and daughter-in-law are like mother and daughter. If there is a rift, talk it out clearly. Go in quickly and soothe the senior Madam.\"","They offered Huan Qingtang a graceful way out.","Huan Qingtang merely shook her head, her demeanor composed and expression gentle: \"My mother-in-law is punishing this daughter-in-law—it is only proper. I shall kneel and wait until her anger subsides. That is my filial duty.\"","Then she added, \"Everyone, please go about your business. We shall stop here for today.\"","Even while kneeling, she issued commands.","Her confidants naturally felt she carried great authority, confident they would not suffer under her leadership. Those who disliked her sneered inwardly.","Most of the stewards, however, were simply trying to get by. They usually held no strong allegiance.","Huan Qingtang's senior maidservant urged the crowd to attend to their duties, effectively telling them all to leave.","Cheng Zhao followed them out.","Once outside the Hall of Cherished Brightness, Old Nurse Qian quietly said to Cheng Zhao: \"With things this tense, won't the Grand Madam have to step in?\"","\"It's fine. We didn't join the row,\" Cheng Zhao said with a smile.","Old Nurse Qian told her to take care and went off to the main kitchen to work.","Cheng Zhao retrieved the gate ledger and began reorganizing the records of social engagements and gifts received during the birthday banquet.","The gifts were first recorded in the gate ledger, then the ledger was handed over to the storeroom, where the staff would enter them into their own records before storing them away.","Because this matter required a handover, Cheng Zhao needed to have it sorted out early.","If tomorrow, the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law in the Hall of Cherished Brightness made peace and brought up this matter during their duties, Cheng Zhao would be handing them a weapon if she had left any errors. They would gladly use it to trample over her, distracting from the day's farce.","Since she had to go over the accounts, Cheng Zhao did not return to Verdant Splendor Court. She had to meet with the stewards from the outer gate's ledger office.","She decided to work at Dawn Radiance Court instead.","Dawn Radiance Court was spotless and desolate, with only the young servant Nanfeng present.","When he saw Cheng Zhao arrive, it was as if the place suddenly had supervision. He ran off again and soon vanished.","Cheng Zhao's maidservants Suyue and Qiubai assisted her.","The stewards had already sorted everything out. Cheng Zhao merely made modifications based on their work, gaining a better grasp of the gifts to understand the social connections of the Duke of State's household.","Before they knew it, it was noon.","\"Madam, will you dine here, or return to the courtyard?\" Qiubai asked.","Cheng Zhao was hungry; her eyes and mind had been working hard all morning.","\"Have the meal served here,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"After eating, I'll take a walk back to settle my digestion.\"","Qiubai went to make arrangements.","As she stepped out of the east side room, she came face to face with Zhou Yuanshen.","\"Lord Duke of State,\" she greeted, deliberately raising her voice.","Cheng Zhao heard her.","She came out as well and performed the curtsy greeting to Zhou Yuanshen: \"Lord Duke of State, have you had your midday meal?\"","\"No.\"","\"Qiubai, go to the main kitchen and tell them to prepare the Lord Duke's noonday meal,\" Cheng Zhao instructed.","Qiubai acknowledged the order.","Under normal circumstances, the main kitchen did not prepare meals for Zhou Yuanshen or the Second Master, as both were on duty outside the estate.","Days off were the exception.","But the Duke of State's main kitchen always kept a full supply of ingredients. If someone wanted an extra meal, they could simply pay for it out of pocket—the materials were on hand.","Cheng Zhao's standard meal would already be ready; all Qiubai had to do was go and fetch it. Zhou Yuanshen's meal would need to be cooked from scratch, so it would take a bit longer.","He approached, first observing Cheng Zhao's expression.","Cheng Zhao knew what he was thinking—about the incident that had happened here last time, the quarrel between them, and whether she still held a grudge.","But she did not dwell on matters that had already been turned over. She refused to let herself get stuck in trivial affairs that had no bearing on her future.","Thus, she stepped forward and took Zhou Yuanshen's hand: \"Let me help you change your clothes.\"","She unfastened his light wind cloak.","Zhou Yuanshen's gaze shifted from probing to calm.","His dark eyes settled on her face. With no other expression, he simply asked: \"Are you hungry?\"","\"No. Been tired all morning,\" Cheng Zhao said. \"I was just thinking about resting a bit.\"","The young servant Nanfeng returned.","He came in to pay his respects first, then fetched water for Zhou Yuanshen to wash his hands, and finally served tea.","The couple settled on the kang bed by the window in the side room. Cheng Zhao leaned against a bolster cushion, relaxing as she told him all about what had happened that day at the Hall of Cherished Brightness.","Zhou Yuanshen took a slow sip of his tea: \"She shouldn't have made such a scene. The tally tokens haven't been returned yet—starting a fight like this just weakens her position.\"","He meant Madam Song.","When organizing the birthday banquet, Madam Song had willingly passed the hot potato, handing the tally tokens to Huan Qingtang.","Who could say Huan Qingtang hadn't deliberately provoked her today?","With Madam Song losing her temper so spectacularly, the Grand Madam would likely have to respond somehow. Perhaps the tally tokens would end up permanently in Huan Qingtang's hands.","\"But it probably won't happen for now,\" Zhou Yuanshen added. \"The tally tokens will still go back to First Uncle's wife.\"","Because the imperial betrothal and shared inheritance had not been decreed that night at the birthday banquet.","Without that relationship, the title of \"mother-in-law\" would always hang over Huan Qingtang's head. She wasn't yet qualified to take over Madam Song's authority over the household."]},{"number":98,"title":"Chapter 98: Is Being a Duchess the Best Prospect","paragraphs":["Cheng Zhao chatted idly with Zhou Yuanshen.","\"...My humble opinion, Duke, is that the affairs of Chengming Hall appear chaotic but are actually quite clear. The one truly in charge of Chengming Hall is Grandmother,\" said Cheng Zhao.","No matter how Madam Song and Huan Qingtang stirred things up, or who managed more or less, it did not change this fact. As long as the old madam lived, there was only one mistress of this Duke's mansion.","Zhou Yuanshen looked up, his gaze focused intently on her: \"Cheng Zhao, it is good that you can see the truth through layers of disguise. This saves you from wasting effort on futile struggles.\"","Once you see clearly, you know the path to take and where to go.","\"Sister-in-law also sees it clearly. The only one who is muddle-headed is Aunt,\" said Cheng Zhao.","Then she added, \"It is not that she is incompetent. She is simply trapped within this mountain and cannot see its entirety. Without her example, I and Sister-in-law would be just as trapped in the mountain.\"","It was Aunt's recent circumstances that repeatedly reminded Cheng Zhao, forcing her to see reality.","\"Cheng Zhao, do not sympathize with anyone. Some people, you think they are human, but they have long been devoured by the tiger, becoming only a ghost without a soul. If you try to pull them out, you are merely delivering yourself into the tiger's mouth,\" said Zhou Yuanshen.","Was he talking about the Madam, or Huan Qingtang and Mu Jiang?","Before Cheng Zhao could figure it out, Zhou Yuanshen continued, \"Do not let yourself become food in the tiger's mouth either.\"","\"Rest assured, I will protect myself,\" said Cheng Zhao.","She added, \"My mother says that any kindness without authority is merely cowardice. Once you are cowardly, everyone steps on you, and kindness becomes ridiculous. I will not blindly sympathize with anyone.\"","Zhou Yuanshen nodded slightly: \"Your mother is very wise, and you are also very perceptive, understanding after one lesson.\"","He praised Cheng Zhao and also praised her mother. Cheng Zhao was very happy inside and smiled brightly.","Zhou Yuanshen averted his gaze, his Adam's apple moving slightly, and drank the remaining tea in his cup all at once.","He stood up: \"I just remembered something; I need to go out. Have my portion of the meal distributed. Eat yours yourself. I will come back tonight.\"","He took his cloak and turned to leave.","Cheng Zhao acknowledged.","Qiubai, along with a rough maid from the kitchen, carried a large food box back and happened to see Zhou Yuanshen striding away.","\"... His Grace is not hungry? Even if busy, he could eat two bites before leaving,\" Qiubai said to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao: \"He said he suddenly remembered something; it must be urgent.\"","\"What could be so urgent?\" Qiubai muttered.","\"Many things outside,\" said Cheng Zhao.","She managed the gatehouse, the main kitchen, her own Nonghua Courtyard, and occasionally checked on her dowry investments; she was busy every day herself.","Zhou Yuanshen managed the outer courtyard of the Duke's mansion and also had three official posts, so who knows how busy he was. It was reasonable for him to say he had things to do.","Cheng Zhao did not want to waste time on things someone had already clearly explained. She picked up her chopsticks: \"I am a bit hungry.\"","She left two dishes and pointed to the rest: \"You and Nanfeng share.\"","\"Yes, Young Madam,\" said Qiubai.","Nanfeng was a growing boy with an appetite bigger than an ox's; he ate everything cleanly.","He also told Qiubai many \"little secrets\" from within the mansion.","Qiubai relayed them to Cheng Zhao.","Cheng Zhao found it amusing.","That day, Zhou Yuanshen returned to Nonghua Courtyard very late.","The faint scent of wine clung to him.","It was not strong or unpleasant.","\"... Your Grace, if you plan to return next time, please come earlier,\" said Cheng Zhao.","It was too late and disturbed her sleep.","Just as she finished speaking, Zhou Yuanshen pulled her into an embrace.","He sealed her lips.","\"Cheng Zhao,\" he whispered, his voice thick and sticky like syrup, sweet and clinging, enough to make one numb and dizzy.","Cheng Zhao felt lightheaded from his kisses.","\"Cheng Zhao, do not address me as 'Your Grace' in the bedchamber,\" he said after releasing her lips for a moment. \"Is being the Duchess truly your best prospect, Cheng Zhao? You cannot be so lackluster.\"","Cheng Zhao's heart skipped a beat.","These words forced her to overthink, almost scaring her to death.","Was the man spewing nonsense because he had drunk too much? How dare he say such things? He might not fear death, but Cheng Zhao did.","Cheng Zhao cupped his face, trying to sober him up a little.","He grabbed her hand and kissed her palm as if by reflex. He looked up at her, his gaze urgent and greedy, with a touch of bloodthirsty ferocity, fixing on her unwaveringly.","Apart from that time Aunt was drugged, he was almost always coldly rational; even when most wild, his expression remained calm.","But now, he was not even drunk and yet he looked dazed, carrying a certain ferocity, revealing another side of his nature.","Cheng Zhao felt she did not know him.","Thinking carefully, how could she claim to know him?","Did she know what spear techniques or calligraphy style he practiced daily? What clothes or food he preferred?","Every day he went to court; did she know which government office he went to first afterward, whether it was fixed or random?","Even his body—she had never really looked at it carefully.","Even several times when it was not nighttime, she would turn her face away and tightly shut her eyes.","Thinking of this, Cheng Zhao wanted to look back at him, but her body went weak first.","\"Cheng Zhao, touch me,\" he said, pulling her hand over.","This time, Cheng Zhao did not resist, nor did she close her eyes. Under the slight influence of wine, his skin was scalding hot; only when she touched him did she realize how cold her own hands were.","Her hands were too cold, and he was too hot—both of them trembled at the touch, and his breath immediately became three parts heavier.","His gaze held both endurance and frenzy.","Zhou Yuanshen even brought the small corner lamp from the bedside table closer.","Cheng Zhao saw his broad chest, not overly dark skin, and the clearly defined muscles of his abdomen. The waistline curved sharply downward, with clear lines continuing below.","On his chest and waistline were a few scars, not very noticeable.","But on his shoulder was a much more savage scar, as if something had gnawed it. The scar was chaotic, resembling a headless wolf perched on his shoulder.","Cheng Zhao, lost in passion, was still captivated by it.","She had never seen it before.","\"... What bit you to leave that?\" she asked.","It must have hurt terribly at the time, extremely painful.","Yet the scar left behind was so beautiful, like the gnarled branches of a dead old tree—art born from cruelty and pain, mesmerizing.","Zhou Yuanshen: \"Kiss it, and I'll tell you.\"","Cheng Zhao leaned forward and kissed the strange scar on his shoulder. His Adam's apple moved rapidly as he eagerly captured her lips.","He kissed her, the passionate kiss too intense, possessing her lips and tongue.","However, just as Cheng Zhao was burning with discomfort, he slowed down.","He asked Cheng Zhao: \"Can you feel me?\"","He teased her slowly, muttering incoherent words.","Cheng Zhao, holding tightly to his neck, was incredibly frustrated: \"Zhou Yuanshen, if you keep playing these tricks, don't even think about staying the night in Nonghua Courtyard!\"","Remembering something, she added, \"Twice a month, you agreed. This month you...\"","He kissed her again, stopping her words and preventing her from continuing.","After that, he behaved himself.","Afterward, Cheng Zhao was exhausted, yet she still went to offer incense to Buddha.","She kowtowed piously.","Hoping to conceive soon.","Pleasure in the bed curtains was fine, but also tiring. Sometimes Cheng Zhao just wanted to sleep early."]},{"number":99,"title":"Chapter 99: Calculation","paragraphs":["When Cheng Zhao woke up in the morning, Zhou Yuanshen had surprisingly not left yet.","Their bed was like a small, warm chamber, with a canopy hanging on the outside; inside it was a large bed, complete with a footstool, bedside tables, and a row of drawers and compartments; and then beyond that was the actual sleeping area.","Within the sleeping area, there was another curtain hung. When it was cold, both the outer canopy and inner curtain were lowered, plunging the bed into pitch darkness; when it was hot, only a thin gauze curtain was hung, and a screen was placed in front of the bed.","A horn-paned lamp sat on the bedside table, fitted with a shade, leaving only a sliver of light seeping through cracks, blurry and dim through the curtains.","When Cheng Zhao first awoke, she could barely make out Zhou Yuanshen’s silhouette, but she had no idea how bright it was outside. Still, having slept very well, she guessed it was already late.","She nudged Zhou Yuanshen: “Lord of the Manor, it’s time to get up.”","Then she added with an unnecessary question, “Are you off duty today?”","Zhou Yuanshen stirred.","“Yes,” he said.","He sat up and, ignoring that Cheng Zhao was still groggy, quickly lifted the outer canopy. Light rushed in, stinging Cheng Zhao’s eyes.","He briskly went to change clothes and wash up, his face expressionless. There was none of the relaxed ease after a sound sleep, nor did he seem about to lose his temper. In short, he was very distant.","Outside the canopy, the morning sun had already risen, casting warm rays on the rear window.","Cheng Zhao was also running late.","She asked Nanny Li, “Why didn’t you wake me?”","Nanny Li replied, “You still have half an hour before you need to report to the Hall of Honoring Heirs, so there’s no rush.”","Cheng Zhao: “...Half an hour is nowhere near enough time?”","Nanny Li chuckled, “The Lord of the Manor is off duty today, so I thought you could sleep a little longer.”","It was rare for the couple to have such an intimate moment together.","Nanny Li had specifically asked the maid Mingyu from the outer study and confirmed that the Lord of the Manor had no early commitments today, so she let them sleep in.","A maid was combing Cheng Zhao’s hair when Nanny Li came in with a bowl of bird’s nest porridge: “Eat something first to fill your stomach.”","Zhou Yuanshen re-entered, and Suyue, along with another senior maid, helped him dress.","Once he was fully dressed, he said, “I’ll have breakfast in the outer study. I need to go to the Eastern Palace this morning. I have an appointment with the Crown Prince, and I’m almost late.”","Cheng Zhao: “...”","He strode off.","Unlike his fervent attitude when he had come home last night, he had returned to being cold and aloof this morning, keeping her at arm’s length. Cheng Zhao felt dizzy, as if he hadn’t been “satisfied” last night.","But clearly...","Men really do draw a clear line between what happens in bed and matters outside the bedroom.","His passion was only a fleeting “urge.”","Cheng Zhao suddenly realized that she was nothing special to him. When he was passionate, he was merely amusing himself with her.","“...Well, it’s not like I lost anything,” she thought, sipping her bird’s nest porridge slowly.","She just shouldn’t misunderstand his attitude, mistaking his warmth for genuine affection. As for the pleasure within the curtains, he had given that to Cheng Zhao too.","Having been “satisfied” last night, she was in a very good mood this morning, feeling unusually generous.","She had no time for breakfast, finishing only the bowl of bird’s nest porridge before rinsing her mouth and rushing to the Hall of Honoring Heirs.","Qiubai himself drove a small oilcloth cart, whipping the horse furiously for fear Cheng Zhao would be late.","When Cheng Zhao arrived, Huan Qingtang had already taken her seat and was speaking to the stewards; the eldest madam had not yet emerged from her inner chamber.","“...The madam said she is unwell today, so she’ll leave matters to the eldest daughter-in-law to handle as she sees fit.” A trusted stewardess from Madam Song came to the main hall and said this.","Everyone in the hall exchanged glances.","Only yesterday had the eldest madam confronted Huan Qingtang, and now today she was hiding away from affairs. The underlying attitude was quite subtle.","It somewhat resembled the period when the eldest madam had been “resting due to illness.”","“Could it be that the eldest madam has been confined to her quarters by the old madam again?” the stewards wondered among themselves.","If that were the case, then the old madam was Huan Qingtang’s patron. From now on, the eldest daughter-in-law would command great respect and could not be underestimated.","As for Cheng Zhao, who had clearly shown great ability and shone brilliantly at the birthday banquet, she seemed to have been overshadowed yet again.","“Grandmother mentioned that in a few days, she wants to go to the Temple of Double Yang for an offering. The birthday banquet was very lively, and grandmother is happy, so she plans to hold a three-day Peaceful Purification Ritual there,” Huan Qingtang said with a smile.","The Peaceful Purification Ritual was a common, grand prayer ceremony, praying for the nation’s peace and favorable weather.","The Emperor had favored the Manor of Chen State with a special gift by personally congratulating the old madam on her birthday. The Zhou family holding this ritual to pray for peace under heaven was also a way of repaying the imperial grace.","“Have the dates been chosen?” asked a steward.","Cheng Zhao sat quietly to the side, listening silently.","“The twenty-fifth is a good date,” Huan Qingtang said. “I checked the almanac. That day is favorable for all matters. If no one objects, I’ll inform grandmother.”","She conducted herself like the head of the household, having already made her decision.","Everyone agreed.","Cheng Zhao also said, “I defer to grandmother and eldest sister-in-law’s arrangements.”","She wore a proper smile on her face, her tone warm and gentle.","Halfway through the morning, after a batch of stewards had finished reporting and left the Hall of Honoring Heirs, they couldn’t help whispering about Cheng Zhao and Huan Qingtang.","Neither of these young madams was simple.","“They have their own opinions and can make decisions. The old madam likes people who have a clear mind. Back then, when the eldest madam asked her opinion about everything, the old madam scolded her for it,” the steward praised Huan Qingtang.","Another steward praised Cheng Zhao: “She’s calm and composed, not a flicker of change on her face. Even though she shone at the banquet, she still didn’t overshadow the eldest daughter-in-law.”","Both possessed a wisdom and scheming far beyond their years.","One generation surpasses the next. Compared to the previous two madams, these two young madams of the Zhou family were much deeper in their schemes and calculations.","It was truly hard to predict which of them would come out on top by the end.","The next day, they confirmed the date for going to the Temple of Double Yang to hold the Peaceful Purification Ritual: the day after, the twenty-fifth of the third lunar month.","The old madam would attend in person.","Cheng Zhao felt a vague unease. She sent Nanny Li back to the Cheng family and asked Suyue to go to her elder sister, seeking information about all kinds of details regarding the Temple of Double Yang.","In the mid-afternoon, before Nanny Li and Suyue had returned, Zhou Yuanshen arrived home first.","Cheng Zhao told him about the matter.","“...Strictly speaking, the birthday banquet wasn’t well done. Sister-in-law’s side was full of flaws. The dishes ‘Lotus Seed Soup’ and ‘Dance of the Cranes’ were both heavily criticized. Given grandmother’s nature, this would be the time to keep a low profile. The Temple of Double Yang is a grand temple, and holding a Peaceful Purification Ritual there will draw plenty of attention. Isn’t this inviting gossip and criticism?” Cheng Zhao analyzed it for Zhou Yuanshen.","Among Taoist offerings for blessings, the Peaceful Purification Ritual was the grandest because it prayed for the prosperity of the nation.","A ceremony like this would be noted by all the meritorious noble families in the capital, once again thrusting Huan Qingtang into the spotlight. Faced with unfavorable rumors, letting things cool down and be forgotten would be the wiser approach.","If the old madam was trying to promote Huan Qingtang, raising the idea of holding such a ritual now made Cheng Zhao question the intentions behind it.","Zhou Yuanshen’s manner was cold, but he listened intently to what Cheng Zhao said.","“It is indeed a bit odd,” Zhou Yuanshen said.","“You don’t think I’m being overly suspicious, Lord of the Manor?”","“Being suspicious isn’t wrong. I don’t fully trust grandmother’s actions either. It’s good for you to be more cautious,” Zhou Yuanshen replied.","Then he added, “Cheng Zhao, you might have incurred grandmother’s displeasure. If you value your life, you need to be even more careful.”","Because during the birthday banquet, while Huan Qingtang lost face, Cheng Zhao stole the spotlight. This outcome had slipped out of the old madam’s control.","That was what she found most unacceptable.","As for how her aunt had died, Zhou Yuanshen had heard his father recount the story several times.","After that incident, his father had become disheartened, given up on any ambition for the title, and done nothing. Regarding the old madam, he heeded her every word.","He had to survive—he had a wife and children.","The old madam called him a lost cause that could not be propped up.","Even toward her own daughter, who might one day become an empress, the grand madam could be ruthless, simply because she had gone “out of control”—let alone someone as insignificant as Cheng Zhao.","Besides, the eldest branch had lost three men, and not all of them had died from illness.","Zhou Yuanshen knew that his eldest cousin had always been in poor health, frail and sickly. But his eldest uncle and second cousin had not been weak or prone to illness since childhood. The second cousin had even been a military officer, having followed their grandfather in his youth—and they had died even earlier."]},{"number":100,"title":"Chapter 100: We Are in Cahoots","paragraphs":["Zhou Yuanshen quickly regained his composure.","He looked at Cheng Zhao, wondering if she had heeded his warning. If she hadn't, he would need to prepare in advance; of course, even if she had heard him, he still had to make some arrangements to avoid trouble.","As for Cheng Zhao, after hearing his words, her expression turned serious.","She nodded. \"I've sent people to ask my mother and my eldest sister.\"","Zhou Yuanshen gave a slight nod.","A maid served tea, and he took a slow sip before saying to Cheng Zhao, \"I do know a bit about the Double Ninth Temple.\"","\"What do you know?\"","\"The Double Ninth Temple has a very famous Taoist priest whose secular surname is Yang. Some call him Heavenly Master Yang. The world only knows he excels in alchemy. He also has a Taoist name, Zhichang. What makes him most valued by the emperor is his mastery of the Mystic Gate Arts and his ability to arrange geomancy arrays.\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Upon hearing this, Cheng Zhao tried to recall: \"I've heard of this Heavenly Master Yang. People say his immortal pills are miraculous.\"","It was her fourth brother, Cheng Chao, who had mentioned him. Cheng Chao had spoken of Heavenly Master Yang when referring to the Prince of An, that is, Helian Xuan's father.","\"The prince was gravely ill, suffering terribly. Fortunately, Heavenly Master Yang's pills eased his pain. The master said his pills only relieve pain, not save lives, but Ah Xuan and the princess still held great hope,\" Cheng Chao had said at the time.","Not long after, the Prince of An passed away.","No one in the Prince of An's household blamed Heavenly Master Yang; they were only grateful that he had made the prince more comfortable in his final moments, allowing him to leave with a measure of dignity.","The Cheng family also dealt with Taoist priests and monks, but Cheng Zhao had been too young when she was betrothed, so she never interacted with such people.","\"...Does he have real skill, or is he a fraud?\" Cheng Zhao asked.","From Cheng Chao's account, it seemed Heavenly Master Yang wasn't a liar.","\"At least in the Mystic Gate Arts, he has genuine ability. The arrays he sets up are quite formidable,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Cheng Zhao recalled that military tactics also used formations, though they differed from those of Taoist priests.","\"Lord Duke, have you studied the Mystic Gate Arts?\" she asked.","If he hadn't, he probably wouldn't have stated so decisively that Heavenly Master Yang was skilled; he would have sounded more speculative.","\"I've studied the basics,\" Zhou Yuanshen said. \"Matters of talent—genius like this appears only once in centuries. Most people, even if they study hard, only grasp the basics and barely get their foot in the door.\"","\"Knowing even a bit of the basics is impressive,\" Cheng Zhao said.","The couple chatted idly for a while.","By evening, Mama Li and Su Yue had both returned.","Cheng Zhao told them not to avoid Zhou Yuanshen and to speak directly about what they had learned.","Mama Li had gone back to the Cheng residence and reported first: \"The lady said that although peace rites are common, for any meritorious aristocratic family holding such rites, allied households would rush to send gifts.\"","She added, \"The Duke's mansion just hosted a birthday celebration, and now they're making such a public display—it's a bit strange. The lady told you and the Lord Duke to be watchful.\"","She also mentioned Heavenly Master Yang.","Mama Li said: \"Master Zhichang's medicines can both cure and kill; his formations are eerie, capable of conjuring fog out of thin air. My lady doesn't understand the trick behind it.\"","It was roughly the same as the inside information Zhou Yuanshen had shared.","However, Cheng Zhao's mother had little understanding of Mystic Gate Arts and was skeptical of it, which was why she used the word \"eerie.\"","Su Yue then relayed the eldest sister's reminder.","The eldest sister also mentioned the gift-giving and Heavenly Master Yang's immortal pills.","\"The eldest miss also said the Double Ninth Temple is lush with bamboo,\" Su Yue said.","Cheng Zhao glanced at Zhou Yuanshen.","He explained: \"Bamboo groves are used to set up Mystic Gate arrays. One should not tread into them lightly.\"","Then he added, \"Of course, don't fixate too much on it, or you might overlook other aspects and fall into a trap instead.\"","Cheng Zhao's mother had deep knowledge, her eldest sister had made sharp observations, and as for Zhou Yuanshen, he likely knew about as much as the old lady did.","For the evening meal, the couple went to Jade Residence mainly to inform the Second Madam.","\"...During the rites, you'll just be seated. It's just a matter of passing the time,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","Second Madam replied, \"I'll take good care of Zhao Zhao. Don't worry.\"","Zhou Yuanqi asked, \"Do we have to go?\"","\"Probably not.\"","\"I want to go,\" he said.","Cheng Zhao wasn't keen on taking him and teased him: \"Why's that? I thought you didn't care for watching rites—mostly women go to them.\"","\"But I love watching the excitement,\" he said with a straight face.","Second Madam: \"What excitement could there be?\"","\"Can't guess, so I need to see for myself,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Cheng Zhao: \"...\"","This little brat had caught onto something again. Too clever.","Second Madam: \"...\"","Sometimes she really wanted to knock some sense into him.","Cheng Zhao was about to stop him, but Zhou Yuanshen spoke up: \"Let him go. I'm going anyway, so we can go together.\"","Zhou Yuanqi pouted: \"I don't want to go with you. I'll go with my sister-in-law and my mother. I'm a child.\"","Children could mingle with the womenfolk.","\"You're not a child anymore,\" Zhou Yuanshen said.","\"You don't get to decide that,\" Zhou Yuanqi shot back.","\"Then who does?\" Zhou Yuanshen asked. \"Next time we have a banquet, would you like to sit at the children's table?\"","\"I don't want that—I'm not that young...\"","\"So are you old or young?\" Zhou Yuanshen pressed.","The back-and-forth quibbling between the brothers left Second Madam stunned: When had Zhou Yuanshen ever acted so childish?","He fired off witty remarks one after another, cornering Zhou Yuanqi until he couldn't talk back.","In Second Madam's memory, Zhou Yuanshen had been a well-behaved boy since childhood.","When he was little, he had fair skin, even prettier than Zhou Yuanqi, and everyone adored him. Later, he spent his days running through the military camps, faster than a foal, sturdy and strong.","When he got older and the situation stabilized, the family returned to the capital, and Zhou Yuanshen attended the clan school. The teachers praised him for his perseverance and talent.","His discord with his eldest cousin, Zhou Yuancheng, had started because he constantly outshone the latter at school. Excelling in both civil and military arts, he was the most outstanding male of that generation.","The eldest grandson, Zhou Yuancheng, often stirred up trouble for him just for that reason. But Zhou Yuancheng frequently suffered from headaches and fever, and whenever they argued, he would fall ill afterward—sometimes feigning, sometimes real, hard to tell.","The eldest branch and the old lady always blamed Zhou Yuanshen.","Second Madam had argued many times with her sister-in-law and mother-in-law over this.","Zhou Yuanshen never said much.","He simply left the clan school quietly and followed his maternal grandfather to the border region.","It wasn't until he earned the title of General Who Pacifies the West and his maternal grandfather passed away that he returned to the capital.","Second Madam always felt he had endured a lot of grievances and unfairness, and as his mother, she always lost in arguments and couldn't stand up for him.","That's why, in her memory, he had never acted childlike. He seemed unwilling to trouble his parents, always good and outstanding.","Meanwhile, Zhou Yuanqi, thoroughly frustrated, dragged Cheng Zhao into it: \"Are you with me or not? Are we on the same side?\"","Cheng Zhao blinked. \"Yes.\"","Zhou Yuanqi lifted his chin triumphantly.","Zhou Yuanshen looked at Cheng Zhao.","She explained, \"At that time, all of us from the second branch will be together. We really are on the same side, Lord Duke. How about you join us too?\"","\"Don't need him,\" Zhou Yuanqi said.","Anyway, he'd have to rope someone else in eventually. Better not compete with Grandmother for a hot-tempered brute—his father said Grandmother was formidable.","\"Why not?\" Cheng Zhao asked. \"He's noble and honorable. If he's with us, we'll have an advantage.\"","Second Madam couldn't take it anymore: \"How old are you people?\"","Even a ten-year-old child wouldn't so openly \"form cliques.\"","\"Mother, you are also on our side,\" said Cheng Zhao.","The Second Madam: \"...\""]}]);
